-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc1-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER for sections 3.1 to 45 (Part I, General) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C. 1985, c. C-46.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused).
-- Each question below asks what that person would ask about Part I, General: whether what they did outside
-- Canada is within Canada's reach (section 7), whether they can be convicted at all (sections 6, 9, 13, 15), whether
-- twice (sections 7(6), 12), whether they are a party to an offence or guilty of an attempt (sections 21 to 24), and
-- which defences or justifications they have (sections 16, 17, 25 to 35, 43 and 45), and what proof, procedure and
-- notice the Code allows against them (sections 4(7), 7(10), 7(11), 20, 25.4).
--
-- ASSUMED, NOT RULED: a few questions are asked as the person who acts under a power or a duty, because the accused may
-- be that person: sections 25(5), 25.1, 31(2) and 32(1) (a peace officer, a public officer), 29 and 33(1) (the duty to
-- have a warrant, give notice, disperse), and, less plainly, 28, 30 and 31(1). The brief says never a seat for an
-- official; a reader who takes that strictly can drop them without touching layer 1.
--
-- NOTHING HERE IS NEW LAW. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list),
-- each with an @desc worded as the accused would be asked, builds the layer-1 inputs in its WHERE, and calls layer-1
-- functions. Each question calls one layer-1 function once, and its title asks what that function answers (NOTES.md
-- lists every pair), with these exceptions: section 4(3) calls the two paragraphs (a) and (b) and takes either; sections 25.1, 34 and 35 call the function of their
-- subsection (8) or (1) and the functions of the subsections that limit it, and answer as the section's own text
-- composes them. No rule is restated here.
--
-- WHAT AN ANSWER MEANS. Every question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (not covered), except two whose
-- answer is a value: section 10(3) answers a province or territory, and section 16(3) answers the party on whom the
-- burden of proof lies. JUST FALSE means the text itself says no in its own words; NOTHING means the text does not
-- answer on those facts. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. A question about a defence or justification
-- answers JUST FALSE as "this section gives no defence on these facts", never as "no defence at all"; a question
-- that asks whether a bar holds answers JUST TRUE when the bar holds. For section 7, JUST FALSE means "this
-- subsection does not deem it committed in Canada"; another subsection may.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT ASKED. No seat for an official: the designation, reporting, publication and notification machinery of
-- sections 25.1(1), (3) to (7), (12) and (13), 25.2, 25.3 and 25.4(2), the clerk's signature in section 3.1(2) and the
-- court's duties in section 33.1(2) have no question of their own. Nor do the rules of reading and the definitions
-- that ask nothing of the accused (sections 3.1(1), 4(1), 4(2), 4(4) to (6.1), 4(8), 5, 6(3), 7(2.02), 7(2.34),
-- 7(2.38), 7(8), 7(9)), the repealed or blank sections, and a few provisions a later pass could ask about (sections 7(5.1), 10(3)
-- Part XXI, 11, 22(3), 24(2), 27.1(2), 29(2) notice and 33(3)). NOTES.md lists every layer-1 function that no
-- question reaches, with the reason.
--
-- Names: every question and every helper begins "Under section N," or "ccc1 ", so that no other part's question
-- can share a name.

§ `The Criminal Code (Canada), sections 3.1 to 45 -- the accused's questions`

§§ `Sections 3.1 to 6 -- possession, the presumption of innocence, and offences outside Canada`

-- Asked by anyone charged: whether the thing counts as in your possession, whether you are presumed not guilty and what punishment can follow, and whether a conviction for an offence outside Canada is barred.

@export Under section 4(3), do I have the thing in possession, or is it deemed to be in the custody and possession of each and all of the persons who have it?
GIVEN `I have it in my personal possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have it in your personal possession?
      `I knowingly have it in the actual possession or custody of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly have it in the actual possession or custody of another person?
      `I knowingly have it in a place for the use or benefit of myself or another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly have it in any place, whether or not that place belongs to or is occupied by you, for the use or benefit of yourself or of another person?
      `it is in the custody or possession of one of two or more persons, and I am one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in the custody or possession of one of two or more persons who, with the knowledge and consent of the rest, have it, you being one of them?
      `the rest know of it and consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the rest of those persons know that one of them has it, and consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4(3), do I have the thing in possession, or is it deemed to be in the custody and possession of each and all of the persons who have it` IS
    `ccc1 either of` (`s 4(3)(a) the person has the thing in possession` `I have it in my personal possession` `I knowingly have it in the actual possession or custody of another person` `I knowingly have it in a place for the use or benefit of myself or another`) (`s 4(3)(b) the thing is deemed to be in the custody and possession of each and all of them` `it is in the custody or possession of one of two or more persons, and I am one of them` `the rest know of it and consent`)

@export Under section 4(7), may the court require me to appear before it for examination or cross-examination?
GIVEN `the person appears to have signed an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement in accordance with subsection (6) or (6.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appear to have signed an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement in accordance with subsection (6) or (6.1)?
      `the examination or cross-examination is in respect of the issue of proof of service or of the giving or sending of any notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of service or of the giving or sending of any notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4(7), may the court require me to appear before it for examination or cross-examination` IS
    `s 4(7) the court may require the person to appear before it for examination or cross-examination` `the person appears to have signed an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement in accordance with subsection (6) or (6.1)` `the examination or cross-examination is in respect of the issue of proof of service or of the giving or sending of any notice`

@export Under section 6(1)(a), am I deemed not to be guilty of the offence?
GIVEN `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an enactment create the offence and authorize a punishment to be imposed in respect of it?
      `the person has been convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of the offence?
      `the person has been discharged under section 730 of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been discharged of the offence under section 730?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 6(1)(a), am I deemed not to be guilty of the offence` IS
    `s 6(1)(a) the person is deemed not to be guilty of the offence` `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` `the person has been convicted of the offence` `the person has been discharged under section 730 of the offence`

@export Under section 6(1)(b), am I liable to the punishment?
GIVEN `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an enactment create the offence and authorize a punishment to be imposed in respect of it?
      `the person is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of the offence, or discharged of it under section 730?
      `the punishment is the punishment prescribed by this Act or by the enactment that creates the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the punishment you are asking about the punishment that the Criminal Code, or the Act that creates the offence, prescribes for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 6(1)(b), am I liable to the punishment` IS
    `s 6(1)(b) the person is liable to the punishment` `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` `the person is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` `the punishment is the punishment prescribed by this Act or by the enactment that creates the offence`

@export Under section 6(2), is my conviction or discharge under section 730 barred because the offence was committed outside Canada?
GIVEN `the offence was committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed outside Canada?
      `this Act or another Act of Parliament provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Criminal Code, or another Act of Parliament, provide otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 6(2), is my conviction or discharge under section 730 barred because the offence was committed outside Canada` IS
    `s 6(2) conviction or discharge under section 730 is barred because the offence was committed outside Canada` `the offence was committed outside Canada` `this Act or another Act of Parliament provides otherwise`

§§ `Section 7 -- Acts or omissions outside Canada that are deemed to have been committed in Canada`

-- Asked only by a person who is alleged to have done something outside Canada, on an aircraft, a ship, a platform, in space or against persons abroad. A JUST FALSE answer means "this subsection does not deem it committed in Canada"; another subsection may.

@export Under section 7(1), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada?
GIVEN `aircraft` IS A `s 7(1) the aircraft` @desc Was it on or in respect of an aircraft registered in Canada, an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person qualified to register it in Canada, or any other aircraft? Choose which, or that it was not an aircraft.
      `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the aircraft in flight when you did it? (An aircraft is in flight while it is flying, and from the time all its external doors are closed after boarding until a door is opened for getting off: section 7(8).)
      `the flight terminated in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the flight end in Canada?
      `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` IS A `Class of offence` @desc If you had done it in Canada, would it have been an indictable offence, an offence punishable only on summary conviction, or an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction? Choose which.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(1), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada` IS
    `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `aircraft` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)`) `the flight terminated in Canada` `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada`

@export Under section 7(2), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada?
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it outside Canada?
      `circumstance` IS A `s 7(2) circumstance` @desc Were you on an aircraft in flight, in relation to an aircraft in service, in relation to an air navigation facility used in international air navigation, or at or in relation to an airport serving international civil aviation? Choose which, or none of those.
      `section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the Criminal Code offence that what you did would be if it had been done in Canada? (for example 235, or 78.1)
      `subsection or paragraph of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection or paragraph of that section, written as the Code writes it (for example (2) or (a))? Leave it empty if the offence is the whole section.
      `relation` IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence` @desc If what you did outside Canada had been done in Canada, would it have been the offence itself, a conspiracy to commit it, an attempt to commit it, being an accessory after the fact to it, or counselling in relation to it? Choose which, or none of those.
      `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the aircraft in flight when you did it (section 7(8))?
      `the aircraft is in service, by s 7(9)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the aircraft in service when you did it (section 7(9))?
      `the person is, after the commission, present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you did it, were you present in Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(2), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada` IS
    `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` `circumstance` (`Provision of the Code` OF `section number of the offence`, `subsection or paragraph of the offence`) `relation` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)`) (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the aircraft is in service, by s 7(9)`) `the person is, after the commission, present in Canada`

@export Under section 7(2.01), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada?
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it outside Canada?
      `section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the Criminal Code offence that what you did would be if it had been done in Canada? (for example 235, or 78.1)
      `subsection or paragraph of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection or paragraph of that section, written as the Code writes it (for example (2) or (a))? Leave it empty if the offence is the whole section.
      `relation` IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence` @desc If what you did outside Canada had been done in Canada, would it have been the offence itself, a conspiracy to commit it, an attempt to commit it, being an accessory after the fact to it, or counselling in relation to it? Choose which, or none of those.
      `it is in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention?
      `ground (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `ground (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you someone who is not a citizen of any state and who ordinarily resides in Canada?
      `ground (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act who is, after the commission of your act or omission, present in Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(2.01), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada` IS
    `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` (`Provision of the Code` OF `section number of the offence`, `subsection or paragraph of the offence`) `relation` `it is in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1 of the Convention` `the grounds that hold`
    WHERE
        `the grounds that hold` MEANS (append (IF `ground (a)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (b)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.01)(b) the person is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada` ELSE EMPTY) (IF `ground (c)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.01)(c) the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada` ELSE EMPTY)))

@export Under section 7(2.1), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada?
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it outside Canada?
      `it is against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of any state, or a ship navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of any state, or a ship navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state?
      `section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the Criminal Code offence that what you did would be if it had been done in Canada? (for example 235, or 78.1)
      `subsection or paragraph of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection or paragraph of that section, written as the Code writes it (for example (2) or (a))? Leave it empty if the offence is the whole section.
      `relation` IS A `s 7 how the act or omission relates to the offence` @desc If what you did outside Canada had been done in Canada, would it have been the offence itself, a conspiracy to commit it, an attempt to commit it, being an accessory after the fact to it, or counselling in relation to it? Choose which, or none of those.
      `ground (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada?
      `ground (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed against or on board a ship registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament?
      `ground (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed by a Canadian citizen?
      `ground (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed by a person who is not a citizen of any state and who ordinarily resides in Canada?
      `ground (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed by a person who is, after the commission of the offence, present in Canada?
      `ground (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed in such a way as to seize, injure or kill, or threaten to injure or kill, a Canadian citizen?
      `ground (g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed in an attempt to compel the Government of Canada to do or refrain from doing any act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(2.1), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada` IS
    `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` `it is against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of any state, or a ship navigating or scheduled to navigate beyond the territorial sea of any state` (`Provision of the Code` OF `section number of the offence`, `subsection or paragraph of the offence`) `relation` `the grounds that hold`
    WHERE
        `the grounds that hold` MEANS (append (IF `ground (a)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.1)(a) the act or omission is committed against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (b)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.1)(b) the act or omission is committed against or on board a ship registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (c)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (d)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.1)(d) the act or omission is committed by a person who is not a citizen of any state and who ordinarily resides in Canada` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (e)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.1)(e) the act or omission is committed by a person who is, after the commission of the offence, present in Canada` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (f)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.1)(f) the act or omission is committed in such a way as to seize, injure or kill, or threaten to injure or kill, a Canadian citizen` ELSE EMPTY) (IF `ground (g)` THEN LIST `s 7(2.1)(g) the act or omission is committed in an attempt to compel the Government of Canada to do or refrain from doing any act` ELSE EMPTY)))))))

@export Under section 7(2.2), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada?
