@export Under section 7(3), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada?
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it outside Canada?
      `s 2 internationally protected person: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person against whom it was done an internationally protected person (a head of state, head of government or minister of foreign affairs, or a representative or official of a state or international organization who is entitled to special protection under international law, or a family member)?
      `it is against the person of that internationally protected person or against property referred to in section 431 used by that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it against the person of that internationally protected person, or against property referred to in section 431 used by that person?
      `section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the Criminal Code offence that what you did would be if it had been done in Canada? (for example 235, or 78.1)
      `subsection or paragraph of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection or paragraph of that section, written as the Code writes it (for example (2) or (a))? Leave it empty if the offence is the whole section.
      `ground (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament?
      `ground (b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed on an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act?
      `ground (b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission committed on an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations?
      `ground (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen, or someone who is, after your act or omission has been committed, present in Canada?
      `ground (d)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission against a person who enjoys the status of an internationally protected person by virtue of the functions that person performs on behalf of Canada?
      `ground (d)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act or omission against a member of the family of a person described in subparagraph (i) who qualifies under paragraph (b) or (d) of the definition internationally protected person in section 2?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(3), is what I did deemed to have been committed in Canada` IS
    `s 7(3) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `s 2 internationally protected person: the person against whom the act or omission is committed is one`) `it is against the person of that internationally protected person or against property referred to in section 431 used by that person` (`Provision of the Code` OF `section number of the offence`, `subsection or paragraph of the offence`) `the grounds that hold`
    WHERE
        `the grounds that hold` MEANS (append (IF `ground (a)` THEN LIST `s 7(3)(a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (b)(i)` THEN LIST `s 7(3)(b)(i) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (b)(ii)` THEN LIST `s 7(3)(b)(ii) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (c)` THEN LIST `s 7(3)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen or is, after the act or omission has been committed, present in Canada` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF `ground (d)(i)` THEN LIST `s 7(3)(d)(i) the act or omission is against a person who enjoys the status of an internationally protected person by virtue of the functions that person performs on behalf of Canada` ELSE EMPTY) (IF `ground (d)(ii)` THEN LIST `s 7(3)(d)(ii) the act or omission is against a member of the family of a person described in subparagraph (i) who qualifies under paragraph (b) or (d) of the definition internationally protected person in section 2` ELSE EMPTY))))))

