GIVEN `the offence requires the prosecution to prove negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence require the prosecution to prove negligence?
      `s 2 organization: the accused is one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an organization (a public body, body corporate, society, company, firm, partnership, trade union or municipality, or an association of persons that is created for a common purpose, has an operational structure and holds itself out to the public as an association of persons)?
      `s 2 representative: the person acting is a representative of the organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who acted a representative of your organization (a director, partner, employee, member, agent or contractor of it)?
      `s 2 senior officer: the officer responsible for the aspect of the activities, or the officers collectively, are senior officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer responsible for the aspect of your activities that is relevant to the offence, or are your officers collectively, a senior officer or senior officers (a representative who plays an important role in establishing your policies or is responsible for managing an important aspect of your activities)?
      `acting within the scope of their authority, one of its representatives is a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of the organization's representatives, acting within the scope of their authority, a party to the offence?
      `acting within the scope of their authority, two or more of its representatives engage in conduct, whether by act or omission, such that, if it had been the conduct of only one representative, that representative would have been a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do two or more of the organization's representatives, acting within the scope of their authority, engage in conduct, by act or omission, such that if it had been the conduct of only one representative, that representative would have been a party to the offence?
      `the senior officer who is responsible for the aspect of the organization's activities that is relevant to the offence departs markedly from the standard of care that, in the circumstances, could reasonably be expected to prevent a representative of the organization from being a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the senior officer who is responsible for the aspect of the organization's activities that is relevant to the offence depart markedly from the standard of care that, in the circumstances, could reasonably be expected to prevent a representative of the organization from being a party to the offence?
      `the senior officers, collectively, depart markedly from that standard of care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the senior officers, collectively, depart markedly from that standard of care?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22.1, does the section make the organization a party to the offence` IS
    `s 22.1 the section makes the organization a party to the offence` `the offence requires the prosecution to prove negligence` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `s 2 organization: the accused is one`) (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `s 2 representative: the person acting is a representative of the organization`) (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `s 2 senior officer: the officer responsible for the aspect of the activities, or the officers collectively, are senior officers`) `acting within the scope of their authority, one of its representatives is a party to the offence` `acting within the scope of their authority, two or more of its representatives engage in conduct, whether by act or omission, such that, if it had been the conduct of only one representative, that representative would have been a party to the offence` `the senior officer who is responsible for the aspect of the organization's activities that is relevant to the offence departs markedly from the standard of care that, in the circumstances, could reasonably be expected to prevent a representative of the organization from being a party to the offence` `the senior officers, collectively, depart markedly from that standard of care`

@export Under section 22.2, does the section make the organization a party to the offence?
GIVEN `the offence requires the prosecution to prove fault other than negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence require the prosecution to prove fault other than negligence?
      `s 2 organization: the accused is one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an organization (a public body, body corporate, society, company, firm, partnership, trade union or municipality, or an association of persons that is created for a common purpose, has an operational structure and holds itself out to the public as an association of persons)?
      `s 2 senior officer: the person acting is one of the organization's senior officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who acted one of your senior officers (a representative who plays an important role in establishing your policies or is responsible for managing an important aspect of your activities)?
      `the senior officer acts with the intent at least in part to benefit the organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a senior officer act with the intent at least in part to benefit the organization?
      `acting within the scope of their authority, the senior officer is a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a senior officer, acting within the scope of their authority, a party to the offence?
      `having the mental state required to be a party to the offence and acting within the scope of their authority, the senior officer directs the work of other representatives of the organization so that they do the act or make the omission specified in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a senior officer, having the mental state required to be a party to the offence and acting within the scope of their authority, direct the work of other representatives of the organization so that they do the act or make the omission specified in the offence?
      `knowing that a representative of the organization is or is about to be a party to the offence, the senior officer does not take all reasonable measures to stop them from being a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Knowing that a representative of the organization is or is about to be a party to the offence, does a senior officer fail to take all reasonable measures to stop the representative from being a party to the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22.2, does the section make the organization a party to the offence` IS
    `s 22.2 the section makes the organization a party to the offence` `the offence requires the prosecution to prove fault other than negligence` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `s 2 organization: the accused is one`) (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `s 2 senior officer: the person acting is one of the organization's senior officers`) `the senior officer acts with the intent at least in part to benefit the organization` `acting within the scope of their authority, the senior officer is a party to the offence` `having the mental state required to be a party to the offence and acting within the scope of their authority, the senior officer directs the work of other representatives of the organization so that they do the act or make the omission specified in the offence` `knowing that a representative of the organization is or is about to be a party to the offence, the senior officer does not take all reasonable measures to stop them from being a party to the offence`

@export Under section 23(1), am I an accessory after the fact to the offence?
