      `the person does or omits to do anything for the purpose of carrying out the intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do or omit to do anything for the purpose of carrying out the intention?
      `it was possible under the circumstances to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it possible under the circumstances to commit the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(1), am I guilty of an attempt to commit the offence` IS
    `s 24(1) the person is guilty of an attempt to commit the offence` `the person has an intent to commit an offence` `the person does or omits to do anything for the purpose of carrying out the intention` `it was possible under the circumstances to commit the offence`

§§ `Sections 25 to 25.4 -- Protection of persons acting under authority`

-- Asked by a peace officer, public officer or private person who is charged with an offence for something done in enforcing the law. Section 25.1(3) to (7), 25.2 and 25.3 are addressed to officials and have no question here.

@export Under section 25(1), am I justified in doing what I was required or authorized by law to do?
GIVEN `the person is required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law?
      `capacity` IS A `s 25(1) the capacity in which the person acts` @desc In which capacity did you act: as a private person required or authorized by law to act, as a peace officer or public officer, in aid of a peace officer or public officer, by virtue of your office, or in none of those capacities? Choose which.
      `my capacity as a possible peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a peace officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `my capacity as a possible public officer` IS A `s 2 public officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a public officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `the person acts on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act on reasonable grounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(1), am I justified in doing what I was required or authorized by law to do` IS
    `s 25(1) the person is justified in doing what they are required or authorized to do` `the person is required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law` `capacity` (`ccc1 either of` (`s 2 peace officer` `my capacity as a possible peace officer`) (`s 2 public officer` `my capacity as a possible public officer`)) `the person acts on reasonable grounds`

@export Under section 25(1), am I justified in using as much force as is necessary for that purpose?
GIVEN `the person is required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law?
      `capacity` IS A `s 25(1) the capacity in which the person acts` @desc In which capacity did you act: as a private person required or authorized by law to act, as a peace officer or public officer, in aid of a peace officer or public officer, by virtue of your office, or in none of those capacities? Choose which.
      `my capacity as a possible peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a peace officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `my capacity as a possible public officer` IS A `s 2 public officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a public officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `the person acts on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act on reasonable grounds?
      `the force used is as much as is necessary for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force used as much as is necessary for that purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(1), am I justified in using as much force as is necessary for that purpose` IS
    `s 25(1) the person is justified in using as much force as is necessary for that purpose` (`s 25(1) the person is justified in doing what they are required or authorized to do` `the person is required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law` `capacity` (`ccc1 either of` (`s 2 peace officer` `my capacity as a possible peace officer`) (`s 2 public officer` `my capacity as a possible public officer`)) `the person acts on reasonable grounds`) `the force used is as much as is necessary for that purpose`

@export Under section 25(2), am I justified in executing the process or in carrying out the sentence?
GIVEN `the person is required or authorized by law to execute a process or to carry out a sentence, or is assisting a person who is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required or authorized by law to execute a process or to carry out a sentence, or are you assisting a person who is?
      `the person required or authorized acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act in good faith?
      `the process or sentence is defective, or was issued or imposed without jurisdiction or in excess of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the process or sentence defective, or was it issued or imposed without jurisdiction or in excess of jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(2), am I justified in executing the process or in carrying out the sentence` IS
    `s 25(2) the person is justified in executing the process or in carrying out the sentence` `the person is required or authorized by law to execute a process or to carry out a sentence, or is assisting a person who is` `the person required or authorized acts in good faith` `the process or sentence is defective, or was issued or imposed without jurisdiction or in excess of jurisdiction`

@export Under section 25(3), does subsection (3) bar justification under subsection (1) for the force?
GIVEN `the force is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force you used intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm?
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary for the self-preservation of the person or the preservation of any one under that person's protection from death or grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that the force is necessary for your self-preservation or the preservation of any one under your protection from death or grievous bodily harm?
      `subsection (4) or (5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection (4) or (5) apply to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(3), does subsection (3) bar justification under subsection (1) for the force` IS
    `s 25(3) subsection (3) bars justification under subsection (1) for the force` `the force is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm` `the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary for the self-preservation of the person or the preservation of any one under that person's protection from death or grievous bodily harm` `subsection (4) or (5) applies`

@export Under section 25(4), am I justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm to the person to be arrested?
GIVEN `my capacity as a possible peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a peace officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `the person is lawfully assisting the peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you lawfully assisting the peace officer?
      `the peace officer is proceeding lawfully to arrest, with or without warrant, the person to be arrested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the peace officer proceeding lawfully to arrest the person, with or without warrant?
      `the offence for which the person is to be arrested is one for which that person may be arrested without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence for which the person is to be arrested one for which that person may be arrested without warrant?
      `the person to be arrested takes flight to avoid arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person to be arrested take flight to avoid arrest?
      `the peace officer or other person using the force believes on reasonable grounds that the force is necessary for the purpose of protecting the peace officer, the person lawfully assisting the peace officer or any other person from imminent or future death or grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, using the force, believe on reasonable grounds that the force is necessary for the purpose of protecting the peace officer, the person lawfully assisting the peace officer or any other person from imminent or future death or grievous bodily harm?
      `the flight cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the flight not be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(4), am I justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm to the person to be arrested` IS
    `s 25(4) the person is justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm to the person to be arrested` (`s 2 peace officer` `my capacity as a possible peace officer`) `the person is lawfully assisting the peace officer` `the peace officer is proceeding lawfully to arrest, with or without warrant, the person to be arrested` `the offence for which the person is to be arrested is one for which that person may be arrested without warrant` `the person to be arrested takes flight to avoid arrest` `the peace officer or other person using the force believes on reasonable grounds that the force is necessary for the purpose of protecting the peace officer, the person lawfully assisting the peace officer or any other person from imminent or future death or grievous bodily harm` `the flight cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner`

@export Under section 25(5), am I, a peace officer, justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm against the inmate?
GIVEN `my capacity as a possible peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a peace officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `the inmate is escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inmate escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act?
      `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that any of the inmates of the penitentiary poses a threat of death or grievous bodily harm to the peace officer or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, a peace officer, believe on reasonable grounds that any of the inmates of the penitentiary poses a threat of death or grievous bodily harm to you or any other person?
      `the escape cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the escape not be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25(5), am I, a peace officer, justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm against the inmate` IS
    `s 25(5) the peace officer is justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm against the inmate` (`s 2 peace officer` `my capacity as a possible peace officer`) `the inmate is escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that any of the inmates of the penitentiary poses a threat of death or grievous bodily harm to the peace officer or any other person` `the escape cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner`

@export Under section 25.1, am I, a public officer, justified, subject to subsections (9), (11) and (14)?
GIVEN `my capacity as a possible peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a peace officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `my capacity as a possible public officer` IS A `s 2 public officer capacity` @desc If you acted as a public officer, in which capacity under section 2 did you act? Choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if you were in none of the listed capacities.
      `the person has the powers of a peace officer under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the powers of a peace officer under an Act of Parliament?
      `the public officer is engaged in the investigation of an offence under, or the enforcement of, an Act of Parliament or in the investigation of criminal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you engaged in the investigation of an offence under, or the enforcement of, an Act of Parliament or in the investigation of criminal activity?
      `the public officer is designated under subsection (3) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you designated under subsection (3) or (6)?
      `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that the commission of your act or omission, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances?
      `the act or omission would be likely to result in loss of or serious damage to property, or is a directing of an act or omission under subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your act or omission be likely to result in loss of or serious damage to property, or is it a directing of an act or omission under subsection (10)?
      `the conditions set out in paragraphs (8)(a) to (c) are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions set out in paragraphs 25.1(8)(a) to (c) met?
      `the public officer is personally authorized in writing to commit the act or omission, or direct its commission, by a senior official who believes on reasonable grounds that committing it, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you personally authorized in writing to commit your act or omission, or direct its commission, by a senior official who believes on reasonable grounds that committing it, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances?
      `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the grounds for obtaining an authorization under paragraph (a) exist but it is not feasible in the circumstances to obtain the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that the grounds for obtaining an authorization under paragraph (a) exist but it is not feasible in the circumstances to obtain the authorization?
      `necessary` IS A `s 25.1(9)(b) what the act or omission is necessary to do` @desc What was your act or omission necessary to do: preserve the life or safety of any person, prevent the compromise of the identity of an undercover public officer, a confidential informant or a covert person, prevent the imminent loss or destruction of evidence of an indictable offence, or none of those? Choose which.
      `conduct` IS A `s 25.1(11) the conduct` @desc Which is your conduct: the intentional or criminally negligent causing of death or bodily harm to another person, the wilful attempt to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice, conduct that would violate the sexual integrity of an individual, or other conduct? Choose which.
      `the act or omission constitutes an offence under a provision of Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or of the regulations made under it or a provision of Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your act or omission constitute an offence under a provision of Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or of the regulations made under it or a provision of Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25.1, am I, a public officer, justified, subject to subsections (9), (11) and (14)` IS
    `s 25.1 the public officer is justified, subject to subsections (9), (11) and (14)` (`s 25.1(8) the public officer is justified in committing the act or omission` (`s 25.1(1) the person is a public officer` (`s 2 peace officer` `my capacity as a possible peace officer`) (`s 2 public officer` `my capacity as a possible public officer`) `the person has the powers of a peace officer under an Act of Parliament`) `the public officer is engaged in the investigation of an offence under, or the enforcement of, an Act of Parliament or in the investigation of criminal activity` `the public officer is designated under subsection (3) or (6)` `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances`) (`s 25.1(9) subsection (9) bars the public officer's justification` `the act or omission would be likely to result in loss of or serious damage to property, or is a directing of an act or omission under subsection (10)` `the conditions set out in paragraphs (8)(a) to (c) are met` `the public officer is personally authorized in writing to commit the act or omission, or direct its commission, by a senior official who believes on reasonable grounds that committing it, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances` `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the grounds for obtaining an authorization under paragraph (a) exist but it is not feasible in the circumstances to obtain the authorization` `necessary`) (`s 25.1(11) the section justifies the conduct` `conduct`) (`s 25.1(14) the section justifies the act or omission` `the act or omission constitutes an offence under a provision of Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or of the regulations made under it or a provision of Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act`)

@export Under section 25.1(10), am I justified in committing the act or omission at the direction of a public officer?
GIVEN `a public officer directs the person to commit the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a public officer direct you to commit the act or omission?
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the public officer has the authority to give that direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe on reasonable grounds that the public officer had the authority to give that direction?
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission is for the purpose of assisting the public officer in the public officer's law enforcement duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe on reasonable grounds that committing the act or omission was for the purpose of assisting the public officer in the public officer's law enforcement duties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 25.1(10), am I justified in committing the act or omission at the direction of a public officer` IS
    `s 25.1(10) the person is justified in committing the act or omission at the direction of a public officer` `a public officer directs the person to commit the act or omission` `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the public officer has the authority to give that direction` `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission is for the purpose of assisting the public officer in the public officer's law enforcement duties`

