§§ `Sections 26 to 33 -- Force, arrest, breach of the peace and riots`

-- Asked by a person charged with an offence committed while using force, arresting, or suppressing a riot.

@export Under section 26, am I criminally responsible for the excess of force I used?
GIVEN `the person is authorized by law to use force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you authorized by law to use force?
      `the force used is in excess of what the law authorizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force used in excess of what the law authorizes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 26, am I criminally responsible for the excess of force I used` IS
    `s 26 the person is criminally responsible for the excess of force` `the person is authorized by law to use force` `the force used is in excess of what the law authorizes`

@export Under section 27, am I justified in using the force?
GIVEN `the force is used to prevent the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force used to prevent the commission of an offence?
      `the person who committed the offence, if it were committed, might be arrested without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offence were committed, might the person who committed it be arrested without warrant?
      `the offence would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the person or property of anyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the offence be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the person or property of anyone?
      `the force is used to prevent anything being done that, on reasonable grounds, the person believes would, if it were done, be an offence mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force used to prevent anything being done that, on reasonable grounds, you believe would, if it were done, be an offence for which the person who committed it might be arrested without warrant and that would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to a person or property?
      `the force is as much as is reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force as much as is reasonably necessary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 27, am I justified in using the force` IS
    `s 27 the person is justified in using the force` `the force is used to prevent the commission of an offence` `the person who committed the offence, if it were committed, might be arrested without warrant` `the offence would be likely to cause immediate and serious injury to the person or property of anyone` `the force is used to prevent anything being done that, on reasonable grounds, the person believes would, if it were done, be an offence mentioned in paragraph (a)` `the force is as much as is reasonably necessary`

@export Under section 27.1(1), am I, the person on the aircraft, justified in using the force?
GIVEN `the aircraft is in flight, by s 7(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the aircraft in flight (section 7(8))?
