      `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to damage or destroy the property, or make it inoperative, or is doing so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to damage or destroy the property, or make it inoperative, or is doing so?
      `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from entering the property, or removing that person from the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act that constitutes the offence committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from entering the property, or removing that person from the property?
      `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from taking, damaging or destroying the property or from making it inoperative, or retaking the property from that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act that constitutes the offence committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from taking, damaging or destroying the property or from making it inoperative, or retaking the property from that person?
      `the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act committed reasonable in the circumstances?
      `the person who believes on reasonable grounds that they are, or who is believed on reasonable grounds to be, in peaceable possession of the property does not have a claim of right to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you believe on reasonable grounds that you are in peaceable possession of the property, or are believed on reasonable grounds to be: do you lack a claim of right to it?
      `the other person is entitled to its possession by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person entitled to its possession by law?
      `the other person is doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law?
      `the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 35, am I not guilty of the offence, subject to subsections (2) and (3)` IS
    `s 35 the person is not guilty of the offence, subject to subsections (2) and (3)` (`s 35(1) the person is not guilty of the offence` `they believe on reasonable grounds that they are in peaceable possession of property` `they are acting under the authority of, or lawfully assisting, a person whom they believe on reasonable grounds is in peaceable possession of property` `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to enter, is entering or has entered the property without being entitled by law to do so` `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to take the property, is doing so or has just done so` `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to damage or destroy the property, or make it inoperative, or is doing so` `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from entering the property, or removing that person from the property` `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from taking, damaging or destroying the property or from making it inoperative, or retaking the property from that person` `the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances`) (`s 35(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the other person is entitled to possession` `the person who believes on reasonable grounds that they are, or who is believed on reasonable grounds to be, in peaceable possession of the property does not have a claim of right to it` `the other person is entitled to its possession by law`) (`s 35(3) subsection (1) does not apply because the other person is acting in the administration or enforcement of the law` `the other person is doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law` `the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully`)

@export Under section 43, am I justified in using force by way of correction toward the pupil or child?
GIVEN `who` IS A `s 43 the person is` @desc Are you a schoolteacher, a parent, a person standing in the place of a parent, or another person? Choose which.
      `the pupil or child is under their care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the pupil or child under your care?
      `the force is used by way of correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force used by way of correction?
      `the force does not exceed what is reasonable under the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the force not exceed what is reasonable under the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 43, am I justified in using force by way of correction toward the pupil or child` IS
    `s 43 the person is justified in using force by way of correction toward the pupil or child` `who` `the pupil or child is under their care` `the force is used by way of correction` `the force does not exceed what is reasonable under the circumstances`

@export Under section 45, am I protected from criminal responsibility for performing a surgical operation?
GIVEN `the person performs a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you perform a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person?
      `the operation is performed with reasonable care and skill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the operation performed with reasonable care and skill?
      `it is reasonable to perform the operation, having regard to the state of health of the person at the time the operation is performed and to all the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it reasonable to perform the operation, having regard to the state of health of the person on whom it is performed at the time the operation is performed and to all the circumstances of the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 45, am I protected from criminal responsibility for performing a surgical operation` IS
    `s 45 the person is protected from criminal responsibility for performing the surgical operation` `the person performs a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person` `the operation is performed with reasonable care and skill` `it is reasonable to perform the operation, having regard to the state of health of the person at the time the operation is performed and to all the circumstances of the case`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc2 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc2-seat.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART II (ss 46 to 83) -- THE SEAT LAYER (layer 2). Lines 850-1248 of the text.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an
-- offence, what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what
-- follows from a conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no
-- charge-generator contract.) There is never a seat for an official: sections addressed to an official (s 67, s 70(1), s 52.1(6)) are encoded in layer 1 for what
-- they decide, and appear here only as what they mean to the person (s 68, s 70(3)).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, one per fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The layer-1
-- modules' answers are called, never restated. Where a rule turns on a term of section 2 the person states the facts the keel's definition asks (its kind
-- enumeration), and the keel's function (`ccc-definitions`) is called. Where a rule turns on a term the Code borrows from outside the sources (the Canadian
-- Passport Order, the Citizenship Act, the law of nations, regulations, section 342.1(2), section 467.1(1)) the person says "yes" only if they know it holds:
-- a "yes" is JUST TRUE and anything else is NOTHING, never JUST FALSE, because the person's "no" or "I do not know" is not the text's own no.
--
-- READING A RESULT. JUST TRUE: yes, on the text's own words. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "unless", a flat negative,
-- a period fixed in the text's own words). NOTHING: not covered by this section (an offence element is unmet, a case lies outside a limit the text sets, a
-- borrowed term is not shown). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE: "not covered" is not "not guilty".
--
-- PENALTY. A section that says "guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction" states no penalty: it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which is not
-- in this part. A question about a penalty answers the class of the offence, what the section states on indictment, and says when section 787(1) applies instead.
-- Names: every question begins "Under section N,"; each question's name asks the question its body answers, in the same direction.

DECLARE `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty` HAS
    `the class of the offence`  IS A `Class of offence`
    `the most imprisonment the section states on indictment`  IS AN Imprisonment
    `the least imprisonment the section states on indictment`  IS AN Imprisonment
    `the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in the section: section 787(1) applies`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Not a fact the person can state: only the seam value of section 787(1), which no question here reads (a placeholder that states nothing).
`Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

GIVEN class IS A `Class of offence`
      limbs IS A LIST OF Punishment
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
`Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` MEANS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty` WITH
        `the class of the offence` IS class
        `the most imprisonment the section states on indictment` IS `the first limb`'s `maximum imprisonment`
        `the least imprisonment the section states on indictment` IS `the first limb`'s `minimum imprisonment`
        `the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in the section: section 787(1) applies` IS NOT (class EQUALS `an indictable offence`)
    WHERE
        `the first limb` MEANS
            CONSIDER limbs
            WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN first
            WHEN EMPTY THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

GIVEN limbs IS A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`Under sections 46 to 83, the most imprisonment the first limb states, if the section states a penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER limbs
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the section states no penalty for the case
    WHEN JUST stated THEN
        CONSIDER stated
        WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (first's `maximum imprisonment`)
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no limb

GIVEN yes IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` MEANS
    IF yes THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the person's "no" or "I do not know" is not the text's own no

§ `Treason: sections 46 to 48 (lines 850-887)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then trial. Section 48 is a bar on the prosecution; section 47(3) a rule of proof.

@ref Criminal Code s 46(1), s 46(3)(a)
@export Under section 46(1) and (3)(a), is what I did high treason?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 46(1) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I did it in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it in Canada?
      `I am a Canadian citizen or I owe allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen, or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46(1) and (3)(a), is what I did high treason` IS
    `s 46(1) or (3)(a) high treason is committed` `what I did` `I did it in Canada` `I am a Canadian citizen or I owe allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada`

@ref Criminal Code s 46(2), s 46(3)(b)
@export Under section 46(2) and (3)(b), is what I did treason?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 46(2) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I did it in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it in Canada?
      `I am a Canadian citizen or I owe allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen, or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada?
      `I acted without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without lawful authority? (Asked for the communication of information.)
      `I knew or ought to have known that the information might be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or ought you to have known, that the information might be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada?
      `I manifested my intention by an overt act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you manifest the intention by an overt act? (Asked where you formed an intention.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46(2) and (3)(b), is what I did treason` IS
    `s 46(2) or (3)(b) treason is committed` `what I did` `I did it in Canada` `I am a Canadian citizen or I owe allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` `I acted without lawful authority` `I knew or ought to have known that the information might be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` `I manifested my intention by an overt act`

@ref Criminal Code s 46(4)
@export Under section 46(4), is the act of conspiring an overt act of treason?
GIVEN `it is treason to conspire with the person I conspired with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it treason to conspire with that person (as section 46(2)(c) or (e) makes it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 46(4), is the act of conspiring an overt act of treason` IS
    `s 46(4) the act of conspiring is an overt act of treason` `it is treason to conspire with the person I conspired with`

@ref Criminal Code s 47(1), s 47(4)
@export Under section 47(1), what penalty does the section state for high treason?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 47(1), what penalty does the section state for high treason` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 47(1) the class of the offence of high treason`) (`s 47(1) the punishment for high treason`)

@ref Criminal Code s 47(2)
@export Under section 47(2), what is the most imprisonment I face for treason?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 46(2) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `a state of war exists between Canada and another country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a state of war exist between Canada and another country when you did it?
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
DECIDE `Under section 47(2), what is the most imprisonment I face for treason` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, the most imprisonment the first limb states, if the section states a penalty` (`s 47(2) the punishment for treason` `what I did` `a state of war exists between Canada and another country`)

@ref Criminal Code s 47(3)
@export Under section 47(3), is a conviction of me for high treason or treason barred because only one witness gives evidence against me?
GIVEN `the offence charged is high treason or treason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with high treason or treason?
      `the conviction would rest on the evidence of only one witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a conviction rest on the evidence of only one witness?
      `that witness's evidence is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that witness's evidence corroborated in a material particular by other evidence that implicates you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 47(3), is a conviction of me for high treason or treason barred because only one witness gives evidence against me` IS
    `s 47(3) a conviction of high treason or treason on that evidence is barred` `the offence charged is high treason or treason` `the conviction would rest on the evidence of only one witness` `that witness's evidence is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates me`

@ref Criminal Code s 47(4)
@export Under section 47(4), is the sentence of imprisonment for life for high treason a minimum punishment?
GIVEN `the question arises for the purposes of Part XXIII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the question arise for the purposes of Part XXIII (sentencing)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 47(4), is the sentence of imprisonment for life for high treason a minimum punishment` IS
    `s 47(4) the sentence of imprisonment for life prescribed by subsection 47(1) is a minimum punishment` `the question arises for the purposes of Part XXIII`

@ref Criminal Code s 48(1)
@export Under section 48(1), is a prosecution of me for treason by force or violence barred because more than three years have passed?
GIVEN `I am charged with treason as defined by paragraph 46(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with treason by using force or violence to overthrow the government (paragraph 46(2)(a))?
      `the date the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the offence alleged to have been committed?
      `the date the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the proceedings commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48(1), is a prosecution of me for treason by force or violence barred because more than three years have passed` IS
    `s 48(1) the proceedings are barred by the three-year limit` `I am charged with treason as defined by paragraph 46(2)(a)` `the date the offence is alleged to have been committed` `the date the proceedings were commenced`

@ref Criminal Code s 48(2)
@export Under section 48(2), is a prosecution of me for treasonable words barred because the information or the warrant came too late?
GIVEN `the proceedings are for an overt act of treason expressed by open and considered speech` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings under section 47 for an overt act of treason expressed or declared by open and considered speech?
      `an information setting out the overt act and the words was laid under oath before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an information setting out the overt act and the words laid under oath before a justice?
      `the date the words are alleged to have been spoken` IS A DATE @desc On what date are the words alleged to have been spoken?
      `the date the information was laid` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the information laid?
      `a warrant for my arrest was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a warrant for your arrest issued?
      `the date the warrant was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the warrant issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48(2), is a prosecution of me for treasonable words barred because the information or the warrant came too late` IS
    `s 48(2) the proceedings are barred unless the information and warrant came in time` `the proceedings are for an overt act of treason expressed by open and considered speech` `an information setting out the overt act and the words was laid under oath before a justice` `the date the words are alleged to have been spoken` `the date the information was laid` `a warrant for my arrest was issued` `the date the warrant was issued`

§ `Prohibited acts: sections 49 to 56 (lines 889-970)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, election and pre-trial procedure (the consents of ss 52.3 and 54), trial (s 55).

@ref Criminal Code s 50(1)(a)
@export Under section 50(1)(a), have I committed the offence of helping a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada?
GIVEN `I incited, or wilfully assisted, a subject of such a state to leave Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you incite, or wilfully assist, a subject of a state to leave Canada?
      `the state is at war with Canada, or Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities against its forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that state at war with Canada, or are Canadian Forces engaged in hostilities against its forces (whether or not a state of war exists)?
      `the leaving was without the consent of the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the leaving without the consent of the Crown?
      `I can establish that assistance to the state or its forces was not intended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that assistance to that state, or to its forces, was not intended by what you did?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 50(1)(a), have I committed the offence of helping a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` IS
    `s 50(1)(a) the person assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` `I incited, or wilfully assisted, a subject of such a state to leave Canada` `the state is at war with Canada, or Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities against its forces` `the leaving was without the consent of the Crown` `I can establish that assistance to the state or its forces was not intended`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `Under section 50(1)(b), have I committed the offence of not preventing a treason I knew was about to happen`; retitled: the body tests whether the person informed a justice of the peace or other peace officer or made other reasonable efforts, not whether the treason was prevented; answer unchanged
@ref Criminal Code s 50(1)(b)
@export Under section 50(1)(b), have I committed the offence of neither informing a peace officer nor making other reasonable efforts to prevent a treason I knew was about to happen?
GIVEN `I knew that another person was about to commit high treason or treason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that another person was about to commit high treason or treason?
      `I told someone about it with all reasonable dispatch` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell someone about it with all reasonable dispatch?
      `the person I told is` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc If you told someone, who is that person? Choose the description that fits, or the last choice if none does (or if you told nobody).
      `I made other reasonable efforts to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make other reasonable efforts to prevent that person from committing it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 50(1)(b), have I committed the offence of neither informing a peace officer nor making other reasonable efforts to prevent a treason I knew was about to happen` IS
    `s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` `I knew that another person was about to commit high treason or treason` `I told someone about it with all reasonable dispatch` (`s 2 peace officer` `the person I told is`) `I made other reasonable efforts to prevent it`

@ref Criminal Code s 50(2)
@export Under section 50(2), what penalty does the section state for an offence under section 50(1)?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 50(2), what penalty does the section state for an offence under section 50(1)` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 50(2) the class of the offence under subsection 50(1)`) (`s 50(2) the punishment for an offence under subsection 50(1)`)

@ref Criminal Code s 51
@export Under section 51, have I intimidated Parliament or a legislature by an act of violence?
GIVEN `I did an act of violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do an act of violence?
      `I did it in order to intimidate Parliament or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it in order to intimidate Parliament or the legislature of a province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 51, have I intimidated Parliament or a legislature by an act of violence` IS
    `s 51 the person intimidates Parliament or the legislature of a province` `I did an act of violence` `I did it in order to intimidate Parliament or the legislature of a province`

@ref Criminal Code s 51
@export Under section 51, what penalty does the section state for intimidating Parliament or a legislature?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 51, what penalty does the section state for intimidating Parliament or a legislature` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 51 the class of the offence`) (`s 51 the punishment`)

@ref Criminal Code s 52(1) to (5)
@export Under section 52(1), have I committed sabotage?
GIVEN `what I did impaired the efficiency or impeded the working of a vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your act or omission impair the efficiency or impede the working of any vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing?
      `what I did caused property, whoever owned it, to be lost, damaged or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your act or omission cause property, by whomever it may be owned, to be lost, damaged or destroyed?
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I stopped work over a failure to agree with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason what you did could be a prohibited act that you stopped work because your employer and you failed to agree on a matter relating to your employment?
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I stopped work over a failure of my employer and my bargaining agent to agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you stopped work because your employer and a bargaining agent acting for you failed to agree on a matter relating to your employment?
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I stopped work as part of a combination for reasonable protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you stopped work as a result of taking part in a combination of workers or employees for their own reasonable protection?
      `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I attended at or near a dwelling-house or place only to obtain or communicate information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you attended at or near, or approached, a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information?
      `I was taking part in advocacy, protest or dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you participating in advocacy, protest or dissent?
      `I intended to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada?
      `I intended to endanger the safety or security of the forces of another state lawfully present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to endanger the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 52(1), have I committed sabotage` IS
    `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` `what I did impaired the efficiency or impeded the working of a vessel, vehicle, aircraft, machinery, apparatus or other thing` `what I did caused property, whoever owned it, to be lost, damaged or destroyed` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I stopped work over a failure to agree with my employer` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I stopped work over a failure of my employer and my bargaining agent to agree` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I stopped work as part of a combination for reasonable protection` `the only reason it could be a prohibited act is that I attended at or near a dwelling-house or place only to obtain or communicate information` `I was taking part in advocacy, protest or dissent` `I intended to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada` `I intended to endanger the safety or security of the forces of another state lawfully present in Canada`

@ref Criminal Code s 52(1)
@export Under section 52(1), what penalty does the section state for sabotage?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 52(1), what penalty does the section state for sabotage` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 52(1) the class of the offence of sabotage`) (`s 52(1) the punishment for sabotage` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

@ref Criminal Code s 52.1(1) to (5), s 52.1(2)
@export Under section 52.1(1), have I committed sabotage of an essential infrastructure?
GIVEN `I interfered with access to an essential infrastructure, or caused it to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you interfere with access to a facility or system, or cause it to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use?
      `the facility or system is of the kind` IS A `s 52.1(2) kind of infrastructure` @desc What kind of infrastructure is it? Choose the kind that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `it is a facility or system, public or private, completed or under construction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a facility or system, whether public or private, completed or under construction?
      `it provides or distributes services essential to the health, safety, security or economic well-being of persons in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide or distribute (or is it intended to provide or distribute) services that are essential to the health, safety, security or economic well-being of persons in Canada?
      `I know that regulations under section 52.1(6) prescribe it as essential infrastructure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that regulations under section 52.1(6) prescribe this infrastructure? (Answer yes only if you know.)
      `I intended to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada?
      `I intended to endanger the safety or security of the forces of another state lawfully present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to endanger the safety or security of the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada that are lawfully present in Canada?
      `I intended to cause a serious risk to the health or safety of the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to cause a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public?
      `the only reason for the offence is that I stopped work over a failure to agree with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you stopped work because your employer and you failed to agree on a matter relating to your employment?
      `the only reason for the offence is that I stopped work over a failure of my employer and my bargaining agent to agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you stopped work because your employer and a bargaining agent acting for you failed to agree?
      `the only reason for the offence is that I stopped work as part of a combination for reasonable protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you stopped work as a result of taking part in a combination of workers or employees for their own reasonable protection?
      `the only reason for the offence is that I attended at or near a dwelling-house or place only to obtain or communicate information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason that you attended at or near, or approached, a dwelling-house or place for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information?
      `I was taking part in advocacy, protest or dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you participating in advocacy, protest or dissent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 52.1(1), have I committed sabotage of an essential infrastructure` IS
    `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` `I interfered with access to an essential infrastructure, or caused it to be lost, inoperable, unsafe or unfit for use` (`s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `the facility or system is of the kind` `it is a facility or system, public or private, completed or under construction` `it provides or distributes services essential to the health, safety, security or economic well-being of persons in Canada` (`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` `I know that regulations under section 52.1(6) prescribe it as essential infrastructure`)) `I intended to endanger the safety, security or defence of Canada` `I intended to endanger the safety or security of the forces of another state lawfully present in Canada` `I intended to cause a serious risk to the health or safety of the public` `the only reason for the offence is that I stopped work over a failure to agree with my employer` `the only reason for the offence is that I stopped work over a failure of my employer and my bargaining agent to agree` `the only reason for the offence is that I stopped work as part of a combination for reasonable protection` `the only reason for the offence is that I attended at or near a dwelling-house or place only to obtain or communicate information` `I was taking part in advocacy, protest or dissent`

@ref Criminal Code s 52.1(1)
