      `the thing is a device in the ordinary sense of the word` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a device in the ordinary sense of the word?
      `the thing is a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2)? (Answer yes only if you know.)
      `I intended that it be used to carry out sabotage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that it be used, in whole or in part, to carry out an offence under subsection 52(1) or 52.1(1)?
      `I knew that it would be used to carry out sabotage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that it would be used, in whole or in part, to carry out an offence under subsection 52(1) or 52.1(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 52.2(1), have I committed the offence of dealing in a device for sabotage` IS
    `s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` `I made, possessed, sold or distributed the thing` (`s 52.2(3) the thing is a device` `the thing is a device in the ordinary sense of the word` (`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` `the thing is a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2)`)) `I intended that it be used to carry out sabotage` `I knew that it would be used to carry out sabotage`

@ref Criminal Code s 52.2(2)
@export Under section 52.2(2), what penalty does the section state for the device offence?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 52.2(2), what penalty does the section state for the device offence` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 52.2(2) the class of the offence under subsection 52.2(1)`) (`s 52.2(2) the punishment for an offence under subsection 52.2(1)` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

@ref Criminal Code s 52.3
