§ `Official documents: sections 56.1 to 58 (lines 972-1020)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then election and pre-trial procedure (the place of trial, s 57(6)).

@ref Criminal Code s 56.1(1) to (3)
@export Under section 56.1(1), have I committed the identity document offence?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 56.1(1) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
      `the document is of the kind` IS A `s 56.1(3) kind of document` @desc What kind of document is it? Choose the kind that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `the document was issued, or purports to be issued, by a department or agency of a government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued, or does it purport to be issued, by a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial or foreign government?
      `the document is a passport as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a passport as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order? (Answer yes only if you know.)
      `the document relates or purports to relate to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate, or purport to relate, in whole or in part, to another person?
      `I acted in good faith in the ordinary course of my business, employment or office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in good faith, in the ordinary course of your business or employment or in the exercise of the duties of your office?
      `I acted for genealogical purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act for genealogical purposes?
      `I acted with the consent of the person to whom it relates, of a person authorized to consent for them, or of the entity that issued it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with the consent of the person to whom the document relates, of a person authorized to consent on their behalf, or of the entity that issued it?
      `I acted for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56.1(1), have I committed the identity document offence` IS
    `s 56.1(1) the person commits the identity document offence` `what I did` `I had a lawful excuse` (`s 56.1(3) the document is an identity document` `the document is of the kind` `the document was issued, or purports to be issued, by a department or agency of a government` (`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` `the document is a passport as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order`)) `the document relates or purports to relate to another person` `I acted in good faith in the ordinary course of my business, employment or office` `I acted for genealogical purposes` `I acted with the consent of the person to whom it relates, of a person authorized to consent for them, or of the entity that issued it` `I acted for a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice`

