DECIDE `Under section 57(3), have I possessed a forged passport, or a passport in respect of which a false statement offence under section 57(2) has been committed` IS
    `s 57(3) the person possesses a forged passport` `I had the passport in my possession` `I had a lawful excuse` (`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` `the document is a passport as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Passport Order`) `the passport is forged` `an offence under subsection 57(2) has been committed in respect of the passport`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `Under section 57(3), what penalty does the section state for possessing a forged passport`; retitled: the penalty is for both objects of subsection 57(3); answer unchanged
@ref Criminal Code s 57(3)
