§ `Sedition and military forces: sections 59 to 62 (lines 1022-1057)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then trial.

@ref Criminal Code s 59(4), s 60
@export Under section 59(4) and section 60, do I have a seditious intention?
GIVEN `I taught or advocated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you teach or advocate something?
      `I published or circulated a writing that advocated it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you publish or circulate a writing that advocates something?
      `what was taught or advocated is the use of force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what was taught or advocated (by you, or in the writing) the use of force?
      `the use of force is without the authority of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the use of force be without the authority of law?
      `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force advocated as a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada?
      `the good-faith intention I held is` IS A `s 60 intention` @desc If you held one of these intentions in good faith, which is it? Choose the last choice if none.
      `I held that intention in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you hold that intention in good faith?
      `I would be treated as having a seditious intention by reason only of that intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be treated as having a seditious intention by reason only of that intention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 59(4) and section 60, do I have a seditious intention` IS
    `s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention` `I taught or advocated` `I published or circulated a writing that advocated it` `what was taught or advocated is the use of force` `the use of force is without the authority of law` `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada` `the good-faith intention I held is` `I held that intention in good faith` `I would be treated as having a seditious intention by reason only of that intention`

@ref Criminal Code s 59(1) to (4), s 60, s 61
@export Under section 61, have I committed a seditious offence?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 61 act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I taught or advocated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you teach or advocate something?
      `I published or circulated a writing that advocated it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you publish or circulate a writing that advocates something?
      `what was taught or advocated is the use of force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what was taught or advocated (by you, or in the writing) the use of force?
      `the use of force is without the authority of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the use of force be without the authority of law?
      `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the force advocated as a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada?
      `the good-faith intention I held is` IS A `s 60 intention` @desc If you held one of these intentions in good faith, which is it? Choose the last choice if none.
      `I held that intention in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you hold that intention in good faith?
      `I would be treated as having a seditious intention by reason only of that intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be treated as having a seditious intention by reason only of that intention?
      `what I published is a libel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you published a libel?
      `the number of persons party to the agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are party to the agreement? (Asked for a seditious conspiracy.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61, have I committed a seditious offence` IS
    `s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` `what I did` (`s 59(1) the words are seditious words` `the answer on seditious intention`) (`s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel` `what I published is a libel` `the answer on seditious intention`) (`s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` `the number of persons party to the agreement` `the answer on seditious intention`)
    WHERE
        `the answer on seditious intention` MEANS `s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention` `I taught or advocated` `I published or circulated a writing that advocated it` `what was taught or advocated is the use of force` `the use of force is without the authority of law` `the force is a means of accomplishing a governmental change within Canada` `the good-faith intention I held is` `I held that intention in good faith` `I would be treated as having a seditious intention by reason only of that intention`

@ref Criminal Code s 61
@export Under section 61, what penalty does the section state for a seditious offence?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 61, what penalty does the section state for a seditious offence` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 61 the class of the offence`) (`s 61 the punishment`)

@ref Criminal Code s 62(1), s 62(2), s 2 Canadian Forces
@export Under section 62(1), have I committed an offence in relation to a member of a military force?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 62(1) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I acted intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act intentionally?
      `the member belongs to the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the member belong to the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada?
      `the member belongs to the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the member belong to the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada?
      `those forces are lawfully present in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those forces lawfully present in Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 62(1), have I committed an offence in relation to a member of a military force` IS
    `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `what I did` `I acted intentionally` (`s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` (`s 2 Canadian Forces` `the member belongs to the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada`) `the member belongs to the naval, army or air forces of a state other than Canada` `those forces are lawfully present in Canada`)

@ref Criminal Code s 62(1)
@export Under section 62(1), what penalty does the section state for an offence in relation to a member of a military force?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 62(1), what penalty does the section state for an offence in relation to a member of a military force` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 62(1) the class of the offence`) (`s 62(1) the punishment` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

§ `Unlawful assemblies and riots: sections 63 to 69 (lines 1059-1099)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then trial. The persons in section 67 are officials: their duty is in layer 1, and what it means to the person is the thirty minutes of section 68(b).

@ref Criminal Code s 63(1) to (3)
@export Under section 63, were the persons assembled an unlawful assembly?
GIVEN `the number of persons assembled` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons were assembled?
      `they assembled with intent to carry out a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they assemble with intent to carry out a common purpose?
      `they assembled in such a manner, or so conducted themselves, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood to fear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they assemble in such a manner, or so conduct themselves when assembled, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood of the assembly to fear?
      `the fear was on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fear on reasonable grounds?
      `the fear was that they would disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fear that they would disturb the peace tumultuously?
      `the fear was that they would by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fear that they would, by that assembly, needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously?
      `they were lawfully assembled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they lawfully assembled to begin with?
      `they conducted themselves with a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they conduct themselves with a common purpose?
      `they were assembled to protect the dwelling-house of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they assembled to protect the dwelling-house of any one of them?
      `the place they protected is` IS A `s 2 dwelling-house kind` @desc What kind of place did they protect? Choose the description that fits.
      `the persons they protected it against were threatening to break and enter it to commit an indictable offence there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the persons they protected it against threatening to break and enter it for the purpose of committing an indictable offence there?
      `that is the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 63, were the persons assembled an unlawful assembly` IS
    `the persons are unlawfully assembled by section 63`
    WHERE
        `the persons are unlawfully assembled by section 63` MEANS `s 63 the persons are unlawfully assembled` `the number of persons assembled` `they assembled with intent to carry out a common purpose` `they assembled in such a manner, or so conducted themselves, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood to fear` `the fear was on reasonable grounds` `the fear was that they would disturb the peace tumultuously` `the fear was that they would by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously` `they were lawfully assembled` `they conducted themselves with a common purpose` `they were assembled to protect the dwelling-house of one of them` (`s 2 dwelling-house` `the place they protected is`) `the persons they protected it against were threatening to break and enter it to commit an indictable offence there` `that is the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled`

@ref Criminal Code s 64
@export Under section 64, was the assembly a riot?
GIVEN `the number of persons assembled` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons were assembled?
      `they assembled with intent to carry out a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they assemble with intent to carry out a common purpose?
      `they assembled in such a manner, or so conducted themselves, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood to fear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they assemble in such a manner, or so conduct themselves when assembled, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood of the assembly to fear?
      `the fear was on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fear on reasonable grounds?
      `the fear was that they would disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fear that they would disturb the peace tumultuously?
      `the fear was that they would by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fear that they would, by that assembly, needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously?
      `they were lawfully assembled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they lawfully assembled to begin with?
      `they conducted themselves with a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they conduct themselves with a common purpose?
      `they were assembled to protect the dwelling-house of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they assembled to protect the dwelling-house of any one of them?
      `the place they protected is` IS A `s 2 dwelling-house kind` @desc What kind of place did they protect? Choose the description that fits.
      `the persons they protected it against were threatening to break and enter it to commit an indictable offence there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the persons they protected it against threatening to break and enter it for the purpose of committing an indictable offence there?
      `that is the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled?
      `the assembly had begun to disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the assembly begun to disturb the peace tumultuously?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64, was the assembly a riot` IS
    `the assembly is a riot by section 64`
    WHERE
        `the persons are unlawfully assembled by section 63` MEANS `s 63 the persons are unlawfully assembled` `the number of persons assembled` `they assembled with intent to carry out a common purpose` `they assembled in such a manner, or so conducted themselves, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood to fear` `the fear was on reasonable grounds` `the fear was that they would disturb the peace tumultuously` `the fear was that they would by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously` `they were lawfully assembled` `they conducted themselves with a common purpose` `they were assembled to protect the dwelling-house of one of them` (`s 2 dwelling-house` `the place they protected is`) `the persons they protected it against were threatening to break and enter it to commit an indictable offence there` `that is the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled`
        `the assembly is a riot by section 64` MEANS `s 64 the unlawful assembly is a riot` `the persons are unlawfully assembled by section 63` `the assembly had begun to disturb the peace tumultuously`

@ref Criminal Code s 65(1), s 64
@export Under section 65(1), have I taken part in a riot?
GIVEN `the number of persons assembled` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons were assembled?
      `they assembled with intent to carry out a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they assemble with intent to carry out a common purpose?
