      `I took part in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take part in it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(1), have I taken part in a riot` IS
    `s 65(1) the person takes part in a riot` `I took part in it` `the assembly is a riot by section 64`
    WHERE
        `the persons are unlawfully assembled by section 63` MEANS `s 63 the persons are unlawfully assembled` `the number of persons assembled` `they assembled with intent to carry out a common purpose` `they assembled in such a manner, or so conducted themselves, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood to fear` `the fear was on reasonable grounds` `the fear was that they would disturb the peace tumultuously` `the fear was that they would by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously` `they were lawfully assembled` `they conducted themselves with a common purpose` `they were assembled to protect the dwelling-house of one of them` (`s 2 dwelling-house` `the place they protected is`) `the persons they protected it against were threatening to break and enter it to commit an indictable offence there` `that is the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled`
        `the assembly is a riot by section 64` MEANS `s 64 the unlawful assembly is a riot` `the persons are unlawfully assembled by section 63` `the assembly had begun to disturb the peace tumultuously`

@ref Criminal Code s 65(1)
@export Under section 65(1), what penalty does the section state for taking part in a riot?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 65(1), what penalty does the section state for taking part in a riot` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 65(1) the class of the offence of taking part in a riot`) (`s 65(1) the punishment for taking part in a riot` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

