@ref Criminal Code s 68, s 67
@export Under section 68, have I committed an offence related to the proclamation?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 68 act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I opposed, hindered or assaulted, wilfully and with force, a person making or about to make the proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you oppose, hinder or assault, wilfully and with force, a person who was making, or about to begin to make, the proclamation referred to in section 67?
      `the proclamation was not made as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the proclamation not made as a result?
      `the proclamation was made at the place where I was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the proclamation referred to in section 67 made at the place where you were?
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe the proclamation would have been made there if someone had not opposed, hindered or assaulted the person who would have made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable grounds to believe that the proclamation would have been made in that place if some person had not opposed, hindered or assaulted, wilfully and with force, a person who would have made it?
      `the minutes since the proclamation was made, or since I had those grounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes have passed since the proclamation was made (paragraph (b)), or since you came to have those reasonable grounds (paragraph (c)), up to the time you peaceably dispersed and left or, if you have not left, up to now?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 68, have I committed an offence related to the proclamation` IS
    `s 68 the person commits an offence related to the proclamation` `what I did` `I opposed, hindered or assaulted, wilfully and with force, a person making or about to make the proclamation` `the proclamation was not made as a result` `the proclamation was made at the place where I was` `I had reasonable grounds to believe the proclamation would have been made there if someone had not opposed, hindered or assaulted the person who would have made it` `the minutes since the proclamation was made, or since I had those grounds`

