DECIDE `Under section 70(3), what penalty does the section state for contravening an order made under section 70` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 70(3) the class of the offence`) (`s 70(3) the punishment` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

@ref Criminal Code s 72(1)
@export Under section 72(1), have I committed forcible entry?
GIVEN `I entered real property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter real property?
      `the property was in the actual and peaceable possession of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property in the actual and peaceable possession of another?
      `I entered in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(1), have I committed forcible entry` IS
    `s 72(1) the person commits forcible entry` `I entered real property` `the property was in the actual and peaceable possession of another` `I entered in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one`

@ref Criminal Code s 72(1.1)
@export Under section 72(1.1), does it matter whether I was entitled to enter the property or meant to take possession?
GIVEN `the question arises for the purposes of subsection 72(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the question arise for the purposes of subsection 72(1) (forcible entry)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(1.1), does it matter whether I was entitled to enter the property or meant to take possession` IS
    `s 72(1.1) the person's entitlement to enter the real property, or intention of taking possession of it, is material` `the question arises for the purposes of subsection 72(1)`

@ref Criminal Code s 72(2)
@export Under section 72(2), have I committed forcible detainer?
GIVEN `I was in actual possession of real property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in actual possession of real property?
      `I was without colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you without colour of right?
      `I detained it in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you detain it in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace?
      `I detained it against a person entitled by law to possession of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you detain it against a person who is entitled by law to possession of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(2), have I committed forcible detainer` IS
    `s 72(2) the person commits forcible detainer` `I was in actual possession of real property` `I was without colour of right` `I detained it in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one` `I detained it against a person entitled by law to possession of it`

@ref Criminal Code s 72, s 73
@export Under section 73, have I committed forcible entry or forcible detainer?
GIVEN `I entered real property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter real property?
      `the property was in the actual and peaceable possession of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property in the actual and peaceable possession of another?
      `I entered in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace?
      `I was in actual possession of real property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in actual possession of real property?
      `I was without colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you without colour of right?
      `I detained it in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you detain it in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace?
      `I detained it against a person entitled by law to possession of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you detain it against a person who is entitled by law to possession of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73, have I committed forcible entry or forcible detainer` IS
    `s 73 the person commits forcible entry or forcible detainer` (`s 72(1) the person commits forcible entry` `I entered real property` `the property was in the actual and peaceable possession of another` `I entered in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one`) (`s 72(2) the person commits forcible detainer` `I was in actual possession of real property` `I was without colour of right` `I detained it in a manner likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of one` `I detained it against a person entitled by law to possession of it`)

@ref Criminal Code s 73
@export Under section 73, what penalty does the section state for forcible entry or forcible detainer?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 73, what penalty does the section state for forcible entry or forcible detainer` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 73 the class of the offence`) (`s 73 the punishment` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

§ `Piracy and offences against air or maritime safety: sections 74 to 78.1 (lines 1133-1187)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then trial.

@ref Criminal Code s 74(1)
@export Under section 74(1), have I committed piracy?
GIVEN `what I did is piracy by the law of nations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you did piracy by the law of nations? (Answer yes only if you know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1), have I committed piracy` IS
    `s 74(1) the person commits piracy` (`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` `what I did is piracy by the law of nations`)

@ref Criminal Code s 74(2)
@export Under section 74(2), what penalty does the section state for piracy?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 74(2), what penalty does the section state for piracy` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 74(2) the class of the offence of piracy`) (`s 74(2) the punishment for piracy`)

@ref Criminal Code s 75
@export Under section 75, have I committed a piratical act?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 75 act` @desc Which of these did you do (in or out of Canada)? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `the ship is a Canadian ship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship a Canadian ship?
      `I acted without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without lawful authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 75, have I committed a piratical act` IS
    `s 75 the person commits a piratical act` `what I did` `the ship is a Canadian ship` `I acted without lawful authority`

@ref Criminal Code s 75
@export Under section 75, what penalty does the section state for a piratical act?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 75, what penalty does the section state for a piratical act` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 75 the class of the offence`) (`s 75 the punishment`)

@ref Criminal Code s 76
@export Under section 76, have I committed hijacking?
GIVEN `I acted unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act unlawfully?
      `I seized or exercised control of an aircraft by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you seize or exercise control of an aircraft by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation?
      `my intent was` IS A `s 76 intent` @desc What was your intent? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76, have I committed hijacking` IS
    `s 76 the person commits hijacking` `I acted unlawfully` `I seized or exercised control of an aircraft by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation` `my intent was`

@ref Criminal Code s 76
@export Under section 76, what penalty does the section state for hijacking?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 76, what penalty does the section state for hijacking` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 76 the class of the offence`) (`s 76 the punishment`)

@ref Criminal Code s 77
@export Under section 77, have I endangered the safety of an aircraft or airport?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 77 act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `the aircraft was in flight` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the aircraft in flight?
      `the aircraft was in service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the aircraft in service?
      `the airport serves international civil aviation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the airport one serving international civil aviation?
      `I used a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use a weapon?
      `I used a weapon, substance or device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use a weapon, substance or device?
      `my act caused or was likely to cause serious injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your act cause, or was it likely to cause, serious injury or death?
      `my act endangered, or was likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your act endanger, or was it likely to endanger, the safety named in the paragraph (of the aircraft, of the aircraft in flight, or at the airport)?
      `I knew the information to be false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know the information to be false? (Asked for communicating information.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77, have I endangered the safety of an aircraft or airport` IS
    `s 77 the person endangers the safety of an aircraft or airport` `what I did` `the aircraft was in flight` `the aircraft was in service` `the airport serves international civil aviation` `I used a weapon` `I used a weapon, substance or device` `my act caused or was likely to cause serious injury or death` `my act endangered, or was likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names` `I knew the information to be false`

@ref Criminal Code s 77
@export Under section 77, what penalty does the section state for endangering the safety of an aircraft or airport?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 77, what penalty does the section state for endangering the safety of an aircraft or airport` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 77 the class of the offence`) (`s 77 the punishment`)

@ref Criminal Code s 78(1), s 78(2), s 2 peace officer, offensive weapon, explosive substance
@export Under section 78(1), have I taken an offensive weapon or an explosive substance on board a civil aircraft?
GIVEN `my capacity is` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc In what capacity do you act? Choose the description that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I was engaged in the execution of my duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a peace officer engaged in the execution of your duty?
      `the craft is an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the craft an aircraft?
      `it was operated by the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it operated by the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada?
      `it was operated by a police force in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it operated by a police force in Canada?
      `it was operated by persons enforcing the Customs Act or the Excise Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it operated by persons engaged in the administration or enforcement of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001?
      `I took the thing on board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take the thing on board the aircraft?
      `the thing is an offensive weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an offensive weapon as section 2 defines it? (Answer yes only if you know.)
      `the thing is` IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind` @desc If it is an explosive substance, which description fits? Choose the last choice if none does.
      `the consent position was` IS A `s 78(1) consent position` @desc Which of these describes the consent of the owner or operator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(1), have I taken an offensive weapon or an explosive substance on board a civil aircraft` IS
    `s 78(1) the person takes an offensive weapon or an explosive substance on board a civil aircraft` (`s 2 peace officer` `my capacity is`) `I was engaged in the execution of my duty` (`s 78(2) the aircraft is a civil aircraft` `the craft is an aircraft` (`s 2 Canadian Forces` `it was operated by the armed forces of Her Majesty raised by Canada`) `it was operated by a police force in Canada` `it was operated by persons enforcing the Customs Act or the Excise Acts`) `I took the thing on board` (`s 2 offensive weapon` (`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` `the thing is an offensive weapon`)) (`s 2 explosive substance` `the thing is`) `the consent position was`

@ref Criminal Code s 78(1)
@export Under section 78(1), what penalty does the section state for taking an offensive weapon or an explosive substance on board a civil aircraft?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 78(1), what penalty does the section state for taking an offensive weapon or an explosive substance on board a civil aircraft` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 78(1) the class of the offence`) (`s 78(1) the punishment`)

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(1), s 78.1(5)
@export Under section 78.1(1), have I seized control of a ship or fixed platform?
GIVEN `I seized or exercised control by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you seize or exercise control by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation?
      `it is a vessel of any description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a vessel of any description?
      `it is permanently attached to the seabed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it permanently attached to the seabed?
      `it is a warship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a warship?
      `it is used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it being used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes?
      `it has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been withdrawn from navigation or is it laid up?
      `it is an artificial island or a marine installation or structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an artificial island or a marine installation or structure?
      `it is for exploration or exploitation of resources or other economic purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purpose of exploration or exploitation of resources or for other economic purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78.1(1), have I seized control of a ship or fixed platform` IS
    `s 78.1(1) the person seizes control of a ship or fixed platform` `I seized or exercised control by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation` `the thing is a ship by section 78.1(5)` `the thing is a fixed platform by section 78.1(5)`
    WHERE
        `the thing is a ship by section 78.1(5)` MEANS `s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship` `it is a vessel of any description` `it is permanently attached to the seabed` `it is a warship` `it is used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes` `it has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up`
        `the thing is a fixed platform by section 78.1(5)` MEANS `s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform` `it is an artificial island or a marine installation or structure` `it is permanently attached to the seabed` `it is for exploration or exploitation of resources or other economic purposes`

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(2), s 78.1(5)
@export Under section 78.1(2), have I endangered the safety of a ship or fixed platform?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 78.1(2) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `it is a vessel of any description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a vessel of any description?
      `it is permanently attached to the seabed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it permanently attached to the seabed?
      `it is a warship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a warship?
      `it is used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it being used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes?
      `it has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been withdrawn from navigation or is it laid up?
      `it is an artificial island or a marine installation or structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an artificial island or a marine installation or structure?
      `it is for exploration or exploitation of resources or other economic purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purpose of exploration or exploitation of resources or for other economic purposes?
      `my act was likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your act likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78.1(2), have I endangered the safety of a ship or fixed platform` IS
    `s 78.1(2) the person endangers the safety of a ship or fixed platform` `what I did` `the thing is a ship by section 78.1(5)` `the thing is a fixed platform by section 78.1(5)` `my act was likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform`
    WHERE
        `the thing is a ship by section 78.1(5)` MEANS `s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship` `it is a vessel of any description` `it is permanently attached to the seabed` `it is a warship` `it is used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes` `it has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up`
        `the thing is a fixed platform by section 78.1(5)` MEANS `s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform` `it is an artificial island or a marine installation or structure` `it is permanently attached to the seabed` `it is for exploration or exploitation of resources or other economic purposes`

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(3)
@export Under section 78.1(3), have I communicated false information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship?
GIVEN `I communicated information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you communicate information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship?
      `I knew the information to be false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know the information to be false?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78.1(3), have I communicated false information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship` IS
    `s 78.1(3) the person communicates false information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship` `I communicated information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship` `I knew the information to be false`

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(4)
@export Under section 78.1(4), have I threatened to commit an offence under section 78.1(2)(a), (b) or (c)?
GIVEN `I threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you threaten to commit the offence?
      `the offence threatened is` IS A `s 78.1(4) threatened offence` @desc Which offence did you threaten to commit? Choose the one that fits.
      `I threatened it in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing an act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you threaten it in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing any act?
      `the threat was likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the threat likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78.1(4), have I threatened to commit an offence under section 78.1(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS
    `s 78.1(4) the person threatens to commit an offence under paragraph 78.1(2)(a), (b) or (c)` `I threatened` `the offence threatened is` `I threatened it in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing an act` `the threat was likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform`

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(1) to (4)
@export Under section 78.1, what penalty does the section state for the offences in subsections (1) to (4)?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 78.1, what penalty does the section state for the offences in subsections (1) to (4)` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 78.1 the class of the offences in subsections (1) to (4)`) (`s 78.1 the punishment for the offences in subsections (1) to (4)`)

§ `Dangerous materials and devices: explosives, sections 79 to 82.1 (lines 1189-1218)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then trial and sentence (s 82.1).

@ref Criminal Code s 79, s 2 explosive substance
@export Under section 79, am I under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by an explosive substance?
GIVEN `I have the thing in my possession or under my care or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the thing in your possession or under your care or control?
      `the thing is` IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind` @desc Which description fits the thing? Choose the last choice if none does.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79, am I under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by an explosive substance` IS
    `s 79 the person is under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by the explosive substance` `I have the thing in my possession or under my care or control` (`s 2 explosive substance` `the thing is`)

@ref Criminal Code s 79, s 80
@export Under section 80, have I committed the offence of breach of the duty of care with an explosive substance?
GIVEN `I have the thing in my possession or under my care or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the thing in your possession or under your care or control?
      `the thing is` IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind` @desc Which description fits the thing? Choose the last choice if none does.
      `I failed to perform that duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to perform that duty?
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 80, have I committed the offence of breach of the duty of care with an explosive substance` IS
    `s 80 the person commits the offence of breach of duty` (`s 79 the person is under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by the explosive substance` `I have the thing in my possession or under my care or control` (`s 2 explosive substance` `the thing is`)) `I failed to perform that duty` `I had a lawful excuse`

@ref Criminal Code s 80
@export Under section 80, what class of offence is breach of the duty of care with an explosive substance?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 80, what class of offence is breach of the duty of care with an explosive substance` IS
    `s 80 the class of the offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 80
@export Under section 80, what is the most imprisonment I face for breach of the duty of care, given what happened as a result?
GIVEN `what happened as a result` IS A `s 80 result` @desc What happened as a result of your failure? Choose the one that fits.
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
DECIDE `Under section 80, what is the most imprisonment I face for breach of the duty of care, given what happened as a result` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, the most imprisonment the first limb states, if the section states a penalty` (`s 80 the punishment` `what happened as a result`)

@ref Criminal Code s 81(1), s 2 explosive substance
@export Under section 81(1), have I committed an offence by using explosives?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 81(1) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `I had the intent the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have the intent the paragraph names (to cause an explosion, to do bodily harm, to destroy or damage property, to endanger life or cause serious damage, or to enable another person to do so)?
      `the explosion was likely to cause serious bodily harm or death or serious damage to property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the explosion likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or serious damage to property? (Asked for paragraph (a).)
      `the thing is` IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind` @desc Which description fits the thing? Choose the last choice if none does.
      `the thing is a corrosive fluid or another dangerous substance or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a corrosive fluid, or any other dangerous substance or thing? (Asked for paragraphs (b)(ii) and (iii).)
      `I acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without lawful excuse? (Asked for paragraph (c).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 81(1), have I committed an offence by using explosives` IS
    `s 81(1) the person commits an offence by using explosives` `what I did` `I had the intent the paragraph names` `the explosion was likely to cause serious bodily harm or death or serious damage to property` (`s 2 explosive substance` `the thing is`) `the thing is a corrosive fluid or another dangerous substance or thing` `I acted without lawful excuse`

@ref Criminal Code s 81(2)
@export Under section 81(2), what is the most imprisonment I face for using explosives?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 81(1) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
DECIDE `Under section 81(2), what is the most imprisonment I face for using explosives` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, the most imprisonment the first limb states, if the section states a penalty` (`s 81(2) the punishment` `what I did`)

@ref Criminal Code s 81(2)
@export Under section 81(2), what class of offence is using explosives?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 81(2), what class of offence is using explosives` IS
    `s 81(2) the class of the offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 82(1), s 2 explosive substance
@export Under section 82(1), have I possessed an explosive substance without lawful excuse?
GIVEN `I made the thing, or had it in my possession or under my care or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the thing, or have it in your possession or under your care or control?
      `the thing is` IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind` @desc Which description fits the thing? Choose the last choice if none does.
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 82(1), have I possessed an explosive substance without lawful excuse` IS
    `s 82(1) the person possesses an explosive substance without lawful excuse` `I made the thing, or had it in my possession or under my care or control` (`s 2 explosive substance` `the thing is`) `I had a lawful excuse`

@ref Criminal Code s 82(1)
@export Under section 82(1), what penalty does the section state for possessing an explosive substance?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 82(1), what penalty does the section state for possessing an explosive substance` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 82(1) the class of the offence`) (`s 82(1) the punishment` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

@ref Criminal Code s 82(2), s 2 explosive substance, s 2 criminal organization
@export Under section 82(2), have I possessed an explosive substance for or with a criminal organization?
GIVEN `I made the thing, or had it in my possession or under my care or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the thing, or have it in your possession or under your care or control?
      `the thing is` IS A `s 2 explosive substance kind` @desc Which description fits the thing? Choose the last choice if none does.
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
      `it was for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group?
      `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the group a criminal organization as section 467.1(1) defines it? (Answer yes only if you know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 82(2), have I possessed an explosive substance for or with a criminal organization` IS
    `s 82(2) the person possesses an explosive substance for or with a criminal organization` `I made the thing, or had it in my possession or under my care or control` (`s 2 explosive substance` `the thing is`) `I had a lawful excuse` `it was for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` (`s 2 criminal organization` (`Under sections 46 to 83, a borrowed answer the person is sure of` `the group is a criminal organization`))

@ref Criminal Code s 82(2)
@export Under section 82(2), what penalty does the section state for possessing an explosive substance for or with a criminal organization?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 82(2), what penalty does the section state for possessing an explosive substance for or with a criminal organization` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 82(2) the class of the offence`) (`s 82(2) the punishment`)

@ref Criminal Code s 82.1
@export Under section 82.1, must a sentence for possessing an explosive for a criminal organization be served consecutively to my other punishment or sentence?
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 82(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence imposed for an offence under subsection 82(2)?
      `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other punishment imposed for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events?
      `I am subject to the other sentence at the time this sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to another sentence at the time this sentence is imposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 82.1, must a sentence for possessing an explosive for a criminal organization be served consecutively to my other punishment or sentence` IS
    `s 82.1 the sentence must be served consecutively to the other punishment or sentence` `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 82(2)` `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` `I am subject to the other sentence at the time this sentence is imposed`

§ `Nuclear material, radioactive material and devices: sections 82.2 to 82.7 (lines 1219-1233)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then trial.

@ref Criminal Code s 82.2, s 2 radioactive material
