§ `Prize fights: section 83 (lines 1235-1247)`
-- Stage: investigation and arrest, then trial.

@ref Criminal Code s 83(1), s 83(2)
@export Under section 83, have I taken part in a prize fight?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 83(1) act` @desc Which of these did you do? Choose the one that fits, or the last choice if none does.
      `it was an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet?
      `it was between two persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it between two persons?
      `the two persons had met for that purpose by previous arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the two persons met for that purpose by previous arrangement made by or for them?
      `it was a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport held in a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport with fists, hands or feet held in a province?
      `the sport is on the programme of the IOC or the IPC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sport on the programme of the International Olympic Committee or the International Paralympic Committee?
      `the sport has been designated by the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sport been designated by the province's lieutenant governor in council or by another person or body they specified?
      `the province requires permission for the contest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the province's lieutenant governor in council, or the person or body they specified, require permission?
      `the contest was held with their permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contest held with their permission?
      `it was a boxing contest or mixed martial arts contest held in a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a boxing contest or mixed martial arts contest held in a province?
      `it was held with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it held with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board, commission or similar body established by or under the authority of the province's legislature for the control of sport?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83, have I taken part in a prize fight` IS
    `s 83(1) the person takes part in a prize fight` `what I did` (`s 83(2) the encounter is a prize fight` `it was an encounter or fight with fists, hands or feet` `it was between two persons` `the two persons had met for that purpose by previous arrangement` `it was a contest between amateur athletes in a combative sport held in a province` `the sport is on the programme of the IOC or the IPC` `the sport has been designated by the province` `the province requires permission for the contest` `the contest was held with their permission` `it was a boxing contest or mixed martial arts contest held in a province` `it was held with the permission or under the authority of an athletic board`)

@ref Criminal Code s 83(1)
@export Under section 83(1), what penalty does the section state for engaging in a prize fight?
GIVETH A `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty`
DECIDE `Under section 83(1), what penalty does the section state for engaging in a prize fight` IS
    `Under sections 46 to 83, what the section states about the penalty of the offence` (`s 83(1) the class of the offence`) (`s 83(1) the punishment` `Under sections 46 to 83, a placeholder for the penalty of section 787(1)`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc3 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc3-seat.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism (ss 83.01 to 83.33): THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence, what its gravity and penalty
-- are, what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the
-- model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person asks about Part II.1: is what I did an offence, what is the most I can be sentenced to,
-- may I be arrested and held, what must I be given and by when, what happens to my property, and what can I do about it. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds
-- the records the layer-1 rules expect from plain inputs and calls them. Where a rule turns on a term another section defines ("terrorist activity", "terrorist group", "terrorism offence", "dwelling-house"),
-- the person answers a three-way choice (yes, no, I do not know) and "I do not know" reaches the rule as NOTHING, never as FALSE.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list), each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. Judgments the Code hands to a judge or an officer
-- ("reasonable grounds", "satisfied") are asked as the person's best plain answer. A record field no rule reads gets a fixed placeholder, with a comment.
-- Names: every question begins "Under section N,"; every helper and type begins with the section label of the rule it serves.
--
-- GROUPS (the website's "Has this happened to you?" heads): § groups follow the Code's own order. The groups that arise only in a situation the person may not be in are marked in the heading:
-- the authorization regime (ss 83.031 to 83.0392; if you have applied for or hold an authorization), the list of entities (ss 83.05 to 83.07; if your group is on, or may be put on, the list), seizure and
-- forfeiture (ss 83.13 to 83.17; if your property has been seized, restrained or forfeited), and recognizance with conditions (s 83.3 and following; if a peace officer has arrested you or laid an information).
--
-- READING A RESULT: JUST TRUE yes, JUST FALSE no (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING not covered (the text is silent, the answer turns on a judgment or term the person did not settle, or the case lies outside
-- what the section says). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc3)".
-- Dates are `Date day month year`; a period in hours is a number of hours; money is dollars.

DECLARE `s 83.01(1) seat answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.01(1) seat yes`
    `s 83.01(1) seat no`
    `s 83.01(1) seat I do not know`

GIVEN answer IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) seat yes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) seat no` THEN JUST FALSE   -- SEAT-ANSWER: not an answer of the Act: the person's own answer "no" to a question about a defined term, handed to the layer-1 rule
    WHEN `s 83.01(1) seat I do not know` THEN NOTHING   -- SEAT-ANSWER: "I do not know": the layer-1 rule receives NOTHING, never FALSE

GIVEN length IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 83.02 seat the length of time in words` MEANS
    CONCAT
        (IF length's years GREATER THAN 0 THEN CONCAT (TOSTRING (length's years)), (IF length's years EQUALS 1 THEN " year" ELSE " years") ELSE ""),
        (IF length's months GREATER THAN 0 THEN CONCAT " ", (TOSTRING (length's months)), (IF length's months EQUALS 1 THEN " month" ELSE " months") ELSE ""),
        (IF length's days GREATER THAN 0 THEN CONCAT " ", (TOSTRING (length's days)), (IF length's days EQUALS 1 THEN " day" ELSE " days") ELSE ""),
        (IF length's `less a day` THEN " less a day" ELSE "")

GIVEN punishment IS A Punishment
GIVETH A STRING
`s 83.02 seat the punishment in words` MEANS
    CONCAT
        (CONSIDER punishment's `mode`
         WHEN `by indictment` THEN "On indictment: "
         WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN "On summary conviction: "),
        (CONSIDER punishment's `maximum imprisonment`
         WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN "no maximum term of imprisonment is stated in the section"
         WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN "imprisonment for life"
         WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` OF term THEN CONCAT "imprisonment for a term of not more than ", (`s 83.02 seat the length of time in words` term)),
        (CONSIDER punishment's `minimum imprisonment`
         WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN ""
         WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN "; a minimum of imprisonment for life"
         WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` OF minimum THEN CONCAT "; a minimum of imprisonment for a term of ", (`s 83.02 seat the length of time in words` minimum)),
        (CONSIDER punishment's `maximum fine`
         WHEN `no fine is stated` THEN ""
         WHEN `a fine in the discretion of the court` THEN "; a fine in the discretion of the court"
         WHEN `a fine of` OF amount THEN CONCAT "; a fine of not more than $", (TOSTRING amount))

GIVEN punishments IS A LIST OF Punishment
GIVETH A STRING
`s 83.02 seat the punishments in words` MEANS
    CONSIDER punishments
    WHEN EMPTY THEN ""
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONCAT
            (`s 83.02 seat the punishment in words` first),
            (CONSIDER rest
             WHEN EMPTY THEN ""
             WHEN second FOLLOWED BY more THEN CONCAT " ; ", (`s 83.02 seat the punishments in words` rest))

-- The summary-conviction limb of 83.231(2) and (3) states no penalty: it falls under the general penalty of section 787(1), which is in another part of the Code and which the person states
-- (years, months, days, whether "less a day", and the fine). Nothing here supplies a figure from memory.
GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER
      `the months` IS A NUMBER
      `the days` IS A NUMBER
      `the term is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 83.231 seat the general summary penalty from the figures the person states` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `the imprisonment`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `the fine`, `no fine is stated`
    WHERE
        `the imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `the years` EQUALS 0 AND `the months` EQUALS 0 AND `the days` EQUALS 0 AND NOT `the term is less a day`
            THEN `no imprisonment is stated`
            ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` `the length of time`
        `the length of time` MEANS `Length of time` OF `the years`, `the months`, `the days`, `the term is less a day`
        `the fine` MEANS
            IF `the fine in dollars` EQUALS 0 THEN `no fine is stated` ELSE `a fine of` `the fine in dollars`

§ `Part II.1 Terrorism -- the meaning of the words (s 83.01)`

§§ `Terrorist activity and terrorist group`

@export Under section 83.01(1), is the act or omission I am asking about a terrorist activity?
GIVEN `the form my conduct takes` IS A `s 83.01(1) form of the conduct` @desc Is it the act or omission itself, or a conspiracy, an attempt, a threat, being an accessory after the fact, or counselling in relation to it?
      `the listed offence it would be if committed in Canada` IS A `s 83.01(1)(a) listed offence` @desc If it would be one of the offences the definition lists in paragraph (a) (hijacking, attacks on civil aviation, internationally protected persons, hostage-taking, nuclear material, airport violence, maritime navigation, fixed platforms, terrorist bombing, financing of terrorism), which one? Otherwise choose the "none of the offences listed" entry.
      `it was committed in whole or in part for a political, religious or ideological purpose, objective or cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done at least partly for a political, religious or ideological purpose, objective or cause?
      `it was committed in whole or in part with the intention of intimidating the public, or a segment of the public, with regard to its security, or compelling a person, a government or an organization to do or refrain from doing any act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done at least partly intending to intimidate the public (or a part of it) about its security, including economic security, or to compel a person, a government or a domestic or international organization to do or refrain from doing something?
      `it intentionally caused death or serious bodily harm to a person by the use of violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it intentionally cause death or serious bodily harm to a person by the use of violence?
      `it intentionally endangered a person’s life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it intentionally endanger a person's life?
      `it intentionally caused a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it intentionally cause a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any part of the public?
      `it intentionally caused substantial property damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it intentionally cause substantial damage to public or private property?
      `that damage was likely to result in death, serious bodily harm, endangering a life or a serious risk to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that property damage likely to result in death, serious bodily harm, endangering a life, or a serious risk to the health or safety of the public?
      `it intentionally caused serious interference with or serious disruption of an essential service, facility or system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it intentionally cause serious interference with or disruption of an essential service, facility or system, public or private?
      `the interference or disruption was a result of advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that interference or disruption result from advocacy, protest, dissent or a stoppage of work?
      `that advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work was not intended to result in death, serious bodily harm, endangering a life or a serious risk to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work NOT intended to cause death, serious bodily harm, endangering a life or a serious risk to health or safety?
      `it was committed during an armed conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it committed during an armed conflict?
      `at the time and place it was in accordance with international law applicable to the conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time and place, was it in accordance with customary or conventional international law applicable to the conflict?
      `it was an activity of the military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an activity of the military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties?
      `that activity was governed by other rules of international law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that activity governed by other rules of international law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.01(1), is the act or omission I am asking about a terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.01(1) the act or omission is a terrorist activity` `the form my conduct takes` `the listed offence it would be if committed in Canada` `my paragraph (b) facts` `my exclusion facts`
    WHERE
        `my paragraph (b) facts` MEANS `s 83.01(1)(b) facts` WITH
            `committed in whole or in part for a political, religious or ideological purpose, objective or cause` IS `it was committed in whole or in part for a political, religious or ideological purpose, objective or cause`
            `committed in whole or in part with the intention of intimidating the public, or a segment of the public, with regard to its security, including its economic security, or compelling a person, a government or a domestic or an international organization to do or to refrain from doing any act` IS `it was committed in whole or in part with the intention of intimidating the public, or a segment of the public, with regard to its security, or compelling a person, a government or an organization to do or refrain from doing any act`
            `intentionally causes death or serious bodily harm to a person by the use of violence` IS `it intentionally caused death or serious bodily harm to a person by the use of violence`
            `intentionally endangers a person’s life` IS `it intentionally endangered a person’s life`
            `intentionally causes a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public` IS `it intentionally caused a serious risk to the health or safety of the public or any segment of the public`
            `intentionally causes substantial property damage, whether to public or private property` IS `it intentionally caused substantial property damage`
            `causing that damage is likely to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C)` IS `that damage was likely to result in death, serious bodily harm, endangering a life or a serious risk to health or safety`
            `intentionally causes serious interference with or serious disruption of an essential service, facility or system, whether public or private` IS `it intentionally caused serious interference with or serious disruption of an essential service, facility or system`
            `the interference or disruption results from advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work` IS `the interference or disruption was a result of advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work`
            `that advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work is not intended to result in the conduct or harm referred to in any of clauses (A) to (C)` IS `that advocacy, protest, dissent or stoppage of work was not intended to result in death, serious bodily harm, endangering a life or a serious risk to health or safety`
        `my exclusion facts` MEANS `s 83.01(1) exclusion facts` WITH
            `the act or omission is committed during an armed conflict` IS `it was committed during an armed conflict`
            `at the time and in the place of its commission it is in accordance with customary international law or conventional international law applicable to the conflict` IS `at the time and place it was in accordance with international law applicable to the conflict`
            `it is an activity undertaken by military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties` IS `it was an activity of the military forces of a state in the exercise of their official duties`
            `that activity is governed by other rules of international law` IS `that activity was governed by other rules of international law`

@export Under section 83.01(1), is the group I am asking about a terrorist group?
GIVEN `what kind of thing the group is` IS A `s 83.01(1) entity kind` @desc What is it: a person, a group, a trust, a partnership, a fund, an unincorporated association, an organization, or none of those?
      `one of its purposes or activities is facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity one of its purposes or activities?
      `it is on the list of entities established under section 83.05` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it on the list of entities that the Governor in Council has established under section 83.05?
      `it is an association of such entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an association of entities of the kind just described (entities with such a purpose, or listed entities)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.01(1), is the group I am asking about a terrorist group` IS
    `s 83.01(1) the group is a terrorist group` `what kind of thing the group is` `one of its purposes or activities is facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity` `it is on the list of entities established under section 83.05` `it is an association of such entities`

@export Under section 83.01(1.1), does the expression of my political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion come within paragraph (b) of the definition of terrorist activity?
GIVEN `all I did was express a political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was all I did to express a political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion?
      `it was an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Was it also an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b) (the purpose, the intention and one of the kinds of harm)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.01(1.1), does the expression of my political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion come within paragraph (b) of the definition of terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.01(1.1) the expression of thought, belief or opinion comes within paragraph (b)` `all I did was express a political, religious or ideological thought, belief or opinion` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `it was an act or omission that satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)`)

@export Under section 83.01(1.2), does a suicide bombing come within paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of terrorist activity?
GIVEN `the act was a suicide bombing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act a suicide bombing?
      `it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (a)` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Does it satisfy the criteria of paragraph (a) (one of the listed convention offences)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Does it satisfy the criteria of paragraph (b) (the purpose, the intention and one of the kinds of harm)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.01(1.2), does a suicide bombing come within paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.01(1.2) a suicide bombing comes within paragraph (a) or (b)` `the act was a suicide bombing` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (a)`) (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `it satisfies the criteria of paragraph (b)`)

§ `Collecting, providing and making available property (ss 83.02 and 83.03)`

§§ `Is what I did an offence?`

@export Under section 83.02, is what I did the offence of providing or collecting property to carry out terrorist offences?
GIVEN `I provided or collected property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide or collect property, directly or indirectly?
      `I did it wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it wilfully?
      `I had lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful justification or excuse?
      `I intended that the property be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that the property be used, in whole or in part, to carry out the act below?
      `I knew that the property would be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the property would be used, in whole or in part, to carry out the act below?
      `the offence the property would be used to carry out` IS A `s 83.01(1)(a) listed offence` @desc If the use was to carry out one of the offences listed in paragraph (a) of the definition of terrorist activity, which one? Otherwise choose the "none of the offences listed" entry.
      `it was to carry out another act intended to cause death or serious bodily harm to a civilian or to a person not taking an active part in the hostilities in a situation of armed conflict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it to carry out another act or omission intended to cause death or serious bodily harm to a civilian or to anyone not taking an active part in the hostilities in an armed conflict?
      `the purpose of that act, by its nature or context, was to intimidate the public or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose of that act, by its nature or context, to intimidate the public or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.02, is what I did the offence of providing or collecting property to carry out terrorist offences` IS
    `s 83.02 the person is guilty of the offence` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 83.02 facts` WITH
            `provides or collects property` IS `I provided or collected property`
            `does so wilfully` IS `I did it wilfully`
            `has lawful justification or excuse` IS `I had lawful justification or excuse`
            `intends that the property be used` IS `I intended that the property be used`
            `knows that the property will be used` IS `I knew that the property would be used`
            `the offence the use would carry out, if any` IS `the offence the property would be used to carry out`
            `the other act or omission the use would carry out` IS `my other-act facts`
        `my other-act facts` MEANS `s 83.02(b) facts` WITH
            `the act or omission is intended to cause death or serious bodily harm to a civilian or to any other person not taking an active part in the hostilities in a situation of armed conflict` IS `it was to carry out another act intended to cause death or serious bodily harm to a civilian or to a person not taking an active part in the hostilities in a situation of armed conflict`
            `the purpose of that act or omission, by its nature or context, is to intimidate the public, or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act` IS `the purpose of that act, by its nature or context, was to intimidate the public or to compel a government or an international organization to do or refrain from doing any act`

@export Under section 83.03(1), is what I did the offence of providing or making available property or services for terrorist purposes?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 83.03 act` @desc What did you do: collect property, provide property or financial or related services, invite a person to provide them, make them available, or none of those?
      `I did it wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it wilfully?
      `I had lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful justification or excuse?
      `I intended that they be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that the property or services be used, in whole or in part, for the purpose below?
      `I knew that they would be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that they would be used, in whole or in part, for the purpose below?
      `the purpose was facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose to facilitate or carry out a terrorist activity?
      `the purpose was benefiting a person facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the purpose to benefit a person who is facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity?
      `my sole purpose was humanitarian assistance activities under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your sole purpose to carry out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law?
      `I used reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.03(1), is what I did the offence of providing or making available property or services for terrorist purposes` IS
    `s 83.03(1) the person is guilty of the offence` `my facts` `my humanitarian answer`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 83.03(1) facts` WITH
            `what the person does` IS `what I did`
            `does so wilfully` IS `I did it wilfully`
            `has lawful justification or excuse` IS `I had lawful justification or excuse`
            `intends that they be used` IS `I intended that they be used`
            `knows that they will be used` IS `I knew that they would be used`
            `the purpose is facilitating or carrying out any terrorist activity` IS `the purpose was facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity`
            `the purpose is benefiting any person who is facilitating or carrying out such an activity` IS `the purpose was benefiting a person facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity`
        `my humanitarian answer` MEANS `s 83.03(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person carrying out humanitarian assistance activities` `my humanitarian facts`
        `my humanitarian facts` MEANS `s 83.03(4) facts` WITH
            `carries out the acts for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law` IS `my sole purpose was humanitarian assistance activities under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law`
            `uses reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups` IS `I used reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups`

@export Under section 83.03(2), is what I did the offence of providing or making available property or services for use by a terrorist group?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 83.03 act` @desc What did you do: collect property, provide property or financial or related services, invite a person to provide them, make them available, or none of those?
      `I did it wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it wilfully?
      `I had lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful justification or excuse?
      `I knew that they would be used by or would benefit the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that, in whole or in part, they would be used by or would benefit the group?
      `the group is a terrorist group` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is the group a terrorist group within section 83.01(1)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `I acted under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032?
      `my sole purpose was humanitarian assistance activities under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your sole purpose to carry out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law?
      `I used reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.03(2), is what I did the offence of providing or making available property or services for use by a terrorist group` IS
    `s 83.03(2) the person is guilty of the offence` `my facts` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the group is a terrorist group`) `my authorization answer` `my humanitarian answer`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 83.03(2) facts` WITH
            `what the person does` IS `what I did`
            `does so wilfully` IS `I did it wilfully`
            `has lawful justification or excuse` IS `I had lawful justification or excuse`
            `knows that, in whole or part, they will be used by or will benefit the group` IS `I knew that they would be used by or would benefit the group`
        `my authorization answer` MEANS `s 83.03(3) subsection (2) does not apply to a person acting under and in accordance with an authorization` `I acted under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032`
        `my humanitarian answer` MEANS `s 83.03(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person carrying out humanitarian assistance activities` `my humanitarian facts`
        `my humanitarian facts` MEANS `s 83.03(4) facts` WITH
            `carries out the acts for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law` IS `my sole purpose was humanitarian assistance activities under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law`
            `uses reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups` IS `I used reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups`

@export Under section 83.03(3), does my authorization take me outside the offence in section 83.03(2)?
GIVEN `I acted under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry out the acts under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.03(3), does my authorization take me outside the offence in section 83.03(2)` IS
    `s 83.03(3) subsection (2) does not apply to a person acting under and in accordance with an authorization` `I acted under and in accordance with an authorization granted under section 83.032`

@export Under section 83.03(4), does my humanitarian assistance work take me outside the offences in sections 83.03(1) and (2)?
GIVEN `my sole purpose was humanitarian assistance activities under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your sole purpose to carry out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law?
      `I used reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.03(4), does my humanitarian assistance work take me outside the offences in sections 83.03(1) and (2)` IS
    `s 83.03(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person carrying out humanitarian assistance activities` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 83.03(4) facts` WITH
            `carries out the acts for the sole purpose of carrying out humanitarian assistance activities conducted under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law` IS `my sole purpose was humanitarian assistance activities under the auspices of impartial humanitarian organizations in accordance with international law`
            `uses reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups` IS `I used reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to terrorist groups`

§§ `What is the most I can be sentenced to?`

@export Under section 83.02, what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 83.02, what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS `s 83.02 seat the punishment in words` `s 83.02 the punishment of the offence`

@export Under section 83.03(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 83.03(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS `s 83.02 seat the punishment in words` `s 83.03(1) the punishment of the offence`

@export Under section 83.03(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 83.03(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS `s 83.02 seat the punishment in words` `s 83.03(2) the punishment of the offence`

§ `Authorization to carry out an activity that would otherwise be an offence (ss 83.031 to 83.0392; if you have applied for, or hold, an authorization)`

§§ `Can I be authorized, and for how long?`

@export Under section 83.032(4), am I eligible to be granted an authorization?
GIVEN `I am in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Canada?
      `I am a Canadian` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc If you are outside Canada, are you a Canadian (a Canadian citizen, a permanent resident, or a body corporate incorporated and continued under the laws of Canada or a province)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.032(4), am I eligible to be granted an authorization` IS
    `s 83.032(4) the person is eligible to be granted an authorization` `I am in Canada` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `I am a Canadian`)

@export Under section 83.032(1), may the Public Safety Minister authorize my activity?
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an application to the Public Safety Minister for an authorization?
      `I am in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Canada?
      `I am a Canadian` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc If you are outside Canada, are you a Canadian? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `the activity is in a geographic area controlled by a terrorist group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the activity in a specified geographic area that is controlled by a terrorist group?
      `the activity would otherwise be prohibited under section 83.03(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the activity otherwise be prohibited under section 83.03(2) (providing or making available property or services for use by a terrorist group)?
      `what the activity is for` IS A `s 83.032(1) purpose` @desc What is the activity for: health services, education services, programs to help people earn a livelihood, programs to promote or protect human rights, services related to immigration, supporting a federal minister's or department's operations conducted for another purpose, or none of those?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.032(1), may the Public Safety Minister authorize my activity` IS
    `s 83.032(1) the Public Safety Minister may authorize the activity` `my facts` `my eligibility`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 83.032(1) facts` WITH
            `an application has been made` IS `I have applied`
            `the activity is in a specified geographic area that is controlled by a terrorist group` IS `the activity is in a geographic area controlled by a terrorist group`
            `the activity would otherwise be prohibited under subsection 83.03(2)` IS `the activity would otherwise be prohibited under section 83.03(2)`
            `the purpose` IS `what the activity is for`
        `my eligibility` MEANS `s 83.032(4) the person is eligible to be granted an authorization` `I am in Canada` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `I am a Canadian`)

@export Under section 83.032(9), may the Public Safety Minister grant me the authorization?
GIVEN `they are satisfied that there is no practical way to carry out the activity without creating a risk that a terrorist group will use or benefit from the property or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that there is no practical way to carry out the activity proposed in the application without creating a risk that, in whole or in part, a terrorist group will use or benefit from the property or financial or related services at issue?
      `they are satisfied that the benefits of carrying out the activity outweigh that risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the benefits of carrying out the activity outweigh that risk?
      `they took into account the referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister take into account the referral to the other Ministers?
      `they took into account the security review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister take into account the security review conducted under section 83.032(10)?
      `they took into account any mitigation measures and other terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister take into account any mitigation measures to minimize that risk, and any other terms and conditions, that may be included in the authorization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.032(9), may the Public Safety Minister grant me the authorization` IS
    `s 83.032(9) the Public Safety Minister may grant the authorization` `the Minister's conditions`
    WHERE
        `the Minister's conditions` MEANS `s 83.032(9) conditions` WITH
            `they are satisfied that there is no practical way to carry out the activity proposed in the application without creating a risk that, in whole or in part, a terrorist group will use or benefit from the property or financial or related services at issue` IS `they are satisfied that there is no practical way to carry out the activity without creating a risk that a terrorist group will use or benefit from the property or services`
            `they are satisfied that the benefits of carrying out of that activity outweigh that risk` IS `they are satisfied that the benefits of carrying out the activity outweigh that risk`
            `they took into account the referral` IS `they took into account the referral`
            `they took into account the security review conducted under subsection (10)` IS `they took into account the security review`
            `they took into account any mitigation measures to minimize that risk, and any other terms and conditions, that may be included in the authorization` IS `they took into account any mitigation measures and other terms and conditions`

@export Under section 83.032(13), does my authorization apply to me?
GIVEN `the authorization was granted to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the authorization granted to you?
      `I am involved in carrying out a specified activity in accordance with the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you involved, directly or indirectly, in carrying out an activity specified in the authorization in accordance with it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.032(13), does my authorization apply to me` IS
    `s 83.032(13) the authorization applies to the person` `the authorization was granted to me` `I am involved in carrying out a specified activity in accordance with the authorization`

@export Under section 83.032(14), is my authorization valid on a given day?
GIVEN `the day the authorization takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day does (or did) the authorization take effect?
      `the years of validity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole years does the authorization specify as its period of validity? (0 if less than a year)
      `the further months of validity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further whole months does the authorization specify? (0 if none)
      `the further days of validity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further days does the authorization specify? (0 if none)
      `the period is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the period end a day short, as a period "less a day" does? (No for an ordinary period.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking whether the authorization is valid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.032(14), is my authorization valid on a given day` IS
    `s 83.032(14) the authorization is valid on the day` `the day the authorization takes effect` `the period of validity` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `the period of validity` MEANS `Length of time` WITH
            years IS `the years of validity`
            months IS `the further months of validity`
            days IS `the further days of validity`
            `less a day` IS `the period is less a day`

@export Under section 83.033(2), am I barred from making a new application for the same activity?
GIVEN `the new application is for the same activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new application for the same activity as the one refused?
      `the day I was given notice of the refusal` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you given notice of the refusal?
      `the day I make the new application` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the new application?
      `the Minister who gave the notice is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister who gave you the notice satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.033(2), am I barred from making a new application for the same activity` IS
    `s 83.033(2) the applicant is barred from making a new application` `the new application is for the same activity` `the day I was given notice of the refusal` `the day I make the new application` `the Minister who gave the notice is satisfied that there has been a material change of circumstances`

@export Under section 83.035(1), may the Public Safety Minister renew my authorization?
GIVEN `I have applied for the renewal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an application for the renewal of your authorization?
      `I applied within any period set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply within any period set out in the regulations?
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you apply for the renewal?
      `the last day on which my authorization is valid` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which your authorization is valid?
      `the renewal: years` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many whole years do you seek renewal? (0 if less than a year)
      `the renewal: further months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further months? (0 if none)
      `the renewal: further days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further days? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.035(1), may the Public Safety Minister renew my authorization` IS
    `s 83.035(1) the Public Safety Minister may renew the authorization` `I have applied for the renewal` `I applied within any period set out in the regulations` `the day I applied` `the last day on which my authorization is valid` `the period for which renewal is sought`
    WHERE
        `the period for which renewal is sought` MEANS `Length of time` OF `the renewal: years`, `the renewal: further months`, `the renewal: further days`, FALSE

@export Under section 83.037, may the Public Safety Minister suspend or revoke my authorization or restrict its scope?
GIVEN `the authorization was granted under section 83.032` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the authorization granted under section 83.032?
      `a person to whom it applies fails to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person to whom the authorization applies fail to comply with it, including any terms and conditions in it?
      `I fail without reasonable excuse to report or to give the information requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as the person it was granted to, fail without reasonable excuse to comply with a reporting requirement or to provide information requested under section 83.034?
      `the Minister is no longer satisfied that the condition in section 83.032(9)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister no longer satisfied that the benefits of carrying out the activity outweigh the risk (section 83.032(9)(b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.037, may the Public Safety Minister suspend or revoke my authorization or restrict its scope` IS
    `s 83.037 the Public Safety Minister may suspend or revoke the authorization or restrict its scope` `the authorization was granted under section 83.032` `a person to whom it applies fails to comply with it` `I fail without reasonable excuse to report or to give the information requested` `the Minister is no longer satisfied that the condition in section 83.032(9)(b) is met`

§ `Using or possessing property (s 83.04)`

§§ `Is what I did an offence?`

@export Under section 83.04, is what I did the offence of using or possessing property for terrorist purposes?
GIVEN `I used property for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use property, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity?
      `I possessed property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess property?
      `I intended that it be used for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that it be used, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity?
      `I knew that it would be used for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that it would be used, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for that purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.04, is what I did the offence of using or possessing property for terrorist purposes` IS
    `s 83.04 the person is guilty of the offence` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 83.04 facts` WITH
            `uses property, directly or indirectly, in whole or in part, for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity` IS `I used property for the purpose of facilitating or carrying out a terrorist activity`
            `possesses property` IS `I possessed property`
            `intends that it be used for that purpose` IS `I intended that it be used for that purpose`
            `knows that it will be used for that purpose` IS `I knew that it would be used for that purpose`

§§ `What is the most I can be sentenced to?`

@export Under section 83.04, what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 83.04, what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS `s 83.02 seat the punishment in words` `s 83.04 the punishment of the offence`

§ `The list of terrorist entities (ss 83.05 to 83.07; if your group is on, or may be put on, the list)`

@export Under section 83.05(1), may the Governor in Council place my group on the list of entities?
GIVEN `the Governor in Council acts on the recommendation of the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Governor in Council acting on a recommendation of the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness?
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that my group has knowingly carried out, attempted to carry out, participated in or facilitated a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that your group has knowingly carried out, attempted to carry out, participated in or facilitated a terrorist activity?
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that my group has knowingly acted on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with such an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that your group has knowingly acted on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with an entity of that kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.05(1), may the Governor in Council place my group on the list of entities` IS
    `s 83.05(1) the Governor in Council may place the entity on the list` `the Governor in Council acts on the recommendation of the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that my group has knowingly carried out, attempted to carry out, participated in or facilitated a terrorist activity` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that my group has knowingly acted on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with such an entity`

@export Under section 83.05(5), may I apply to a judge for judicial review of the Minister's decision?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the notice of the Minister's decision on your application to be removed from the list?
      `the day I apply to the judge` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you apply, or did you apply, to a judge for judicial review?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.05(5), may I apply to a judge for judicial review of the Minister's decision` IS
    `s 83.05(5) the applicant may apply to a judge for judicial review` `the day I received the notice of the decision` `the day I apply to the judge`

@export Under section 83.05(8), is my listed group barred from making another application to be removed from the list?
GIVEN `my group has made a previous application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your group made a previous application under section 83.05(2) to be removed from the list?
      `there has been a material change in its circumstances since its last application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the time of its last application, has there been a material change in its circumstances?
      `the Minister has completed a review of it under section 83.05(8.1) since then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister completed a review under section 83.05(8.1) with respect to your group since then?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.05(8), is my listed group barred from making another application to be removed from the list` IS
    `s 83.05(8) the listed entity is barred from making another application` `my group has made a previous application` `there has been a material change in its circumstances since its last application` `the Minister has completed a review of it under section 83.05(8.1) since then`

@export Under section 83.07(1), may my entity apply in writing to the Minister for a certificate that it is not the listed entity?
GIVEN `its name is the same as or similar to a name on the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entity's name the same as or similar to the name, appearing on the list, of a listed entity?
      `it claims not to be that listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your entity claim not to be that listed entity?
      `the application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application in writing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.07(1), may my entity apply in writing to the Minister for a certificate that it is not the listed entity` IS
    `s 83.07(1) the entity may apply in writing to the Minister for a certificate` `its name is the same as or similar to a name on the list` `it claims not to be that listed entity` `the application is in writing`

@export Under section 83.07(2), must the Minister issue me a certificate?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that I am not that listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that your entity is not that listed entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.07(2), must the Minister issue me a certificate` IS
    `s 83.07(2) the Minister must issue the certificate` `the Minister is satisfied that I am not that listed entity`

§ `Freezing of property (ss 83.08 to 83.12)`

§§ `May I deal with this property? Must I tell the police?`

@export Under section 83.08(1), am I barred from the dealing, transaction or service I describe in respect of property of a terrorist group?
GIVEN `I am in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Canada?
      `I am a Canadian` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc If you are outside Canada, are you a Canadian (a Canadian citizen, a permanent resident, or a body corporate incorporated and continued under the laws of Canada or a province)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `what I did or would do` IS A `s 83.08(1) act` @desc What is it: dealing in the property, entering into or facilitating a transaction in respect of it, providing financial or related services in respect of it, or none of those?
      `I would do it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you do it knowingly?
      `the property is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group?
      `the group is a terrorist group` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is the group a terrorist group within section 83.01(1)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.08(1), am I barred from the dealing, transaction or service I describe in respect of property of a terrorist group` IS
    `s 83.08(1) the person is barred from the act` `I am in Canada` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `I am a Canadian`) `what I did or would do` `I would do it knowingly` `the property is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the group is a terrorist group`)

@export Under section 83.08(2), am I free from civil liability for measures I took to comply with section 83.08(1)?
GIVEN `I acted reasonably in taking, or omitting to take, measures to comply with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act reasonably in taking, or omitting to take, measures to comply with section 83.08(1)?
      `I took all reasonable steps to satisfy myself that the property was owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take all reasonable steps to satisfy yourself that the property was owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.08(2), am I free from civil liability for measures I took to comply with section 83.08(1)` IS
    `s 83.08(2) the person is not liable in the civil action` `I acted reasonably in taking, or omitting to take, measures to comply with subsection (1)` `I took all reasonable steps to satisfy myself that the property was owned or controlled by or on behalf of a terrorist group`

@export Under section 83.09(4), am I outside sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 because another person has a ministerial authorization?
GIVEN `another person obtained an authorization under section 83.09(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another person obtained an authorization from the Minister under section 83.09(1)?
      `I am involved in carrying out the activity or transaction the authorization relates to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you involved in carrying out the activity or transaction, or class of them, to which that authorization relates?
      `the terms and conditions of the authorization, if any, are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the terms and conditions of the authorization, if there are any, met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.09(4), am I outside sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11 because another person has a ministerial authorization` IS
    `s 83.09(4) the other person is not subject to sections 83.08, 83.1 and 83.11` `another person obtained an authorization under section 83.09(1)` `I am involved in carrying out the activity or transaction the authorization relates to` `the terms and conditions of the authorization, if any, are met`

@export Under section 83.1(1)(a), must I tell the Commissioner of the RCMP or the Director of CSIS of the existence of property in my possession or control?
GIVEN `I am in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Canada?
      `I am a Canadian` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc If you are outside Canada, are you a Canadian? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `the property is in my possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property in your possession or control?
      `I know that it is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that it is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group?
      `the group is a terrorist group` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is the group a terrorist group within section 83.01(1)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.1(1)(a), must I tell the Commissioner of the RCMP or the Director of CSIS of the existence of property in my possession or control` IS
    `s 83.1(1)(a) the person must disclose the existence of the property` `I am in Canada` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `I am a Canadian`) `the property is in my possession or control` `I know that it is owned or controlled by or on behalf of the group` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the group is a terrorist group`)

@export Under section 83.1(1)(b), must I also tell the Commissioner of the RCMP or the Director of CSIS about information on a transaction in respect of that property?
GIVEN `I must disclose the existence of the property under section 83.1(1)(a)` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Must you disclose the existence of the property under section 83.1(1)(a)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `I have information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of that property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of that property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.1(1)(b), must I also tell the Commissioner of the RCMP or the Director of CSIS about information on a transaction in respect of that property` IS
    `s 83.1(1)(b) the person must disclose information about the transaction` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `I must disclose the existence of the property under section 83.1(1)(a)`) `I have information about a transaction or proposed transaction in respect of that property`

@export Under section 83.1(2), am I protected from criminal and civil proceedings for a disclosure I made in good faith?
GIVEN `I made the disclosure in good faith under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the disclosure in good faith under section 83.1(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.1(2), am I protected from criminal and civil proceedings for a disclosure I made in good faith` IS
    `s 83.1(2) no criminal or civil proceedings lie against the person` `I made the disclosure in good faith under subsection (1)`

@export Under section 83.11(2), by what day must my business make its next report, if my last report was on a given day?
GIVEN `the day of my last report` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make your last report?
      `the period specified by regulation, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If a regulation specifies a period for reports, how many days? Enter 0 if no period is specified (then the report is monthly).
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 83.11(2), by what day must my business make its next report, if my last report was on a given day` IS
    `s 83.11(2) the day by which the next report is due` `the day of my last report` (IF `the period specified by regulation, in days` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST `the period specified by regulation, in days` ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no period specified by regulation was entered (0), so the rule's own monthly default applies

@export Under section 83.12(1), is what I did the offence of contravening the freezing, disclosure or audit sections?
GIVEN `I contravened section 83.08` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene section 83.08 (dealing in property of a terrorist group)?
      `I contravened section 83.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene section 83.1 (failing to disclose)?
      `I contravened section 83.11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene section 83.11 (failing to determine whether you hold property, or to report)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.12(1), is what I did the offence of contravening the freezing, disclosure or audit sections` IS
    `s 83.12(1) the person is guilty of the offence` `I contravened section 83.08` `I contravened section 83.1` `I contravened section 83.11`

@export Under section 83.12(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 83.12(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS `s 83.02 seat the punishments in words` `s 83.12(1) the punishments of the offence`

§ `Seizure, restraint and forfeiture of property (ss 83.13 to 83.17; if your property has been seized, restrained or forfeited)`

@export Under section 83.13(6), must the judge require notice to be given to me, and may the judge hear me, before ordering the property destroyed?
GIVEN `the judge is about to make a destruction order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge about to make an order that the property be destroyed?
      `in the judge's opinion I appear to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the judge's opinion, do you appear to have a valid interest in the property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
