    `s 83.18(2) the circumstance does not prevent an offence under subsection (1)` `the circumstance`

@export Under section 83.18(3), is this conduct participating in or contributing to an activity of a terrorist group?
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `s 83.18(3) conduct` @desc What did you do: provide or receive training or recruit someone to receive it, provide a skill or expertise, recruit someone to facilitate or commit a terrorism offence (in Canada or outside), enter or remain in a country for a terrorist group, make yourself available on a terrorist group's instructions, or something else?
      `the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc If the conduct is recruiting or making yourself available, is the offence a terrorism offence as section 2 defines that term? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.18(3), is this conduct participating in or contributing to an activity of a terrorist group` IS
    `s 83.18(3) the conduct is participating in or contributing to an activity of a terrorist group` `the conduct` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the offence is a terrorism offence`)

@export Under section 83.18(4), may the court consider this factor in deciding whether I participated in or contributed to an activity of a terrorist group?
GIVEN `the factor` IS A `s 83.18(4) factor` @desc Which factor: whether you use a name, word, symbol or other representation that identifies, or is associated with, the group; frequently associate with any of the persons who constitute the group; receive any benefit from the group; or repeatedly engage in activities at the instruction of any of the persons who constitute the group; or another factor?
