§ `Harbouring or concealing, and hoaxes (ss 83.23 and 83.231)`

§§ `Is what I did an offence?`

@export Under section 83.23(1), is what I did the offence of harbouring or concealing a person who has carried out a terrorist activity?
GIVEN `I knowingly harboured or concealed another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly harbour or conceal another person?
      `I knew that person had carried out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that person had carried out a terrorist activity?
      `it was for the purpose of enabling that person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for the purpose of enabling that person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity?
      `the terrorist activity that person carried out is a terrorism offence` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is the terrorist activity that person carried out a terrorism offence as section 2 defines that term? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.23(1), is what I did the offence of harbouring or concealing a person who has carried out a terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.23(1) the person is guilty of the offence` `I knowingly harboured or concealed another person` `I knew that person had carried out a terrorist activity` `it was for the purpose of enabling that person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the terrorist activity that person carried out is a terrorism offence`)

@export Under section 83.23(2), is what I did the offence of harbouring or concealing a person who is likely to carry out a terrorist activity?
GIVEN `I knowingly harboured or concealed another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly harbour or conceal another person?
      `I knew that person was likely to carry out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that person was likely to carry out a terrorist activity?
      `it was for the purpose of enabling that person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for the purpose of enabling that person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.23(2), is what I did the offence of harbouring or concealing a person who is likely to carry out a terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.23(2) the person is guilty of the offence` `I knowingly harboured or concealed another person` `I knew that person was likely to carry out a terrorist activity` `it was for the purpose of enabling that person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity`

@export Under section 83.231(1), is what I did the offence of conveying information or committing an act that causes a reasonable apprehension of terrorist activity?
GIVEN `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
      `I intended to cause a person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to cause a person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property?
      `I conveyed, or caused to be conveyed, information likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you convey, or cause or procure to be conveyed, information that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur?
      `I believed that information to be true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that information to be true?
      `I committed an act likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit an act that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur?
      `I believed that such activity was occurring or would occur` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that such activity was occurring or would occur?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.231(1), is what I did the offence of conveying information or committing an act that causes a reasonable apprehension of terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.231(1) the person commits the offence` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 83.231(1) facts` WITH
            `the person has a lawful excuse` IS `I had a lawful excuse`
            `the person intends to cause a person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property` IS `I intended to cause a person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property`
            `the person conveys, or causes or procures to be conveyed, information that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur` IS `I conveyed, or caused to be conveyed, information likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur`
            `the person believes the information to be true` IS `I believed that information to be true`
            `the person commits an act that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur` IS `I committed an act likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur`
            `the person believes that such activity is occurring or will occur` IS `I believed that such activity was occurring or would occur`

@export Under section 83.231(3), is what I did the offence of causing bodily harm by conveying information or committing an act that causes a reasonable apprehension of terrorist activity?
GIVEN `what I did is an offence under section 83.231(1)` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is what you did an offence under section 83.231(1)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `I thereby caused bodily harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you thereby cause bodily harm to any other person?
      `that harm is bodily harm as section 2 defines it` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is that harm "bodily harm" as section 2 defines it (any hurt or injury that interferes with the health or comfort of the person and that is more than merely transient or trifling in nature)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.231(3), is what I did the offence of causing bodily harm by conveying information or committing an act that causes a reasonable apprehension of terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.231(3) the person commits the offence causing bodily harm` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `what I did is an offence under section 83.231(1)`) `I thereby caused bodily harm to another person` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `that harm is bodily harm as section 2 defines it`)

