GIVEN `what I did is an offence under section 83.231(1)` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is what you did an offence under section 83.231(1)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `I thereby caused the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you thereby cause the death of any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.231(4), is what I did the offence of causing death by conveying information or committing an act that causes a reasonable apprehension of terrorist activity` IS
    `s 83.231(4) the person commits the offence causing death` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `what I did is an offence under section 83.231(1)`) `I thereby caused the death of another person`

§§ `What is the most I can be sentenced to?`

@export Under section 83.23(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to, if the terrorism offence is or is not one punishable by imprisonment for life?
GIVEN `the terrorism offence is punishable by imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the terrorism offence that person carried out punishable by imprisonment for life?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 83.23(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to, if the terrorism offence is or is not one punishable by imprisonment for life` IS
    `s 83.02 seat the punishment in words` (`s 83.23(1) the punishment of the offence` `the punishment the terrorism offence carries`)
    WHERE
        -- Only the term of imprisonment of the other offence is read by the rule; the other fields are fixed placeholders.
        `the punishment the terrorism offence carries` MEANS
            Punishment OF `by indictment`, (IF `the terrorism offence is punishable by imprisonment for life` THEN `imprisonment for life` ELSE `no imprisonment is stated`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@export Under section 83.23(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to?
