    `s 83.25(1) the proceedings may be commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `I am alleged to have committed a terrorism offence`) `I am alleged to have committed an offence under section 83.12` `the offence is alleged to have occurred outside the province in which the proceedings are commenced`

@export Under section 83.25(2), may I be tried and punished as if the offence had been committed in the territorial division where I am tried?
GIVEN `it is an offence referred to in section 83.25(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offence referred to in section 83.25(1) (a terrorism offence or an offence under section 83.12, alleged and proceeded with as that subsection describes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.25(2), may I be tried and punished as if the offence had been committed in the territorial division where I am tried` IS
    `s 83.25(2) the accused may be tried and punished as if the offence had been committed in the territorial division` `it is an offence referred to in section 83.25(1)`

§§ `Will my sentences run one after the other?`

@export Under section 83.26(a), is my sentence to be served consecutively to the other punishment imposed on me for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence this sentence is imposed for` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence this sentence is imposed for, as printed in the Code (for example 83.18)?
      `my sentence is one of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this sentence one of life imprisonment?
      `the other punishment is a sentence of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other punishment imposed on you a sentence of life imprisonment?
      `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other punishment for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.26(a), is my sentence to be served consecutively to the other punishment imposed on me for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS
    `s 83.26(a) the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other punishment` `the offence` `my sentence is one of life imprisonment` `the other punishment is a sentence of life imprisonment` `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events`
    WHERE
        -- Only the section number is read by the rule; the subsection is a fixed placeholder.
        `the offence` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence this sentence is imposed for`, ""

@export Under section 83.26(b), is my sentence to be served consecutively to the other sentence to which I am subject when it is imposed?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence this sentence is imposed for` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence this sentence is imposed for, as printed in the Code (for example 83.18)?
      `my sentence is one of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this sentence one of life imprisonment?
      `the other sentence is one of life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other sentence one of life imprisonment?
      `I am subject to the other sentence when this sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to the other sentence at the time this sentence is imposed?
      `the other sentence is for an offence under one of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other sentence for an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.26(b), is my sentence to be served consecutively to the other sentence to which I am subject when it is imposed` IS
    `s 83.26(b) the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other sentence` `the offence` `my sentence is one of life imprisonment` `the other sentence is one of life imprisonment` `I am subject to the other sentence when this sentence is imposed` `the other sentence is for an offence under one of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23`
    WHERE
        -- Only the section number is read by the rule; the subsection is a fixed placeholder.
        `the offence` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence this sentence is imposed for`, ""

§§ `Am I liable to imprisonment for life because the offence is also a terrorist activity?`

@export Under section 83.27, am I liable to imprisonment for life because the act constituting my indictable offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, subject to the notice required by subsection (2)?
GIVEN `I am convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you convicted of an indictable offence?
      `a sentence of imprisonment for life is imposed for the offence as a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is imprisonment for life the minimum punishment for the offence?
      `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Does the act or omission constituting the offence also constitute a terrorist activity within section 83.01(1)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `the prosecutor satisfies the court that I was notified before making a plea that this would be sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor satisfy the court that you were notified, before making a plea, that the application of section 83.27(1) would be sought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.27, am I liable to imprisonment for life because the act constituting my indictable offence also constitutes a terrorist activity, subject to the notice required by subsection (2)` IS
    `s 83.27 the person is liable to imprisonment for life, subject to subsection (2)` `the answer of subsection (1)` `the prosecutor satisfies the court that I was notified before making a plea that this would be sought`
    WHERE
        `the answer of subsection (1)` MEANS `s 83.27(1) the person is liable to imprisonment for life` `I am convicted of an indictable offence` `a sentence of imprisonment for life is imposed for the offence as a minimum punishment` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the act or omission constituting the offence also constitutes a terrorist activity`)

@export Under section 83.27(2), does section 83.27(1) fail to apply to me because I was not notified before making a plea?
GIVEN `the prosecutor satisfies the court that I was notified before making a plea that this would be sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor satisfy the court that you were notified, before making a plea, that the application of section 83.27(1) would be sought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.27(2), does section 83.27(1) fail to apply to me because I was not notified before making a plea` IS
    `s 83.27(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `the prosecutor satisfies the court that I was notified before making a plea that this would be sought`

§ `Recognizance with conditions (ss 83.3 to 83.33; if a peace officer has arrested you, or laid or may lay an information, to prevent a terrorist activity)`

§§ `The information, and arrest without a warrant (s 83.3(1) to (6))`

@export Under section 83.3(1), is a peace officer barred from laying an information about me without the Attorney General's consent?
GIVEN `the Attorney General has consented to the peace officer laying the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General consented to the peace officer laying the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(1), is a peace officer barred from laying an information about me without the Attorney General's consent` IS
    `s 83.3(1) the peace officer is barred from laying an information` `the Attorney General has consented to the peace officer laying the information`

@export Under section 83.3(2), may a peace officer lay an information before a provincial court judge about me?
GIVEN `the Attorney General has consented to the peace officer laying the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General consented to the peace officer laying the information?
      `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that a terrorist activity may be carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer believe on reasonable grounds that a terrorist activity may be carried out?
      `the peace officer suspects on reasonable grounds that a recognizance with conditions on me, or my arrest, is necessary to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer suspect on reasonable grounds that the imposition of a recognizance with conditions on a person, or the arrest of a person, is necessary to prevent the carrying out of the terrorist activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(2), may a peace officer lay an information before a provincial court judge about me` IS
    `s 83.3(2) the peace officer may lay an information before a provincial court judge` `the Attorney General has consented to the peace officer laying the information` `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that a terrorist activity may be carried out` `the peace officer suspects on reasonable grounds that a recognizance with conditions on me, or my arrest, is necessary to prevent it`

@export Under section 83.3(4), may a peace officer arrest me without a warrant and have me detained in custody?
GIVEN `the grounds for laying an information exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the grounds for laying an information (that a terrorist activity may be carried out, and that a recognizance with conditions on a person or the person's arrest is necessary to prevent it) exist?
      `exigent circumstances make it impracticable to lay an information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of exigent circumstances, would it be impracticable to lay an information under section 83.3(2)?
      `an information has been laid and a summons has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an information been laid under section 83.3(2), and a summons been issued?
      `the peace officer suspects on reasonable grounds that my detention is necessary to prevent a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer suspect on reasonable grounds that your detention in custody is necessary to prevent a terrorist activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(4), may a peace officer arrest me without a warrant and have me detained in custody` IS
    `s 83.3(4) the peace officer may arrest the person without a warrant and cause the person to be detained in custody` `the grounds for laying an information exist` `exigent circumstances make it impracticable to lay an information` `an information has been laid and a summons has been issued` `the peace officer suspects on reasonable grounds that my detention is necessary to prevent a terrorist activity`

@export Under section 83.3(5), must the peace officer lay an information or release me?
GIVEN `I was arrested without a warrant because the grounds existed but laying an information was impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you arrested without a warrant in the circumstance described in section 83.3(4)(a)(i) (the grounds existed, but by reason of exigent circumstances it was impracticable to lay an information)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(5), must the peace officer lay an information or release me` IS
    `s 83.3(5) the peace officer must lay an information or release the person` `I was arrested without a warrant because the grounds existed but laying an information was impracticable`

@export Under section 83.3(6), when must I be taken before a provincial court judge?
GIVEN `the peace officer is satisfied that I should be released without conditions, and so releases me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the peace officer satisfied that you should be released from custody without conditions before you appear, and does so release you?
      `a provincial court judge is available within 24 hours after my arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a provincial court judge available within 24 hours after you have been arrested?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(6), when must I be taken before a provincial court judge` IS
    CONSIDER `s 83.3(6) the rule for taking the person before a provincial court judge` `the peace officer is satisfied that I should be released without conditions, and so releases me` `a provincial court judge is available within 24 hours after my arrest`
    WHEN `s 83.3(6)(a) the person is to be taken before a provincial court judge without unreasonable delay and in any event within 24 hours` THEN "Without unreasonable delay, and in any event within 24 hours after the arrest."
    WHEN `s 83.3(6)(b) the person is to be taken before a provincial court judge as soon as feasible` THEN "As soon as feasible."
    WHEN `s 83.3(6) the person is not to be taken before a provincial court judge because the peace officer released the person without conditions` THEN "You are not to be taken before a provincial court judge, because the peace officer was satisfied you should be released without conditions and released you."

@export Under section 83.3(6)(a), was I taken before a provincial court judge without unreasonable delay and within 24 hours of my arrest?
GIVEN `the number of hours after my arrest at which I was taken before a provincial court judge` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after your arrest were you taken before a provincial court judge?
      `it was without unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it without unreasonable delay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(6)(a), was I taken before a provincial court judge without unreasonable delay and within 24 hours of my arrest` IS
    `s 83.3(6)(a) the person is taken before a provincial court judge in time` `the number of hours after my arrest at which I was taken before a provincial court judge` `it was without unreasonable delay`

§§ `Before the judge: release, or detention on cause shown (s 83.3(7) to (7.2))`

@export Under section 83.3(7)(a), must the judge order that I be released because no information has been laid?
GIVEN `no information has been laid under section 83.3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no information been laid under section 83.3(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(7)(a), must the judge order that I be released because no information has been laid` IS
    `s 83.3(7)(a) the judge must order that the person be released` `no information has been laid under section 83.3(2)`

@export Under section 83.3(7)(b)(i), must the judge order that I be released unless the peace officer shows cause for my detention?
GIVEN `an information has been laid under section 83.3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an information been laid under section 83.3(2)?
      `the peace officer who laid the information shows cause why my detention is justified on one or more of the three grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer who laid the information show cause why your detention in custody is justified on one or more of the grounds in section 83.3(7)(b)(i) (to ensure your appearance, for the protection or safety of the public, or to maintain confidence in the administration of justice)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(7)(b)(i), must the judge order that I be released unless the peace officer shows cause for my detention` IS
    `s 83.3(7)(b)(i) the judge must order that the person be released` `an information has been laid under section 83.3(2)` `the peace officer who laid the information shows cause why my detention is justified on one or more of the three grounds`

@export Under section 83.3(7)(b)(ii), is the adjournment of my hearing within 48 hours?
GIVEN `I am not released under section 83.3(7)(b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not released under section 83.3(7)(b)(i) (so that you remain in custody)?
      `the adjournment, in hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours is the adjournment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(7)(b)(ii), is the adjournment of my hearing within 48 hours` IS
    `s 83.3(7)(b)(ii) the adjournment is within 48 hours` `I am not released under section 83.3(7)(b)(i)` `the adjournment, in hours`

@export Under section 83.3(7.1)(a), must the judge order that I be released at the end of the first adjournment?
GIVEN `the judge adjourned the matter and I remain in custody at the end of the period of adjournment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge adjourn the matter under section 83.3(7)(b)(ii), and do you remain in custody at the end of the period of adjournment?
      `a peace officer shows cause why my detention is justified on one or more of the three grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a peace officer show cause why your detention in custody is justified on one or more of the grounds in section 83.3(7)(b)(i)(A) to (C)?
      `the peace officer satisfies the judge that the investigation is being conducted diligently and expeditiously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer satisfy the judge that the investigation in relation to which you are detained is being conducted diligently and expeditiously?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(7.1)(a), must the judge order that I be released at the end of the first adjournment` IS
    `s 83.3(7.1)(a) the judge must order that the person be released` `the judge adjourned the matter and I remain in custody at the end of the period of adjournment` `a peace officer shows cause why my detention is justified on one or more of the three grounds` `the peace officer satisfies the judge that the investigation is being conducted diligently and expeditiously`

@export Under section 83.3(7.1)(b), is the second adjournment of my hearing within 48 hours?
GIVEN `I am not released under section 83.3(7.1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not released under section 83.3(7.1)(a) (so that you remain in custody)?
      `the adjournment, in hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours is the adjournment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(7.1)(b), is the second adjournment of my hearing within 48 hours` IS
    `s 83.3(7.1)(b) the adjournment is within 48 hours` `I am not released under section 83.3(7.1)(a)` `the adjournment, in hours`

@export Under section 83.3(7.2)(a), must the judge order that I be released at the end of the second adjournment?
GIVEN `the judge adjourned the matter again and I remain in custody at the end of the period of adjournment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge adjourn the matter under section 83.3(7.1)(b), and do you remain in custody at the end of the period of adjournment?
      `a peace officer shows cause why my detention is justified on one or more of the three grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a peace officer show cause why your detention in custody is justified on one or more of the grounds in section 83.3(7)(b)(i)(A) to (C)?
      `the peace officer satisfies the judge that the investigation is being conducted diligently and expeditiously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer satisfy the judge that the investigation in relation to which you are detained is being conducted diligently and expeditiously?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(7.2)(a), must the judge order that I be released at the end of the second adjournment` IS
    `s 83.3(7.2)(a) the judge must order that the person be released` `the judge adjourned the matter again and I remain in custody at the end of the period of adjournment` `a peace officer shows cause why my detention is justified on one or more of the three grounds` `the peace officer satisfies the judge that the investigation is being conducted diligently and expeditiously`

@export Under section 83.3(7.2)(b), is a third adjournment of my hearing within 48 hours?
GIVEN `I am not released under section 83.3(7.2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not released under section 83.3(7.2)(a) (so that you remain in custody)?
      `the adjournment, in hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours is the adjournment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(7.2)(b), is a third adjournment of my hearing within 48 hours` IS
    `s 83.3(7.2)(b) the adjournment is within 48 hours` `I am not released under section 83.3(7.2)(a)` `the adjournment, in hours`

§§ `The recognizance, and its conditions (s 83.3(8) to (14))`

@export Under section 83.3(8)(a), may the judge order that I enter into a recognizance for this period?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion?
      `the recognizance: years` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many whole years is the recognizance to run? (0 if less than a year)
      `the recognizance: further months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further months? (0 if none)
      `the recognizance: further days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further days? (0 if none)
      `the judge is also satisfied that I was previously convicted of a terrorism offence` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is the judge also satisfied that you were convicted previously of a terrorism offence as section 2 defines that term (the gate of section 83.3(8.1), which allows a period of up to two years)? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(8)(a), may the judge order that I enter into a recognizance for this period` IS
    `s 83.3(8)(a) the judge may order that the person enter into a recognizance` `the judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the peace officer has reasonable grounds for the suspicion` `the period` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the judge is also satisfied that I was previously convicted of a terrorism offence`)
    WHERE
        `the period` MEANS `Length of time` OF `the recognizance: years`, `the recognizance: further months`, `the recognizance: further days`, FALSE

@export Under section 83.3(8.1), may the judge order that I enter into the recognizance for a longer period because I was previously convicted of a terrorism offence?
GIVEN `the judge is also satisfied that I was convicted previously of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge also satisfied that you were convicted previously of an offence?
      `the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Is that offence a terrorism offence as section 2 defines that term? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(8.1), may the judge order that I enter into the recognizance for a longer period because I was previously convicted of a terrorism offence` IS
    `s 83.3(8.1) the judge may order the recognizance for a longer period` `the judge is also satisfied that I was convicted previously of an offence` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `the offence is a terrorism offence`)

@export Under section 83.3(8)(b), must the judge order that I be released, subject to the recognizance?
GIVEN `I was not released under section 83.3(7)(b)(i), (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not released under section 83.3(7)(b)(i), (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a) (so that you were still in custody at the hearing)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(8)(b), must the judge order that I be released, subject to the recognizance` IS
    `s 83.3(8)(b) the judge must order that the person be released, subject to the recognizance` `I was not released under section 83.3(7)(b)(i), (7.1)(a) or (7.2)(a)`

@export Under section 83.3(9), may the judge commit me to prison for a term of this many months for refusing to enter into the recognizance?
GIVEN `I fail or refuse to enter into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail or refuse to enter into the recognizance?
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months would the judge commit you to prison?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(9), may the judge commit me to prison for a term of this many months for refusing to enter into the recognizance` IS
    `s 83.3(9) the judge may commit the person to prison` `I fail or refuse to enter into the recognizance` `the term of imprisonment, in months`

@export Under section 83.3(10), must the judge add a firearms and weapons condition to my recognizance?
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of me or any other person, to include the condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge decide that it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of you or any other person, to include the condition that you be prohibited from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(10), must the judge add a firearms and weapons condition to my recognizance` IS
    `s 83.3(10) the judge must add the condition to the recognizance` `the judge decides that it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of me or any other person, to include the condition`

@export Under section 83.3(10), may the condition in my recognizance prohibit me from possessing this thing?
GIVEN `the thing` IS A `s 83.3(10) thing` @desc What is the thing: a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition, an explosive substance, or something that is none of those?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(10), may the condition in my recognizance prohibit me from possessing this thing` IS
    `s 83.3(10) the condition may prohibit the thing` `the thing`

@export Under section 83.3(11), must the judge specify the manner and method of surrender in my recognizance?
GIVEN `the judge adds the firearms and weapons condition to my recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge add the condition described in section 83.3(10) to your recognizance?
      `the judge specifies how the things in my possession are to be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge specify in it the manner and method by which the things in your possession are to be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with?
      `the judge specifies how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates I hold are to be surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge specify in it the manner and method by which the authorizations, licences and registration certificates you hold are to be surrendered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(11), must the judge specify the manner and method of surrender in my recognizance` IS
    `s 83.3(11) the judge must specify the manner and method` `the judge adds the firearms and weapons condition to my recognizance` `the judge specifies how the things in my possession are to be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with` `the judge specifies how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates I hold are to be surrendered`

@export Under section 83.3(11.1), must the judge add a passport condition and specify the period in my recognizance?
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge decide that it is desirable, to prevent the carrying out of a terrorist activity, to include a condition that you deposit your passport, or surrender any other travel document, with the judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(11.1), must the judge add a passport condition and specify the period in my recognizance` IS
    `s 83.3(11.1) the judge must add the passport condition and specify the period` `the judge decides that it is desirable`

@export Under section 83.3(11.2), must the judge add a geographic-area condition and specify the period in my recognizance?
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge decide that it is desirable, to prevent the carrying out of a terrorist activity, to include a condition that you remain within a specified geographic area?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(11.2), must the judge add a geographic-area condition and specify the period in my recognizance` IS
    `s 83.3(11.2) the judge must add the geographic-area condition and specify the period` `the judge decides that it is desirable`

@export Under section 83.3(11.2), am I barred from leaving the specified geographic area?
GIVEN `my recognizance includes the condition that I remain within a specified geographic area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your recognizance include a condition that you remain within a specified geographic area?
      `I have written permission to leave that area from the judge or any individual the judge designated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have written permission to leave that area from the judge or any individual designated by the judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(11.2), am I barred from leaving the specified geographic area` IS
    `s 83.3(11.2) the person is barred from leaving the specified geographic area` `my recognizance includes the condition that I remain within a specified geographic area` `I have written permission to leave that area from the judge or any individual the judge designated`

@export Under section 83.3(12), must the judge include a statement of reasons in the record because no firearms, passport or geographic condition was added?
GIVEN `the judge does not add any condition described in section 83.3(10), (11.1) or (11.2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge not add a condition described in section 83.3(10), (11.1) or (11.2) to your recognizance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(12), must the judge include a statement of reasons in the record because no firearms, passport or geographic condition was added` IS
    `s 83.3(12) the judge must include a statement of reasons in the record` `the judge does not add any condition described in section 83.3(10), (11.1) or (11.2)`

@export Under section 83.3(13), may the judge vary the conditions of my recognizance?
GIVEN `the application is by the peace officer, the Attorney General or me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application by the peace officer, the Attorney General or you?
      `the judge is the judge, or another judge of the same court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the judge who made the order, or another judge of the same court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(13), may the judge vary the conditions of my recognizance` IS
    `s 83.3(13) the judge may vary the conditions` `the application is by the peace officer, the Attorney General or me` `the judge is the judge, or another judge of the same court`

@export Under section 83.3(14), does this provision apply to the proceedings under section 83.3?
GIVEN `the section number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the provision you are asking about (for example 810)?
      `the subsection` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, as the Code writes it (for example (4))? Leave empty if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.3(14), does this provision apply to the proceedings under section 83.3` IS
    `s 83.3(14) the provision applies to proceedings under this section` `the provision`
    WHERE
        `the provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number`, `the subsection`

§ `Sunset of section 83.3, and what follows (ss 83.31 to 83.33)`

@export Under section 83.32(1), has section 83.3 ceased to have effect on this day?
GIVEN `the day the National Security Act, 2017 received royal assent` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the National Security Act, 2017 receive royal assent?
      `the operation of section 83.3 has been extended by resolution of both Houses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the operation of section 83.3 been extended by a resolution passed by both Houses of Parliament before the end of the period then running?
      `the last day of the most recent extension` IS A DATE @desc If it has been extended, what is the last day of the most recent extension? (Enter any date if it has not been extended.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking whether section 83.3 has ceased to have effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.32(1), has section 83.3 ceased to have effect on this day` IS
    `s 83.32(1) section 83.3 has ceased to have effect on the day` `the day the National Security Act, 2017 received royal assent` `the most recent extension, if there is one` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `the most recent extension, if there is one` MEANS
            IF `the operation of section 83.3 has been extended by resolution of both Houses`
            THEN JUST `the last day of the most recent extension`
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no extension by resolution was entered, so the rule counts the fifth anniversary only

@export Under section 83.33(2), must I be released when section 83.3 ceases to have effect?
GIVEN `section 83.3 has ceased to have effect` IS A `s 83.01(1) seat answer` @desc Has section 83.3 ceased to have effect in accordance with section 83.32? Answer yes, no or I do not know.
      `I am detained in custody under section 83.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in custody under section 83.3?
      `I was taken before a judge under section 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you taken before a judge under section 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 83.33(2), must I be released when section 83.3 ceases to have effect` IS
    `s 83.33(2) the person must be released when section 83.3 ceases to have effect` (`s 83.01(1) seat the answer as a yes, a no or not known` `section 83.3 has ceased to have effect`) `I am detained in custody under section 83.3` `I was taken before a judge under section 83.3(6) before section 83.3 ceased to have effect`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc4 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc4-seat.l4 -- layer 2 for lines 1904-2381 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: sections 84 to 110.3 (PART III, Firearms and Other Weapons, first half).
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking, on facts they can state, whether what they did is an offence,
-- what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a conviction.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
-- This layer asks, of that person, the questions that sections 84 to 110.3 answer: what the thing they hold is (section 84), whether what they did with it is an offence
-- (sections 85 to 108), what the offence's class and punishment are, and whether and for how long a court must or may forbid them to possess firearms and other weapons (sections 109 to 110.3).
--
-- Nothing here is new law.  Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, a choice from a list of words) and calls the rule of layer 1; no rule is restated here.
-- A thing, a firearm or a weapon is named by a word from a list in the question; a word that is not on the list gives NOTHING ("not covered"), never FALSE.
-- Where layer 1 asks for the answer of a term of section 2 or of the regulations (which are not among the sources), the question takes it as "yes", "no" or "not known";
-- "not known" is passed on as NOTHING, and the answer is then NOTHING unless the text decides the case without it.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).  Each question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes on the facts given;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a closed definition, an unmet element of the offence, an exception that applies, an "unless");
--   NOTHING     "not covered": the text is silent, lists without closing the list, points to something outside the sources (the regulations, section 787(1), another part),
--               or limits its prohibition in its own wording ("without lawful excuse", "otherwise than under the authority of") and the case is within the limit.
--   NOTHING is never "no": a person for whom a question answers NOTHING has not been told that what they did is lawful.
-- Questions whose name begins "...how is the offence classified" answer a record (section 89(2), the one offence here that is punishable on summary conviction only, asks only how it is classified): how the section classifies the offence (indictable, summary, or both),
-- the punishment if prosecuted by indictment (NOTHING where there is none) and the punishment on summary conviction (always NOTHING here: the section states none, and section 787(1) is another part's).
-- Names: each question begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering, so that no two parts' questions share a name.

-- Internal helpers: they turn the person's words into the types of layer 1.  They are not questions.
DECLARE `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` HAS
    `how the offence is classified`                 IS A `Class of offence`
    `the punishment if prosecuted by indictment`    IS A MAYBE Punishment
    `the punishment on summary conviction`          IS A MAYBE Punishment

GIVEN choice IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 84(1) kind of thing`
`ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF choice EQUALS "prohibited firearm" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm`
        IF choice EQUALS "restricted firearm" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm`
        IF choice EQUALS "non-restricted firearm" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm`
        IF choice EQUALS "prohibited weapon" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
        IF choice EQUALS "restricted weapon" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
        IF choice EQUALS "replica firearm" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm`
        IF choice EQUALS "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm`
        IF choice EQUALS "firearm part" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
        IF choice EQUALS "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition`
        IF choice EQUALS "prohibited ammunition" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`
        IF choice EQUALS "cross-bow" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a cross-bow`
        IF choice EQUALS "explosive substance" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: an explosive substance`
        IF choice EQUALS "none of these" THEN JUST `s 84(1) kind: a thing that is none of those`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists

GIVEN answer IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF answer EQUALS "yes" THEN JUST TRUE   -- an input value: the person's own answer
        IF answer EQUALS "no" THEN JUST FALSE   -- an input value: the person's own answer, not the text's no
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "not known", or a word the question does not list

GIVEN answer IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc4 seat: an exception that applies or not` MEANS
    IF answer EQUALS "yes"
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- an input value: the person's own answer
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an exception that does not apply leaves the rule as the text states it

GIVEN choice IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 2 intimate partner relationship`
`ccc4 seat: the relationship named by` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF choice EQUALS "current spouse" THEN JUST `a current spouse`
        IF choice EQUALS "former spouse" THEN JUST `a former spouse`
        IF choice EQUALS "current common-law partner" THEN JUST `a current common-law partner`
        IF choice EQUALS "former common-law partner" THEN JUST `a former common-law partner`
        IF choice EQUALS "current dating partner" THEN JUST `a current dating partner`
        IF choice EQUALS "former dating partner" THEN JUST `a former dating partner`
        IF choice EQUALS "some other relationship" THEN JUST `a person in some other relationship to the person`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists

GIVEN choice IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Class of offence`
`ccc4 seat: the class named by` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF choice EQUALS "indictable only" THEN JUST `an indictable offence`
        IF choice EQUALS "summary conviction only" THEN JUST `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
        IF choice EQUALS "either" THEN JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists

GIVEN choice IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Mode of proceeding`
`ccc4 seat: the mode of proceeding named by` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF choice EQUALS "by indictment" THEN JUST `by indictment`
        IF choice EQUALS "on summary conviction" THEN JUST `on summary conviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists

GIVEN choice IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 109(1) how the person comes before the court for sentence`
`ccc4 seat: how the person comes before the court named by` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF choice EQUALS "convicted" THEN JUST `s 109(1) the person is convicted`
        IF choice EQUALS "discharged under section 730" THEN JUST `s 109(1) the person is discharged under section 730`
        IF choice EQUALS "neither" THEN JUST `s 109(1) the person is neither convicted nor discharged under section 730`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists

GIVEN first IS A MAYBE Punishment
      second IS A MAYBE Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`ccc4 seat: the first punishment that is stated` MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN second

GIVEN years IS A NUMBER
      `less a day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Length of time`
`ccc4 seat: a length of time in whole years` MEANS `Length of time` OF years, 0, 0, `less a day`


§ `Part III -- Interpretation (section 84): what is the thing I hold or did something with?`
-- Situation: the person holds or dealt with a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition and wants to know which class of thing it is, because the offences and the penalties turn on the class.

@ref s 84(1) "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm"; s 84(2)
@export Under section 84(1), is my firearm a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm?
GIVEN `it is a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a firearm in the sense of section 2: a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged and that is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person, including its frame or receiver and anything that can be adapted for use as a firearm?
      `it is designed, altered or intended to be aimed and fired by the action of one hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a handgun: designed, altered or intended to be aimed and fired by the action of one hand (whether or not it has been redesigned or altered to be aimed and fired by both hands)?
      `the length of its barrel in millimetres` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the length of its barrel in millimetres: for a revolver from the muzzle to the breach end in front of the cylinder, for any other firearm from the muzzle to and including the chamber, not counting a muzzle-flash suppressor, recoil reducer or other accessory? (The question under section 84(2) works this out.)
      `it is designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge?
      `the handgun is prescribed and for use in International Shooting Union competitions` IS A STRING @desc If it is a handgun: do the regulations prescribe it as one that is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union, and is it for use in them? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `it is adapted from a rifle or shotgun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been adapted from a rifle or shotgun, by sawing, cutting or any other alteration?
      `its length in millimetres as so adapted` IS A NUMBER @desc If it has been so adapted, how long is it in millimetres (overall)? Enter 0 if it has not been adapted.
      `it can discharge projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capable of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger, or was it assembled, or designed and manufactured, with that capability (whether or not altered to discharge only one projectile)?
      `the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited firearm` IS A STRING @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited firearm? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `it is an unlawfully manufactured firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an unlawfully manufactured firearm, regardless of the means or method of manufacture?
      `it discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it discharge centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner?
      `the capacity of the detachable cartridge magazine it was originally designed with` IS A NUMBER @desc With what capacity, in cartridges, was it originally designed to take a detachable cartridge magazine? Enter 0 if it was not.
      `it was designed and manufactured on or after the day the second paragraph (e) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it designed and manufactured on or after the day on which the second paragraph (e) of the definition of prohibited firearm (the one for a semi-automatic firearm that is not a handgun) comes into force?
      `the shortest length in millimetres to which it can be reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc To what shortest length in millimetres can it be reduced, by folding, telescoping or otherwise, and still be fired? Enter its overall length if it cannot be reduced.
      `the regulations prescribe it to be a restricted firearm` IS A STRING @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be a restricted firearm (a firearm of another kind)? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A `s 84(1) class of firearm`
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my firearm a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm` IS
    `s 84(1) the class of firearm it is` (JUST `it is a firearm`) `prohibited` `restricted`
    WHERE
        `handgun` MEANS `s 84(1) handgun` (JUST `it is a firearm`) `it is designed, altered or intended to be aimed and fired by the action of one hand`
        `automatic` MEANS `s 84(1) automatic firearm` (JUST `it is a firearm`) `it can discharge projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` `it can discharge projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger`
        `prohibited` MEANS `s 84(1) prohibited firearm` (JUST `it is a firearm`) `handgun` `the length of its barrel in millimetres` `it is designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the handgun is prescribed and for use in International Shooting Union competitions`) (NOT (`the handgun is prescribed and for use in International Shooting Union competitions` EQUALS "no")) `it is adapted from a rifle or shotgun` `its length in millimetres as so adapted` `automatic` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited firearm`) `it is an unlawfully manufactured firearm` `it discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner` `the capacity of the detachable cartridge magazine it was originally designed with` `it was designed and manufactured on or after the day the second paragraph (e) comes into force`
        `restricted` MEANS `s 84(1) restricted firearm` (JUST `it is a firearm`) `handgun` `prohibited` `the length of its barrel in millimetres` `it discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner` `the shortest length in millimetres to which it can be reduced` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be a restricted firearm`)

@ref s 84(2)
@export Under section 84(2), what is the length of my firearm’s barrel in millimetres?
GIVEN `it is a revolver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a revolver?
      `the distance from the muzzle to the breach end in front of the cylinder` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is a revolver: what is the distance in millimetres from the muzzle of the barrel to the breach end immediately in front of the cylinder? Enter 0 if it is not a revolver.
      `the distance from the muzzle to and including the chamber` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is not a revolver: what is the distance in millimetres from the muzzle of the barrel to and including the chamber? Enter 0 if it is a revolver.
      `the length of any component, part or accessory within that distance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the length in millimetres of any component, part or accessory within that distance, including one designed or intended to suppress the muzzle flash or reduce recoil? Enter 0 if none.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 84(2), what is the length of my firearm’s barrel in millimetres` IS
    `s 84(2) the length of the barrel of a firearm in millimetres` `it is a revolver` `the distance from the muzzle to the breach end in front of the cylinder` `the distance from the muzzle to and including the chamber` `the length of any component, part or accessory within that distance`

@ref s 84(1) "antique firearm"
@export Under section 84(1), is my firearm an antique firearm?
GIVEN `it is a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a firearm in the sense of section 2?
      `the year in which it was manufactured` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it manufactured?
      `it was designed to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it designed to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition?
      `it has been redesigned to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been redesigned to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition?
      `the regulations prescribe it to be an antique firearm` IS A STRING @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be an antique firearm? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my firearm an antique firearm` IS
    `s 84(1) antique firearm` (JUST `it is a firearm`) `the year in which it was manufactured` `it was designed to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition` `it has been redesigned to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be an antique firearm`)

@ref s 84(1) "prohibited device"
@export Under section 84(1), is my device a prohibited device?
GIVEN `it is a component or part of a weapon, or an accessory for use with a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a component or part of a weapon, or an accessory for use with a weapon?
      `the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited device` IS A STRING @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited device? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `it is a handgun barrel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a handgun barrel?
      `the length of the handgun barrel in millimetres` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is a handgun barrel: how long is it in millimetres? Enter 0 if it is not.
      `the handgun barrel is prescribed as one the definition does not include` IS A STRING @desc If it is a handgun barrel: do the regulations prescribe it as one that the definition does not include? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `the handgun barrel is for use in International Shooting Union competitions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a handgun barrel: is it for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union?
      `it is designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm?
      `it is a cartridge magazine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a cartridge magazine: a device or container from which ammunition may be fed into the firing chamber of a firearm?
      `it is a replica firearm` IS A STRING @desc Is it a replica firearm (see the question about replica firearms)? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my device a prohibited device` IS
    `s 84(1) prohibited device` `it is a component or part of a weapon, or an accessory for use with a weapon` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited device`) `it is a handgun barrel` `the length of the handgun barrel in millimetres` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the handgun barrel is prescribed as one the definition does not include`) `the handgun barrel is for use in International Shooting Union competitions` `it is designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm` (`s 84(1) cartridge magazine` `it is a cartridge magazine`) (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `it is a replica firearm`)

@ref s 84(1) "prohibited weapon"
@export Under section 84(1), is my weapon a prohibited weapon?
GIVEN `it is a knife with a blade that opens automatically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a knife that has a blade that opens automatically by gravity or centrifugal force or by hand pressure applied to a button, spring or other device in or attached to the handle?
      `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use in causing death or injury to any person?
      `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person?
      `it is a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a firearm?
      `the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited weapon` IS A STRING @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited weapon? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my weapon a prohibited weapon` IS
    `s 84(1) prohibited weapon` `it is a knife with a blade that opens automatically` (`s 2 weapon` `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` (JUST `it is a firearm`) FALSE FALSE) (JUST `it is a firearm`) (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be a prohibited weapon`)

@ref s 84(1) "restricted weapon"
@export Under section 84(1), is my weapon a restricted weapon?
GIVEN `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use in causing death or injury to any person?
      `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person?
      `it is a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a firearm?
      `the regulations prescribe it to be a restricted weapon` IS A STRING @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be a restricted weapon? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my weapon a restricted weapon` IS
    `s 84(1) restricted weapon` (`s 2 weapon` `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` (JUST `it is a firearm`) FALSE FALSE) (JUST `it is a firearm`) (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be a restricted weapon`)

@ref s 84(1) "prohibited ammunition", "ammunition"
@export Under section 84(1), is my thing prohibited ammunition?
GIVEN `the kind of ammunition` IS A STRING @desc Is it a cartridge containing a projectile designed to be discharged from a firearm? Choose one of: "cartridge", "caseless cartridge", "shot shell" or "none of these".
      `it is a projectile of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a projectile of any kind?
      `the regulations prescribe it to be prohibited ammunition` IS A STRING @desc Do the regulations prescribe it to be prohibited ammunition? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my thing prohibited ammunition` IS
    `s 84(1) prohibited ammunition` (`s 84(1) ammunition` `the ammunition kind named`) `it is a projectile of any kind` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be prohibited ammunition`)
    WHERE
        `the ammunition kind named` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of ammunition` EQUALS "cartridge" THEN `s 84(1) ammunition: a cartridge containing a projectile designed to be discharged from a firearm`
                IF `the kind of ammunition` EQUALS "caseless cartridge" THEN `s 84(1) ammunition: a caseless cartridge`
                IF `the kind of ammunition` EQUALS "shot shell" THEN `s 84(1) ammunition: a shot shell`
                OTHERWISE `s 84(1) ammunition: a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 84(1) "replica firearm"
@export Under section 84(1), is my device a replica firearm?
GIVEN `it is designed or intended to exactly resemble a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a device designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, a firearm?
      `the muzzle velocity in metres per second` IS A NUMBER @desc At what muzzle velocity, in metres per second, is the firearm it resembles designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile?
      `the muzzle energy in joules` IS A NUMBER @desc At what muzzle energy, in joules, is the firearm it resembles designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile?
      `it is itself a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the device itself a firearm in the sense of section 2?
      `the firearm it resembles is an antique firearm` IS A STRING @desc Is the firearm it resembles an antique firearm (see the question about antique firearms)? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my device a replica firearm` IS
    `s 84(1) replica firearm` `it is designed or intended to exactly resemble a firearm` `the muzzle velocity in metres per second` `the muzzle energy in joules` (JUST `it is itself a firearm`) (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the firearm it resembles is an antique firearm`)

@ref s 84(1) "cross-bow"
@export Under section 84(1), is my device a cross-bow?
GIVEN `it has a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a device with a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock?
      `it is designed to propel an arrow, bolt or quarrel on a trajectory guided by a barrel or groove` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it designed to propel an arrow, a bolt, a quarrel or any similar projectile on a trajectory guided by a barrel or groove?
      `it is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my device a cross-bow` IS
    `s 84(1) cross-bow` `it has a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock` `it is designed to propel an arrow, bolt or quarrel on a trajectory guided by a barrel or groove` `it is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death`

@ref s 84(1) "firearm part"
@export Under section 84(1), is my thing a firearm part?
GIVEN `it is a barrel for a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a barrel for a firearm?
      `it is a slide for a handgun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a slide for a handgun?
      `the regulations prescribe it to be a firearm part` IS A STRING @desc If it is some other part: do the regulations prescribe it to be a firearm part? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `it is designed exclusively for a firearm that subsection 84(3) deems not to be a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a barrel or a slide: is it designed exclusively for use on a firearm that subsection 84(3) deems not to be a firearm?
      `the regulations otherwise prescribe that it is a firearm part` IS A STRING @desc If it is such a barrel or slide: do the regulations otherwise prescribe that it is a firearm part? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is my thing a firearm part` IS
    `s 84(1) firearm part` `it is a barrel for a firearm` `it is a slide for a handgun` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations prescribe it to be a firearm part`) `it is designed exclusively for a firearm that subsection 84(3) deems not to be a firearm` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the regulations otherwise prescribe that it is a firearm part`)

@ref s 84(3)
@export Under section 84(3), does the Code deem my weapon not to be a firearm for the purposes of the section I am asking about?
GIVEN `the section you are asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code are you asking about, for example 91 or 117.03?
      `the purpose is a provision of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose a provision of the Firearms Act?
      `it is an antique firearm` IS A STRING @desc Is the weapon an antique firearm (see the question about antique firearms)? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `it is a device designed exclusively for signalling, distress, blank cartridges or industrial projectiles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a device designed exclusively for signalling, for notifying of distress, for firing blank cartridges or for firing stud cartridges, explosive-driven rivets or other industrial projectiles?
      `the person in possession intends it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person in possession of it intend it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed?
      `it is a shooting device designed exclusively for slaughtering, tranquillizing or lines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a shooting device designed exclusively for the slaughtering of domestic animals, the tranquillizing of animals or the discharging of projectiles with lines attached to them?
      `it is any other barrelled weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it any other barrelled weapon?
      `it is proved that it is not designed or adapted to discharge such a projectile` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that it is not designed or adapted to discharge a projectile at a muzzle velocity exceeding 152.4 metres per second or a muzzle energy exceeding 5.7 joules, or a projectile designed or adapted to attain such a velocity or energy?
      `the muzzle velocity in metres per second` IS A NUMBER @desc At what muzzle velocity, in metres per second, is it designed or adapted to discharge a projectile?
      `the muzzle energy in joules` IS A NUMBER @desc At what muzzle energy, in joules, is it designed or adapted to discharge a projectile?
      `the velocity in metres per second that a projectile it discharges is designed or adapted to attain` IS A NUMBER @desc What velocity, in metres per second, is a projectile it discharges designed or adapted to attain?
      `the energy in joules that a projectile it discharges is designed or adapted to attain` IS A NUMBER @desc What energy, in joules, is a projectile it discharges designed or adapted to attain?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(3), does the Code deem my weapon not to be a firearm for the purposes of the section I am asking about` IS
    `s 84(3) the weapon is deemed not to be a firearm for the purposes of the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section you are asking about`, "") `the purpose is a provision of the Firearms Act` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `it is an antique firearm`) `it is a device designed exclusively for signalling, distress, blank cartridges or industrial projectiles` `the person in possession intends it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed` `it is a shooting device designed exclusively for slaughtering, tranquillizing or lines` `it is any other barrelled weapon` `it is proved that it is not designed or adapted to discharge such a projectile` `the muzzle velocity in metres per second` `the muzzle energy in joules` `the velocity in metres per second that a projectile it discharges is designed or adapted to attain` `the energy in joules that a projectile it discharges is designed or adapted to attain`

@ref s 84(4)(a)
@export Under section 84(4), am I the holder of an authorization or a licence?
GIVEN `the authorization or licence has been issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authorization or licence been issued to you?
      `I continue to hold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you continue to hold it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(4), am I the holder of an authorization or a licence` IS
    `s 84(4)(a) the person is the holder of an authorization or a licence` `the authorization or licence has been issued to me` `I continue to hold it`

@ref s 84(4)(b)
@export Under section 84(4), am I the holder of a registration certificate for a firearm?
GIVEN `the registration certificate has been issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registration certificate been issued to you?
      `I continue to hold the registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you continue to hold it?
      `I possess the registration certificate with the permission of its lawful holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you possess the registration certificate with the permission of its lawful holder?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(4), am I the holder of a registration certificate for a firearm` IS
    `s 84(4)(b) the person is the holder of a registration certificate for a firearm` `the registration certificate has been issued to me` `I continue to hold the registration certificate` `I possess the registration certificate with the permission of its lawful holder`

@ref s 84(5)
@export Under section 84(5), must my earlier conviction be counted as an earlier offence in deciding whether I have committed a second or subsequent offence?
GIVEN `the section for which the question is asked` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section are you being sentenced: 99, 100 or 103?
      `the subsection for which the question is asked` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection of that section, for example "(2)"?
      `the section of the earlier offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code were you earlier convicted?
      `the subsection of the earlier offence` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection of that section, for example "(1)"? Use "" if none.
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a firearm used in the commission of the earlier offence?
      `the day you were convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the earlier offence?
      `the day you were convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed?
      `the number of days you spent in custody between those two days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did you spend in custody between those two days?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(5), must my earlier conviction be counted as an earlier offence in deciding whether I have committed a second or subsequent offence` IS
    `s 84(5) the earlier offence is to be considered as an earlier offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section for which the question is asked`, `the subsection for which the question is asked`) (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the earlier offence`, `the subsection of the earlier offence`) `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` `the day you were convicted of the earlier offence` `the day you were convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` `the number of days you spent in custody between those two days`

@ref s 84(6)
@export Under section 84(6), was my first offence the earlier offence for the purposes of subsection (5)?
GIVEN `the day I committed the first offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you commit the first offence?
      `the day I was convicted of the first offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the first offence?
      `the day I committed the second offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you commit the second offence?
      `the day I was convicted of the second offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the second offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(6), was my first offence the earlier offence for the purposes of subsection (5)` IS
    `s 84(6) offence one is the earlier offence for the purposes of subsection (5)` (`s 84(6) offence` OF `the day I committed the first offence`, `the day I was convicted of the first offence`) (`s 84(6) offence` OF `the day I committed the second offence`, `the day I was convicted of the second offence`)

@ref s 84(1) "transfer"
@export Under section 84(1), is what I did a transfer?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A STRING @desc What did you do? Choose one of: "sell", "provide", "barter", "give", "lend", "rent", "send", "transport", "ship", "distribute", "deliver" or "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is what I did a transfer` IS
    `s 84(1) transfer` (`ccc4 seat: the transfer act named by` `what I did`)
    WHERE
        `ccc4 seat: the transfer act named by` MEANS
            GIVEN word IS A STRING
            YIELD
                BRANCH
                    IF word EQUALS "sell" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: sell`
                    IF word EQUALS "provide" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: provide`
                    IF word EQUALS "barter" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: barter`
                    IF word EQUALS "give" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: give`
                    IF word EQUALS "lend" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: lend`
                    IF word EQUALS "rent" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: rent`
                    IF word EQUALS "send" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: send`
                    IF word EQUALS "transport" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: transport`
                    IF word EQUALS "ship" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: ship`
                    IF word EQUALS "distribute" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: distribute`
                    IF word EQUALS "deliver" THEN `s 84(1) transfer: deliver`
                    OTHERWISE `s 84(1) transfer: an act that is none of those`

@ref s 84(1) "export"
@export Under section 84(1), is what I did an export?
GIVEN `it is an export from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you export it from Canada?
      `it is the exportation of goods imported into Canada and shipped in transit through Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you export goods from Canada that were imported into Canada and shipped in transit through Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is what I did an export` IS
    `s 84(1) export` `it is an export from Canada` `it is the exportation of goods imported into Canada and shipped in transit through Canada`

@ref s 84(1) "import"
@export Under section 84(1), is what I did an import?
GIVEN `it is an import into Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you import it into Canada?
      `it is the importation of goods shipped in transit through Canada and exported from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you import into Canada goods that are shipped in transit through Canada and exported from Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is what I did an import` IS
    `s 84(1) import` `it is an import into Canada` `it is the importation of goods shipped in transit through Canada and exported from Canada`

@ref s 84(1) "prohibition order"
@export Under section 84(1), is the order I am subject to a prohibition order?
GIVEN `it is an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament?
      `it prohibits me from possessing any of the listed things` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it prohibit you from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 84(1), is the order I am subject to a prohibition order` IS
    `s 84(1) prohibition order` `it is an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` `it prohibits me from possessing any of the listed things`

§ `Use Offences (sections 85 to 87): did what I did with a firearm make me guilty of an offence, and how grave is it?`
-- Situation: the person used, carried, handled, stored or pointed a firearm.  Ask this group only if they did.

@ref s 85(1)
@export Under section 85(1), have I committed an offence by using a firearm in the commission of an offence?
GIVEN `the kind of thing I used` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I used it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it?
      `the section of the indictable offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code is the indictable offence you were committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after?
      `the subsection of the indictable offence` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection of that section, for example "(1)"? Use "" if none.
      `I used it while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it while committing an indictable offence?
      `I used it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it while attempting to commit an indictable offence?
      `I used it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 85(1), have I committed an offence by using a firearm in the commission of an offence` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing I used`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 85(1) the person commits an offence by using a firearm in the commission of an offence` k `I used it` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the indictable offence`, `the subsection of the indictable offence`) `I used it while committing an indictable offence` `I used it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` `I used it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence`

@ref s 85(2)
@export Under section 85(2), have I committed an offence by using an imitation firearm in the commission of an offence?
GIVEN `it imitates a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it imitate a firearm?
      `it is a replica firearm` IS A STRING @desc Is it a replica firearm (see the question about replica firearms)? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `I used it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it?
      `I used it while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it while committing an indictable offence?
      `I used it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it while attempting to commit an indictable offence?
      `I used it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 85(2), have I committed an offence by using an imitation firearm in the commission of an offence` IS
    `s 85(2) the person commits an offence by using an imitation firearm in the commission of an offence` (`s 84(1) imitation firearm` `it imitates a firearm` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `it is a replica firearm`)) `I used it` `I used it while committing an indictable offence` `I used it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` `I used it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence`

@export Under section 85(3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 85(3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 85(3) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 85(3) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 85(4)
@export Under section 85(4), must my sentence for using a firearm or an imitation firearm be served consecutively to my other punishment or sentence?
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence imposed for an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2)?
      `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there another punishment imposed on you for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events?
      `I am subject to another sentence when this one is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to another sentence at the time this one is imposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 85(4), must my sentence for using a firearm or an imitation firearm be served consecutively to my other punishment or sentence` IS
    `s 85(4) the sentence must be served consecutively to the other punishment or sentence` `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2)` `the other punishment is for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` `I am subject to another sentence when this one is imposed`

@ref s 86(1)
@export Under section 86(1), have I committed an offence of careless use of a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I used, carried, handled, shipped, transported or stored it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use, carry, handle, ship, transport or store it?
      `I did so in a careless manner or without reasonable precautions for the safety of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so in a careless manner or without reasonable precautions for the safety of other persons?
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86(1), have I committed an offence of careless use of a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 86(1) the person commits an offence of careless use of a firearm, etc.` k `I used, carried, handled, shipped, transported or stored it` `I did so in a careless manner or without reasonable precautions for the safety of other persons` `I had a lawful excuse`

@ref s 86(2)
@export Under section 86(2), have I committed an offence by contravening a storage regulation?
GIVEN `I contravened a regulation made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene a regulation made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act?
      `the regulation is about storage, handling, transportation, shipping, display, advertising or mail-order sales of firearms or restricted weapons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the regulation about the storage, handling, transportation, shipping, display, advertising or mail-order sales of firearms or restricted weapons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 86(2), have I committed an offence by contravening a storage regulation` IS
    `s 86(2) the person commits an offence by contravening a storage regulation, etc.` `I contravened a regulation made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act` `the regulation is about storage, handling, transportation, shipping, display, advertising or mail-order sales of firearms or restricted weapons`

@ref s 86(3)
@export Under section 86(3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVEN `this is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 86(3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 86(3) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 86(3)(a) the punishment on indictment` `this is a second or subsequent offence`), NOTHING   -- the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 87(1)
@export Under section 87(1), have I committed the offence of pointing a firearm?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I pointed it at another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you point it at another person (whether or not it was loaded)?
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87(1), have I committed the offence of pointing a firearm` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 87(1) the person commits the offence of pointing a firearm` k `I pointed it at another person` `I had a lawful excuse`

@export Under section 87(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 87(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 87(2) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 87(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

§ `Possession Offences (sections 88 to 98.1): did what I possessed or carried make me guilty of an offence, and how grave is it?`
-- Situation: the person possessed, carried or kept a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition, or broke into a place for a firearm.

@ref s 88(1)
@export Under section 88(1), have I committed an offence by possessing a weapon for a dangerous purpose?
GIVEN `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use in causing death or injury to any person?
      `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person?
      `it is an imitation of a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an imitation of a weapon?
      `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I carried or possessed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry or possess it?
      `the purpose was dangerous to the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your purpose dangerous to the public peace?
      `the purpose was the committing of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your purpose the committing of an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 88(1), have I committed an offence by possessing a weapon for a dangerous purpose` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 88(1) the person commits an offence of possession of a weapon for a dangerous purpose` (`s 2 weapon` `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` (JUST (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` k)) FALSE TRUE) `it is an imitation of a weapon` k `I carried or possessed it` `the purpose was dangerous to the public peace` `the purpose was the committing of an offence`

@export Under section 88(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 88(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 88(2) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 88(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 89(1)
@export Under section 89(1), have I committed an offence by carrying a weapon while attending a public meeting?
GIVEN `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use in causing death or injury to any person?
      `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person?
      `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I carried it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry it?
      `I was attending or on the way to attend a public meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you attending, or on the way to attend, a public meeting?
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 89(1), have I committed an offence by carrying a weapon while attending a public meeting` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 89(1) the person commits an offence of carrying a weapon while attending a public meeting` (`s 2 weapon` `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` (JUST (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` k)) FALSE FALSE) k `I carried it` `I was attending or on the way to attend a public meeting` `I had a lawful excuse`

@export Under section 89(2), how is the offence classified?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 89(2), how is the offence classified` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 89(2) the class of the offence`, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 90(1)
@export Under section 90(1), have I committed an offence by carrying a concealed weapon?
GIVEN `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use in causing death or injury to any person?
      `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used, designed to be used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating any person?
      `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I carried it concealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry it concealed?
      `I am authorized under the Firearms Act to carry it concealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you authorized under the Firearms Act to carry it concealed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 90(1), have I committed an offence by carrying a concealed weapon` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 90(1) the person commits an offence of carrying a concealed weapon` (`s 2 weapon` `it is used, designed or intended to cause death or injury` `it is used, designed or intended to threaten or intimidate` (JUST (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` k)) FALSE FALSE) k `I carried it concealed` `I am authorized under the Firearms Act to carry it concealed`

@export Under section 90(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
