@ref s 94(1)
@export Under section 94(1), have I committed an offence as an occupant of a motor vehicle in which I knew there was a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition?
GIVEN `it is a vehicle drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vehicle drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power?
      `it is railway equipment` IS A STRING @desc Is the vehicle railway equipment? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `I am an occupant of the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an occupant of the vehicle?
      `the kind of thing in the vehicle` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I knew there was such a thing in the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that there was such a thing in the vehicle?
      `I or another occupant holds a licence under which that occupant may possess the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a firearm: did you or another occupant hold a licence under which that occupant may possess the firearm?
      `I or another occupant holds an authorization and a registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a prohibited or restricted firearm: did you or another occupant hold an authorization and a registration certificate for it?
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant held a licence for the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a firearm: did you have reasonable grounds to believe that another occupant held a licence under which that occupant may possess the firearm?
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant held an authorization and a registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a prohibited or restricted firearm: did you have reasonable grounds to believe that another occupant held an authorization and a registration certificate for it?
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant could not be convicted by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable grounds to believe that another occupant was a person who could not be convicted of an offence under the Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament?
      `I or another occupant holds an authorization or a licence to transport it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a weapon, device or ammunition: did you or another occupant hold an authorization or a licence under which that occupant may transport it?
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant held an authorization or a licence to transport it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a weapon, device or ammunition: did you have reasonable grounds to believe that another occupant held an authorization or a licence under which that occupant may transport it?
      `on becoming aware I attempted to leave the vehicle to the extent feasible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On becoming aware of it, did you attempt to leave the vehicle, to the extent that it was feasible to do so?
      `on becoming aware I actually left the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On becoming aware of it, did you actually leave the vehicle?
      `an occupant came into possession of it by the operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, or any other occupant, come into possession of it by the operation of law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 94(1), have I committed an offence as an occupant of a motor vehicle in which I knew there was a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing in the vehicle`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 94(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized possession in a motor vehicle` (`s 2 motor vehicle` `it is a vehicle drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `it is railway equipment`)) `I am an occupant of the vehicle` k `I knew there was such a thing in the vehicle` (`s 94(1)(a) the occupant is within the exception for a firearm` k `I or another occupant holds a licence under which that occupant may possess the firearm` `I or another occupant holds an authorization and a registration certificate for it` `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant held a licence for the firearm` `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant held an authorization and a registration certificate for it` `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant could not be convicted by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or another Act`) (`s 94(1)(b) the occupant is within the exception for a weapon, device or ammunition` `I or another occupant holds an authorization or a licence to transport it` `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant held an authorization or a licence to transport it` `I had reasonable grounds to believe another occupant could not be convicted by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or another Act`) (`s 94(3) subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant who attempted to leave or left the motor vehicle` `on becoming aware I attempted to leave the vehicle to the extent feasible` `on becoming aware I actually left the vehicle`) (`s 94(4) subsection (1) does not apply when an occupant came into possession by the operation of law` `an occupant came into possession of it by the operation of law`)

