    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 98.1 the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 98.1 the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the penalty on summary conviction: this offence is indictable only, so there is none

§ `Trafficking, Assembling, Computer Data, Export and Import Offences (sections 99 to 104.1): did what I made, sold, transferred, possessed, imported or exported make me guilty of an offence, and how grave is it?`
-- Situation: the person made, transferred, offered, possessed for transfer, imported, exported or altered a firearm, weapon, device, part, ammunition or computer data.

@ref s 99(1)
@export Under section 99(1), have I committed the offence of weapons trafficking?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I manufactured it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you manufacture it?
      `I transferred it` IS A STRING @desc Did you transfer it (sell, provide, barter, give, lend, rent, send, transport, ship, distribute or deliver), whether or not for consideration? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `I offered to manufacture or transfer it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you offer to manufacture or transfer it?
      `I knew that I was not authorized to do so under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that you were not authorized to do so under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 99(1), have I committed the offence of weapons trafficking` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 99(1) the person commits an offence of weapons trafficking` k `I manufactured it` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `I transferred it`) `I offered to manufacture or transfer it` `I knew that I was not authorized to do so under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations`

@ref 99(2) and (3)
@export Under section 99(2) and (3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVEN `the kind of thing the object in question is` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `this is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 99(2) and (3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing the object in question is`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN
        JUST (`ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 99(2) the class of the offence`, (`ccc4 seat: the first punishment that is stated` (`s 99(2) the punishment when the object in question is a firearm, device, part or ammunition` k `this is a second or subsequent offence`) (`s 99(3) the punishment in any other case` k)), NOTHING)   -- the third field: no penalty on summary conviction is stated; this offence is indictable only

@ref s 100(1)
@export Under section 100(1), have I committed the offence of possession for the purpose of weapons trafficking?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you possess it?
      `I possess it for the purpose of transferring it` IS A STRING @desc Do you possess it for the purpose of transferring it, whether or not for consideration? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `I possess it for the purpose of offering to transfer it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you possess it for the purpose of offering to transfer it?
      `I know that I am not authorized to transfer it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that you are not authorized to transfer it under the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 100(1), have I committed the offence of possession for the purpose of weapons trafficking` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 100(1) the person commits an offence of possession for the purpose of weapons trafficking` k `I possess it` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `I possess it for the purpose of transferring it`) `I possess it for the purpose of offering to transfer it` `I know that I am not authorized to transfer it`

@ref 100(2) and (3)
@export Under section 100(2) and (3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVEN `the kind of thing the object in question is` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `this is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 100(2) and (3), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing the object in question is`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN
        JUST (`ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 100(2) the class of the offence`, (`ccc4 seat: the first punishment that is stated` (`s 100(2) the punishment when the object in question is a firearm, device, part or ammunition` k `this is a second or subsequent offence`) (`s 100(3) the punishment in any other case` k)), NOTHING)   -- the third field: no penalty on summary conviction is stated; this offence is indictable only

@ref s 101(1)
@export Under section 101(1), have I committed an offence by transferring a firearm, weapon, device, part or ammunition without authority?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I transferred it to a person` IS A STRING @desc Did you transfer it (sell, provide, barter, give, lend, rent, send, transport, ship, distribute or deliver) to any person? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `the transfer was under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transfer under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 101(1), have I committed an offence by transferring a firearm, weapon, device, part or ammunition without authority` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 101(1) the person commits an offence of transfer without authority` k (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `I transferred it to a person`) `the transfer was under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations`

@export Under section 101(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
