DECIDE `Under section 104.1(1), have I committed an offence by altering a cartridge magazine so that it becomes a prohibited device` IS
    `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the thing I altered is a cartridge magazine`) `before the alteration it was not a prohibited device` `I altered it` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `after the alteration it is a prohibited device`) `I had a lawful excuse`

@export Under section 104.1(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 104.1(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 104.1(2) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 104.1(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

§ `Lost, Destroyed or Defaced Weapons (sections 105 to 108): did I fail to report, or report falsely, or tamper with a serial number?`
-- Situation: the person lost, found or destroyed a firearm, weapon, device, ammunition, licence or certificate, or made a report about it, or its serial number was altered.

@ref s 105(1)(a)
@export Under section 105(1)(a), have I committed an offence by not reporting the loss or theft of a firearm, weapon, device, ammunition or document?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate?
      `I lost it or it was stolen from my possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose it, or was it stolen from your possession?
      `I did not with reasonable despatch report the loss to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to report the loss with reasonable despatch to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(1)(a), have I committed an offence by not reporting the loss or theft of a firearm, weapon, device, ammunition or document` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` k `it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` `I lost it or it was stolen from my possession` `I did not with reasonable despatch report the loss to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer`

@ref s 105(1)(b)
@export Under section 105(1)(b), have I committed an offence by not delivering up or reporting a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition that I found?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I found it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you find it?
      `I had reasonable grounds to believe that it had been lost or abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable grounds to believe that it had been lost or abandoned?
      `I did not with reasonable despatch deliver it or report the finding to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to deliver it, or report the finding, with reasonable despatch to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(1)(b), have I committed an offence by not delivering up or reporting a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition that I found` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` k `I found it` `I had reasonable grounds to believe that it had been lost or abandoned` `I did not with reasonable despatch deliver it or report the finding to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer`

@export Under section 105(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 105(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 105(2) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 105(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 106(1)
@export Under section 106(1), have I committed an offence by not reporting the destruction of a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I destroyed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you destroy it?
      `I became aware of its destruction and it was in my possession before its destruction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become aware of its destruction, and was it in your possession before its destruction?
      `I did not with reasonable despatch report the destruction to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to report the destruction with reasonable despatch to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 106(1), have I committed an offence by not reporting the destruction of a firearm, weapon, device or ammunition` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` k `I destroyed it` `I became aware of its destruction and it was in my possession before its destruction` `I did not with reasonable despatch report the destruction to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer`

@export Under section 106(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 106(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 106(2) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 106(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 107(1)
@export Under section 107(1), have I committed an offence by knowingly making a false report or statement about a loss, theft or destruction?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate?
      `I made a report or statement before a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a report or statement before a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer?
      `it concerns the loss, theft or destruction of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it concern the loss, theft or destruction of it?
      `it is false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it false?
      `I made it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it knowingly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(1), have I committed an offence by knowingly making a false report or statement about a loss, theft or destruction` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` k `it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate` `I made a report or statement before a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer` `it concerns the loss, theft or destruction of it` `it is false` `I made it knowingly`

@export Under section 107(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 107(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 107(2) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 107(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 107(3)
@export Under section 107(3), is what I said a report or statement?
GIVEN `what I said` IS A STRING @desc What did you assert? Choose one of: "fact", "opinion", "belief", "knowledge" or "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(3), is what I said a report or statement` IS
    `s 107(3) report or statement` (`the assertion named`)
    WHERE
        `the assertion named` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `what I said` EQUALS "fact" THEN `s 107(3) assertion: of fact`
                IF `what I said` EQUALS "opinion" THEN `s 107(3) assertion: of opinion`
                IF `what I said` EQUALS "belief" THEN `s 107(3) assertion: of belief`
                IF `what I said` EQUALS "knowledge" THEN `s 107(3) assertion: of knowledge`
                OTHERWISE `s 107(3) assertion: a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 108(1)
@export Under section 108(1), have I committed an offence of tampering with a serial number?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `I altered, defaced or removed a serial number on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you alter, deface or remove a serial number on it?
      `I possess it knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you possess it knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed?
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(1), have I committed an offence of tampering with a serial number` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` k `I altered, defaced or removed a serial number on it` `I possess it knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` `I had a lawful excuse`

@export Under section 108(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment?
GIVETH A `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence`
DECIDE `Under section 108(2), how is the offence classified and what is the punishment if I am prosecuted by indictment` IS
    `ccc4 seat: the penalty of the offence` OF `s 108(2) the class of the offence`, JUST (`s 108(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`), NOTHING   -- the third field: the penalty on summary conviction is not stated in this section; it is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes

@ref s 108(3)
@export Under section 108(3), am I not guilty of an offence under paragraph 108(1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `the serial number has been replaced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the serial number been replaced?
      `a registration certificate setting out the new serial number has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a registration certificate in respect of the firearm been issued setting out a new serial number for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(3), am I not guilty of an offence under paragraph 108(1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` k `the serial number has been replaced` `a registration certificate setting out the new serial number has been issued`

@ref s 108(4)
@export Under section 108(4), is the evidence that I possess a firearm with an obliterated serial number proof that I knew it had been altered?
GIVEN `I possess the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you possess the firearm?
      `the serial number has been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the serial number been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary (that you did not know)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(4), is the evidence that I possess a firearm with an obliterated serial number proof that I knew it had been altered` IS
    `s 108(4) the evidence is proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` `I possess the firearm` `the serial number has been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time` `there is evidence to the contrary`

§ `Prohibition Orders (sections 109 to 110.3): must or may a court forbid me to possess firearms and other weapons, for how long, and what can be done to me and to the records?`
-- Situation: the person has been convicted of, or discharged under section 730 of, an offence, or someone has applied for an emergency order against them.  Ask only if so.

@ref s 109(1)(a); s 3.01
@export Under section 109(1)(a), is my offence one in which violence was used and for which I may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more?
GIVEN `the class of my offence` IS A STRING @desc Is the offence indictable only, punishable on summary conviction only, or either? Choose one of: "indictable only", "summary conviction only" or "either".
      `the mode of proceeding` IS A STRING @desc How is it being prosecuted? Choose one of: "by indictment" or "on summary conviction".
      `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was violence against a person used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence?
      `the kind of offence for section 3.01` IS A STRING @desc Is the offence one that section 3.01 counts as one in which violence is used? Choose one of: "of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose", "criminal harassment (section 264)", "trafficking in persons (section 279.01)", "trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years (section 279.011)" or "none of these".
      `the offence carries imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence carry imprisonment for life?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in whole years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in whole years? Enter 0 if it states none.
      `the longest term is "less a day"` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that term stated as "less a day" (for example two years less a day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1)(a), is my offence one in which violence was used and for which I may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the class named by` `the class of my offence`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST c THEN
        CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the mode of proceeding named by` `the mode of proceeding`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
        WHEN JUST m THEN `s 109(1)(a) the offence is one in which violence was used and for which the person may be sentenced to imprisonment for ten years or more` (`s 109(1) the offence is an indictable offence` c m) `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` (`ccc4 seat: section 3.01 counts the offence`) (`s 109(1)(a) the maximum imprisonment is ten years or more` `the maximum imprisonment`)
    WHERE
        `the maximum imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `the offence carries imprisonment for life`
            THEN `imprisonment for life`
            ELSE IF `the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in whole years` EQUALS 0
                 THEN `no imprisonment is stated`
                 ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`ccc4 seat: a length of time in whole years` `the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in whole years` `the longest term is "less a day"`)
        `ccc4 seat: section 3.01 counts the offence` MEANS `s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` (`the keel's offence kind`) (`s 3.01(2) subsection (1) applies with respect to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 109, "(1)"))
        `the keel's offence kind` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose" THEN `an offence that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "criminal harassment (section 264)" THEN `an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment)`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "trafficking in persons (section 279.01)" THEN `an offence under section 279.01 (trafficking in persons)`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years (section 279.011)" THEN `an offence under section 279.011 (trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years)`
                OTHERWISE `an offence that is none of those`

@ref s 109(1)(b)
@export Under section 109(1)(b), is my offence one that paragraph (b) names?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code were you convicted?
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection of that section, for example "(1)"? Use "" if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1)(b), is my offence one that paragraph (b) names` IS
    `s 109(1)(b) the offence is one of those the paragraph names` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)

@ref s 109(1)(c) and (c.1)
@export Under section 109(1)(c) and (c.1), is my offence one relating to a contravention of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act that the paragraphs name?
GIVEN `the Act` IS A STRING @desc Under which Act? Choose one of: "Controlled Drugs and Substances Act", "Cannabis Act" or "another Act".
      `the section of that Act` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of that Act?
      `the subsection of that section` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection, for example "(1)"? Use "" if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1)(c) and (c.1), is my offence one relating to a contravention of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act that the paragraphs name` IS
    `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (`s 109(1)(c) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act that the paragraph names` `the contravention`), (`s 109(1)(c.1) the offence relates to the contravention of a subsection of the Cannabis Act that the paragraph names` `the contravention`))
    WHERE
        `the contravention` MEANS `s 109(1) a contravention of another Act` OF `the Act named`, `the section of that Act`, `the subsection of that section`
        `the Act named` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the Act` EQUALS "Controlled Drugs and Substances Act" THEN `s 109(1) the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
                IF `the Act` EQUALS "Cannabis Act" THEN `s 109(1) the Cannabis Act`
                OTHERWISE `s 109(1) another Act of Parliament`

@ref s 109(1)(d)
@export Under section 109(1)(d), is my offence one that involves a thing I was already prohibited from possessing?
GIVEN `the kind of thing the offence involves` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence involve that thing, or is it the subject-matter of the offence?
      `at the time of the offence I was prohibited by an order from possessing any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the offence, were you prohibited by any order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament from possessing any such thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1)(d), is my offence one that involves a thing I was already prohibited from possessing` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing the offence involves`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 109(1)(d) the offence involves a thing the person was prohibited from possessing` k `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing` `at the time of the offence I was prohibited by an order from possessing any such thing`

@ref s 109(1)
@export Under section 109(1), must the court make a prohibition order against me?
GIVEN `how I come before the court` IS A STRING @desc Are you convicted, or discharged under section 730? Choose one of: "convicted", "discharged under section 730" or "neither".
      `my offence is referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c.1)` IS A STRING @desc Is your offence one referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1) (the questions under section 109(1)(a), (b) and (c) tell you)? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `my offence is within paragraph (d)` IS A STRING @desc Is your offence within paragraph 109(1)(d) (the question under section 109(1)(d) tells you)? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1), must the court make a prohibition order against me` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: how the person comes before the court named by` `how I come before the court`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST h THEN `s 109(1) the court must make a prohibition order` h (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `my offence is referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c.1)`) (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `my offence is within paragraph (d)`)

@ref s 109(2) and (3)
@export Under section 109(2) and (3), for how long must the order forbid me to possess the thing?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `this is my first conviction for or discharge from the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your first conviction for, or discharge from, the offence to which the order relates?
      `I am imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you imprisoned, or subject to imprisonment, for the offence?
      `the day of my release from imprisonment` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you released from imprisonment after conviction for the offence (by expiration of sentence, commencement of statutory release or grant of parole)? Give any date if you are not imprisoned.
      `the day of my conviction or discharge` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of, or discharged from, the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 109 period of the prohibition`
DECIDE `Under section 109(2) and (3), for how long must the order forbid me to possess the thing` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST k THEN `s 109(2) and (3) the period for which the order prohibits the thing` k `this is my first conviction for or discharge from the offence` `I am imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` `the day of my release from imprisonment` `the day of my conviction or discharge`

@ref s 109(4)
@export Under section 109(4), is what I received a release from imprisonment?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A STRING @desc How were you released from confinement? Choose one of: "expiration of sentence", "commencement of statutory release", "grant of parole" or "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(4), is what I received a release from imprisonment` IS
    `s 109(4) release from imprisonment` (`the release named`)
    WHERE
        `the release named` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `what happened` EQUALS "expiration of sentence" THEN `s 109(4) release: by reason of expiration of sentence`
                IF `what happened` EQUALS "commencement of statutory release" THEN `s 109(4) release: by reason of commencement of statutory release`
                IF `what happened` EQUALS "grant of parole" THEN `s 109(4) release: by reason of grant of parole`
                OTHERWISE `s 109(4) release: by reason of something else`

@ref s 109(5)
@export Under section 109(5), does the section I am asking about apply to an order made against me?
GIVEN `the section` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code are you asking about? Subsection 109(5) names sections 113 to 117.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(5), does the section I am asking about apply to an order made against me` IS
    `s 109(5) the section applies in respect of every order made under subsection (1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")

@ref s 110(1); s 3.01
@export Under section 110(1), must the court consider whether to make a prohibition order against me?
GIVEN `how I come before the court` IS A STRING @desc Are you convicted, or discharged under section 730? Choose one of: "convicted", "discharged under section 730" or "neither".
      `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was violence against a person used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence?
      `my offence is referred to in paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1)` IS A STRING @desc Is your offence one referred to in any of paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1) (see the questions under section 109(1))? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `the kind of thing the offence involves` IS A STRING @desc What kind of thing is it? Choose one of: "prohibited firearm", "restricted firearm", "non-restricted firearm", "prohibited weapon", "restricted weapon", "replica firearm", "prohibited device (other than a replica firearm)", "firearm part", "ammunition (other than prohibited ammunition)", "prohibited ammunition", "cross-bow", "explosive substance" or "none of these". The questions under section 84(1) tell you which class a firearm, device, weapon or ammunition is in.
      `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence involve that thing, or is it the subject-matter of the offence?
      `at the time of the offence I was prohibited by an order from possessing any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the offence, were you prohibited by any order from possessing any such thing?
      `the kind of offence for section 3.01` IS A STRING @desc Is the offence one that section 3.01 counts as one in which violence is used? Choose one of: "of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose", "criminal harassment (section 264)", "trafficking in persons (section 279.01)", "trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years (section 279.011)" or "none of these".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110(1), must the court consider whether to make a prohibition order against me` IS
    CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: how the person comes before the court named by` `how I come before the court`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
    WHEN JUST h THEN
        CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the kind of thing named by` `the kind of thing the offence involves`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the choice is not one of the words the question lists
        WHEN JUST k THEN `s 110(1) the court must consider whether it is desirable to make a prohibition order` h `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` (`s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` (`the keel's offence kind`) (`s 3.01(2) subsection (1) applies with respect to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 110, "(1)"))) (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `my offence is referred to in paragraphs 109(1)(a) to (c.1)`) k `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, that thing` `at the time of the offence I was prohibited by an order from possessing any such thing`
    WHERE
        `the keel's offence kind` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose" THEN `an offence that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "criminal harassment (section 264)" THEN `an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment)`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "trafficking in persons (section 279.01)" THEN `an offence under section 279.01 (trafficking in persons)`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years (section 279.011)" THEN `an offence under section 279.011 (trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years)`
                OTHERWISE `an offence that is none of those`

@ref s 110(1)
@export Under section 110(1), must the court make a prohibition order against me?
GIVEN `the court must consider whether it is desirable` IS A STRING @desc Must the court consider whether it is desirable to make a prohibition order (see the question under section 110(1))? Answer "yes", "no" or "not known".
      `the court decides that it is desirable in the interests of the safety of me or of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court decide that it is desirable, in the interests of the safety of you or of any other person, to make the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110(1), must the court make a prohibition order against me` IS
    `s 110(1) the court must make a prohibition order` (`ccc4 seat: yes, no or not known` `the court must consider whether it is desirable`) `the court decides that it is desirable in the interests of the safety of me or of any other person`

@ref s 110(2)
@export Under section 110(2), what is the latest day on which a discretionary prohibition order may end?
GIVEN `I am imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you imprisoned, or subject to imprisonment, for the offence?
      `the day of my release from imprisonment` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you released from imprisonment after conviction for the offence? Give any date if you are not imprisoned.
      `the day of my conviction or discharge` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of, or discharged from, the offence?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 110(2), what is the latest day on which a discretionary prohibition order may end` IS
    `s 110(2) the latest day on which the order may end` `I am imprisoned or subject to imprisonment for the offence` `the day of my release from imprisonment` `the day of my conviction or discharge`

@ref s 110(2.1); s 3.01
@export Under section 110(2.1), may a discretionary prohibition order be imposed on me for life or for any shorter duration?
GIVEN `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was violence used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence?
      `the kind of offence for section 3.01` IS A STRING @desc Is the offence one that section 3.01 counts as one in which violence is used? Choose one of: "of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose", "criminal harassment (section 264)", "trafficking in persons (section 279.01)", "trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years (section 279.011)" or "none of these".
      `the relationship of the person against whom violence was used` IS A STRING @desc Was the violence against your intimate partner? Choose one of: "current spouse", "former spouse", "current common-law partner", "former common-law partner", "current dating partner", "former dating partner", "some other relationship" or "none".
      `the violence was against a child or parent of me or of my intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the violence used, threatened or attempted against a child or parent of you or of your intimate partner?
      `the violence was against a person who resides with me or with my intimate partner, child or parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the violence used, threatened or attempted against any person who resides with you or with your intimate partner, child or parent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110(2.1), may a discretionary prohibition order be imposed on me for life or for any shorter duration` IS
    `s 110(2.1) the order may be imposed for life or for any shorter duration` `violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the offence` (`s 3.01(1) the offence counts as an offence in the commission of which violence is used, threatened or attempted against any person or class of persons` (`the keel's offence kind`) (`s 3.01(2) subsection (1) applies with respect to the provision` (`Provision of the Code` OF 110, "(2.1)"))) (`the intimate partner answer`) `the violence was against a child or parent of me or of my intimate partner` `the violence was against a person who resides with me or with my intimate partner, child or parent`
    WHERE
        `the intimate partner answer` MEANS
            CONSIDER `ccc4 seat: the relationship named by` `the relationship of the person against whom violence was used`
            WHEN JUST r THEN `s 2 intimate partner` r
            WHEN NOTHING THEN IF `the relationship of the person against whom violence was used` EQUALS "none" THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING   -- an input value: "none" is the person's own answer
        `the keel's offence kind` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose" THEN `an offence that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "criminal harassment (section 264)" THEN `an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment)`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "trafficking in persons (section 279.01)" THEN `an offence under section 279.01 (trafficking in persons)`
                IF `the kind of offence for section 3.01` EQUALS "trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years (section 279.011)" THEN `an offence under section 279.011 (trafficking of a person under the age of 18 years)`
                OTHERWISE `an offence that is none of those`

@ref s 110(3)
@export Under section 110(3), must the court give reasons for not making a prohibition order or for not forbidding everything?
GIVEN `the court does not make an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court decline to make an order under subsection 110(1)?
      `the court makes an order but does not forbid everything` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court make an order but not forbid the possession of everything referred to in subsection 110(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110(3), must the court give reasons for not making a prohibition order or for not forbidding everything` IS
    `s 110(3) the court must include in the record a statement of its reasons` `the court does not make an order` `the court makes an order but does not forbid everything`

@ref s 110.1(1)
@export Under section 110.1(1), may someone apply, without notice to me, for an emergency prohibition order against me?
GIVEN `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of safety that I possess any such thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the applicant believe on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable, in the interests of the safety of you or of any other person, that you should possess any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(1), may someone apply, without notice to me, for an emergency prohibition order against me` IS
    `s 110.1(1) any person may make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an order` `the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of safety that I possess any such thing`

@ref s 110.1(2)
@export Under section 110.1(2), may the provincial court judge hear the application against me in private?
GIVEN `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge consider that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(2), may the provincial court judge hear the application against me in private` IS
    `s 110.1(2) the provincial court judge may hold the hearing in private` `the judge considers that it is necessary to protect the security of the applicant or of anyone known to the applicant`

@ref s 110.1(3)
@export Under section 110.1(3), must the provincial court judge make an emergency prohibition order against me?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection 110.1(1) exist?
      `the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(3), must the provincial court judge make an emergency prohibition order against me` IS
    `s 110.1(3) the provincial court judge must make an emergency prohibition order` `the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` `the judge is satisfied that an order should be made without delay to ensure the immediate protection of any person`

@ref s 110.1(3)
@export Under section 110.1(3), is the period the order is for within the limit of thirty days?
GIVEN `the years in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years is the period specified in the order?
      `the months in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months is the period specified in the order, in addition?
      `the days in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the period specified in the order, in addition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(3), is the period the order is for within the limit of thirty days` IS
    `s 110.1(3) the period specified in the order is within the limit of thirty days` (`Length of time` OF `the years in the period`, `the months in the period`, `the days in the period`, FALSE)

@ref s 110.1(4)
@export Under section 110.1(4), must a copy of the emergency order be served on me?
GIVEN `an order has been made against me under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made against you under subsection 110.1(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(4), must a copy of the emergency order be served on me` IS
    `s 110.1(4) a copy of the order must be served on the person to whom it is addressed` `an order has been made against me under subsection 110.1(3)`

@ref s 110.1(5)
@export Under section 110.1(5), may a provincial court judge issue a warrant to search for and seize the things I am forbidden to possess?
GIVEN `I am subject to an order made under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to an order made under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `the judge is satisfied on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe I possess a prohibited thing in a building, receptacle or place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that you possess, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order?
      `the judge is satisfied on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of safety for me to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of safety, for you to possess the thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(5), may a provincial court judge issue a warrant to search for and seize the things I am forbidden to possess` IS
    `s 110.1(5) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant to search and seize` `I am subject to an order made under subsection 110.1(3)` `the judge is satisfied on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe I possess a prohibited thing in a building, receptacle or place` `the judge is satisfied on oath that it is not desirable in the interests of safety for me to possess it`

@ref s 110.1(6)
@export Under section 110.1(6), may a peace officer search for and seize the things I am forbidden to possess without a warrant?
GIVEN `I am subject to an order made under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to an order made under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable for me to possess a prohibited thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the peace officer satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable, in the interests of safety, for you to possess a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order?
      `the grounds for obtaining a warrant exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection 110.1(5) exist?
      `by reason of a possible danger it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of a possible danger to the safety of you or of any other person, would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(6), may a peace officer search for and seize the things I am forbidden to possess without a warrant` IS
    `s 110.1(6) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` `I am subject to an order made under subsection 110.1(3)` `the peace officer is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is not desirable for me to possess a prohibited thing` `the grounds for obtaining a warrant exist` `by reason of a possible danger it would not be practicable to obtain a warrant`

@ref s 110.1(7)
@export Under section 110.1(7), must the peace officer who searched report to a justice?
GIVEN `the peace officer executed a warrant referred to in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer execute a warrant referred to in subsection 110.1(5)?
      `the peace officer conducted a search without a warrant under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer conduct a search without a warrant under subsection 110.1(6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(7), must the peace officer who searched report to a justice` IS
    `s 110.1(7) the peace officer must make a report to a justice` `the peace officer executed a warrant referred to in subsection (5)` `the peace officer conducted a search without a warrant under subsection (6)`

@ref s 110.1(8)
@export Under section 110.1(8), when must the things seized from me or surrendered by me be returned to me?
GIVEN `a date is fixed for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a date been fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) in respect of you?
      `an order is made against me under subsection 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made against you under subsection 111(5)?
      `the order made against me under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the order made against you under subsection 110.1(3) been revoked?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 110.1(8) the occasion for returning the things and documents`
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(8), when must the things seized from me or surrendered by me be returned to me` IS
    `s 110.1(8) the occasion on which the things and documents must be returned to the person` `a date is fixed for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` `an order is made against me under subsection 111(5)` `the order made against me under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked`

@ref s 110.1(9)
@export Under section 110.1(9), does the section I am asking about apply to the emergency order made against me?
GIVEN `the section` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code are you asking about? Subsection 110.1(9) names sections 113, 114 and 116.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(9), does the section I am asking about apply to the emergency order made against me` IS
    `s 110.1(9) the section applies in respect of every order made under subsection (3)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")

@ref s 110.1(10)
@export Under section 110.1(10), is the judge a provincial court judge within the meaning of the sections it names?
GIVEN `the section` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section are you asking about: 110.1, 110.4, 111, 112, 117.0101, 117.0104, 117.011 or 117.012?
      `the judge has jurisdiction in the territorial division where I reside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge have jurisdiction in the territorial division where the person against whom the application was brought (you) resides?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.1(10), is the judge a provincial court judge within the meaning of the sections it names` IS
    `s 110.1(10) provincial court judge` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "") `the judge has jurisdiction in the territorial division where I reside`

@ref s 110.2(1)
@export Under section 110.2(1), may a provincial court judge order that information about the order made against me be kept from the public?
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `the judge acts on the application of the person who applied or on the judge’s own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge acting on the application of the person who applied for the order, or on the judge’s own motion?
      `the judge considers it necessary to protect the security of that person or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge consider that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.2(1), may a provincial court judge order that information about the order made against me be kept from the public` IS
    `s 110.2(1) a provincial court judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, information` `an order has been made under subsection 110.1(3)` `the judge acts on the application of the person who applied or on the judge’s own motion` `the judge considers it necessary to protect the security of that person or of anyone known to the person`

@ref s 110.2(2) and (3)
@export Under section 110.2(2) and (3), on what day does the order keeping information from the public end?
GIVEN `a date is fixed for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1) before the order under 110.1(3) expires or is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked, has a date been fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)?
      `the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1)` IS A DATE @desc What is the date fixed? Give any date if none is fixed.
      `the order under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3) revoked before that date?
      `the day on which the order under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked` IS A DATE @desc On what day is it revoked? Give any date if it is not.
      `the order keeping information from the public is revoked earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order keeping information from the public revoked earlier?
      `the day on which the order under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the order made under subsection 110.1(3) expire or get revoked?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 110.2(2) and (3), on what day does the order keeping information from the public end` IS
    `s 110.2(2) and (3) the day on which an order made under subsection (1) ends` `a date is fixed for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1) before the order under 110.1(3) expires or is revoked` `the date fixed under subsection 110.4(1)` `the order under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked before that date` `the day on which the order under subsection 110.1(3) is revoked` `the order keeping information from the public is revoked earlier` `the day on which the order under subsection 110.1(3) expires or is revoked`

@ref s 110.2(4)
@export Under section 110.2(4), must the documents about the order made against me be sealed?
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection 110.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made under subsection 110.2(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.2(4), must the documents about the order made against me be sealed` IS
    `s 110.2(4) the documents must be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` `an order has been made under subsection 110.2(1)`

@ref s 110.2(5)
@export Under section 110.2(5), may an application to revoke or vary the order keeping information from the public be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge?
GIVEN `an order was made under subsection 110.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under subsection 110.2(1)?
      `the application is made to the judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.2(5), may an application to revoke or vary the order keeping information from the public be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` IS
    `s 110.2(5) an application to revoke the order or vary its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge` `an order was made under subsection 110.2(1)` `the application is made to the judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge`

@ref s 110.3(1)
@export Under section 110.3(1), may a provincial court judge order that the documents I receive be edited to remove identifying information?
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1)?
      `the judge acts on the application of the person who applied or on the judge’s own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge acting on the application of the person who applied for the order, or on the judge’s own motion?
      `the judge considers it necessary to protect the security of that person or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge consider that it is necessary to protect the security of the person or of anyone known to the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.3(1), may a provincial court judge order that the documents I receive be edited to remove identifying information` IS
    `s 110.3(1) a provincial court judge may make an order to delete identifying information` `an order has been made under subsection 110.1(3) or 110.2(1)` `the judge acts on the application of the person who applied or on the judge’s own motion` `the judge considers it necessary to protect the security of that person or of anyone known to the person`

@ref s 110.3(1)
@export Under section 110.3(1), what does an order to delete identifying information direct?
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 110.3(1) direction`
DECIDE `Under section 110.3(1), what does an order to delete identifying information direct` IS
    `s 110.3(1) what the order directs`

@ref s 110.3(2)
@export Under section 110.3(2), may the order to delete identifying information be for any period, definite or indefinite?
GIVEN `the judge considers the period necessary to protect the security of the person who applied or of anyone known to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge consider the period (definite or indefinite) necessary to protect the security of the person who applied for the order or of anyone known to the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.3(2), may the order to delete identifying information be for any period, definite or indefinite` IS
    `s 110.3(2) the order may be for the period, whether definite or indefinite` `the judge considers the period necessary to protect the security of the person who applied or of anyone known to the person`

@ref s 110.3(3)
@export Under section 110.3(3), must the originals of the documents be sealed?
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection 110.3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made under subsection 110.3(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.3(3), must the originals of the documents be sealed` IS
    `s 110.3(3) the originals must be placed in a packet and sealed by the judge` `an order has been made under subsection 110.3(1)`

@ref s 110.3(4)
@export Under section 110.3(4), may an application to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge?
GIVEN `an order was made under subsection 110.3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under subsection 110.3(1)?
      `the application is made to the judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made to the provincial court judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.3(4), may an application to revoke or vary the order to delete identifying information be made to the judge who made it or to another provincial court judge` IS
    `s 110.3(4) an application to revoke the order or vary its terms and conditions may be made to the provincial court judge` `an order was made under subsection 110.3(1)` `the application is made to the judge who made the order or to another provincial court judge`

@ref s 110.3(5)
@export Under section 110.3(5), does an order to delete identifying information still apply to the hearing of the application against me?
GIVEN `a date is fixed for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a date been fixed under subsection 110.4(1) for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)?
      `the order made under section 110.3 is still in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under section 110.3 still in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.3(5), does an order to delete identifying information still apply to the hearing of the application against me` IS
    `s 110.3(5) the order made under this section applies in respect of that hearing` `a date is fixed for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` `the order made under section 110.3 is still in force`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc5 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc5-seat.l4 -- LAYER 2, the seat layer, for lines 2382-2989 of the Criminal Code (Canada): Part III from s 110.4 to s 117.15, and Part IV (ss 118 to 149).
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence,
-- what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply, and what follows. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer
-- instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
-- It IMPORTs the layer-1 modules and calls their rules; it never restates a rule. Every question begins "Under section N,", has @export and @desc, and takes plain inputs
-- (yes/no): one per fact the person can state. Where the Code defines a term the person cannot be sure of (peace officer, public officer, ...), the person says what they
-- believe, and a "no" is passed on as NOTHING (not shown), never as FALSE, except where the text asks for a person who is NOT one.
-- A result of JUST TRUE answers the question as asked; JUST FALSE is the text's own "no" (an exception or a bar); NOTHING means the text does not decide it on these facts.
-- Summary-conviction limbs that state no penalty point to section 787(1), which is outside this part; the seat asks the class of the offence and the indictable maximum.

§ `Part III continued -- orders prohibiting possession (ss 110.4 to 117)`

§§ `s 110.4 Order under subsection 111(5)`

@export Under section 110.4(1), may the provincial court judge fix a date for the hearing of an application for an order against me under subsection 111(5)?
GIVEN `Has a provincial court judge made an emergency prohibition order against you under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a provincial court judge made an emergency prohibition order against you under subsection 110.1(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(1), may the provincial court judge fix a date for the hearing of an application for an order against me under subsection 111(5)` IS
    `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge may fix a date for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` (IF `Has a provincial court judge made an emergency prohibition order against you under subsection 110.1(3)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 110.4(1), is the provincial court judge bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to me?
GIVEN `Has a provincial court judge made an emergency prohibition order against you under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a provincial court judge made an emergency prohibition order against you under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `Has the judge fixed a date for the hearing of an application against you under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge fixed a date for the hearing of an application against you under subsection 111(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(1), is the provincial court judge bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to me` IS
    `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person` (IF `Has a provincial court judge made an emergency prohibition order against you under subsection 110.1(3)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Has the judge fixed a date for the hearing of an application against you under subsection 111(1)`

@export Under section 110.4(2)(a), is the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) deemed an application made under subsection 111(1)?
GIVEN `Is it the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3)?
      `Is the purpose the purpose of subsection 111(2) (the hearing date and notice on an ordinary application)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose the purpose of subsection 111(2) (the hearing date and notice on an ordinary application)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(2)(a), is the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) deemed an application made under subsection 111(1)` IS
    `s 110.4(2)(a) the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) is deemed an application made under subsection 111(1)` `Is it the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3)` `Is the purpose the purpose of subsection 111(2) (the hearing date and notice on an ordinary application)`


@export Under section 110.4(2)(b), who becomes the applicant in my case?
GIVEN `Did someone other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer make the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer make the application for the emergency order against you?
      `Where was the application made` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory was the application made? One of: Ontario, Quebec, Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island, Newfoundland and Labrador, New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan, Alberta, Yukon, Northwest Territories, Nunavut.
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(2)(b), who becomes the applicant in my case` IS
    `s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` `Did someone other than a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer make the application` `Where was the application made`


@export Under section 110.4(3), is the date fixed for the hearing before the end of the period of the order I am under?
GIVEN `On what date is the hearing fixed` IS A DATE @desc On what date has the hearing been fixed? (a date, for example 2026-03-01)
      `On what day does the period of the emergency order end` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the period for which the emergency order against you is in force end?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(3), is the date fixed for the hearing before the end of the period of the order I am under` IS
    `s 110.4(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order` `On what date is the hearing fixed` `On what day does the period of the emergency order end`

@export Under section 110.4(3), may the provincial court judge adjourn the hearing on my application?
GIVEN `Is the application to adjourn made by the applicant, or by you as the person against whom the order is sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application to adjourn made by the applicant, or by you as the person against whom the order is sought?
      `Is the application made before, or at any time during, the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made before, or at any time during, the hearing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(3), may the provincial court judge adjourn the hearing on my application` IS
    `s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` `Is the application to adjourn made by the applicant, or by you as the person against whom the order is sought` `Is the application made before, or at any time during, the hearing`

@export Under section 110.4(4), is the provincial court judge bound to cause notice of the application and of the hearing date to be served on the Attorney General?
GIVEN `Does the Attorney General become the applicant in the application under subsection 111(1), under paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General become the applicant in the application under subsection 111(1), under paragraph (2)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(4), is the provincial court judge bound to cause notice of the application and of the hearing date to be served on the Attorney General` IS
    `s 110.4(4) the provincial court judge is bound to cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` `Does the Attorney General become the applicant in the application under subsection 111(1), under paragraph (2)(b)`

@export Under section 110.4(5), is the provincial court judge bound to cancel the hearing because my emergency order was revoked before the application was heard?
GIVEN `Has the judge revoked the emergency order made against you under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge revoked the emergency order made against you under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `Has the application for an order against you under subsection 111(5) not yet been heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the application for an order against you under subsection 111(5) not yet been heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110.4(5), is the provincial court judge bound to cancel the hearing because my emergency order was revoked before the application was heard` IS
    `s 110.4(5) the provincial court judge is bound to cancel the hearing` `Has the judge revoked the emergency order made against you under subsection 110.1(3)` `Has the application for an order against you under subsection 111(5) not yet been heard`

§§ `s 111 Application for prohibition order`

@export Under section 111(1), may a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting me from possessing firearms and similar things?
GIVEN `Is the applicant a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
      `Is the applicant a firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a firearms officer?
      `Is the applicant a chief firearms officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a chief firearms officer?
      `Does the applicant believe, on reasonable grounds, that it is not desirable in the interests of your safety or anyone else's that you should possess a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the applicant believe, on reasonable grounds, that it is not desirable in the interests of your safety or anyone else's that you should possess a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(1), may a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting me from possessing firearms and similar things` IS
    `s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` (IF `Is the applicant a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Is the applicant a firearms officer` `Is the applicant a chief firearms officer` `Does the applicant believe, on reasonable grounds, that it is not desirable in the interests of your safety or anyone else's that you should possess a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance`

@export Under section 111(2), is the provincial court judge bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice of it be given to me?
GIVEN `Has an application been made under subsection 111(1) for an order against you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made under subsection 111(1) for an order against you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(2), is the provincial court judge bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice of it be given to me` IS
    `s 111(2) the provincial court judge is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given to the person` `Has an application been made under subsection 111(1) for an order against you`

@export Under section 111(3), is the provincial court judge bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and me?
GIVEN `Is the hearing of the application under subsection 111(1) being held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hearing of the application under subsection 111(1) being held?
      `Is the judge proceeding in your absence (ex parte) under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge proceeding in your absence (ex parte) under subsection (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(3), is the provincial court judge bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and me` IS
    `s 111(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person` `Is the hearing of the application under subsection 111(1) being held` `Is the judge proceeding in your absence (ex parte) under subsection (4)`

@export Under section 111(4), may the provincial court judge hear and determine the application in my absence?
GIVEN `Is the application made under subsection 111(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under subsection 111(1)?
      `Are you absent from the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent from the hearing?
      `Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(4), may the provincial court judge hear and determine the application in my absence` IS
    `s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` `Is the application made under subsection 111(1)` `Are you absent from the hearing` (IF `Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 111(5), is the provincial court judge bound to make an order prohibiting me from possessing firearms and similar things?
GIVEN `Has the hearing of the application against you under subsection 111(1) concluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the hearing of the application against you under subsection 111(1) concluded?
      `Is the judge satisfied that the circumstances in subsection 111(1) exist (that it is not desirable in the interests of safety that you possess such things)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the circumstances in subsection 111(1) exist (that it is not desirable in the interests of safety that you possess such things)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(5), is the provincial court judge bound to make an order prohibiting me from possessing firearms and similar things` IS
    `s 111(5) the provincial court judge is bound to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing the things` `Has the hearing of the application against you under subsection 111(1) concluded` `Is the judge satisfied that the circumstances in subsection 111(1) exist (that it is not desirable in the interests of safety that you possess such things)`


@export Under section 111(5), is the period of the order I face not more than five years?
GIVEN `For how many whole years does the order last` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many whole years does the order last? (0 if it lasts less than a year)
      `For how many further whole months does the order last` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many further whole months (beyond the whole years) does the order last?
      `For how many further days does the order last` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many further days (beyond the whole years and months) does the order last?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(5), is the period of the order I face not more than five years` IS
    `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF `For how many whole years does the order last`, `For how many further whole months does the order last`, `For how many further days does the order last`, FALSE)

@export Under section 111(5), does the order I face begin on the day on which it is made?
GIVEN `On what day was the order made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made? (a date, for example 2026-03-10)
      `On what day does the order say its period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the order say its period begins?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(5), does the order I face begin on the day on which it is made` IS
    `s 111(5) the order begins on the day on which it is made` `On what day was the order made` `On what day does the order say its period begins`

@export Under section 111(6), is the provincial court judge bound to include a statement of reasons in the record where no order, or a narrower order, is made?
GIVEN `Did the judge decline to make an order against you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge decline to make an order against you?
      `Did the judge make an order but not prohibit the possession of everything the application named` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge make an order but not prohibit the possession of everything the application named?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(6), is the provincial court judge bound to include a statement of reasons in the record where no order, or a narrower order, is made` IS
    `s 111(6) the provincial court judge is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` `Did the judge decline to make an order against you` `Did the judge make an order but not prohibit the possession of everything the application named`


@export Under section 111(7), do sections 113 to 117 apply to the order made against me
GIVEN `Is the order made under subsection 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order against you an order made under subsection 111(5)?
      `Which section of the Code are you asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of the section you are asking about, for example 114 or 115.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(7), do sections 113 to 117 apply to the order made against me` IS
    `s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` `Is the order made under subsection 111(5)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `Which section of the Code are you asking about`, "")

@export Under section 111(8), may I appeal to the superior court against the order the provincial court judge made against me?
GIVEN `Are you the person to whom the order relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person to whom the order relates?
      `Is the appellant the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the Attorney General?
      `Did the provincial court judge make an order against you under subsection 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the provincial court judge make an order against you under subsection 111(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(8), may I appeal to the superior court against the order the provincial court judge made against me` IS
    `s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order` `Are you the person to whom the order relates` `Is the appellant the Attorney General` `Did the provincial court judge make an order against you under subsection 111(5)`

@export Under section 111(9), may the Attorney General appeal to the superior court against the judge's decision not to make an order against me?
GIVEN `Is the appellant the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the Attorney General?
      `Did the judge decline to make an order under subsection 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge decline to make an order under subsection 111(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(9), may the Attorney General appeal to the superior court against the judge's decision not to make an order against me` IS
    `s 111(9) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the decision not to make an order` `Is the appellant the Attorney General` `Did the judge decline to make an order under subsection 111(5)`


@export Under section 111(10), does a provision of Part XXVII apply to my appeal to the superior court
GIVEN `Which section of Part XXVII is in question` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of the section of Part XXVII you are asking about, for example 813.
      `Is it a provision of Part XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the section a provision of Part XXVII (Summary Convictions)?
      `Is the appeal made under subsection (8) or (9)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal the appeal that subsection (8) or (9) of section 111 gives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 111(10), does a provision of Part XXVII apply to my appeal to the superior court` IS
    `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` `Which section of Part XXVII is in question` `Is it a provision of Part XXVII` `Is the appeal made under subsection (8) or (9)`

§§ `s 112 Revocation of prohibition order under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5)`

@export Under section 112, may a provincial court judge revoke the order made against me?
GIVEN `Do you, the person against whom the order was made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5), make the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, the person against whom the order was made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5), make the application?
      `Is the judge satisfied that the circumstances for which the order was made have ceased to exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the circumstances for which the order was made have ceased to exist?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 112, may a provincial court judge revoke the order made against me` IS
    `s 112 a provincial court judge may revoke the order` `Do you, the person against whom the order was made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5), make the application` `Is the judge satisfied that the circumstances for which the order was made have ceased to exist`

§§ `s 113 Lifting of prohibition order for sustenance or employment`

@export Under section 113(1), may the competent authority make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for me for sustenance or employment despite the prohibition order?
GIVEN `Are you, or will you be, a person against whom a prohibition order is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or will you be, a person against whom a prohibition order is made?
      `Have you established to the competent authority's satisfaction that you need a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap to sustain yourself or your family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established to the competent authority's satisfaction that you need a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap to sustain yourself or your family?
      `Have you established to the competent authority's satisfaction that a prohibition order would be a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established to the competent authority's satisfaction that a prohibition order would be a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(1), may the competent authority make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for me for sustenance or employment despite the prohibition order` IS
    `s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment` `Are you, or will you be, a person against whom a prohibition order is made` `Have you established to the competent authority's satisfaction that you need a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap to sustain yourself or your family` `Have you established to the competent authority's satisfaction that a prohibition order would be a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to you`

@export Under section 113(2), may the competent authority make an order for me under section 113(1) after taking into account my criminal record, the offence and safety?
GIVEN `Has the authority taken into account your criminal record, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authority taken into account your criminal record, if any?
      `Has the authority taken into account the nature and circumstances of the offence, if any, for which the prohibition order was or will be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authority taken into account the nature and circumstances of the offence, if any, for which the prohibition order was or will be made?
      `Has the authority taken into account your safety and the safety of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the authority taken into account your safety and the safety of other persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(2), may the competent authority make an order for me under section 113(1) after taking into account my criminal record, the offence and safety` IS
    `s 113(2) the competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the factors into account` `Has the authority taken into account your criminal record, if any` `Has the authority taken into account the nature and circumstances of the offence, if any, for which the prohibition order was or will be made` `Has the authority taken into account your safety and the safety of other persons`

@export Under section 113(3)(a), is the chief firearms officer barred from denying me an authorization, licence or registration certificate solely on the basis of the prohibition order or my offence?
GIVEN `Is the denial based solely on the prohibition order against you, or on your commission of an offence for which a prohibition order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the denial based solely on the prohibition order against you, or on your commission of an offence for which a prohibition order was made?
      `Has an order been made in your favour under subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made in your favour under subsection 113(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(3)(a), is the chief firearms officer barred from denying me an authorization, licence or registration certificate solely on the basis of the prohibition order or my offence` IS
    `s 113(3)(a) an authorization, licence or registration certificate is barred from being denied solely on the basis of the prohibition order or the offence` `Is the denial based solely on the prohibition order against you, or on your commission of an offence for which a prohibition order was made` `Has an order been made in your favour under subsection 113(1)`

@export Under section 113(3)(b), may an authorization or licence be issued to me for the duration of the order?
GIVEN `Has an order been made in your favour under subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made in your favour under subsection 113(1)?
      `Is the authorization or licence issued for sustenance or employment purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authorization or licence issued for sustenance or employment purposes?
      `Does the order set out terms and conditions, and is the issue not in accordance with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order set out terms and conditions, and is the issue not in accordance with them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(3)(b), may an authorization or licence be issued to me for the duration of the order` IS
    `s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order` `Has an order been made in your favour under subsection 113(1)` `Is the authorization or licence issued for sustenance or employment purposes` `Does the order set out terms and conditions, and is the issue not in accordance with them`

@export Under section 113(3)(b), may the chief firearms officer attach further terms and conditions to my authorization or licence?
GIVEN `Are the further terms and conditions consistent with the purpose for which the authorization or licence is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the further terms and conditions consistent with the purpose for which the authorization or licence is issued?
      `Are they consistent with the terms and conditions set out in the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they consistent with the terms and conditions set out in the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(3)(b), may the chief firearms officer attach further terms and conditions to my authorization or licence` IS
    `s 113(3)(b) the chief firearms officer may attach further terms and conditions to the authorization or licence` `Are the further terms and conditions consistent with the purpose for which the authorization or licence is issued` `Are they consistent with the terms and conditions set out in the order`

@export Under section 113(4), may an order lifting the prohibition for sustenance or employment be made during the proceedings I am in?
GIVEN `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 109(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 109(1)?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 110(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 110(1)?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 111(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 111(5)?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 117.05(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 117.05(4)?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 515(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 515(2)?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under paragraph 732.1(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under paragraph 732.1(3)(d)?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under section 810` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under section 810?
      `Are the proceedings for an order under section 810.03` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an order under section 810.03?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(4), may an order lifting the prohibition for sustenance or employment be made during the proceedings I am in` IS
    `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 109(1)` `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 110(1)` `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 110.1(3)` `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 111(5)` `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 117.05(4)` `Are the proceedings for an order under subsection 515(2)` `Are the proceedings for an order under paragraph 732.1(3)(d)` `Are the proceedings for an order under section 810` `Are the proceedings for an order under section 810.03`

@export Under section 113(5), is the authority the competent authority?
GIVEN `Is the authority the one that made the prohibition order, or has jurisdiction to make it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authority the one that made the prohibition order, or has jurisdiction to make it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(5), is the authority the competent authority` IS
    `s 113(5) competent authority` `Is the authority the one that made the prohibition order, or has jurisdiction to make it`

§§ `s 114 Requirement to surrender`

@export Under section 114, may the authority that makes a prohibition order against me require me to surrender things and documents to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer?
GIVEN `Has an authority made a prohibition order against you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authority made a prohibition order against you?
      `Is the thing, whose possession the order prohibits, in your possession on the commencement of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing, whose possession the order prohibits, in your possession on the commencement of the order?
      `Do you hold, on the commencement of the order, an authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to a thing the order prohibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, on the commencement of the order, an authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to a thing the order prohibits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 114, may the authority that makes a prohibition order against me require me to surrender things and documents to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` IS
    `s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents` `Has an authority made a prohibition order against you` `Is the thing, whose possession the order prohibits, in your possession on the commencement of the order` `Do you hold, on the commencement of the order, an authorization, licence or registration certificate relating to a thing the order prohibits`

@export Under section 114, is the authority bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for me to surrender things and documents?
GIVEN `Does the order require you to surrender things or documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order require you to surrender things or documents?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 114, is the authority bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for me to surrender things and documents` IS
    `s 114 the authority is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering` `Does the order require you to surrender things or documents`

@export Under section 114, does section 117.01 not apply to me during the period the order specifies for surrendering?
GIVEN `Does the order require you to surrender things or documents and specify a period for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order require you to surrender things or documents and specify a period for it?
      `Is it a day within the period the order specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a day within the period the order specifies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 114, does section 117.01 not apply to me during the period the order specifies for surrendering` IS
    `s 114 section 117.01 does not apply to the person during the specified period` `Does the order require you to surrender things or documents and specify a period for it` `Is it a day within the period the order specifies`

§§ `s 115 Forfeiture`

@export Under section 115(1.1), does the forfeiture in section 115(1) not apply to the order made against me?
GIVEN `Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `Is the order made under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under section 515?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(1.1), does the forfeiture in section 115(1) not apply to the order made against me` IS
    `s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order` `Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3)` `Is the order made under section 515`

@export Under section 115(1), is a thing whose possession the prohibition order prohibits forfeited to Her Majesty?
GIVEN `Is the thing one whose possession the prohibition order prohibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing one whose possession the prohibition order prohibits?
      `On the commencement of the order, is the thing in your possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the commencement of the order, is the thing in your possession?
      `On the commencement of the order, has the thing been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the commencement of the order, has the thing been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer?
      `Does the prohibition order specify otherwise than forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prohibition order specify otherwise than forfeiture?
      `s 115(1.1): Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3)?
      `s 115(1.1): Is the order made under section 515` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under section 515?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(1), is a thing whose possession the prohibition order prohibits forfeited to Her Majesty` IS
    `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` `Is the thing one whose possession the prohibition order prohibits` `On the commencement of the order, is the thing in your possession` `On the commencement of the order, has the thing been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer` `Does the prohibition order specify otherwise than forfeiture` (`s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order` `s 115(1.1): Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3)` `s 115(1.1): Is the order made under section 515`)

@export Under section 115(2), is a thing forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs?
GIVEN `Is the thing forfeited to Her Majesty under section 115(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing forfeited to Her Majesty under section 115(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(2), is a thing forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs` IS
    `s 115(2) the thing forfeited is to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs` `Is the thing forfeited to Her Majesty under section 115(1)`

§§ `s 116 Authorizations revoked or amended`

@export Under section 116(1), is my authorization, licence or registration certificate revoked or amended on the commencement of the prohibition order?
GIVEN `Does your authorization, licence or registration certificate relate to a thing the prohibition order prohibits you from possessing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your authorization, licence or registration certificate relate to a thing the prohibition order prohibits you from possessing?
      `Was it issued to you, the person against whom the prohibition order is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued to you, the person against whom the prohibition order is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
