    `s 116(1) the authorization, licence or registration certificate is revoked or amended on the commencement of the prohibition order` `Does your authorization, licence or registration certificate relate to a thing the prohibition order prohibits you from possessing` `Was it issued to you, the person against whom the prohibition order is made`

@export Under section 116(2), does my authorization, licence or registration certificate remain revoked or amended, because the order is under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515 and still in force?
GIVEN `Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515?
      `Is the day one within the period during which the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day one within the period during which the order is in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(2), does my authorization, licence or registration certificate remain revoked or amended, because the order is under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515 and still in force` IS
    `s 116(2) the authorization, licence or registration certificate remains revoked or amended` `Is the order made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515` `Is the day one within the period during which the order is in force`

§§ `s 117 Return to owner`

@export Under section 117, is the competent authority bound to order the thing returned to me as its owner, or its proceeds or value paid to me?
GIVEN `Are you a person, other than the person against whom a prohibition order was or will be made, who applies for an order under section 117` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person, other than the person against whom a prohibition order was or will be made, who applies for an order under section 117?
      `Are you the owner of a thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 115(1), and lawfully entitled to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the owner of a thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 115(1), and lawfully entitled to possess it?
      `Is the prohibition order an order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prohibition order an order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1)?
      `Did you have no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence for which the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence for which the order was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117, is the competent authority bound to order the thing returned to me as its owner, or its proceeds or value paid to me` IS
    `s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` `Are you a person, other than the person against whom a prohibition order was or will be made, who applies for an order under section 117` `Are you the owner of a thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 115(1), and lawfully entitled to possess it` `Is the prohibition order an order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1)` `Did you have no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence for which the order was made`


@export Under section 117, what must the competent authority order for me as the owner
GIVEN `Does the thing still exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the thing still exist (has it not been sold or destroyed)?
      `Was the thing sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing sold? (answer no if it still exists or was destroyed)
GIVETH A `s 117 order for the owner`
DECIDE `Under section 117, what must the competent authority order for me as the owner` IS
    `s 117 what the order for the owner is` (IF `Does the thing still exist` THEN `s 117 the thing still exists` ELSE IF `Was the thing sold` THEN `s 117 the thing was sold` ELSE `s 117 the thing was destroyed`)

§ `Part III continued -- offences, and limitations on access (ss 117.01 to 117.012)`

§§ `s 117.01 Possession contrary to order`

@export Under section 117.01(4), does section 117.01(1) not apply to me because I possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as the result of an order under section 113(1)?
GIVEN `Did you possess the firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to you as the result of an order under subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess the firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to you as the result of an order under subsection 113(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.01(4), does section 117.01(1) not apply to me because I possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as the result of an order under section 113(1)` IS
    `s 117.01(4) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as a result of an order under subsection 113(1)` `Did you possess the firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to you as the result of an order under subsection 113(1)`

@export Under section 117.01, is possessing a weapon while prohibited by an order, or wilfully failing to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate, an offence on what I did?
GIVEN `s 117.01(1): Is the thing you possess a firearm, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you possess a firearm, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 117.01(1))
      `s 117.01(1): Is the thing you possess a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition or prohibited ammunition, as subsection 84(1) defines those terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you possess a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition or prohibited ammunition, as subsection 84(1) defines those terms? (s 117.01(1))
      `s 117.01(1): Is the thing you possess an explosive substance, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you possess an explosive substance, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 117.01(1))
      `s 117.01(1): Are you prohibited from possessing it by an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you prohibited from possessing it by an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament? (s 117.01(1))
      `s 117.01(4): Did you possess the firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to you as the result of an order under subsection 113(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess the firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to you as the result of an order under subsection 113(1)? (s 117.01(1))
      `s 117.01(2): Did you wilfully fail to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer an authorization, licence or registration certificate you hold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you wilfully fail to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer an authorization, licence or registration certificate you hold? (s 117.01(2))
      `s 117.01(2): Were you required to surrender it by an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you required to surrender it by an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament? (s 117.01(2))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.01, is possessing a weapon while prohibited by an order, or wilfully failing to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate, an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 117.01(3) the person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence` (`s 117.01(1) the person possesses a prohibited thing while prohibited from doing so by an order` (IF `s 117.01(1): Is the thing you possess a firearm, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) (IF `s 117.01(1): Is the thing you possess a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition or prohibited ammunition, as subsection 84(1) defines those terms` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) (IF `s 117.01(1): Is the thing you possess an explosive substance, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 117.01(1): Are you prohibited from possessing it by an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` (`s 117.01(4) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possessed a firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued as a result of an order under subsection 113(1)` `s 117.01(4): Did you possess the firearm in accordance with an authorization or licence issued to you as the result of an order under subsection 113(1)`)) (`s 117.01(2) the person wilfully fails to surrender an authorization, licence or registration certificate when required by an order` `s 117.01(2): Did you wilfully fail to surrender to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer an authorization, licence or registration certificate you hold` `s 117.01(2): Were you required to surrender it by an order made under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament`)

@export Under section 117.01(3), is an offence under section 117.01(1) or (2) indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 117.01(3), is an offence under section 117.01(1) or (2) indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 117.01(3) the class of the offence`

@export Under section 117.01(3)(a), what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment for an offence under section 117.01?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 117.01(3)(a), what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment for an offence under section 117.01` IS
    `s 117.01(3)(a) the punishment on indictment`

§§ `s 117.0101 Application for emergency limitations on access order`

@export Under section 117.0101(1), may a person make an ex parte application to a provincial court judge for an emergency order limiting access to things in my possession?
