      `s 117.0101(10): Is the judge satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of the emergency order can reasonably be complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of the emergency order can reasonably be complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.0101(6), may the provincial court judge issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search for and seize things in my possession` IS
    `s 117.0101(6) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search and seize` `Is the judge satisfied, by information on oath, that there are reasonable grounds to believe you possess, in a building, receptacle or place, a thing whose use and possession are subject to the terms of the emergency order` `Is the judge satisfied that it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess the thing` (`s 117.0101(10) the judge may issue the warrant or include the requirement to surrender` `s 117.0101(10): Is the judge satisfied that there is no other way to ensure that the terms and conditions of the emergency order can reasonably be complied with`)

@export Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant?
GIVEN `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
      `Are you subject to an emergency order made under subsection 117.0101(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to an emergency order made under subsection 117.0101(3)?
      `Is the peace officer satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess a thing whose use and possession are subject to the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the peace officer satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess a thing whose use and possession are subject to the terms of the order?
      `Do the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection 117.0101(6) exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection 117.0101(6) exist?
      `Would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant by reason of a possible danger to anyone's safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant by reason of a possible danger to anyone's safety?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.0101(7), may a peace officer search for and seize things in my possession without a warrant` IS
    `s 117.0101(7) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (IF `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Are you subject to an emergency order made under subsection 117.0101(3)` `Is the peace officer satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess a thing whose use and possession are subject to the terms of the order` `Do the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection 117.0101(6) exist` `Would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant by reason of a possible danger to anyone's safety`

@export Under section 117.0101(8), is the peace officer who searched or seized bound to make a report immediately to a justice?
GIVEN `Did the peace officer execute a warrant referred to in subsection 117.0101(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer execute a warrant referred to in subsection 117.0101(6)?
      `Did the peace officer conduct a search without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer conduct a search without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.0101(8), is the peace officer who searched or seized bound to make a report immediately to a justice` IS
    `s 117.0101(8) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` `Did the peace officer execute a warrant referred to in subsection 117.0101(6)` `Did the peace officer conduct a search without a warrant under subsection 117.0101(7)`

