    `s 117.011(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person` `Is the hearing of the application under subsection 117.011(1) being held` `Is the judge proceeding in your absence (ex parte) under subsection (4)`

@export Under section 117.011(4), may the provincial court judge hear and determine the application in my absence?
GIVEN `Is the application made under subsection 117.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under subsection 117.011(1)?
      `Are you absent from the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent from the hearing?
      `Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.011(4), may the provincial court judge hear and determine the application in my absence` IS
    `s 117.011(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` `Is the application made under subsection 117.011(1)` `Are you absent from the hearing` (IF `Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

