§ `Part III continued -- search and seizure (ss 117.02 to 117.06)`

§§ `s 117.02 Search and seizure without warrant where offence committed`

@export Under section 117.02(1), may a peace officer search me, my vehicle or my premises other than a dwelling-house without a warrant, and seize things?
GIVEN `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
      `Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that a weapon, imitation firearm, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that a weapon, imitation firearm, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence?
      `Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that an offence involving a firearm, imitation firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance is being or has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that an offence involving a firearm, imitation firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance is being or has been committed?
      `Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that evidence of the offence is likely to be found on a person, in a vehicle, or in a place or premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that evidence of the offence is likely to be found on a person, in a vehicle, or in a place or premises?
      `Is the place or premises a dwelling-house, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place or premises a dwelling-house, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
      `Do the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist?
      `By reason of exigent circumstances, would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of exigent circumstances, would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.02(1), may a peace officer search me, my vehicle or my premises other than a dwelling-house without a warrant, and seize things` IS
    `s 117.02(1) the peace officer may search without a warrant and seize` (IF `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that a weapon, imitation firearm, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence` `Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that an offence involving a firearm, imitation firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance is being or has been committed` `Does the peace officer believe, on reasonable grounds, that evidence of the offence is likely to be found on a person, in a vehicle, or in a place or premises` (IF `Is the place or premises a dwelling-house, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) `Do the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist` `By reason of exigent circumstances, would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant`

@export Under section 117.02(2), is a thing seized from me under section 117.02(1) to be dealt with in accordance with sections 490 and 491?
GIVEN `Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.02(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.02(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.02(2), is a thing seized from me under section 117.02(1) to be dealt with in accordance with sections 490 and 491` IS
    `s 117.02(2) the thing seized is to be dealt with in accordance with sections 490 and 491` `Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.02(1)`

§§ `s 117.03 Seizure on failure to produce authorization`

@export Under section 117.03(1), may a peace officer seize my firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition because I did not produce an authorization or licence on demand?
GIVEN `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
      `Were you found in possession of a prohibited, restricted or non-restricted firearm and did you fail, on demand, to produce for inspection an authorization or licence for it (and, for a prohibited or restricted firearm, a registration certificate)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found in possession of a prohibited, restricted or non-restricted firearm and did you fail, on demand, to produce for inspection an authorization or licence for it (and, for a prohibited or restricted firearm, a registration certificate)?
      `Were you found in possession of a prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition and did you fail, on demand, to produce for inspection an authorization or licence for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found in possession of a prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition and did you fail, on demand, to produce for inspection an authorization or licence for it?
      `Is your possession of it, in the circumstances in which it is found, authorized by a provision of Part III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your possession of it, in the circumstances in which it is found, authorized by a provision of Part III?
      `Are you under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who may lawfully possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who may lawfully possess it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.03(1), may a peace officer seize my firearm, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition because I did not produce an authorization or licence on demand` IS
    `s 117.03(1) the peace officer may seize the firearm, weapon, device or ammunition` (IF `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Were you found in possession of a prohibited, restricted or non-restricted firearm and did you fail, on demand, to produce for inspection an authorization or licence for it (and, for a prohibited or restricted firearm, a registration certificate)` `Were you found in possession of a prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition and did you fail, on demand, to produce for inspection an authorization or licence for it` `Is your possession of it, in the circumstances in which it is found, authorized by a provision of Part III` `Are you under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who may lawfully possess it`


@export Under section 117.03(2), is the thing seized from me to be returned without delay?
GIVEN `Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.03(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.03(1) (on a failure to produce an authorization or licence on demand)?
      `On what date was the thing seized` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the thing seized from you?
      `On what date did you claim the thing` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you claim the thing?
      `Did you produce a licence under which you are lawfully entitled to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you produce for inspection a licence under which you are lawfully entitled to possess the thing?
      `Is the thing a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm?
      `Did you also produce an authorization and registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you also produce an authorization and a registration certificate for it? (answer no if the thing is not a prohibited or restricted firearm)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.03(2), is the thing seized from me to be returned without delay` IS
    `s 117.03(2) the thing is to be returned without delay` `Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.03(1)` (`s 117.03(2) the claim is made within 14 days after the seizure` `On what date was the thing seized` `On what date did you claim the thing`) `Did you produce a licence under which you are lawfully entitled to possess it` `Is the thing a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm` `Did you also produce an authorization and registration certificate for it`

@export Under section 117.03(3), is the peace officer bound to take the thing seized from me forthwith before a provincial court judge, because it was not claimed and returned as subsection (2) provides?
GIVEN `Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.03(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.03(1)?
      `Was the thing claimed and returned as and when subsection 117.03(2) provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing claimed and returned as and when subsection 117.03(2) provides?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.03(3), is the peace officer bound to take the thing seized from me forthwith before a provincial court judge, because it was not claimed and returned as subsection (2) provides` IS
    `s 117.03(3) the peace officer is bound to take the thing forthwith before a provincial court judge` `Was the thing seized from you under subsection 117.03(1)` `Was the thing claimed and returned as and when subsection 117.03(2) provides`

@export Under section 117.03(3), may the provincial court judge declare the thing seized from me forfeited to Her Majesty?
GIVEN `Was the thing taken before the judge under section 117.03(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing taken before the judge under section 117.03(3)?
      `Did the judge give you, or the owner if known, an opportunity to establish that you are lawfully entitled to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge give you, or the owner if known, an opportunity to establish that you are lawfully entitled to possess it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.03(3), may the provincial court judge declare the thing seized from me forfeited to Her Majesty` IS
    `s 117.03(3) the provincial court judge may declare the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` `Was the thing taken before the judge under section 117.03(3)` `Did the judge give you, or the owner if known, an opportunity to establish that you are lawfully entitled to possess it`

§§ `s 117.04 Application for warrant to search and seize`

@export Under section 117.04(1), may a justice issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search a building, receptacle or place and seize my weapons and authorizations?
GIVEN `Is the person a justice, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a justice, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
      `Has a peace officer applied for the warrant with respect to you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a peace officer applied for the warrant with respect to you?
      `Is the justice satisfied, by information on oath, that there are reasonable grounds to believe you possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance in a building, receptacle or place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice satisfied, by information on oath, that there are reasonable grounds to believe you possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance in a building, receptacle or place?
      `Is the justice satisfied that it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice satisfied that it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.04(1), may a justice issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search a building, receptacle or place and seize my weapons and authorizations` IS
    `s 117.04(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to search the building, receptacle or place and seize` (IF `Is the person a justice, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Has a peace officer applied for the warrant with respect to you` `Is the justice satisfied, by information on oath, that there are reasonable grounds to believe you possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance in a building, receptacle or place` `Is the justice satisfied that it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess it`

@export Under section 117.04(2), may a peace officer search for and seize my weapons and authorizations without a warrant?
GIVEN `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
      `Is the peace officer satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the peace officer satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance?
      `Do the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection 117.04(1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection 117.04(1) exist?
      `Would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant by reason of a possible danger to anyone's safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant by reason of a possible danger to anyone's safety?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.04(2), may a peace officer search for and seize my weapons and authorizations without a warrant` IS
    `s 117.04(2) the peace officer may search for and seize without a warrant` (IF `Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Is the peace officer satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe it is not desirable, in the interests of anyone's safety, that you possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` `Do the grounds for obtaining a warrant under subsection 117.04(1) exist` `Would it not be practicable to obtain a warrant by reason of a possible danger to anyone's safety`

@export Under section 117.04(3), is the peace officer who searched or seized bound to make a report immediately to a justice?
GIVEN `Did the peace officer execute a warrant referred to in subsection 117.04(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer execute a warrant referred to in subsection 117.04(1)?
      `Did the peace officer conduct a search without a warrant under subsection 117.04(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer conduct a search without a warrant under subsection 117.04(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.04(3), is the peace officer who searched or seized bound to make a report immediately to a justice` IS
    `s 117.04(3) the peace officer is bound to make a report immediately to a justice having jurisdiction` `Did the peace officer execute a warrant referred to in subsection 117.04(1)` `Did the peace officer conduct a search without a warrant under subsection 117.04(2)`

@export Under section 117.04(3), does the peace officer's report show what the subsection requires?
GIVEN `Does the report, of the execution of a warrant, show the things or documents seized (if any) and the date of execution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report, of the execution of a warrant, show the things or documents seized (if any) and the date of execution?
      `Does the report, of a search without a warrant, show the grounds on which the officer concluded they were entitled to search, and the things or documents seized (if any)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the report, of a search without a warrant, show the grounds on which the officer concluded they were entitled to search, and the things or documents seized (if any)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.04(3), does the peace officer's report show what the subsection requires` IS
    `s 117.04(3) the report shows what the subsection requires` `Does the report, of the execution of a warrant, show the things or documents seized (if any) and the date of execution` `Does the report, of a search without a warrant, show the grounds on which the officer concluded they were entitled to search, and the things or documents seized (if any)`

@export Under section 117.04(4), is every authorization, licence and registration certificate I hold revoked as at the time of the seizure?
GIVEN `Did a peace officer seize something from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a peace officer seize something from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)?
      `Was the peace officer unable, at the time of the seizure, to seize an authorization or licence under which you may possess the thing and, for a firearm, a registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the peace officer unable, at the time of the seizure, to seize an authorization or licence under which you may possess the thing and, for a firearm, a registration certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.04(4), is every authorization, licence and registration certificate I hold revoked as at the time of the seizure` IS
    `s 117.04(4) every authorization, licence and registration certificate held by the person is revoked as at the time of the seizure` `Did a peace officer seize something from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` `Was the peace officer unable, at the time of the seizure, to seize an authorization or licence under which you may possess the thing and, for a firearm, a registration certificate`

§§ `s 117.05 Application for disposition`


@export Under section 117.05(1), is the justice bound to fix a date for the hearing of the peace officer's application about the things seized from me and direct that notice of it be given?
GIVEN `Was a thing or document seized from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a thing or document seized from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)?
      `Is the application for the disposition made by a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for an order for the disposition of the thing or document made by a peace officer?
      `On what date was the warrant executed or the seizure made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the warrant executed, or the seizure made without a warrant?
      `On what date was the application made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application for the order for the disposition made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(1), is the justice bound to fix a date for the hearing of the peace officer's application about the things seized from me and direct that notice of it be given` IS
    `s 117.05(1) the justice is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice of it be given` `Was a thing or document seized from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` `Is the application for the disposition made by a peace officer` (`s 117.05(1) the application is made within 30 days after the execution or the seizure` `On what date was the warrant executed or the seizure made` `On what date was the application made`)

@export Under section 117.05(2), may the justice hear and determine the application in my absence?
GIVEN `Is the application made under subsection 117.05(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under subsection 117.05(1)?
      `Are you, the person from whom the thing or document was seized, absent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, the person from whom the thing or document was seized, absent?
      `Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(2), may the justice hear and determine the application in my absence` IS
    `s 117.05(2) the justice may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` `Is the application made under subsection 117.05(1)` `Are you, the person from whom the thing or document was seized, absent` (IF `Are the circumstances those in which a summary conviction court may, under Part XXVII, proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 117.05(3), is the justice bound to hear all relevant evidence, including evidence of the value of the thing?
GIVEN `Is the hearing of the application under subsection 117.05(1) being held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hearing of the application under subsection 117.05(1) being held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(3), is the justice bound to hear all relevant evidence, including evidence of the value of the thing` IS
    `s 117.05(3) the justice is bound to hear all relevant evidence, including evidence respecting the value of the thing` `Is the hearing of the application under subsection 117.05(1) being held`

@export Under section 117.05(4)(a), is the justice bound to order that the things seized from me be forfeited to Her Majesty or otherwise disposed of?
GIVEN `Following the hearing, does the justice find that it is not desirable, in the interests of your safety or anyone's, that you should possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Following the hearing, does the justice find that it is not desirable, in the interests of your safety or anyone's, that you should possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(4)(a), is the justice bound to order that the things seized from me be forfeited to Her Majesty or otherwise disposed of` IS
    `s 117.05(4)(a) the justice is bound to order that any thing seized be forfeited to Her Majesty or otherwise disposed of` `Following the hearing, does the justice find that it is not desirable, in the interests of your safety or anyone's, that you should possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance`

@export Under section 117.05(4)(b), is the justice bound to order that my possession of weapons and similar things be prohibited?
GIVEN `Following the hearing, does the justice find that it is not desirable, in the interests of your safety or anyone's, that you should possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Following the hearing, does the justice find that it is not desirable, in the interests of your safety or anyone's, that you should possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance?
      `Is the justice satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(4)(b), is the justice bound to order that my possession of weapons and similar things be prohibited` IS
    `s 117.05(4)(b) the justice is bound to order that the person's possession be prohibited` `Following the hearing, does the justice find that it is not desirable, in the interests of your safety or anyone's, that you should possess a weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance` `Is the justice satisfied that the circumstances warrant such an action`


@export Under section 117.05(4)(b), is the period of the order I face not more than five years?
GIVEN `For how many whole years does the order last` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many whole years does the order last? (0 if it lasts less than a year)
      `For how many further whole months does the order last` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many further whole months (beyond the whole years) does the order last?
      `For how many further days does the order last` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many further days (beyond the whole years and months) does the order last?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(4)(b), is the period of the order I face not more than five years` IS
    `s 117.05(4)(b) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF `For how many whole years does the order last`, `For how many further whole months does the order last`, `For how many further days does the order last`, FALSE)

@export Under section 117.05(4)(b), does the order I face begin on the day on which it is made?
GIVEN `On what day was the order made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made? (a date, for example 2026-03-10)
      `On what day does the order say its period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the order say its period begins?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(4)(b), does the order I face begin on the day on which it is made` IS
    `s 117.05(4)(b) the order begins on the day on which it is made` `On what day was the order made` `On what day does the order say its period begins`

@export Under section 117.05(5), is the justice bound to include a statement of reasons in the record where no order, or a narrower order, is made?
GIVEN `Did the justice decline to make an order under subsection 117.05(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the justice decline to make an order under subsection 117.05(4)?
      `Did the justice make an order but not prohibit the possession of all the things the subsection refers to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the justice make an order but not prohibit the possession of all the things the subsection refers to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(5), is the justice bound to include a statement of reasons in the record where no order, or a narrower order, is made` IS
    `s 117.05(5) the justice is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` `Did the justice decline to make an order under subsection 117.05(4)` `Did the justice make an order but not prohibit the possession of all the things the subsection refers to`


@export Under section 117.05(6), do sections 113 to 117 apply to the order made against me
GIVEN `Is the order made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order against you an order made under subsection (4)?
      `Which section of the Code are you asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of the section you are asking about, for example 114 or 115.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(6), do sections 113 to 117 apply to the order made against me` IS
    `s 117.05(6) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` `Is the order made under subsection (4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `Which section of the Code are you asking about`, "")

@export Under section 117.05(7), may I appeal to the superior court against the order the justice made?
GIVEN `Are you the person in respect of whom the order is made, or from whom the thing was seized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person in respect of whom the order is made, or from whom the thing was seized?
      `Did the justice make an order under subsection 117.05(4) in respect of you, or of a thing seized from you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the justice make an order under subsection 117.05(4) in respect of you, or of a thing seized from you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(7), may I appeal to the superior court against the order the justice made` IS
    `s 117.05(7) the person may appeal to the superior court against the order` `Are you the person in respect of whom the order is made, or from whom the thing was seized` `Did the justice make an order under subsection 117.05(4) in respect of you, or of a thing seized from you`

@export Under section 117.05(8), may the Attorney General appeal to the superior court against the justice's failure to make the finding or the order?
GIVEN `Did the justice not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the justice not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)?
      `Did the justice make the finding but not make an order prohibiting possession under paragraph 117.05(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the justice make the finding but not make an order prohibiting possession under paragraph 117.05(4)(b)?
      `Is the appellant the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appellant the Attorney General?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(8), may the Attorney General appeal to the superior court against the justice's failure to make the finding or the order` IS
    `s 117.05(8) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the failure to make the finding or the order` `Did the justice not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)` `Did the justice make the finding but not make an order prohibiting possession under paragraph 117.05(4)(b)` `Is the appellant the Attorney General`


@export Under section 117.05(9), does a provision of Part XXVII apply to my appeal to the superior court
GIVEN `Which section of Part XXVII is in question` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of the section of Part XXVII you are asking about, for example 813.
      `Is it a provision of Part XXVII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the section a provision of Part XXVII (Summary Convictions)?
      `Is the appeal made under subsection (7) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal the appeal that subsection (7) or (8) of section 117.05 gives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.05(9), does a provision of Part XXVII apply to my appeal to the superior court` IS
    `s 117.05(9) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` `Which section of Part XXVII is in question` `Is it a provision of Part XXVII` `Is the appeal made under subsection (7) or (8)`

§§ `s 117.06 Where no finding or application`


@export Under section 117.06(1), is the thing or document seized from me to be returned to me?
GIVEN `Was the thing or document seized from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing or document seized from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)?
      `On what date was the warrant executed or the seizure made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the warrant executed, or the seizure made without a warrant?
      `What is today's date for this question` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which you are asking?
      `Was an application made under subsection 117.05(1) within thirty days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an application for an order for the disposition made under subsection 117.05(1) within thirty days after that date?
      `Did the justice not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If an application was made in time, did the justice not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.06(1), is the thing or document seized from me to be returned to me` IS
    `s 117.06(1) the thing or document is to be returned to the person from whom it was seized` `Was the thing or document seized from you under subsection 117.04(1) or (2)` (`s 117.06(1)(a) no application was made within thirty days` `On what date was the warrant executed or the seizure made` `What is today's date for this question` `Was an application made under subsection 117.05(1) within thirty days`) (`Was an application made under subsection 117.05(1) within thirty days` AND `Did the justice not make a finding as described in subsection 117.05(4)`)

@export Under section 117.06(2), may the justice order that the revocation of my authorization, licence or registration certificate be reversed and it be restored?
GIVEN `Was the thing returned to you under subsection 117.06(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing returned to you under subsection 117.06(1)?
      `Was an authorization, licence or registration certificate of yours revoked under subsection 117.04(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an authorization, licence or registration certificate of yours revoked under subsection 117.04(4)?
      `Is the person the justice referred to in paragraph 117.06(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the justice referred to in paragraph 117.06(1)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117.06(2), may the justice order that the revocation of my authorization, licence or registration certificate be reversed and it be restored` IS
    `s 117.06(2) the justice may order that the revocation be reversed and the authorization, licence or registration certificate restored` `Was the thing returned to you under subsection 117.06(1)` `Was an authorization, licence or registration certificate of yours revoked under subsection 117.04(4)` `Is the person the justice referred to in paragraph 117.06(1)(b)`

§ `Part III continued -- exempted persons and general provisions (ss 117.07 to 117.15)`

§§ `s 117.07 Public officers`

@export Under section 117.07(2), am I a public officer for the purposes of section 117.07?
GIVEN `Are you a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term?
