§ `Part IV -- Interpretation: section 118 ("In this Part")`

@export Under section 118, is what I said evidence or a statement?
GIVEN `Is what was said an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what was said an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge?
      `Is the assertion material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assertion material?
      `Is the assertion admissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assertion admissible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 118, is what I said evidence or a statement` IS
    `s 118 evidence or statement` `Is what was said an assertion of fact, opinion, belief or knowledge` `Is the assertion material` `Is the assertion admissible`


@export Under section 118, is the proceeding a judicial proceeding?
GIVEN `Where was the proceeding held` IS A `s 118 forum` @desc Where was the proceeding held? One of: s 118(a) in or under the authority of a court of justice; s 118(b) before the Senate or House of Commons or a committee of either, or a legislative council, legislative assembly or house of assembly or a committee of it authorized by law to administer an oath; s 118(c) before a court, judge, justice, provincial court judge or coroner; s 118(d) before an arbitrator or umpire, or a person or body authorized by law to make an inquiry and take evidence under oath; s 118(e) before a tribunal by which a legal right or legal liability may be established; or s 118 before none of those.
      `Is the proceeding invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason? (It does not matter to the answer.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 118, is the proceeding a judicial proceeding` IS
    `s 118 judicial proceeding` `Where was the proceeding held` `Is the proceeding invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason`

@export Under section 118, was I a witness?
GIVEN `Did you give evidence orally under oath or by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give evidence orally under oath or by affidavit?
      `Where was the evidence given` IS A `s 118 forum` @desc Where was the evidence given? (the kinds of forum are listed at "Under section 118, is the proceeding a judicial proceeding")
      `Is the proceeding invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason? (It does not matter to the answer.)
      `Are you a child of tender years who gave evidence but not under oath because the person presiding found you did not understand the nature of an oath` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a child of tender years who gave evidence but not under oath, because the person presiding found that you did not understand the nature of an oath?
      `Are you competent to be a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you competent to be a witness? (It does not matter to the answer.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 118, was I a witness` IS
    `s 118 witness` `Did you give evidence orally under oath or by affidavit` (`s 118 judicial proceeding` `Where was the evidence given` `Is the proceeding invalid for want of jurisdiction or for any other reason`) `Are you a child of tender years who gave evidence but not under oath because the person presiding found you did not understand the nature of an oath` `Are you competent to be a witness`

@export Under section 118, am I an official?
GIVEN `What do you hold` IS A `s 118 position` @desc What do you hold? One of: s 118(a) an office or appointment under the government; s 118(b) a civil or military commission; s 118(c) a position or an employment in a public department; or s 118 a position that is none of those.
      `Are you appointed or elected to discharge a public duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you appointed or elected to discharge a public duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 118, am I an official` IS
    `s 118 official` (`s 118 office` `What do you hold`) `Are you appointed or elected to discharge a public duty`

§ `Part IV -- Corruption and Disobedience (ss 119-130.1)`

§§ `s 119 Bribery of judicial officers, etc.`

@export Under section 119(1), is accepting, obtaining, giving or offering a benefit corruptly, in connection with a judicial office or a legislature, an offence on what I did?
GIVEN `s 119(1)(a): Do you hold a judicial office, or are you a member of Parliament or of a provincial legislature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a judicial office, or are you a member of Parliament or of a provincial legislature? (s 119(1)(a))
      `s 119(1)(a): Did you, directly or indirectly, accept, obtain, agree to accept or try to obtain, for yourself or anyone else, money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, accept, obtain, agree to accept or try to obtain, for yourself or anyone else, money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment? (s 119(1)(a))
      `s 119(1)(a): Did you act corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act corruptly? (s 119(1)(a))
      `s 119(1)(a): Was it in respect of something you did or left undone, or will do or leave undone, in your official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in respect of something you did or left undone, or will do or leave undone, in your official capacity? (s 119(1)(a))
      `s 119(1)(b): Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment to a judicial officer or legislator, or to anyone for their benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment to a judicial officer or legislator, or to anyone for their benefit? (s 119(1)(b))
      `s 119(1)(b): Did you act corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act corruptly? (s 119(1)(b))
      `s 119(1)(b): Was it in respect of something that person did or left undone, or will, in their official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in respect of something that person did or left undone, or will, in their official capacity? (s 119(1)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(1), is accepting, obtaining, giving or offering a benefit corruptly, in connection with a judicial office or a legislature, an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 119(1) the person is guilty of an indictable offence under subsection (1)` (`s 119(1)(a) the holder of a judicial office or legislator corruptly accepts or obtains a benefit` `s 119(1)(a): Do you hold a judicial office, or are you a member of Parliament or of a provincial legislature` `s 119(1)(a): Did you, directly or indirectly, accept, obtain, agree to accept or try to obtain, for yourself or anyone else, money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment` `s 119(1)(a): Did you act corruptly` `s 119(1)(a): Was it in respect of something you did or left undone, or will do or leave undone, in your official capacity`) (`s 119(1)(b) the person corruptly gives or offers a benefit to a judicial officer or legislator` `s 119(1)(b): Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment to a judicial officer or legislator, or to anyone for their benefit` `s 119(1)(b): Did you act corruptly` `s 119(1)(b): Was it in respect of something that person did or left undone, or will, in their official capacity`)

@export Under section 119(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 119(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 119(1) the class of the offence`

@export Under section 119(1), what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 119(1), what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment` IS
    `s 119(1) the punishment on indictment`

@export Under section 119(2), are the proceedings against me barred for want of the written consent of the Attorney General of Canada?
GIVEN `Are the proceedings against you being brought under section 119` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against you being brought under section 119?
      `Do you hold a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a judicial office?
      `Has the Attorney General of Canada consented in writing to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General of Canada consented in writing to the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119(2), are the proceedings against me barred for want of the written consent of the Attorney General of Canada` IS
    `s 119(2) the proceedings against a holder of a judicial office are barred for want of the written consent of the Attorney General of Canada` `Are the proceedings against you being brought under section 119` `Do you hold a judicial office` `Has the Attorney General of Canada consented in writing to the proceedings`

§§ `s 120 Bribery of officers`

@export Under section 120, is corruptly taking or giving a benefit, in connection with the administration of justice, an offence on what I did?
