      `s 120(a): Did you act with intent to procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to procure or facilitate the commission of an offence? (s 120(a))
      `s 120(a): Did you act with intent to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed, or intends to commit, an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed, or intends to commit, an offence? (s 120(a))
      `s 120(b): Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment to an officer of the kind section 120(a) names, or to anyone for their benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment to an officer of the kind section 120(a) names, or to anyone for their benefit? (s 120(b))
      `s 120(b): Did you act corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act corruptly? (s 120(b))
      `s 120(b): Did you act with intent that the officer should interfere with the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent that the officer should interfere with the administration of justice? (s 120(b))
      `s 120(b): Did you act with intent that the officer should procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent that the officer should procure or facilitate the commission of an offence? (s 120(b))
      `s 120(b): Did you act with intent that the officer should protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed, or intends to commit, an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent that the officer should protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed, or intends to commit, an offence? (s 120(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 120, is corruptly taking or giving a benefit, in connection with the administration of justice, an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 120 the person is guilty of an indictable offence under section 120` (`s 120(a) the officer or person employed in the administration of criminal law corruptly accepts or obtains a benefit with a stated intent` (IF `s 120(a): Are you a justice, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) (IF `s 120(a): Is the person a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) (IF `s 120(a): Is the person a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 120(a): Are you a police commissioner or an officer of a juvenile court, or employed in the administration of criminal law` `s 120(a): Did you, directly or indirectly, accept, obtain, agree to accept or try to obtain, for yourself or anyone else, money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment` `s 120(a): Did you act corruptly` `s 120(a): Did you act with intent to interfere with the administration of justice` `s 120(a): Did you act with intent to procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` `s 120(a): Did you act with intent to protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed, or intends to commit, an offence`) (`s 120(b) the person corruptly gives or offers a benefit to an officer with a stated intent` `s 120(b): Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer money, valuable consideration, an office, a place or employment to an officer of the kind section 120(a) names, or to anyone for their benefit` `s 120(b): Did you act corruptly` `s 120(b): Did you act with intent that the officer should interfere with the administration of justice` `s 120(b): Did you act with intent that the officer should procure or facilitate the commission of an offence` `s 120(b): Did you act with intent that the officer should protect from detection or punishment a person who has committed, or intends to commit, an offence`)

