      `s 121(1)(a): Being an official, did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept something from anyone, for yourself or another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Being an official, did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept something from anyone, for yourself or another person? (s 121(1)(a))
      `s 121(1)(a): Was it a loan, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a loan, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind? (s 121(1)(a))
      `s 121(1)(a): Was it given or received as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given or received as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission? (s 121(1)(a))
      `s 121(1)(a): Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government? (s 121(1)(a))
      `s 121(1)(a): Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow? (s 121(1)(a))
      `s 121(1)(a): Is the official in fact able to do what is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the official in fact able to do what is proposed? (s 121(1)(a))
      `s 121(1)(b): Do you have dealings of any kind with the government, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have dealings of any kind with the government, directly or indirectly? (s 121(1)(b))
      `s 121(1)(b): Did you pay a commission or reward to, or confer an advantage or benefit of any kind on, an employee or official of the government you deal with, or a member of their family, or anyone for their benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay a commission or reward to, or confer an advantage or benefit of any kind on, an employee or official of the government you deal with, or a member of their family, or anyone for their benefit? (s 121(1)(b))
      `s 121(1)(b): Was it with respect to those dealings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it with respect to those dealings? (s 121(1)(b))
      `s 121(1)(b): Do you have the written consent of the head of the branch of government with which you deal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the written consent of the head of the branch of government with which you deal? (s 121(1)(b))
      `s 121(1)(c): Are you an official or employee of the government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an official or employee of the government? (s 121(1)(c))
      `s 121(1)(c): Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept a commission, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind, for yourself or another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept a commission, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind, for yourself or another person? (s 121(1)(c))
      `s 121(1)(c): Was it from a person who has dealings with the government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it from a person who has dealings with the government? (s 121(1)(c))
      `s 121(1)(c): Do you have the written consent of the head of the branch of government that employs you, or of which you are an official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the written consent of the head of the branch of government that employs you, or of which you are an official? (s 121(1)(c))
      `s 121(1)(d): Do you have, or pretend to have, influence with the government, a minister of the government or an official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, or pretend to have, influence with the government, a minister of the government or an official? (s 121(1)(d))
      `s 121(1)(d): Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept, for yourself or another person, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept, for yourself or another person, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind? (s 121(1)(d))
      `s 121(1)(d): Was it as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission? (s 121(1)(d))
      `s 121(1)(d): Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government? (s 121(1)(d))
      `s 121(1)(d): Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow? (s 121(1)(d))
      `s 121(1)(d): Was it in connection with the appointment of any person, including yourself, to an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with the appointment of any person, including yourself, to an office? (s 121(1)(d))
      `s 121(1)(e): Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer, or agree to give or offer, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind to a minister or an official, or to anyone for their benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer, or agree to give or offer, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind to a minister or an official, or to anyone for their benefit? (s 121(1)(e))
      `s 121(1)(e): Was it as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission, by that minister or official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission, by that minister or official? (s 121(1)(e))
      `s 121(1)(e): Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government? (s 121(1)(e))
      `s 121(1)(e): Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow? (s 121(1)(e))
      `s 121(1)(e): Was it in connection with the appointment of any person, including yourself, to an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with the appointment of any person, including yourself, to an office? (s 121(1)(e))
      `s 121(1)(f): Have you made a tender to obtain a contract with the government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a tender to obtain a contract with the government? (s 121(1)(f))
