      `s 121(1)(f): Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind from another tenderer, for yourself or someone else, for the withdrawal of your own tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind from another tenderer, for yourself or someone else, for the withdrawal of your own tender? (s 121(1)(f))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 121(1), is giving, taking or arranging a benefit in dealings with the government an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 121(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` (`s 121(1)(a) the person gives to an official, or an official takes, a benefit for cooperation or influence in government business` (IF `s 121(1)(a): Is the person an official, as section 118 defines the term (a person who holds an office, or is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 121(1)(a): Did you, directly or indirectly, give, offer or agree to give or offer something to an official, to a member of an official's family, or to anyone for an official's benefit` `s 121(1)(a): Being an official, did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept something from anyone, for yourself or another person` `s 121(1)(a): Was it a loan, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` `s 121(1)(a): Was it given or received as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission` `s 121(1)(a): Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` `s 121(1)(a): Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow` `s 121(1)(a): Is the official in fact able to do what is proposed`) (`s 121(1)(b) the person having dealings with the government pays or confers a benefit on its employee or official without written consent` `s 121(1)(b): Do you have dealings of any kind with the government, directly or indirectly` `s 121(1)(b): Did you pay a commission or reward to, or confer an advantage or benefit of any kind on, an employee or official of the government you deal with, or a member of their family, or anyone for their benefit` `s 121(1)(b): Was it with respect to those dealings` `s 121(1)(b): Do you have the written consent of the head of the branch of government with which you deal`) (`s 121(1)(c) the official or employee of the government takes a benefit from a person dealing with it without written consent` `s 121(1)(c): Are you an official or employee of the government` `s 121(1)(c): Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept a commission, reward, advantage or benefit of any kind, for yourself or another person` `s 121(1)(c): Was it from a person who has dealings with the government` `s 121(1)(c): Do you have the written consent of the head of the branch of government that employs you, or of which you are an official`) (`s 121(1)(d) the person with, or pretending to have, influence demands or accepts a reward for it` `s 121(1)(d): Do you have, or pretend to have, influence with the government, a minister of the government or an official` `s 121(1)(d): Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept, for yourself or another person, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind` `s 121(1)(d): Was it as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission` `s 121(1)(d): Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` `s 121(1)(d): Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow` `s 121(1)(d): Was it in connection with the appointment of any person, including yourself, to an office`) (`s 121(1)(e) the person gives or offers a reward to a minister or an official for cooperation or influence` `s 121(1)(e): Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer, or agree to give or offer, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind to a minister or an official, or to anyone for their benefit` `s 121(1)(e): Was it as consideration for cooperation, assistance, exercise of influence, or an act or omission, by that minister or official` `s 121(1)(e): Was it in connection with the transaction of business with, or any matter of business relating to, the government` `s 121(1)(e): Was it in connection with a claim against Her Majesty, or a benefit Her Majesty is authorized or entitled to bestow` `s 121(1)(e): Was it in connection with the appointment of any person, including yourself, to an office`) (`s 121(1)(f) the person having tendered for a government contract gives, offers, demands or accepts a reward for a tender's withdrawal` `s 121(1)(f): Have you made a tender to obtain a contract with the government` `s 121(1)(f): Did you, directly or indirectly, give or offer, or agree to give or offer, a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind to another tenderer, their family or someone for their benefit, for the withdrawal of their tender` `s 121(1)(f): Did you, directly or indirectly, demand, accept, or offer or agree to accept a reward, advantage or benefit of any kind from another tenderer, for yourself or someone else, for the withdrawal of your own tender`)

