GIVEN `Is the person an official, as section 118 defines the term (a person who holds an office, or is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an official, as section 118 defines the term (a person who holds an office, or is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty)?
      `Did you commit fraud or a breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit fraud or a breach of trust?
      `Was it in connection with the duties of your office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in connection with the duties of your office?
      `Would it be an offence if it were committed in relation to a private person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it be an offence if it were committed in relation to a private person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 122, is an official's fraud or breach of trust in connection with the duties of their office an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 122 the official commits fraud or a breach of trust in connection with the duties of their office` (IF `Is the person an official, as section 118 defines the term (a person who holds an office, or is appointed or elected to discharge a public duty)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `Did you commit fraud or a breach of trust` `Was it in connection with the duties of your office` `Would it be an offence if it were committed in relation to a private person`

@export Under section 122, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
