§§ `s 129 Offences relating to public or peace officer`

@export Under section 129, is resisting or obstructing an officer, or a person executing process, or failing to assist an officer, an offence on what I did?
GIVEN `s 129(a): Is the officer a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 129(a))
      `s 129(a): Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 129(a))
      `s 129(a): Did you resist or wilfully obstruct the officer in the execution of their duty, or a person lawfully acting in aid of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you resist or wilfully obstruct the officer in the execution of their duty, or a person lawfully acting in aid of the officer? (s 129(a))
      `s 129(b): Is the officer a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 129(b))
      `s 129(b): Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 129(b))
      `s 129(b): Did you omit to assist the officer in arresting a person or in preserving the peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you omit to assist the officer in arresting a person or in preserving the peace? (s 129(b))
      `s 129(b): Did you have a reasonable excuse for not assisting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for not assisting? (s 129(b))
      `s 129(b): Had you been given reasonable notice that you were required to assist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you been given reasonable notice that you were required to assist? (s 129(b))
      `s 129(c): Did you resist or wilfully obstruct a person in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods, or in making a lawful distress or seizure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you resist or wilfully obstruct a person in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods, or in making a lawful distress or seizure? (s 129(c))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 129, is resisting or obstructing an officer, or a person executing process, or failing to assist an officer, an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 129 the person is guilty of an offence under section 129` (`s 129(a) the person resists or wilfully obstructs a public officer or peace officer in the execution of their duty` (IF `s 129(a): Is the officer a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) (IF `s 129(a): Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 129(a): Did you resist or wilfully obstruct the officer in the execution of their duty, or a person lawfully acting in aid of the officer`) (`s 129(b) the person omits without reasonable excuse to assist a public officer or peace officer after reasonable notice` (IF `s 129(b): Is the officer a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) (IF `s 129(b): Is the officer a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 129(b): Did you omit to assist the officer in arresting a person or in preserving the peace` `s 129(b): Did you have a reasonable excuse for not assisting` `s 129(b): Had you been given reasonable notice that you were required to assist`) (`s 129(c) the person resists or wilfully obstructs a person in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods, or in a lawful distress or seizure` `s 129(c): Did you resist or wilfully obstruct a person in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods, or in making a lawful distress or seizure`)

@export Under section 129, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 129, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 129 the class of the offence`

