GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 129(d), what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment` IS
    `s 129(d) the punishment on indictment`

§§ `s 130 Personating peace officer`

@export Under section 130(1), is falsely representing myself to be a peace officer or public officer, or using a badge or uniform that way, an offence on what I did?
GIVEN `s 130(1)(a): Did you falsely represent yourself to be a peace officer or a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you falsely represent yourself to be a peace officer or a public officer? (s 130(1)(a))
      `s 130(1)(b): Are you a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 130(1)(b))
      `s 130(1)(b): Are you a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 130(1)(b))
      `s 130(1)(b): Did you use a badge or an article of uniform or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use a badge or an article of uniform or equipment? (s 130(1)(b))
      `s 130(1)(b): Was it in a manner likely to cause people to believe you are a peace officer or a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in a manner likely to cause people to believe you are a peace officer or a public officer? (s 130(1)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 130(1), is falsely representing myself to be a peace officer or public officer, or using a badge or uniform that way, an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 130(1) the person commits an offence under subsection (1)` (`s 130(1)(a) the person falsely represents themselves to be a peace officer or a public officer` `s 130(1)(a): Did you falsely represent yourself to be a peace officer or a public officer`) (`s 130(1)(b) the person who is neither uses a badge, uniform or equipment likely to cause others to believe they are one` (IF `s 130(1)(b): Are you a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `s 130(1)(b): Are you a public officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) `s 130(1)(b): Did you use a badge or an article of uniform or equipment` `s 130(1)(b): Was it in a manner likely to cause people to believe you are a peace officer or a public officer`)

