§ `Part IV -- Misleading Justice (ss 131-143)`

§§ `s 131 Perjury`

@export Under section 131(3), do subsections 131(1) and (1.1) not apply to a statement I made without being specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make it?
GIVEN `Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(3), do subsections 131(1) and (1.1) not apply to a statement I made without being specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make it` IS
    `s 131(3) subsections (1) and (1.1) do not apply to a statement made by a person not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make it` `Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement`

@export Under section 131(1), is making a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation, knowing it is false and with intent to mislead, perjury on what I did?
GIVEN `Did you make the statement before a person authorized by law to permit it to be made before them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the statement before a person authorized by law to permit it to be made before them?
      `Was it a false statement made under oath or solemn affirmation, by affidavit, solemn declaration, deposition or orally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a false statement made under oath or solemn affirmation, by affidavit, solemn declaration, deposition or orally?
      `Did you act with intent to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to mislead?
      `Did you know that the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the statement was false?
      `s 131(3): Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(1), is making a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation, knowing it is false and with intent to mislead, perjury on what I did` IS
    `s 131(1) the person commits perjury by a false statement under oath or solemn affirmation` `Did you make the statement before a person authorized by law to permit it to be made before them` `Was it a false statement made under oath or solemn affirmation, by affidavit, solemn declaration, deposition or orally` `Did you act with intent to mislead` `Did you know that the statement was false` (`s 131(3) subsections (1) and (1.1) do not apply to a statement made by a person not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make it` `s 131(3): Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement`)

@export Under section 131(1.1), is making a false statement by video link or under a mutual legal assistance order, knowing it is false and with intent to mislead, perjury on what I did?
GIVEN `Did you give evidence under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act (evidence by video or audio link from outside Canada)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give evidence under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act (evidence by video or audio link from outside Canada)?
      `Did you give evidence or a statement under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give evidence or a statement under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act?
      `Did you make a false statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a false statement?
      `Did you act with intent to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to mislead?
      `Did you know that the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the statement was false?
      `Was the statement made otherwise than in accordance with the formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada where you were virtually present or heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement made otherwise than in accordance with the formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada where you were virtually present or heard?
      `s 131(3): Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement?
      `Was the statement made under oath or solemn affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement made under oath or solemn affirmation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(1.1), is making a false statement by video link or under a mutual legal assistance order, knowing it is false and with intent to mislead, perjury on what I did` IS
    `s 131(1.1) the person commits perjury by a false statement given by video link or under a mutual legal assistance order` `Did you give evidence under subsection 46(2) of the Canada Evidence Act (evidence by video or audio link from outside Canada)` `Did you give evidence or a statement under an order made under section 22.2 of the Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` `Did you make a false statement` `Did you act with intent to mislead` `Did you know that the statement was false` `Was the statement made otherwise than in accordance with the formalities required by the law of the place outside Canada where you were virtually present or heard` (`s 131(3) subsections (1) and (1.1) do not apply to a statement made by a person not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make it` `s 131(3): Were you not specially permitted, authorized or required by law to make the statement`) `Was the statement made under oath or solemn affirmation`

@export Under section 131(2), does section 131(1) apply to my statement whether or not it was made in a judicial proceeding?
GIVEN `Is it a false statement of the kind section 131(1) describes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a false statement of the kind section 131(1) describes?
      `Was it made in a judicial proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in a judicial proceeding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 131(2), does section 131(1) apply to my statement whether or not it was made in a judicial proceeding` IS
    `s 131(2) subsection (1) applies whether or not the statement is made in a judicial proceeding` `Is it a false statement of the kind section 131(1) describes` `Was it made in a judicial proceeding`

§§ `s 132 Punishment`

@export Under section 132, is a person who commits perjury guilty of an indictable offence?
GIVEN `Did what you did amount to perjury under section 131` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did what you did amount to perjury under section 131?
