§ `Part IV -- Escapes and Rescues (ss 144-149)`

§§ `s 144 Prison breach`

@export Under section 144, is breaking a prison, or breaking out of a cell within one, to escape or set someone free an offence on what I did?
GIVEN `s 144(a): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)? (s 144(a))
      `s 144(a): Did you, by force or violence, break the prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, by force or violence, break the prison? (s 144(a))
      `s 144(a): Did you act with intent to set at liberty yourself, or anyone else confined in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to set at liberty yourself, or anyone else confined in it? (s 144(a))
      `s 144(b): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)? (s 144(b))
      `s 144(b): Are you confined in a cell or other place within the prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you confined in a cell or other place within the prison? (s 144(b))
      `s 144(b): Did you break out of, or make a breach in, the cell or other place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you break out of, or make a breach in, the cell or other place? (s 144(b))
      `s 144(b): Did you act with intent to escape forcibly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to escape forcibly? (s 144(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 144, is breaking a prison, or breaking out of a cell within one, to escape or set someone free an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 144 the person is guilty of an offence under section 144` (`s 144(a) the person by force or violence breaks a prison with intent to set at liberty a person confined in it` (IF `s 144(a): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 144(a): Did you, by force or violence, break the prison` `s 144(a): Did you act with intent to set at liberty yourself, or anyone else confined in it`) (`s 144(b) the person confined in a prison with intent to escape forcibly breaks out of, or makes a breach in, a cell or other place within it` (IF `s 144(b): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 144(b): Are you confined in a cell or other place within the prison` `s 144(b): Did you break out of, or make a breach in, the cell or other place` `s 144(b): Did you act with intent to escape forcibly`)

@export Under section 144, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 144, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 144 the class of the offence`

@export Under section 144, what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 144, what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment` IS
    `s 144 the punishment on indictment`

