DECIDE `Under section 145(5)(b), is failing without lawful excuse to comply with an order under section 515(12), 516.1(1) or 522(2.1) an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 145(5)(b) the person bound by an order under section 515(12), 516.1(1) or 522(2.1) fails without lawful excuse to comply` `Are you bound to comply with an order under subsection 515(12), 516.1(1) or 522(2.1)` `Did you fail to comply with that order` `Did you have a lawful excuse for what you did or left undone` (`s 145(8) the failure is with lawful excuse because the Attorney General has made an election under section 50 of the Contraventions Act` `s 145(8): Is it a failure to attend court as a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order requires, to comply with a condition of an undertaking or release order, or to appear at the time and place stated for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` `s 145(8): Before the failure, did the Attorney General, within the meaning of the Contraventions Act, make an election under section 50 of that Act`)

@export Under section 145(5), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
