    `s 145(11) the certificate is barred from reception in evidence for want of reasonable notice before the trial` `Is the certificate tendered against you under section 145(9)` `Before the trial, did the party who intends to produce the certificate give you reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of it`

§§ `s 146 Permitting or assisting escape`

@export Under section 146, is permitting an escape, conveying a thing into a prison to help one, or procuring a prisoner's improper discharge an offence on what I did?
GIVEN `s 146(a): Do you have a person in lawful custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a person in lawful custody? (s 146(a))
      `s 146(a): Did you permit that person to escape by failing to perform a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you permit that person to escape by failing to perform a legal duty? (s 146(a))
      `s 146(b): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)? (s 146(b))
      `s 146(b): Did you convey, or cause to be conveyed, anything into the prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you convey, or cause to be conveyed, anything into the prison? (s 146(b))
      `s 146(b): Did you act with intent to facilitate the escape of a person imprisoned in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to facilitate the escape of a person imprisoned in it? (s 146(b))
      `s 146(c): Did you direct or procure the discharge of a prisoner under colour of pretended authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you direct or procure the discharge of a prisoner under colour of pretended authority? (s 146(c))
      `s 146(c): Was the prisoner not entitled to be discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the prisoner not entitled to be discharged? (s 146(c))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 146, is permitting an escape, conveying a thing into a prison to help one, or procuring a prisoner's improper discharge an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 146 the person is guilty of an offence under section 146` (`s 146(a) the person permits a person in lawful custody to escape by failing to perform a legal duty` `s 146(a): Do you have a person in lawful custody` `s 146(a): Did you permit that person to escape by failing to perform a legal duty`) (`s 146(b) the person conveys a thing into a prison with intent to facilitate an escape` (IF `s 146(b): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 146(b): Did you convey, or cause to be conveyed, anything into the prison` `s 146(b): Did you act with intent to facilitate the escape of a person imprisoned in it`) (`s 146(c) the person under colour of pretended authority directs or procures the discharge of a prisoner who is not entitled to be discharged` `s 146(c): Did you direct or procure the discharge of a prisoner under colour of pretended authority` `s 146(c): Was the prisoner not entitled to be discharged`)

@export Under section 146, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 146, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 146 the class of the offence`

@export Under section 146, what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 146, what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment` IS
    `s 146 the punishment on indictment`

§§ `s 147 Rescue or permitting escape`

@export Under section 147, is rescuing a person from lawful custody, or helping or wilfully permitting an escape, an offence on what I did?
GIVEN `s 147(a): Did you rescue a person from lawful custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you rescue a person from lawful custody? (s 147(a))
      `s 147(a): Did you assist a person in escaping, or attempting to escape, from lawful custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you assist a person in escaping, or attempting to escape, from lawful custody? (s 147(a))
      `s 147(b): Is the person a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term? (s 147(b))
      `s 147(b): Did you wilfully permit a person in your lawful custody to escape` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you wilfully permit a person in your lawful custody to escape? (s 147(b))
      `s 147(c): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)? (s 147(c))
      `s 147(c): Are you an officer of, or an employee in, the prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of, or an employee in, the prison? (s 147(c))
      `s 147(c): Did you wilfully permit a person to escape from lawful custody in the prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you wilfully permit a person to escape from lawful custody in the prison? (s 147(c))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 147, is rescuing a person from lawful custody, or helping or wilfully permitting an escape, an offence on what I did` IS
    `s 147 the person is guilty of an offence under section 147` (`s 147(a) the person rescues a person from lawful custody or assists a person in escaping or attempting to escape from lawful custody` `s 147(a): Did you rescue a person from lawful custody` `s 147(a): Did you assist a person in escaping, or attempting to escape, from lawful custody`) (`s 147(b) the peace officer wilfully permits a person in their lawful custody to escape` (IF `s 147(b): Is the person a peace officer, as section 2 of the Code defines the term` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 147(b): Did you wilfully permit a person in your lawful custody to escape`) (`s 147(c) the officer of or employee in a prison wilfully permits a person to escape from lawful custody in it` (IF `s 147(c): Is the place a prison, as section 2 of the Code defines the term (it includes a penitentiary, common jail, public or reformatory prison, lock-up, guard-room or other place where persons charged with or convicted of offences are usually kept in custody)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `s 147(c): Are you an officer of, or an employee in, the prison` `s 147(c): Did you wilfully permit a person to escape from lawful custody in the prison`)

@export Under section 147, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 147, is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 147 the class of the offence`

@export Under section 147, what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 147, what is the greatest imprisonment I face on indictment` IS
    `s 147 the punishment on indictment`

