      `Did you escape from lawful custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you escape from lawful custody?
      `Were you, without lawful excuse, at large before the end of a term of imprisonment you were sentenced to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, without lawful excuse, at large before the end of a term of imprisonment you were sentenced to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 149(2), is what I did an escape` IS
    `s 149(2) escape` `Did you break prison` `Did you escape from lawful custody` `Were you, without lawful excuse, at large before the end of a term of imprisonment you were sentenced to`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc6 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc6-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER for Part V of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, ss 150 to 182 (sexual offences, public morals and disorderly conduct).
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence, what its gravity
-- and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply, and what follows from a conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09,
-- but this is a plain seat layer: no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer asks the questions of the modules imported above and calls their rules; it restates none. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), one per fact
-- the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. A borrowed term of section 2 (dwelling-house, night, peace officer, common-law partner) is asked as a fact (guide section 4):
-- the person says yes or no, and the answer is passed to the layer-1 rule as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE, so that a NOTHING from one of those definitions is not reachable from here (the layer-1 tests cover that path).
-- The terms of section 150 are worked out from the person's facts by `s 150 ...`.
-- Every question name begins "Under section N," so that no two parts' questions can share a name. A question's name asks what its body answers, in the same direction: a bar is asked as "does the bar apply",
-- a defence as "does section N give me a defence", a power as "may the court ...", a duty as "must the court ...". JUST FALSE and NOTHING are not turned into each other (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
-- Where an offence section says "or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction" and states no penalty, the penalty is that of s 787(1) (another part): the punishments questions return, for that limb,
-- the placeholder `ss 150 to 182 the penalty of s 787(1) is not stated in Part V`, which says that Part V states none.

`ss 150 to 182 the penalty of s 787(1) is not stated in Part V` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`


§ `s 150 -- the words of this Part`

@export Under section 150, am I a guardian of the other person?
GIVEN `I have in law the custody or control of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, in law, the custody or control of the other person?
      `I have in fact the custody or control of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, in fact (whatever the law says), the custody or control of the other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150, am I a guardian of the other person` IS
    `s 150 guardian` `I have in law the custody or control of the other person` `I have in fact the custody or control of the other person`

@export Under section 150, is the place a public place?
GIVEN `the public have access to it as of right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the public have access to the place as of right?
      `the public have access to it by an express invitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the public have access to the place by an express invitation?
      `the public have access to it by an implied invitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the public have access to the place by an implied invitation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150, is the place a public place` IS
    `s 150 public place` `the public have access to it as of right` `the public have access to it by an express invitation` `the public have access to it by an implied invitation`

@export Under section 150, is the place a theatre?
GIVEN `the place is open to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place open to the public?
      `entertainments are given there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are entertainments given there (whether or not a charge is made for admission)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150, is the place a theatre` IS
    `s 150 theatre` `the place is open to the public` `entertainments are given there`

@export Under section 150, is the part of the body in question a sexual organ?
GIVEN `the part of the body` IS A `s 150 part of the body` @desc Which part of the body: s 150 genital organs, s 150 breasts that are female breasts, s 150 breasts that appear to be female breasts, s 150 the anal region, or s 150 a part of the body that is none of those?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150, is the part of the body in question a sexual organ` IS
    `s 150 sexual organs` `the part of the body`

§ `s 150.1 -- consent as a defence, and mistake of age`

-- Situational: only for a person charged with one of the offences the section names (ss 151, 152, 153(1), 160(3), 173(2), 271 to 273, and the offences of subsection (5)).

@export Under section 150.1, what does the section say about whether the complainant's consent is a defence?
GIVEN `the section under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 151, or 271)?
      `the subsection under which I am charged` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection are you charged, as the Code writes it (for example "(1)"), or "" if the section has none?
      `the complainant's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old was the complainant at the time of the alleged offence, in years?
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you at the time of the alleged offence, in years?
      `I am in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant?
      `the complainant is in a relationship of dependency with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the complainant a person with whom you have a relationship of dependency (they depend on you)?
      `my relationship with the complainant is exploitative of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your relationship with the complainant exploitative of them?
      `on that day I was the complainant's common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the day on which subsection 150.1(2.2) came into force, were you the complainant's common-law partner (cohabiting in a conjugal relationship for at least a year)?
      `on that day I had been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for less than one year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, had you been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for less than one year?
      `on that day we had had, or were expecting to have, a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, had you and the complainant had, or were you expecting to have, a child as a result of the relationship?
      `immediately before the day subsection 150.1(2.3) came into force I was married to the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the day on which subsection 150.1(2.3) came into force, were you married to the complainant?
GIVETH A `s 150.1 consent as a defence`
DECIDE `Under section 150.1, what does the section say about whether the complainant's consent is a defence` IS
    `s 150.1 whether it is a defence that the complainant consented` `my charge` `my relationship` `my transitional facts`
    WHERE
        `my charge` MEANS `s 150.1 charge` WITH
            `the offence charged` IS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section under which I am charged`, `the subsection under which I am charged`
            `the age of the complainant, in years` IS `the complainant's age in years`
            `the age of the accused, in years` IS `my age in years`
        `my relationship` MEANS `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant` WITH
            `the accused is in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant` IS `I am in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant`
            `the accused is a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency` IS `the complainant is in a relationship of dependency with me`
            `the accused is in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant` IS `my relationship with the complainant is exploitative of the complainant`
        `my transitional facts` MEANS `s 150.1 transitional facts` WITH
            `s 2 common-law partner: on the day on which subsection 150.1(2.2) came into force the accused was the complainant's common-law partner` IS (IF `on that day I was the complainant's common-law partner` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
            `on that day the accused had been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for a period of less than one year` IS `on that day I had been cohabiting with the complainant in a conjugal relationship for less than one year`
            `on that day the accused and the complainant had had, or were expecting to have, a child as a result of the relationship` IS `on that day we had had, or were expecting to have, a child`
            `immediately before the day on which subsection 150.1(2.3) came into force the accused was married to the complainant` IS `immediately before the day subsection 150.1(2.3) came into force I was married to the complainant`

@export Under section 150.1(3), does the bar apply so that I may not be tried because I was aged twelve or thirteen?
GIVEN `the section under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 151, or 271)?
      `the subsection under which I am charged` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection are you charged, as the Code writes it (for example "(1)"), or "" if the section has none?
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you at the time of the alleged offence, in years?
      `I am in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant?
      `the complainant is in a relationship of dependency with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the complainant a person with whom you have a relationship of dependency (they depend on you)?
      `my relationship with the complainant is exploitative of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your relationship with the complainant exploitative of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150.1(3), does the bar apply so that I may not be tried because I was aged twelve or thirteen` IS
    `s 150.1(3) no person aged twelve or thirteen shall be tried: the bar applies` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section under which I am charged`, `the subsection under which I am charged`) `my age in years` `my relationship`
    WHERE
        `my relationship` MEANS `s 150.1 relationship of the accused to the complainant` WITH
            `the accused is in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant` IS `I am in a position of trust or authority towards the complainant`
            `the accused is a person with whom the complainant is in a relationship of dependency` IS `the complainant is in a relationship of dependency with me`
            `the accused is in a relationship with the complainant that is exploitative of the complainant` IS `my relationship with the complainant is exploitative of the complainant`

@export Under section 150.1(4), does the bar apply so that my belief that the complainant was 16 or older is no defence?
GIVEN `the section under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 151, or 271)?
      `the subsection under which I am charged` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection are you charged, as the Code writes it (for example "(1)"), or "" if the section has none?
      `I believed that the complainant was 16 years of age or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the complainant was 16 years of age or more at the time?
      `I took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take all reasonable steps to find out the complainant's age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150.1(4), does the bar apply so that my belief that the complainant was 16 or older is no defence` IS
    `s 150.1(4) the belief that the complainant was 16 or more is not a defence: the bar applies` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section under which I am charged`, `the subsection under which I am charged`) `I believed that the complainant was 16 years of age or more` `I took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant`

@export Under section 150.1(5), does the bar apply so that my belief that the complainant was 18 or older is no defence?
GIVEN `the section under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 151, or 271)?
      `the subsection under which I am charged` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection are you charged, as the Code writes it (for example "(1)"), or "" if the section has none?
      `I believed that the complainant was 18 years of age or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe that the complainant was 18 years of age or more at the time?
      `I took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take all reasonable steps to find out the complainant's age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150.1(5), does the bar apply so that my belief that the complainant was 18 or older is no defence` IS
