      `what I counselled or incited them to do` IS A `s 153.1(1) what the person counselled or incited the other person to do` @desc What did you counsel or incite them to do: s 153.1(1)(a) touch, s 153.1(1)(b) expose their own sexual organs, or s 153.1(1) something else?
      `they voluntarily agreed to the sexual activity in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they voluntarily agree to the sexual activity in question?
      `their agreement was present at the time the activity took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was their agreement present at the time the activity took place?
      `another circumstance in which no consent is obtained applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did another circumstance apply in which no consent is obtained (including one of section 265(3))?
      `no consent was obtained for a reason in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any of the circumstances of subsection (3) present (words of another, unconscious, incapable, abuse of trust, lack of agreement expressed, agreement withdrawn)?
