§ `ss 162 to 162.2 -- voyeurism, intimate images and the Internet prohibition`

-- Situational for the last two questions: only for a person convicted, or discharged on the conditions of a probation order, of an offence the section names.

@export Under section 162(1), is what I did voyeurism?
GIVEN `what I did to the other person` IS A `s 162(1) what the person did` @desc What did you do: s 162(1) observed (including by mechanical or electronic means), s 162(1) made a visual recording of, or s 162(1) neither?
      `I did it surreptitiously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it surreptitiously?
      `the other person was in circumstances that give rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the other person in circumstances that give rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy?
      `the other person was in a place where a person can reasonably be expected to be nude or nearly nude, to expose their sexual organs or to be engaged in explicit sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the other person in a place where a person can reasonably be expected to be nude or nearly nude, to expose their sexual organs or to be engaged in explicit sexual activity?
      `the other person was nude, nearly nude, exposing their sexual organs, or engaged in explicit sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the other person nude, nearly nude, exposing their sexual organs, or engaged in explicit sexual activity?
      `I did it for the purpose of observing or recording a person in such a state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it for the purpose of observing or recording a person in such a state or engaged in such an activity?
      `I did it for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it for a sexual purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 162(1), is what I did voyeurism` IS
    `s 162(1) the conduct is the offence of voyeurism` `what I did to the other person` `I did it surreptitiously` `the other person was in circumstances that give rise to a reasonable expectation of privacy` `the other person was in a place where a person can reasonably be expected to be nude or nearly nude, to expose their sexual organs or to be engaged in explicit sexual activity` `the other person was nude, nearly nude, exposing their sexual organs, or engaged in explicit sexual activity` `I did it for the purpose of observing or recording a person in such a state` `I did it for a sexual purpose`

