GIVEN `I acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without lawful excuse?
      `I loitered or prowled on the property of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you loiter or prowl on the property of another person?
      `it was at night` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it at night?
      `I was near a dwelling-house situated on that property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it near a dwelling-house situated on that property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 177, is what I did trespassing at night` IS
    `s 177 the conduct is the offence of trespassing at night` `I acted without lawful excuse` `I loitered or prowled on the property of another person` (IF `it was at night` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `I was near a dwelling-house situated on that property` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 177, what punishment am I liable to for trespassing at night?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 177, what punishment am I liable to for trespassing at night` IS
    `s 177 the punishment on summary conviction` `ss 150 to 182 the penalty of s 787(1) is not stated in Part V`

@export Under section 180(1), is what I did committing a common nuisance?
GIVEN `I did an unlawful act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do an unlawful act?
      `I failed to discharge a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to discharge a legal duty?
      `what I thereby did` IS A `s 180(2) what the unlawful act or failure endangers or obstructs` @desc What did the act or failure do: s 180(2)(a) endangers the lives, safety, health, property or comfort of the public, s 180(2)(b) obstructs the public in the exercise or enjoyment of a right common to all, or s 180(2) none of those?
      `by doing so I endanger the lives, safety or health of the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you thereby endanger the lives, safety or health of the public?
      `by doing so I cause physical injury to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you thereby cause physical injury to any person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 180(1), is what I did committing a common nuisance` IS
    `s 180(1) the conduct is the offence of committing a common nuisance` (`s 180(2) the person commits a common nuisance` `I did an unlawful act` `I failed to discharge a legal duty` `what I thereby did`) `by doing so I endanger the lives, safety or health of the public` `by doing so I cause physical injury to any person`

@export Under section 180(1), what punishments am I liable to for a common nuisance?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 180(1), what punishments am I liable to for a common nuisance` IS
    LIST `s 180(1) the punishment on indictment`, (`s 180(1) the punishment on summary conviction` `ss 150 to 182 the penalty of s 787(1) is not stated in Part V`)

@export Under section 182, is what I did an offence concerning a dead human body?
GIVEN `I neglected, without lawful excuse, a duty about the burial of a dead human body or human remains` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you neglect, without lawful excuse, to perform a duty imposed on you by law or undertaken by you with reference to the burial of a dead human body or human remains?
      `I improperly or indecently interfered with, or offered an indignity to, a dead human body or human remains` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you improperly or indecently interfere with, or offer an indignity to, a dead human body or human remains, whether buried or not?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 182, is what I did an offence concerning a dead human body` IS
    `s 182 the conduct is the offence concerning a dead human body` `I neglected, without lawful excuse, a duty about the burial of a dead human body or human remains` `I improperly or indecently interfered with, or offered an indignity to, a dead human body or human remains`

@export Under section 182, what punishments am I liable to for an offence concerning a dead human body?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 182, what punishments am I liable to for an offence concerning a dead human body` IS
    LIST `s 182 the punishment on indictment`, (`s 182 the punishment on summary conviction` `ss 150 to 182 the penalty of s 787(1) is not stated in Part V`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc7 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI (Invasion of Privacy), sections 183 to 196.1 -- THE SEAT LAYER (ccc7).
-- Source of the law: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence, what its gravity and penalty are,
-- what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model,
-- as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer asks, for that person, the questions Part VI answers: whether listening in, recording, possessing a listening device or passing on what was intercepted is an offence and what the penalty is;
-- which saving provisions protect them; what the police and the Crown had to do before using an interception against them (authorizations, the sealed packet, notice before the evidence is used, further particulars);
-- what happens to their right to be told they were intercepted; and what follows from a conviction (forfeiture of the device, punitive damages).
-- Nothing here is new law: every question builds the records of the layer-1 modules from plain inputs and calls their rules. There is no seat for an official: what the judge, the Attorney General and the Minister do is asked only
-- as what it means for the person (what may be done to them, what they must be given and by when). Section 195 (the annual reports) addresses only officials and has no question here.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (full statement in NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc7)"): a yes/no question answers JUST TRUE (yes, on the text's own words), JUST FALSE (no, in the text's own words),
-- or NOTHING (not covered: the text is silent, lists without closing the list, or the answer turns on a term in another part). NOTHING is never "no". An offence question's JUST FALSE says that this subsection
-- does not make the conduct an offence; it is not a finding of innocence and says nothing about other offences. A "may ... if" question whose conditions are not met answers NOTHING, not "no" (ruling of 2026-11-12);
-- a "may ... where" question answers JUST FALSE when the "where" is not met (each is listed in NOTES.md under the fork register, because the 2026-11-12 ruling leaves that reading undecided);
-- a permission the text limits with "up to" or "not exceeding" (thirty-six hours, one year, five thousand dollars) answers NOTHING beyond the limit, because the text grants up to it and does not say that more is refused;
-- a requirement that an authorization or extension "shall" not exceed a period (sixty days, three years) answers JUST FALSE beyond it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. One input per fact the person can state; where the law's own term is borrowed from another section or Act ("criminal organization", "terrorism offence", "computer system as defined in section 342.1(2)",
-- "reasonable grounds") it is asked as a plain fact. In the questions about an ordinary private communication, whether it was a radio-based telephone communication is a plain yes/no (assumed, not ruled);
-- the questions about radio-based telephone communications work it out. The summary-conviction limb of every offence states no penalty: section 787(1), in another part, supplies it, so the penalty questions here answer the
-- indictment limb only and say so.

§ `Section 183 -- Definitions: what Part VI covers`

-- Plumbing used by several questions: the layer-1 definitions, called from plain facts.
GIVEN `it is a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 seat the thing is a device within Part VI` MEANS
    `s 183 electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device` `it is a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`

GIVEN `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who made it was in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was meant for a person in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was a radio-based telephone communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 seat the communication is a private communication` MEANS
    `s 183 private communication` `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` `the person who made it was in Canada` `it was meant for a person in Canada` `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was a radio-based telephone communication`) `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it`

GIVEN statute IS A `s 183 statute`
      section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 183 provision of an Act`
`s 183 seat the provision of an Act` MEANS
    `s 183 provision of an Act` WITH `statute` IS statute, `section` IS section, `subsection` IS subsection

@export Under section 183, is the offence I am suspected of an offence within Part VI's definition of offence?
GIVEN form IS A `s 2 form of the charge` @desc How are you charged or suspected: with the offence itself, a conspiracy to commit it, an attempt to commit it, being an accessory after the fact, or counselling it?
      statute IS A `s 183 statute` @desc Which Act is the offence in? (The Criminal Code, or one of the other Acts section 183 names.)
      section IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence, as a decimal (for example 380 for fraud, 83.02, 462.31)?
      subsection IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection or paragraph of the offence, as the Act writes it (for example "(1)", "(3.1)", "(1)(e)"), or "" for the whole section?
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is a criminal organization offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that the offence is a criminal organization offence?
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is a terrorism offence of the kind in paragraph (b) or (c) of that definition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that it is an indictable offence committed for a terrorist group, or one whose act is also a terrorist activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183, is the offence I am suspected of an offence within Part VI's definition of offence` IS
    `s 183 offence` form (`s 183 seat the provision of an Act` statute section subsection) `there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is a criminal organization offence` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that it is a terrorism offence of the kind in paragraph (b) or (c) of that definition`

@export Under section 183, is the communication a private communication?
GIVEN `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a spoken conversation or a telecommunication (a call, message or email)?
      `the person who made it was in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made it in Canada?
      `it was meant for a person in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it meant to be received by a person in Canada?
      `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the person who made it reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it?
      `it was a radio-based telephone communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a radio call made over equipment used mainly to connect to the public telephone network (a cordless or mobile phone call)?
      `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had it been scrambled or otherwise treated to stop anyone but the person meant to receive it understanding it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183, is the communication a private communication` IS
    `s 183 seat the communication is a private communication` `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` `the person who made it was in Canada` `it was meant for a person in Canada` `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` `it was a radio-based telephone communication` `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it`

@export Under section 183, is the thing I used a device within Part VI?
GIVEN `it is a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a device or apparatus that is used, or can be used, to intercept a private communication (a bug, tap or recorder)?
      `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a hearing aid that corrects the user's subnormal hearing to not better than normal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183, is the thing I used a device within Part VI` IS
    `s 183 seat the thing is a device within Part VI` `it is a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`

@export Under section 183, is this person a police officer for the purposes of Part VI?
GIVEN `the person is an officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer, constable or other person employed to preserve and maintain the public peace?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183, is this person a police officer for the purposes of Part VI` IS
    `s 183 police officer` `the person is an officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace`

@export Under section 183, is a lawyer of this kind a solicitor for the purposes of Part VI?
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory is the lawyer admitted?
      practitioner IS A `s 183 kind of legal practitioner` @desc Is the lawyer an advocate, a notary, a barrister, a solicitor, or none of those?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183, is a lawyer of this kind a solicitor for the purposes of Part VI` IS
    `s 183 solicitor` province practitioner

§ `Section 183.1 -- Consent of one of several people`

@export Under section 183.1, does this section make the consent of one person on the communication sufficient consent?
GIVEN `the communication was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made by more than one person, or meant by the person who made it to be received by more than one person?
      `one of those persons consented to the interception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did one of those persons consent to the interception?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183.1, does this section make the consent of one person on the communication sufficient consent` IS
    `s 183.1 the section makes one person's consent sufficient consent` `the communication was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` `one of those persons consented to the interception`

§ `Section 184 -- Interception`

-- Plumbing: the saving provision of subsection 184(2), worked out from plain facts by calling the layer-1 limbs. Used by the questions on 184(1) and 184.5(1) (which takes 184(2) by 184.5(2)).
GIVEN `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of those persons consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument I acted under was given under` IS A `s 183 kind of instrument`
      `I intercepted in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intercepted under section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I aided in good faith a person acting under an authorization or section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I believed on reasonable grounds that the person I aided was acting under an authorization or section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interception was necessary for providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intercepted to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184 seat subsection 184(2) does not apply to me` MEANS
    `s 184(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the person`
        (`s 184(2)(a) the person has the consent to intercept` `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` (`s 183.1 the section makes one person's consent sufficient consent` `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` `one of those persons consented`))
        (`s 184(2)(b) the person intercepts in accordance with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4, or aids a person who is`
            (`s 183 authorization` `the instrument I acted under was given under` `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication`)
            `I intercepted in accordance with that instrument`
            (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `I intercepted under section 184.4`)
            `I aided in good faith a person acting under an authorization or section 184.4`
            `I believed on reasonable grounds that the person I aided was acting under an authorization or section 184.4`)
        (`s 184(2)(c) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts in one of the three ways`
            (`s 184(2)(c)(i) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts as necessary to provide the service` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was necessary for providing the service`)
            (`s 184(2)(c)(ii) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts in service observing or random monitoring` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks`)
            (`s 184(2)(c)(iii) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts to protect their rights or property` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service`))
        (`s 184(2)(d) a spectrum management officer intercepts to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized use of a frequency` `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` `I intercepted to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or transmission`)
        (`s 184(2)(e) a person in control of a computer system intercepts as reasonably necessary to manage or protect it` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)`) `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)`)

@export Under section 184(1), have I committed the offence of intercepting a private communication?
GIVEN `I used a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use a device or apparatus that is used, or can be used, to intercept a private communication?
      `it was a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device a hearing aid that corrects the user's subnormal hearing to not better than normal?
      `what I did with the communication` IS A `s 183 act on a communication` @desc What did you do: listen to it, record it, acquire it, acquire its substance, meaning or purport, or something else?
      `I did it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it knowingly?
      `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the communication a spoken conversation or a telecommunication (a call, message or email)?
      `the person who made it was in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made it in Canada?
      `it was meant for a person in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it meant to be received by a person in Canada?
      `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the person who made it reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it?
      `it was a radio-based telephone communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a radio call made over equipment used mainly to connect to the public telephone network?
      `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had it been scrambled or otherwise treated to stop anyone but the person meant to receive it understanding it?
      `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who made the communication, or the person it was meant for, consent (expressly or by implication) to your intercepting it?
      `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made by more than one person, or meant for more than one person?
      `one of those persons consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did one of those persons consent?
      `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act under a judge's order that authorizes the interception of a private communication?
      `the instrument I acted under was given under` IS A `s 183 kind of instrument` @desc Was that order given under subsection 184.2(3), under section 186, under subsection 188(2), or under none of those?
      `I intercepted in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intercept in accordance with that order?
      `I intercepted under section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intercept as a police officer in an emergency under section 184.4?
      `I aided in good faith a person acting under an authorization or section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you in good faith help another person in the interception?
      `I believed on reasonable grounds that the person I aided was acting under an authorization or section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe on reasonable grounds that the person you helped was acting under an authorization or section 184.4?
      `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public?
      `my interception was necessary for providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception necessary for providing the service?
      `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it service observing or random monitoring necessary for mechanical or service quality control checks?
      `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it necessary to protect your rights or property directly related to providing the service?
      `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management?
      `I intercepted to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intercept in order to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission?
      `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the communication originate from, go to, or pass through a computer system (as section 342.1(2) defines it)?
      `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or the person you act for, in possession or control of that computer system?
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception reasonably necessary for managing the quality of service of the computer system?
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an act that would be an offence under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(1), have I committed the offence of intercepting a private communication` IS
    `s 184(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection`
        `the device`
        (`s 183 intercept` `what I did with the communication`)
        `I did it knowingly`
        (`s 183 seat the communication is a private communication` `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` `the person who made it was in Canada` `it was meant for a person in Canada` `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` `it was a radio-based telephone communication` `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it`)
        `the saving provision`
    WHERE
        `the device` MEANS `s 183 seat the thing is a device within Part VI` `I used a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` `it was a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`
        `the saving provision` MEANS
            `s 184 seat subsection 184(2) does not apply to me` `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` `one of those persons consented` `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication` `the instrument I acted under was given under` `I intercepted in accordance with that instrument` `I intercepted under section 184.4` `I aided in good faith a person acting under an authorization or section 184.4` `I believed on reasonable grounds that the person I aided was acting under an authorization or section 184.4` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was necessary for providing the service` `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks` `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service` `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` `I intercepted to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or transmission` `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)`

@export Under section 184(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 184(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 184(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN term's years
    OTHERWISE 0

@export Under section 184(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 184(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 184(1) the class of the offence`

@export Under section 184(2)(a), does the consent of a person on the communication save me from the offence in section 184(1)?
GIVEN `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who made the communication, or the person it was meant for, consent, expressly or by implication, to your intercepting it?
      `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made by more than one person, or meant for more than one person?
      `one of those persons consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did one of those persons consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(2)(a), does the consent of a person on the communication save me from the offence in section 184(1)` IS
    `s 184(2)(a) the person has the consent to intercept` `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` (`s 183.1 the section makes one person's consent sufficient consent` `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` `one of those persons consented`)

@export Under section 184(2)(c), am I a person providing a communication service to the public who intercepted in one of the three ways that paragraph lists?
GIVEN `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public?
      `my interception was necessary for providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception necessary for providing the service?
      `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it service observing or random monitoring necessary for mechanical or service quality control checks?
      `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it necessary to protect your rights or property directly related to providing the service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(2)(c), am I a person providing a communication service to the public who intercepted in one of the three ways that paragraph lists` IS
    `s 184(2)(c) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts in one of the three ways`
        (`s 184(2)(c)(i) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts as necessary to provide the service` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was necessary for providing the service`)
        (`s 184(2)(c)(ii) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts in service observing or random monitoring` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks`)
        (`s 184(2)(c)(iii) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts to protect their rights or property` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service`)

@export Under section 184(2)(e), am I a person in possession or control of a computer system, or acting for one, who intercepted as reasonably necessary to manage or protect it?
GIVEN `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the communication originate from, go to, or pass through a computer system (as section 342.1(2) defines it)?
      `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or the person you act for, in possession or control of that computer system?
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception reasonably necessary for managing the quality of service of the computer system?
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an act that would be an offence under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(2)(e), am I a person in possession or control of a computer system, or acting for one, who intercepted as reasonably necessary to manage or protect it` IS
    `s 184(2)(e) a person in control of a computer system intercepts as reasonably necessary to manage or protect it` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)`) `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)`

@export Under section 184(3), can a private communication intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph 184(2)(e) be used or retained?
GIVEN `it was intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it intercepted by a person in possession or control of a computer system, or acting for them, as paragraph 184(2)(e) describes?
      `it is essential to identify, isolate or prevent harm to the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it essential to identify, isolate or prevent harm to the computer system?
      `it is to be disclosed in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to be disclosed in a way that subsection 193(2) permits (for example as evidence, or to a peace officer)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184(3), can a private communication intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph 184(2)(e) be used or retained` IS
    `s 184(3) a private communication intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e) can be used or retained` `it was intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e)` `it is essential to identify, isolate or prevent harm to the computer system` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it is to be disclosed in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2)`)

§ `Section 184.1 -- Interception to prevent bodily harm (situation: an agent of the state recorded a communication with one party's consent)`

@export Under section 184.1(1), may an agent of the state intercept a private communication to prevent bodily harm?
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a peace officer?
      `the person is acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer?
      `the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception made with a device (a bug, tap or recorder)?
      `it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a private communication (one the speaker could expect to stay private)?
      `one party to the communication consented to the interception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who made the communication, or the person it was meant for, consent to the interception?
      `the agent believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodily harm to the person who consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agent believe, on reasonable grounds, that there is a risk of bodily harm to the person who consented?
      `the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the interception to prevent that bodily harm?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184.1(1), may an agent of the state intercept a private communication to prevent bodily harm` IS
    `s 184.1(1) an agent of the state may intercept a private communication`
        (`s 184.1(4) agent of the state` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person is a peace officer`) `the person is acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer`)
        (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it`)
        (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it`)
        `one party to the communication consented to the interception`
        `the agent believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodily harm to the person who consented`
        `the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm`

@export Under section 184.1(2), are the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under subsection 184.1(1) inadmissible as evidence?
GIVEN `it was obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection 184.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it obtained from an interception made under section 184.1(1) (to prevent bodily harm, with one party's consent)?
      `the proceedings are ones in which bodily harm is alleged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding one in which actual, attempted or threatened bodily harm is alleged (including an application for an authorization, a search warrant or an arrest warrant)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184.1(2), are the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under subsection 184.1(1) inadmissible as evidence` IS
    `s 184.1(2) the contents are inadmissible as evidence` `it was obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection 184.1(1)` `the proceedings are ones in which bodily harm is alleged`

§ `Section 184.2 -- Interception with consent and an authorization (situation: police recorded a call with one party's consent)`

@export Under section 184.2(1), may a person intercept a private communication with one party's consent and an authorization?
GIVEN `the interception is by a device, as section 183 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception made with a device (a bug, tap or recorder)?
      `it is a private communication, as section 183 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a private communication (one the speaker could expect to stay private)?
      `the person who made it, or the person it was meant for, has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who made the communication, or the person it was meant for, consented to the interception?
      `an authorization has been obtained under subsection 184.2(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judge given an authorization under subsection 184.2(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184.2(1), may a person intercept a private communication with one party's consent and an authorization` IS
    `s 184.2(1) a person may intercept a private communication with the consent of a party and an authorization`
        (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the interception is by a device, as section 183 defines it`)
        (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it is a private communication, as section 183 defines it`)
        `the person who made it, or the person it was meant for, has consented`
        `an authorization has been obtained under subsection 184.2(3)`

@export Under section 184.2(4), is the period of the authorization within the limit in paragraph (e): sixty days, or the longer period section 186.1 allows?
GIVEN `the day the authorization's period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the authorization's period begin?
      `the day the authorization's period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what date does it end?
      statute IS A `s 183 statute` @desc Which Act is the offence the authorization concerns in?
      section IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of that offence, as a decimal?
      subsection IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection or paragraph of that offence, as the Act writes it ("" for the whole section)?
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group?
      `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that group a criminal organization?
      `the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a terrorism offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184.2(4), is the period of the authorization within the limit in paragraph (e): sixty days, or the longer period section 186.1 allows` IS
    `s 184.2(4)(e) the period of the authorization is within the limit` `the day the authorization's period begins` `the day the authorization's period ends`
        (`s 186.1 a period exceeding sixty days is permitted for the offence` (`s 183 seat the provision of an Act` statute section subsection) `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` (`s 2 criminal organization` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the group is a criminal organization`)) (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the offence is a terrorism offence`))

§ `Section 184.4 -- Immediate interception: imminent harm (situation: a police officer intercepted without an authorization)`

@export Under section 184.4, may a police officer intercept a private communication without an authorization in an emergency?
GIVEN `the person is employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer, constable or other person employed to preserve and maintain the public peace?
      `the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception made with a device (a bug, tap or recorder)?
      `it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a private communication (one the speaker could expect to stay private)?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that an authorization could not, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under any other provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that, given the urgency, an authorization could not with reasonable diligence be obtained under any other provision of Part VI?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that the interception was immediately necessary to prevent an offence that would cause serious harm to any person or to property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that the interception was immediately necessary to prevent an offence that would cause serious harm to any person or property?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that the originator or intended recipient is the person who would commit the offence or its victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that either the person who made the communication or the person it was meant for is the person who would commit the offence, or is its victim or intended victim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184.4, may a police officer intercept a private communication without an authorization in an emergency` IS
    `s 184.4 a police officer may intercept a private communication`
        (`s 183 police officer` `the person is employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace`)
        (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the interception was by a device, as section 183 defines it`)
        (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it was a private communication, as section 183 defines it`)
        `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that an authorization could not, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under any other provision of this Part`
        `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that the interception was immediately necessary to prevent an offence that would cause serious harm to any person or to property`
        `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that the originator or intended recipient is the person who would commit the offence or its victim`

§ `Section 184.5 -- Radio-based telephone communications`

@export Under section 184.5(1), have I committed the offence of intercepting a radio-based telephone communication?
GIVEN `I used a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use a device or apparatus that is used, or can be used, to intercept a private communication?
      `it was a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device a hearing aid that corrects the user's subnormal hearing to not better than normal?
      `what I did with the communication` IS A `s 183 act on a communication` @desc What did you do: listen to it, record it, acquire it, acquire its substance, meaning or purport, or something else?
      `I acted maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act maliciously?
      `I acted for gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act for gain?
      `it was a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act?
      `it was made over apparatus used primarily for connection to a network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made over apparatus used primarily for connection to a telephone network?
      `the network is a telecommunication facility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that network a telecommunication facility?
      `the network's primary purpose is a land line-based telephone service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the network's primary purpose to provide a land line-based telephone service?
      `the service is provided to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service provided to the public?
      `the service is provided for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service provided for compensation?
      `the originator or the person it was meant for was in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the communication, or the person it was meant for, in Canada?
      `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who made the communication, or the person it was meant for, consent to your intercepting it?
      `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made by more than one person, or meant for more than one person?
      `one of those persons consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did one of those persons consent?
      `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act under a judge's order that authorizes the interception of a private communication?
      `the instrument I acted under was given under` IS A `s 183 kind of instrument` @desc Was that order given under subsection 184.2(3), under section 186, under subsection 188(2), or under none of those?
      `I intercepted in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intercept in accordance with that order?
      `I intercepted under section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intercept as a police officer in an emergency under section 184.4?
      `I aided in good faith a person acting under an authorization or section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you in good faith help another person in the interception?
      `I believed on reasonable grounds that the person I aided was acting under an authorization or section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you believe on reasonable grounds that the person you helped was acting under an authorization or section 184.4?
      `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public?
      `my interception was necessary for providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception necessary for providing the service?
      `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it service observing or random monitoring necessary for mechanical or service quality control checks?
      `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it necessary to protect your rights or property directly related to providing the service?
      `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management?
      `I intercepted to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intercept in order to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission?
      `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the communication originate from, go to, or pass through a computer system (as section 342.1(2) defines it)?
      `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or the person you act for, in possession or control of that computer system?
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interception reasonably necessary for managing the quality of service of the computer system?
      `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an act that would be an offence under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 184.5(1), have I committed the offence of intercepting a radio-based telephone communication` IS
    `s 184.5(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection`
        (`s 183 seat the thing is a device within Part VI` `I used a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` `it was a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`)
        (`s 183 intercept` `what I did with the communication`)
        `I acted maliciously`
        `I acted for gain`
        (`s 183 radio-based telephone communication` `it was a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act` `it was made over apparatus used primarily for connection to a network` (`s 183 public switched telephone network` `the network is a telecommunication facility` `the network's primary purpose is a land line-based telephone service` `the service is provided to the public` `the service is provided for compensation`))
        `the originator or the person it was meant for was in Canada`
        `the saving provision`
    WHERE
        `the saving provision` MEANS
            `s 184 seat subsection 184(2) does not apply to me` `a person who made it or was meant to receive it consented` `it was made by more than one person or meant for more than one person` `one of those persons consented` `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication` `the instrument I acted under was given under` `I intercepted in accordance with that instrument` `I intercepted under section 184.4` `I aided in good faith a person acting under an authorization or section 184.4` `I believed on reasonable grounds that the person I aided was acting under an authorization or section 184.4` `I provide a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` `my interception was necessary for providing the service` `my interception was service observing or random monitoring necessary for quality control checks` `my interception was necessary to protect my rights or property directly related to providing the service` `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` `I intercepted to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or transmission` `it passed through a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` `I or the person I act for is in possession or control of that computer system` `my interception was reasonably necessary to manage the quality of service of the computer system` `my interception was reasonably necessary to protect the computer system against an offence under section 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)`

@export Under section 184.5(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 184.5(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 184.5(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN term's years
    OTHERWISE 0

@export Under section 184.5(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 184.5(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 184.5(1) the class of the offence`

§ `Section 185 -- What the application for an authorization had to contain (situation: police obtained a wiretap authorization about me)`

@export Under section 185(1), did the application for the authorization about me meet the requirements of the subsection?
GIVEN `the application was made ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application made ex parte (without notice to the person concerned)?
      `the application was made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in writing?
      `it was made to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, or a judge as defined in section 552?
      signatory IS A `s 185(1) signatory` @desc Who signed it: the provincial Attorney General, the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, an agent designated by the Minister or Deputy Minister, an agent designated by the provincial Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General, or someone else?
      `the offence is one the Government of Canada may prosecute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence under investigation one for which proceedings may be instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or for the Attorney General of Canada?
      `it was accompanied by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it accompanied by an affidavit?
      `the affidavit gave the facts relied on and the particulars of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the affidavit give the facts relied on to justify the belief that an authorization should be given, with particulars of the offence?
      `the affidavit named the type of private communication to be intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it state the type of private communication proposed to be intercepted?
      `the affidavit gave the names, addresses, occupations, place and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it give the names, addresses and occupations (if known) of the persons concerned, a general description of the place and of the manner of interception?
      `the affidavit gave the earlier applications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it give the number of earlier applications relating to the offence and a named person that were withdrawn or refused?
      `the affidavit gave the period requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it state the period for which the authorization was requested?
      `the affidavit dealt with other investigative procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it say whether other investigative procedures had been tried and failed, or were unlikely to succeed, or that urgency made them impractical?
      statute IS A `s 183 statute` @desc Which Act is the offence in?
      section IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence, as a decimal?
      subsection IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection or paragraph of the offence, as the Act writes it ("" for the whole section)?
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group?
      `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that group a criminal organization?
      `the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a terrorism offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 185(1), did the application for the authorization about me meet the requirements of the subsection` IS
    `s 185(1) the application meets the requirements of the subsection`
        `the application was made ex parte` `the application was made in writing` `it was made to a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552`
        signatory `the offence is one the Government of Canada may prosecute` `it was accompanied by an affidavit`
        `the affidavit gave the facts relied on and the particulars of the offence` `the affidavit named the type of private communication to be intercepted` `the affidavit gave the names, addresses, occupations, place and manner`
        `the affidavit gave the earlier applications` `the affidavit gave the period requested` `the affidavit dealt with other investigative procedures`
        (`s 185(1.1) paragraph (1)(h) does not apply to the application` (`s 183 seat the provision of an Act` statute section subsection) `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` (`s 2 criminal organization` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the group is a criminal organization`)) (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the offence is a terrorism offence`))

§ `Section 186 -- When a judge may give an authorization, how long it may last, and the lawyer's office (situation: an authorization was given about me)`

@export Under section 186(1), may a judge give an authorization to intercept my communications?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that it would be in the best interests of the administration of justice to give the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that it would be in the best interests of the administration of justice to give the authorization?
      `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed?
      `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures are unlikely to succeed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that other investigative procedures are unlikely to succeed?
      `the judge is satisfied that urgency makes it impractical to investigate using only other procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the urgency of the matter makes it impractical to investigate the offence using only other investigative procedures?
      `the judge is satisfied that the application is in relation to the offence in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the application is in relation to the offence you are asking about?
      statute IS A `s 183 statute` @desc Which Act is the offence in?
      section IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence, as a decimal?
      subsection IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection or paragraph of the offence, as the Act writes it ("" for the whole section)?
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group?
      `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that group a criminal organization?
      `the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a terrorism offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 186(1), may a judge give an authorization to intercept my communications` IS
    `s 186(1) an authorization may be given under section 186`
        `the judge is satisfied that it would be in the best interests of the administration of justice to give the authorization`
        `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures have been tried and have failed`
        `the judge is satisfied that other investigative procedures are unlikely to succeed`
        `the judge is satisfied that urgency makes it impractical to investigate using only other procedures`
        (`s 186(1.1) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` `the judge is satisfied that the application is in relation to the offence in question` (`s 183 seat the provision of an Act` statute section subsection) `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` (`s 2 criminal organization` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the group is a criminal organization`)) (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the offence is a terrorism offence`))

@export Under section 186(2), does the bar apply against giving an authorization to intercept a private communication at a solicitor's office or residence, or other place solicitors use to consult clients?
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory is your lawyer admitted?
      practitioner IS A `s 183 kind of legal practitioner` @desc Is your lawyer an advocate, a notary, a barrister, a solicitor, or none of those?
      `the place is a lawyer's office or residence or a place used by lawyers to consult clients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place the office or residence of a solicitor, or another place ordinarily used by a solicitor and other solicitors to consult clients?
      `the judge is satisfied that the lawyer or someone close to the practice has been or is about to become a party to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the solicitor, a solicitor practising with them, an employee or a member of the solicitor's household has been or is about to become a party to an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 186(2), does the bar apply against giving an authorization to intercept a private communication at a solicitor's office or residence, or other place solicitors use to consult clients` IS
    `s 186(2) the bar applies: no authorization may be given to intercept a private communication at a solicitor’s place` (`s 183 solicitor` province practitioner) `the place is a lawyer's office or residence or a place used by lawyers to consult clients` `the judge is satisfied that the lawyer or someone close to the practice has been or is about to become a party to an offence`

