§ `Section 187 -- The sealed packet (situation: the interception evidence is to be used at my trial)`

@export Under section 187(1.4), may the trial judge order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed?
GIVEN `the person is a judge before whom my trial is to be held with jurisdiction in the province where the authorization was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge one before whom your trial is to be held and who has jurisdiction in the province in which the authorization was given?
      `a matter relevant to the authorization or evidence obtained under it is in issue at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any matter relevant to the authorization, or any evidence obtained under it, in issue at your trial?
      `I apply for the order to consult the documents to prepare for trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the order in order to consult the documents to prepare for trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 187(1.4), may the trial judge order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed` IS
    `s 187(1.4) the trial judge may order that the sealed packet be opened and its contents removed` `the person is a judge before whom my trial is to be held with jurisdiction in the province where the authorization was given` `a matter relevant to the authorization or evidence obtained under it is in issue at the trial` `I apply for the order to consult the documents to prepare for trial`

@export Under section 187(4), is the judge barred from giving me a copy of the application documents until the prosecutor has deleted parts?
GIVEN `a prosecution has been commenced and I applied under subsection (1.3) or (1.4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prosecution been commenced, and have you applied for an order to copy and examine the documents under subsection 187(1.3) or (1.4)?
      `the prosecutor has deleted the parts believed prejudicial to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecutor deleted the parts of the copy that the prosecutor believes would be prejudicial to the public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 187(4), is the judge barred from giving me a copy of the application documents until the prosecutor has deleted parts` IS
    `s 187(4) the judge shall not yet provide a copy of the document to the accused` `a prosecution has been commenced and I applied under subsection (1.3) or (1.4)` `the prosecutor has deleted the parts believed prejudicial to the public interest`

@export Under section 187(5), must I be provided with an edited copy of the document?
GIVEN `the prosecutor has deleted the parts to be given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecutor deleted the parts of the copy to be given to you under subsection 187(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 187(5), must I be provided with an edited copy of the document` IS
    `s 187(5) the accused is to be provided with an edited copy of the document` `the prosecutor has deleted the parts to be given to me`

@export Under section 187(7), may I ask the trial judge to order that the deleted parts be made available to me?
GIVEN `I have been provided with an edited copy under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been provided with an edited copy of the document under subsection 187(5)?
      `I make the request to the judge before whom my trial is to be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making the request to the judge before whom your trial is to be held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 187(7), may I ask the trial judge to order that the deleted parts be made available to me` IS
    `s 187(7) the accused may request that the deleted part be made available` `I have been provided with an edited copy under subsection (5)` `I make the request to the judge before whom my trial is to be held`

@export Under section 187(7), must the judge order that a deleted part be made available to me?
GIVEN `in the judge's opinion the part is required for me to make full answer and defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the judge's opinion, is the deleted part required for you to make full answer and defence?
      `in the judge's opinion a judicial summary would not be sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the judge's opinion, would a judicial summary of the part not be sufficient?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 187(7), must the judge order that a deleted part be made available to me` IS
    `s 187(7) the judge shall order that a copy of the part be made available to the accused` `in the judge's opinion the part is required for me to make full answer and defence` `in the judge's opinion a judicial summary would not be sufficient`

§ `Section 188 -- Emergency authorizations and shields (situation: an authorization was given in an emergency, or I acted under one)`

@export Under section 188(2), may a judge give an emergency authorization for the period it states?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the urgency requires interception to begin before an authorization could be obtained under section 186` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the urgency of the situation requires interception to commence before an authorization could, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under section 186?
      `the authorization is given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authorization given in writing?
      `the period of the authorization, in hours` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many hours is the authorization given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188(2), may a judge give an emergency authorization for the period it states` IS
    `s 188(2) the judge may give an authorization for a period of up to thirty-six hours` `the judge is satisfied that the urgency requires interception to begin before an authorization could be obtained under section 186` `the authorization is given in writing` `the period of the authorization, in hours`

@export Under section 188(5), may the trial judge deem the evidence inadmissible?
GIVEN `the evidence was obtained under a subsequent authorization given under section 188` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the evidence obtained by an interception under a later authorization given under section 188?
      `the later application was based on the same facts as the earlier one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trial judge find that the later application was based on the same facts as the application for the original authorization?
      `it involved the interception of the same person or persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it involve the interception of the communications of the same person or persons?
      `it related to the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it relate to the same offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188(5), may the trial judge deem the evidence inadmissible` IS
    `s 188(5) the trial judge may deem the evidence inadmissible` `the evidence was obtained under a subsequent authorization given under section 188` `the later application was based on the same facts as the earlier one` `it involved the interception of the same person or persons` `it related to the same offence`

@export Under section 188.2, do I incur no criminal or civil liability for anything reasonably done further to an authorization or to section 184.1 or 184.4?
GIVEN `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act under a judge's order that authorizes the interception of a private communication?
      `the instrument I acted under was given under` IS A `s 183 kind of instrument` @desc Was that order given under subsection 184.2(3), under section 186, under subsection 188(2), or under none of those?
      `I acted in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in accordance with that order?
      `I acted under section 184.1 or 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act under section 184.1 (to prevent bodily harm) or 184.4 (in an emergency)?
      `I aided in good faith a person I believed on reasonable grounds was so acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you in good faith aid a person whom you believed on reasonable grounds was acting in accordance with an authorization or under section 184.1 or 184.4?
      `what I did was reasonably done further to the authorization or that section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you did reasonably done further to the authorization, or to that section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 188.2, do I incur no criminal or civil liability for anything reasonably done further to an authorization or to section 184.1 or 184.4` IS
    `s 188.2 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability` (`s 183 authorization` `the instrument I acted under was given under` `the instrument I acted under authorizes interception of a private communication`) `I acted in accordance with that instrument` `I acted under section 184.1 or 184.4` `I aided in good faith a person I believed on reasonable grounds was so acting` `what I did was reasonably done further to the authorization or that section`

§ `Sections 189 and 190 -- Notice before the intercepted communication is used against me; privilege; further particulars`

@export Under section 189(5), is the intercepted communication barred from being received in evidence against me?
GIVEN `it is the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under Part VI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under Part VI (or under an authorization given under it) what the Crown wants to use?
      `the party gave me reasonable notice of the intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the party who intends to use it given you reasonable notice of that intention?
      form IS A `s 189(5) form in which the contents will be adduced` @desc Will it be used as a recording, as spoken (viva voce) evidence, or in some other form?
      `the notice came with a transcript` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice come with a transcript of the communication?
      `the notice came with a statement of full particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice come with a statement setting out full particulars of the communication?
      `the notice came with a statement of time, place, date and the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice come with a statement of the time, place and date of the communication and the parties to it, if known?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 189(5), is the intercepted communication barred from being received in evidence against me` IS
    `s 189(5) the contents shall not be received in evidence` `it is the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception under Part VI` `the party gave me reasonable notice of the intention` form `the notice came with a transcript` `the notice came with a statement of full particulars` `the notice came with a statement of time, place, date and the parties`

@export Under section 189(6), does information obtained by an interception remain privileged and inadmissible as evidence?
GIVEN `the information was obtained by an interception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained by an interception?
      `but for the interception it would have been privileged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the interception, would it have been privileged (for example solicitor-client)?
      `the person who enjoys the privilege consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person who enjoys the privilege consent to its use?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 189(6), does information obtained by an interception remain privileged and inadmissible as evidence` IS
    `s 189(6) the information remains privileged and inadmissible as evidence` `the information was obtained by an interception` `but for the interception it would have been privileged` `the person who enjoys the privilege consents`

@export Under section 190, may the judge order that further particulars of the intercepted communication be given to me?
GIVEN `I have been given notice under subsection 189(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, as the accused, been given notice under subsection 189(5)?
      `the person is a judge of the court in which my trial is being or is to be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge a judge of the court in which your trial is being or is to be held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 190, may the judge order that further particulars of the intercepted communication be given to me` IS
    `s 190 the judge may order that further particulars be given of the private communication` `I have been given notice under subsection 189(5)` `the person is a judge of the court in which my trial is being or is to be held`

§ `Section 191 -- Possession of a device (situation: I have, sold or bought a listening device)`

@export Under section 191(1), have I committed the offence of possessing, selling or purchasing an intercepting device?
GIVEN `I possessed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess the device or component?
      `I did an act of selling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sell it, or do an act that counts as selling?
      `the act of selling` IS A `s 183 act of selling` @desc What was the act: offering it for sale, exposing it for sale, having it in possession for sale, distributing it, advertising it for sale, or something else?
      `I purchased it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you purchase it?
      `it is a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a device or apparatus that is used, or can be used, to intercept a private communication?
      `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a hearing aid that corrects the user's subnormal hearing to not better than normal?
      `it is a component of such a device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a component of such a device?
      `I knew that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications?
      `I am employed to keep the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace?
      `my possession was in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your possession in the course of that employment?
      `the instrument I possessed it for authorizes interception of a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess it for use under a judge's order that authorizes the interception of a private communication?
      `the instrument I possessed it for was given under` IS A `s 183 kind of instrument` @desc Was that order given under subsection 184.2(3), under section 186, under subsection 188(2), or under none of those?
      `I possessed it to use it in an interception in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess it for the purpose of using it in an interception made or to be made in accordance with that order?
      `I possessed it under the direction of a police officer to assist that officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess it under the direction of a police officer in order to assist that officer in the course of the officer's duties?
      `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces?
      `my possession was in the course of my duties as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your possession in the course of your duties as such an officer, servant or member?
      `I possessed it under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you possess it under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 191(1), have I committed the offence of possessing, selling or purchasing an intercepting device` IS
    `s 191(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection`
        `I possessed it`
        (IF `I did an act of selling` THEN `s 183 sell` `the act of selling` ELSE JUST FALSE)
        `I purchased it`
        (`s 183 electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device` `it is a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`)
        `it is a component of such a device`
        `I knew that its design renders it primarily useful for surreptitious interception of private communications`
        (`s 191(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the person`
            (`s 191(2)(a) a police officer is in possession in the course of employment` (`s 183 police officer` `I am employed to keep the public peace`) `I possessed it` `my possession was in the course of my employment`)
            (`s 191(2)(b) a person is in possession to use it in an interception in accordance with an authorization` (`s 183 authorization` `the instrument I possessed it for was given under` `the instrument I possessed it for authorizes interception of a private communication`) `I possessed it to use it in an interception in accordance with that instrument`)
            (`s 191(2)(b.1) a person is in possession under the direction of a police officer to assist that officer` `I possessed it under the direction of a police officer to assist that officer`)
            (`s 191(2)(c) an officer, servant or member of the Canadian Forces is in possession in the course of duties` `I am an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada or a member of the Canadian Forces` `my possession was in the course of my duties as such`)
            (`s 191(2)(d) a person is in possession under the authority of a licence` `I possessed it under the authority of a licence issued by the Minister`))

@export Under section 191(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 191(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 191(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN term's years
    OTHERWISE 0

@export Under section 191(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 191(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 191(1) the class of the offence`

§ `Section 192 -- Forfeiture of the device (situation: I was convicted under section 184 or 191)`

@export Under section 192(1), may the device be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty?
GIVEN `I am convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191?
      `the device is one by which the offence was committed or whose possession was the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a device by means of which the offence was committed, or the possession of which constituted the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 192(1), may the device be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty` IS
    `s 192(1) the device may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty` `I am convicted of an offence under section 184 or 191` `the device is one by which the offence was committed or whose possession was the offence`

@export Under section 192(2), is an order for forfeiture of this equipment barred?
GIVEN `the thing is a communication provider's facilities or equipment used in a section 184 offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing telephone, telegraph or other communication facilities or equipment owned by a person providing that service to the public (or forming part of their service or system), by which an offence under section 184 was committed?
      `that provider was a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that provider a party to the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 192(2), is an order for forfeiture of this equipment barred` IS
    `s 192(2) no order for forfeiture shall be made` `the thing is a communication provider's facilities or equipment used in a section 184 offence` `that provider was a party to the offence`

§ `Section 193 -- Using or disclosing what was intercepted (situation: I passed on or used an intercepted communication)`

-- Plumbing: subsections 193(2) and 193(3) together ("Subsection (1) does not apply to"), worked out from plain facts by calling the layer-1 limbs. Used by the questions on 193(1) and 193.1(1) (which takes 193(2) and (3) by 193.1(2)).
GIVEN `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the private communication was lawfully intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating a communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating a department or agency of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that thing is a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my disclosure was necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a foreign authority responsible for investigating or prosecuting offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intended the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what I disclosed had already been lawfully disclosed in giving evidence in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 193 seat subsection 193(1) does not apply to me` MEANS
    `s 183 three-valued any of`
        (LIST
            `s 193(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the person`
                (`s 193(2)(a) the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence` `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings`)
                (`s 193(2)(b) the disclosure is in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` `the private communication was lawfully intercepted`)
                (`s 193(2)(c) the disclosure is in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190` `I disclosed it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190`)
                (`s 193(2)(d) the disclosure is necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` `I disclosed it in the course of operating a communication service to the public` `I disclosed it in the course of operating a department or agency of the Government of Canada` `I disclosed it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `that thing is a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)`) `my disclosure was necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)`)
                (`s 193(2)(e) the disclosure is made to a peace officer, prosecutor or foreign authority in the interests of the administration of justice` `I disclosed it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a foreign authority responsible for investigating or prosecuting offences` `I intended the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere`)
                (`s 193(2)(f) the disclosure is made to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` `I disclosed it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` `it was for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of that Act`)
            , `s 193(3) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who discloses what was already lawfully disclosed in evidence` `what I disclosed had already been lawfully disclosed in giving evidence in proceedings`)

@export Under section 193(1), have I committed the offence of using or disclosing an intercepted private communication?
GIVEN `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the communication a spoken conversation or a telecommunication (a call, message or email)?
      `the person who made it was in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made it in Canada?
      `it was meant for a person in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it meant to be received by a person in Canada?
      `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the person who made it reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it?
      `it was a radio-based telephone communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a radio call made over equipment used mainly to connect to the public telephone network?
      `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had it been scrambled or otherwise treated to stop anyone but the person meant to receive it understanding it?
      `it was intercepted by a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it intercepted by a device or apparatus that is used, or can be used, to intercept a private communication?
      `the device was a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that device a hearing aid that corrects the user's subnormal hearing to not better than normal?
      `the interception was without the consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it intercepted without the express or implied consent of the person who made it and of the person it was meant for?
      `I acted without the express consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without the express consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for?
      `I acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act knowingly?
      `I used or disclosed it or part of it, or its substance, meaning or purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use or disclose the communication, or part of it, or its substance, meaning or purpose?
      `I disclosed that it existed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose the existence of the communication?
      `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of, or for the purpose of, giving evidence in civil or criminal proceedings or other proceedings in which you may be required to give evidence on oath?
      `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of, or for the purpose of, a criminal investigation?
      `the private communication was lawfully intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the communication lawfully intercepted?
      `I disclosed it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under an order under section 190?
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating a communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of operating a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public?
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating a department or agency of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of operating a department or an agency of the Government of Canada?
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system?
      `that thing is a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that a computer system as section 342.1(2) defines it?
      `my disclosure was necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your disclosure necessarily incidental to an interception by a service provider, a spectrum management officer or a computer system operator (paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e))?
      `I disclosed it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a foreign authority responsible for investigating or prosecuting offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada, or to a person or authority responsible in a foreign state for investigating or prosecuting offences?
      `I intended the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere?
      `I disclosed it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service?
      `it was for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that to enable the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act?
      `what I disclosed had already been lawfully disclosed in giving evidence in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had what you disclosed already been lawfully disclosed in the course of, or for the purpose of, giving evidence in those proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 193(1), have I committed the offence of using or disclosing an intercepted private communication` IS
    `s 193(1) the person commits an offence under the subsection`
        (`s 183 seat the communication is a private communication` `it was an oral communication or a telecommunication` `the person who made it was in Canada` `it was meant for a person in Canada` `the person who made it could reasonably expect that nobody but the person meant to receive it would intercept it` `it was a radio-based telephone communication` `it was treated electronically or otherwise to stop anyone else understanding it`)
        (`s 183 seat the thing is a device within Part VI` `it was intercepted by a device or apparatus used, or capable of being used, to intercept a private communication` `the device was a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`)
        `the interception was without the consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for`
        `I acted without the express consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for`
        `I acted knowingly`
        `I used or disclosed it or part of it, or its substance, meaning or purpose`
        `I disclosed that it existed`
        (`s 193 seat subsection 193(1) does not apply to me` `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings` `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` `the private communication was lawfully intercepted` `I disclosed it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190` `I disclosed it in the course of operating a communication service to the public` `I disclosed it in the course of operating a department or agency of the Government of Canada` `I disclosed it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system` `that thing is a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` `my disclosure was necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` `I disclosed it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a foreign authority responsible for investigating or prosecuting offences` `I intended the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere` `I disclosed it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` `it was for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of that Act` `what I disclosed had already been lawfully disclosed in giving evidence in proceedings`)

@export Under section 193(1.1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 193(1.1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 193(1.1)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN term's years
    OTHERWISE 0

@export Under section 193(1.1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 193(1.1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 193(1.1) the class of the offence`

§ `Section 193.1 -- Using or disclosing a radio-based telephone communication`

@export Under section 193.1(1), have I committed the offence of using or disclosing an intercepted radio-based telephone communication?
GIVEN `it was a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act?
      `it was made over apparatus used primarily for connection to a network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made over apparatus used primarily for connection to a telephone network?
      `the network is a telecommunication facility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that network a telecommunication facility?
      `the network's primary purpose is a land line-based telephone service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the network's primary purpose to provide a land line-based telephone service?
      `the service is provided to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service provided to the public?
      `the service is provided for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service provided for compensation?
      `I used or disclosed it, or disclosed that it existed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use or disclose the communication, or disclose that it existed?
      `I acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act knowingly?
      `the originator or the person it was meant for was in Canada when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made it, or the person it was meant for, in Canada when it was made?
      `it was intercepted by a device without the consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it intercepted by an electromagnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device without the express or implied consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for?
      `I do not have the consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you lack the express or implied consent of the person who made it and of the person it was meant for?
      `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of, or for the purpose of, giving evidence in proceedings in which you may be required to give evidence on oath?
      `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of, or for the purpose of, a criminal investigation?
      `the private communication was lawfully intercepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the communication lawfully intercepted?
      `I disclosed it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190?
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating a communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of operating a communication service to the public?
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating a department or agency of the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of operating a department or an agency of the Government of Canada?
      `I disclosed it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system?
      `that thing is a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that a computer system as section 342.1(2) defines it?
      `my disclosure was necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your disclosure necessarily incidental to an interception by a service provider, a spectrum management officer or a computer system operator?
      `I disclosed it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a foreign authority responsible for investigating or prosecuting offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada, or to a person or authority responsible in a foreign state for investigating or prosecuting offences?
      `I intended the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere?
      `I disclosed it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service?
      `it was for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that to enable the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act?
      `what I disclosed had already been lawfully disclosed in giving evidence in proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had what you disclosed already been lawfully disclosed in the course of, or for the purpose of, giving evidence in those proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 193.1(1), have I committed the offence of using or disclosing an intercepted radio-based telephone communication` IS
    `s 193.1(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection`
        `the radio-based telephone communication`
        `I used or disclosed it, or disclosed that it existed`
        `I acted knowingly`
        `the originator or the person it was meant for was in Canada when it was made`
        `it was intercepted by a device without the consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for`
        `I do not have the consent of the person who made it or the person it was meant for`
        (IF `s 193.1(2) subsections 193(2) and (3) apply to the disclosure` (`the radio-based telephone communication` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN `s 193 seat subsection 193(1) does not apply to me` `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of giving evidence in proceedings` `I disclosed it in the course of or for the purpose of a criminal investigation` `the private communication was lawfully intercepted` `I disclosed it in giving notice under section 189 or furnishing further particulars under section 190` `I disclosed it in the course of operating a communication service to the public` `I disclosed it in the course of operating a department or agency of the Government of Canada` `I disclosed it in the course of operating services relating to the management or protection of a computer system` `that thing is a computer system as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` `my disclosure was necessarily incidental to an interception described in paragraph 184(2)(c), (d) or (e)` `I disclosed it to a peace officer or prosecutor in Canada or to a foreign authority responsible for investigating or prosecuting offences` `I intended the disclosure to be in the interests of the administration of justice in Canada or elsewhere` `I disclosed it to the Director of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service or an employee of the Service` `it was for the purpose of enabling the Service to perform its duties and functions under section 12 of that Act` `what I disclosed had already been lawfully disclosed in giving evidence in proceedings`
         ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `the radio-based telephone communication` MEANS
            `s 183 radio-based telephone communication` `it was a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act` `it was made over apparatus used primarily for connection to a network` (`s 183 public switched telephone network` `the network is a telecommunication facility` `the network's primary purpose is a land line-based telephone service` `the service is provided to the public` `the service is provided for compensation`)

@export Under section 193.1(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 193.1(1), what is the most I can be imprisoned for if I am prosecuted by indictment, in years` IS
    CONSIDER `s 193.1(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN term's years
    OTHERWISE 0

@export Under section 193.1(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 193.1(1), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 193.1(1) the class of the offence`

§ `Section 194 -- Damages (situation: I was convicted under section 184, 184.5, 193 or 193.1)`

@export Under section 194(1), what is the most the court may order me to pay as punitive damages, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 194(1), what is the most the court may order me to pay as punitive damages, in dollars` IS
    `s 194(1) the most that may be ordered as punitive damages, in dollars`

@export Under section 194(1), may the court order me to pay punitive damages to the person aggrieved?
GIVEN `the offence I was convicted of` IS A `Provision of the Code` @desc Of which offence were you convicted? (The section number as a decimal, for example 184 or 193.1, and the subsection as the Code writes it, or "".)
      `the person aggrieved applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person aggrieved apply for the order?
      `the order is made when sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made at the time sentence is imposed?
      `the amount, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, would the court order you to pay?
      `the person has commenced a Crown Liability Act action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that person commenced an action under Part II of the Crown Liability Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 194(1), may the court order me to pay punitive damages to the person aggrieved` IS
    `s 194(1) the court may order the accused to pay punitive damages to the person aggrieved` `the offence I was convicted of` `the person aggrieved applies` `the order is made when sentence is imposed` `the amount, in dollars` (`s 194(2) no amount shall be ordered to be paid to the person` `the person has commenced a Crown Liability Act action`)

@export Under section 194(4), may the amount ordered be taken out of the moneys found in my possession?
GIVEN `an amount has been ordered to be paid under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered you to pay an amount under subsection 194(1)?
      `the moneys were found in my possession at the time of my arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the moneys found in your possession at the time of your arrest?
      `others dispute who owns the moneys or has the right to possess them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do claimants other than you dispute who owns the moneys or has the right to possess them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 194(4), may the amount ordered be taken out of the moneys found in my possession` IS
    `s 194(4) the amount may be taken out of the moneys found in the possession of the accused` `an amount has been ordered to be paid under subsection (1)` `the moneys were found in my possession at the time of my arrest` `others dispute who owns the moneys or has the right to possess them`

§ `Sections 196 and 196.1 -- My right to be told, in writing, that my communications were intercepted`

@export Under section 196(1), by what date must I be notified in writing of the interception?
GIVEN `the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period for which the authorization was given or renewed end?
      `a judge fixed another period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a judge fix a longer period under subsection 185(3) or 196(3)?
      `the other period, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many years was that period? (0 if none or if it has months and days only.)
      `the other period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the other period, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the days the running of the period was suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days was the running of the period suspended while an application for an extension was pending? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 196(1), by what date must I be notified in writing of the interception` IS
    `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` `the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ended`
        (IF `a judge fixed another period` THEN JUST (`Length of time` WITH years IS `the other period, in years`, months IS `the other period, in months`, days IS `the other period, in days`, `less a day` IS FALSE) ELSE NOTHING)
        `the days the running of the period was suspended`

@export Under section 196(1), was the written notice I received given in time?
GIVEN `the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period for which the authorization was given or renewed end?
      `a judge fixed another period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a judge fix a longer period under subsection 185(3) or 196(3)?
      `the other period, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many years was that period? (0 if none.)
      `the other period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the other period, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the days the running of the period was suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days was the running suspended while an application for an extension was pending? (0 if none.)
      `the day I was given notice in writing` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you given notice in writing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196(1), was the written notice I received given in time` IS
    `s 196(1) the notice was given in time` `the day I was given notice in writing`
        (`s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` `the day the period for which the authorization was given or renewed ended`
            (IF `a judge fixed another period` THEN JUST (`Length of time` WITH years IS `the other period, in years`, months IS `the other period, in months`, days IS `the other period, in days`, `less a day` IS FALSE) ELSE NOTHING)
            `the days the running of the period was suspended`)

@export Under section 196(3), must the judge grant an extension of the time for notifying me?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied, on the affidavit, that the investigation of the offence to which the authorization relates is continuing?
      `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that a subsequent investigation, commenced as a result of information from that investigation, is continuing?
      `the subsequent offence is listed in section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence of the subsequent investigation one listed in section 183?
      `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196(3), must the judge grant an extension of the time for notifying me` IS
    `s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` `the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence is continuing` `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation is continuing` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the subsequent offence is listed in section 183`) `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application`

@export Under section 196(5), must the judge grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the time for notifying me?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to the offence in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied, on the affidavit, that the investigation is in relation to the offence you are asking about?
      statute IS A `s 183 statute` @desc Which Act is the offence in?
      section IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence, as a decimal?
      subsection IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection or paragraph of the offence, as the Act writes it ("" for the whole section)?
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group?
      `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that group a criminal organization?
      `the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a terrorism offence?
      `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196(5), must the judge grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the time for notifying me` IS
    `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` `the judge is satisfied that the investigation is in relation to the offence in question` (`s 183 seat the provision of an Act` statute section subsection) `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` (`s 2 criminal organization` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the group is a criminal organization`)) (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the offence is a terrorism offence`) `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application`

@export Under section 196.1(1), by what date must I be notified in writing of the interception?
GIVEN `the day the interception occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the police officer's interception under section 184.4 occur?
      `a judge granted an extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a judge grant an extension of the 90-day period under subsection 196.1(3) or (5)?
      `the extension, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many years was the extension? (0 if none.)
      `the extension, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the extension, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the days the running of the period was suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days was the running suspended while an application for an extension was pending? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 196.1(1), by what date must I be notified in writing of the interception` IS
    `s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` `the day the interception occurred`
        (IF `a judge granted an extension` THEN JUST (`Length of time` WITH years IS `the extension, in years`, months IS `the extension, in months`, days IS `the extension, in days`, `less a day` IS FALSE) ELSE NOTHING)
        `the days the running of the period was suspended`

@export Under section 196.1(1), was the written notice I received given in time?
GIVEN `the day the interception occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the police officer's interception under section 184.4 occur?
      `a judge granted an extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a judge grant an extension of the 90-day period under subsection 196.1(3) or (5)?
      `the extension, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many years was the extension? (0 if none.)
      `the extension, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many months in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the extension, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days in addition? (0 if none.)
      `the days the running of the period was suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days was the running suspended while an application for an extension was pending? (0 if none.)
      `the day I was given notice in writing` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you given notice in writing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196.1(1), was the written notice I received given in time` IS
    `s 196.1(1) the notice was given in time` `the day I was given notice in writing`
        (`s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` `the day the interception occurred`
            (IF `a judge granted an extension` THEN JUST (`Length of time` WITH years IS `the extension, in years`, months IS `the extension, in months`, days IS `the extension, in days`, `less a day` IS FALSE) ELSE NOTHING)
            `the days the running of the period was suspended`)

@export Under section 196.1(3), must the judge grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the 90 days for notifying me?
GIVEN `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application?
      `the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied, on the affidavit, that the investigation of the offence to which the interception relates is continuing?
      `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that a subsequent investigation, commenced as a result of information from that investigation, is continuing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196.1(3), must the judge grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the 90 days for notifying me` IS
    `s 196.1(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` `the judge is satisfied that the investigation of the offence is continuing` `the judge is satisfied that a subsequent investigation is continuing`

@export Under section 196.1(5), must the judge grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the 90 days for notifying me?
GIVEN `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application?
      `the judge is satisfied that the interception relates to an investigation of the offence in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied, on the affidavit, that the interception relates to an investigation of the offence you are asking about?
      statute IS A `s 183 statute` @desc Which Act is the offence in?
      section IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence, as a decimal?
      subsection IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection or paragraph of the offence, as the Act writes it ("" for the whole section)?
      `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group?
      `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that group a criminal organization?
      `the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a terrorism offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 196.1(5), must the judge grant an extension, or a subsequent extension, of the 90 days for notifying me` IS
    `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` `the judge is of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant granting the application` `the judge is satisfied that the interception relates to an investigation of the offence in question` (`s 183 seat the provision of an Act` statute section subsection) `it was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` (`s 2 criminal organization` (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the group is a criminal organization`)) (`s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the offence is a terrorism offence`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc8 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 197 to 269.1 (Part VII, disorderly houses, gaming and betting, and the first third of Part VIII,
-- offences against the person) -- THE SEAT LAYER, written by part agent ccc8.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer asks, from that person's side, the questions that sections 197 to 269.1 answer: whether what they did is an offence, how serious the offence is and what it can cost them,
-- what defences, exemptions and onuses the text gives them, and what the text lets be done to them or their property (arrest, search, seizure, forfeiture, sentence).
-- It calls the layer-1 rules in the ccc8 modules and the section 2 definitions in ccc-definitions.l4; nothing is restated here.
-- A provision that addresses only an official (a justice, a court, a peace officer) appears only as what it means to the person ("Under section 236(2), must the court consider ...");
-- there is no seat for an official.
--
-- NAMES. Every question begins "Under section N," with the Code's own numbering, so that no two parts' questions can share a name and each says the scope its answer claims.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each question takes one input per fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked ("Did you ...?").
-- A fact that a layer-1 rule takes as MAYBE BOOLEAN because another section answers it (the term "firearm", "bodily harm", "weapon", "intimate partner", "peace officer" and the like in section 2)
-- is built here from the facts that section asks, by calling the ccc-definitions.l4 function; a fact that another PART answers and that this layer cannot build
-- (a criminal organization under s 467.1(1), a terrorist activity under s 83.01(1), violence under s 3.01, forgery under s 366, a document under s 321) is asked as one yes-or-no fact whose @desc
-- says what the section it comes from requires, and is passed on as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE. The person cannot answer "not covered", so those questions are as definite as the person's own answers.
-- A fact that another section OF THIS RANGE answers (for example "is it culpable homicide?", "is it murder?", "did you commit the offence in section 247(1)?") is asked as one yes-or-no fact
-- whose @desc points to the question under that section, so that no question needs thirty inputs; where the facts that section needs are few (criminal negligence, the definition of a common gaming house,
-- the duties of section 215(1), the criteria of section 241.2(1)) the seat builds the answer from them instead. The person's yes is passed on as JUST TRUE and a no as JUST FALSE, so a "not covered" in the
-- earlier question has to be carried by the person's own reading of it (assumed, not ruled).
-- A record field that a rule never reads is not asked: every input below is read by the rule the question calls (checked when the file was written, by a script that is not shipped).
-- Answers a person cannot state at all (the Punishment of section 787(1), the general penalty on summary conviction) are not asked: see the next paragraph.
--
-- GRAVITY AND PENALTY. For each offence there are two questions, one for whether the person has committed it and one for how serious it is and what it can cost.
-- The second returns the record below. Its list holds the punishments that the section itself states (the indictable limb, or the whole of it where the offence is
-- indictable only), taken from the layer-1 constants. Where the section also makes the offence punishable on summary conviction and states no penalty for that, the Code's section 787(1)
-- (outside this part, encoded by another part) supplies the general penalty: the record says so in its last field and does not guess the penalty (assumed, not ruled).
-- A summary-only offence with no limb of its own has an empty list and that last field TRUE.
--
-- WHAT THE ANSWERS MEAN. MAYBE BOOLEAN answers follow the corpus convention (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc8)"): JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no;
-- NOTHING is "this section does not say". For an offence, JUST TRUE means the facts you state meet the section; NOTHING means they do not meet it as the section is worded
-- (not "you are innocent"). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- This is information about what the text says, not legal advice.

DECLARE `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
    HAS `Under sections 197 to 269.1, how serious the offence is`                                      IS A `Class of offence`
        `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the punishments that the section itself states`                   IS A LIST OF Punishment
        `Under sections 197 to 269.1, section 787(1) also supplies a penalty on summary conviction`     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN class IS A `Class of offence`
      `the punishments that the section states` IS A LIST OF Punishment
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty` OF class, `the punishments that the section states`, `the class is or includes summary conviction`
    WHERE
        `the class is or includes summary conviction` MEANS class EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction` OR class EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Is the place a common gaming house or a common betting house (section 197)`

-- Definitions that the offences turn on. A person who keeps, is found in, or lets a place may ask whether it is a "common gaming house" or "common betting house" at all.
@export Under section 197(1), is the place I am accused of keeping a common gaming house?
GIVEN `the place is a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a place? (The Code counts any place, whether or not it is covered or enclosed, used permanently or temporarily, or in anyone's exclusive use.)
      `the place is kept for gain and people resort to it to play games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place kept for gain, with people resorting to it to play games?
      `the place is kept or used to play games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place kept or used for playing games, whether or not for gain?
      `a bank is kept by some but not all of the players` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is a bank kept by one or more, but not all, of the players?
      `the bets or proceeds go to the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is all or any part of the bets or proceeds paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of the place?
      `a fee is charged to the players` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is a fee charged to or paid by the players, directly or indirectly, for the privilege of playing, taking part or using gaming equipment?
      `the chances of winning are not equal for everyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, are the chances of winning not equally favourable to everyone who plays, including whoever conducts the game?
      `the place is a genuine social club` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place occupied and used by an incorporated genuine social club (or a branch of one)?
      `the club's games pay the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the whole or any part of the bets or proceeds of the games played in it paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of it?
      `the club charges a fee for the games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a fee charged for the right or privilege of taking part in the games played in it?
      `the club's fee is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that fee charged under the authority and terms of a licence issued by the Attorney General of the province where the place is, or by a person or authority he specifies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 197(1), is the place I am accused of keeping a common gaming house` MEANS
    (`s 197(1) common gaming house` `the place is a place` `the place is kept for gain and people resort to it to play games` `the place is kept or used to play games` `a bank is kept by some but not all of the players` `the bets or proceeds go to the keeper` `a fee is charged to the players` `the chances of winning are not equal for everyone` (`s 197(2) the place is not a common gaming house within paragraph (a) or subparagraph (b)(ii) or (iii) of the definition` `the place is a genuine social club` `the club's games pay the keeper` `the club charges a fee for the games` `the club's fee is licensed`))

@export Under section 197(1), is the place I am accused of keeping a common betting house?
GIVEN `the place is a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a place? (The Code counts any place, whether or not it is covered or enclosed, used permanently or temporarily, or in anyone's exclusive use.)
      `the place is opened, kept or used so that people can bet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place opened, kept or used to enable, encourage or help people who resort to it to bet among themselves or with the keeper?
      `the place is opened, kept or used to receive or pay bets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place opened, kept or used to enable anyone to receive, record, register, transmit or pay bets, or to announce the results of betting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 197(1), is the place I am accused of keeping a common betting house` MEANS
    (`s 197(1) common betting house` `the place is a place` `the place is opened, kept or used so that people can bet` `the place is opened, kept or used to receive or pay bets`)

@export Under section 197(1), am I the keeper of the place?
GIVEN `I am an owner or occupier of the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an owner or occupier of the place?
      `I assist or act on behalf of an owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you assist, or act on behalf of, an owner or occupier of the place?
      `I appear to be, or to assist or act for, an owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appear to be an owner or occupier of the place, or to assist or act for one?
      `I have the care or management of the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the care or management of the place?
      `I use the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the place, permanently or temporarily, with or without the owner's or occupier's consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 197(1), am I the keeper of the place` MEANS
    `s 197(1) keeper` `I am an owner or occupier of the place` `I assist or act on behalf of an owner or occupier` `I appear to be, or to assist or act for, an owner or occupier` `I have the care or management of the place` `I use the place`

@export Under section 197(3), is it for me, not the prosecution, to prove that the place falls within the exception in section 197(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Under section 197(3), is it for me, not the prosecution, to prove that the place falls within the exception in section 197(2)` MEANS
    `s 197(3) the party who bears the onus of proving the exception in subsection 197(2)` EQUALS `the accused`

@export Under section 197(4), can the place still be a common gaming house although part of the game is played elsewhere, or it was used only once?
GIVEN `the place is used to play part of a game and another part is played elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place used to play part of a game, with another part of the game played elsewhere?
      `the stake that is played for is in some other place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the stake that is played for in some other place?
      `the place was used on only one occasion for games in which a bank is kept, the proceeds go to the keeper, a fee is charged or the chances are unequal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the place used on only one occasion for playing games in which a bank is kept, the proceeds go to the keeper, a fee is charged or the chances are unequal?
      `I or someone acting for or with me used another place on another occasion in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, or anyone acting for or with you, use another place on another occasion in that way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 197(4), can the place still be a common gaming house although part of the game is played elsewhere, or it was used only once` MEANS
    `s 197(4) the circumstance does not prevent the place from being a common gaming house` `the place is used to play part of a game and another part is played elsewhere` `the stake that is played for is in some other place` `the place was used on only one occasion for games in which a bank is kept, the proceeds go to the keeper, a fee is charged or the chances are unequal` `I or someone acting for or with me used another place on another occasion in that way`

§ `Search, arrest, seizure and forfeiture (section 199)`

-- Only arises if a place has been searched, a person taken into custody or a thing seized: ask "Has this happened to you?" before showing the group.
@export Under section 199(1), may a justice issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to enter and search the place?
GIVEN `the offence named in the information is under section` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code is the offence named in the information on oath? (Give the number, for example 201.)
      `a justice is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe the offence is being committed at a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a justice satisfied, by information on oath, that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the offence is being committed at the place?
      `the place is within the justice's jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place within the justice's jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 199(1), may a justice issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to enter and search the place` MEANS
    `s 199(1) a justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to enter and search the place` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence named in the information is under section`, "") `a justice is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe the offence is being committed at a place` `the place is within the justice's jurisdiction`

@export Under section 199(1), does a warrant for the place let me be taken into custody?
GIVEN `a warrant has been issued for the place under section 199(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a search warrant been issued for the place under section 199(1)?
      `I was found in or at the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found in or at the place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 199(1), does a warrant for the place let me be taken into custody` MEANS
    `s 199(1) the warrant authorizes the taking of the person into custody` `a warrant has been issued for the place under section 199(1)` `I was found in or at the place`

@export Under section 199(2), may a peace officer take me into custody without a warrant?
GIVEN `the person taking me into custody is a peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc In what capacity is the person taking you into custody acting? (Choose the one that fits; "a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace" is the usual one.)
      `the place is a common gaming house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a common gaming house, as section 197(1) defines it? (Answer yes only if you have worked that out; see the question under section 197(1).)
      `the officer finds me keeping the common gaming house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer find you keeping the common gaming house?
      `the officer finds me in the common gaming house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer find you in the common gaming house?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 199(2), may a peace officer take me into custody without a warrant` MEANS
    `s 199(2) the peace officer may take the person into custody without a warrant` (`s 2 peace officer` `the person taking me into custody is a peace officer`) (JUST `the place is a common gaming house`) `the officer finds me keeping the common gaming house` `the officer finds me in the common gaming house`

@export Under section 199(2), may a peace officer seize something I have?
GIVEN `the person seizing is a peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc In what capacity is the person seizing the thing acting? (Choose the one that fits.)
      `the thing may be evidence that a common gaming house is being kept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the thing be evidence that the offence of keeping a common gaming house is being committed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 199(2), may a peace officer seize something I have` MEANS
    `s 199(2) the peace officer may seize the thing` (`s 2 peace officer` `the person seizing is a peace officer`) `the thing may be evidence that a common gaming house is being kept`

@export Under section 199(3), may the court declare what was seized from me forfeited?
GIVEN `the thing was seized under section 199` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing seized under section 199?
      `the thing has been brought before a court, judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the thing been brought before a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge?
      `another law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another law expressly provide otherwise for the thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 199(3), may the court declare what was seized from me forfeited` MEANS
    `s 199(3) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may declare the thing forfeited` `the thing was seized under section 199` `the thing has been brought before a court, judge or justice` `another law expressly provides otherwise`

@export Under section 199(3), must the thing declared forfeited be disposed of as the Attorney General directs?
GIVEN `the thing has been declared forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the thing been declared forfeited?
      `I have shown sufficient cause why it should not be forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you shown sufficient cause why it should not be forfeited?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 199(3), must the thing declared forfeited be disposed of as the Attorney General directs` MEANS
    `s 199(3) the forfeited thing shall be disposed of or dealt with as the Attorney General may direct` `the thing has been declared forfeited` `I have shown sufficient cause why it should not be forfeited`

§ `Keeping, being found in, and betting offences (sections 201 to 203)`

@export Under section 201(1), have I committed the offence of keeping a common gaming house or common betting house?
GIVEN `I keep the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you keep the place (as its owner, occupier, manager or user: see the question under section 197(1) on who is a keeper)?
      `the place is a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a place? (The Code counts any place, whether or not it is covered or enclosed, used permanently or temporarily, or in anyone's exclusive use.)
      `the place is kept for gain and people resort to it to play games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place kept for gain, with people resorting to it to play games?
      `the place is kept or used to play games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place kept or used for playing games, whether or not for gain?
      `a bank is kept by some but not all of the players` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is a bank kept by one or more, but not all, of the players?
      `the bets or proceeds go to the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is all or any part of the bets or proceeds paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of the place?
      `a fee is charged to the players` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is a fee charged to or paid by the players, directly or indirectly, for the privilege of playing, taking part or using gaming equipment?
      `the chances of winning are not equal for everyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, are the chances of winning not equally favourable to everyone who plays, including whoever conducts the game?
      `the place is a genuine social club` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place occupied and used by an incorporated genuine social club (or a branch of one)?
      `the club's games pay the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the whole or any part of the bets or proceeds of the games played in it paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of it?
      `the club charges a fee for the games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a fee charged for the right or privilege of taking part in the games played in it?
      `the club's fee is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that fee charged under the authority and terms of a licence issued by the Attorney General of the province where the place is, or by a person or authority he specifies?
      `the place is opened, kept or used so that people can bet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place opened, kept or used to enable, encourage or help people who resort to it to bet among themselves or with the keeper?
      `the place is opened, kept or used to receive or pay bets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place opened, kept or used to enable anyone to receive, record, register, transmit or pay bets, or to announce the results of betting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 201(1), have I committed the offence of keeping a common gaming house or common betting house` MEANS
    `s 201(1) the person commits the offence of keeping a common gaming house or common betting house` `I keep the place` (`s 197(1) disorderly house` (`s 197(1) common betting house` `the place is a place` `the place is opened, kept or used so that people can bet` `the place is opened, kept or used to receive or pay bets`) (`s 197(1) common gaming house` `the place is a place` `the place is kept for gain and people resort to it to play games` `the place is kept or used to play games` `a bank is kept by some but not all of the players` `the bets or proceeds go to the keeper` `a fee is charged to the players` `the chances of winning are not equal for everyone` (`s 197(2) the place is not a common gaming house within paragraph (a) or subparagraph (b)(ii) or (iii) of the definition` `the place is a genuine social club` `the club's games pay the keeper` `the club charges a fee for the games` `the club's fee is licensed`)))

@export Under section 201(1), how serious is the offence of keeping a common gaming house or common betting house, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 201(1), how serious is the offence of keeping a common gaming house or common betting house, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 201(1) the class of the offence` (LIST `s 201(1)(a) the indictable limb`)

@export Under section 201(2), have I committed the offence of being found in, or letting the use of, a gaming or betting house?
GIVEN `I was found in the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found in the place?
      `I had lawful excuse for being found in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse for being found in it? (The burden of proving one is a matter for the court; answer yes only if you say you did.)
      `I am the owner, landlord, lessor, tenant, occupier or agent of the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the owner, landlord, lessor, tenant, occupier or agent of the place?
      `I knowingly let or allowed the place to be used as a common gaming house or common betting house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly permit the place to be let or used for the purposes of a common gaming house or common betting house?
      `the place is a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a place? (The Code counts any place, whether or not it is covered or enclosed, used permanently or temporarily, or in anyone's exclusive use.)
      `the place is kept for gain and people resort to it to play games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place kept for gain, with people resorting to it to play games?
      `the place is kept or used to play games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place kept or used for playing games, whether or not for gain?
      `a bank is kept by some but not all of the players` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is a bank kept by one or more, but not all, of the players?
      `the bets or proceeds go to the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is all or any part of the bets or proceeds paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of the place?
      `a fee is charged to the players` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, is a fee charged to or paid by the players, directly or indirectly, for the privilege of playing, taking part or using gaming equipment?
      `the chances of winning are not equal for everyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In those games, are the chances of winning not equally favourable to everyone who plays, including whoever conducts the game?
      `the place is a genuine social club` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place occupied and used by an incorporated genuine social club (or a branch of one)?
      `the club's games pay the keeper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the whole or any part of the bets or proceeds of the games played in it paid, directly or indirectly, to the keeper of it?
      `the club charges a fee for the games` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a fee charged for the right or privilege of taking part in the games played in it?
      `the club's fee is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that fee charged under the authority and terms of a licence issued by the Attorney General of the province where the place is, or by a person or authority he specifies?
      `the place is opened, kept or used so that people can bet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place opened, kept or used to enable, encourage or help people who resort to it to bet among themselves or with the keeper?
      `the place is opened, kept or used to receive or pay bets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place opened, kept or used to enable anyone to receive, record, register, transmit or pay bets, or to announce the results of betting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 201(2), have I committed the offence of being found in, or letting the use of, a gaming or betting house` MEANS
    `s 201(2) the person commits the offence of being found in, or permitting the use of, a gaming or betting house` (`s 197(1) disorderly house` (`s 197(1) common betting house` `the place is a place` `the place is opened, kept or used so that people can bet` `the place is opened, kept or used to receive or pay bets`) (`s 197(1) common gaming house` `the place is a place` `the place is kept for gain and people resort to it to play games` `the place is kept or used to play games` `a bank is kept by some but not all of the players` `the bets or proceeds go to the keeper` `a fee is charged to the players` `the chances of winning are not equal for everyone` (`s 197(2) the place is not a common gaming house within paragraph (a) or subparagraph (b)(ii) or (iii) of the definition` `the place is a genuine social club` `the club's games pay the keeper` `the club charges a fee for the games` `the club's fee is licensed`))) `I was found in the place` `I had lawful excuse for being found in it` `I am the owner, landlord, lessor, tenant, occupier or agent of the place` `I knowingly let or allowed the place to be used as a common gaming house or common betting house`

@export Under section 201(2), how serious is the offence of being found in, or letting the use of, a gaming or betting house, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 201(2), how serious is the offence of being found in, or letting the use of, a gaming or betting house, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 201(2) the class of the offence` EMPTY

@export Under section 202(1), have I committed one of the offences of betting, book-making or pool-selling?
GIVEN `which of these did I do` IS A `s 202(1) act` @desc Which of the acts listed in section 202(1)(a) to (j) did you do?
      `the thing is a periodical published in good faith for another purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information in a newspaper, magazine or other periodical published in good faith primarily for a purpose other than publishing such information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
