§ `Duties tending to preservation of life (sections 214 to 218)`

@export Under section 215(1), am I under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life?
GIVEN `I am a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family of the child?
      `the child's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in years?
      `the other person is my spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person your spouse (in the ordinary meaning of the word)?
      `I am cohabiting with the other person in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you cohabiting with the other person in a conjugal relationship?
      `the months I have cohabited with the other person` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months have you so cohabited? (A common-law partner is someone with whom you have cohabited for at least one year.)
      `the other person is in my charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person under your charge?
      `the other person cannot withdraw from my charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person unable, by reason of detention, age, illness, mental disorder or other cause, to withdraw from your charge?
      `the other person cannot provide necessaries of life for themselves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person unable to provide themselves with necessaries of life?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 215(1), am I under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life` MEANS
    (`s 215(1) the person is under a legal duty` (`s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` `I am a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family` `the child's age in years`) (`s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` `the other person is my spouse` (`s 2 common-law partner` `I am cohabiting with the other person in a conjugal relationship` `the months I have cohabited with the other person`)) (`s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` `the other person is in my charge` `the other person cannot withdraw from my charge` `the other person cannot provide necessaries of life for themselves`))

@export Under section 215(2), have I committed the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life?
GIVEN `I am a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family of the child?
      `the child's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in years?
      `the other person is my spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person your spouse (in the ordinary meaning of the word)?
      `I am cohabiting with the other person in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you cohabiting with the other person in a conjugal relationship?
      `the months I have cohabited with the other person` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months have you so cohabited? (A common-law partner is someone with whom you have cohabited for at least one year.)
      `the other person is in my charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person under your charge?
      `the other person cannot withdraw from my charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person unable, by reason of detention, age, illness, mental disorder or other cause, to withdraw from your charge?
      `the other person cannot provide necessaries of life for themselves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person unable to provide themselves with necessaries of life?
      `I failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to perform the duty?
      `I had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a lawful excuse for failing? (Whether the excuse is lawful is for the court; answer yes if you say you did.)
      `the person owed the duty is in destitute or necessitous circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the duty is owed in destitute or necessitous circumstances?
      `the failure endangers life or is likely to endanger health permanently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the failure endanger the life of the person owed the duty, or cause or is it likely to cause their health to be endangered permanently?
      `the failure endangers life or is likely to injure health permanently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the failure endanger the life of the person owed the duty, or cause or is it likely to cause their health to be injured permanently?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 215(2), have I committed the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` MEANS
    `s 215(2) the person commits the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life` (`s 215(1) the person is under a legal duty` (`s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` `I am a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family` `the child's age in years`) (`s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` `the other person is my spouse` (`s 2 common-law partner` `I am cohabiting with the other person in a conjugal relationship` `the months I have cohabited with the other person`)) (`s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` `the other person is in my charge` `the other person cannot withdraw from my charge` `the other person cannot provide necessaries of life for themselves`)) ((`s 215(1)(a) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life for the child` `I am a parent, foster parent, guardian or head of a family` `the child's age in years`) EQUALS JUST TRUE OR (`s 215(1)(b) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to their spouse or common-law partner` `the other person is my spouse` (`s 2 common-law partner` `I am cohabiting with the other person in a conjugal relationship` `the months I have cohabited with the other person`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE) ((`s 215(1)(c) the person is under a legal duty to provide necessaries of life to a person under his charge` `the other person is in my charge` `the other person cannot withdraw from my charge` `the other person cannot provide necessaries of life for themselves`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `I failed to perform the duty` `I had a lawful excuse` `the person owed the duty is in destitute or necessitous circumstances` `the failure endangers life or is likely to endanger health permanently` `the failure endangers life or is likely to injure health permanently`

@export Under section 215(3), how serious is the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 215(3), how serious is the offence of failing to provide necessaries of life, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 215(3) the class of the offence` (LIST `s 215(3)(a) the indictable limb`)

@export Under section 215(4), does a month's failure to provide for my child count as proof that I failed without lawful excuse?
GIVEN `the date from which I failed to make provision for the child's maintenance` IS A DATE @desc From what date did you fail to make provision for the maintenance of the child?
      `the date as at which this is assessed` IS A DATE @desc As at what date is it to be assessed?
      `the child is my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child a child of yours?
      `the child's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in years?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary (that you had a lawful excuse)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 215(4), does a month's failure to provide for my child count as proof that I failed without lawful excuse` MEANS
    `s 215(4)(c) the failure for one month is proof that the person failed without lawful excuse to provide necessaries of life for the child` `the date from which I failed to make provision for the child's maintenance` `the date as at which this is assessed` `the child is my child` `the child's age in years` `there is evidence to the contrary`

@export Under section 215(4), does my recognizing a child as mine count as proof that the child is mine?
GIVEN `I have in any way recognized the child as my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you in any way recognized the child as being your child?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 215(4), does my recognizing a child as mine count as proof that the child is mine` MEANS
    `s 215(4)(b) the recognition is proof that the child is his child` `I have in any way recognized the child as my child` `there is evidence to the contrary`

@export Under section 215(4), is it a defence that my spouse, partner or child received necessaries of life from someone else?
GIVEN `the spouse, common-law partner or child is receiving or has received necessaries of life from another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your spouse, common-law partner or child receiving, or did they receive, necessaries of life from another person?
      `that other person is not under a legal duty to provide them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that other person not under a legal duty to provide them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 215(4), is it a defence that my spouse, partner or child received necessaries of life from someone else` MEANS
    `s 215(4)(d) the receipt of necessaries of life from another person is a defence` `the spouse, common-law partner or child is receiving or has received necessaries of life from another person` `that other person is not under a legal duty to provide them`

@export Under section 216, am I under a legal duty to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care in giving medical treatment or doing a dangerous act?
GIVEN `I undertake to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you undertake to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person?
      `I undertake to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you undertake to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person?
      `it is a case of necessity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a case of necessity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 216, am I under a legal duty to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care in giving medical treatment or doing a dangerous act` MEANS
    `s 216 the person is under a legal duty to have and to use reasonable knowledge, skill and care` `I undertake to administer surgical or medical treatment to another person` `I undertake to do any other lawful act that may endanger the life of another person` `it is a case of necessity`

@export Under section 217, am I under a legal duty to do an act I have undertaken?
GIVEN `I undertake to do an act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you undertaken to do an act?
      `an omission to do the act is or may be dangerous to life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an omission to do the act dangerous to life, or may it be?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 217, am I under a legal duty to do an act I have undertaken` MEANS
    `s 217 the person is under a legal duty to do the act` `I undertake to do an act` `an omission to do the act is or may be dangerous to life`

@export Under section 217.1, am I under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm to those whose work I direct?
GIVEN `I undertake, or have the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you undertake, or have the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 217.1, am I under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm to those whose work I direct` MEANS
    `s 217.1 the person is under a legal duty to take reasonable steps to prevent bodily harm` `I undertake, or have the authority, to direct how another person does work or performs a task`

@export Under section 218, have I committed the offence of abandoning a child?
GIVEN `I unlawfully abandoned or exposed a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you unlawfully abandon or expose a child?
      `the child's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in years?
      `the child's life is or is likely to be endangered or its health is or is likely to be permanently injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child's life endangered or likely to be, or its health permanently injured or likely to be?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 218, have I committed the offence of abandoning a child` MEANS
    `s 218 the person commits the offence of abandoning a child` `I unlawfully abandoned or exposed a child` `the child's age in years` `the child's life is or is likely to be endangered or its health is or is likely to be permanently injured`

@export Under section 218, how serious is the offence of abandoning a child, and what can it cost me?
