§ `Criminal negligence and homicide (sections 219 to 228)`

-- Only arises if a person has died or been injured.
@export Under section 219(1), am I criminally negligent?
GIVEN `I did something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do something (anything at all) that you say was not criminal negligence?
      `I failed to do something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to do something?
      `what I failed to do was a duty imposed by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you failed to do a duty imposed on you by law?
      `I showed wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In doing it or failing to do it, did you show wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 219(1), am I criminally negligent` MEANS
    (`s 219(1) the person is criminally negligent` `I did something` (IF `I failed to do something` THEN `s 219(2) duty` `what I failed to do was a duty imposed by law` ELSE JUST FALSE) `I showed wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons`)

@export Under section 220, have I committed the offence of causing death by criminal negligence?
GIVEN `I did something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do something (anything at all) that you say was not criminal negligence?
      `I failed to do something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to do something?
      `what I failed to do was a duty imposed by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you failed to do a duty imposed on you by law?
      `I showed wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In doing it or failing to do it, did you show wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons?
      `I thereby caused the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your criminal negligence cause the death of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 220, have I committed the offence of causing death by criminal negligence` MEANS
    `s 220 the person commits the offence of causing death by criminal negligence` (`s 219(1) the person is criminally negligent` `I did something` (IF `I failed to do something` THEN `s 219(2) duty` `what I failed to do was a duty imposed by law` ELSE JUST FALSE) `I showed wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons`) `I thereby caused the death of another person`

@export Under section 220, how serious is the offence of causing death by criminal negligence, and what can it cost me?
GIVEN `a firearm was used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a firearm used in the commission of the offence?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 220, how serious is the offence of causing death by criminal negligence, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 220 the class of the offence` (`s 220 the punishment` `a firearm was used in the commission of the offence`)

@export Under section 221, have I committed the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence?
GIVEN `I did something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do something (anything at all) that you say was not criminal negligence?
      `I failed to do something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to do something?
      `what I failed to do was a duty imposed by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you failed to do a duty imposed on you by law?
      `I showed wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In doing it or failing to do it, did you show wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons?
      `the bodily harm was caused by my criminal negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt or injury caused by your criminal negligence?
      `there was a hurt or injury to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a hurt or injury to a person?
      `the hurt or injury interferes with the person's health or comfort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the hurt or injury interfere with the person's health or comfort?
      `the hurt or injury is more than merely transient or trifling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hurt or injury more than merely transient or trifling in nature?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 221, have I committed the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence` MEANS
    `s 221 the person commits the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence` (`s 219(1) the person is criminally negligent` `I did something` (IF `I failed to do something` THEN `s 219(2) duty` `what I failed to do was a duty imposed by law` ELSE JUST FALSE) `I showed wanton or reckless disregard for the lives or safety of other persons`) (IF `the bodily harm was caused by my criminal negligence` THEN (`s 2 bodily harm` `there was a hurt or injury to a person` `the hurt or injury interferes with the person's health or comfort` `the hurt or injury is more than merely transient or trifling`) ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 221, how serious is the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 221, how serious is the offence of causing bodily harm by criminal negligence, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 221 the class of the offence` (LIST `s 221(a) the indictable limb`)

@export Under section 222(1), have I committed homicide?
GIVEN `I caused the death of a human being, directly or indirectly, by any means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, directly or indirectly, by any means, cause the death of a human being?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 222(1), have I committed homicide` MEANS
    `s 222(1) the person commits homicide` `I caused the death of a human being, directly or indirectly, by any means`

@export Under section 222(5), have I committed culpable homicide?
GIVEN `I caused the death of a human being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the death of a human being?
      `I did it by means of an unlawful act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it by means of an unlawful act?
      `I did it by criminal negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it by criminal negligence? (Answer yes only if you have worked that out: see the question under section 219(1).)
      `I did it by causing the person, by threats or fear of violence or by deception, to do something that caused their death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it by causing that human being, by threats or fear of violence or by deception, to do anything that caused his death?
      `I did it by wilfully frightening a child or sick person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it by wilfully frightening a child or a sick person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 222(5), have I committed culpable homicide` MEANS
    `s 222(5) the person commits culpable homicide` `I caused the death of a human being` `I did it by means of an unlawful act` (JUST `I did it by criminal negligence`) `I did it by causing the person, by threats or fear of violence or by deception, to do something that caused their death` `I did it by wilfully frightening a child or sick person`

@export Under section 222(3), is my homicide an offence?
GIVEN `it is homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it homicide? (See the question under section 222(1).)
      `it is culpable homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it culpable homicide? (See the question under section 222(5).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 222(3), is my homicide an offence` MEANS
    `s 222(3) the homicide is an offence` (JUST `it is homicide`) (JUST `it is culpable homicide`)

@export Under section 223(2), have I committed homicide by injuring a child before or during its birth?
GIVEN `I caused injury to a child before or during its birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause injury to a child before or during its birth?
      `the child has completely proceeded from the body of its mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child completely proceeded from the body of its mother?
      `the child is in a living state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child in a living state?
      `the child died after becoming a human being, as a result of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the child die, after becoming a human being, as a result of the injury?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 223(2), have I committed homicide by injuring a child before or during its birth` MEANS
    `s 223(2) the person commits homicide by injuring a child before or during its birth` `I caused injury to a child before or during its birth` (IF `the child died after becoming a human being, as a result of the injury` THEN `s 223(1) the child has become a human being` `the child has completely proceeded from the body of its mother` `the child is in a living state` ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 224, am I treated as having caused a death that my act or omission resulted in even if other causes contributed?
GIVEN `I did a thing by an act or omission that resulted in the death of a human being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, by an act or omission, do a thing that resulted in the death of a human being?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 224, am I treated as having caused a death that my act or omission resulted in even if other causes contributed` MEANS
    `s 224 the person causes the death of the human being by virtue of this section` `I did a thing by an act or omission that resulted in the death of a human being`

@export Under section 225, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a dangerous bodily injury I caused?
GIVEN `I caused a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause to a human being a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature?
      `death resulted from the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did death result from the injury?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 225, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a dangerous bodily injury I caused` MEANS
    `s 225 the person causes the death of the human being by virtue of this section` `I caused a bodily injury that is of itself of a dangerous nature` `death resulted from the injury`

@export Under section 226, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a bodily injury I caused?
GIVEN `I caused a bodily injury that resulted in death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause to a human being a bodily injury that results in death?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 226, am I treated as having caused a death that followed a bodily injury I caused` MEANS
    `s 226 the person causes the death of the human being by virtue of this section` `I caused a bodily injury that resulted in death`

@export Under section 227(1), have I committed culpable homicide by providing medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I am entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province?
      `I am a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered nurse?
      `I am entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled, under the laws of a province, to practise as a nurse practitioner (or under an equivalent designation)?
      `I am entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients?
      `I administered a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you administer a substance to a person?
      `the administering was at their request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the administering at their request?
      `the substance caused their death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the substance cause their death?
      `I prescribed or provided a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you prescribe or provide a substance to a person?
      `the prescribing or providing was at their request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the prescribing or providing at their request?
      `it was so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death?
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in accordance with section 241.2 (the safeguards)?
      `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 227(1), have I committed culpable homicide by providing medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 227(1) the practitioner commits culpable homicide` (`s 227(5) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (IF `s 241.1 medical practitioner` `I am entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `s 241.1 nurse practitioner` `I am a registered nurse` `I am entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner` `I am entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients`)) (`s 227(5) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (`s 241.1 medical assistance in dying` `I administered a substance to a person` `the administering was at their request` `the substance caused their death` `I prescribed or provided a substance to a person` `the prescribing or providing was at their request` `it was so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death`)) `it is in accordance with section 241.2` (`s 227(3) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`)

@export Under section 227(2), am I a party to culpable homicide because I helped a practitioner provide medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I did something for the purpose of aiding a practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying?
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in accordance with section 241.2?
      `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 227(2), am I a party to culpable homicide because I helped a practitioner provide medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 227(2) the person is a party to culpable homicide` `I did something for the purpose of aiding a practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying` `it is in accordance with section 241.2` (`s 227(3) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`)

@export Under section 227(4), does the rule that no one may consent to death being inflicted on them apply to me when I receive medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I consent to have death inflicted on me by medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to have death inflicted on you by means of medical assistance in dying?
      `it is provided in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it provided in accordance with section 241.2?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 227(4), does the rule that no one may consent to death being inflicted on them apply to me when I receive medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 227(4) section 14 applies to the person` `I consent to have death inflicted on me by medical assistance in dying` `it is provided in accordance with section 241.2`

@export Under section 228, have I committed culpable homicide by influencing a mind alone?
GIVEN `I caused the death of a human being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the death of a human being?
      `it was by any influence on the mind alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it by any influence on the mind alone?
      `it was by any disorder or disease resulting from influence on the mind alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it by any disorder or disease resulting from influence on the mind alone?
      `I caused the death of a child or sick person by wilfully frightening him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the death of a child or sick person by wilfully frightening him?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 228, have I committed culpable homicide by influencing a mind alone` MEANS
    `s 228 the person commits culpable homicide` `I caused the death of a human being` `it was by any influence on the mind alone` `it was by any disorder or disease resulting from influence on the mind alone` `I caused the death of a child or sick person by wilfully frightening him`

§ `Murder, manslaughter, infanticide and attempts (sections 229 to 240)`

-- Only arises if a person has died or been attacked with intent to kill: ask "Has this happened to you?" before showing the group.
@export Under section 229, is it murder?
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it culpable homicide? (Answer yes only if you have worked that out: see the question under section 222(5).)
      `I meant to cause the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to cause the death of the human being?
      `I meant to cause bodily harm that I knew was likely to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to cause bodily harm that you knew was likely to cause death?
      `I was reckless whether death ensued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless whether death ensued or not?
      `I killed another by accident or mistake while meaning to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, meaning to cause death to a human being (or bodily harm you knew was likely to cause death), and being reckless whether death ensued, by accident or mistake cause the death of another human being?
      `I did something I knew was likely to cause death, for an unlawful object, and caused a death by doing so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an unlawful object, did you do something that you knew was likely to cause death, and by doing so cause the death of a human being?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 229, is it murder` MEANS
    `s 229 culpable homicide is murder` (JUST `it is culpable homicide`) `I meant to cause the death` `I meant to cause bodily harm that I knew was likely to cause death` `I was reckless whether death ensued` `I killed another by accident or mistake while meaning to cause death` `I did something I knew was likely to cause death, for an unlawful object, and caused a death by doing so`

@export Under section 231(2), is the murder first degree murder because it was planned and deliberate?
GIVEN `it was planned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it planned?
      `it was deliberate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it deliberate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(2), is the murder first degree murder because it was planned and deliberate` MEANS
    `s 231(2) the murder is first degree murder` `it was planned` `it was deliberate`

@export Under section 231(3), was the murder planned and deliberate because it was committed for money or anything of value?
GIVEN `it was committed under an arrangement under which money or anything of value passes or is promised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it committed pursuant to an arrangement under which money or anything of value passes, or is intended to pass or is promised, from one person to another?
      `that was as consideration for causing or assisting in causing the death of anyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that as consideration for the other's causing or assisting in causing the death of anyone, or counselling another to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(3), was the murder planned and deliberate because it was committed for money or anything of value` MEANS
    `s 231(3) the murder is planned and deliberate` `it was committed under an arrangement under which money or anything of value passes or is promised` `that was as consideration for causing or assisting in causing the death of anyone`

@export Under section 231(4), is the murder first degree murder because the victim was a police officer, prison officer or prison worker?
GIVEN `the victim was a police officer, constable, sheriff or other person employed for the preservation of the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim a police officer, police constable, constable, sheriff, deputy sheriff, sheriff's officer or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace?
      `the victim was a warden, guard or other officer or permanent employee of a prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim a warden, deputy warden, instructor, keeper, jailer, guard or other officer or permanent employee of a prison?
      `the victim was a person working in a prison with permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim a person working in a prison with the permission of the prison authorities?
      `the victim was acting in the course of their duties or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim acting in the course of their duties (or, for a person working in a prison with permission, of their work there)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(4), is the murder first degree murder because the victim was a police officer, prison officer or prison worker` MEANS
    `s 231(4) the murder is first degree murder because of the victim` `the victim was a police officer, constable, sheriff or other person employed for the preservation of the public peace` `the victim was a warden, guard or other officer or permanent employee of a prison` `the victim was a person working in a prison with permission` `the victim was acting in the course of their duties or work`

@export Under section 231(5), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing or attempting another listed offence?
GIVEN `the section of the Code of the offence I was committing or attempting` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code was the offence you were committing or attempting? (For example 271. Give only the number.)
      `the subsection of that section, if any` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection of that section? (For example (1); leave blank if it is the whole section.)
      `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the death while committing or attempting to commit that offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(5), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing or attempting another listed offence` MEANS
    `s 231(5) the murder is first degree murder because of the offence being committed` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the Code of the offence I was committing or attempting`, `the subsection of that section, if any`) `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit that offence`

@export Under section 231(5.1), is the murder first degree murder because of coercive control, exploitation, a sexual offence or hate?
GIVEN `the death was caused while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct with intent to cause the victim to believe that their physical or psychological safety was threatened?
      `how the victim stands to me` IS A `s 2 intimate partner relationship` @desc What was the victim to you? (Choose the one that fits; "intimate partner" includes a current or former spouse, common-law partner or dating partner.)
      `the death was caused while exercising control, direction or influence over the victim's movements with intent to exploit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused while exercising control, direction or influence over the victim's movements with intent to exploit the victim, within the meaning of section 279.04?
      `the death was caused while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature, or an offence for a sexual purpose?
      `the death was caused while motivated by hate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused while motivated by hate based on colour, race, religion, national or ethnic origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or mental or physical disability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(5.1), is the murder first degree murder because of coercive control, exploitation, a sexual offence or hate` MEANS
    `s 231(5.1) the murder is first degree murder because of the circumstances` `the death was caused while engaging in, or after having engaged in, a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct` (`s 2 intimate partner` `how the victim stands to me`) `the death was caused while exercising control, direction or influence over the victim's movements with intent to exploit` `the death was caused while committing or attempting to commit an offence of a sexual nature` `the death was caused while motivated by hate`

@export Under section 231(6), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing criminal harassment?
GIVEN `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit criminal harassment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the death while committing or attempting to commit an offence under section 264 (criminal harassment)?
      `I did so with intent to cause the victim to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, was threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it with intent to cause the victim to believe that their physical or psychological safety, or that of anyone known to them, was threatened?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(6), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing criminal harassment` MEANS
    `s 231(6) the murder is first degree murder because of criminal harassment` `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit criminal harassment` `I did so with intent to cause the victim to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, was threatened`

@export Under section 231(6.01), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing an indictable offence that is a terrorist activity?
GIVEN `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the death while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence under the Criminal Code or another Act of Parliament?
      `the act or omission also constitutes a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act or omission constituting the offence also constitute a terrorist activity, as section 83.01(1) defines that? (Answer yes or no; that definition is in another part of the Code.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(6.01), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing an indictable offence that is a terrorist activity` MEANS
    `s 231(6.01) the murder is first degree murder because of terrorist activity` `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence` (JUST `the act or omission also constitutes a terrorist activity`)

@export Under section 231(6.1), is the murder first degree murder because it was for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization?
GIVEN `the death was caused for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization, as section 467.1(1) defines that? (Answer yes or no; that definition is in another part of the Code.)
      `the death was caused while committing an indictable offence for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused while committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence, for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(6.1), is the murder first degree murder because it was for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization` MEANS
    `s 231(6.1) the murder is first degree murder because of a criminal organization` (JUST `the death was caused for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization`) (JUST `the death was caused while committing an indictable offence for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization`)

@export Under section 231(6.2), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing intimidation of a justice system participant?
GIVEN `the section of the Code of the offence I was committing or attempting` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code was the offence you were committing or attempting? (For example 423.1. Give only the number.)
      `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the death while committing or attempting to commit that offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(6.2), is the murder first degree murder because I caused the death while committing intimidation of a justice system participant` MEANS
    `s 231(6.2) the murder is first degree murder because of intimidation` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the Code of the offence I was committing or attempting`, "") `I caused the death while committing or attempting to commit that offence`

@export Under section 231(7), is the murder second degree murder?
GIVEN `it is murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it murder? (Answer yes only if you have worked that out: see the question under section 229.)
      `it is first degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it first degree murder, by any of the routes in sections 231(2) to (6.2)? (See the questions under section 231.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 231(7), is the murder second degree murder` MEANS
    `s 231(7) the murder is second degree murder` (JUST `it is murder`) (JUST `it is first degree murder`)

@export Under section 231, which kind of homicide offence have I committed: first degree murder, second degree murder, manslaughter or infanticide?
GIVEN `it is culpable homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it culpable homicide? (See the question under section 222(5).)
      `it is murder after any reduction under section 232(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it murder, taking into account any reduction to manslaughter for provocation? (See the questions under sections 229 and 232(1).)
      `it is infanticide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it infanticide? (See the question under section 233.)
      `it is first degree murder by one of the routes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it first degree murder by one of the routes in sections 231(2) to (6.2)? (See the questions under section 231.)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of homicide offence`
`Under section 231, which kind of homicide offence have I committed: first degree murder, second degree murder, manslaughter or infanticide` MEANS
    `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` (JUST `it is culpable homicide`) (JUST `it is murder after any reduction under section 232(1)`) (JUST `it is infanticide`) (LIST (JUST `it is first degree murder by one of the routes`))

@export Under section 232(1), is my culpable homicide reduced to manslaughter because I acted in the heat of passion on provocation?
GIVEN `it would otherwise be murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would it otherwise be murder? (See the question under section 229.)
      `I acted in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation?
      `there was provocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there provocation as section 232(2) defines it? (See the question under section 232(2).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 232(1), is my culpable homicide reduced to manslaughter because I acted in the heat of passion on provocation` MEANS
    `s 232(1) the culpable homicide is reduced to manslaughter` (JUST `it would otherwise be murder`) `I acted in the heat of passion caused by sudden provocation` (JUST `there was provocation`)

@export Under section 232(2), was the victim's conduct provocation?
GIVEN `the victim's conduct would constitute an indictable offence under the Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the victim's conduct constitute an indictable offence under the Criminal Code?
      `that offence is punishable by imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence punishable by imprisonment for life?
      `the maximum imprisonment for it, whole years` IS A NUMBER @desc If not for life, what is the maximum term of imprisonment for it? Give the whole years here (for example 5).
      `the maximum imprisonment for it, further months` IS A NUMBER @desc And the further months, if any (for example 0).
      `the maximum imprisonment is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the maximum "less a day" (for example "two years less a day")?
      `the conduct would deprive an ordinary person of the power of self-control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conduct of such a nature as to be sufficient to deprive an ordinary person of the power of self-control?
      `I acted on it on the sudden` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act on it on the sudden?
      `I acted before there was time for my passion to cool` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act before there was time for your passion to cool?
      `the victim is deemed to have given provocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the victim do something that they had a legal right to do, or that you incited them to do in order to give you an excuse for causing death or bodily harm? (See the question under section 232(3).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 232(2), was the victim's conduct provocation` MEANS
