`Under section 241(1), how serious is counselling or aiding suicide, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 241(1) the class of the offence` `s 241(1) the punishment`

@export Under section 241(2), do I, as a practitioner, commit the offence of aiding suicide when I provide medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I am entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province?
      `I am a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered nurse?
      `I am entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled, under the laws of a province, to practise as a nurse practitioner (or under an equivalent designation)?
      `I am entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients?
      `I administered a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you administer a substance to a person?
      `the administering was at their request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the administering at their request?
      `the substance caused their death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the substance cause their death?
      `I prescribed or provided a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you prescribe or provide a substance to a person?
      `the prescribing or providing was at their request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the prescribing or providing at their request?
      `it was so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death?
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in accordance with section 241.2 (the safeguards)?
      `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241(2), do I, as a practitioner, commit the offence of aiding suicide when I provide medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 241(2) the practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (`s 241(7) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (IF `s 241.1 medical practitioner` `I am entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `s 241.1 nurse practitioner` `I am a registered nurse` `I am entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner` `I am entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients`)) (`s 241(7) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (`s 241.1 medical assistance in dying` `I administered a substance to a person` `the administering was at their request` `the substance caused their death` `I prescribed or provided a substance to a person` `the prescribing or providing was at their request` `it was so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death`)) `it is in accordance with section 241.2` (`s 241(6) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`)

@export Under section 241(3), am I a party to the offence of aiding suicide when I help a practitioner provide medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I did something for the purpose of aiding a practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying?
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in accordance with section 241.2?
      `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241(3), am I a party to the offence of aiding suicide when I help a practitioner provide medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 241(3) the person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` `I did something for the purpose of aiding a practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying` `it is in accordance with section 241.2` (`s 241(6) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`)

@export Under section 241(4), do I, as a pharmacist, commit the offence of aiding suicide when I dispense a substance for medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I am entitled to practise pharmacy under the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to practise pharmacy under the laws of a province?
      `I dispensed a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you dispense a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner?
      `I dispensed it further to a prescription written by a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you dispense it further to a prescription written by such a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2?
      `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241(4), do I, as a pharmacist, commit the offence of aiding suicide when I dispense a substance for medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 241(4) the pharmacist commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (`s 241(7) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (`s 241.1 pharmacist` `I am entitled to practise pharmacy under the laws of a province`)) `I dispensed a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` `I dispensed it further to a prescription written by a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2` (`s 241(6) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`)

@export Under section 241(5), do I commit the offence of aiding suicide when I help a person self-administer a substance prescribed for medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I did something at another person's explicit request to help them self-administer a substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At another person's explicit request, did you do anything for the purpose of aiding that person to self-administer a substance?
