      `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241(5), do I commit the offence of aiding suicide when I help a person self-administer a substance prescribed for medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 241(5) the person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` `I did something at another person's explicit request to help them self-administer a substance` `the substance had been prescribed for that person as part of medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2` (`s 241(6) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` `I had a reasonable but mistaken belief about a fact that is an element of the exemption`)

@export Under section 241(5.1), do I commit an offence by giving a person information about medical assistance in dying?
