§ `Medical assistance in dying (sections 241.1 to 241.4)`

-- Only arises for a practitioner, pharmacist or helper involved in medical assistance in dying: ask "Were you involved in medical assistance in dying?" before showing the group.
@export Under section 241.1, is what I did medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I am entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province?
      `I am a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered nurse?
      `I am entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled, under the laws of a province, to practise as a nurse practitioner (or under an equivalent designation)?
      `I am entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients?
      `I administered a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you administer a substance to a person?
      `the administering was at their request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the administering at their request?
      `the substance caused their death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the substance cause their death?
      `I prescribed or provided a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you prescribe or provide a substance to a person?
      `the prescribing or providing was at their request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the prescribing or providing at their request?
      `it was so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241.1, is what I did medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 241.1 medical assistance in dying` ((IF `s 241.1 medical practitioner` `I am entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `s 241.1 nurse practitioner` `I am a registered nurse` `I am entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner` `I am entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients`) EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `I administered a substance to a person`) `the administering was at their request` `the substance caused their death` ((IF `s 241.1 medical practitioner` `I am entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `s 241.1 nurse practitioner` `I am a registered nurse` `I am entitled under the laws of a province to practise as a nurse practitioner` `I am entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients`) EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `I prescribed or provided a substance to a person`) `the prescribing or providing was at their request` `it was so that they could self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death`

@export Under section 241.2(1), does the person who has asked me for medical assistance in dying meet all of the criteria?
GIVEN `the person is eligible for health services funded by a government in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person eligible, or but for any minimum period of residence or waiting period would they be eligible, for health services funded by a government in Canada?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years?
      `the person is capable of making decisions with respect to their health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person capable of making decisions with respect to their health?
      `the person has a serious and incurable illness, disease or disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a serious and incurable illness, disease or disability?
      `the illness, disease or disability relied on is a mental illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the illness, disease or disability relied on a mental illness?
      `the person is in an advanced state of irreversible decline in capability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person in an advanced state of irreversible decline in capability?
      `the person has enduring suffering that is intolerable and cannot be relieved acceptably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the illness, disease, disability or decline cause the person enduring physical or psychological suffering that is intolerable to them and that cannot be relieved under conditions that they consider acceptable?
      `the person made a voluntary request not made as a result of external pressure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person make a voluntary request for medical assistance in dying that was not made as a result of external pressure?
      `the person gave informed consent after being told the means available to relieve suffering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person give informed consent to receive medical assistance in dying after having been informed of the means available to relieve their suffering, including palliative care?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241.2(1), does the person who has asked me for medical assistance in dying meet all of the criteria` MEANS
    `s 241.2(1) the person meets all of the criteria` `the person is eligible for health services funded by a government in Canada` `the person's age in years` `the person is capable of making decisions with respect to their health` (`s 241.2(2) the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition` `the person has a serious and incurable illness, disease or disability` (`s 241.2(2.1) a mental illness is not considered to be an illness, disease or disability` `the illness, disease or disability relied on is a mental illness`) `the person is in an advanced state of irreversible decline in capability` `the person has enduring suffering that is intolerable and cannot be relieved acceptably`) `the person made a voluntary request not made as a result of external pressure` `the person gave informed consent after being told the means available to relieve suffering`

@export Under section 241.2(1), may the person receive medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `the person meets all of the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person meet all of the criteria in section 241.2(1)? (See the question above.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241.2(1), may the person receive medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 241.2(1) the person may receive medical assistance in dying` (JUST `the person meets all of the criteria`)

-- What a practitioner must do before and when providing medical assistance in dying (section 241.2): the safeguards that decide whether the practitioner has committed the offence of section 241.3.
@export Under section 241.2(3), have I met the safeguards before providing medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable?
GIVEN `I am of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria in section 241.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in section 241.2(1)?
      `the written request was signed and dated by the person or another person on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the request made in writing and signed and dated by the person, or by another person on their behalf under section 241.2(4)?
      `it was signed and dated after the person was informed that they have a grievous and irremediable medical condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that they have a grievous and irremediable medical condition?
      `I am satisfied that the request was signed and dated before an independent witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you satisfied that the request was signed and dated before an independent witness who then also signed and dated it?
      `the person was informed that they may withdraw their request at any time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person informed that they may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request?
      `another practitioner gave a written opinion confirming the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria in section 241.2(1)?
      `I am satisfied that the other practitioner and I are independent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you satisfied that you and the other practitioner are independent?
      `the person has difficulty communicating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have difficulty communicating?
      `I took all necessary measures to give a reliable means of understanding and communicating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information given to them and communicate their decision?
      `immediately before I gave an opportunity to withdraw and ensured express consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before providing medical assistance in dying, did you give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that they gave express consent?
      `the requirement of paragraph (3)(h) is waived under section 241.2(3.2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement of paragraph (3)(h) (the final opportunity to withdraw and express consent) waived under section 241.2(3.2) (the person lost capacity after a written arrangement)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241.2(3), have I met the safeguards before providing medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable` MEANS
    `s 241.2(3) the practitioner has met the safeguards before providing medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable` (`s 241.2(3)(a) the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria` `I am of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria in section 241.2(1)`) (`s 241.2(3)(b) to (h) the requirements have been met` `the written request was signed and dated by the person or another person on their behalf` `it was signed and dated after the person was informed that they have a grievous and irremediable medical condition` `I am satisfied that the request was signed and dated before an independent witness` `the person was informed that they may withdraw their request at any time` `another practitioner gave a written opinion confirming the criteria` `I am satisfied that the other practitioner and I are independent` `the person has difficulty communicating` `I took all necessary measures to give a reliable means of understanding and communicating` `immediately before I gave an opportunity to withdraw and ensured express consent` (JUST `the requirement of paragraph (3)(h) is waived under section 241.2(3.2)`))

