      `the requirements of paragraphs 241.2(3)(b) to (h) were met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the requirements of paragraphs 241.2(3)(b) to (h) met? (The written request, the witness, the second opinion and the rest: see section 241.2(3).)
      `the requirements of paragraphs 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k) were met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the requirements of paragraphs 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k) met? (Where natural death is not reasonably foreseeable: see section 241.2(3.1).)
      `I informed the pharmacist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you inform the pharmacist, before any pharmacist dispensed the substance, that the substance was intended for medical assistance in dying?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
