      `I did so with intent to wound, maim or disfigure, to endanger life or to prevent an arrest or detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so with intent to wound, maim or disfigure any person, to endanger the life of any person or to prevent the arrest or detention of any person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 244.1, have I committed the offence of discharging an air gun or compressed gas gun with intent` MEANS
    `s 244.1 the person commits the offence of discharging an air or compressed gas gun or pistol with intent` `the thing discharged is an air or compressed gas gun or pistol` `I discharged it at any person` `I did so with intent to wound, maim or disfigure, to endanger life or to prevent an arrest or detention`

@export Under section 244.1, how serious is discharging an air gun or compressed gas gun with intent, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 244.1, how serious is discharging an air gun or compressed gas gun with intent, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 244.1 the class of the offence` `s 244.1 the punishment`

@export Under section 244.2(1), have I committed the offence of discharging a firearm recklessly?
GIVEN `the thing is a barrelled weapon from which a projectile can be discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a barrelled weapon from which any shot, bullet or other projectile can be discharged?
      `the thing is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person?
      `the thing is a frame or receiver of such a barrelled weapon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a frame or receiver of such a barrelled weapon?
      `the thing can be adapted for use as a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be adapted for use as a firearm?
      `I intentionally discharged it into or at a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intentionally discharge it into or at a place?
      `the place is a building or structure, or part of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a building or structure, or part of one?
      `the place is a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer?
      `I knew that, or was reckless as to whether, another person was present in the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that, or were you reckless as to whether, another person was present in the place?
      `I intentionally discharged it while reckless as to the life or safety of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intentionally discharge it while being reckless as to the life or safety of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 244.2(1), have I committed the offence of discharging a firearm recklessly` MEANS
    `s 244.2(1) the person commits the offence of discharging a firearm recklessly` (`s 2 firearm` `the thing is a barrelled weapon from which a projectile can be discharged` `the thing is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death` `the thing is a frame or receiver of such a barrelled weapon` `the thing can be adapted for use as a firearm`) (IF `I intentionally discharged it into or at a place` THEN `s 244.2(2) place` `the place is a building or structure, or part of one` `the place is a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer` ELSE JUST FALSE) `I knew that, or was reckless as to whether, another person was present in the place` `I intentionally discharged it while reckless as to the life or safety of another person`

@export Under section 244.2(3), how serious is discharging a firearm recklessly, and what can it cost me?
GIVEN `a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm was used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm used in the commission of the offence?
      `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, as section 467.1(1) defines that? (Answer yes or no; that definition is in another part of the Code.)
      `it is my first offence as the section counts earlier offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your first offence, counting earlier offences as the section says? (See the question on earlier convictions under the same section.)
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 244.2(3), how serious is discharging a firearm recklessly, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 244.2(3) the class of the offence` (`s 244.2(3) the punishment` (`s 244.2(3) the limb that applies` `a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm was used` (JUST `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`) (JUST `it is my first offence as the section counts earlier offences`)))

@export Under section 244.2(4), does an earlier conviction count as an earlier offence for my sentence for discharging a firearm recklessly?
GIVEN `the section of the Code of the earlier offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code was the earlier offence? (For example 244. Give only the number.)
      `the subsection of that section, if any` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection of that section? (For example (1); leave blank if it is the whole section.)
      `a firearm was used in the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a firearm used in the commission of the earlier offence?
      `the day I was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the earlier offence?
      `the day I was convicted of the present offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the offence for which you are now being sentenced?
      `the days I spent in custody between those two days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did you spend in custody between those two days?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 244.2(4), does an earlier conviction count as an earlier offence for my sentence for discharging a firearm recklessly` MEANS
    `s 244.2(4) the earlier conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the Code of the earlier offence`, `the subsection of that section, if any`) `a firearm was used in the earlier offence` `the day I was convicted of the earlier offence` `the day I was convicted of the present offence` `the days I spent in custody between those two days`

@export Under section 244.2(5), does the order in which I committed my offences matter to the question of an earlier offence for discharging a firearm recklessly?
GIVEN `the question is whether I have committed a second or subsequent offence for the purpose of section 244.2(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question whether you have committed a second or subsequent offence for the purpose of section 244.2(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 244.2(5), does the order in which I committed my offences matter to the question of an earlier offence for discharging a firearm recklessly` MEANS
    `s 244.2(5) the sequence of commission of offences is to be considered` `the question is whether I have committed a second or subsequent offence for the purpose of section 244.2(4)`

§ `Noxious things, overcoming resistance, traps and transportation (sections 245 to 248)`

@export Under section 245(1), have I committed the offence of administering a noxious thing?
GIVEN `I administered, or caused to be administered, or caused another person to take, poison or another destructive or noxious thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you administer, or cause to be administered to another person, or cause another person to take, poison or any other destructive or noxious thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 245(1), have I committed the offence of administering a noxious thing` MEANS
    `s 245(1) the person commits the offence of administering a noxious thing` `I administered, or caused to be administered, or caused another person to take, poison or another destructive or noxious thing`

@export Under section 245(1), how serious is administering a noxious thing, and what can it cost me?
GIVEN `which intent did I have` IS A `s 245(1) intent` @desc Did you act with intent to endanger the life of, or to cause bodily harm to, that person, or with intent to aggrieve or annoy that person?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 245(1), how serious is administering a noxious thing, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` (`s 245(1) the class of the offence` `which intent did I have`) `the limbs for the intent`
        WHERE
            `the limbs for the intent` MEANS
                CONSIDER `which intent did I have`
                    WHEN `s 245(1)(a) with intent to endanger the life of or to cause bodily harm to that person` THEN LIST `s 245(1)(a) the indictable limb`
                    WHEN `s 245(1)(b) with intent to aggrieve or annoy that person` THEN LIST `s 245(1)(b) the indictable limb`

@export Under section 245(2), does section 245(1) apply to me when I provided or helped with medical assistance in dying?
GIVEN `I am a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying? (See the question under section 241.1.)
      `I did something for the purpose of aiding a practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying?
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in accordance with section 241.2?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 245(2), does section 245(1) apply to me when I provided or helped with medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    `s 245(2) subsection 245(1) applies to the person` (JUST `I am a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying`) (JUST `I did something for the purpose of aiding a practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying`) `it is in accordance with section 241.2`

@export Under section 246, have I committed the offence of overcoming resistance to the commission of an offence?
GIVEN `I acted with intent to enable or assist myself or another person to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to enable or assist yourself or another person to commit an indictable offence?
      `I attempted to choke, suffocate or strangle another person, or to render them insensible, unconscious or incapable of resistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you attempt, by any means, to choke, suffocate or strangle another person, or by any means calculated to choke, suffocate or strangle attempt to render another person insensible, unconscious or incapable of resistance?
      `I administered, or attempted to administer, a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you administer, or cause to be administered, or attempt to administer or cause to be taken, a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 246, have I committed the offence of overcoming resistance to the commission of an offence` MEANS
    `s 246 the person commits the offence of overcoming resistance to commission of an offence` `I acted with intent to enable or assist myself or another person to commit an indictable offence` `I attempted to choke, suffocate or strangle another person, or to render them insensible, unconscious or incapable of resistance` `I administered, or attempted to administer, a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing`

@export Under section 246, how serious is overcoming resistance to the commission of an offence, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 246, how serious is overcoming resistance to the commission of an offence, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 246 the class of the offence` `s 246 the punishment`

@export Under section 247(1), have I committed the offence of setting a trap that is likely to cause death or bodily harm?
GIVEN `I acted with intent to cause death or bodily harm to a person, whether ascertained or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to cause death or bodily harm to a person, whether ascertained or not?
      `I set or placed a trap, device or other thing likely to cause death or bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you set or place a trap, device or other thing that is likely to cause death or bodily harm to a person?
      `I knowingly allowed such a trap, device or thing to remain in a place I occupy or possess` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Being in occupation or possession of a place, did you knowingly permit such a trap, device or other thing to remain in that place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 247(1), have I committed the offence of setting a trap that is likely to cause death or bodily harm` MEANS
    `s 247(1) the person commits the offence of setting a trap likely to cause bodily harm` `I acted with intent to cause death or bodily harm to a person, whether ascertained or not` `I set or placed a trap, device or other thing likely to cause death or bodily harm` `I knowingly allowed such a trap, device or thing to remain in a place I occupy or possess`

@export Under section 247(1), how serious is setting a trap likely to cause death or bodily harm, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 247(1), how serious is setting a trap likely to cause death or bodily harm, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 247(1) the class of the offence` (LIST `s 247(1) the indictable limb`)

@export Under section 247(2), have I committed the offence of setting a trap and causing bodily harm?
GIVEN `I committed the offence in section 247(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit the offence of setting a trap in section 247(1)? (See the question under section 247(1).)
      `the bodily harm was caused by doing so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the harm caused by doing so?
      `there was a hurt or injury to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a hurt or injury to a person?
      `the hurt or injury interferes with the person's health or comfort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the hurt or injury interfere with the person's health or comfort?
      `the hurt or injury is more than merely transient or trifling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hurt or injury more than merely transient or trifling in nature?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 247(2), have I committed the offence of setting a trap and causing bodily harm` MEANS
    `s 247(2) the person commits the offence of setting a trap and causing bodily harm` (JUST `I committed the offence in section 247(1)`) (IF `the bodily harm was caused by doing so` THEN (`s 2 bodily harm` `there was a hurt or injury to a person` `the hurt or injury interferes with the person's health or comfort` `the hurt or injury is more than merely transient or trifling`) ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 247(2), how serious is setting a trap and causing bodily harm, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 247(2), how serious is setting a trap and causing bodily harm, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 247(2) the class of the offence` (LIST `s 247(2)(a) the indictable limb`)

@export Under section 247(3), have I committed the offence of setting a trap in a place kept or used for committing an indictable offence?
GIVEN `I committed the offence in section 247(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit the offence of setting a trap in section 247(1)? (See the question under section 247(1).)
      `it was in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 247(3), have I committed the offence of setting a trap in a place kept or used for committing an indictable offence` MEANS
    `s 247(3) the person commits the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place` (JUST `I committed the offence in section 247(1)`) `it was in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence`

@export Under section 247(3), how serious is setting a trap in a place kept for committing an indictable offence, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 247(3), how serious is setting a trap in a place kept for committing an indictable offence, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 247(3) the class of the offence` (LIST `s 247(3)(a) the indictable limb`)

@export Under section 247(4), have I committed the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place and thereby causing bodily harm?
GIVEN `I committed the offence in section 247(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit the offence of setting a trap in section 247(1)? (See the question under section 247(1).)
      `it was in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence?
      `I thereby caused bodily harm to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you thereby cause hurt or injury to a person?
      `there was a hurt or injury to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a hurt or injury to a person?
      `the hurt or injury interferes with the person's health or comfort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the hurt or injury interfere with the person's health or comfort?
      `the hurt or injury is more than merely transient or trifling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hurt or injury more than merely transient or trifling in nature?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 247(4), have I committed the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place and thereby causing bodily harm` MEANS
    `s 247(4) the person commits the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place and causing bodily harm` (JUST `I committed the offence in section 247(1)`) `it was in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence` (IF `I thereby caused bodily harm to a person` THEN (`s 2 bodily harm` `there was a hurt or injury to a person` `the hurt or injury interferes with the person's health or comfort` `the hurt or injury is more than merely transient or trifling`) ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 247(4), how serious is setting a trap in an offence-related place and thereby causing bodily harm, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 247(4), how serious is setting a trap in an offence-related place and thereby causing bodily harm, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 247(4) the class of the offence` `s 247(4) the punishment`

@export Under section 247(5), have I committed the offence of setting a trap and thereby causing death?
GIVEN `I committed the offence in section 247(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit the offence of setting a trap in section 247(1)? (See the question under section 247(1).)
      `I thereby caused the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you thereby cause the death of any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 247(5), have I committed the offence of setting a trap and thereby causing death` MEANS
    `s 247(5) the person commits the offence of setting a trap and causing death` (JUST `I committed the offence in section 247(1)`) `I thereby caused the death of another person`

@export Under section 247(5), how serious is setting a trap and thereby causing death, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 247(5), how serious is setting a trap and thereby causing death, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 247(5) the class of the offence` `s 247(5) the punishment`

@export Under section 248, have I committed the offence of interfering with transportation facilities?
GIVEN `I acted with intent to endanger the safety of any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to endanger the safety of any person?
      `I placed anything on, or did anything to, property used for transporting persons or goods by land, water or air` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you place anything on, or do anything to, any property that is used for or in connection with the transportation of persons or goods by land, water or air?
      `that is likely to cause death or bodily harm to persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you did likely to cause death or bodily harm to persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 248, have I committed the offence of interfering with transportation facilities` MEANS
    `s 248 the person commits the offence of interfering with transportation facilities` `I acted with intent to endanger the safety of any person` `I placed anything on, or did anything to, property used for transporting persons or goods by land, water or air` `that is likely to cause death or bodily harm to persons`

@export Under section 248, how serious is interfering with transportation facilities, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 248, how serious is interfering with transportation facilities, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 248 the class of the offence` `s 248 the punishment`

§ `Impeding rescue, and the duty to guard openings and excavations (sections 262 and 263)`

@export Under section 262, have I committed the offence of impeding an attempt to save a life?
GIVEN `I prevented or impeded, or tried to prevent or impede, a person attempting to save their own life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you prevent or impede, or attempt to prevent or impede, a person who was attempting to save their own life?
      `I, without reasonable cause, prevented or impeded, or tried to prevent or impede, a person attempting to save another person's life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Without reasonable cause, did you prevent or impede, or attempt to prevent or impede, a person who was attempting to save the life of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 262, have I committed the offence of impeding an attempt to save a life` MEANS
    `s 262 the person commits the offence of impeding an attempt to save life` `I prevented or impeded, or tried to prevent or impede, a person attempting to save their own life` `I, without reasonable cause, prevented or impeded, or tried to prevent or impede, a person attempting to save another person's life`

@export Under section 262, how serious is impeding an attempt to save a life, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 262, how serious is impeding an attempt to save a life, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 262 the class of the offence` (LIST `s 262 the indictable limb`)

@export Under section 263(1), am I under a legal duty to guard an opening I made in ice?
GIVEN `I made, or caused to be made, an opening in ice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make, or cause to be made, an opening in ice?
      `the ice is open to or frequented by the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ice open to or frequented by the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 263(1), am I under a legal duty to guard an opening I made in ice` MEANS
    `s 263(1) the person is under a legal duty to guard the opening in ice` `I made, or caused to be made, an opening in ice` `the ice is open to or frequented by the public`

@export Under section 263(2), am I under a legal duty to guard an excavation I left on land?
GIVEN `I left an excavation on land that I own or have charge or supervision of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave an excavation on land that you own or of which you have charge or supervision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 263(2), am I under a legal duty to guard an excavation I left on land` MEANS
    `s 263(2) the person is under a legal duty to guard the excavation on land` `I left an excavation on land that I own or have charge or supervision of`

@export Under section 263(3), what offence have I committed by failing to guard an opening in ice or an excavation?
GIVEN `I made an opening in ice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make, or cause to be made, an opening in ice?
      `the ice is open to or frequented by the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ice open to or frequented by the public?
      `I left an excavation on land that I own or have charge or supervision of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave an excavation on land that you own or of which you have charge or supervision?
      `I failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to perform the duty to guard it?
      `the death of a person resulted from the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the death of any person result from the failure?
      `bodily harm to a person resulted from the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did bodily harm to any person result from the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 263(3) offence`
`Under section 263(3), what offence have I committed by failing to guard an opening in ice or an excavation` MEANS
    `s 263(3) the offence the person commits` (IF `s 263(1) the person is under a legal duty to guard the opening in ice` `I made an opening in ice` `the ice is open to or frequented by the public` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `s 263(2) the person is under a legal duty to guard the excavation on land` `I left an excavation on land that I own or have charge or supervision of`) `I failed to perform the duty` `the death of a person resulted from the failure` `bodily harm to a person resulted from the failure`

@export Under section 263(3), how serious is the offence of failing to guard an opening or excavation, and what can it cost me?
GIVEN `which offence is it` IS A `s 263(3) offence` @desc Which offence is it: manslaughter, an offence under section 269, or an offence punishable on summary conviction? (See the question under section 263(3).)
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is manslaughter, was a firearm used in its commission?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 263(3), how serious is the offence of failing to guard an opening or excavation, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` (`s 263(3) the class of the offence` `which offence is it`) `the limbs for the offence`
        WHERE
            `the limbs for the offence` MEANS
                CONSIDER `which offence is it`
                    WHEN `s 263(3)(a) manslaughter` THEN `s 236(1) the punishment` `a firearm was used in the commission of the manslaughter`
                    WHEN `s 263(3)(b) an offence under section 269` THEN LIST `s 269(a) the indictable limb`
                    WHEN `s 263(3)(c) an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN EMPTY

§ `Violence against an intimate partner (section 263.1)`

@export Under section 263.1(1), have I committed the offence of violence against an intimate partner?
GIVEN `I committed an offence in which violence was used, threatened or attempted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit an offence in which violence was used, threatened or attempted? (Violence as section 3.01 describes it: that is in another part of the Code.)
      `the violence was against my intimate partner` IS A `s 2 intimate partner relationship` @desc What was the person against whom the violence was used, threatened or attempted to you? (Choose the one that fits; "intimate partner" includes a current or former spouse, common-law partner or dating partner.)
      `the violence is as section 3.01 describes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the violence of the kind that section 3.01 describes (the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 263.1(1), have I committed the offence of violence against an intimate partner` MEANS
    `s 263.1(1) the person commits the offence of violence against an intimate partner` `I committed an offence in which violence was used, threatened or attempted` (JUST `the violence is as section 3.01 describes`) (`s 2 intimate partner` `the violence was against my intimate partner`)

@export Under section 263.1(3), what is the longest term of imprisonment I am liable to on indictment for violence against an intimate partner?
GIVEN `the maximum penalty of the included offence is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence you committed one for which the maximum penalty is imprisonment for life?
      `the maximum term of the included offence, whole years` IS A NUMBER @desc If not for life, what is the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence you committed? Give the whole years (for example 5).
      `the maximum term of the included offence, further months` IS A NUMBER @desc And the further months, if any (for example 0).
      `the maximum term of the included offence is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the maximum "less a day" (for example "two years less a day")?
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`Under section 263.1(3), what is the longest term of imprisonment I am liable to on indictment for violence against an intimate partner` MEANS
    `s 263.1(3) the term of imprisonment of which the person is liable` (IF `the maximum penalty of the included offence is imprisonment for life` THEN `imprisonment for life` ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF `the maximum term of the included offence, whole years`, `the maximum term of the included offence, further months`, 0, `the maximum term of the included offence is less a day`))

@export Under section 263.1(2), may proceedings against me for violence against an intimate partner be commenced the way they were?
GIVEN `the mode in which proceedings were commenced` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc How were the proceedings commenced: by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the offence you committed be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings?
      `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the offence you committed be prosecuted only by way of indictment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 263.1(2), may proceedings against me for violence against an intimate partner be commenced the way they were` MEANS
    `s 263.1(2) proceedings under subsection (1) may be commenced in that mode` `the mode in which proceedings were commenced` `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings` `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of indictment`

@export Under section 263.1(4), do the other provisions that would apply to the offence I committed apply to my offence under section 263.1(1)?
