§ `Criminal harassment and threats (sections 264 and 264.1)`

@export Under section 264(1), have I committed the offence of criminal harassment?
GIVEN `I repeatedly followed the other person, or anyone known to them, from place to place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repeatedly follow the other person, or anyone known to them, from place to place?
      `I monitored the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or anyone known to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you monitor the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or of anyone known to them?
      `I repeatedly communicated with the other person or anyone known to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repeatedly communicate with, directly or indirectly, the other person or anyone known to them?
      `I beset or watched the dwelling-house or place where the other person or anyone known to them resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you beset or watch the dwelling-house, or place where the other person, or anyone known to them, resides, works, carries on business or happens to be?
      `I engaged in threatening conduct directed at the other person or anyone or any animal known to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you engage in threatening conduct directed at the other person, or at anyone or any animal known to them?
      `I acted with intent to harass another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with intent to harass another person?
      `I knew that I would be harassing another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that you would be harassing another person?
      `I was reckless as to whether I would be harassing another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you reckless as to whether you would be harassing another person?
      `I did so without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so without lawful authority?
      `the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the other person to believe that their safety, or that of anyone known to them, is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In all the circumstances, could the conduct reasonably be expected to cause the other person to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 264(1), have I committed the offence of criminal harassment` MEANS
    `s 264(1) the person commits the offence of criminal harassment` `I acted with intent to harass another person` `I knew that I would be harassing another person` `I was reckless as to whether I would be harassing another person` (`s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` `I repeatedly followed the other person, or anyone known to them, from place to place` `I monitored the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or anyone known to them` `I repeatedly communicated with the other person or anyone known to them` `I beset or watched the dwelling-house or place where the other person or anyone known to them resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` `I engaged in threatening conduct directed at the other person or anyone or any animal known to them`) `I did so without lawful authority` `the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the other person to believe that their safety, or that of anyone known to them, is threatened`

@export Under section 264(2), is what I did the prohibited conduct of criminal harassment?
GIVEN `I repeatedly followed the other person, or anyone known to them, from place to place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repeatedly follow the other person, or anyone known to them, from place to place?
      `I monitored the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or anyone known to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you monitor the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or of anyone known to them?
      `I repeatedly communicated with the other person or anyone known to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repeatedly communicate with, directly or indirectly, the other person or anyone known to them?
      `I beset or watched the dwelling-house or place where the other person or anyone known to them resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you beset or watch the dwelling-house, or place where the other person, or anyone known to them, resides, works, carries on business or happens to be?
      `I engaged in threatening conduct directed at the other person or anyone or any animal known to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you engage in threatening conduct directed at the other person, or at anyone or any animal known to them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 264(2), is what I did the prohibited conduct of criminal harassment` MEANS
    (`s 264(2) the conduct is the prohibited conduct mentioned in subsection (1)` `I repeatedly followed the other person, or anyone known to them, from place to place` `I monitored the location, movements, actions or social interactions of the other person or anyone known to them` `I repeatedly communicated with the other person or anyone known to them` `I beset or watched the dwelling-house or place where the other person or anyone known to them resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` `I engaged in threatening conduct directed at the other person or anyone or any animal known to them`)

