@export Under section 264(4), must the court treat my breach of an order or undertaking as an aggravating factor when it sentences me for criminal harassment?
GIVEN `I am convicted of an offence under section 264` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence under section 264?
      `I contravened an order under section 161 or a recognizance under section 810, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When you committed the offence, were you contravening the terms or conditions of an order made under section 161 or a recognizance entered into under section 810, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2?
      `I contravened another similar order, recognizance or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When you committed the offence, were you contravening the terms or conditions of any other order, recognizance or undertaking, made under the common law, the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature, that is similar in effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 264(4), must the court treat my breach of an order or undertaking as an aggravating factor when it sentences me for criminal harassment` MEANS
    `s 264(4) the court shall consider the contravention as an aggravating factor` `I am convicted of an offence under section 264` `I contravened an order under section 161 or a recognizance under section 810, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2` `I contravened another similar order, recognizance or undertaking`

@export Under section 264(5), must the court give reasons if it decides not to give effect to that aggravating factor?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the aggravating factor exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied of the existence of the aggravating factor in section 264(4)?
      `the court decides not to give effect to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court decide not to give effect to it for sentencing purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 264(5), must the court give reasons if it decides not to give effect to that aggravating factor` MEANS
    `s 264(5) the court shall give reasons for its decision` `the court is satisfied that the aggravating factor exists` `the court decides not to give effect to it`

