GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 264(6), does a person's safety include their psychological safety` MEANS
    `s 264(6) a person's safety includes their psychological safety` `the safety in question is the person's psychological safety`

@export Under section 264.1(1), have I committed the offence of uttering threats?
GIVEN `which threat did I make` IS A `s 264.1(1) threat` @desc Which kind of threat did you make: to cause death or bodily harm to any person, to burn, destroy or damage property, or to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is someone's property?
      `I knowingly uttered, conveyed or caused a person to receive the threat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, in any manner, knowingly utter, convey or cause any person to receive the threat?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 264.1(1), have I committed the offence of uttering threats` MEANS
    `s 264.1(1) the person commits the offence of uttering threats` `which threat did I make` `I knowingly uttered, conveyed or caused a person to receive the threat`

@export Under section 264.1(1), how serious is uttering threats, and what can it cost me?
GIVEN `which threat did I make` IS A `s 264.1(1) threat` @desc Which kind of threat did you make?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 264.1(1), how serious is uttering threats, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 264.1 the class of the offence` `the limbs for the threat`
        WHERE
            `the limbs for the threat` MEANS
                CONSIDER `which threat did I make`
                    WHEN `s 264.1(1)(a) a threat to cause death or bodily harm to any person` THEN LIST `s 264.1(2)(a) the indictable limb`
                    WHEN `s 264.1(1)(b) a threat to burn, destroy or damage real or personal property` THEN LIST `s 264.1(3)(a) the indictable limb`
                    WHEN `s 264.1(1)(c) a threat to kill, poison or injure an animal or bird that is the property of any person` THEN LIST `s 264.1(3)(a) the indictable limb`

