      `it was to intimidate or coerce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for a purpose including intimidating or coercing the person or a third person?
      `it was for a reason based on discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for any reason based on discrimination of any kind?
      `it arose only from lawful sanctions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act or omission arise only from, or was it inherent in or incidental to, lawful sanctions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 269.1(1), have I committed the offence of torture` MEANS
    `s 269.1(1) the person commits the offence of torture` (`s 269.1(2) official` (`s 2 peace officer` `the capacity in which I act as a peace officer`) (`s 2 public officer` `the capacity in which I act as a public officer`) (`s 2 Canadian Forces` `I am a member of the armed forces raised by Canada`) `I may exercise powers under a foreign state's law that would in Canada be exercised by such a person`) `I acted at the instigation of, or with the consent or acquiescence of, an official` (`s 269.1(2) torture` `severe pain or suffering was intentionally inflicted on a person` `it was to obtain information or a statement` `it was to punish for an act committed or suspected` `it was to intimidate or coerce` `it was for a reason based on discrimination` `it arose only from lawful sanctions`)

@export Under section 269.1(1), how serious is torture, and what can it cost me?
GIVETH A `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty`
`Under section 269.1(1), how serious is torture, and what can it cost me` MEANS
    `Under sections 197 to 269.1, the gravity and the penalty of an offence` `s 269.1(1) the class of the offence` `s 269.1(1) the punishment`

@export Under section 269.1(3), is it a defence to torture that I was ordered to do it or that there were exceptional circumstances?
GIVEN `I was ordered by a superior or a public authority to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you ordered by a superior or a public authority to perform the act or omission?
      `it is alleged to have been justified by exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it alleged to have been justified by exceptional circumstances, including a state of war, a threat of war, internal political instability or any other public emergency?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 269.1(3), is it a defence to torture that I was ordered to do it or that there were exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    `s 269.1(3) the circumstance is a defence to a charge under this section` `I was ordered by a superior or a public authority to do it` `it is alleged to have been justified by exceptional circumstances`

@export Under section 269.1(4), is a statement obtained by torture admissible in evidence?
GIVEN `the statement was obtained as a result of an offence under section 269.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement obtained as a result of the commission of an offence under section 269.1?
      `it is in proceedings over which Parliament has jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in proceedings over which Parliament has jurisdiction?
      `it is tendered as evidence that the statement was so obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it tendered only as evidence that the statement was so obtained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 269.1(4), is a statement obtained by torture admissible in evidence` MEANS
    `s 269.1(4) the statement is admissible in evidence` `the statement was obtained as a result of an offence under section 269.1` `it is in proceedings over which Parliament has jurisdiction` `it is tendered as evidence that the statement was so obtained`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc9 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc9-seat.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), ss 270 to 278.31 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence,
-- what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a
-- conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer asks the questions the part of the Code in lines 5032 to 5568 (ss 270 to 278.31) answers for that person: assaulting and disarming a peace officer, sexual assault,
-- consent and the belief in it, removing a child from Canada, corroboration, evidence of the complainant's sexual activity and its procedure, and records of the complainant or a witness.
-- It calls the rules of the layer-1 modules and restates none. Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person
-- would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect are built in each question's WHERE. Section 2 terms are worked out by the keel's functions where its inputs are plain
-- (`s 2 peace officer`, `s 2 public officer`, `s 2 weapon`); other borrowed answers (s 265 assault, s 2 bodily harm, s 2 firearm, s 2.1 restricted and prohibited firearm, s 467.1(1)
-- criminal organization, s 445.01(4) law enforcement officer) are asked as the fact they are and wrapped as `JUST`, never as a guess.
--
-- HOW A RESULT READS (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled): the result of a question that returns MAYBE BOOLEAN is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING.
-- NOTHING means "the text does not answer this question on these facts", never "no". A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- QUESTION NAMES say the direction the layer-1 rule answers in: a bar is asked as a bar ("is ... barred"), a permission as a permission ("may the judge ...").
--
-- THE SUMMARY-CONVICTION PENALTY. Where a section says only "an offence punishable on summary conviction", the penalty is the general penalty of section 787(1), which another part encodes. This layer
-- therefore asks for the punishment on indictment and for the class of offence, and does not state a summary penalty it does not have. The unused section 787(1) input of the layer-1 punishment
-- functions is given a fixed placeholder below.

`s 270 seat: the s 787(1) penalty is not read for an indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Assaulting and disarming a peace officer (ss 270 to 270.1)`

@export Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer (assault on an officer in the execution of duty, with intent to resist an arrest, or on a person executing process)?
GIVEN `I assaulted the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you assault the person (apply force to them intentionally, without their consent, or threaten to)?
      `the capacity of the person I assaulted, as a peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc In what capacity was the person a peace officer? (choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if they were not one)
      `the capacity of the person I assaulted, as a public officer` IS A `s 2 public officer capacity` @desc In what capacity was the person a public officer? (choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if they were not one)
      `the officer was engaged in the execution of the officer's duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the officer engaged in the execution of their duty?
      `the person I assaulted was acting in aid of such an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person you assaulted acting in aid of such an officer?
      `I meant to resist or prevent the arrest or detention of myself or another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to resist or prevent the arrest or detention of yourself or of another person?
      `that arrest or detention was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that arrest or detention lawful?
      `the person I assaulted was engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person you assaulted engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods?
      `the person I assaulted was making a lawful distress or seizure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person you assaulted making a lawful distress or seizure?
      `I meant to rescue something taken under lawful process, distress or seizure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to rescue something that had been taken under lawful process, distress or seizure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer` IS
    `s 270(1) the accused commits the offence of assaulting a peace officer` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 270(1) facts` WITH
                    `the accused assaults the person, by s 265` IS JUST `I assaulted the person`
                    `the person assaulted is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS `s 2 public officer` `the capacity of the person I assaulted, as a public officer`
                    `the person assaulted is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS `s 2 peace officer` `the capacity of the person I assaulted, as a peace officer`
                    `the officer is engaged in the execution of his duty` IS `the officer was engaged in the execution of the officer's duty`
                    `the person assaulted is acting in aid of such an officer` IS `the person I assaulted was acting in aid of such an officer`
                    `the accused intends to resist or prevent the arrest or detention of himself or another person` IS `I meant to resist or prevent the arrest or detention of myself or another person`
                    `the arrest or detention is lawful` IS `that arrest or detention was lawful`
                    `the person assaulted is engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods` IS `the person I assaulted was engaged in the lawful execution of a process against lands or goods`
                    `the person assaulted is making a lawful distress or seizure` IS `the person I assaulted was making a lawful distress or seizure`
                    `the accused intends to rescue anything taken under lawful process, distress or seizure` IS `I meant to rescue something taken under lawful process, distress or seizure`

@export Under section 270(2), what punishment can I face on indictment for assaulting a peace officer (imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years)?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 270(2), what is the most serious punishment I can face on indictment for assaulting a peace officer` IS
    `s 270(2) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` `by indictment` `s 270 seat: the s 787(1) penalty is not read for an indictable limb`

@export Under section 270(2), is assaulting a peace officer an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or either?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 270(2), is assaulting a peace officer an indictable offence, a summary conviction offence or both` IS
    `s 270(2) the class of the offence`

@export Under section 270.01(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer with a weapon (or an imitation) or causing bodily harm?
GIVEN `I committed an assault referred to in section 270` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit an assault referred to in section 270 (an assault on a peace officer within section 270(1))?
      `I carried, used or threatened to use a thing in committing the assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry, use or threaten to use a thing in committing the assault?
      `the thing was used, designed or intended for use in causing death or injury to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing used, designed or intended for use in causing death or injury to a person?
      `the thing was used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating a person?
      `the thing was a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing a firearm?
      `I carried, used or threatened to use an imitation of a weapon in committing the assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry, use or threaten to use an imitation of a weapon in committing the assault?
      `I caused the complainant bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the complainant bodily harm (any hurt or injury that interferes with their health or comfort and is more than merely transient or trifling)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270.01(1), do I commit the offence of assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` IS
    `s 270.01(1) the accused commits the offence of assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 270.01(1) facts` WITH
                    `the accused commits an assault referred to in section 270` IS JUST `I committed an assault referred to in section 270`
                    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon, by s 2 weapon` IS IF `I carried, used or threatened to use a thing in committing the assault` THEN `s 2 weapon` `the thing was used, designed or intended for use in causing death or injury to a person` `the thing was used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating a person` (JUST `the thing was a firearm`) FALSE FALSE ELSE JUST FALSE
                    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use an imitation of a weapon` IS `I carried, used or threatened to use an imitation of a weapon in committing the assault`
                    `the accused causes bodily harm to the complainant, by s 2 bodily harm` IS JUST `I caused the complainant bodily harm`

@export Under section 270.01(2), what punishment can I face on indictment for assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm (imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years)?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 270.01(2), what is the most serious punishment I can face on indictment for assaulting a peace officer with a weapon or causing bodily harm` IS
    `s 270.01(2) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` `by indictment` `s 270 seat: the s 787(1) penalty is not read for an indictable limb`

@export Under section 270.02, do I commit aggravated assault of a peace officer (wounding, maiming, disfiguring or endangering the life of the complainant in committing an assault referred to in section 270)?
GIVEN `I committed an assault referred to in section 270` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit an assault referred to in section 270?
      `I wounded the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you wound the complainant?
      `I maimed the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you maim the complainant?
      `I disfigured the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disfigure the complainant?
      `I endangered the life of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you endanger the life of the complainant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270.02, do I commit aggravated assault of a peace officer` IS
    `s 270.02 the accused, in committing the assault, wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 270.02 facts` WITH
                    `the accused commits an assault referred to in section 270` IS JUST `I committed an assault referred to in section 270`
                    `the accused wounds the complainant` IS `I wounded the complainant`
                    `the accused maims the complainant` IS `I maimed the complainant`
                    `the accused disfigures the complainant` IS `I disfigured the complainant`
                    `the accused endangers the life of the complainant` IS `I endangered the life of the complainant`

@export Under section 270.02, what punishment can I face for aggravated assault of a peace officer (an indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years)?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 270.02, what punishment can I face for aggravated assault of a peace officer` IS
    `s 270.02 the punishment`

@export Under section 270.03, must my sentence for assaulting a peace officer (or with a weapon or causing bodily harm, or aggravated assault) committed against a law enforcement officer be served consecutively to any other punishment from the same event?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence (for example 270, 270.01, 270.02)?
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence, written as "(1)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections)?
      `the offence was committed against a law enforcement officer as defined in subsection 445.01(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed against a law enforcement officer as defined in subsection 445.01(4) (a peace officer or other person named there)?
      `another punishment is imposed on me for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another punishment imposed on you for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270.03, must my sentence be served consecutively to any other punishment` IS
    `s 270.03 the sentence shall be served consecutively to any other punishment` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`) (JUST `the offence was committed against a law enforcement officer as defined in subsection 445.01(4)`) `another punishment is imposed on me for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events`

@export Under section 270.1(1), do I commit the offence of disarming a peace officer (taking or trying to take a weapon from a peace officer on duty without their consent)?
GIVEN `I took or tried to take a weapon from the peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take, or try to take, a weapon from the peace officer?
      `the thing was designed to be used to cause injury or death to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing designed to be used to cause injury or death to a person?
      `the thing was designed to be used to temporarily incapacitate a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing designed to be used to temporarily incapacitate a person?
      `the weapon was in the possession of the peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the weapon in the possession of the peace officer?
      `the capacity of the person as a peace officer` IS A `s 2 peace officer capacity` @desc In what capacity was the person a peace officer? (choose "a person in a capacity that is none of those" if they were not one)
      `the peace officer consented to my taking it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer consent to your taking it?
      `the peace officer was engaged in the execution of their duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the peace officer engaged in the execution of their duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 270.1(1), do I commit the offence of disarming a peace officer` IS
    `s 270.1(1) the accused commits the offence of disarming a peace officer` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 270.1(1) facts` WITH
                    `the accused takes or attempts to take a weapon` IS `I took or tried to take a weapon from the peace officer`
                    `the thing is a weapon, by s 270.1(2)` IS `s 270.1(2) the thing is a weapon for the purpose of subsection (1)` `the thing was designed to be used to cause injury or death to a person` `the thing was designed to be used to temporarily incapacitate a person`
                    `the weapon is in the possession of a peace officer` IS `the weapon was in the possession of the peace officer`
                    `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS `s 2 peace officer` `the capacity of the person as a peace officer`
                    `the peace officer consents to the taking` IS `the peace officer consented to my taking it`
                    `the peace officer is engaged in the execution of his or her duty` IS `the peace officer was engaged in the execution of their duty`

@export Under section 270.1(3), what punishment can I face on indictment for disarming a peace officer (imprisonment for a term of not more than five years)?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 270.1(3), what is the most serious punishment I can face on indictment for disarming a peace officer` IS
    `s 270.1(3) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` `by indictment` `s 270 seat: the s 787(1) penalty is not read for an indictable limb`

§ `Sexual assault, consent and removal of a child from Canada (ss 271 to 273.3)`

@export Under section 271, am I guilty of the offence of sexual assault?
GIVEN `I committed a sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit a sexual assault (an assault, as section 265 describes it, of a sexual nature)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 271, am I guilty of the offence of sexual assault` IS
    `s 271 the accused is guilty of the offence of sexual assault` (JUST `I committed a sexual assault`)

@export Under section 271, what punishment can I face for sexual assault, on indictment or on summary conviction, depending on whether the complainant is under 16?
GIVEN `how I am convicted` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Are you convicted by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the complainant's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old was the complainant, in years, at the time (for example 15 or 15.5)?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 271, what punishment can I face for sexual assault` IS
    `s 271 the punishment on the mode of proceeding` `how I am convicted` `the complainant's age in years`

@export Under section 272(1), do I commit the offence of sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party, causing bodily harm, choking, or being a party to the offence with another person?
GIVEN `I committed a sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit a sexual assault?
      `I carried, used or threatened to use a thing in committing the sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry, use or threaten to use a thing in committing the sexual assault?
      `the thing was used, designed or intended for use in causing death or injury to a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing used, designed or intended for use in causing death or injury to a person?
      `the thing was used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating a person?
      `the thing was a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing a firearm?
      `I carried, used or threatened to use an imitation of a weapon in committing the sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you carry, use or threaten to use an imitation of a weapon in committing the sexual assault?
      `I threatened to cause bodily harm to a person other than the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you threaten to cause bodily harm to a person other than the complainant?
      `I caused the complainant bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the complainant bodily harm?
      `I choked, suffocated or strangled the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you choke, suffocate or strangle the complainant?
      `I was a party to the offence with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a party to the offence with any other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(1), do I commit the offence of sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm` IS
    `s 272(1) the accused commits the offence of sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 272(1) facts` WITH
                    `the accused commits a sexual assault` IS JUST `I committed a sexual assault`
                    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use a weapon, by s 2 weapon` IS IF `I carried, used or threatened to use a thing in committing the sexual assault` THEN `s 2 weapon` `the thing was used, designed or intended for use in causing death or injury to a person` `the thing was used or intended for use for the purpose of threatening or intimidating a person` (JUST `the thing was a firearm`) FALSE FALSE ELSE JUST FALSE
                    `the accused carries, uses or threatens to use an imitation of a weapon` IS `I carried, used or threatened to use an imitation of a weapon in committing the sexual assault`
                    `the accused threatens to cause bodily harm to a person other than the complainant` IS `I threatened to cause bodily harm to a person other than the complainant`
                    `the accused causes bodily harm to the complainant, by s 2 bodily harm` IS JUST `I caused the complainant bodily harm`
                    `the accused chokes, suffocates or strangles the complainant` IS `I choked, suffocated or strangled the complainant`
                    `the accused is a party to the offence with any other person` IS `I was a party to the offence with another person`

@export Under section 272(2), what punishment can I face (a restricted or prohibited firearm, or any firearm for a criminal organization; another firearm; a complainant under 16; any other case)? The answer is NOTHING where two of the limbs overlap.
GIVEN `a restricted firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a restricted firearm used in committing the offence?
      `a prohibited firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a prohibited firearm used in committing the offence?
      `a firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any firearm used in committing the offence?
      `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization?
      `this is a second or subsequent offence within subsection 272(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence within subsection 272(3) (see the question about subsection 272(3))?
      `the complainant's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old was the complainant, in years, at the time?
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 272(2), what punishment can I face for sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm` IS
    `s 272(2) the punishment` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 272(2) facts` WITH
                    `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm` IS JUST `a restricted firearm was used in the offence`
                    `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm` IS JUST `a prohibited firearm was used in the offence`
                    `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm` IS JUST `a firearm was used in the offence`
                    `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS JUST `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`
                    `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by subsection (3)` IS JUST `this is a second or subsequent offence within subsection 272(3)`
                    `the complainant's age in years` IS `the complainant's age in years`

@export Under section 272(2), which limbs of the punishment apply to the offence (the answer lists each limb that applies; two can apply together)?
GIVEN `a restricted firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a restricted firearm used in committing the offence?
      `a prohibited firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a prohibited firearm used in committing the offence?
      `a firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any firearm used in committing the offence?
      `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization?
      `this is a second or subsequent offence within subsection 272(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence within subsection 272(3)?
      `the complainant's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old was the complainant, in years, at the time?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 272(2) limb`)
DECIDE `Under section 272(2), which limbs of the punishment apply to me` IS
    `s 272(2) the limbs that apply` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 272(2) facts` WITH
                    `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm` IS JUST `a restricted firearm was used in the offence`
                    `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm` IS JUST `a prohibited firearm was used in the offence`
                    `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm` IS JUST `a firearm was used in the offence`
                    `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS JUST `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`
                    `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by subsection (3)` IS JUST `this is a second or subsequent offence within subsection 272(3)`
                    `the complainant's age in years` IS `the complainant's age in years`

@export Under section 272(3) (with 272(4)), does my earlier conviction count as an earlier offence, so that the present one is a second or subsequent offence?
GIVEN `the section number of my earlier offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were earlier convicted of (for example 85, 244, 272)?
      `the subsection of my earlier offence` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of that offence, written as "(1)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections)?
      `a firearm was used in committing my earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a firearm used in committing the earlier offence?
      `the day I was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the earlier offence (year-month-day)?
      `the day I am convicted of the present offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed (year-month-day)?
      `the days I spent in custody since the earlier conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have you spent in custody since the earlier conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 272(3), does my earlier conviction count as an earlier offence` IS
    `s 272(3) the earlier conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` `the earlier conviction` `the day I am convicted of the present offence`
    WHERE
        `the earlier conviction` MEANS `s 272(3) earlier conviction` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of my earlier offence`, `the subsection of my earlier offence`), `a firearm was used in committing my earlier offence`, `the day I was convicted of the earlier offence`, `the days I spent in custody since the earlier conviction`

@export Under section 273(1), do I commit aggravated sexual assault (wounding, maiming, disfiguring or endangering the life of the complainant in committing a sexual assault)?
GIVEN `I committed a sexual assault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit a sexual assault?
      `I wounded the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you wound the complainant?
      `I maimed the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you maim the complainant?
      `I disfigured the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disfigure the complainant?
      `I endangered the life of the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you endanger the life of the complainant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273(1), do I commit aggravated sexual assault` IS
    `s 273(1) the accused, in committing a sexual assault, wounds, maims, disfigures or endangers the life of the complainant` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 273(1) facts` WITH
                    `the accused commits a sexual assault` IS JUST `I committed a sexual assault`
                    `the accused wounds the complainant` IS `I wounded the complainant`
                    `the accused maims the complainant` IS `I maimed the complainant`
                    `the accused disfigures the complainant` IS `I disfigured the complainant`
                    `the accused endangers the life of the complainant` IS `I endangered the life of the complainant`

@export Under section 273(2), what punishment can I face for aggravated sexual assault (imprisonment for life, with the minimums the firearm and age limbs state)? The answer is NOTHING where two of the limbs overlap.
GIVEN `a restricted firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a restricted firearm used in committing the offence?
      `a prohibited firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a prohibited firearm used in committing the offence?
      `a firearm was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any firearm used in committing the offence?
      `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization?
      `this is a second or subsequent offence within subsection 273(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a second or subsequent offence within subsection 273(3) (see the question about subsection 273(3))?
      `the complainant's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old was the complainant, in years, at the time?
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 273(2), what punishment can I face for aggravated sexual assault` IS
    `s 273(2) the punishment` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 272(2) facts` WITH
                    `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 restricted firearm` IS JUST `a restricted firearm was used in the offence`
                    `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2.1 prohibited firearm` IS JUST `a prohibited firearm was used in the offence`
                    `any firearm is used in the commission of the offence, by s 2 firearm` IS JUST `a firearm was used in the offence`
                    `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS JUST `the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`
                    `the offence is a second or subsequent offence, by subsection (3)` IS JUST `this is a second or subsequent offence within subsection 273(3)`
                    `the complainant's age in years` IS `the complainant's age in years`

@export Under section 273(3) (with 273(4)), does my earlier conviction count as an earlier offence, so that the present one is a second or subsequent offence?
GIVEN `the section number of my earlier offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were earlier convicted of (for example 85, 244, 272)?
      `the subsection of my earlier offence` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of that offence, written as "(1)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections)?
      `a firearm was used in committing my earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a firearm used in committing the earlier offence?
      `the day I was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of the earlier offence (year-month-day)?
      `the day I am convicted of the present offence` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed (year-month-day)?
      `the days I spent in custody since the earlier conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have you spent in custody since the earlier conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273(3), does my earlier conviction count as an earlier offence` IS
    `s 273(3) the earlier conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` `the earlier conviction` `the day I am convicted of the present offence`
    WHERE
        `the earlier conviction` MEANS `s 272(3) earlier conviction` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of my earlier offence`, `the subsection of my earlier offence`), `a firearm was used in committing my earlier offence`, `the day I was convicted of the earlier offence`, `the days I spent in custody since the earlier conviction`

@export Under section 273.1(1.1), was there consent present at the time the sexual activity took place (voluntary agreement to the activity in question, present at that time, and not within section 273.1(2) or section 265(3))?
GIVEN `the complainant voluntarily agreed to engage in the sexual activity in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the complainant voluntarily agree to engage in the sexual activity in question?
      `the agreement was present at the time the sexual activity took place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement present at the time the sexual activity took place?
      `the agreement was expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant?
      `the complainant was unconscious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the complainant unconscious?
      `the complainant was incapable of consenting for a reason other than unconsciousness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the complainant incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than unconsciousness?
      `I induced the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you induce the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority?
      `the complainant expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the complainant express, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity?
      `the complainant, having consented, expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having consented to engage in sexual activity, did the complainant express, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue?
      `no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no consent obtained under subsection 265(3) (the complainant submits or does not resist by reason of force, threats, fear, fraud or abuse of authority)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273.1(1.1), was there consent present at the time the sexual activity took place` IS
    `s 273.1(1.1) there is consent present at the time the sexual activity takes place` (`s 273.1(1) the complainant consents, for the purposes of sections 271, 272 and 273` `the complainant voluntarily agreed to engage in the sexual activity in question` (`s 273.1(2) no consent is obtained` `the circumstances`) (JUST `no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3)`)) `the agreement was present at the time the sexual activity took place`
    WHERE
        `the circumstances` MEANS `s 273.1(2) facts` WITH
                    `the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant` IS `the agreement was expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant`
                    `the complainant is unconscious` IS `the complainant was unconscious`
                    `the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than unconsciousness` IS `the complainant was incapable of consenting for a reason other than unconsciousness`
                    `the accused induces the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority` IS `I induced the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority`
                    `the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity` IS `the complainant expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity`
                    `the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity` IS `the complainant, having consented, expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue`

@export Under section 273.1(2), is no consent obtained (the agreement was expressed by another person, the complainant was unconscious or incapable, I abused a position of trust, power or authority, or the complainant expressed a lack of agreement or withdrew it)? The list does not limit the circumstances (section 273.1(3)), so the answer is NOTHING when none applies.
GIVEN `the agreement was expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant?
      `the complainant was unconscious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the complainant unconscious?
      `the complainant was incapable of consenting for a reason other than unconsciousness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the complainant incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than unconsciousness?
      `I induced the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you induce the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority?
      `the complainant expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the complainant express, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity?
      `the complainant, having consented, expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having consented to engage in sexual activity, did the complainant express, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273.1(2), is no consent obtained` IS
    `s 273.1(2) no consent is obtained` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 273.1(2) facts` WITH
                    `the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant` IS `the agreement was expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant`
                    `the complainant is unconscious` IS `the complainant was unconscious`
                    `the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than unconsciousness` IS `the complainant was incapable of consenting for a reason other than unconsciousness`
                    `the accused induces the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority` IS `I induced the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority`
                    `the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity` IS `the complainant expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity`
                    `the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity` IS `the complainant, having consented, expressed, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue`

@export Under section 273.2, is my belief that the complainant consented barred as a defence to a charge of sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon or aggravated sexual assault?
GIVEN `the section number of the charge` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the charge (271, 272 or 273)?
      `I say I believed that the complainant consented to the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you say you believed that the complainant consented to the activity that is the subject of the charge?
      `my belief arose from my self-induced intoxication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your belief arise from your self-induced intoxication?
      `my belief arose from my recklessness or wilful blindness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your belief arise from your recklessness or wilful blindness?
      `my belief arose from a circumstance in which no consent is obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your belief arise from a circumstance in which no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3) or 273.1(2) or (3)?
      `I did not take reasonable steps to ascertain that the complainant was consenting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to you at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting?
      `there is no evidence that the complainant's agreement was affirmatively expressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no evidence that the complainant's voluntary agreement was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273.2, is my belief that the complainant consented barred as a defence` IS
    `s 273.2 the accused's belief in consent is not a defence` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 273.2 facts` WITH
                    `the charge` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the charge`, "")
                    `the accused says the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity` IS `I say I believed that the complainant consented to the activity`
                    `the belief arose from the accused's self-induced intoxication` IS `my belief arose from my self-induced intoxication`
                    `the belief arose from the accused's recklessness or wilful blindness` IS `my belief arose from my recklessness or wilful blindness`
                    `the belief arose from a circumstance in which no consent is obtained under subsection 265(3) or 273.1(2) or (3)` IS `my belief arose from a circumstance in which no consent is obtained`
                    `the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting` IS `I did not take reasonable steps to ascertain that the complainant was consenting`
                    `there is no evidence that the complainant's voluntary agreement was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct` IS `there is no evidence that the complainant's agreement was affirmatively expressed`

@export Under section 273.3(1), is what I did prohibited (the person's residence and age, the offence that the act intended abroad would be in Canada, and what I did and intended, are asked below)?
GIVEN `I did something for the purpose of removing the person from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do anything for the purpose of removing the person from Canada?
      `the person is ordinarily resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person ordinarily resident in Canada?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years?
      `I intended that an act be committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that an act be committed outside Canada?
      `the section number of the offence the act would be in Canada` IS A NUMBER @desc Against which section of the Criminal Code would that act be an offence if committed in Canada (for example 151, 153, 271, 293.1)?
      `the subsection of that offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection, written as "(3)" (leave it empty if the section has no subsections or none matters)?
      `that act, if committed in Canada, would be an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that act, if committed in Canada, be an offence in respect of that person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 273.3(1), is what I did prohibited` IS
    `s 273.3(1) the accused does something that the subsection prohibits` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 273.3(1) facts` WITH
                    `the accused does something for the purpose of removing the person from Canada` IS `I did something for the purpose of removing the person from Canada`
                    `the person is ordinarily resident in Canada` IS `the person is ordinarily resident in Canada`
                    `the person's age in years` IS `the person's age in years`
                    `the accused intends that an act be committed outside Canada` IS `I intended that an act be committed outside Canada`
                    `the act, if committed in Canada, would be an offence in respect of that person against` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence the act would be in Canada`, `the subsection of that offence`)
                    `the act, if committed in Canada, would be an offence` IS `that act, if committed in Canada, would be an offence`

@export Under section 273.3(2), what punishment can I face on indictment for contravening section 273.3 (imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years)?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 273.3(2), what is the most serious punishment I can face on indictment for removing a young person from Canada` IS
    `s 273.3(2) the punishment on the mode of proceeding` `by indictment` `s 270 seat: the s 787(1) penalty is not read for an indictable limb`

§ `Corroboration and recent complaint (ss 274, 275)`

@export Under section 274, is no corroboration required for a conviction of the offence I am charged with?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence I am charged with` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with (for example 271)?
      `the subsection of the offence I am charged with` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, written as "(2)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections or none that matters)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 274, is no corroboration required for a conviction` IS
    `s 274 no corroboration is required for a conviction` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence I am charged with`, `the subsection of the offence I am charged with`)

@export Under section 275, are the rules relating to evidence of recent complaint abrogated for the offence I am charged with?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence I am charged with` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with (for example 271)?
      `the subsection of the offence I am charged with` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, written as "(2)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections or none that matters)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 275, are the rules relating to evidence of recent complaint abrogated for my charge` IS
    `s 275 the rules relating to evidence of recent complaint are abrogated for the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence I am charged with`, `the subsection of the offence I am charged with`)

§ `Evidence of the complainant's sexual activity (ss 276 to 277)`

@export Under section 276(1), is evidence that the complainant engaged in sexual activity not admissible to support an inference that, by reason of its sexual nature, the complainant is more likely to have consented or is less worthy of belief?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence I am charged with` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with (for example 271)?
      `the subsection of the offence I am charged with` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, written as "(2)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections or none that matters)?
      `my offence is otherwise of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the sections the subsection names, is the offence one of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose?
      `the evidence is of sexual activity itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence of sexual activity itself (with the accused or with any other person)?
      `the evidence is a communication made for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence a communication made for a sexual purpose?
      `the content of the evidence is of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the content of the evidence of a sexual nature?
      `the evidence is of sexual inactivity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence of sexual inactivity?
      `the evidence is offered to support an inference that the complainant is more likely to have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence offered to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of the activity, the complainant is more likely to have consented?
      `the evidence is offered to support an inference that the complainant is less worthy of belief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence offered to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of the activity, the complainant is less worthy of belief?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 276(1), is evidence of the complainant's sexual activity not admissible to support the inference` IS
    `s 276(1) the evidence is not admissible to support the inference` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 276(1) facts` WITH
                    `the offence charged` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence I am charged with`, `the subsection of the offence I am charged with`)
                    `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose` IS `my offence is otherwise of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose`
                    `the evidence is evidence that the complainant has engaged in sexual activity, by s 276(4) and (5)` IS `the evidence of sexual activity`
                    `the evidence is adduced to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant is more likely to have consented to the sexual activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge` IS `the evidence is offered to support an inference that the complainant is more likely to have consented`
                    `the evidence is adduced to support an inference that, by reason of the sexual nature of that activity, the complainant is less worthy of belief` IS `the evidence is offered to support an inference that the complainant is less worthy of belief`
        `the evidence of sexual activity` MEANS `s 270 helper: at least one of these holds` (LIST JUST `the evidence is of sexual activity itself`, `s 276(4) the communication is sexual activity` `the evidence is a communication made for a sexual purpose` `the content of the evidence is of a sexual nature`, `s 276(5) evidence of sexual inactivity is evidence of sexual activity` `the evidence is of sexual inactivity`)

@export Under section 276(2), is evidence of the complainant's sexual activity other than that of the charge barred from being adduced, because the judge has not determined, by the procedure, that the conditions are met?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence I am charged with` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with (for example 271)?
      `the subsection of the offence I am charged with` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, written as "(2)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections or none that matters)?
      `my offence is otherwise of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the sections the subsection names, is the offence one of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose?
      `the evidence is of sexual activity other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence of sexual activity other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge?
      `who seeks to adduce the evidence` IS A `s 276(2) who seeks to adduce the evidence` @desc Who seeks to adduce the evidence: the accused (or someone on the accused's behalf), the prosecutor, or someone else?
      `the judge has made a determination in accordance with the procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge made a determination in accordance with the procedures in sections 276.01, 276.02, 276.06, 276.1, 278.3 and 278.35, as the case may be?
      `the determination is that the evidence is not adduced for the forbidden purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that the evidence is not being adduced for the purpose of supporting an inference described in subsection (1)?
      `the determination is that the evidence is relevant to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that the evidence is relevant to an issue at trial?
      `the determination is that the evidence is of specific instances of sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that the evidence is of specific instances of sexual activity?
      `the determination is that the evidence has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that the evidence has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice?
      `the determination is that the evidence has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that the evidence has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 276(2), is evidence of the complainant's other sexual activity barred from being adduced` IS
    `s 276(2) the evidence is barred from being adduced` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 276(2) facts` WITH
                    `the offence charged` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence I am charged with`, `the subsection of the offence I am charged with`)
                    `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose` IS `my offence is otherwise of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose`
                    `the evidence is of sexual activity other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge` IS `the evidence is of sexual activity other than the sexual activity that forms the subject matter of the charge`
                    `who seeks to adduce the evidence` IS `who seeks to adduce the evidence`
                    `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has made a determination in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 276.01, 276.02, 276.06, 276.1, 278.3 and 278.35, as the case may be` IS `the judge has made a determination in accordance with the procedures`
                    `the determination is that the evidence is not being adduced for the purpose of supporting an inference described in subsection (1)` IS `the determination is that the evidence is not adduced for the forbidden purpose`
                    `the determination is that the evidence is relevant to an issue at trial` IS `the determination is that the evidence is relevant to an issue at trial`
                    `the determination is that the evidence is of specific instances of sexual activity` IS `the determination is that the evidence is of specific instances of sexual activity`
                    `the determination is that the evidence has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice` IS `the determination is that the evidence has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice`
                    `the determination is that the evidence has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice` IS `the determination is that the evidence has probative value that is not outweighed by the danger of prejudice`

@export Under section 276.01(1), may an application be made by me, or on my behalf, to the judge for a hearing to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)?
GIVEN `the application is made by me or on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by you or on your behalf?
      `the application is made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice?
      `the application is for a hearing under section 276.02 to determine admissibility under subsection 276(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for a hearing under section 276.02 to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 276.01(1), may I apply for a hearing to determine whether evidence of the complainant's sexual activity is admissible` IS
    `s 276.01(1) the application may be made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice for a hearing` `the application is made by me or on my behalf` `the application is made to the judge, provincial court judge or justice` `the application is for a hearing under section 276.02 to determine admissibility under subsection 276(2)`

@export Under section 276.01(2), does my application meet the requirements of form and content (in writing, with an affidavit of detailed particulars and relevance, a copy given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk)?
GIVEN `my application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application in writing?
      `my application is accompanied by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it accompanied by an affidavit?
      `the affidavit sets out detailed particulars of the evidence I seek to adduce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit set out detailed particulars of the evidence you seek to adduce?
      `the affidavit sets out the relevance of the evidence to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit set out the relevance of that evidence to an issue at trial?
      `a copy has been given to the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the application and the affidavit been given to the prosecutor?
      `a copy has been filed with the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy been filed with the clerk of the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 276.01(2), does my application meet the requirements of form and content` IS
    `s 276.01(2) the application meets the requirements of form and content` `my application is in writing` `my application is accompanied by an affidavit` `the affidavit sets out detailed particulars of the evidence I seek to adduce` `the affidavit sets out the relevance of the evidence to an issue at trial` `a copy has been given to the prosecutor` `a copy has been filed with the clerk of the court`

@export Under section 276.01(4), must the judge grant my application and hold a hearing (if satisfied that it meets section 276.01(2), that the copy was given and filed at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval the judge allows, and that the evidence is capable of being admissible)?
GIVEN `my application meets the requirements of form and content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application meet the requirements of form and content (see the question under section 276.01(2))?
      `the day I gave the prosecutor the copy and filed it with the clerk` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the prosecutor the copy and file it with the clerk (year-month-day)?
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the hearing (year-month-day)?
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge allow a shorter interval in the interests of justice?
      `the evidence is capable of being admissible under subsection 276(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence sought to be adduced capable of being admissible under subsection 276(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 276.01(4), must the judge grant my application and hold a hearing` IS
    `s 276.01(4) the judge shall grant the application and hold a hearing under section 276.02` (JUST `my application meets the requirements of form and content`) (`s 276.01(4) the copy was given and filed at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows` `the day I gave the prosecutor the copy and filed it with the clerk` `the day of the hearing` `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`) `the evidence is capable of being admissible under subsection 276(2)`

@export Under section 276.01(5), have I caused a copy of my application to be given to the complainant by a person other than myself, as required once the judge grants the application and agrees to hold the hearing?
GIVEN `a copy of my application has been given to the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of your application been given to the complainant?
      `it was given by a person other than me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given by a person other than you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 276.01(5), have I caused a copy of my application to be given to the complainant as required` IS
    `s 276.01(5) the copy has been given to the complainant as the subsection requires` `a copy of my application has been given to the complainant` `it was given by a person other than me`

@export Under section 276.02(2), is the complainant a compellable witness at the hearing to determine whether evidence of sexual activity is admissible (they may appear and make submissions)?
GIVEN `it is a hearing to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the hearing to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 276.02(2), is the complainant a compellable witness at the hearing` IS
    `s 276.02(2) the complainant is a compellable witness at the hearing` `it is a hearing to determine whether evidence is admissible under subsection 276(2)`

@export Under section 276.03(1), is publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the contents of the application, the hearing or the determination prohibited (subject to the exceptions in subsection (1.1))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 276.03(1) matter` @desc What is it that would be published? (the contents of an application, the evidence or representations at the hearing, the judge's decision on the application, or the determination and reasons)
      `the judge has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right of privacy, ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted?
      `the determination is that the evidence is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that the evidence is admissible?
      `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made in the course of the administration of justice?
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not to make the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the disclosure not one of making the information known in the community?
      `the disclosure is made by the complainant or a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made by the complainant or a witness?
      `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure about that complainant or witness and their particulars?
      `the discloser did not reveal another protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person disclosing avoid intentionally or recklessly revealing the identity of, or particulars likely to identify, any other person whose identity is protected?
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not to make the information known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the disclosure not one of making the information known to the public?
      `the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the complainant or the witness?
