@export Under section 277, is evidence of the complainant's sexual reputation, general or specific, not admissible to challenge or support the complainant's credibility?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence I am charged with` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with (for example 271)?
      `the subsection of the offence I am charged with` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, written as "(2)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections or none that matters)?
      `the evidence is evidence of sexual reputation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence evidence of sexual reputation, whether general or specific?
      `the evidence is offered to challenge or support the complainant's credibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it offered for the purpose of challenging or supporting the credibility of the complainant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 277, is evidence of the complainant's sexual reputation not admissible` IS
    `s 277 the evidence of sexual reputation is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence I am charged with`, `the subsection of the offence I am charged with`) `the evidence is evidence of sexual reputation` `the evidence is offered to challenge or support the complainant's credibility`

§ `Spouse may be charged (s 278)`

@export Under section 278, may a husband or wife be charged with sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon or aggravated sexual assault in respect of his or her spouse, whether or not they were living together?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence I am charged with` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with (for example 271)?
      `the subsection of the offence I am charged with` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, written as "(2)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections or none that matters)?
      `the complainant is my husband or wife` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the complainant your husband or wife?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278, may I be charged with an offence under section 271, 272 or 273 in respect of my spouse` IS
    `s 278 a husband or wife may be charged with the offence in respect of his or her spouse` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence I am charged with`, `the subsection of the offence I am charged with`) `the complainant is my husband or wife`

§ `Records and therapeutic records of a complainant or witness (ss 278.1 to 278.31)`

@export Under section 278.1, is the thing a "record" (a form of record with personal information and a reasonable expectation of privacy, including medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption and social services records, journals and diaries, but not records made by those investigating or prosecuting the offence)?
GIVEN `it is a form of record that contains personal information with a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy?
      `it is a medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption or social services record, a personal journal or diary, or protected by another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption or social services record, a personal journal or diary, or a record containing personal information protected by another Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature?
      `it was made by a person responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made by a person responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.1, is the thing a record` IS
    `s 278.1 the thing is a record` `it is a form of record that contains personal information with a reasonable expectation of privacy` `it is a medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption or social services record, a personal journal or diary, or protected by another Act` `it was made by a person responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence`

@export Under section 278.1, is the thing a "therapeutic record" (produced in the course of psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling provided by a health care professional entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state)?
GIVEN `it was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling?
      `it was provided by a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the treatment, therapy or counselling provided by a health care professional?
      `the professional is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that professional entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.1, is the thing a therapeutic record` IS
    `s 278.1 the thing is a therapeutic record` `it was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling` `it was provided by a health care professional` `the professional is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide it`

@export Under section 278.11(1), is production to me of a record or therapeutic record held by a third party barred, except under the application procedure of sections 278.12 to 278.19?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence I am charged with` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with (for example 271)?
      `the subsection of the offence I am charged with` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, written as "(2)" (leave it empty for a section with no subsections or none that matters)?
      `my offence is otherwise of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the sections the subsection names, is the offence one of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose?
      `the thing is a record or a therapeutic record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a record or a therapeutic record (see the questions under section 278.1)?
      `the thing relates to a complainant or a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to a complainant or a witness?
      `the holder is the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who holds it the prosecutor?
      `the holder is me, the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who holds it you, the accused?
      `the production is in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the production in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.11(1), is production to me of a third party's record barred except in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19` IS
    `s 278.11(1) production to the accused is barred except in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19` (JUST `the thing is a record or a therapeutic record`) `the thing relates to a complainant or a witness` (`s 278.11(2) the person is a third party` `the holder is the prosecutor` `the holder is me, the accused`) (`s 278.11(1) the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the section applies` (LIST `s 278.11(1) offence in the proceedings` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence I am charged with`, `the subsection of the offence I am charged with`), `my offence is otherwise of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose`, FALSE)) `the production is in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19`

@export Under section 278.12(3), does my application for production of a third party's record meet the requirements of form and content (in writing; particulars and the holder's name; the grounds for a record or for a therapeutic record)?
GIVEN `my application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application in writing?
      `it sets out particulars identifying the record and the name of the person who has it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out particulars identifying the record or therapeutic record and the name of the person who has possession or control of it?
      `the thing I seek is a therapeutic record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you seek a therapeutic record (answer no for a record)?
      `for a record, it sets out the grounds on which the record is likely relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a record, does it set out the grounds on which you rely to establish that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify?
      `for a therapeutic record, it sets out the grounds on which it could raise a reasonable doubt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a therapeutic record, does it set out the grounds on which you rely to establish that it contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to your guilt?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.12(3), does my application for production meet the requirements of form and content` IS
    `s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` `my application is in writing` `it sets out particulars identifying the record and the name of the person who has it` `the thing I seek is a therapeutic record` `for a record, it sets out the grounds on which the record is likely relevant` `for a therapeutic record, it sets out the grounds on which it could raise a reasonable doubt`

@export Under section 278.12(4), are the assertions I rely on (for example that the record exists, relates to treatment, or may relate to credibility) not sufficient on their own to establish that a record is likely relevant or that a therapeutic record could raise a reasonable doubt?
GIVEN `I rely on the assertion (a) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record exists?
      `I rely on the assertion (b) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record relates to medical or psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling that the complainant or witness has received or is receiving?
      `I rely on the assertion (c) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record relates to the incident that is the subject matter of the proceedings?
      `I rely on the assertion (d) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record may disclose a prior inconsistent statement of the complainant or witness?
      `I rely on the assertion (e) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record may relate to the credibility of the complainant or witness?
      `I rely on the assertion (f) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record may relate to the reliability of the testimony of the complainant or witness merely because they have received or are receiving psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling?
      `I rely on the assertion (g) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record may reveal allegations of sexual abuse of the complainant by a person other than you?
      `I rely on the assertion (h) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record relates to the sexual activity of the complainant with any person, including you?
      `I rely on the assertion (i) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record relates to the presence or absence of a recent complaint?
      `I rely on the assertion (j) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record relates to the complainant's sexual reputation?
      `I rely on the assertion (k) about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on the assertion that the record was made close in time to a complaint or to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge?
      `I rely on some other assertion about the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on any other assertion not mentioned above?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.12(4), are the assertions I rely on not sufficient on their own` IS
    `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` `the assertions I rely on`
    WHERE
        `the assertions I rely on` MEANS concat (LIST (IF `I rely on the assertion (a) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(a) that the record or therapeutic record exists` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (b) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(b) that the record or therapeutic record relates to medical or psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling that the complainant or witness has received or is receiving` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (c) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(c) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the incident that is the subject matter of the proceedings` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (d) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(d) that the record or therapeutic record may disclose a prior inconsistent statement of the complainant or witness` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (e) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(e) that the record or therapeutic record may relate to the credibility of the complainant or witness` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (f) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(f) that the record or therapeutic record may relate to the reliability of the testimony of the complainant or witness merely because the complainant or witness has received or is receiving psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (g) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(g) that the record or therapeutic record may reveal allegations of sexual abuse of the complainant by a person other than the accused` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (h) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(h) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the sexual activity of the complainant with any person, including the accused` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (i) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(i) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the presence or absence of a recent complaint` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (j) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(j) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the complainant's sexual reputation` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on the assertion (k) about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4)(k) that the record or therapeutic record was made close in time to a complaint or to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I rely on some other assertion about the record` THEN LIST `s 278.12(4) any other assertion` ELSE EMPTY))

@export Under section 278.12(5), have I served my application on the prosecutor, the record holder, the complainant or witness and anyone else the record relates to, with the subpoena in Form 16.1, at least 60 days before the hearing?
GIVEN `I served the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served the application on the prosecutor?
      `I served the person who has the record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served the application on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record?
      `I served the complainant or witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served the application on the complainant or witness?
      `there is another person to whom, to my knowledge, the record relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there another person to whom, to your knowledge, the record or therapeutic record relates?
      `I served that other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served that other person?
      `I served the subpoena in Form 16.1 on the person who has the record at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve a subpoena in Form 16.1 on the person who has possession or control of the record at the same time?
      `the day I served the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you serve the application (year-month-day)?
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the hearing (year-month-day)?
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge allow a shorter interval in the interests of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.12(5), have I served my application and the subpoena as required` IS
    `s 278.12(5) the accused has served the application as the subsection requires` `I served the prosecutor` `I served the person who has the record` `I served the complainant or witness` `there is another person to whom, to my knowledge, the record relates` `I served that other person` `I served the subpoena in Form 16.1 on the person who has the record at the same time` `the day I served the application` `the day of the hearing` `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`

@export Under section 278.12(7), does it fulfil the service requirement if I personally serve the application or a subpoena on the complainant?
GIVEN `I personally serve the application or a subpoena on the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you personally serve the application or a subpoena on the complainant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.12(7), does my personal service on the complainant fulfil the service requirement` IS
    `s 278.12(7) the accused's personal service on the complainant fulfils the service requirement` `I personally serve the application or a subpoena on the complainant`

@export Under section 278.14(1), may the judge order the person who has the record to produce it to the court for review (the application was made as required, I have established likely relevance or a reasonable doubt, and production is necessary in the interests of justice)?
GIVEN `the application was made in accordance with subsections 278.12(2) to (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application made in accordance with subsections 278.12(2) to (6)?
      `I have established that the record is likely relevant or that the therapeutic record could raise a reasonable doubt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify, or that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to your guilt?
      `the production is necessary in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the production of all or any part of the record necessary in the interests of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.14(1), may the judge order production of the record to the court for review` IS
    `s 278.14(1) the judge may order production of the record or therapeutic record to the court for review` `the application was made in accordance with subsections 278.12(2) to (6)` `I have established that the record is likely relevant or that the therapeutic record could raise a reasonable doubt` `the production is necessary in the interests of justice`

@export Under section 278.16(1), may the judge order a record (not a therapeutic record) to be produced to me, if satisfied it is likely relevant and that its production is necessary in the interests of justice?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the record is likely relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the record, or part of it, is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify?
      `the judge is satisfied that its production is necessary in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that its production is necessary in the interests of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.16(1), may the judge order the record to be produced to me` IS
    `s 278.16(1) the judge may order the record to be produced to the accused` `the judge is satisfied that the record is likely relevant` `the judge is satisfied that its production is necessary in the interests of justice`

@export Under section 278.16(2), may the judge order a therapeutic record to be produced to me, if satisfied it contains evidence likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to my guilt that is not available from any other source?
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that it contains evidence likely to raise a reasonable doubt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the therapeutic record, or part of it, contains evidence that is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to your guilt?
      `the judge is satisfied that the evidence is not available from any other source` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that the evidence is not available from any other source?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.16(2), may the judge order the therapeutic record to be produced to me` IS
    `s 278.16(2) the judge may order the therapeutic record to be produced to the accused` `the judge is satisfied that it contains evidence likely to raise a reasonable doubt` `the judge is satisfied that the evidence is not available from any other source`

@export Under section 278.16(4), may the judge impose a condition on the production of the record to me (editing, a copy only, no disclosure to others, viewing only at the court, no copies, severing details)?
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `s 278.16(4) condition` @desc Which condition: one of those the subsection lists, or another?
      `the judge orders the production of the record to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to you?
      `the condition protects the interests of justice and the privacy, personal security and equality interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the condition protect the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests of the complainant or witness and of any other person to whom the record relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.16(4), may the judge impose the condition on the production to me` IS
    `s 278.16(4) the judge may impose the condition on the production` `the condition` `the judge orders the production of the record to me` `the condition protects the interests of justice and the privacy, personal security and equality interests`

@export Under section 278.16(6), is it barred for me to use in any other proceedings a record that was produced to me under an order under subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the record was produced to me under an order under subsection 278.16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the record produced to you under an order under subsection 278.16(1)?
      `I use it in other proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use it in other proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.16(6), is my use of the record in other proceedings barred` IS
    `s 278.16(6) the use in other proceedings is barred` `the record was produced to me under an order under subsection 278.16(1)` `I use it in other proceedings`

@export Under section 278.16(7), must the court still keep in a sealed package the record it refused to order produced to me (until the later of the end of the time for any appeal and the completion of any appeal)?
GIVEN `the judge refused to order the production of the record to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge refuse to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to you?
      `a court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a court order otherwise?
      `the day the time for any appeal ends` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the time for any appeal end (year-month-day)?
      `the day any appeal is completed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is any appeal completed (year-month-day; the same day as above if there is no appeal)?
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (year-month-day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.16(7), must the court still keep the refused record in a sealed package` IS
    `s 278.16(7) the record must still be kept in a sealed package by the court` `the judge refused to order the production of the record to me` `a court orders otherwise` `the day the time for any appeal ends` `the day any appeal is completed` today

@export Under section 278.18(1), is publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the contents of the application for production, the hearing or the judge's determination prohibited (subject to the exceptions in subsection (1.1))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 278.18(1) matter` @desc What is it that would be published? (the contents of an application for production, the evidence or submissions at the hearing, or the judge's determination and reasons)
      `the judge has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right of privacy, ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted?
      `the determination is that the evidence is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that the evidence is admissible?
      `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made in the course of the administration of justice?
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not to make the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the disclosure not one of making the information known in the community?
      `the disclosure is made by the complainant or a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made by the complainant or a witness?
      `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure about that complainant or witness and their particulars?
      `the discloser did not reveal another protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person disclosing avoid intentionally or recklessly revealing the identity of, or particulars likely to identify, any other person whose identity is protected?
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not to make the information known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the disclosure not one of making the information known to the public?
      `the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the complainant or the witness?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.18(1), is publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the matter prohibited` IS
    `s 278.18(1) the publication, broadcast or transmission of the matter is prohibited` `the matter` `the judge has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` `the determination is that the evidence is admissible` (`s 278.18(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure` `the exception facts`)
    WHERE
        `the exception facts` MEANS `s 276.03(1.1) facts` WITH
                    `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice`
                    `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community` IS `the purpose of the disclosure is not to make the information known in the community`
                    `the disclosure is made by the complainant or a witness` IS `the disclosure is made by the complainant or a witness`
                    `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` IS `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars`
                    `the discloser did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of, or particulars likely to identify, any other person whose identity is protected by this section` IS `the discloser did not reveal another protected person`
                    `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public` IS `the purpose of the disclosure is not to make the information known to the public`
                    `the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the complainant or the witness` IS `the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust`

@export Under section 278.2(1), is production to me of a record or therapeutic record in the possession or control of the prosecutor barred, except under the application procedure of sections 278.21 to 278.28?
