-- Layer 2. A punishment question asks what the accused is liable to; a bar is asked as a bar; a defence as a defence.
§ `Kidnapping, trafficking, hostage-taking and abduction (ss 279 to 286)`

@export Under section 279(1), have I committed the offence of kidnapping?
GIVEN `the person kidnaps a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person kidnaps a person?
      `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be confined or imprisoned against the person’s will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be confined or imprisoned against the person’s will?
      `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be unlawfully sent or transported out of Canada against the person’s will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be unlawfully sent or transported out of Canada against the person’s will?
      `the person kidnaps with intent to hold the person for ransom or to service against the person’s will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person kidnaps with intent to hold the person for ransom or to service against the person’s will?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 279(1), have I committed the offence of kidnapping` IS
    `s 279(1) the person commits the offence of kidnapping` `the person kidnaps a person` `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be confined or imprisoned against the person’s will` `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be unlawfully sent or transported out of Canada against the person’s will` `the person kidnaps with intent to hold the person for ransom or to service against the person’s will`

@export Under section 279(1.1), what punishment am I liable to for kidnapping?
GIVEN `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a restricted firearm used in the commission of the offence?
      `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a prohibited firearm used in the commission of the offence?
      `a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a firearm (of any kind) used in the commission of the offence?
      `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization?
      `the earlier convictions` IS A LIST OF `s 279(1.2) earlier conviction` @desc List each earlier conviction you have: the offence, whether a firearm was used, the day of conviction, and the days in custody between the two convictions.
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you convicted of the offence for which you are now being sentenced?
      `the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) is under 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person kidnapped under 16 years of age?
      `the person who commits the offence is a parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of the person referred to in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of the person kidnapped?
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 279(1.1), what punishment am I liable to for kidnapping` IS
    `s 279(1.1) the punishment` (JUST `a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence`) (JUST `a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence`) (JUST `a firearm is used in the commission of the offence`) (JUST `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`) (`s 279(1.2) the person has committed a second or subsequent offence` `the earlier convictions` `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) `the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) is under 16 years of age` `the person who commits the offence is a parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of the person referred to in that paragraph`

