-- Layer 2. An immunity is asked as the immunity the section gives; the definition of newspaper is answered inside this part.
§ `Defamatory libel (ss 297 to 317)`

@export Under section 297, is the publication a newspaper?
GIVEN `the publication is a paper, magazine or periodical` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the publication is a paper, magazine or periodical?
      `it contains public news, intelligence or reports of events, or any remarks or observations thereon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it contains public news, intelligence or reports of events, or any remarks or observations thereon?
      `it is printed for sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is printed for sale?
      `it is published periodically or in parts or numbers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is published periodically or in parts or numbers?
      `the longest interval in days between the publication of any two such papers, parts or numbers` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest interval, in days, between the publication of any two such papers, parts or numbers?
      `it is printed in order to be dispersed and made public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is printed in order to be dispersed and made public?
      `it contains advertisements, exclusively or principally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it contains advertisements, exclusively or principally?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 297, is the publication a newspaper` IS
    `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` `the publication is a paper, magazine or periodical` `it contains public news, intelligence or reports of events, or any remarks or observations thereon` `it is printed for sale` `it is published periodically or in parts or numbers` `the longest interval in days between the publication of any two such papers, parts or numbers` `it is printed in order to be dispersed and made public` `it contains advertisements, exclusively or principally`

@export Under section 297, does the definition of newspaper apply in the section I ask about?
GIVEN `section` IS A `Provision of the Code` @desc Which section of the Code are you asking about? (give its section number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 297, does the definition of newspaper apply in the section I ask about` IS
    `s 297 the definition applies in the section` `section`

@export Under section 298(1), is the matter a defamatory libel?
GIVEN `the matter is published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter is published?
      `there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it?
      `it is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing that person to hatred, contempt or ridicule?
      `it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 298(1), is the matter a defamatory libel` IS
    `s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` `the matter is published` `there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it` `it is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule` `it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published`

@export Under section 298(2), may a defamatory libel be expressed in this manner and medium?
GIVEN `manner` IS A `s 298(2) the manner of expression` @desc In what manner was the libel expressed? (directly, by insinuation, by irony, or in another manner)
      `medium` IS A `s 298(2) the medium` @desc In what medium was the libel expressed? (in words legibly marked on any substance, by an object signifying a defamatory libel otherwise than by words, or in another medium)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 298(2), may a defamatory libel be expressed in this manner and medium` IS
    `s 298(2) a defamatory libel may be expressed in this manner and medium` `manner` `medium`

@export Under section 299, did I publish a libel?
GIVEN `the person exhibits it in public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person exhibits it in public?
      `the person causes it to be read or seen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person causes it to be read or seen?
      `the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 299, did I publish a libel` IS
    `s 299 the person publishes a libel` `the person exhibits it in public` `the person causes it to be read or seen` `the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames`

@export Under section 300, am I guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that I know is false?
GIVEN `the matter is published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter is published?
      `there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it?
      `it is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing that person to hatred, contempt or ridicule?
      `it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published?
      `the person exhibits it in public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person exhibits it in public?
      `the person causes it to be read or seen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person causes it to be read or seen?
      `the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames?
      `the person knows that the defamatory libel is false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person knows that the defamatory libel is false?
      `a provision of sections 303 to 316 says I am not deemed to publish a defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any provision of sections 303 to 316 say that you are not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of what you did? (answer yes only if one of them clearly applies to you)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 300, am I guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that I know is false` IS
    `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (`s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` `the matter is published` `there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it` `it is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule` `it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published`) (`s 299 the person publishes a libel` `the person exhibits it in public` `the person causes it to be read or seen` `the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames`) `the person knows that the defamatory libel is false` (`ss 303 to 316 a provision says the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel` (LIST (JUST `a provision of sections 303 to 316 says I am not deemed to publish a defamatory libel`)))

@export Under section 300, what punishment am I liable to for publishing a defamatory libel that I know is false?
GIVEN `mode` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the case being prosecuted by indictment, or on summary conviction?
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment @desc What is the general penalty that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
