@export Under section 314, am I not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested?
GIVEN `the person publishes to another person defamatory matter for the purpose of giving information to that person with respect to a subject-matter in which that person has, or is believed on reasonable grounds to have, an interest in knowing the truth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person publishes to another person defamatory matter for the purpose of giving information to that person with respect to a subject-matter in which that person has, or is believed on reasonable grounds to have, an interest in knowing the truth?
      `the conduct of the person who gives the information is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your conduct in giving the information reasonable in the circumstances?
      `the defamatory matter is relevant to the subject-matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the defamatory matter is relevant to the subject-matter?
      `the defamatory matter is true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the defamatory matter is true?
      `if it is not true, it is made without ill-will toward the person who is defamed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the matter is not true, did you publish it without ill-will toward the person who is defamed?
      `if it is not true, it is made in the belief, on reasonable grounds, that it is true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the matter is not true, did you publish it in the belief, on reasonable grounds, that it is true?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 314, am I not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` IS
    `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` `the person publishes to another person defamatory matter for the purpose of giving information to that person with respect to a subject-matter in which that person has, or is believed on reasonable grounds to have, an interest in knowing the truth` `the conduct of the person who gives the information is reasonable in the circumstances` `the defamatory matter is relevant to the subject-matter` `the defamatory matter is true` `if it is not true, it is made without ill-will toward the person who is defamed` `if it is not true, it is made in the belief, on reasonable grounds, that it is true`

@export Under section 315, am I not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong?
GIVEN `the person publishes defamatory matter in good faith for the purpose of seeking remedy or redress for a private or public wrong or grievance from a person who has, or who on reasonable grounds he believes has, the right or is under an obligation to remedy or redress the wrong or grievance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you publish defamatory matter in good faith for the purpose of seeking remedy or redress for a private or public wrong or grievance from a person who has, or who on reasonable grounds you believe has, the right or is under an obligation to remedy or redress the wrong or grievance?
      `he believes that the defamatory matter is true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe that the defamatory matter is true?
      `the defamatory matter is relevant to the remedy or redress that is sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the defamatory matter is relevant to the remedy or redress that is sought?
      `the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 315, am I not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` IS
    `s 315 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` `the person publishes defamatory matter in good faith for the purpose of seeking remedy or redress for a private or public wrong or grievance from a person who has, or who on reasonable grounds he believes has, the right or is under an obligation to remedy or redress the wrong or grievance` `he believes that the defamatory matter is true` `the defamatory matter is relevant to the remedy or redress that is sought` `the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances`

@export Under section 316(1), may I, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature?
GIVEN `the accused is alleged to have published a defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the accused is alleged to have published a defamatory libel?
      `the evidence is to prove that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the evidence is to prove that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 316(1), may I, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` IS
    `s 316(1) the accused may, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` `the accused is alleged to have published a defamatory libel` `the evidence is to prove that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province`

@export Under section 316(2), must the court direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and discharge me?
GIVEN `at some stage in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge is satisfied that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at some stage in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge is satisfied that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 316(2), must the court direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and discharge me` IS
    `s 316(2) the court shall direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and shall discharge the accused` `at some stage in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge is satisfied that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province`

@export Under section 316(3), is the certificate conclusive evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature?
GIVEN `the certificate is under the hand of the Speaker or clerk of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate is under the hand of the Speaker or clerk of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province?
      `it is to the effect that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate, House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is to the effect that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate, House of Commons or the legislature of a province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 316(3), is the certificate conclusive evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` IS
    `s 316(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` `the certificate is under the hand of the Speaker or clerk of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` `it is to the effect that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate, House of Commons or the legislature of a province`

@export Under section 317, may the jury give a general verdict of guilty or not guilty on the whole matter put in issue on the indictment?
GIVEN `on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded?
      `the jury is sworn to try the issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the jury is sworn to try the issue?
