-- Layer 2. Grouped in the text's order. Provisions that address only a judge are asked for what they mean to the accused.
§ `Records in the accused's possession: publication bans, joint applications, reasons (ss 278.32 to 278.98)`

@export Under section 278.32(1), am I prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting this matter about an application for records in an accused's possession?
GIVEN `matter` IS A `s 278.32(1) the matter` @desc What do you want to publish? (a) the contents of the application; (b) evidence, information or representations at the consideration of the application or at the hearing; (c) the decision of the judge on the application; (d) the determination and reasons about admissibility; or none of those
      `an application for a hearing on records in the accused’s possession has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for a hearing on records in the accused's possession been made under section 278.3(1)?
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge, provincial court judge or justice ordered that the decision or the determination and reasons may be published, broadcast or transmitted?
      `the determination is that evidence is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination one that evidence is admissible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.32(1), am I prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting this matter about an application for records in an accused's possession` IS
    `s 278.32(1) publication of the matter is prohibited` `matter` (JUST `an application for a hearing on records in the accused’s possession has been made`) `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` `the determination is that evidence is admissible`

@export Under section 278.32(1.1), is my disclosure outside the prohibition of subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the information is referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you disclosed information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (d) of section 278.32 (the application, the evidence at the hearing, the decision, the determination and reasons)?
      `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the disclosure in the course of the administration of justice?
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your purpose was not to make the information known in the community?
      `the person who made the disclosure is the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the complainant (the person against whom the offence is alleged to have been committed)?
      `the person who made the disclosure is a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a witness (in the proceedings, on the application for records)?
      `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure about you as the complainant or witness, and your own particulars?
      `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of, or particulars likely to identify, any other person whose identity is protected by the section?
      `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your purpose was not to make the information known to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.32(1.1), is my disclosure outside the prohibition of subsection (1)` IS
    `s 278.32(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure` `the information is referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (d)` `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community` (`s 278.32(1.1) the disclosure is made by the complainant or any witness` (JUST `the person who made the disclosure is the complainant`) `the person who made the disclosure is a witness`) `the disclosure is about that complainant or witness and their particulars` `they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section` `the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public`

