@export Under section 278.34, is the determination on the admissibility of records in my possession deemed a question of law for the purposes of the section I name?
GIVEN `the determination is one made under subsection 278.31(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination one made under section 278.31(4) (after a hearing on records in your possession)?
      `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked` IS A `Provision of the Code` @desc For the purposes of which section of the Code do you ask whether the determination is a question of law? (give its section number and subsection)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.34, is the determination on the admissibility of records in my possession deemed a question of law for the purposes of the section I name` IS
    `s 278.34 the determination is deemed to be a question of law` `the determination is one made under subsection 278.31(4)` `the purpose, as the section of the Code for whose purposes the question is asked`

@export Under section 278.35(1), may the prosecutor, the complainant or witness and I jointly apply for a determination without a hearing?
GIVEN `the applicants are the prosecutor and the accused, together with the complainant or any witness to which the record or part relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the applicants the prosecutor and you as the accused, together with the complainant or any witness to whom the record or part relates?
      `the application is made to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made to the judge before whom you are to be, or are being, tried?
      `the application is for a determination whether the record or part is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) without holding a hearing under section 278.31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for a determination whether the record or part is admissible under section 278.29(2), without a hearing under section 278.31?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.35(1), may the prosecutor, the complainant or witness and I jointly apply for a determination without a hearing` IS
    `s 278.35(1) the applicants may jointly apply for a determination without a hearing` `the applicants are the prosecutor and the accused, together with the complainant or any witness to which the record or part relates` `the application is made to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried` `the application is for a determination whether the record or part is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) without holding a hearing under section 278.31`

@export Under section 278.35(2), does our joint application meet the form and content required?
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is made in writing?
      `the application is signed by the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is signed by the applicants?
      `the application sets out the detailed particulars of the record or part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application sets out the detailed particulars of the record or part?
      `it sets out the relevance of that record or part to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it sets out the relevance of that record or part to an issue at trial?
      `the admissibility of the record or part is subject to section 276` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the admissibility of the record or part subject to section 276?
      `it sets out how the record or part meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection 278.29(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it sets out how the record or part meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection 278.29(3)?
      `it sets out that the record or part has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it sets out that the record or part has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice?
      `it sets out any information the applicants consider necessary to assist the judge when the judge takes into account the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it sets out any information the applicants consider necessary to assist the judge when the judge takes into account the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 278.35(2), does our joint application meet the form and content required` IS
    `s 278.35(2) the application meets the form and content required` `the application is made in writing` `the application is signed by the applicants` `the application sets out the detailed particulars of the record or part` `it sets out the relevance of that record or part to an issue at trial` `the admissibility of the record or part is subject to section 276` `it sets out how the record or part meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection 278.29(3)` `it sets out that the record or part has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice` `it sets out any information the applicants consider necessary to assist the judge when the judge takes into account the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3)`

