DECIDE `Under section 286.5(1)(a), am I guilty of the offence of receiving a material benefit from sexual services after the exception of section 286.2(4) and the immunity` IS
    `s 286.2 and s 286.5(1)(a) the person is guilty of the offence after the exception and the immunity` (`s 286.2(1) the person is guilty of the offence of receiving a material benefit from sexual services` `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(1)`) (`s 286.2(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to the person who receives the benefit` `the person receives the benefit in the context of a legitimate living arrangement with the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` `the person receives the benefit as a result of a legal or moral obligation of the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` `the person receives the benefit in consideration for a service or good that they offer, on the same terms and conditions, to the general public` `the person receives the benefit in consideration for a service or good that they do not offer to the general public but that they offered or provided to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` `they did not counsel or encourage that person to provide sexual services` `the benefit is proportionate to the value of the service or good` (`s 286.2(5) subsection (4) does not apply to the person` `the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` `the person used, threatened to use or attempted to use violence, intimidation or coercion in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` `the person abused a position of trust, power or authority in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` `the person provided a drug, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived for the purpose of aiding or abetting that person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration` `the person engaged in conduct, in relation to any person, that would constitute an offence under section 286.3` `the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration`)) (`s 286.5(1)(a) the person is immune from prosecution for an offence under section 286.2` `offence` `the benefit is derived from the provision of their own sexual services`)

