§ `Marriage offences (ss 287 to 296)`

@export Under section 290(1), have I committed bigamy?
GIVEN `the person acts in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person acts in Canada?
      `the person, being married, goes through a form of marriage with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Being married, did you go through a form of marriage with another person?
      `the person, knowing that another person is married, goes through a form of marriage with that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Knowing that another person is married, did you go through a form of marriage with that person?
      `the person, on the same day or simultaneously, goes through a form of marriage with more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, on the same day or simultaneously, go through a form of marriage with more than one person?
      `the person is a Canadian citizen resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person is a Canadian citizen resident in Canada?
      `the person leaves Canada with intent to do anything mentioned in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person leaves Canada with intent to do anything mentioned in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii)?
      `pursuant to that intent, the person does outside Canada anything mentioned in those subparagraphs in circumstances mentioned therein` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: pursuant to that intent, the person does outside Canada anything mentioned in those subparagraphs in circumstances mentioned therein?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 290(1), have I committed bigamy` IS
    `s 290(1) the person commits bigamy` `the person acts in Canada` `the person, being married, goes through a form of marriage with another person` `the person, knowing that another person is married, goes through a form of marriage with that person` `the person, on the same day or simultaneously, goes through a form of marriage with more than one person` `the person is a Canadian citizen resident in Canada` `the person leaves Canada with intent to do anything mentioned in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (iii)` `pursuant to that intent, the person does outside Canada anything mentioned in those subparagraphs in circumstances mentioned therein`

