@export Under section 294, what punishment am I liable to for pretending to solemnize marriage?
GIVEN `mode` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the case being prosecuted by indictment, or on summary conviction?
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment @desc What is the general penalty that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 294, what punishment am I liable to for pretending to solemnize marriage` IS
    `s 294 the punishment` `mode` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@export Under section 295, am I guilty of the offence of solemnizing a marriage contrary to law?
GIVEN `the person is lawfully authorized to solemnize marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person is lawfully authorized to solemnize marriage?
      `the person knowingly solemnizes a marriage in contravention of federal law or the laws of the province in which the marriage is solemnized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this describe you or what you did: the person knowingly solemnizes a marriage in contravention of federal law or the laws of the province in which the marriage is solemnized?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 295, am I guilty of the offence of solemnizing a marriage contrary to law` IS
    `s 295 the person is guilty of the offence of solemnizing a marriage contrary to law` `the person is lawfully authorized to solemnize marriage` `the person knowingly solemnizes a marriage in contravention of federal law or the laws of the province in which the marriage is solemnized`

@export Under section 295, what punishment am I liable to for solemnizing a marriage contrary to law?
GIVEN `mode` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the case being prosecuted by indictment, or on summary conviction?
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment @desc What is the general penalty that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 295, what punishment am I liable to for solemnizing a marriage contrary to law` IS
    `s 295 the punishment` `mode` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc11 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc11-seat.l4 -- the SEAT layer over Part VIII.1 (Offences Relating to Conveyances), sections 320.11 to 320.4, of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- LAYER 2. Source of the law: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking, on facts they can state, whether what they did is an offence, what its gravity and
-- penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's
-- Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer asks the questions Part VIII.1 answers for that person. It IMPORTs the layer-1 modules and the keel's section 2 definitions, builds each layer-1 input from plain facts (yes or no, a number, a date,
-- a choice from a short list worded in the question), and CALLS the layer-1 rule: it restates no rule. A term of section 2 is answered by the keel's own function (s 2 motor vehicle, s 2 bodily harm, s 2 peace officer,
-- s 2 railway equipment), so a NOTHING ("not covered") from it is carried through and never turned into FALSE; the person's "no" to "was it a police officer?" is NOTHING, not "not a peace officer", because
-- the section 2 definition "includes" and is not closed.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE (the text says yes on these facts), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), or NOTHING (not covered). A string that is not one of the listed choices answers NOTHING.
-- Every question begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering. A question's name asks the question its body answers, in the same direction: an offence "have I committed ...", a bar "am I barred ...",
-- an exception "does the exception apply ...", an officer's power "may a peace officer ...". Where the layer-1 function is a power of an official the answer is the power's, and NOTHING when its gate is unmet.
-- There is never a seat for an official: sections 320.37 (a practitioner's immunity), 320.38 (regulations), 320.39 and 320.4 (approvals and designations) are encoded in layer 1 and have no question here, except that
-- whether a device or a person was approved or designated is asked through the question about the definition that turns on it (section 320.11).

GIVEN kind IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Under section 320.11, helper: the kind of conveyance is one of the listed choices` MEANS
    kind EQUALS "motor vehicle" OR kind EQUALS "vessel" OR kind EQUALS "aircraft" OR kind EQUALS "railway equipment" OR kind EQUALS "something else"

GIVEN kind IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 320.11, helper: it is a motor vehicle` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS "motor vehicle" THEN `s 2 motor vehicle` TRUE (JUST FALSE)
        IF `Under section 320.11, helper: the kind of conveyance is one of the listed choices` kind THEN `s 2 motor vehicle` FALSE (JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the kind of conveyance is not one of the listed choices

GIVEN kind IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 320.11, helper: it is a vessel` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS "vessel" THEN `s 320.11 the thing is a vessel` FALSE TRUE
        IF `Under section 320.11, helper: the kind of conveyance is one of the listed choices` kind THEN JUST FALSE   -- the person states a different kind of conveyance
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the kind of conveyance is not one of the listed choices

GIVEN kind IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 320.11, helper: it is railway equipment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS "railway equipment" THEN `s 2 railway equipment` `a machine constructed for movement exclusively on lines of railway, whether or not the machine is capable of independent motion`
        IF `Under section 320.11, helper: the kind of conveyance is one of the listed choices` kind THEN `s 2 railway equipment` `a thing that is none of those`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the kind of conveyance is not one of the listed choices

GIVEN kind IS A STRING
      use IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Under section 320.11, helper: the kind of conveyance is one of the listed choices` kind)
       OR NOT (use EQUALS "drove it" OR use EQUALS "navigated it" OR use EQUALS "assisted in navigating it" OR use EQUALS "participated in the direct control of its motion" OR use EQUALS "had care or control of it" OR use EQUALS "none of these")
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the kind of conveyance or how it was used is not one of the listed choices
    ELSE `s 320.11 the person operates the conveyance`
             (`Under section 320.11, helper: it is a motor vehicle` kind)
             (`Under section 320.11, helper: it is a vessel` kind)
             (kind EQUALS "aircraft")
             (`Under section 320.11, helper: it is railway equipment` kind)
             (use EQUALS "drove it") (use EQUALS "navigated it") (use EQUALS "assisted in navigating it")
             (use EQUALS "participated in the direct control of its motion") (use EQUALS "had care or control of it")

GIVEN isPeace IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` MEANS
    IF isPeace
    THEN `s 2 peace officer` `a police officer, police constable, bailiff, constable, or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace or for the service or execution of civil process`
    ELSE `s 2 peace officer` `a person in a capacity that is none of those`   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "peace officer includes": a person who is not a police officer is not thereby "not a peace officer"

GIVEN mode IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Mode of proceeding`)
`Under section 320.19, helper: the mode of proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF mode EQUALS "by indictment" THEN JUST `by indictment`
        IF mode EQUALS "on summary conviction" THEN JUST `on summary conviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the mode is not one of the two listed choices


§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.11: what a conveyance is, what it is to operate it, and the approved devices`
-- Everything below begins from the thing you were using and what you did with it. Answers are those of section 320.11 and of section 2 (motor vehicle, railway equipment).

@export Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.11, am I treated as having operated the conveyance` IS
    (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`)

@export Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.11, is what I was using a conveyance` IS
    `s 320.11 the thing is a conveyance` (`Under section 320.11, helper: it is a motor vehicle` `my conveyance`) (`Under section 320.11, helper: it is a vessel` `my conveyance`) (`my conveyance` EQUALS "aircraft") (`Under section 320.11, helper: it is railway equipment` `my conveyance`)

@export Under section 320.11, was the device an approved screening device?
GIVEN `the device was an approved screening device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device an approved screening device (designed to ascertain alcohol in the blood and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.11, was the device an approved screening device` IS
    (`s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` `the device was an approved screening device` `the device was an approved screening device`)

@export Under section 320.11, was the instrument an approved instrument?
GIVEN `the instrument was an approved instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument an approved instrument (designed to analyse breath and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.11, was the instrument an approved instrument` IS
    (`s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument`)

@export Under section 320.11, was the container an approved container?
GIVEN `the sample was received into an approved container` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the blood sample received into an approved container (designed for blood samples and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.11, was the container an approved container` IS
    (`s 320.11 the container is an approved container` `the sample was received into an approved container` `the sample was received into an approved container`)

§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.13 to 320.18: the offences`
-- Each question asks whether the facts you state make out the offence the section defines. A NOTHING answer means the text does not say.

@export Under section 320.13(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance in a manner dangerous to the public?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `the way I operated it was dangerous to the public, having regard to all of the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to all of the circumstances, was the way you operated it dangerous to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.13(1), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance in a manner dangerous to the public` IS
    `s 320.13(1) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance in a manner that is dangerous to the public` (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`) `the way I operated it was dangerous to the public, having regard to all of the circumstances`

@export Under section 320.13(2), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing bodily harm to another person?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `the way I operated it was dangerous to the public, having regard to all of the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to all of the circumstances, was the way you operated it dangerous to the public?
      `as a result I caused harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of operating it that way, did you cause harm to another person?
      `the harm was bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the harm any hurt or injury that interfered with the person’s health or comfort and was more than merely transient or trifling?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.13(2), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing bodily harm to another person` IS
    `s 320.13(2) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes bodily harm to another person` (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`) `the way I operated it was dangerous to the public, having regard to all of the circumstances` `as a result I caused harm to another person` (`s 2 bodily harm` `the harm was bodily harm` `the harm was bodily harm` `the harm was bodily harm`)

@export Under section 320.13(3), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing the death of another person?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `the way I operated it was dangerous to the public, having regard to all of the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to all of the circumstances, was the way you operated it dangerous to the public?
      `as a result I caused the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of operating it that way, did you cause the death of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.13(3), have I committed the offence of dangerous operation causing the death of another person` IS
    `s 320.13(3) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance dangerously and, as a result, causes the death of another person` (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`) `the way I operated it was dangerous to the public, having regard to all of the circumstances` `as a result I caused the death of another person`

@export Under section 320.14(1)(a), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired by alcohol or a drug?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your ability to operate the conveyance impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug or by a combination of the two?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.14(1)(a), have I committed the offence of operating a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired by alcohol or a drug` IS
    `s 320.14(1)(a) everyone commits an offence who operates a conveyance while their ability to operate it is impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug` (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`) `my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol or a drug`

-- A sample taken more than two hours after you stopped is carried back to the two hours by section 320.31(4) when it applies; otherwise your measured figure is used.
@export Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `my blood alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood alcohol concentration, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, from the analysis of your breath or blood? (0 if none)
      `how many minutes after I stopped operating it the first breath sample, or the blood sample, was taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes after you stopped operating the conveyance was the first breath sample, or the blood sample, taken?
      `I consumed alcohol after I stopped operating the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consume alcohol after you stopped operating the conveyance?
      `after I stopped operating it I had no reasonable expectation that I would be required to provide a sample of breath or blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you stopped operating it, did you have no reasonable expectation that you would be required to provide a sample of breath or blood?
      `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my blood alcohol concentration as determined under subsection 320.31(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your alcohol consumption consistent with your blood alcohol concentration as determined from the breath or blood analysis?
      `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my having had, when I was operating it, a blood alcohol concentration under 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your alcohol consumption consistent with your having had, when you were operating it, a blood alcohol concentration under 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.14(1)(b), have I committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` IS
    `s 320.14(1)(b) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more` (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`) bacWithin (`s 320.14(5) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` `I consumed alcohol after I stopped operating the conveyance` `after I stopped operating it I had no reasonable expectation that I would be required to provide a sample of breath or blood` `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my blood alcohol concentration as determined under subsection 320.31(1) or (2)` `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my having had, when I was operating it, a blood alcohol concentration under 80 mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`)
    WHERE
        bacWithin MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` `how many minutes after I stopped operating it the first breath sample, or the blood sample, was taken` `my blood alcohol concentration`
            WHEN JUST presumed THEN presumed
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `my blood alcohol concentration`

@export Under section 320.14(1)(c), have I committed the offence of having a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `my blood drug concentration for the drug` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood concentration of the drug, in the units the regulation uses? (0 if none)
      `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for paragraph 320.14(1)(c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What blood drug concentration does the regulation prescribe for that drug for paragraph 320.14(1)(c), in the same units?
      `I consumed the drug after I stopped operating the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consume the drug after you stopped operating the conveyance?
      `after I stopped operating it I had no reasonable expectation that I would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you stopped operating it, did you have no reasonable expectation that you would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.14(1)(c), have I committed the offence of having a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` IS
    `s 320.14(1)(c) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, a blood drug concentration at or above the prescribed concentration` (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`) `my blood drug concentration for the drug` `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for paragraph 320.14(1)(c)` (`s 320.14(6) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or subsection 320.14(4)` `I consumed the drug after I stopped operating the conveyance` `after I stopped operating it I had no reasonable expectation that I would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance`)

@export Under section 320.14(1)(d), have I committed the offence of having alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `my blood alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood alcohol concentration, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, from the analysis of your breath or blood? (0 if none)
      `my blood drug concentration for the drug` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood concentration of the drug, in the units the regulation uses? (0 if none)
      `the blood alcohol concentration prescribed by regulation for the drug and alcohol combined` IS A NUMBER @desc What blood alcohol concentration does the regulation prescribe for alcohol combined with that drug, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for the drug and alcohol combined` IS A NUMBER @desc What blood drug concentration does the regulation prescribe for that drug combined with alcohol, in the same units?
      `I consumed the drug or the alcohol or both after I stopped operating the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consume the drug, the alcohol or both after you stopped operating the conveyance?
      `after I stopped operating it I had no reasonable expectation that I would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you stopped operating it, did you have no reasonable expectation that you would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance?
      `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my blood alcohol concentration as determined under subsection 320.31(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your alcohol consumption consistent with your blood alcohol concentration as determined from the breath or blood analysis?
      `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my having had, when I was operating it, a blood alcohol concentration less than the one prescribed for the combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your alcohol consumption consistent with your having had, when you were operating it, a blood alcohol concentration less than the one prescribed for the drug and alcohol combined?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.14(1)(d), have I committed the offence of having alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` IS
    `s 320.14(1)(d) everyone commits an offence who has, within two hours after ceasing to operate a conveyance, alcohol and drug concentrations at or above those prescribed for the combination` (`Under section 320.11, helper: whether I operated it` `my conveyance` `how I used it`) `my blood alcohol concentration` `my blood drug concentration for the drug` `the blood alcohol concentration prescribed by regulation for the drug and alcohol combined` `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for the drug and alcohol combined` (`s 320.14(7) the exception applies: no person commits an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(d)` `I consumed the drug or the alcohol or both after I stopped operating the conveyance` `after I stopped operating it I had no reasonable expectation that I would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance` `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my blood alcohol concentration as determined under subsection 320.31(1) or (2)` `my alcohol consumption is consistent with my having had, when I was operating it, a blood alcohol concentration less than the one prescribed for the combination`)

@export Under section 320.14(2), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing bodily harm to another person?
GIVEN `I committed an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Suppose you committed an offence under subsection 320.14(1) (impaired operation, or a blood alcohol or drug concentration at or over the limit): is that the case?
      `while operating the conveyance I caused harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While you were operating the conveyance, did you cause harm to another person?
      `the harm was bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the harm any hurt or injury that interfered with the person’s health or comfort and was more than merely transient or trifling?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.14(2), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing bodily harm to another person` IS
    `s 320.14(2) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes bodily harm to another person` (JUST `I committed an offence under subsection 320.14(1)`) `while operating the conveyance I caused harm to another person` (`s 2 bodily harm` `the harm was bodily harm` `the harm was bodily harm` `the harm was bodily harm`)

@export Under section 320.14(3), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing the death of another person?
GIVEN `I committed an offence under subsection 320.14(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Suppose you committed an offence under subsection 320.14(1) (impaired operation, or a blood alcohol or drug concentration at or over the limit): is that the case?
      `while operating the conveyance I caused the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While you were operating the conveyance, did you cause the death of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.14(3), have I committed the offence of impaired or over-the-limit operation causing the death of another person` IS
    `s 320.14(3) everyone commits an offence who commits an offence under subsection 320.14(1) and, while operating the conveyance, causes the death of another person` (JUST `I committed an offence under subsection 320.14(1)`) `while operating the conveyance I caused the death of another person`

@export Under section 320.14(4), have I committed the offence of having a low blood drug concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance?
GIVEN `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `how I used it` IS A STRING @desc How did you use it? Answer exactly one of: drove it, navigated it, assisted in navigating it, participated in the direct control of its motion, had care or control of it, none of these
      `my blood drug concentration for the drug` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood concentration of the drug, in the units the regulation uses? (0 if none)
      `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for subsection 320.14(4)` IS A NUMBER @desc What blood drug concentration does the regulation prescribe for that drug for subsection 320.14(4), in the same units?
      `the blood drug concentration prescribed by regulation for paragraph 320.14(1)(c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What blood drug concentration does the regulation prescribe for that drug for paragraph 320.14(1)(c), in the same units?
      `I consumed the drug after I stopped operating the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consume the drug after you stopped operating the conveyance?
      `after I stopped operating it I had no reasonable expectation that I would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you stopped operating it, did you have no reasonable expectation that you would be required to provide a sample of a bodily substance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.14(4), have I committed the offence of having a low blood drug concentration within two hours after I stopped operating a conveyance` IS
