§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.19 to 320.22 and 320.26: punishment`
-- The offence is named by its place in the Code (its section number and subsection). The punishment of a first, second or subsequent offence follows the count of your earlier convictions under section 320.26.

-- Counting earlier convictions as section 320.26 counts them is applied to sections 320.2 and 320.21 as well (fork F3 in NOTES.md). Section 787(1), which gives the penalty for the summary conviction limb of 320.13(1), 320.16(1), 320.17 and 320.18(1), is outside this Part: its figures are asked.
@export Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section is the offence under? Type the section number as a decimal, for example 320.14 or 320.13
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is the offence under? Type it as the Code writes it, for example (1), (1)(b), (2), (3) or (4); type nothing for a section with no subsections, such as 320.17
      `the mode of proceeding` IS A STRING @desc Is the Crown proceeding by indictment or on summary conviction? Answer exactly: by indictment, or: on summary conviction
      `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under section 320.15?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under the former section 253, 254 or 255 (as those sections read before section 320.26 came into force)?
      `my blood alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood alcohol concentration, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, from the analysis of your breath or blood? (0 if none)
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc Section 787(1) is outside this Part. Type the maximum fine, in dollars, that it sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction (type 0 if it states none; used only for the summary conviction limb of 320.13(1), 320.16(1), 320.17 and 320.18(1))
      `the maximum imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc Type the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction (type 0 if it states none; used only as for the previous question)
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 320.19, what punishment is my offence liable to` IS
    CONSIDER (`Under section 320.19, helper: the mode of proceeding` `the mode of proceeding`)
    WHEN JUST m THEN `s 320.19 the punishment the offence is liable to` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`) m (`s 320.26 the occasion of the offence before the court` (`s 320.26 the number of earlier offences` `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force`)) `my blood alcohol concentration` (`Punishment` WITH `mode` IS `on summary conviction`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (IF `the maximum imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` AT MOST 0 THEN `no imprisonment is stated` ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, `the maximum imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction`, 0, FALSE)), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS (IF `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` AT MOST 0 THEN `no fine is stated` ELSE `a fine of` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction`), `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the mode is not one of the two listed choices

@export Under section 320.19, is my offence an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section is the offence under? Type the section number as a decimal, for example 320.14 or 320.13
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is the offence under? Type it as the Code writes it, for example (1), (1)(b), (2), (3) or (4); type nothing for a section with no subsections, such as 320.17
GIVETH A MAYBE `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 320.19, is my offence an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or both` IS
    `s 320.19 the class of the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)

@export Under section 320.19(3), what is the minimum fine for a first offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b) at my blood alcohol concentration?
GIVEN `my blood alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood alcohol concentration, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, from the analysis of your breath or blood? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE Fine
DECIDE `Under section 320.19(3), what is the minimum fine for a first offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b) at my blood alcohol concentration` IS
    `s 320.19(3) the minimum fine for a first offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` `my blood alcohol concentration`

@export Under section 320.26, is this my first, second or a subsequent offence?
GIVEN `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under section 320.15?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under the former section 253, 254 or 255 (as those sections read before section 320.26 came into force)?
GIVETH A `s 320.19 occasion`
DECIDE `Under section 320.26, is this my first, second or a subsequent offence` IS
    `s 320.26 the occasion of the offence before the court` (`s 320.26 the number of earlier offences` `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force`)

@export Under section 320.22, which aggravating circumstances must the court consider when it sentences me?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section is the offence under? Type the section number as a decimal, for example 320.14 or 320.13
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is the offence under? Type it as the Code writes it, for example (1), (1)(b), (2), (3) or (4); type nothing for a section with no subsections, such as 320.17
      `the commission of the offence resulted in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence result in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person?
      `my conveyance` IS A STRING @desc What kind of conveyance were you using? Answer exactly one of: motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway equipment, something else
      `I was in a race with at least one other motor vehicle or in a contest of speed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in a race with at least one other motor vehicle, or in a contest of speed?
      `the operation is on a street, road or highway or in any other public place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the operation on a street, road or highway, or in any other public place?
      `a person under the age of 16 years was a passenger in the conveyance I was operating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a person under the age of 16 years a passenger in the conveyance you were operating?
      `I was being remunerated for operating the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you being paid for operating the conveyance?
      `my blood alcohol concentration at the time of committing the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood alcohol concentration, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, at the time of committing the offence? (0 if none)
      `I was operating a large motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you operating a large motor vehicle?
      `I was not permitted, under a federal or provincial Act, to operate the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not permitted, under a federal or provincial Act, to operate the conveyance?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under section 320.22, which aggravating circumstances must the court consider when it sentences me` IS
    `s 320.22 the paragraphs of section 320.22 that apply`
        (`s 320.22(a) the court shall consider that the offence resulted in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `the commission of the offence resulted in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person`)
        (`s 320.22(b) the court shall consider that the offender was operating a motor vehicle in a race or contest of speed in a public place` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) (`Under section 320.11, helper: it is a motor vehicle` `my conveyance`) `I was in a race with at least one other motor vehicle or in a contest of speed` `the operation is on a street, road or highway or in any other public place`)
        (`s 320.22(c) the court shall consider that a person under the age of 16 years was a passenger in the conveyance` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `a person under the age of 16 years was a passenger in the conveyance I was operating`)
        (`s 320.22(d) the court shall consider that the offender was being remunerated for operating the conveyance` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `I was being remunerated for operating the conveyance`)
        (`s 320.22(e) the court shall consider that the offender’s blood alcohol concentration at the time of committing the offence was 120 mg or more` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `my blood alcohol concentration at the time of committing the offence`)
        (`s 320.22(f) the court shall consider that the offender was operating a large motor vehicle` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `I was operating a large motor vehicle`)
        (`s 320.22(g) the court shall consider that the offender was not permitted under a federal or provincial Act to operate the conveyance` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `I was not permitted, under a federal or provincial Act, to operate the conveyance`)

§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.23 to 320.25: delay of sentencing, prohibition orders, stay pending appeal`
-- Applies once you have been found guilty (and, for the stay, once an appeal is taken).

@export Under section 320.23(1), may the court delay my sentencing so that I can attend a treatment program?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section is the offence under? Type the section number as a decimal, for example 320.14 or 320.13
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is the offence under? Type it as the Code writes it, for example (1), (1)(b), (2), (3) or (4); type nothing for a section with no subsections, such as 320.17
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor consent?
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent?
      `the court has considered the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court considered the interests of justice?
      `the delay is to allow me to attend a treatment program approved by the province in which I reside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the delay to allow you to attend a treatment program approved by the province in which you live?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.23(1), may the court delay my sentencing so that I can attend a treatment program` IS
    `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` (`s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `the prosecutor consents` `I consent` `the court has considered the interests of justice` `the delay is to allow me to attend a treatment program approved by the province in which I reside`

@export Under section 320.23(1), must the court prohibit me from operating the type of conveyance before sentencing if it delays my sentencing?
GIVEN `the court delays my sentencing under subsection 320.23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court delay your sentencing under subsection 320.23(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.23(1), must the court prohibit me from operating the type of conveyance before sentencing if it delays my sentencing` IS
    `s 320.23(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question` `the court delays my sentencing under subsection 320.23(1)`

@export Under section 320.23(2), is the court relieved of imposing the minimum punishment and a prohibition order if I successfully complete the treatment program?
GIVEN `I successfully complete the treatment program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you successfully completed the treatment program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.23(2), is the court relieved of imposing the minimum punishment and a prohibition order if I successfully complete the treatment program` IS
    `s 320.23(2) the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under section 320.24` `I successfully complete the treatment program`

@export Under section 320.23(2), does the subsection bar the court from directing a discharge under section 730 if I successfully complete the treatment program?
GIVEN `I successfully complete the treatment program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you successfully completed the treatment program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.23(2), does the subsection bar the court from directing a discharge under section 730 if I successfully complete the treatment program` IS
    `s 320.23(2) this subsection bars the court from directing a discharge under section 730` `I successfully complete the treatment program`

@export Under section 320.24(1), must the court make an order prohibiting me from operating the type of conveyance in question?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section is the offence under? Type the section number as a decimal, for example 320.14 or 320.13
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is the offence under? Type it as the Code writes it, for example (1), (1)(b), (2), (3) or (4); type nothing for a section with no subsections, such as 320.17
      `I successfully complete the treatment program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you successfully completed the treatment program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(1), must the court make an order prohibiting me from operating the type of conveyance in question` IS
    `s 320.24(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` (`s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) (`s 320.23(2) the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under section 320.24` `I successfully complete the treatment program`)

@export Under section 320.24(2), what is the least and the greatest period for which the court must prohibit me from operating the type of conveyance?
GIVEN `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under section 320.15?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under the former section 253, 254 or 255 (as those sections read before section 320.26 came into force)?
GIVETH A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(2), what is the least and the greatest period for which the court must prohibit me from operating the type of conveyance` IS
    `s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` (`s 320.26 the occasion of the offence before the court` (`s 320.26 the number of earlier offences` `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force`))

@export Under section 320.24(3), for how long at most may the court prohibit me after a finding of guilt under subsection 320.14(4)?
GIVEN `I am found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(4) (a low blood drug concentration)?
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Length of time`)
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(3), for how long at most may the court prohibit me after a finding of guilt under subsection 320.14(4)` IS
    `s 320.24(3) the longest period for which the court may prohibit the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` `I am found guilty of an offence under subsection 320.14(4)`

@export Under section 320.24(4), may the court make an order prohibiting me from operating the type of conveyance after a finding of guilt of this offence?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section is the offence under? Type the section number as a decimal, for example 320.14 or 320.13
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is the offence under? Type it as the Code writes it, for example (1), (1)(b), (2), (3) or (4); type nothing for a section with no subsections, such as 320.17
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(4), may the court make an order prohibiting me from operating the type of conveyance after a finding of guilt of this offence` IS
    `s 320.24(4) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` (`s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`))

@export Under section 320.24(5), for how long may a discretionary prohibition order last?
GIVEN `the offence I was found guilty of carries imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence you were found guilty of carry imprisonment for life?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If it does not carry life, what is the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in years? (0 if none is stated)
GIVETH A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(5), for how long may a discretionary prohibition order last` IS
    `s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` imprisonment
    WHERE
        imprisonment MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the offence I was found guilty of carries imprisonment for life` THEN `imprisonment for life`
                IF `the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in years` AT MOST 0 THEN `no imprisonment is stated`
                OTHERWISE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF `the longest term of imprisonment the offence carries, in years`, 0, 0, FALSE)

@export Under section 320.24(5.1), on what day does my prohibition order take effect?
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the prohibition order made?
      `the court orders that the prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to an earlier order?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(5.1), on what day does my prohibition order take effect` IS
    `s 320.24(5.1) the day on which the prohibition order takes effect` `the day on which the order is made` `the court orders that the prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order`

@export Under section 320.24(6), has the court met its obligation to cause my prohibition order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me?
GIVEN `the court made a prohibition order under section 320.24` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court make a prohibition order under section 320.24?
      `the court caused the order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court cause the order to be read to you, or a copy of it to be given to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(6), has the court met its obligation to cause my prohibition order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me` IS
    `s 320.24(6) the court has met its obligation to cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` `the court made a prohibition order under section 320.24` `the court caused the order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me`

@export Under section 320.24(7), does the court's failure to cause my prohibition order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me affect the validity of the order?
GIVEN `the court failed to cause the order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court fail to read the order to you, or to give you a copy of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(7), does the court's failure to cause my prohibition order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me affect the validity of the order` IS
    `s 320.24(7) a failure to comply with subsection 320.24(6) affects the validity of the prohibition order` `the court failed to cause the order to be read to me or a copy to be given to me`

@export Under section 320.24(8), does my prohibition order apply to my operation of the motor vehicle in this place?
GIVEN `my prohibition order is in respect of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your prohibition order in respect of a motor vehicle?
      `the operation is on a street, road or highway or in any other public place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the operation on a street, road or highway, or in any other public place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(8), does my prohibition order apply to my operation of the motor vehicle in this place` IS
    `s 320.24(8) the prohibition order applies to the operation of the motor vehicle` (IF `my prohibition order is in respect of a motor vehicle` THEN `s 2 motor vehicle` TRUE (JUST FALSE) ELSE `s 2 motor vehicle` FALSE (JUST FALSE)) `the operation is on a street, road or highway or in any other public place`

@export Under section 320.24(9), may the court order that my prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order?
GIVEN `at the time of the offence I was subject to an order made under the Criminal Code prohibiting me from operating a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the offence, were you subject to an order made under the Criminal Code prohibiting you from operating a conveyance?
      `the new prohibition order prohibits me from operating the same type of conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the new prohibition order prohibit you from operating the same type of conveyance as the earlier order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(9), may the court order that my prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order` IS
    `s 320.24(9) the court may order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order` `at the time of the offence I was subject to an order made under the Criminal Code prohibiting me from operating a conveyance` `the new prohibition order prohibits me from operating the same type of conveyance`

@export Under section 320.24(10), am I still barred from being registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program on this day?
GIVEN `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under section 320.15?
      `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times have you earlier been convicted of an offence under the former section 253, 254 or 255 (as those sections read before section 320.26 came into force)?
      `the day on which my sentence was imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your sentence imposed?
      `the period fixed by the court, in months (0 if the court fixed none)` IS A NUMBER @desc What period, in months, did the court fix for this purpose? (0 if it fixed none)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether you can be registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.24(10), am I still barred from being registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program on this day` IS
    `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` (`s 320.26 the occasion of the offence before the court` (`s 320.26 the number of earlier offences` `the number of my earlier convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 320.15` `the number of my earlier convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force`)) `the day on which my sentence was imposed` (IF `the period fixed by the court, in months (0 if the court fixed none)` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the period fixed by the court, in months (0 if the court fixed none)`) `the day I am asking about`

@export Under section 320.25(1), may a judge stay my prohibition order pending my appeal?
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section is the offence under? Type the section number as a decimal, for example 320.14 or 320.13
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection is the offence under? Type it as the Code writes it, for example (1), (1)(b), (2), (3) or (4); type nothing for a section with no subsections, such as 320.17
      `an appeal is taken against my conviction or my sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an appeal been taken against your conviction or your sentence?
      `the judge is a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken?
      `the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada?
      `the judge is a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.25(1), may a judge stay my prohibition order pending my appeal` IS
    `s 320.25(1) a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken may direct that the prohibition order be stayed pending the appeal` (`s 320.22 the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`)) `an appeal is taken against my conviction or my sentence` `the judge is a judge of the court to which the appeal is taken` `the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada` (`s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada` `the judge is a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken`)

@export Under section 320.25(3), does imposing conditions on the stay of my prohibition order decrease the prohibition period?
GIVEN `conditions are imposed on the stay of my prohibition order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are conditions imposed on the stay of your prohibition order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.25(3), does imposing conditions on the stay of my prohibition order decrease the prohibition period` IS
    `s 320.25(3) the imposition of conditions on a stay decreases the prohibition period` `conditions are imposed on the stay of my prohibition order`

§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.27 to 320.3: demands, samples and warrants`
-- Situational: ask these only if a peace officer has made, or may make, a demand of you, or a blood sample is in question. Each asks the officer's or the justice's POWER; NOTHING means the text does not give it on these facts.

@export Under section 320.27(1)(a), may a peace officer demand that I perform the physical coordination tests and accompany the officer?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had alcohol or a drug in my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that you had alcohol or a drug in your body?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that you had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.27(1)(a), may a peace officer demand that I perform the physical coordination tests and accompany the officer` IS
    `s 320.27(1)(a) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had alcohol or a drug in my body` `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours`

@export Under section 320.27(1)(b), may a peace officer demand that I provide breath samples for an approved screening device?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had alcohol in my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that you had alcohol in your body?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that you had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours?
      `the device was an approved screening device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the device an approved screening device (designed to ascertain alcohol in the blood and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.27(1)(b), may a peace officer demand that I provide breath samples for an approved screening device` IS
    `s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had alcohol in my body` `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` (`s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` `the device was an approved screening device` `the device was an approved screening device`)

@export Under section 320.27(1)(c), may a peace officer demand that I provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had a drug in my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that you had a drug in your body?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that you had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours?
      `the equipment was approved drug screening equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the equipment approved drug screening equipment (approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.27(1)(c), may a peace officer demand that I provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment` IS
    `s 320.27(1)(c) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment and to accompany the peace officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had a drug in my body` `the officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had operated a conveyance within the preceding three hours` (`s 320.11 the equipment is approved drug screening equipment` `the equipment was approved drug screening equipment` `the equipment was approved drug screening equipment`)

@export Under section 320.27(2), may a peace officer demand breath samples from me for an approved screening device while I am operating a motor vehicle?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had an approved screening device in their possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have an approved screening device in their possession?
      `the demand was made in the course of the lawful exercise of powers under an Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature or arising at common law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand made in the course of the lawful exercise of powers under an Act of Parliament, a provincial Act or the common law?
      `I was operating a motor vehicle at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you operating a motor vehicle at the time of the demand?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.27(2), may a peace officer demand breath samples from me for an approved screening device while I am operating a motor vehicle` IS
    `s 320.27(2) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) (`s 320.11 the device is an approved screening device` `the officer had an approved screening device in their possession` `the officer had an approved screening device in their possession`) `the demand was made in the course of the lawful exercise of powers under an Act of Parliament or an Act of a provincial legislature or arising at common law` (IF `I was operating a motor vehicle at the time` THEN `s 2 motor vehicle` TRUE (JUST FALSE) ELSE `s 2 motor vehicle` FALSE (JUST FALSE))

@export Under section 320.28(1)(a)(i), may a peace officer demand that I provide breath samples for an approved instrument?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had operated a conveyance while your ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more (paragraph 320.14(1)(b))?
      `the demand was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand made as soon as practicable?
      `the instrument was an approved instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument an approved instrument (designed to analyse breath and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
      `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the technician designated by the Attorney General to operate approved instruments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(1)(a)(i), may a peace officer demand that I provide breath samples for an approved instrument` IS
    `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` `the demand was made as soon as practicable` (`s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument`) (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples`)

@export Under section 320.28(1)(a)(ii), may a peace officer demand that I provide samples of blood, when the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that, because of my physical condition, I may be incapable of providing breath or it would be impracticable to take it?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had operated a conveyance while your ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more (paragraph 320.14(1)(b))?
      `the demand was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand made as soon as practicable?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that, because of my physical condition, I might be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable to take one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that, because of your physical condition, you might be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable to take one?
      `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person taking the blood sample a qualified medical practitioner (qualified under provincial law to practise medicine)?
      `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person taking the blood sample a qualified technician (designated by the Attorney General to take blood samples)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(1)(a)(ii), may a peace officer demand that I provide samples of blood, when the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that, because of my physical condition, I may be incapable of providing breath or it would be impracticable to take it` IS
    `s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` `the demand was made as soon as practicable` `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that, because of my physical condition, I might be incapable of providing a sample of breath or it would be impracticable to take one` (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified medical practitioner`) (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples`)

@export Under section 320.28(1)(b), may a peace officer demand that I accompany the officer for the taking of samples of breath or blood?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had operated a conveyance while your ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had committed the offence of having a blood alcohol concentration of 80 mg or more (paragraph 320.14(1)(b))?
      `the demand was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand made as soon as practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(1)(b), may a peace officer demand that I accompany the officer for the taking of samples of breath or blood` IS
    `s 320.28(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to accompany the peace officer for the purpose of taking samples of breath or blood` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by alcohol` `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(b)` `the demand was made as soon as practicable`

@export Under section 320.28(2)(a), may a peace officer demand that I submit to an evaluation by an evaluating officer?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had operated a conveyance while your ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)?
      `the demand was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand made as soon as practicable?
      `the officer was an evaluating officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the officer an evaluating officer (a peace officer with the qualifications that the regulations require)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(2)(a), may a peace officer demand that I submit to an evaluation by an evaluating officer` IS
    `s 320.28(2)(a) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to submit to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer and to accompany the peace officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)` `the demand was made as soon as practicable` (`s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the officer was an evaluating officer`) `the officer was an evaluating officer`)

@export Under section 320.28(2)(b), may a peace officer demand that I provide samples of blood for a drug analysis?
GIVEN `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the demand a police officer or other peace officer?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had operated a conveyance while your ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug?
      `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer have reasonable grounds to believe that you had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)?
      `the demand was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand made as soon as practicable?
      `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person taking the blood sample a qualified medical practitioner (qualified under provincial law to practise medicine)?
      `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person taking the blood sample a qualified technician (designated by the Attorney General to take blood samples)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(2)(b), may a peace officer demand that I provide samples of blood for a drug analysis` IS
    `s 320.28(2)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood and to accompany the peace officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the person who made the demand was a police officer or other peace officer`) `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had operated a conveyance while my ability to operate it was impaired to any degree by a drug or by a combination of alcohol and a drug` `the officer had reasonable grounds to believe that I had committed an offence under paragraph 320.14(1)(c) or (d) or subsection 320.14(4)` `the demand was made as soon as practicable` (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified medical practitioner`) (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples`)

@export Under section 320.28(3), may an evaluating officer demand that I provide breath samples for an approved instrument?
GIVEN `the officer was an evaluating officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the officer an evaluating officer (a peace officer with the qualifications that the regulations require)?
      `the evaluating officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had alcohol in my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the evaluating officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that you had alcohol in your body?
      `a demand was not made under subsection 320.28(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a demand not made under subsection 320.28(1)?
      `the demand was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand made as soon as practicable?
      `the instrument was an approved instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument an approved instrument (designed to analyse breath and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
      `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the technician designated by the Attorney General to operate approved instruments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(3), may an evaluating officer demand that I provide breath samples for an approved instrument` IS
    `s 320.28(3) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (`s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the officer was an evaluating officer`) `the officer was an evaluating officer`) `the evaluating officer had reasonable grounds to suspect that I had alcohol in my body` `a demand was not made under subsection 320.28(1)` `the demand was made as soon as practicable` (`s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument`) (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples`)

@export Under section 320.28(4), must the evaluating officer identify the type or types of drugs impairing me?
GIVEN `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer had reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the listed types of drugs, or a combination of alcohol and one of them, was impairing my ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On completion of the evaluation, did the evaluating officer have reasonable grounds to believe that a drug of a type listed in subsection 320.28(5), or a combination of alcohol and such a drug, was impairing your ability to operate a conveyance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(4), must the evaluating officer identify the type or types of drugs impairing me` IS
    `s 320.28(4) the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question` `on completion of the evaluation, the evaluating officer had reasonable grounds to believe that one or more of the listed types of drugs, or a combination of alcohol and one of them, was impairing my ability to operate a conveyance`

