-- Any answer other than the seven types and "other" is read as "other": the types are the seven the text lists (fork F12 in NOTES.md).
@export Under section 320.28(5), is this type of drug one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)?
GIVEN `the type of drug` IS A STRING @desc What type of drug? Answer exactly one of: depressant, inhalant, dissociative anaesthetic, cannabis, stimulant, hallucinogen, narcotic analgesic, other
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(5), is this type of drug one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` IS
    `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` kind
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the type of drug` EQUALS "depressant" THEN `s 320.28(5)(a) a depressant`
                IF `the type of drug` EQUALS "inhalant" THEN `s 320.28(5)(b) an inhalant`
                IF `the type of drug` EQUALS "dissociative anaesthetic" THEN `s 320.28(5)(c) a dissociative anaesthetic`
                IF `the type of drug` EQUALS "cannabis" THEN `s 320.28(5)(d) cannabis`
                IF `the type of drug` EQUALS "stimulant" THEN `s 320.28(5)(e) a stimulant`
                IF `the type of drug` EQUALS "hallucinogen" THEN `s 320.28(5)(f) a hallucinogen`
                IF `the type of drug` EQUALS "narcotic analgesic" THEN `s 320.28(5)(g) a narcotic analgesic`
                OTHERWISE `s 320.28(5) a type of drug that is none of those`

@export Under section 320.28(6), may a sample of my blood be taken under section 320.28?
GIVEN `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person taking the blood sample a qualified medical practitioner (qualified under provincial law to practise medicine)?
      `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person taking the blood sample a qualified technician (designated by the Attorney General to take blood samples)?
      `the person taking the sample was satisfied that taking it would not endanger my health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person taking the blood sample satisfied that taking it would not endanger your health?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(6), may a sample of my blood be taken under section 320.28` IS
    `s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified medical practitioner`) (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples` `the person taking the blood sample was a qualified technician for blood samples`) `the person taking the sample was satisfied that taking it would not endanger my health`

@export Under section 320.28(7), has the duty to receive my blood sample into an approved container and to seal it been met?
GIVEN `the sample was received into an approved container` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the blood sample received into an approved container (designed for blood samples and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
      `the container was subsequently sealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the container subsequently sealed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(7), has the duty to receive my blood sample into an approved container and to seal it been met` IS
    `s 320.28(7) the duty to receive the sample of blood into an approved container and to seal it has been met` (`s 320.11 the container is an approved container` `the sample was received into an approved container` `the sample was received into an approved container`) `the container was subsequently sealed`

@export Under section 320.28(8), has the duty to cause one of my blood samples to be retained for me been met?
GIVEN `samples of my blood were taken under section 320.28` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were samples of your blood taken under section 320.28?
      `one of the samples was retained for analysis by or on behalf of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was one of the samples retained for analysis by or on behalf of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(8), has the duty to cause one of my blood samples to be retained for me been met` IS
    `s 320.28(8) the duty to cause one of the samples to be retained has been met` `samples of my blood were taken under section 320.28` `one of the samples was retained for analysis by or on behalf of me`

@export Under section 320.28(9), does a failure to put my blood sample in an approved container and seal it, or to retain one for me, by itself affect the validity of the taking or the analysis?
GIVEN `there was a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a failure to put the sample in an approved container and seal it, or to retain one for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(9), does a failure to put my blood sample in an approved container and seal it, or to retain one for me, by itself affect the validity of the taking or the analysis` IS
    `s 320.28(9) a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8) by itself affects the validity of the taking of the sample or of an analysis made of it` `there was a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8)`

@export Under section 320.28(10), must the judge order the release of the retained sample of my blood to me?
GIVEN `my application is a summary application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application a summary application by the person from whom the blood samples were taken?
      `a sample was retained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a sample retained?
      `the day on which the samples were taken` IS A DATE @desc On what day were your blood samples taken?
      `the day on which I make the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make (or did you make) the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.28(10), must the judge order the release of the retained sample of my blood to me` IS
    `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` `my application is a summary application` `a sample was retained` `the day on which the samples were taken` `the day on which I make the application`

@export Under section 320.29(1), may a justice issue a warrant for samples of my blood?
GIVEN `the person who issues the warrant is a justice of the peace or a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person issuing the warrant a justice of the peace or a provincial court judge?
      `the justice is satisfied, on an information on oath in Form 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice satisfied, on an information on oath in Form 1, of the matters in paragraphs 320.29(1)(a) to (c)?
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that I operated a conveyance within the preceding eight hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that you operated a conveyance within the preceding eight hours?
      `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to me or another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conveyance involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to you or another person?
      `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conveyance involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person?
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that I have alcohol or a drug in my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to suspect that you have alcohol or a drug in your body?
      `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that, by reason of a physical or mental condition, I am unable to consent to the taking of samples of my blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a qualified medical practitioner of the opinion that, because of a physical or mental condition, you are unable to consent to the taking of samples of your blood?
      `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that the taking of samples of my blood will not endanger my health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a qualified medical practitioner of the opinion that taking the samples will not endanger your health?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.29(1), may a justice issue a warrant for samples of my blood` IS
    `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (IF `the person who issues the warrant is a justice of the peace or a provincial court judge` THEN `s 2 justice` `a justice of the peace` ELSE `s 2 justice` `a judicial officer who is none of those`) `the justice is satisfied, on an information on oath in Form 1` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that I operated a conveyance within the preceding eight hours` (`s 2 bodily harm` `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to me or another person` `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to me or another person` `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in bodily harm to me or another person`) `the conveyance was involved in an accident that resulted in the death of another person` `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that I have alcohol or a drug in my body` `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that, by reason of a physical or mental condition, I am unable to consent to the taking of samples of my blood` `a qualified medical practitioner is of the opinion that the taking of samples of my blood will not endanger my health`

@export Under section 320.29(4), may samples of my blood be taken under the warrant at this time?
GIVEN `a qualified medical practitioner is satisfied that the conditions in subparagraphs 320.29(1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a qualified medical practitioner satisfied that the conditions in subparagraphs 320.29(1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.29(4), may samples of my blood be taken under the warrant at this time` IS
    `s 320.29(4) samples of blood may be taken from the person under the warrant at this time` `a qualified medical practitioner is satisfied that the conditions in subparagraphs 320.29(1)(c)(i) and (ii) continue to exist`

@export Under section 320.29(5), must the peace officer give me a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1?
GIVEN `the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the warrant been executed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.29(5), must the peace officer give me a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1` IS
    `s 320.29(5) the peace officer shall give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken` `the warrant is executed`

@export Under section 320.3, may the samples of my blood be analyzed for blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration?
GIVEN `the samples of my blood were taken for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the samples of your blood taken for the purposes of this Part of the Criminal Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.3, may the samples of my blood be analyzed for blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration` IS
    `s 320.3 the samples may be analyzed to determine the person’s blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration, or both` `the samples of my blood were taken for the purposes of this Part`

§ `Part VIII.1 -- sections 320.31 to 320.35: evidence`
-- Asks what the evidence rules say about the results of the tests, the certificates, disclosure and the presumption that you were operating the conveyance. Situational: ask these once tests were done or you are charged.

@export Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration?
GIVEN `the instrument was an approved instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument an approved instrument (designed to analyse breath and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
      `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the technician designated by the Attorney General to operate approved instruments?
      `the result of the system blank test, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the system blank test run before each breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the result of the system calibration check, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the system calibration check run before each breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the alcohol standard was certified by an analyst` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the alcohol standard certified by an analyst (a person designated by the Attorney General)?
      `the number of minutes between the times when the two breath samples were taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes were there between the times when your two breath samples were taken?
      `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the analysis of your first breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the analysis of your second breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(1), are the results of my breath tests conclusive proof of my blood alcohol concentration` IS
    `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (`s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument`) (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples`) `the result of the system blank test, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` `the result of the system calibration check, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` `the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` (`s 320.11 the person is an analyst` FALSE FALSE `the alcohol standard was certified by an analyst` FALSE) `the number of minutes between the times when the two breath samples were taken` `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`

@export Under section 320.31(1), what blood alcohol concentration do the results of my breath tests conclusively prove?
GIVEN `the instrument was an approved instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument an approved instrument (designed to analyse breath and approved by the Attorney General of Canada)?
      `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the technician designated by the Attorney General to operate approved instruments?
      `the result of the system blank test, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the system blank test run before each breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the result of the system calibration check, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the system calibration check run before each breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the alcohol standard was certified by an analyst` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the alcohol standard certified by an analyst (a person designated by the Attorney General)?
      `the number of minutes between the times when the two breath samples were taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes were there between the times when your two breath samples were taken?
      `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the analysis of your first breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
      `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the result of the analysis of your second breath sample, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(1), what blood alcohol concentration do the results of my breath tests conclusively prove` IS
    `s 320.31(1) the blood alcohol concentration that the results are conclusive proof of, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` (`s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (`s 320.11 the instrument is an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument` `the instrument was an approved instrument`) (`s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of breath samples` `the technician was a qualified technician for breath samples`) `the result of the system blank test, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` `the result of the system calibration check, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` `the target value of the alcohol standard, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` (`s 320.11 the person is an analyst` FALSE FALSE `the alcohol standard was certified by an analyst` FALSE) `the number of minutes between the times when the two breath samples were taken` `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`) `the result of the first analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` `the result of the second analysis, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood`

@export Under section 320.31(2), is the result of the analysis of my blood sample proof of my concentration at the time the sample was taken?
GIVEN `the analysis was made by an analyst` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the analysis of your blood sample made by an analyst (a person designated by the Attorney General)?
      `there is evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(2), is the result of the analysis of my blood sample proof of my concentration at the time the sample was taken` IS
    `s 320.31(2) the result of the analysis of the blood sample is proof of the person’s concentration at the time the sample was taken` (`s 320.11 the person is an analyst` FALSE FALSE `the analysis was made by an analyst` FALSE) `there is evidence tending to show that the analysis was performed improperly`

-- Any answer other than the three listed kinds is read as "any other evidence", which the subsection does not address.
@export Under section 320.31(3), does this evidence tend to show that the analysis of my blood sample was performed improperly?
GIVEN `the kind of evidence` IS A STRING @desc What kind of evidence? Answer exactly one of: the amount of alcohol or a drug I consumed, the rate at which it would have been absorbed or eliminated, a calculation based on those, any other evidence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(3), does this evidence tend to show that the analysis of my blood sample was performed improperly` IS
    `s 320.31(3) the evidence constitutes evidence tending to show that the analysis of the blood sample was performed improperly` kind
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of evidence` EQUALS "the amount of alcohol or a drug I consumed" THEN `s 320.31(3)(a) evidence of the amount of alcohol or a drug that they consumed`
                IF `the kind of evidence` EQUALS "the rate at which it would have been absorbed or eliminated" THEN `s 320.31(3)(b) evidence of the rate at which the alcohol or the drug would have been absorbed or eliminated by their body`
                IF `the kind of evidence` EQUALS "a calculation based on those" THEN `s 320.31(3)(c) a calculation based on the evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of what their blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration would have been at the time the sample was taken`
                OTHERWISE `s 320.31(3) evidence of any other kind`

@export Under section 320.31(4), what blood alcohol concentration am I conclusively presumed to have had within two hours after I stopped operating the conveyance?
GIVEN `how many minutes after I stopped operating it the first breath sample, or the blood sample, was taken` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes after you stopped operating the conveyance was the first breath sample, or the blood sample, taken?
      `my blood alcohol concentration` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your blood alcohol concentration, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood, from the analysis of your breath or blood? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(4), what blood alcohol concentration am I conclusively presumed to have had within two hours after I stopped operating the conveyance` IS
    `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` `how many minutes after I stopped operating it the first breath sample, or the blood sample, was taken` `my blood alcohol concentration`

@export Under section 320.31(5), is the evaluating officer's opinion admissible without qualifying the officer as an expert?
GIVEN `the officer was an evaluating officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the officer an evaluating officer (a peace officer with the qualifications that the regulations require)?
      `the opinion relates to the impairment, by a type of drug that the evaluating officer identified, or by that drug and alcohol, of my ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the evaluating officer’s opinion relate to the impairment, by a type of drug the officer identified (or by that drug and alcohol), of your ability to operate a conveyance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(5), is the evaluating officer's opinion admissible without qualifying the officer as an expert` IS
    `s 320.31(5) the evaluating officer’s opinion is admissible in evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert` (`s 320.11 the person is an evaluating officer` (`Under section 2, helper: a peace officer, as I state it` `the officer was an evaluating officer`) `the officer was an evaluating officer`) `the opinion relates to the impairment, by a type of drug that the evaluating officer identified, or by that drug and alcohol, of my ability to operate a conveyance`

@export Under section 320.31(6), is the drug presumed to have been in my body at the time I operated the conveyance?
GIVEN `the analysis of my sample demonstrates that I have a drug in my body of a type that the evaluating officer identified as impairing my ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the analysis of the sample you provided under subsection 320.28(4) show that you have a drug in your body of a type that the evaluating officer identified as impairing your ability to operate a conveyance?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(6), is the drug presumed to have been in my body at the time I operated the conveyance` IS
    `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been present in the person’s body at the time when the person operated the conveyance` `the analysis of my sample demonstrates that I have a drug in my body of a type that the evaluating officer identified as impairing my ability to operate a conveyance` `there is evidence to the contrary`

@export Under section 320.31(6), is the drug presumed to have been the cause of my impairment?
GIVEN `the analysis of my sample demonstrates that I have a drug in my body of a type that the evaluating officer identified as impairing my ability to operate a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the analysis of the sample you provided under subsection 320.28(4) show that you have a drug in your body of a type that the evaluating officer identified as impairing your ability to operate a conveyance?
      `my impairment is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your impairment proved?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.31(6), is the drug presumed to have been the cause of my impairment` IS
    `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been the cause of the person’s impairment` `the analysis of my sample demonstrates that I have a drug in my body of a type that the evaluating officer identified as impairing my ability to operate a conveyance` `my impairment is proved` `there is evidence to the contrary`

@export Under section 320.31(7), may the result of the analysis of a sample I was not required to provide be admitted even though I was not warned?
