    `s 320.35 the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance` `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 320.14 or 320.15` `it is proved that I occupied the seat or position ordinarily occupied by a person who operates a conveyance` `I establish that I did not occupy that seat or position for the purpose of setting the conveyance in motion`

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.36: use of my samples and results`
-- Situational: ask these once a bodily substance was taken from you or the results of a test were made.

@export Under section 320.36(1), is the use of my bodily substance prohibited?
GIVEN `the bodily substance was obtained under Part VIII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the bodily substance obtained under this Part of the Criminal Code?
      `the use is for a purpose other than an analysis under Part VIII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use for a purpose other than an analysis under this Part of the Criminal Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.36(1), is the use of my bodily substance prohibited` IS
    `s 320.36(1) the use of the bodily substance is prohibited` `the bodily substance was obtained under Part VIII.1` `the use is for a purpose other than an analysis under Part VIII.1`

@export Under section 320.36(2), is the use or disclosure of the results of my tests prohibited?
GIVEN `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the results obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance?
      `the person uses, discloses or allows the disclosure of the results` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results?
      `it is for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs or alcohol or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs or alcohol or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment?
      `the disclosure is to the person to whom the results relate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure to the person to whom the results relate?
      `the results are made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the results made anonymous?
      `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made for statistical or research purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.36(2), is the use or disclosure of the results of my tests prohibited` IS
    `s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` `the person uses, discloses or allows the disclosure of the results` `it is for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs or alcohol or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment` (`s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` `the disclosure is to the person to whom the results relate` `the results are made anonymous` `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes`)

@export Under section 320.36(3), may the results of my tests be disclosed?
GIVEN `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the results obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance?
      `the disclosure is to the person to whom the results relate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure to the person to whom the results relate?
      `the results are made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the results made anonymous?
      `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made for statistical or research purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.36(3), may the results of my tests be disclosed` IS
    `s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` `the disclosure is to the person to whom the results relate` `the results are made anonymous` `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes`

-- The punishment of this offence (an offence punishable on summary conviction; section 787(1) gives the penalty) has no question of its own: the class and the penalty are layer-1 rules (s 320.36(4) the class of the offence; s 320.36(4) the punishment ...).
@export Under section 320.36(4), have I committed the offence of contravening subsection 320.36(1) or (2)?
GIVEN `the bodily substance was obtained under Part VIII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the bodily substance obtained under this Part of the Criminal Code?
      `the use is for a purpose other than an analysis under Part VIII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use for a purpose other than an analysis under this Part of the Criminal Code?
      `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the results obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance?
      `the person uses, discloses or allows the disclosure of the results` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results?
      `it is for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs or alcohol or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs or alcohol or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment?
      `the disclosure is to the person to whom the results relate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure to the person to whom the results relate?
      `the results are made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the results made anonymous?
      `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made for statistical or research purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 320.36(4), have I committed the offence of contravening subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` IS
    `s 320.36(4) everyone commits an offence who contravenes subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` (`s 320.36(1) the use of the bodily substance is prohibited` `the bodily substance was obtained under Part VIII.1` `the use is for a purpose other than an analysis under Part VIII.1`) (`s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` `the person uses, discloses or allows the disclosure of the results` `it is for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs or alcohol or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment` (`s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` `the results were obtained under Part VIII.1 of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` `the disclosure is to the person to whom the results relate` `the results are made anonymous` `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes`))

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc12 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc12-seat.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part IX (Offences Against Rights of Property, ss 321 to 378) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is
-- an offence, what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply, and what follows from a conviction. (Assumed, not ruled:
-- Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer asks the questions Part IX answers for that person. Every question is named "Under section N, ..." so that no two parts' questions share a name,
-- takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a choice from a list), each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked, and calls the layer-1 rule of the
-- same provision (ccc12-part9-*.l4) by NAMED arguments; it never restates a rule. A section 2 term (property, motor vehicle, steal ...) is asked as a fact;
-- where the keel's `ccc-definitions` can work the term out from facts the person can state, it does (`s 2 motor vehicle`, `s 2 steal`).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (details in NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)"): JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's own no,
-- in the words the layer-1 comment quotes (for a flat negative such as "does not commit theft by pledging ...", JUST FALSE means exactly that: no); NOTHING means the text
-- does not answer on these facts (not "no"). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- A punishment question answers with the LIST of limbs the section states (one per mode of proceeding). Where a limb says only "an offence punishable on summary conviction", its
-- penalty is the general penalty of section 787(1), which is outside Part IX and outside the sources: the person (or the form) supplies the two figures it states, and this layer
-- never supplies a number of its own.
-- Exceptions and presumptions are asked as questions of their own beside the offence they qualify (E1 option C: per-section answers); an offence question does not fold them in.
-- A "Have you committed theft (section 322)?" input is the answer the person has from the question under section 322.

§ `Part IX Offences Against Rights of Property -- the accused's questions`

-- The general penalty of section 787(1), as the person states it: a Punishment on summary conviction with the greatest fine and the longest term of imprisonment (in months) given. Not a provision of Part IX.
GIVEN `the greatest fine, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the longest term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Punishment
`ccc12 seat the general penalty of s 787(1) as the person states it` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, `the longest term of imprisonment, in months`, 0, FALSE)
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` `the greatest fine, in dollars`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 321 -- what the words of Part IX mean`
-- Definitions "In this Part": asked because other questions turn on them (break, credit card, document, false document, paper).

@export Under section 321, did I "break" something?
GIVEN `Did you break any part of a thing, inside or outside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you break any part of a thing, inside or outside?
      `Did you open a thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an opening, inside or outside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you open a thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an opening, inside or outside?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 321, did I "break" something` IS
    `s 321 the person breaks` WITH
        `the person broke any part, internal or external` IS `Did you break any part of a thing, inside or outside`
        `the person opened a thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an internal or external opening` IS `Did you open a thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an opening, inside or outside`

@export Under section 321, is the thing a credit card?
GIVEN `Is it a card, plate, coupon book or other device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a card, plate, coupon book or other device?
      `Was it issued or otherwise distributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued or otherwise distributed?
      `Was it issued for use, on presentation, to obtain on credit money, goods, services or any other thing of value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued for use, on presentation, to obtain on credit money, goods, services or any other thing of value?
      `Was it issued for use in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain its services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued for use in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain its services?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 321, is the thing a credit card` IS
    `s 321 the thing is a credit card` WITH
        `it is a card, plate, coupon book or other device` IS `Is it a card, plate, coupon book or other device`
        `it was issued or otherwise distributed` IS `Was it issued or otherwise distributed`
        `the purpose is that it be used on presentation to obtain, on credit, money, goods, services or any other thing of value` IS `Was it issued for use, on presentation, to obtain on credit money, goods, services or any other thing of value`
        `the purpose is that it be used in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain any of the services offered through the machine, unit or device` IS `Was it issued for use in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain its services`

@export Under section 321, is the thing a document?
GIVEN `Is it paper, parchment or other material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paper, parchment or other material?
      `Is anything recorded or marked on it that a person, a computer system or another device can read or understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anything recorded or marked on it that a person, a computer system or another device can read or understand?
      `Is it a credit card (see section 321)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit card (see section 321)?
      `Is it a trademark on an article of commerce, or an inscription on stone or metal or other like material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a trademark on an article of commerce, or an inscription on stone or metal or other like material?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 321, is the thing a document` IS
    `s 321 the thing is a document` WITH
        `it is paper, parchment or other material` IS `Is it paper, parchment or other material`
        `anything capable of being read or understood by a person, computer system or other device is recorded or marked on it` IS `Is anything recorded or marked on it that a person, a computer system or another device can read or understand`
        `it is a credit card, by s 321 the thing is a credit card` IS (JUST `Is it a credit card (see section 321)`)
        `it is a trademark on an article of commerce, or an inscription on stone or metal or other like material` IS `Is it a trademark on an article of commerce, or an inscription on stone or metal or other like material`

@export Under section 321, is the thing an exchequer bill?
GIVEN `What is it: a bank-note, a bond, a note, a debenture, a security, or an instrument of another kind` IS A `s 321 exchequer bill kind` @desc What is it: a bank-note, a bond, a note, a debenture, a security, or an instrument of another kind?
      `Is it issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 321, is the thing an exchequer bill` IS
    `s 321 the thing is an exchequer bill` WITH
        `kind` IS `What is it: a bank-note, a bond, a note, a debenture, a security, or an instrument of another kind`
        `it is issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province` IS `Is it issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province`

@export Under section 321, is the paper exchequer bill paper?
GIVEN `Is it paper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paper?
      `Is it used to manufacture exchequer bills` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used to manufacture exchequer bills?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 321, is the paper exchequer bill paper` IS
    `s 321 the paper is exchequer bill paper` WITH
        `it is paper` IS `Is it paper`
        `it is used to manufacture exchequer bills` IS `Is it used to manufacture exchequer bills`

@export Under section 321, is the document a false document?
GIVEN `Is it a document (see section 321)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a document (see section 321)?
      `Does the whole or a material part of it purport to be made by or on behalf of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the whole or a material part of it purport to be made by or on behalf of a person?
      `Is that person one who did not make it or authorize it to be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person one who did not make it or authorize it to be made?
      `Is that person one who did not in fact exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person one who did not in fact exist?
      `Is it made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it?
      `Is it false in some material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it false in some material particular?
      `Is it made in the name of an existing person, by that person or under their authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made in the name of an existing person, by that person or under their authority?
      `Is it made with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 321, is the document a false document` IS
    `s 321 the document is a false document` WITH
        `it is a document, by s 321 the thing is a document` IS (JUST `Is it a document (see section 321)`)
        `the whole or a material part of it purports to be made by or on behalf of a person` IS `Does the whole or a material part of it purport to be made by or on behalf of a person`
        `that person did not make it or authorize it to be made` IS `Is that person one who did not make it or authorize it to be made`
        `that person did not in fact exist` IS `Is that person one who did not in fact exist`
        `it is made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it` IS `Is it made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it`
        `it is false in some material particular` IS `Is it false in some material particular`
        `it is made in the name of an existing person, by him or under his authority` IS `Is it made in the name of an existing person, by that person or under their authority`
        `it is made with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made` IS `Is it made with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made`

@export Under section 321, is the paper revenue paper?
GIVEN `Is it paper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paper?
      `Is it used to make stamps, licences or permits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used to make stamps, licences or permits?
      `Is it used for a purpose connected with the public revenue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used for a purpose connected with the public revenue?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 321, is the paper revenue paper` IS
    `s 321 the paper is revenue paper` WITH
        `it is paper` IS `Is it paper`
        `it is used to make stamps, licences or permits` IS `Is it used to make stamps, licences or permits`
        `it is used for a purpose connected with the public revenue` IS `Is it used for a purpose connected with the public revenue`


§ `Sections 322 to 334.1 -- theft`
-- Theft and its penalties. The questions on forfeiture (327(2), (3), 333.2(4), (5)) and on the court's duties (333.11, 334.1) arise only after a charge or a conviction: ask "Have I been convicted?" before showing them.

-- Section 322(1) and (2) are two routes to theft (fork F-322-2): the answer is the layer-1 rule `s 322 the person commits theft`, which joins them.
@export Under section 322, have I committed theft?
GIVEN `Did you fraudulently and without colour of right take anything, animate or inanimate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fraudulently and without colour of right take anything, animate or inanimate?
      `Did you fraudulently and without colour of right convert anything, animate or inanimate, to your use or to the use of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fraudulently and without colour of right convert anything, animate or inanimate, to your use or to the use of another person?
      `Did you intend to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of their property or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of their property or interest in it?
      `Did you intend to pledge it or deposit it as security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to pledge it or deposit it as security?
      `Did you intend to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that you may be unable to perform` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that you may be unable to perform?
      `Did you intend to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was when it was taken or converted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was when it was taken or converted?
      `Did you have intent to steal anything` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have intent to steal anything?
      `Did you move it, cause it to move or to be moved, or begin to cause it to become movable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you move it, cause it to move or to be moved, or begin to cause it to become movable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 322, have I committed theft` IS
    `s 322 the person commits theft` `route (1)` `route (2)`
    WHERE
        `route (1)` MEANS
            `s 322(1) the person commits theft` WITH
                `the person fraudulently and without colour of right took anything, whether animate or inanimate` IS `Did you fraudulently and without colour of right take anything, animate or inanimate`
                `the person fraudulently and without colour of right converted anything, whether animate or inanimate, to their use or to the use of another person` IS `Did you fraudulently and without colour of right convert anything, animate or inanimate, to your use or to the use of another person`
                `the intent was to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of their property or interest in it` IS `Did you intend to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of their property or interest in it`
                `the intent was to pledge it or deposit it as security` IS `Did you intend to pledge it or deposit it as security`
                `the intent was to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that the person who parts with it may be unable to perform` IS `Did you intend to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that you may be unable to perform`
                `the intent was to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was at the time it was taken or converted` IS `Did you intend to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was when it was taken or converted`
        `route (2)` MEANS
            `s 322(2) the person commits theft by moving the thing` WITH
                `the person has intent to steal anything` IS `Did you have intent to steal anything`
                `the person moves it or causes it to move or to be moved, or begins to cause it to become movable` IS `Did you move it, cause it to move or to be moved, or begin to cause it to become movable`

@export Under section 322(3), does taking the thing openly stop my taking from being fraudulent?
GIVEN `Did you take or convert it without secrecy and without any attempt at concealment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take or convert it without secrecy and without any attempt at concealment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 322(3), does taking the thing openly stop my taking from being fraudulent` IS
    `s 322(3) the absence of secrecy prevents the taking or conversion from being fraudulent` WITH
        `the taking or conversion was effected without secrecy or attempt at concealment` IS `Did you take or convert it without secrecy and without any attempt at concealment`

@export Under section 322(4), does it matter whether the thing I converted was taken for the purpose of conversion, or was in my lawful possession when I converted it?
GIVEN `Which question is it: whether the thing converted is taken for the purpose of conversion, whether it was in your lawful possession when you converted it, or another question` IS A `s 322(4) question` @desc Which question is it: whether the thing converted is taken for the purpose of conversion, whether it was in your lawful possession when you converted it, or another question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 322(4), does it matter whether the thing I converted was taken for the purpose of conversion, or was in my lawful possession when I converted it` IS
    `s 322(4) the question is material` WITH
        `question` IS `Which question is it: whether the thing converted is taken for the purpose of conversion, whether it was in your lawful possession when you converted it, or another question`

@export Under section 322(5), am I deemed to have a special property or interest in a wild living creature that I keep in captivity?
GIVEN `Do you have a wild living creature in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a wild living creature in captivity?
      `Is it in captivity now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in captivity now?
      `Has it escaped from captivity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it escaped from captivity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 322(5), am I deemed to have a special property or interest in a wild living creature that I keep in captivity` IS
    `s 322(5) the person is deemed to have a special property or interest in the creature` WITH
        `the person has a wild living creature in captivity` IS `Do you have a wild living creature in captivity`
        `the creature is in captivity` IS `Is it in captivity now`
        `the creature has escaped from captivity` IS `Has it escaped from captivity`

@export Under section 323(1), is the owner of marked oyster beds deemed to have a special property or interest in the oysters in them?
GIVEN `Are the oysters and oyster brood in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the oysters and oyster brood in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of a person?
      `Are the beds, layings or fisheries sufficiently marked out or known as that person's property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the beds, layings or fisheries sufficiently marked out or known as that person's property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 323(1), is the owner of marked oyster beds deemed to have a special property or interest in the oysters in them` IS
    `s 323(1) the person is deemed to have a special property or interest in the oysters and oyster brood` WITH
        `oysters and oyster brood are in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of any person` IS `Are the oysters and oyster brood in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of a person`
        `the oyster beds, layings or fisheries are sufficiently marked out or known as the property of that person` IS `Are the beds, layings or fisheries sufficiently marked out or known as that person's property`

@export Under section 323(2), is the indictment against me sufficient though it does not say in which territorial division the oyster bed lies?
GIVEN `Does the indictment describe the oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the indictment describe the oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 323(2), is the indictment against me sufficient though it does not say in which territorial division the oyster bed lies` IS
    `s 323(2) the indictment is sufficient` WITH
        `the indictment describes an oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way` IS `Does the indictment describe the oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way`

@export Under section 324, did I steal what I held as a bailee under a lawful seizure?
GIVEN `Were you a bailee of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a bailee of the thing?
      `Was it under lawful seizure in the execution of the duties of the seizing officer's office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it under lawful seizure in the execution of the duties of the seizing officer's office?
      `Was the seizing officer a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the seizing officer a peace officer?
      `Was the seizing officer a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the seizing officer a public officer?
      `Were you obliged by law or agreement to produce and deliver it to that officer or to another person entitled to it at a certain time and place, or on demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you obliged by law or agreement to produce and deliver it to that officer or to another person entitled to it at a certain time and place, or on demand?
      `Did you fail to produce and deliver it in accordance with your obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to produce and deliver it in accordance with your obligation?
      `Was your failure the result of a wilful act or omission by you` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your failure the result of a wilful act or omission by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 324, did I steal what I held as a bailee under a lawful seizure` IS
    `s 324 the bailee steals the thing under seizure` WITH
        `the person is a bailee of anything` IS `Were you a bailee of the thing`
        `the thing is under lawful seizure in the execution of the duties of the office of the seizing officer` IS `Was it under lawful seizure in the execution of the duties of the seizing officer's office`
        `the seizing officer is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS (JUST `Was the seizing officer a peace officer`)
        `the seizing officer is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS (JUST `Was the seizing officer a public officer`)
        `the person is obliged by law or agreement to produce and deliver it to that officer or to another person entitled thereto at a certain time and place, or on demand` IS `Were you obliged by law or agreement to produce and deliver it to that officer or to another person entitled to it at a certain time and place, or on demand`
        `the person did not produce and deliver it in accordance with the obligation` IS `Did you fail to produce and deliver it in accordance with your obligation`
        `the failure to produce and deliver it is the result of a wilful act or omission by the person` IS `Was your failure the result of a wilful act or omission by you`

-- JUST FALSE here is the text's no: a factor or agent "does not commit theft" by a pledge within the limit. A larger pledge is NOTHING: the section says nothing of it.
@export Under section 325, do I commit theft by pledging or giving a lien on goods or documents of title that were entrusted to me?
GIVEN `Are you a factor or an agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a factor or an agent?
      `Were the goods or documents of title to goods entrusted to you for the purpose of sale or for any other purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the goods or documents of title to goods entrusted to you for the purpose of sale or for any other purpose?
      `Did you pledge them or give a lien on them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pledge them or give a lien on them?
      `For how many dollars was the pledge or lien given` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many dollars was the pledge or lien given?
      `How many dollars did your principal owe you when the goods or documents were pledged or the lien was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dollars did your principal owe you when the goods or documents were pledged or the lien was given?
      `What is the total, in dollars, of any bill of exchange that you accepted for or on account of your principal` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total, in dollars, of any bill of exchange that you accepted for or on account of your principal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 325, do I commit theft by pledging or giving a lien on goods or documents of title that were entrusted to me` IS
    `s 325 the factor or agent commits theft by pledging or giving a lien on goods or documents of title to goods` WITH
        `the person is a factor or an agent` IS `Are you a factor or an agent`
        `the goods or documents of title to goods are entrusted to the person for the purpose of sale or for any other purpose` IS `Were the goods or documents of title to goods entrusted to you for the purpose of sale or for any other purpose`
        `the person pledges them or gives a lien on them` IS `Did you pledge them or give a lien on them`
        `the amount for which the pledge or lien is given, in dollars` IS `For how many dollars was the pledge or lien given`
        `the amount due to the person from the principal at the time the goods or documents are pledged or the lien is given, in dollars` IS `How many dollars did your principal owe you when the goods or documents were pledged or the lien was given`
        `the amount of any bill of exchange that the person has accepted for or on account of the principal, in dollars` IS `What is the total, in dollars, of any bill of exchange that you accepted for or on account of your principal`

@export Under section 326(1), have I committed theft of electricity, gas or a telecommunication service?
GIVEN `Did you act fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act fraudulently?
      `Did you act maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act maliciously?
      `Did you act without colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without colour of right?
      `Did you abstract, consume or use electricity or gas, or cause it to be wasted or diverted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abstract, consume or use electricity or gas, or cause it to be wasted or diverted?
      `Did you use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 326(1), have I committed theft of electricity, gas or a telecommunication service` IS
    `s 326(1) the person commits theft of electricity, gas or a telecommunication service` WITH
        `the person acted fraudulently` IS `Did you act fraudulently`
        `the person acted maliciously` IS `Did you act maliciously`
        `the person acted without colour of right` IS `Did you act without colour of right`
        `the person abstracts, consumes or uses electricity or gas or causes it to be wasted or diverted` IS `Did you abstract, consume or use electricity or gas, or cause it to be wasted or diverted`
        `the person uses any telecommunication facility or obtains any telecommunication service` IS `Did you use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service`

@export Under section 327(1), have I committed the offence of possessing a device to obtain the use of a telecommunication facility or service?
GIVEN `Did you act without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without lawful excuse?
      `Did you make, possess, sell, offer for sale, import, obtain for use, distribute or make available the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make, possess, sell, offer for sale, import, obtain for use, distribute or make available the thing?
      `Is the thing a device (including a component of a device, or a computer program as section 342.1(2) defines it)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a device (including a component of a device, or a computer program as section 342.1(2) defines it)?
      `Is the device designed or adapted primarily to use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service without payment of a lawful charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the device designed or adapted primarily to use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service without payment of a lawful charge?
      `Do you know that the device has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that the device has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 327(1), have I committed the offence of possessing a device to obtain the use of a telecommunication facility or service` IS
    `s 327(1) the person commits the offence of possessing a device to obtain the use of a telecommunication facility or service` WITH
        `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS `Did you act without lawful excuse`
        `the person makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available the thing` IS `Did you make, possess, sell, offer for sale, import, obtain for use, distribute or make available the thing`
        `the thing is a device, by s 327(4) the thing is a device` IS (JUST `Is the thing a device (including a component of a device, or a computer program as section 342.1(2) defines it)`)
        `the device is designed or adapted primarily to use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service without payment of a lawful charge` IS `Is the device designed or adapted primarily to use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service without payment of a lawful charge`
        `the person knows that the device has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose` IS `Do you know that the device has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose`

@export Under section 327(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to for that offence?
GIVEN `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 327(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to for that offence` IS
    `s 327(1) the punishment for the offence` WITH
        `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS (`ccc12 seat the general penalty of s 787(1) as the person states it` `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)

