-- "Except where otherwise provided by law": whether another provision provides the punishment is asked, never guessed (fork F-334).
@export Under section 334, if I am convicted of theft, what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVEN `Was the property stolen a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the property stolen a testamentary instrument?
      `What was the value of what was stolen, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of what was stolen, in dollars?
      `Does another provision of law provide the punishment for this theft (for example section 333.1 for a motor vehicle, or section 338(2) for cattle)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another provision of law provide the punishment for this theft (for example section 333.1 for a motor vehicle, or section 338(2) for cattle)?
      `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
DECIDE `Under section 334, if I am convicted of theft, what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS
    `s 334 the punishment for the person who commits theft` WITH
        `the property stolen is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS (JUST `Was the property stolen a testamentary instrument`)
        `the value of what is stolen, in dollars` IS `What was the value of what was stolen, in dollars`
        `another provision of law otherwise provides the punishment for the theft` IS `Does another provision of law provide the punishment for this theft (for example section 333.1 for a motor vehicle, or section 338(2) for cattle)`
        `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS (`ccc12 seat the general penalty of s 787(1) as the person states it` `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)

@export Under section 334.1(1), must the court consider as an aggravating circumstance that I intended to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant?
GIVEN `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (for example 322, 343, 348, 351 or 354)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (for example 322, 343, 348, 351 or 354)?
      `What is the subsection, if any (for example "(1)"), or "" if none` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, if any (for example "(1)"), or "" if none?
      `Was the offence committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 334.1(1), must the court consider as an aggravating circumstance that I intended to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant` IS
    `s 334.1(1) the court shall consider as an aggravating circumstance that the offence was committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant` WITH
        `the offence` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (for example 322, 343, 348, 351 or 354)`, `What is the subsection, if any (for example "(1)"), or "" if none`)
        `the offence was committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant` IS `Was the offence committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant`

@export Under section 334.1(2), must the court consider as an aggravating circumstance that my offence interfered with an essential infrastructure?
GIVEN `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (322, 343 or 430 are the ones this subsection names)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (322, 343 or 430 are the ones this subsection names)?
      `What is the subsection, if any, or "" if none` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, if any, or "" if none?
      `Is the thing an essential infrastructure (see section 52.1(2))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an essential infrastructure (see section 52.1(2))?
      `Did the offence interfere with the access to or functioning of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence interfere with the access to or functioning of it?
      `Did the offence cause it to be unsafe or unfit for use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence cause it to be unsafe or unfit for use?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 334.1(2), must the court consider as an aggravating circumstance that my offence interfered with an essential infrastructure` IS
    `s 334.1(2) the court shall consider as an aggravating circumstance that the offence interfered with the access to or functioning of an essential infrastructure or caused it to be unsafe or unfit for use` WITH
        `the offence` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (322, 343 or 430 are the ones this subsection names)`, `What is the subsection, if any, or "" if none`)
        `the thing is an essential infrastructure, by s 52.1(2) essential infrastructure` IS (JUST `Is the thing an essential infrastructure (see section 52.1(2))`)
        `the offence interfered with the access to or functioning of it` IS `Did the offence interfere with the access to or functioning of it`
        `the offence caused it to be unsafe or unfit for use` IS `Did the offence cause it to be unsafe or unfit for use`


§ `Sections 335 to 342.2 -- offences resembling theft`
-- Taking a vehicle, breach of trust, cattle, drift timber, destroying documents, credit cards, computers. The questions on forfeiture (342.01(2), (3), 342.2(2), (3)) arise only after a conviction.

-- Subject to subsection (1.1), as the text says: an occupant who attempted to leave, or left, is outside the offence (the layer-1 rule calls `s 335(1.1)`).
@export Under section 335(1), have I taken a motor vehicle or vessel without consent, or been an occupant of one taken without consent?
GIVEN `Is the thing a vehicle drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a vehicle drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power?
      `Is it railway equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it railway equipment?
      `Is the thing a vessel (see section 320.11)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a vessel (see section 320.11)?
      `Did you act without the consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without the consent of the owner?
      `Did you take it with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it, or to cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take it with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it, or to cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated?
      `Were you an occupant of it knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an occupant of it knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner?
      `On becoming aware that it was taken without the owner's consent, did you attempt to leave it, as far as it was feasible to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On becoming aware that it was taken without the owner's consent, did you attempt to leave it, as far as it was feasible to do so?
      `On becoming aware that it was taken without the owner's consent, did you actually leave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On becoming aware that it was taken without the owner's consent, did you actually leave it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 335(1), have I taken a motor vehicle or vessel without consent, or been an occupant of one taken without consent` IS
    `s 335(1) the person is guilty of the offence of taking a motor vehicle or vessel without consent, or of being an occupant of one taken without consent` WITH
        `the thing is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS (`s 2 motor vehicle` `Is the thing a vehicle drawn, propelled or driven by any means other than muscular power` (JUST `Is it railway equipment`))
        `the thing is a vessel, by s 335(2) the thing is a vessel for the purposes of subsection (1)` IS (JUST `Is the thing a vessel (see section 320.11)`)
        `the person acted without the consent of the owner` IS `Did you act without the consent of the owner`
        `the person takes it with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it or cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated` IS `Did you take it with intent to drive, use, navigate or operate it, or to cause it to be driven, used, navigated or operated`
        `the person is an occupant of it knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner` IS `Were you an occupant of it knowing that it was taken without the consent of the owner`
        `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant attempted to leave it, to the extent that it was feasible to do so` IS `On becoming aware that it was taken without the owner's consent, did you attempt to leave it, as far as it was feasible to do so`
        `on becoming aware that it was taken without the consent of the owner, the occupant actually left it` IS `On becoming aware that it was taken without the owner's consent, did you actually leave it`

@export Under section 335(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVEN `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 335(1), what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS
    `s 335(1) the punishment for the offence` WITH
