    `s 339(1) the person is guilty of the offence of taking possession of drift timber` WITH
        `the person acted without the consent of the owner` IS `Did you act without the consent of the owner`
        `the thing is lumber, by s 339(6) lumber` IS (JUST `Is the thing lumber (timber, mast, spar, shingle bolt, sawlog or lumber of any description)`)
        `the thing is lumbering equipment, by s 339(6) lumbering equipment` IS (JUST `Is the thing lumbering equipment (a boom chain, chain, line, shackle or the like)`)
        `the thing is found adrift, cast ashore or lying on or embedded in the bed or bottom, or on the bank or beach, of a river, stream or lake in Canada, or in the harbours or any of the coastal waters of Canada` IS `Was it found adrift, cast ashore or lying on or embedded in the bed or bottom, or on the bank or beach, of a river, stream or lake in Canada, or in the harbours or coastal waters of Canada`
        `the person fraudulently takes, holds, keeps in their possession, conceals, receives, appropriates, purchases or sells it` IS `Did you fraudulently take, hold, keep in your possession, conceal, receive, appropriate, purchase or sell it`
        `the person removes, alters, obliterates or defaces a mark or number on it` IS `Did you remove, alter, obliterate or deface a mark or number on it`
        `the person refuses to deliver it up to the owner or to the person in charge of it on behalf of the owner or to a person authorized by the owner to receive it` IS `Did you refuse to deliver it up to the owner, the person in charge of it for the owner, or a person the owner authorized to receive it`

