        `the transaction is a mortgage or hypothec transaction` IS `Is the transaction a mortgage or hypothec transaction`
        `the part of it that is an amount required to be paid on account of property taxes, in dollars` IS `How many dollars of that is an amount required to be paid on account of property taxes`

-- JUST FALSE is the text's no: those who meet (a), (a.1), (b) and (c) are outside section 347. Where one fails the subsection says nothing of whether section 347 applies: NOTHING.
@export Under section 347.1(2), do section 347 and section 2 of the Interest Act apply to me as a payday lender?
GIVEN `Are you a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition in section 2 of the Bank Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition in section 2 of the Bank Act?
      `Did you enter into, or offer to enter into, a payday loan agreement to receive interest, advertise such an offer, or receive interest under such an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter into, or offer to enter into, a payday loan agreement to receive interest, advertise such an offer, or receive interest under such an agreement?
      `How many dollars are or would be advanced under the agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dollars are or would be advanced under the agreement?
      `What is the term of the agreement, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the term of the agreement, in days?
      `Does the total cost of borrowing under the agreement not exceed the limit fixed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the total cost of borrowing under the agreement not exceed the limit fixed by regulation?
      `Are you licensed or otherwise specifically authorized under the laws of a province to enter into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you licensed or otherwise specifically authorized under the laws of a province to enter into the agreement?
      `Is that province designated by order under section 347.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that province designated by order under section 347.1(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 347.1(2), do section 347 and section 2 of the Interest Act apply to me as a payday lender` IS
    `s 347.1(2) section 347 and section 2 of the Interest Act apply to the person` WITH
        `the person is a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition financial institution in section 2 of the Bank Act` IS `Are you a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition in section 2 of the Bank Act`
        `the person has entered into or has offered to enter into a payday loan agreement to receive interest, has advertised an offer to enter into a payday loan agreement that provides for the receipt of interest, or has received interest under a payday loan agreement` IS `Did you enter into, or offer to enter into, a payday loan agreement to receive interest, advertise such an offer, or receive interest under such an agreement`
        `the amount of money that is or would be advanced under the agreement, in dollars` IS `How many dollars are or would be advanced under the agreement`
        `the term of the agreement, in days` IS `What is the term of the agreement, in days`
        `the total cost of borrowing under the agreement does not or would not exceed the limit fixed by regulation` IS `Does the total cost of borrowing under the agreement not exceed the limit fixed by regulation`
        `the person is licensed or otherwise specifically authorized under the laws of a province to enter into the agreement` IS `Are you licensed or otherwise specifically authorized under the laws of a province to enter into the agreement`
        `the province is designated under subsection (3)` IS `Is that province designated by order under section 347.1(3)`

@export Under section 347.1(2.2), does section 347 apply to me after a new regulation changed the limit?
GIVEN `Did section 347 not apply to you by reason of section 347.1(2) just before the regulation came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did section 347 not apply to you by reason of section 347.1(2) just before the regulation came into force?
      `Did the total cost of borrowing under the agreement not exceed the limit that applied just before the regulation came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the total cost of borrowing under the agreement not exceed the limit that applied just before the regulation came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 347.1(2.2), does section 347 apply to me after a new regulation changed the limit` IS
    `s 347.1(2.2) section 347 applies to the person` WITH
        `section 347 did not apply to the person by reason of subsection (2) immediately before a regulation made under subsection (2.1) came into force` IS `Did section 347 not apply to you by reason of section 347.1(2) just before the regulation came into force`
        `the total cost of borrowing under the agreement did not exceed the limit that applied immediately before the regulation came into force` IS `Did the total cost of borrowing under the agreement not exceed the limit that applied just before the regulation came into force`


§ `Sections 348 to 353.1 -- breaking and entering, and related offences`
-- Breaking and entering, being in a dwelling-house, instruments, master keys and vehicle identification numbers. The question on the court's duty (348.1) arises only on conviction.

@export Under section 348(1), have I committed the offence of breaking and entering, or of breaking out?
GIVEN `Did you break (break a part of a thing or open a thing used to close or cover an opening: see section 321)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you break (break a part of a thing or open a thing used to close or cover an opening: see section 321)?
      `Did you enter (any part of your body, or of an instrument you used, within the thing: see section 350)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter (any part of your body, or of an instrument you used, within the thing: see section 350)?
      `Did you obtain entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within, or enter without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening (section 350)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within, or enter without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening (section 350)?
      `Was the thing a place (a dwelling-house; a building or structure or part of one; a railway vehicle, vessel, aircraft or trailer; or a pen or enclosure for fur-bearing animals: section 348(3))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing a place (a dwelling-house; a building or structure or part of one; a railway vehicle, vessel, aircraft or trailer; or a pen or enclosure for fur-bearing animals: section 348(3))?
      `Did you intend to commit an indictable offence in the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to commit an indictable offence in the place?
      `Did you commit an indictable offence in the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit an indictable offence in the place?
      `Did you break out of the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you break out of the place?
      `Did you break out after committing an indictable offence in the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you break out after committing an indictable offence in the place?
      `Did you break out after entering the place with intent to commit an indictable offence in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you break out after entering the place with intent to commit an indictable offence in it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 348(1), have I committed the offence of breaking and entering, or of breaking out` IS
    `s 348(1) the person commits the offence of breaking and entering, or of breaking out` WITH
        `the person breaks, by s 321 the person breaks` IS (JUST `Did you break (break a part of a thing or open a thing used to close or cover an opening: see section 321)`)
        `the person enters, by s 350(a) the person enters` IS (JUST `Did you enter (any part of your body, or of an instrument you used, within the thing: see section 350)`)
        `the person is deemed to have broken and entered, by s 350(b) the person is deemed to have broken and entered` IS (JUST `Did you obtain entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within, or enter without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening (section 350)`)
        `the thing is a place, by s 348(3) the thing is a place` IS (JUST `Was the thing a place (a dwelling-house; a building or structure or part of one; a railway vehicle, vessel, aircraft or trailer; or a pen or enclosure for fur-bearing animals: section 348(3))`)
        `the person has the intent to commit an indictable offence in the place` IS `Did you intend to commit an indictable offence in the place`
        `the person commits an indictable offence in the place` IS `Did you commit an indictable offence in the place`
        `the person breaks out of the place` IS `Did you break out of the place`
        `the person broke out after committing an indictable offence in the place` IS `Did you break out after committing an indictable offence in the place`
        `the person broke out after entering the place with intent to commit an indictable offence in the place` IS `Did you break out after entering the place with intent to commit an indictable offence in it`

@export Under section 348(1), if I am convicted of breaking and entering, or of breaking out, what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVEN `Was the place a dwelling-house (see section 2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the place a dwelling-house (see section 2)?
      `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
DECIDE `Under section 348(1), if I am convicted of breaking and entering, or of breaking out, what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS
    `s 348(1) the punishment for the offence` WITH
        `the place is a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house` IS (JUST `Was the place a dwelling-house (see section 2)`)
        `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS (`ccc12 seat the general penalty of s 787(1) as the person states it` `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)

@export Under section 348(2)(a), is the evidence that I broke and entered proof that I did so with intent to commit an indictable offence?
GIVEN `Are the proceedings under section 348` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings under section 348?
      `Is there evidence that you broke and entered a place or attempted to break and enter a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that you broke and entered a place or attempted to break and enter a place?
      `Is there evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
