      `What is the subsection, if any (for example "(2)"), or "" if none` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, if any (for example "(2)"), or "" if none?
      `Have you been convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of the offence?
      `Was the offence in relation to a dwelling-house (see section 2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence in relation to a dwelling-house (see section 2)?
      `Was the dwelling-house occupied at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the dwelling-house occupied at the time of the commission of the offence?
      `Did you know that it was occupied, or were you reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that it was occupied, or were you reckless as to whether it was?
      `In committing the offence, did you use violence or threats of violence to a person or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In committing the offence, did you use violence or threats of violence to a person or property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 348.1, must the court consider as an aggravating circumstance that the dwelling-house was occupied` IS
    `s 348.1 the court shall consider as an aggravating circumstance that the dwelling-house was occupied` WITH
        `the offence` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (98, 98.1, 279(2), 343, 346 or 348)`, `What is the subsection, if any (for example "(2)"), or "" if none`)
        `the person is convicted of the offence` IS `Have you been convicted of the offence`
        `the offence is in relation to a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house` IS (JUST `Was the offence in relation to a dwelling-house (see section 2)`)
        `the dwelling-house was occupied at the time of the commission of the offence` IS `Was the dwelling-house occupied at the time of the commission of the offence`
        `the person knew that the dwelling-house was occupied or was reckless as to whether it was occupied` IS `Did you know that it was occupied, or were you reckless as to whether it was`
        `the person, in committing the offence, used violence or threats of violence to a person or property` IS `In committing the offence, did you use violence or threats of violence to a person or property`

