§ `Sections 354 to 360 -- possession and trafficking`
-- Possession and trafficking of property obtained by crime, theft from mail. Sections 359 and 360 are repealed.

@export Under section 354(1), have I committed the offence of possession of property obtained by crime?
GIVEN `Do you have in your possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have in your possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing?
      `Do you know that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment?
      `Do you know that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 354(1), have I committed the offence of possession of property obtained by crime` IS
    `s 354(1) the person commits the offence of possession of property obtained by crime` WITH
        `the person has in their possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing` IS `Do you have in your possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing`
        `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment` IS `Do you know that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment`
        `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment` IS `Do you know that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment`

@export Under section 354(2), is the evidence of my possession of a motor vehicle with a removed or obliterated identification number proof that it was obtained by an offence punishable by indictment?
GIVEN `Are the proceedings in respect of an offence under section 354(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an offence under section 354(1)?
      `Is there evidence that you have in your possession a motor vehicle whose vehicle identification number has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated, or a part of a motor vehicle bearing a vehicle identification number that has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that you have in your possession a motor vehicle whose vehicle identification number has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated, or a part of a motor vehicle bearing a vehicle identification number that has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated?
      `Is there evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 354(2), is the evidence of my possession of a motor vehicle with a removed or obliterated identification number proof that it was obtained by an offence punishable by indictment` IS
    `s 354(2) the evidence is proof that the motor vehicle or part was obtained by an offence punishable by indictment` WITH
        `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under subsection 354(1)` IS `Are the proceedings in respect of an offence under section 354(1)`
        `there is evidence that the person has in their possession a motor vehicle the vehicle identification number of which has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated, or a part of a motor vehicle bearing a vehicle identification number that has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated` IS `Is there evidence that you have in your possession a motor vehicle whose vehicle identification number has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated, or a part of a motor vehicle bearing a vehicle identification number that has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated`
        `there is evidence to the contrary` IS `Is there evidence to the contrary`

