        `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment` IS `Do you know that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment`

@export Under section 355.5, what is the most I can be sentenced to for an offence under section 355.2 or 355.4?
GIVEN `What is the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars?
      `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 355.5, what is the most I can be sentenced to for an offence under section 355.2 or 355.4` IS
    `s 355.5 the punishment for the offence under section 355.2 or 355.4` WITH
        `the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars` IS `What is the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars`
        `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS (`ccc12 seat the general penalty of s 787(1) as the person states it` `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)

@export Under section 356(1), have I committed theft from mail?
GIVEN `Did you steal (commit theft: see section 322)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you steal (commit theft: see section 322)?
      `Was the thing anything sent by post, after it was deposited at a post office and before it was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing anything sent by post, after it was deposited at a post office and before it was delivered?
      `Was the thing anything sent by post, after it was delivered but before it was in the possession of the addressee or of a person who may reasonably be considered to be authorized by the addressee to receive mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing anything sent by post, after it was delivered but before it was in the possession of the addressee or of a person who may reasonably be considered to be authorized by the addressee to receive mail?
      `Was the thing a bag, sack or other container or covering in which mail is conveyed, whether or not it contains mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing a bag, sack or other container or covering in which mail is conveyed, whether or not it contains mail?
      `Was the thing a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation?
      `With intent to steal from the mail, did you make, possess or use a copy of a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation, or a key suited to obtaining access to a receptacle or device provided for the receipt of mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc With intent to steal from the mail, did you make, possess or use a copy of a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation, or a key suited to obtaining access to a receptacle or device provided for the receipt of mail?
      `Do you have in your possession anything that you know has been used to commit such a theft, or anything in respect of which you know that such an offence has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have in your possession anything that you know has been used to commit such a theft, or anything in respect of which you know that such an offence has been committed?
      `Did you fraudulently redirect, or cause to be redirected, anything sent by post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fraudulently redirect, or cause to be redirected, anything sent by post?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 356(1), have I committed theft from mail` IS
    `s 356(1) the person commits the offence of theft from mail` WITH
        `the person steals, by s 2 steal` IS (`s 2 steal` (JUST `Did you steal (commit theft: see section 322)`))
        `the thing is anything sent by post, after it is deposited at a post office and before it is delivered` IS `Was the thing anything sent by post, after it was deposited at a post office and before it was delivered`
        `the thing is anything sent by post, after it is delivered but before it is in the possession of the addressee or of a person who may reasonably be considered to be authorized by the addressee to receive mail` IS `Was the thing anything sent by post, after it was delivered but before it was in the possession of the addressee or of a person who may reasonably be considered to be authorized by the addressee to receive mail`
        `the thing is a bag, sack or other container or covering in which mail is conveyed, whether or not it contains mail` IS `Was the thing a bag, sack or other container or covering in which mail is conveyed, whether or not it contains mail`
        `the thing is a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation` IS `Was the thing a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation`
        `with intent to commit an offence under paragraph (a), the person makes, possesses or uses a copy of a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation, or a key suited to obtaining access to a receptacle or device provided for the receipt of mail` IS `With intent to steal from the mail, did you make, possess or use a copy of a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation, or a key suited to obtaining access to a receptacle or device provided for the receipt of mail`
        `the person has in their possession anything that they know has been used to commit an offence under paragraph (a) or (a.1) or anything in respect of which they know that such an offence has been committed` IS `Do you have in your possession anything that you know has been used to commit such a theft, or anything in respect of which you know that such an offence has been committed`
        `the person fraudulently redirects, or causes to be redirected, anything sent by post` IS `Did you fraudulently redirect, or cause to be redirected, anything sent by post`

@export Under section 356(2), must the indictment allege, or the prosecution prove, that the thing I took from the mail had any value?
GIVEN `Are the proceedings for an offence under section 356` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for an offence under section 356?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 356(2), must the indictment allege, or the prosecution prove, that the thing I took from the mail had any value` IS
    `s 356(2) it is necessary to allege in the indictment or to prove on the trial that the thing had any value` WITH
        `the proceedings are proceedings for an offence under section 356` IS `Are the proceedings for an offence under section 356`

@export Under section 356(3), what is the most I can be sentenced to for theft from mail?
GIVEN `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 356(3), what is the most I can be sentenced to for theft from mail` IS
    `s 356(3) the punishment for the offence` WITH
        `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS (`ccc12 seat the general penalty of s 787(1) as the person states it` `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)

@export Under section 357, have I committed the offence of bringing into Canada property obtained by crime?
GIVEN `Did you bring into or have in Canada anything` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you bring into or have in Canada anything?
      `Did you obtain it outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain it outside Canada?
      `Did you obtain it by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain it by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 357, have I committed the offence of bringing into Canada property obtained by crime` IS
    `s 357 the person commits the offence of bringing into Canada property obtained by crime` WITH
        `the person brings into or has in Canada anything` IS `Did you bring into or have in Canada anything`
        `the person obtained it outside Canada` IS `Did you obtain it outside Canada`
        `the person obtained it by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354` IS `Did you obtain it by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354`

@export Under section 357, what is the most I can be sentenced to?
GIVEN `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 357, what is the most I can be sentenced to` IS
    `s 357 the punishment for the offence` WITH
        `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS (`ccc12 seat the general penalty of s 787(1) as the person states it` `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)

@export Under section 358, is the offence of having in possession complete?
GIVEN `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (342, 354 or 356)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (342, 354 or 356)?
      `What is the subsection and paragraph, if any (for example "(1)(b)"), or "" if none` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection and paragraph, if any (for example "(1)(b)"), or "" if none?
      `Do you have, alone or jointly with another person, possession of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, alone or jointly with another person, possession of the thing?
      `Do you have, alone or jointly with another person, control over the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, alone or jointly with another person, control over the thing?
      `Do you aid in concealing or disposing of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you aid in concealing or disposing of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 358, is the offence of having in possession complete` IS
    `s 358 the offence of having in possession is complete` WITH
        `the offence` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (342, 354 or 356)`, `What is the subsection and paragraph, if any (for example "(1)(b)"), or "" if none`)
        `the person has, alone or jointly with another person, possession of anything mentioned in those sections` IS `Do you have, alone or jointly with another person, possession of the thing`
        `the person has, alone or jointly with another person, control over anything mentioned in those sections` IS `Do you have, alone or jointly with another person, control over the thing`
        `the person aids in concealing or disposing of it` IS `Do you aid in concealing or disposing of it`


§ `Sections 361 to 365 -- false pretences`
-- False pretences and false statements. Section 365 is repealed.

@export Under section 361(1), is what I said a "false pretence"?
GIVEN `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise?
      `Did you know that the representation was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the representation was false?
      `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 361(1), is what I said a "false pretence"` IS
    `s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` WITH
        `it is a representation of a matter of fact either present or past, made by words or otherwise` IS `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise`
        `it is known by the person who makes it to be false` IS `Did you know that the representation was false`
        `it is made with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom it is made to act on it` IS `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it`

-- JUST FALSE is the text's no ("is not a false pretence unless it is carried to such an extent ..."). Past that extent the subsection stops excluding it but does not itself say that it is a false pretence (section 361(1) does): NOTHING.
@export Under section 361(2), is my exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of something a "false pretence"?
GIVEN `Was it exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything?
      `Was it carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 361(2), is my exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of something a "false pretence"` IS
    `s 361(2) the exaggerated commendation or depreciation is a false pretence` WITH
        `the statement is exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything` IS `Was it exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything`
        `it is carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact` IS `Was it carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact`

@export Under section 361(3), is it a question of fact whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact?
GIVEN `Is the question whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 361(3), is it a question of fact whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact` IS
    `s 361(3) the question is a question of fact` WITH
        `the question is whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact` IS `Is the question whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact`

@export Under section 362(1)(a), have I committed the offence of obtaining a thing by a false pretence?
GIVEN `Did you obtain anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or cause it to be delivered to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or cause it to be delivered to another person?
      `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise?
      `Did you know that the representation was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the representation was false?
      `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(1)(a), have I committed the offence of obtaining a thing by a false pretence` IS
    `s 362(1)(a) the person commits the offence of obtaining a thing by a false pretence` WITH
        `the person obtains anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or causes it to be delivered to another person` IS `Did you obtain anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or cause it to be delivered to another person`
        `the means is a false pretence, whether directly or through the medium of a contract obtained by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` IS (`s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` `Did you know that the representation was false` `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it`)

@export Under section 362(1)(b), have I committed the offence of obtaining credit by a false pretence or by fraud?
GIVEN `Did you obtain credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain credit?
      `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise?
      `Did you know that the representation was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the representation was false?
      `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it?
      `Did you obtain it by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain it by fraud?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(1)(b), have I committed the offence of obtaining credit by a false pretence or by fraud` IS
    `s 362(1)(b) the person commits the offence of obtaining credit by a false pretence or by fraud` WITH
        `the person obtains credit` IS `Did you obtain credit`
        `the person does so by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` IS (`s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` `Did you know that the representation was false` `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it`)
        `the person does so by fraud` IS `Did you obtain it by fraud`

@export Under section 362(1)(c), have I committed the offence of making a false statement in writing about financial condition or means to procure a benefit?
GIVEN `Did you knowingly make, or cause to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make, or cause to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing?
      `Did you do so with intent that it should be relied on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so with intent that it should be relied on?
      `Was the statement with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of a person or organization that you are interested in or act for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of a person or organization that you are interested in or act for?
      `What did you do it for the purpose of procuring: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those` IS A `s 362(1)(c) thing procured` @desc What did you do it for the purpose of procuring: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(1)(c), have I committed the offence of making a false statement in writing about financial condition or means to procure a benefit` IS
    `s 362(1)(c) the person commits the offence of making a false statement in writing about financial condition or means to procure a benefit` WITH
        `the person knowingly makes or causes to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing` IS `Did you knowingly make, or cause to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing`
        `the person does so with intent that it should be relied on` IS `Did you do so with intent that it should be relied on`
        `the statement is with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of the person or of any person or organization that the person is interested in or acts for` IS `Was the statement with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of a person or organization that you are interested in or act for`
        `the thing the person does so for the purpose of procuring, in any form whatever, whether for the person's benefit or the benefit of that person or organization` IS `What did you do it for the purpose of procuring: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those`

@export Under section 362(1)(d), have I committed the offence of procuring a benefit on the faith of a false statement in writing?
GIVEN `Do you know that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of another person or organization that you are interested in or act for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of another person or organization that you are interested in or act for?
      `What did you procure on the faith of that statement: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those` IS A `s 362(1)(c) thing procured` @desc What did you procure on the faith of that statement: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(1)(d), have I committed the offence of procuring a benefit on the faith of a false statement in writing` IS
    `s 362(1)(d) the person commits the offence of procuring a benefit on the faith of a false statement in writing` WITH
        `the person knows that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of the person or of another person or organization that the person is interested in or acts for` IS `Do you know that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of another person or organization that you are interested in or act for`
        `the thing the person procures on the faith of that statement, whether for the person's benefit or for the benefit of that person or organization` IS `What did you procure on the faith of that statement: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those`

-- The whole offence of section 362(1) joins the four paragraphs. The two `thing procured` questions are different questions that share one list of things (section 362(1)(c)(i) to (vi)).
@export Under section 362(1), have I committed the offence of false pretence or false statement?
GIVEN `Did you obtain anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or cause it to be delivered to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or cause it to be delivered to another person?
      `Did you obtain credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain credit?
      `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise?
      `Did you know that the representation was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the representation was false?
      `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it?
      `Did you obtain credit by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain credit by fraud?
      `Did you knowingly make, or cause to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make, or cause to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing?
      `Did you do so with intent that it should be relied on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so with intent that it should be relied on?
      `Was the statement with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of a person or organization that you are interested in or act for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of a person or organization that you are interested in or act for?
      `What did you do it for the purpose of procuring: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those` IS A `s 362(1)(c) thing procured` @desc What did you do it for the purpose of procuring: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those?
      `Do you know that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of another person or organization that you are interested in or act for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of another person or organization that you are interested in or act for?
      `What did you procure on the faith of that statement: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those` IS A `s 362(1)(c) thing procured` @desc What did you procure on the faith of that statement: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 362(1), have I committed the offence of false pretence or false statement` IS
    `s 362(1) the person commits the offence of false pretence or false statement` WITH
        `the person commits the offence under paragraph (a), by s 362(1)(a)` IS (`s 362(1)(a) the person commits the offence of obtaining a thing by a false pretence` `Did you obtain anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or cause it to be delivered to another person` (`s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` `Did you know that the representation was false` `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it`))
        `the person commits the offence under paragraph (b), by s 362(1)(b)` IS (`s 362(1)(b) the person commits the offence of obtaining credit by a false pretence or by fraud` `Did you obtain credit` (`s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` `Did you make a representation of a matter of fact, either present or past, by words or otherwise` `Did you know that the representation was false` `Did you make it with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom you made it to act on it`) `Did you obtain credit by fraud`)
        `the person commits the offence under paragraph (c), by s 362(1)(c)` IS (`s 362(1)(c) the person commits the offence of making a false statement in writing about financial condition or means to procure a benefit` `Did you knowingly make, or cause to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing` `Did you do so with intent that it should be relied on` `Was the statement with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of a person or organization that you are interested in or act for` `What did you do it for the purpose of procuring: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those`)
        `the person commits the offence under paragraph (d), by s 362(1)(d)` IS (`s 362(1)(d) the person commits the offence of procuring a benefit on the faith of a false statement in writing` `Do you know that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of you or of another person or organization that you are interested in or act for` `What did you procure on the faith of that statement: the delivery of personal property, the payment of money, the making of a loan, the grant or extension of credit, the discount of an account receivable, the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note, or none of those`)

@export Under section 362(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to for obtaining a thing by a false pretence?
GIVEN `Is the property obtained a testamentary instrument (see section 2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property obtained a testamentary instrument (see section 2)?
      `What is the value of what was obtained, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of what was obtained, in dollars?
      `What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) provides for an offence punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
DECIDE `Under section 362(2), what is the most I can be sentenced to for obtaining a thing by a false pretence` IS
    `s 362(2) the punishment for an offence under paragraph (1)(a)` WITH
        `the property obtained is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS (JUST `Is the property obtained a testamentary instrument (see section 2)`)
        `the value of what is obtained, in dollars` IS `What is the value of what was obtained, in dollars`
