§ `Sections 366 to 378 -- forgery and offences resembling forgery`
-- Forgery, forged documents, stamps, marks, registers and false communications. Sections 370, 371 and 373 are repealed.

@export Under section 366(1), have I committed forgery?
GIVEN `Is the document a false document (see section 321)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a false document (see section 321)?
      `Did you make it, including by altering a genuine document in any material part, by a material addition to it, or by a material alteration of it (section 366(2))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it, including by altering a genuine document in any material part, by a material addition to it, or by a material alteration of it (section 366(2))?
      `Did you know it to be false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know it to be false?
      `Did you intend that it should in any way be used or acted on as genuine, to the prejudice of any one whether within Canada or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that it should in any way be used or acted on as genuine, to the prejudice of any one whether within Canada or not?
      `Did you intend that a person should be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or to refrain from doing anything, whether within Canada or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend that a person should be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or to refrain from doing anything, whether within Canada or not?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 366(1), have I committed forgery` IS
    `s 366(1) the person commits forgery` WITH
        `the document is a false document, by s 321 the document is a false document` IS (JUST `Is the document a false document (see section 321)`)
        `the person makes the false document, including by an act within subsection 366(2), by s 366(2) the act is making a false document` IS (JUST `Did you make it, including by altering a genuine document in any material part, by a material addition to it, or by a material alteration of it (section 366(2))`)
        `the person knows it to be false` IS `Did you know it to be false`
        `the person intends that it should in any way be used or acted on as genuine, to the prejudice of any one whether within Canada or not` IS `Did you intend that it should in any way be used or acted on as genuine, to the prejudice of any one whether within Canada or not`
        `the person intends that a person should be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or to refrain from doing anything, whether within Canada or not` IS `Did you intend that a person should be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or to refrain from doing anything, whether within Canada or not`

@export Under section 366(2), is what I did "making a false document"?
GIVEN `What did you do: alter a genuine document in any material part; make a material addition to a genuine document or add to it a false date, attestation, seal or other thing that is material; make a material alteration in a genuine document by erasure, obliteration, removal or in any other way; or something else` IS A `s 366(2) act` @desc What did you do: alter a genuine document in any material part; make a material addition to a genuine document or add to it a false date, attestation, seal or other thing that is material; make a material alteration in a genuine document by erasure, obliteration, removal or in any other way; or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 366(2), is what I did "making a false document"` IS
    `s 366(2) the act is making a false document` WITH
        `act` IS `What did you do: alter a genuine document in any material part; make a material addition to a genuine document or add to it a false date, attestation, seal or other thing that is material; make a material alteration in a genuine document by erasure, obliteration, removal or in any other way; or something else`

