      `What is the subsection, if any (for example "(1)"), or "" if none` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection, if any (for example "(1)"), or "" if none?
      `Are you a public officer, as defined in section 25.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a public officer, as defined in section 25.1(1)?
      `Were the acts alleged to constitute the offence committed by you for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of your duties or employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the acts alleged to constitute the offence committed by you for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of your duties or employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 368.2, am I as a public officer guilty of an offence under sections 366 to 368.1 for acts done only to maintain a covert identity` IS
    `s 368.2 the public officer is guilty of an offence under any of sections 366 to 368.1` WITH
        `the offence` IS (`Provision of the Code` OF `What is the number of the section of the Code that the offence is under (366, 367, 368 or 368.1)`, `What is the subsection, if any (for example "(1)"), or "" if none`)
        `the person is a public officer, as defined in subsection 25.1(1), by s 25.1(1) public officer` IS (JUST `Are you a public officer, as defined in section 25.1(1)`)
        `the acts alleged to constitute the offence were committed by the public officer for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of the public officer's duties or employment` IS `Were the acts alleged to constitute the offence committed by you for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of your duties or employment`

@export Under section 369, have I committed the offence of dealing in exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or public seals?
GIVEN `Did you act without lawful authority or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act without lawful authority or excuse?
      `Did you make, use or possess the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make, use or possess the thing?
      `Is it exchequer bill paper (see section 321)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it exchequer bill paper (see section 321)?
      `Is it revenue paper (see section 321)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it revenue paper (see section 321)?
      `Is it paper that is used to make bank-notes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paper that is used to make bank-notes?
      `Is it paper that is intended to resemble exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or paper used to make bank-notes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paper that is intended to resemble exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or paper used to make bank-notes?
      `Did you make, reproduce or use a public seal of Canada or of a province, or the seal of a public body or authority in Canada or of a court of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make, reproduce or use a public seal of Canada or of a province, or the seal of a public body or authority in Canada or of a court of law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 369, have I committed the offence of dealing in exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or public seals` IS
    `s 369 the person commits the offence of dealing in exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or public seals` WITH
        `the person acted without lawful authority or excuse` IS `Did you act without lawful authority or excuse`
        `the person makes, uses or possesses the thing` IS `Did you make, use or possess the thing`
        `the thing is exchequer bill paper, by s 321 the paper is exchequer bill paper` IS (JUST `Is it exchequer bill paper (see section 321)`)
        `the thing is revenue paper, by s 321 the paper is revenue paper` IS (JUST `Is it revenue paper (see section 321)`)
        `the thing is paper that is used to make bank-notes` IS `Is it paper that is used to make bank-notes`
        `the thing is paper that is intended to resemble paper mentioned in subparagraph (a)(i)` IS `Is it paper that is intended to resemble exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or paper used to make bank-notes`
        `the person makes, reproduces or uses a public seal of Canada or of a province, or the seal of a public body or authority in Canada or of a court of law` IS `Did you make, reproduce or use a public seal of Canada or of a province, or the seal of a public body or authority in Canada or of a court of law`

