--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused). Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model
-- (the maintainer, 2026-11-09), but this is a plain seat layer with no charge-generator contract.
--
-- Every question is named to begin "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering, has @export and @desc, takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, choices from a list),
-- and is grouped under a § heading in the text's order. Each question calls the layer-1 function whose name its title restates (the two questions "apart from subsection (7)" and "apart from subsection (5)" add the limb they answer), and nothing else:
--   * an OFFENCE question answers whether what the accused did is the offence, the class of the offence and the punishments it is liable to (one record);
--   * the other questions answer the saving, the presumption, the bar, the order of the court or the definition the section states.
-- A layer-1 input that is itself an answer (written in layer 1 as "..., by s N") is computed inside the question by calling the layer-1 function that gives it, and the facts
-- THAT function asks are asked here; the one exception is "is it a testamentary instrument?", which is asked as a plain yes/no because the keel's answer cannot be JUST FALSE (NOTES.md, fork F13). A fact that belongs to another part of the Code (for example "computer data", section 342.1(2)) is asked as a plain yes/no.
-- Section 787(1) (the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction) is another part's: three plain figures are asked wherever the text of this part leaves the
-- summary limb to it.
-- Reading a result (as NOTES.md says): JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no; NOTHING is "the text does not answer this case". A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The seat has no questions for the court: a power or duty of the court is asked from the accused's side ("may the court ...", "must the court ...") and answers what may be done to the accused.

DECLARE `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` HAS
    `s 380 to 447.1 whether what I did is the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 380 to 447.1 the class of the offence, if it is one` IS A MAYBE (`Class of offence`)
    `s 380 to 447.1 the punishments the offence is liable to, if it is one` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)

-- Section 787(1) lies outside Parts X and XI (another part's), so the seat asks for what it sets, as three plain figures, and builds the limb the text of this part leaves to it.
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
      `less a day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Punishment
`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, months, 0, `less a day`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `a fine of` fine, `no fine is stated`

§ `Fraud, ss 379 to 381`

-- calls `s 379 goods`
@export Under section 379, is the thing goods?
GIVEN `the thing is the subject of trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is the subject of trade or commerce?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 379, is the thing goods` MEANS
    `s 379 goods` `the thing is the subject of trade or commerce`

-- calls `s 380(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud`, `s 380(1) the class of the offence` and `s 380(1) the punishments`
@export Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means?
      `the person defrauds the public or any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you defraud the public or any person?
      `what the person defrauds of, as property` IS A `s 2 property kind` @desc What kind of property is it (section 2, "property")? Choose the one that applies.
      `what the person defrauds of is money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that what the person defrauds of is money?
      `what the person defrauds of, as a valuable security` IS A `s 2 valuable security kind` @desc What kind of valuable security is it (section 2, "valuable security")? Choose the one that applies.
      `what the person defrauds of is a service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that what the person defrauds of is a service?
      `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subject-matter of the offence a testamentary instrument (a will, a codicil, or another testamentary writing or appointment)? Answer in your own judgment; the Code says only that the term includes those.
      `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 380(1), is what I did the offence of fraud, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 380(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud` `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` `the person defrauds the public or any person` `what the person defrauds of, as property` `what the person defrauds of is money` `what the person defrauds of, as a valuable security` `what the person defrauds of is a service`)
        (`s 380(1) the class of the offence` (`s 380(1)(a) the subject-matter is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars` (JUST `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument`) `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars`) (`s 380(1)(b) the value of the subject-matter does not exceed five thousand dollars` `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars`))
        (`s 380(1) the punishments` (`s 380(1)(a) the subject-matter is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars` (JUST `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument`) `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars`) (`s 380(1)(b) the value of the subject-matter does not exceed five thousand dollars` `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars`) (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`))

-- calls `s 380(1)(a) the subject-matter is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars`
@export Under section 380(1)(a), is the subject-matter a testamentary instrument, or does its value exceed five thousand dollars?
GIVEN `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subject-matter of the offence a testamentary instrument (a will, a codicil, or another testamentary writing or appointment)? Answer in your own judgment; the Code says only that the term includes those.
      `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380(1)(a), is the subject-matter a testamentary instrument, or does its value exceed five thousand dollars` MEANS
    `s 380(1)(a) the subject-matter is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars` (JUST `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument`) `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars`

-- calls `s 380(1)(b) the value of the subject-matter does not exceed five thousand dollars`
@export Under section 380(1)(b), does the value of the subject-matter not exceed five thousand dollars?
GIVEN `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380(1)(b), does the value of the subject-matter not exceed five thousand dollars` MEANS
    `s 380(1)(b) the value of the subject-matter does not exceed five thousand dollars` `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars`

-- calls `s 380(1.1) the court shall impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years`
@export Under section 380(1.1), must the court impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years?
GIVEN `the person is prosecuted on indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are prosecuted on indictment?
      `the person is convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1)?
      `the total value of the subject-matter of the offences, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the subject-matter of the offences, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380(1.1), must the court impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years` MEANS
    `s 380(1.1) the court shall impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years` `the person is prosecuted on indictment` `the person is convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1)` `the total value of the subject-matter of the offences, in dollars`

-- calls `s 380(2) the conduct is the offence of affecting the public market`, `s 380(2) the class of the offence` and `s 380(2) the punishments`
@export Under section 380(2), is what I did the offence of affecting the public market, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means?
      `the person acts with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with intent to defraud?
      `the person affects the public market price of stocks, shares, merchandise or anything that is offered for sale to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you affect the public market price of stocks, shares, merchandise or anything that is offered for sale to the public?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 380(2), is what I did the offence of affecting the public market, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 380(2) the conduct is the offence of affecting the public market` `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` `the person acts with intent to defraud` `the person affects the public market price of stocks, shares, merchandise or anything that is offered for sale to the public`)
        (JUST `s 380(2) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 380(2) the punishments`))

-- calls `s 380.1(1) the court shall consider the circumstance as aggravating`
@export Under section 380.1(1), must the court consider the circumstance as aggravating?
GIVEN `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence for which the sentence is imposed? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence for which the sentence is imposed, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `circumstance (s 380.1(1))` IS A `s 380.1(1) circumstance` @desc Choose the circumstance that applies (section 380.1(1)).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.1(1), must the court consider the circumstance as aggravating` MEANS
    `s 380.1(1) the court shall consider the circumstance as aggravating` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (section number)`, `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (subsection)`) `circumstance (s 380.1(1))`

-- calls `s 380.1(1.1) the court shall consider the value of the fraud as aggravating`
@export Under section 380.1(1.1), must the court consider the value of the fraud as aggravating?
GIVEN `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence for which the sentence is imposed? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence for which the sentence is imposed, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `the value of the fraud committed, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the fraud committed, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.1(1.1), must the court consider the value of the fraud as aggravating` MEANS
    `s 380.1(1.1) the court shall consider the value of the fraud as aggravating` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (section number)`, `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (subsection)`) `the value of the fraud committed, in dollars`

-- calls `s 380.1(2) the court shall not consider the circumstance as mitigating`
@export Under section 380.1(2), is the court barred from considering the circumstance as mitigating?
GIVEN `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence for which the sentence is imposed? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence for which the sentence is imposed, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `circumstance (s 380.1(2))` IS A `s 380.1(2) circumstance` @desc Choose the circumstance that applies (section 380.1(2)).
      `the circumstance was relevant to, contributed to, or was used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the circumstance was relevant to, contributed to, or was used in the commission of the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.1(2), is the court barred from considering the circumstance as mitigating` MEANS
    `s 380.1(2) the court shall not consider the circumstance as mitigating` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (section number)`, `the offence for which the sentence is imposed (subsection)`) `circumstance (s 380.1(2))` `the circumstance was relevant to, contributed to, or was used in the commission of the offence`

-- calls `s 380.1(3) the court shall cause the circumstances it took into account to be stated in the record`
@export Under section 380.1(3), must the court cause the circumstances it took into account to be stated in the record?
GIVEN `the offence for which the sentence is determined (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence for which the sentence is determined? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the offence for which the sentence is determined (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence for which the sentence is determined, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.1(3), must the court cause the circumstances it took into account to be stated in the record` MEANS
    `s 380.1(3) the court shall cause the circumstances it took into account to be stated in the record` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence for which the sentence is determined (section number)`, `the offence for which the sentence is determined (subsection)`)

-- calls `s 380.2(1) the activity is one the order may prohibit`
@export Under section 380.2(1), is the activity one the order may prohibit?
GIVEN `activity (s 380.2(1))` IS A `s 380.2(1) activity` @desc Choose the activity that applies (section 380.2(1)).
      `the employment or volunteer capacity involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the employment or volunteer capacity involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.2(1), is the activity one the order may prohibit` MEANS
    `s 380.2(1) the activity is one the order may prohibit` `activity (s 380.2(1))` `the employment or volunteer capacity involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person`

-- calls `s 380.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering`
@export Under section 380.2(1), may the court make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering?
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are convicted of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)?
      `the offender is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730 of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730 of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.2(1), may the court make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering` MEANS
    `s 380.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering` `the offender is convicted of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)` `the offender is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730 of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)`

-- calls `s 380.2(2) the prohibition may be for the period`
@export Under section 380.2(2), may the prohibition be for the period?
GIVEN `the court considers the period appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court considers the period appropriate?
      `the period is a period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the period is a period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.2(2), may the prohibition be for the period` MEANS
    `s 380.2(2) the prohibition may be for the period` `the court considers the period appropriate` `the period is a period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment`

-- calls `s 380.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order`
@export Under section 380.2(3), may the court vary the conditions prescribed in the order?
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the order, or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court is the court that made the order, or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province?
      `the offender or the prosecutor has applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you or the prosecutor applied?
      `the court has heard the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court has heard the parties?
      `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 380.2(3), may the court vary the conditions prescribed in the order` MEANS
    `s 380.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` `the court is the court that made the order, or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province` `the offender or the prosecutor has applied` `the court has heard the parties` `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances`

-- calls `s 380.2(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition`, `s 380.2(4) the class of the offence` and `s 380.2(4) the punishments`
@export Under section 380.2(4), is what I did the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are bound by an order of prohibition?
      `the person does not comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do not comply with the order?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 380.2(4), is what I did the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 380.2(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` `the person does not comply with the order`)
        (JUST `s 380.2(4) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 380.2(4) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 381 the conduct is the offence of using the mails to defraud`, `s 381 the class of the offence` and `s 381 the punishments`
@export Under section 381, is what I did the offence of using the mails to defraud, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person makes use of the mails` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you make use of the mails?
      `the purpose is transmitting or delivering letters or circulars concerning schemes devised or intended to deceive or defraud the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purpose is transmitting or delivering letters or circulars concerning schemes devised or intended to deceive or defraud the public?
      `the purpose is obtaining money under false pretences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the purpose is obtaining money under false pretences?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 381, is what I did the offence of using the mails to defraud, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 381 the conduct is the offence of using the mails to defraud` `the person makes use of the mails` `the purpose is transmitting or delivering letters or circulars concerning schemes devised or intended to deceive or defraud the public` `the purpose is obtaining money under false pretences`)
        (JUST `s 381 the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 381 the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

§ `Securities, title and trade secrets, ss 382 to 392`

-- calls `s 382 the conduct is the offence of fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions`, `s 382 the class of the offence` and `s 382 the punishments`
@export Under section 382, is what I did the offence of fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts through the facility of a stock exchange, curb market or other market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act through the facility of a stock exchange, curb market or other market?
      `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance of active public trading in a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with intent to create a false or misleading appearance of active public trading in a security?
      `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market price of a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with intent to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market price of a security?
      `the person effects a transaction in the security that involves no change in the beneficial ownership thereof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you effect a transaction in the security that involves no change in the beneficial ownership thereof?
      `the person enters an order for the purchase of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the sale of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you enter an order for the purchase of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the sale of the security have been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons?
      `the person enters an order for the sale of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the purchase of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you enter an order for the sale of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the purchase of the security have been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 382, is what I did the offence of fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 382 the conduct is the offence of fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions` `the person acts through the facility of a stock exchange, curb market or other market` `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance of active public trading in a security` `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market price of a security` `the person effects a transaction in the security that involves no change in the beneficial ownership thereof` `the person enters an order for the purchase of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the sale of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons` `the person enters an order for the sale of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the purchase of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons`)
        (JUST `s 382 the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 382 the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 382.1(1) the conduct is the offence of buying or selling a security using inside information`, `s 382.1(1) the class of the offence` and `s 382.1(1) the punishments`
@export Under section 382.1(1), is what I did the offence of buying or selling a security using inside information, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person directly or indirectly buys or sells a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you directly or indirectly buy or sell a security?
      `the person knowingly uses the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you knowingly use the information?
      `the information relates to or affects the issuer of a security or a security that they have issued, or are about to issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information relates to or affects the issuer of a security or a security that they have issued, or are about to issue?
      `the information has not been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information has not been generally disclosed?
