-- calls `s 389(1) the conduct is the offence of fraudulent disposal of goods on which money advanced`, `s 389(1) the class of the offence` and `s 389(1) the punishments`
@export Under section 389(1), is what I did the offence of fraudulent disposal of goods on which money advanced, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person has shipped or delivered to the keeper of a warehouse or to a factor, an agent or a carrier anything on which the consignee has advanced money or has given valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have shipped or delivered to the keeper of a warehouse or to a factor, an agent or a carrier anything on which the consignee have advanced money or have given valuable security?
      `the person thereafter disposes of it in a manner that is different from and inconsistent with any agreement made between the person and the consignee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you thereafter dispose of it in a manner that is different from and inconsistent with any agreement made between the person and the consignee?
      `the person acts with intent to deceive, defraud or injure the consignee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with intent to deceive, defraud or injure the consignee?
      `the person knowingly and wilfully aids or assists any person to make a disposition of anything to which paragraph (a) applies for the purpose of deceiving, defrauding or injuring the consignee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you knowingly and wilfully aid or assist any person to make a disposition of anything to which paragraph (a) apply for the purpose of deceiving, defrauding or injuring the consignee?
      `before disposing of the thing in a manner different from and inconsistent with the agreement, the person pays or tenders to the consignee the full amount of money or valuable security that the consignee has advanced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before disposing of the thing in a manner different from and inconsistent with the agreement, the person pays or tenders to the consignee the full amount of money or valuable security that the consignee has advanced?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 389(1), is what I did the offence of fraudulent disposal of goods on which money advanced, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 389(1) the conduct is the offence of fraudulent disposal of goods on which money advanced` `the person has shipped or delivered to the keeper of a warehouse or to a factor, an agent or a carrier anything on which the consignee has advanced money or has given valuable security` `the person thereafter disposes of it in a manner that is different from and inconsistent with any agreement made between the person and the consignee` `the person acts with intent to deceive, defraud or injure the consignee` `the person knowingly and wilfully aids or assists any person to make a disposition of anything to which paragraph (a) applies for the purpose of deceiving, defrauding or injuring the consignee` (`s 389(2) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under section 389` `before disposing of the thing in a manner different from and inconsistent with the agreement, the person pays or tenders to the consignee the full amount of money or valuable security that the consignee has advanced`))
        (JUST `s 389(1) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 389(1) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

