-- calls `s 394(5) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3)`, `s 394(5) the class of the offence` and `s 394(5) the punishments`
@export Under section 394(5), am I guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3), and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person is the holder of a lease or licence issued under an Act relating to the mining of valuable minerals, or by the owner of land that is supposed to contain valuable minerals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are the holder of a lease or licence issued under an Act relating to the mining of valuable minerals, or by the owner of land that is supposed to contain valuable minerals?
      `the person, by a fraudulent device or contrivance, defrauds or attempts to defraud any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you, by a fraudulent device or contrivance, defraud or attempts to defraud any person?
      `the person is defrauded of valuable minerals obtained under or reserved by the lease or licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you defrauded, or attempted to defraud, the other person of valuable minerals obtained under or reserved by the lease or licence?
      `the person is defrauded of money or a valuable interest or thing payable in respect of valuable minerals obtained or rights reserved by the lease or licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you defrauded, or attempted to defraud, the other person of money or a valuable interest or thing payable in respect of valuable minerals obtained or rights reserved by the lease or licence?
      `the person fraudulently conceals or makes a false statement with respect to the amount of valuable minerals obtained under the lease or licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you fraudulently conceal or make a false statement with respect to the amount of valuable minerals obtained under the lease or licence?
      `what the mineral is` IS A `s 2 valuable mineral kind` @desc What mineral is it (section 2, "valuable mineral")? Choose the one that applies.
      `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram?
      `the person sells the mineral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you sell the mineral?
      `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed?
      `the person is the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority?
      `the person buys the mineral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you buy the mineral?
      `the person has reason to believe that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have reason to believe that the seller are not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 394(5), am I guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3), and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 394(5) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3)` (`s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` `the person is the holder of a lease or licence issued under an Act relating to the mining of valuable minerals, or by the owner of land that is supposed to contain valuable minerals` `the person, by a fraudulent device or contrivance, defrauds or attempts to defraud any person` `the person is defrauded of valuable minerals obtained under or reserved by the lease or licence` `the person is defrauded of money or a valuable interest or thing payable in respect of valuable minerals obtained or rights reserved by the lease or licence` `the person fraudulently conceals or makes a false statement with respect to the amount of valuable minerals obtained under the lease or licence` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`) (`s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` `the person sells the mineral` `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed` `the person is the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`) (`s 394(3) the person contravenes subsection (3)` `the person buys the mineral` `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed` `the person has reason to believe that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`))
        (JUST `s 394(5) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 394(5) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

