      `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that, contrary to the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, any valuable mineral is deposited in a place or held by a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that, contrary to the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, any valuable mineral is deposited in a place or held by a person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
