    `s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` `an information in writing is laid under oath before a justice` (`s 2 peace officer` `capacity (peace officer)`) (`s 2 public officer` `capacity (public officer)`) `the public officer has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and its duties include the enforcement of the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that, contrary to the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, any valuable mineral is deposited in a place or held by a person`

