GIVEN `the order was made under paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order was made under paragraph (2)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 395(3), does an appeal lie from the order` MEANS
    `s 395(3) an appeal lies from the order` `the order was made under paragraph (2)(b)`

-- calls `s 396(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples`, `s 396(1) the class of the offence` and `s 396(1) the punishments`
@export Under section 396(1), is what I did the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person adds anything to or removes anything from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you add anything to or remove anything from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well?
      `the person adds anything to, removes anything from or tampers with a sample or material taken from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well for the purpose of being assayed, tested or otherwise valued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you add anything to, remove anything from or tamper with a sample or material taken from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well for the purpose of being assayed, tested or otherwise valued?
      `the person acts with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of the assay, test or valuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of the assay, test or valuation?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 396(1), is what I did the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 396(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples` `the person adds anything to or removes anything from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well` `the person adds anything to, removes anything from or tampers with a sample or material taken from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well for the purpose of being assayed, tested or otherwise valued` `the person acts with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of the assay, test or valuation`)
        (JUST `s 396(1) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 396(1) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 396(2) the evidence is proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation`
@export Under section 396(2), is the evidence proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceedings are under subsection (1)?
      `there is evidence that something has been added to or removed from anything to which subsection (1) applies, or that it has been tampered with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is evidence that something has been added to or removed from anything to which subsection (1) applies, or that it has been tampered with?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 396(2), is the evidence proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation` MEANS
    `s 396(2) the evidence is proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation` `the proceedings are under subsection (1)` `there is evidence that something has been added to or removed from anything to which subsection (1) applies, or that it has been tampered with` `there is evidence to the contrary`

§ `False documents and identity, ss 397 to 405`

-- calls `s 397(1) the conduct is the offence of falsifying a book or document`, `s 397(1) the class of the offence` and `s 397(1) the punishments`
@export Under section 397(1), is what I did the offence of falsifying a book or document, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with intent to defraud?
      `the thing is a book, paper, writing or document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is a book, paper, writing or document?
      `what the thing is, as a valuable security` IS A `s 2 valuable security kind` @desc What kind of valuable security is it (section 2, "valuable security")? Choose the one that applies.
      `the person destroys, mutilates, alters, falsifies or makes a false entry in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you destroy, mutilate, alter, falsify or make a false entry in it?
      `the person omits a material particular from, or alters a material particular in, it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you omit a material particular from, or alter a material particular in, it?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 397(1), is what I did the offence of falsifying a book or document, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 397(1) the conduct is the offence of falsifying a book or document` `the person acts with intent to defraud` `the thing is a book, paper, writing or document` `what the thing is, as a valuable security` `the person destroys, mutilates, alters, falsifies or makes a false entry in it` `the person omits a material particular from, or alters a material particular in, it`)
        (JUST `s 397(1) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 397(1) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 397(2) the conduct is the offence of being privy to the falsifying of a book or document`, `s 397(2) the class of the offence` and `s 397(2) the punishments`
@export Under section 397(2), is what I did the offence of being privy to the falsifying of a book or document, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to defraud their creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with intent to defraud their creditors?
      `the person is privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1)?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 397(2), is what I did the offence of being privy to the falsifying of a book or document, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 397(2) the conduct is the offence of being privy to the falsifying of a book or document` `the person acts with intent to defraud their creditors` `the person is privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1)`)
        (JUST `s 397(2) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 397(2) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

