      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 401(1), is what I did the offence of obtaining carriage by false billing, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 401(1) the conduct is the offence of obtaining carriage by false billing` `the person acts by means of a false or misleading representation` `the person knowingly obtains or attempts to obtain the carriage of anything by any person into a country, province, district or other place` `the importation or transportation of it is, in the circumstances of the case, unlawful there`)
        (JUST `s 401(1) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 401(1) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 401(2) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty`
@export Under section 401(2), is the thing forfeited to Her Majesty?
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are convicted of an offence under subsection (1)?
      `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 401(2), is the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    `s 401(2) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1)` `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed`

-- calls `s 402.1 the information is identity information`
@export Under section 402.1, is the information identity information?
GIVEN `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` IS A NUMBER @desc For which section of the Code do you ask whether the information is identity information? (Enter the section number, for example 402.2 or 403.)
      `kind (s 402.1)` IS A `s 402.1 kind of information` @desc Choose the kind of information that applies (section 402.1).
      `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 402.1, is the information identity information` MEANS
    `s 402.1 the information is identity information` `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` `kind (s 402.1)` `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual`

-- calls `s 402.2(1) the conduct is the offence of identity theft`, `s 402.2(5) the class of the offence` and `s 402.2(5) the punishments`
@export Under section 402.2(1), is what I did the offence of identity theft, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person obtains or possesses another person’s identity information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you obtain or possess another person’s identity information?
      `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` IS A NUMBER @desc For which section of the Code do you ask whether the information is identity information? (Enter the section number, for example 402.2 or 403.)
      `kind (s 402.1)` IS A `s 402.1 kind of information` @desc Choose the kind of information that applies (section 402.1).
      `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual?
      `the person acts with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence?
      `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence?
      `the offence (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the offence (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 402.2(1), is what I did the offence of identity theft, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 402.2(1) the conduct is the offence of identity theft` `the person obtains or possesses another person’s identity information` (`s 402.1 the information is identity information` `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` `kind (s 402.1)` `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual`) `the person acts with intent to use it to commit an indictable offence` `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` (`s 402.2(3) the offence is one the subsection includes` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence (section number)`, `the offence (subsection)`)))
        (JUST `s 402.2(5) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 402.2(5) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 402.2(2) the conduct is the offence of trafficking in identity information`, `s 402.2(5) the class of the offence` and `s 402.2(5) the punishments`
@export Under section 402.2(2), is what I did the offence of trafficking in identity information, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person transmits, makes available, distributes, sells or offers for sale another person’s identity information, or has it in their possession for any of those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you transmit, make available, distribute, sell or offer for sale another person’s identity information, or have it in their possession for any of those purposes?
      `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` IS A NUMBER @desc For which section of the Code do you ask whether the information is identity information? (Enter the section number, for example 402.2 or 403.)
      `kind (s 402.1)` IS A `s 402.1 kind of information` @desc Choose the kind of information that applies (section 402.1).
      `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual?
      `the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the information will be used to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know that, or are reckless as to whether, the information will be used to commit an indictable offence?
      `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence?
      `the offence (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the offence (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 402.2(2), is what I did the offence of trafficking in identity information, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 402.2(2) the conduct is the offence of trafficking in identity information` `the person transmits, makes available, distributes, sells or offers for sale another person’s identity information, or has it in their possession for any of those purposes` (`s 402.1 the information is identity information` `the section for whose purposes the question is asked` `kind (s 402.1)` `the information is of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual`) `the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, the information will be used to commit an indictable offence` `that offence includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` (`s 402.2(3) the offence is one the subsection includes` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence (section number)`, `the offence (subsection)`)))
        (JUST `s 402.2(5) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 402.2(5) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 402.2(3) the offence is one the subsection includes`
