-- calls `s 415(a) the conduct is the offence of concealing wreck`, `s 415 the class of the offence` and `s 415 the punishments`
@export Under section 415(a), is what I did the offence of concealing wreck, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `s 2 wreck kind` @desc What is the thing (section 2, "wreck")? Choose the one that applies.
      `the person secretes wreck, defaces or obliterates the marks on wreck, uses any means to disguise or conceal the fact that anything is wreck, or in any manner conceals the character of wreck` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you secrete wreck, deface or obliterate the marks on wreck, use any means to disguise or conceal the fact that anything are wreck, or in any manner conceal the character of wreck?
      `the concealment is from a person who is entitled to inquire into the wreck` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the concealment is from a person who is entitled to inquire into the wreck?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 415(a), is what I did the offence of concealing wreck, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 415(a) the conduct is the offence of concealing wreck` `what the thing is` `the person secretes wreck, defaces or obliterates the marks on wreck, uses any means to disguise or conceal the fact that anything is wreck, or in any manner conceals the character of wreck` `the concealment is from a person who is entitled to inquire into the wreck`)
        (JUST `s 415 the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 415 the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver`, `s 415 the class of the offence` and `s 415 the punishments`
@export Under section 415(b), is what I did the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `s 2 wreck kind` @desc What is the thing (section 2, "wreck")? Choose the one that applies.
      `the person receives wreck, knowing that it is wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you receive wreck, knowing that it are wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck?
      `the hours since the person received the wreck` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours have passed since you received the wreck?
      `the person informed the receiver of wreck` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you inform the receiver of wreck that you had received the wreck?
      `the hours after receipt at which the person informed the receiver of wreck` IS A NUMBER @desc If you informed the receiver of wreck, how many hours after you received the wreck did you do so? (Enter 0 if you did not.)
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 415(b), is what I did the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `what the thing is` `the person receives wreck, knowing that it is wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck` `the hours since the person received the wreck` (IF `the person informed the receiver of wreck` THEN JUST `the hours after receipt at which the person informed the receiver of wreck` ELSE NOTHING))
        (JUST `s 415 the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 415 the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

