@export Under section 420(1), is what I did the offence of buying military stores, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person buys, receives or detains military stores from a member of the Canadian Forces or from a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you buy, receive or detain military stores from a member of the Canadian Forces or from a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom?
      `the stores are owned by Her Majesty or are stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave is accountable to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the stores are owned by Her Majesty or are stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave is accountable to Her Majesty?
      `the person establishes that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you establish that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave were accountable to Her Majesty?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 420(1), is what I did the offence of buying military stores, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 420(1) the conduct is the offence of buying military stores` `the person buys, receives or detains military stores from a member of the Canadian Forces or from a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom` `the stores are owned by Her Majesty or are stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave is accountable to Her Majesty` (`s 420(2) the person is saved from conviction of an offence under section 420` `the person establishes that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty`))
        (JUST `s 420(1) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 420(1) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 420(2) the person is saved from conviction of an offence under section 420`
@export Under section 420(2), am I saved from conviction of an offence under section 420?
GIVEN `the person establishes that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you establish that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave were accountable to Her Majesty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 420(2), am I saved from conviction of an offence under section 420` MEANS
    `s 420(2) the person is saved from conviction of an offence under section 420` `the person establishes that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty`

