§ `Contracts, intimidation, threats and secret commissions, ss 422 to 427`

-- calls `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract`, `s 422(1) the class of the offence` and `s 422(1) the punishments`
@export Under section 422(1), is what I did the offence of criminal breach of contract, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person wilfully breaks a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you wilfully break a contract?
      `the person knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the probable consequences of doing so, whether alone or in combination with others, will be the consequence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know or have reasonable cause to believe that the probable consequences of doing so, whether alone or in combination with others, will be the consequence?
      `consequence (s 422(1))` IS A `s 422(1) probable consequence` @desc Choose the probable consequence that applies (section 422(1)).
      `reason (s 422(2))` IS A `s 422(2) reason for stopping work` @desc Choose the reason for stopping work that applies (section 422(2)).
      `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to have wilfully broken the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to have wilfully broken the contract?
      `before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken?
      `any provision for the final settlement of differences, without stoppage of work, contained in or by law deemed to be contained in a collective agreement is complied with and effect given thereto` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any provision for the final settlement of differences, without stoppage of work, contained in or by law deemed to be contained in a collective agreement is complied with and effect given thereto?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 422(1), is what I did the offence of criminal breach of contract, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` `the person wilfully breaks a contract` `the person knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the probable consequences of doing so, whether alone or in combination with others, will be the consequence` `consequence (s 422(1))` (`s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` `reason (s 422(2))` `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to have wilfully broken the contract` `before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken` `any provision for the final settlement of differences, without stoppage of work, contained in or by law deemed to be contained in a collective agreement is complied with and effect given thereto`))
        (JUST `s 422(1) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 422(1) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)`
