GIVEN `the person is an agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an agent?
      `the person is an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an employee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 426(4), is the person an agent` MEANS
    `s 426(4) the person is an agent` `the person is an agent` `the person is an employee`

§ `Mischief, ss 428 to 432`

-- calls `s 428 property`
@export Under section 428, is the thing property?
GIVEN `the thing is real or personal corporeal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is real or personal corporeal property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 428, is the thing property` MEANS
    `s 428 property` `the thing is real or personal corporeal property`

-- calls `s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event`
@export Under section 429(1), am I deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event?
GIVEN `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you cause the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it are their duty to do?
      `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event?
      `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are reckless whether the event occurs or not?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 429(1), am I deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` MEANS
    `s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not`

-- calls `s 429(2) the person shall not be convicted of the offence`
@export Under section 429(2), is it the case that the person shall not be convicted of the offence?
GIVEN `the offence (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the offence (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the offence, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `the person acts with legal justification or excuse or colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act with legal justification or excuse or colour of right?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 429(2), is it the case that the person shall not be convicted of the offence` MEANS
    `s 429(2) the person shall not be convicted of the offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence (section number)`, `the offence (subsection)`) `the person acts with legal justification or excuse or colour of right`

-- calls `s 429(3)(a) the person’s partial interest does not prevent guilt of the offence`
@export Under section 429(3)(a), does the person’s partial interest not prevent guilt of the offence?
GIVEN `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing?
      `the person has a partial interest in what is destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have a partial interest in what are destroyed or damaged?
      `the person caused the destruction or damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you caused the destruction or damage?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 429(3)(a), does the person’s partial interest not prevent guilt of the offence` MEANS
    `s 429(3)(a) the person’s partial interest does not prevent guilt of the offence` `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing` `the person has a partial interest in what is destroyed or damaged` `the person caused the destruction or damage`

-- calls `s 429(3)(b) the person’s total interest does not prevent guilt of the offence`
@export Under section 429(3)(b), does the person’s total interest not prevent guilt of the offence?
GIVEN `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing?
      `the person has a total interest in what is destroyed or damaged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have a total interest in what are destroyed or damaged?
      `the person caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 429(3)(b), does the person’s total interest not prevent guilt of the offence` MEANS
    `s 429(3)(b) the person’s total interest does not prevent guilt of the offence` `it is an offence to destroy or to damage the thing` `the person has a total interest in what is destroyed or damaged` `the person caused the destruction or damage with intent to defraud`

-- calls `s 430(1) the conduct is mischief in relation to property`
@export Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property?
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act wilfully?
      `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you cause the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it are their duty to do?
      `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event?
      `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are reckless whether the event occurs or not?
      `act (s 430(1))` IS A `s 430(1) act` @desc Choose the act that applies (section 430(1)).
      `the thing is real or personal corporeal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is real or personal corporeal property?
      `reason (s 430(6))` IS A `s 430(6) reason for stopping work` @desc Choose the reason for stopping work that applies (section 430(6)).
      `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief?
      `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you attend at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place?
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 430(1), is what I did mischief in relation to property` MEANS
    `s 430(1) the conduct is mischief in relation to property` `the person acts wilfully` (`s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not`) `act (s 430(1))` (`s 428 property` `the thing is real or personal corporeal property`) (`s 430(6) the person is saved from committing mischief` `reason (s 430(6))` `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief`) (`s 430(7) the person is saved from committing mischief` `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`)

-- calls `s 430(1.1) the conduct is mischief in relation to computer data`
@export Under section 430(1.1), is what I did mischief in relation to computer data?
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act wilfully?
      `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you cause the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it are their duty to do?
      `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event?
      `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are reckless whether the event occurs or not?
      `act (s 430(1.1))` IS A `s 430(1.1) act` @desc Choose the act that applies (section 430(1.1)).
      `s 342.1(2) computer data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is computer data (as section 342.1(2) of the Criminal Code defines it)?
      `reason (s 430(6))` IS A `s 430(6) reason for stopping work` @desc Choose the reason for stopping work that applies (section 430(6)).
      `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief?
      `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you attend at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place?
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 430(1.1), is what I did mischief in relation to computer data` MEANS
    `s 430(1.1) the conduct is mischief in relation to computer data` `the person acts wilfully` (`s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not`) `act (s 430(1.1))` (`s 430(8) the thing is computer data` (JUST `s 342.1(2) computer data`)) (`s 430(6) the person is saved from committing mischief` `reason (s 430(6))` `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief`) (`s 430(7) the person is saved from committing mischief` `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`)

-- calls `s 430(2) the conduct is the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life`, `s 430(2) the class of the offence` and `s 430(2) the punishments`
@export Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act wilfully?
      `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you cause the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it are their duty to do?
      `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event?
      `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are reckless whether the event occurs or not?
      `act (s 430(1))` IS A `s 430(1) act` @desc Choose the act that applies (section 430(1)).
      `the thing is real or personal corporeal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is real or personal corporeal property?
      `reason (s 430(6))` IS A `s 430(6) reason for stopping work` @desc Choose the reason for stopping work that applies (section 430(6)).
      `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief?
      `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you attend at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place?
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information?
      `act (s 430(1.1))` IS A `s 430(1.1) act` @desc Choose the act that applies (section 430(1.1)).
      `s 342.1(2) computer data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is computer data (as section 342.1(2) of the Criminal Code defines it)?
      `the mischief causes actual danger to life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mischief causes actual danger to life?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 430(2), is what I did the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 430(2) the conduct is the offence of mischief that causes actual danger to life` (`ccc13 any of` (LIST `s 430(1) the conduct is mischief in relation to property` `the person acts wilfully` (`s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not`) `act (s 430(1))` (`s 428 property` `the thing is real or personal corporeal property`) (`s 430(6) the person is saved from committing mischief` `reason (s 430(6))` `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief`) (`s 430(7) the person is saved from committing mischief` `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`), `s 430(1.1) the conduct is mischief in relation to computer data` `the person acts wilfully` (`s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not`) `act (s 430(1.1))` (`s 430(8) the thing is computer data` (JUST `s 342.1(2) computer data`)) (`s 430(6) the person is saved from committing mischief` `reason (s 430(6))` `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief`) (`s 430(7) the person is saved from committing mischief` `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`))) `the mischief causes actual danger to life`)
        (JUST `s 430(2) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 430(2) the punishments`))

-- calls `s 430(3) the conduct is the offence of mischief in relation to property of great value`, `s 430(3) the class of the offence` and `s 430(3) the punishments`
@export Under section 430(3), is what I did the offence of mischief in relation to property of great value, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act wilfully?
      `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you cause the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it are their duty to do?
      `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you know that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event?
      `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are reckless whether the event occurs or not?
      `act (s 430(1))` IS A `s 430(1) act` @desc Choose the act that applies (section 430(1)).
      `the thing is real or personal corporeal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the thing is real or personal corporeal property?
      `reason (s 430(6))` IS A `s 430(6) reason for stopping work` @desc Choose the reason for stopping work that applies (section 430(6)).
      `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief?
      `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you attend at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place?
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information?
      `the property is a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property a testamentary instrument (a will, a codicil, or another testamentary writing or appointment)? Answer in your own judgment; the Code says only that the term includes those.
      `the value of the property, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the property, in dollars?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 430(3), is what I did the offence of mischief in relation to property of great value, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 430(3) the conduct is the offence of mischief in relation to property of great value` (`s 430(1) the conduct is mischief in relation to property` `the person acts wilfully` (`s 429(1) the person is deemed wilfully to have caused the occurrence of the event` `the person causes the occurrence of an event by doing an act or by omitting to do an act that it is their duty to do` `the person knows that the act or omission will probably cause the occurrence of the event` `the person is reckless whether the event occurs or not`) `act (s 430(1))` (`s 428 property` `the thing is real or personal corporeal property`) (`s 430(6) the person is saved from committing mischief` `reason (s 430(6))` `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to commit mischief`) (`s 430(7) the person is saved from committing mischief` `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`)) (`s 430(3) the property is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars` (JUST `the property is a testamentary instrument`) `the value of the property, in dollars`))
        (JUST `s 430(3) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 430(3) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 430(3) the property is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars`
@export Under section 430(3), is the property a testamentary instrument, or does its value exceed five thousand dollars?
GIVEN `the property is a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property a testamentary instrument (a will, a codicil, or another testamentary writing or appointment)? Answer in your own judgment; the Code says only that the term includes those.
      `the value of the property, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the property, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 430(3), is the property a testamentary instrument, or does its value exceed five thousand dollars` MEANS
    `s 430(3) the property is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars` (JUST `the property is a testamentary instrument`) `the value of the property, in dollars`

