-- calls `s 443(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with international boundary marks, etc.`, `s 443(1) the class of the offence` and `s 443(1) the punishments`
@export Under section 443(1), is what I did the offence of interfering with international boundary marks, etc., and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person intentionally pulls down, defaces, alters or removes the boundary mark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you intentionally pull down, deface, alter or remove the boundary mark?
      `the mark is a boundary mark lawfully placed to mark any international, provincial, county or municipal boundary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mark is a boundary mark lawfully placed to mark any international, provincial, county or municipal boundary?
      `the mark is a boundary mark lawfully placed by a land surveyor to mark any limit, boundary or angle of a concession, range, lot or parcel of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mark is a boundary mark lawfully placed by a land surveyor to mark any limit, boundary or angle of a concession, range, lot or parcel of land?
      `the person is a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor?
      `the person takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before taking it up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you take up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it were before taking it up?
      `the person takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you take up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position?
      `the person establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you establish a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 443(1), is what I did the offence of interfering with international boundary marks, etc., and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 443(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with international boundary marks, etc.` `the person intentionally pulls down, defaces, alters or removes the boundary mark` `the mark is a boundary mark lawfully placed to mark any international, provincial, county or municipal boundary` `the mark is a boundary mark lawfully placed by a land surveyor to mark any limit, boundary or angle of a concession, range, lot or parcel of land` (`s 443(2) the land surveyor does not commit an offence under subsection (1)` `the person is a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor` `the person takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before taking it up` `the person takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position` `the person establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained`))
        (JUST `s 443(1) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 443(1) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 443(2) the land surveyor does not commit an offence under subsection (1)`
@export Under section 443(2), does the land surveyor not commit an offence under subsection (1)?
GIVEN `the person is a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor?
      `the person takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before taking it up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you take up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it were before taking it up?
      `the person takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you take up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position?
      `the person establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you establish a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 443(2), does the land surveyor not commit an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    `s 443(2) the land surveyor does not commit an offence under subsection (1)` `the person is a land surveyor acting in their operations as a land surveyor` `the person takes up, when necessary, a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) and carefully replaces it as it was before taking it up` `the person takes up a boundary mark mentioned in paragraph (1)(b) in the course of surveying for a highway or other work that, when completed, will make it impossible or impracticable for that boundary mark to occupy its original position` `the person establishes a permanent record of the original position sufficient to permit that position to be ascertained`

§ `Animals, ss 444 to 447.1`

-- calls `s 445(1) the conduct is the offence of injuring or endangering other animals`, `s 445(2) the class of the offence` and `s 445(2) the punishments`
@export Under section 445(1), is what I did the offence of injuring or endangering other animals, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person acts wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act wilfully?
      `the person acts without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you act without lawful excuse?
      `the person kills, maims, wounds, poisons or injures dogs, birds or animals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you kill, maim, wound, poison or injure dogs, birds or animals?
      `the person places poison in such a position that it may easily be consumed by dogs, birds or animals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you place poison in such a position that it may easily be consumed by dogs, birds or animals?
      `the dogs, birds or animals are kept for a lawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the dogs, birds or animals are kept for a lawful purpose?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
