GIVEN `the person by wilful neglect causes damage or injury to animals or birds while they are being driven or conveyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you by wilful neglect cause damage or injury to animals or birds while they are being driven or conveyed?
      `the person is the owner or the person having the custody or control of a domestic animal or a bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are the owner or the person having the custody or control of a domestic animal or a bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is in captivity?
      `the person abandons it in distress or wilfully neglects or fails to provide suitable and adequate food, water, shelter and care for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you abandon it in distress or wilfully neglect or fail to provide suitable and adequate food, water, shelter and care for it?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 446(1), is what I did the offence of causing damage or injury to animals, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 446(1) the conduct is the offence of causing damage or injury to animals` `the person by wilful neglect causes damage or injury to animals or birds while they are being driven or conveyed` `the person is the owner or the person having the custody or control of a domestic animal or a bird or an animal or a bird wild by nature that is in captivity` `the person abandons it in distress or wilfully neglects or fails to provide suitable and adequate food, water, shelter and care for it`)
        (JUST `s 446(2) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 446(2) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 446(3) the evidence is proof that the damage or injury was caused by wilful neglect`
@export Under section 446(3), is the evidence proof that the damage or injury was caused by wilful neglect?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(a)?
      `there is evidence that the person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it damage or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is evidence that the person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it damage or injury?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 446(3), is the evidence proof that the damage or injury was caused by wilful neglect` MEANS
    `s 446(3) the evidence is proof that the damage or injury was caused by wilful neglect` `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)(a)` `there is evidence that the person failed to exercise reasonable care or supervision of an animal or a bird thereby causing it damage or injury` `there is evidence to the contrary`

-- calls `s 447(1) the conduct is the offence of keeping an arena for animal fighting`, `s 447(2) the class of the offence` and `s 447(2) the punishments`
@export Under section 447(1), is what I did the offence of keeping an arena for animal fighting, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person builds, makes, maintains or keeps an arena for animal fighting on premises that the person owns or occupies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you build, make, maintain or keep an arena for animal fighting on premises that the person own or occupy?
      `the person allows such an arena to be built, made, maintained or kept on such premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you allow such an arena to be built, made, maintained or kept on such premises?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 447(1), is what I did the offence of keeping an arena for animal fighting, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 447(1) the conduct is the offence of keeping an arena for animal fighting` `the person builds, makes, maintains or keeps an arena for animal fighting on premises that the person owns or occupies` `the person allows such an arena to be built, made, maintained or kept on such premises`)
        (JUST `s 447(2) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 447(2) the punishments`))

-- calls `s 447.1(1)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused from owning or having an animal or a bird`
@export Under section 447.1(1)(a), may the court make an order prohibiting the accused from owning or having an animal or a bird?
GIVEN `the sentence for which the order is made (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the sentence for which the order is made? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the sentence for which the order is made (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the sentence for which the order is made, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 447.1(1)(a), may the court make an order prohibiting the accused from owning or having an animal or a bird` MEANS
    `s 447.1(1)(a) the court may make an order prohibiting the accused from owning or having an animal or a bird` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the sentence for which the order is made (section number)`, `the sentence for which the order is made (subsection)`)

-- calls `s 447.1(1)(a) the prohibition must be for a minimum of five years`
@export Under section 447.1(1)(a), must the prohibition be for a minimum of five years?
GIVEN `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence is a second or subsequent offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 447.1(1)(a), must the prohibition be for a minimum of five years` MEANS
    `s 447.1(1)(a) the prohibition must be for a minimum of five years` `the offence is a second or subsequent offence`

-- calls `s 447.1(1)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of taking care of the animal or bird`
@export Under section 447.1(1)(b), may the court order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of taking care of the animal or bird?
GIVEN `the sentence for which the order is made (section number)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the sentence for which the order is made? (for example 380 or 445.01)
      `the sentence for which the order is made (subsection)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of the sentence for which the order is made, written as the Code writes it, for example (2)? (Leave it empty if there is none.)
      `the Attorney General has applied or the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Attorney General has applied or the court acts on its own motion?
      `the payee is a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal or a bird as a result of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the payee is a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal or a bird as a result of the commission of the offence?
      `the costs are readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the costs are readily ascertainable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 447.1(1)(b), may the court order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of taking care of the animal or bird` MEANS
    `s 447.1(1)(b) the court may order the accused to pay the reasonable costs of taking care of the animal or bird` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the sentence for which the order is made (section number)`, `the sentence for which the order is made (subsection)`) `the Attorney General has applied or the court acts on its own motion` `the payee is a person or an organization that has taken care of an animal or a bird as a result of the commission of the offence` `the costs are readily ascertainable`

-- calls `s 447.1(2) the conduct is the offence of contravening an order of prohibition`, `s 447.1(2) the class of the offence` and `s 447.1(2) the punishments`
@export Under section 447.1(2), is what I did the offence of contravening an order of prohibition, and what are its class and punishments?
GIVEN `the person contravenes an order made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you contravene an order made under paragraph (1)(a)?
      `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Section 787(1) is outside Parts X and XI, so this question asks you for it.)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) of the Criminal Code sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction? (Enter 0 if it sets none.)
      `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that maximum term of imprisonment "less a day" (for example, two years less a day is 24 months, less a day)?
GIVETH A `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence`
`Under section 447.1(2), is what I did the offence of contravening an order of prohibition, and what are its class and punishments` MEANS
    `s 380 to 447.1 answer about an offence` OF
        (`s 447.1(2) the conduct is the offence of contravening an order of prohibition` `the person contravenes an order made under paragraph (1)(a)`)
        (JUST `s 447.1(2) the class of the offence`)
        (JUST (`s 447.1(2) the punishments` (`ccc13 seat the s 787(1) penalty` `the maximum fine, in dollars, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, that section 787(1) sets for an offence punishable on summary conviction` `that maximum term of imprisonment under section 787(1) is less a day`)))

-- calls `s 447.1(3) sections 740 to 741.2 apply to the order`
@export Under section 447.1(3), do sections 740 to 741.2 apply to the order?
GIVEN `the order is made under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is made under paragraph (1)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 447.1(3), do sections 740 to 741.2 apply to the order` MEANS
    `s 447.1(3) sections 740 to 741.2 apply to the order` `the order is made under paragraph (1)(b)`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc14 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc14-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER over ccc14's layer 1 (Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, lines 7875-8523: PART XII Offences Relating to Currency,
-- PART XII.2 Proceeds of Crime, PART XIII Attempts, Conspiracies, Accessories).
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an
-- offence, what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply, and what follows from a conviction.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, a short choice) that the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person
-- would be asked. The layer-1 rules are called with those inputs and never restated here. Where a layer-1 rule takes the answer of a definition in another provision
-- (for example "counterfeit money", section 448, which "includes" a list), the person states that fact yes or no: a yes is JUST TRUE; a no is NOT COVERED (NOTHING),
-- never a no, because an "includes" definition does not say no. Where the definition "means" something, a no is JUST FALSE. Each use is marked below.
-- A result of JUST TRUE is a yes on the text's own words; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
-- Questions are named for what the answer says. Offence questions ask "have I committed ...", a bar is asked as "is ... barred", a power is asked as "may ...".
-- A question about a provision that addresses only an official (a judge, the Attorney General, a peace officer, a clerk) asks what it means for the person.
-- Not encoded as questions in this layer (they have no fact the person can state, or are machinery): the regulation-making powers of ss 462.3(2), 462.5 and 467.1(4).
-- NEEDS-CORE.md lists what the lead should hoist. The pure helpers below carry the prefix `ccc14 seat ` (they belong to no provision).

-- A yes to an "includes" definition is JUST TRUE; a no is NOT COVERED, never a no.
GIVEN yes IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc14 seat includes answer` MEANS
    IF yes
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the definition lists without closing the list, so a person who states "no" is not covered, not excluded

-- A yes to a "means" definition is JUST TRUE; a no is JUST FALSE (the text closes the definition).
GIVEN yes IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc14 seat means answer` MEANS
    IF yes
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the definition "means" the stated thing and nothing else

-- The form of the charge, as one short word.
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 2 form of the charge`
`ccc14 seat form of the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF word EQUALS "offence" THEN `the offence itself`
        IF word EQUALS "conspiracy" THEN `a conspiracy to commit the offence`
        IF word EQUALS "attempt" THEN `an attempt to commit the offence`
        IF word EQUALS "accessory" THEN `being an accessory after the fact in relation to the offence`
        IF word EQUALS "counselling" THEN `counselling in relation to the offence`
        OTHERWISE `a form of participation that is none of those`

-- The class of an offence from two yes-or-no answers.
GIVEN indictable IS A BOOLEAN, summary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`ccc14 seat class of the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF indictable AND summary THEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
        IF indictable THEN `an indictable offence`
        OTHERWISE `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- The longest term of imprisonment from "life" and a number of years (0 means none is stated).
GIVEN life IS A BOOLEAN, years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`ccc14 seat longest term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF life THEN `imprisonment for life`
        IF years GREATER THAN 0 THEN `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF FLOOR years, FLOOR ((years MINUS FLOOR years) TIMES 12), 0, FALSE)
        OTHERWISE `no imprisonment is stated`

-- The indictable limb (or only limb) of an offence, from "life" and a number of years.
GIVEN life IS A BOOLEAN, years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Punishment
`ccc14 seat indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `ccc14 seat longest term` life years, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- The limbs of an offence the person describes (an indictable limb, a summary limb, or both).
GIVEN indictable IS A BOOLEAN, summary IS A BOOLEAN, life IS A BOOLEAN, years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`ccc14 seat punishment limbs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF indictable AND summary
        THEN LIST (`ccc14 seat indictable limb` life years), (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
        IF indictable THEN LIST (`ccc14 seat indictable limb` life years)
        OTHERWISE LIST (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

-- The longest term of imprisonment on indictment among a list of limbs.
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Punishment
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`ccc14 seat the longest term on indictment` MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no imprisonment is stated`
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF p's `mode` EQUALS `by indictment`
        THEN p's `maximum imprisonment`
        ELSE `ccc14 seat the longest term on indictment` rest

§ `PART XII -- Offences Relating to Currency (ss 448 to 462)`
-- Ask this group if you are, or may be, accused of making, having, passing or dealing in counterfeit money, coins, tokens or likenesses of bank-notes.

@export Under section 448, is the thing counterfeit money?
GIVEN `false coin or paper money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a false coin or false paper money that resembles, or is apparently intended to resemble or pass for, a current coin or current paper money?
      `forged bank-note` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a forged bank-note or a forged blank bank-note, complete or incomplete?
      `altered genuine money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a genuine coin or genuine paper money that is prepared or altered to resemble or pass for current money of a higher denomination?
      `re-milled coin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a current coin from which the milling was removed by filing or cutting the edges and on which new milling was made to restore its appearance?
      `cased coin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a coin cased with gold, silver or nickel that is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin?
      `washed or coloured coin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a coin or piece of metal that is washed or coloured to look like gold, silver or nickel and is intended to resemble or pass for a current gold, silver or nickel coin?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448, is the thing counterfeit money` IS
    `s 448 counterfeit money` `false coin or paper money` `forged bank-note` `altered genuine money` `re-milled coin` `cased coin` `washed or coloured coin`

@export Under section 448, is the thing a counterfeit token of value?
GIVEN `counterfeit stamp or evidence of value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a counterfeit excise stamp, postage stamp or other evidence of value, by whatever name it is described?
      `valueless genuine money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it genuine coin or paper money that has no value as money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448, is the thing a counterfeit token of value` IS
    `s 448 counterfeit token of value` `counterfeit stamp or evidence of value` `valueless genuine money`

@export Under section 448, is the coin or paper money current?
GIVEN `lawfully current` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it lawfully current in Canada or elsewhere by virtue of a law, proclamation or regulation in force in Canada or elsewhere?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448, is the coin or paper money current` IS
    `s 448 current` `lawfully current`

@export Under section 448, is what I did uttering?
GIVEN `I sold, paid, tendered or put it off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sell, pay, tender or put off the coin or money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 448, is what I did uttering` IS
    `s 448 utter` (IF `I sold, paid, tendered or put it off` THEN `s 448 sell` ELSE `s 448 an act that is none of those named`)

@export Under section 449, have I committed the offence of making counterfeit money?
GIVEN `counterfeit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing counterfeit money (see the section 448 question)?
      `I made or began to make it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it, or begin to make it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 449, have I committed the offence of making counterfeit money` IS
    `s 449 the person commits the offence of making counterfeit money` (`ccc14 seat includes answer` `counterfeit`) `I made or began to make it`

@export Under section 449, what punishment can I be given for making counterfeit money?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 449, what punishment can I be given for making counterfeit money` IS
    `s 449 the punishment`

@export Under section 450, have I committed the offence of buying, having or bringing in counterfeit money?
GIVEN `counterfeit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing counterfeit money?
      `I had no lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have NO lawful justification or excuse? (Answer yes if you had none.)
      `I bought, received or offered to buy or receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you buy, receive, or offer to buy or receive it?
      `I had it in my custody or possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have it in your custody or possession?
      `I brought it into Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you bring it into Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 450, have I committed the offence of buying, having or bringing in counterfeit money` IS
    `s 450 the person commits the offence of possessing, etc., counterfeit money` (`ccc14 seat includes answer` `counterfeit`) `I had no lawful justification or excuse` `I bought, received or offered to buy or receive it` `I had it in my custody or possession` `I brought it into Canada`

@export Under section 450, what punishment can I be given for buying, having or bringing in counterfeit money?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 450, what punishment can I be given for buying, having or bringing in counterfeit money` IS
    `s 450 the punishment`

@export Under section 451, have I committed the offence of having gold or silver clippings or filings?
GIVEN `I had no lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have NO lawful justification or excuse? (Answer yes if you had none.)
      `I had gold or silver filings, clippings or bullion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have in your custody or possession gold or silver filings, clippings or bullion, or gold or silver in dust, solution or otherwise?
      `it came from impairing a current coin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it produced or obtained by impairing, diminishing or lightening a current gold or silver coin?
      `I knew that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know it had been so produced or obtained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 451, have I committed the offence of having gold or silver clippings or filings` IS
    `s 451 the person commits the offence of having clippings, etc.` `I had no lawful justification or excuse` `I had gold or silver filings, clippings or bullion` `it came from impairing a current coin` `I knew that`

@export Under section 451, what punishment can I be given for having gold or silver clippings or filings?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 451, what punishment can I be given for having gold or silver clippings or filings` IS
    `s 451 the punishment`

@export Under section 452, have I committed the offence of uttering counterfeit money or taking it out of Canada?
GIVEN `counterfeit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing counterfeit money?
      `I had no lawful justification or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have NO lawful justification or excuse? (Answer yes if you had none.)
      `I uttered it or used it as genuine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you utter it, offer to utter it, or use it as if it were genuine?
      `I exported it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you export it, send it, or take it out of Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 452, have I committed the offence of uttering counterfeit money or taking it out of Canada` IS
    `s 452 the person commits the offence of uttering, etc., counterfeit money` (`ccc14 seat includes answer` `counterfeit`) `I had no lawful justification or excuse` `I uttered it or used it as genuine` `I exported it`

@export Under section 452, what punishment can I be given for uttering counterfeit money?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 452, what punishment can I be given for uttering counterfeit money` IS
    `s 452 the punishment`

@export Under section 453, have I committed the offence of uttering coin?
GIVEN `I meant to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mean to defraud?
      `I knew what I was doing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you utter it knowingly?
      `it is a coin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you uttered a coin?
      `the coin is current` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that coin current (lawfully current in Canada or elsewhere)?
      `it is a piece of metal that looks like a coin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it instead a piece of metal or mixed metals that resembles in size, figure or colour a current coin for which it was uttered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 453, have I committed the offence of uttering coin` IS
    `s 453 the person commits the offence of uttering coin` `I meant to defraud` `I knew what I was doing` `it is a coin` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the coin is current`) `it is a piece of metal that looks like a coin`

@export Under section 453, what punishment can I be given for uttering coin?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 453, what punishment can I be given for uttering coin` IS
    `s 453 the punishment`

@export Under section 454, have I committed the offence concerning slugs and tokens?
GIVEN `I had no lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have NO lawful excuse? (Answer yes if you had none.)
      `I made, sold or had it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you manufacture, produce, sell or have in your possession the thing?
      `it is meant to be used in place of a coin or token` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it intended to be fraudulently used in substitution for a coin or token of value that a coin or token-operated device is designed to receive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 454, have I committed the offence concerning slugs and tokens` IS
    `s 454 the person commits the offence concerning slugs and tokens` `I had no lawful excuse` `I made, sold or had it` `it is meant to be used in place of a coin or token`

@export Under section 454, what punishment can I be given for slugs and tokens?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 454, what punishment can I be given for slugs and tokens` IS
    `s 454 the punishment`

@export Under section 455, have I committed the offence of clipping coin or uttering clipped coin?
GIVEN `the coin is current` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the coin current?
      `it is a gold or silver coin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a gold or silver coin?
      `I impaired it so it would pass` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you impair, diminish or lighten it with intent that it should pass for a current gold or silver coin?
      `I uttered it knowing it was impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you utter a coin knowing that it had been impaired, diminished or lightened in that way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 455, have I committed the offence of clipping coin or uttering clipped coin` IS
    `s 455 the person commits the offence of clipping or of uttering clipped coin` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the coin is current`) `it is a gold or silver coin` `I impaired it so it would pass` `I uttered it knowing it was impaired`

@export Under section 455, what punishment can I be given for clipping or uttering clipped coin?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 455, what punishment can I be given for clipping or uttering clipped coin` IS
    `s 455 the punishment`

@export Under section 456, have I committed the offence of defacing current coins?
GIVEN `the coin is current` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the coin current?
      `I defaced it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deface it?
      `I uttered it after it was defaced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you utter it after it had been defaced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 456, have I committed the offence of defacing current coins` IS
    `s 456 the person commits the offence of defacing current coins` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the coin is current`) `I defaced it` `I uttered it after it was defaced`

@export Under section 456, what punishment can I be given for defacing current coins?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 456, what punishment can I be given for defacing current coins` IS
    `s 456 the punishment`

@export Under section 457(3), have I committed the offence of making or circulating a likeness of a bank-note or of a government or bank obligation or security?
