§ `PART XIII -- Attempts, Conspiracies, Accessories (ss 463 to 467.14)`
-- Ask this group if you are, or may be, accused of attempting an offence, helping afterwards, counselling an offence, conspiring, or taking part in a criminal organization.

@export Under section 463, have I committed an offence by attempting to commit an offence, or by being an accessory after the fact?
GIVEN `I attempted or was an accessory after the fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you attempt to commit an offence, or were you an accessory after the fact to its commission?
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another law expressly provide a different rule for this offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 463, have I committed an offence by attempting to commit an offence, or by being an accessory after the fact` IS
    `s 463 the person is guilty of an offence by attempting, or by being an accessory after the fact` `I attempted or was an accessory after the fact` `the law expressly provides otherwise`

@export Under section 463, what punishment can I be given for attempting an offence or being an accessory after the fact?
GIVEN `the offence is indictable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the offence attempted (or counselled) be prosecuted by indictment?
      `it can also be tried as a summary conviction offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it also be punished on summary conviction?
      `it carries life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the longest punishment for it, on indictment, imprisonment for life?
      `longest term in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If not life: what is the longest term of imprisonment for it on indictment, in years? (0 if the section states none)
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another law expressly provide a different rule for this offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
DECIDE `Under section 463, what punishment can I be given for attempting an offence or being an accessory after the fact` IS
    `s 463 the punishment for attempting to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to, an offence` (`ccc14 seat class of the offence` `the offence is indictable` `it can also be tried as a summary conviction offence`) (`ccc14 seat indictable limb` `it carries life imprisonment` `longest term in years`) `the law expressly provides otherwise`

