      `the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence in fact committed?
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another law expressly provide a different rule for this offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 464, have I committed an offence by counselling an offence that was not committed` IS
    `s 464 the person is guilty of an offence by counselling an offence that is not committed` `I counselled another person to commit an offence` `the offence was committed` `the law expressly provides otherwise`

@export Under section 464, what punishment can I be given for counselling an offence that was not committed?
GIVEN `the offence is indictable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the offence attempted (or counselled) be prosecuted by indictment?
      `it can also be tried as a summary conviction offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it also be punished on summary conviction?
      `it carries life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the longest punishment for it, on indictment, imprisonment for life?
      `longest term in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If not life: what is the longest term of imprisonment for it on indictment, in years? (0 if the section states none)
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another law expressly provide a different rule for this offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
DECIDE `Under section 464, what punishment can I be given for counselling an offence that was not committed` IS
    `s 464 the punishment for counselling an offence that is not committed` (`ccc14 seat class of the offence` `the offence is indictable` `it can also be tried as a summary conviction offence`) (`ccc14 seat indictable limb` `it carries life imprisonment` `longest term in years`) `the law expressly provides otherwise`

@export Under section 465(1), have I committed the offence of conspiracy?
GIVEN `I conspired to commit murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you conspire with any one to commit murder, or to cause another person to be murdered, whether in Canada or not?
      `I conspired to prosecute an innocent person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you conspire with any one to prosecute a person for an alleged offence, knowing they did not commit it?
      `I conspired to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you conspire with any one to commit an indictable offence?
      `the offence is provided for in (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that offence one provided for in paragraph (a) or (b) (murder, or prosecuting an innocent person)?
      `I conspired to commit a summary conviction offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you conspire with any one to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction?
      `the law expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another law expressly provide a different rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 465(1), have I committed the offence of conspiracy` IS
    `ccc14 either answer holds` (`ccc14 either answer holds` (`s 465(1)(a) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to commit murder` `I conspired to commit murder` `the law expressly provides otherwise`) (`s 465(1)(b) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to prosecute a person for an offence they did not commit` `I conspired to prosecute an innocent person` `the law expressly provides otherwise`)) (`ccc14 either answer holds` (`s 465(1)(c) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to commit an indictable offence` `I conspired to commit an indictable offence` `the offence is provided for in (a) or (b)` `the law expressly provides otherwise`) (`s 465(1)(d) the person is guilty of the offence of conspiring to commit an offence punishable on summary conviction` `I conspired to commit a summary conviction offence` `the law expressly provides otherwise`))

