GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 465(7), am I deemed to have been tried and dealt with in Canada because I was tried abroad` IS
    `s 465(7) the person is deemed to have been tried and dealt with in Canada` `I am alleged to have conspired under (3) or (4)` `I was tried and dealt with outside Canada` `I could have pleaded autrefois acquit or convict, pardon or expungement`

@export Under section 466(1), is the agreement a conspiracy in restraint of trade?
GIVEN `number of persons to the agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are party to the agreement?
      `to do an unlawful act in restraint of trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an agreement to do, or to procure to be done, any unlawful act in restraint of trade?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 466(1), is the agreement a conspiracy in restraint of trade` IS
    `s 466(1) the agreement is a conspiracy in restraint of trade` `number of persons to the agreement` `to do an unlawful act in restraint of trade`

@export Under section 466(2), are the purposes of my trade union unlawful just because they restrain trade?
GIVEN `they are the purposes of a trade union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the purposes of a trade union?
      `they are unlawful only because they restrain trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they unlawful only because they are in restraint of trade?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 466(2), are the purposes of my trade union unlawful just because they restrain trade` IS
    `s 466(2) the purposes of a trade union are unlawful within the meaning of subsection (1)` `they are the purposes of a trade union` `they are unlawful only because they restrain trade`

@export Under section 467(1), am I barred from being convicted of conspiracy because I only refused to work or acted for a trade combination?
GIVEN `the only reason for conviction is that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the conviction be only because of the conduct in paragraph (a) or (b)?
      `I refused to work with a workman or for an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse to work with a workman or for an employer?
      `I did an act for a trade combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do, or cause to be done, an act for the purpose of a trade combination?
      `that act is an offence expressly punishable by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that act an offence expressly punishable by law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467(1), am I barred from being convicted of conspiracy because I only refused to work or acted for a trade combination` IS
    `s 467(1) the person is barred from being convicted of the offence of conspiracy` `the only reason for conviction is that conduct` `I refused to work with a workman or for an employer` `I did an act for a trade combination` `that act is an offence expressly punishable by law`

@export Under section 467.1(1), is my group a criminal organization?
GIVEN `it is a group however organized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a group, however organized?
      `number of persons` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons compose it, in or outside Canada?
      `its main purpose is offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have as one of its main purposes or main activities the facilitation or commission of one or more offences?
      `they would bring a material benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would those offences, if committed, likely result in the direct or indirect receipt of a material benefit, including a financial benefit, by the group or any of its members?
      `the offences are serious offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those offences serious offences (the section 467.1(1) question)?
      `it formed randomly for a single offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a group of persons that formed randomly for the immediate commission of a single offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.1(1), is my group a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.1(1) the group is a criminal organization` `it is a group however organized` `number of persons` `its main purpose is offences` `they would bring a material benefit` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the offences are serious offences`) `it formed randomly for a single offence`

@export Under section 467.1(1), is the offence a serious offence?
GIVEN `the offence is indictable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the offence be prosecuted by indictment under this or any other Act of Parliament?
      `it can also be tried as a summary conviction offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it also be punished on summary conviction?
      `it carries life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its longest punishment, on indictment, imprisonment for life?
      `longest term in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If not life: what is its longest term of imprisonment on indictment, in years? (0 if none is stated)
      `it is prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it another offence prescribed by regulation as a serious offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.1(1), is the offence a serious offence` IS
    `s 467.1(1) the offence is a serious offence` (`ccc14 seat class of the offence` `the offence is indictable` `it can also be tried as a summary conviction offence`) (`ccc14 seat longest term` `it carries life imprisonment` `longest term in years`) `it is prescribed by regulation`

@export Under section 467.11(1), have I committed the offence of participating in the activities of a criminal organization?
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the group a criminal organization (the section 467.1(1) question)?
      `I meant to enhance its ability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act for the purpose of enhancing the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence?
      `I acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act knowingly?
      `I participated or contributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, by act or omission, participate in or contribute to any activity of the criminal organization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.11(1), have I committed the offence of participating in the activities of a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.11(1) the person commits the offence of participating in the activities of a criminal organization` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the group is a criminal organization`) `I meant to enhance its ability` `I acted knowingly` `I participated or contributed`

@export Under section 467.11(1), what punishment can I be given for participating in the activities of a criminal organization?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 467.11(1), what punishment can I be given for participating in the activities of a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.11(1) the punishment`

@export Under section 467.111, have I committed the offence of recruiting members for a criminal organization?
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the group a criminal organization (the section 467.1(1) question)?
      `I meant to enhance its ability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act for the purpose of enhancing the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence?
      `I recruited, solicited, encouraged, coerced or invited someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you recruit, solicit, encourage, coerce or invite a person to join the criminal organization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.111, have I committed the offence of recruiting members for a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.111 the person commits the offence of recruiting members for a criminal organization` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the group is a criminal organization`) `I meant to enhance its ability` `I recruited, solicited, encouraged, coerced or invited someone`

@export Under section 467.111, what punishment can I be given for recruiting members for a criminal organization?
GIVEN `the person is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person you recruited, solicited, encouraged or invited under 18 years of age?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 467.111, what punishment can I be given for recruiting members for a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.111 the punishment` `the person is under 18`

@export Under section 467.12(1), have I committed an indictable offence for a criminal organization?
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the group a criminal organization (the section 467.1(1) question)?
      `I was a party to an indictable offence or counselled it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a party to an indictable offence, or did you counsel any person to be a party to it?
      `it was for the criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, the criminal organization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.12(1), have I committed an indictable offence for a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.12(1) the person commits the offence of committing an offence for a criminal organization` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the group is a criminal organization`) (`ccc14 seat includes answer` `I was a party to an indictable offence or counselled it`) `it was for the criminal organization`

@export Under section 467.12(1), what punishment can I be given for committing an indictable offence for a criminal organization?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 467.12(1), what punishment can I be given for committing an indictable offence for a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.12(1) the punishment`

@export Under section 467.12(2), must the Crown prove that I knew who the members of the criminal organization were?
GIVEN `the prosecution is under section 467.12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prosecution for an offence under section 467.12(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.12(2), must the Crown prove that I knew who the members of the criminal organization were` IS
    `s 467.12(2) it is necessary for the prosecutor to prove that the accused knew the identity of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization` `the prosecution is under section 467.12(1)`

@export Under section 467.13(1), have I committed the offence of instructing the commission of an offence for a criminal organization?
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the group a criminal organization (the section 467.1(1) question)?
      `I am one of its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of the persons who constitute the criminal organization?
      `I knowingly instructed someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly instruct, directly or indirectly, any person to commit an offence?
      `it was for the criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, the criminal organization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.13(1), have I committed the offence of instructing the commission of an offence for a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.13(1) the person commits the offence of instructing the commission of an offence for a criminal organization` (`ccc14 seat means answer` `the group is a criminal organization`) `I am one of its members` `I knowingly instructed someone` `it was for the criminal organization`

@export Under section 467.13(1), what punishment can I be given for instructing the commission of an offence for a criminal organization?
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
DECIDE `Under section 467.13(1), what punishment can I be given for instructing the commission of an offence for a criminal organization` IS
    `s 467.13(1) the punishment`

@export Under section 467.14, must my sentence for a criminal organization offence be served consecutively to other punishment?
GIVEN `section number` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section was the sentence imposed: 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13? (type the number, for example 467.12)
      `another punishment for the same event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was another punishment imposed on you for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events?
      `another sentence at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to another sentence at the time this sentence is imposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 467.14, must my sentence for a criminal organization offence be served consecutively to other punishment` IS
    `s 467.14 the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other punishment or sentence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `section number`, "") `another punishment for the same event` `another sentence at the time`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc15 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc15-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER for Part XIV (Jurisdiction), sections 468 to 482.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence,
-- what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a
-- conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
-- This part's questions are the ones Part XIV answers for that person: which court may try them and where, whether they must be tried by jury, what follows if they abscond
-- during the trial, where the offence is treated as committed, what follows for an offence at sea or outside Canada, and what the rules of court and case management ask of them.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the accused can state (yes or no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), each with an @desc worded as the
-- accused would be asked. The records and the answers of other provisions that the layer-1 modules expect are built here, in each question's WHERE, from those inputs, and the SAME
-- layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated. A field that a rule does not read is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
-- Answers of section 2 are worked out by calling the keel's `s 2 ...` functions from the court and province the accused names.
-- Provisions that address only an official (the rule-making powers of ss 482(1) to (3), 482(5) and 482.1(1), the clerk's powers) are asked only for what they mean to the accused.
-- There is no seat for an official.
-- Where a question needs another provision's answer as a fact the accused can state ("does section 477.1 apply to what I did", "I have appeared as the subsection allows"), it asks that as a plain yes or no (fork: plain-fact-seams, NOTES.md F18).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. Every answer is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING. JUST TRUE: yes, on the text's own words. JUST FALSE: no, because the text says no in its own words.
-- NOTHING: not covered; the text does not say, or points outside what is encoded, or limits itself in its own words and the case falls outside the limit. NOTHING is never "no".
-- Where a heading below marks a situation the accused may not be in (absconding, a trial at sea, a plea of guilty in another province), the form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.

§ `Part XIV -- Jurisdiction`

§§ `Which court may try me (ss 468 to 471)`

-- Helpers that build the records. They are not questions.
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER
      form IS A `s 469 form of the charge`
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 469 facts of the charge`
`Under section 469, the facts of my charge` MEANS
    `s 469 facts of the charge` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the offence`, ""), form, `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act`, `the accused is the holder of a judicial office`, `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder`   -- the subsection of the offence is not read by s 469: a placeholder

GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER
      form IS A `s 469 form of the charge`
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 469, the answer for my charge` MEANS
    `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`Under section 469, the facts of my charge` `the section of the offence` form `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `the accused is the holder of a judicial office` `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder`)

@ref s 468
@export Under section 468, does a superior court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with?
GIVEN `the court that is to try me` IS A `s 2 named court` @desc Which court is to try you? Choose it from the list (for example the Superior Court of Justice in Ontario, the Superior Court in Quebec, the Supreme Court in Nova Scotia).
      `the province or territory where that court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does that court sit?
      `how the Code classifies the offence` IS A `Class of offence` @desc How does the Criminal Code classify the offence you are charged with, as you are being prosecuted now: an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or an offence that is both (if the prosecutor has already chosen how to proceed, pick that way)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 468, does a superior court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` MEANS
    `s 468 the superior court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` `the court that is to try me` `the province or territory where that court sits`) `how the Code classifies the offence`

@ref s 469
@export Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469?
GIVEN `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 235)? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact to it, with attempting to commit it, with conspiring to commit it, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence you are said to have helped after it was committed high treason, treason or murder?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 469, is the offence I am charged with one of those listed in section 469` MEANS
    `Under section 469, the answer for my charge` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder`

@ref s 469
@export Under section 469, does a court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with?
GIVEN `the court that is to try me` IS A `s 2 named court` @desc Which court is to try you? Choose it from the list (for example the Ontario Court of Justice, or a provincial court judge).
      `the province or territory where that court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does that court sit?
      `how the Code classifies the offence` IS A `Class of offence` @desc How does the Criminal Code classify the offence you are charged with, as you are being prosecuted now: an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or an offence that is both (if the prosecutor has already chosen how to proceed, pick that way)?
      `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 235)? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact to it, with attempting to commit it, with conspiring to commit it, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence you are said to have helped after it was committed high treason, treason or murder?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 469, does a court of criminal jurisdiction have jurisdiction to try the offence I am charged with` MEANS
    `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (`s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction` `the court that is to try me` `the province or territory where that court sits`) `how the Code classifies the offence` (`Under section 469, the answer for my charge` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder`)

-- Helper: whether the court has power to try the offence, by section 468 for a superior court of criminal jurisdiction and by section 469 for a court of criminal jurisdiction.
GIVEN court IS A `s 2 named court`
      province IS A `Province or territory`
      class IS A `Class of offence`
      `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER
      form IS A `s 469 form of the charge`
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 470, the court has power to try my offence` MEANS
    IF `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` court province EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `s 468 the superior court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` court province) class
    ELSE `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (`s 2 court of criminal jurisdiction` court province) class (`Under section 469, the answer for my charge` `the section of the offence` form `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `the accused is the holder of a judicial office` `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder`)

@ref s 470
@export Under section 470, is the court competent to try me for the offence?
GIVEN `the court that is to try me` IS A `s 2 named court` @desc Which court is to try you? Choose it from the list.
      `the province or territory where that court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does that court sit?
      `how the Code classifies the offence` IS A `Class of offence` @desc How does the Criminal Code classify the offence you are charged with, as you are being prosecuted now?
      `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact, with attempting, with conspiring, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence high treason, treason or murder?
      `another provision of the Criminal Code takes away the court's competence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any other provision of the Criminal Code take away this court's competence to try you?
      `I was found within the territorial jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found within the territorial jurisdiction of the court (the area it covers)?
      `I was arrested within the territorial jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you arrested within the territorial jurisdiction of the court?
      `I am in custody within the territorial jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in custody within the territorial jurisdiction of the court?
      `I have been ordered to be tried by that court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been ordered to be tried by that court?
      `I have been ordered to be tried by another court whose jurisdiction was transferred to that court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been ordered to be tried by another court whose jurisdiction has by lawful authority been transferred to that court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 470, is the court competent to try me for the offence` MEANS
    `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence`
        (`Under section 470, the court has power to try my offence` `the court that is to try me` `the province or territory where that court sits` `how the Code classifies the offence` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder`)
        (JUST `another provision of the Criminal Code takes away the court's competence`)
        `I was found within the territorial jurisdiction of the court` `I was arrested within the territorial jurisdiction of the court` `I am in custody within the territorial jurisdiction of the court`
        `I have been ordered to be tried by that court` `I have been ordered to be tried by another court whose jurisdiction was transferred to that court`

@ref s 471
@export Under section 471, must I be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury?
GIVEN `how the Code classifies the offence` IS A `Class of offence` @desc How does the Criminal Code classify the offence you are charged with, as you are being prosecuted now: an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or an offence that is both (if the prosecutor has already chosen how to proceed, pick that way)?
      `a provision of the Criminal Code expressly provides that I am to be tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Criminal Code expressly provide that you are to be tried without a jury (for example because you and the Attorney General consented under section 473, or because of the way you elected to be tried)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 471, must I be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` MEANS
    `s 471 the accused shall be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `how the Code classifies the offence` (JUST `a provision of the Criminal Code expressly provides that I am to be tried without a jury`)

§§ `Trial without a jury (s 473)`

-- Helper: subsection (1) for my trial, from the plain facts of the charge, the two consents and the court.
GIVEN `the section of the offence` IS A NUMBER
      form IS A `s 469 form of the charge`
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      court IS A `s 2 named court`
      province IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 473(1), the answer for my trial` MEANS
    `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
        (`Under section 469, the answer for my charge` `the section of the offence` form `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `the accused is the holder of a judicial office` `the accused is an accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder`)
        `I consent` `the Attorney General consents` (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` court province)

@ref s 473(1)
@export Under section 473(1), may I be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction?
GIVEN `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 235)? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact to it, with attempting to commit it, with conspiring to commit it, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence high treason, treason or murder?
      `I consent to be tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to be tried without a jury?
      `the Attorney General consents to my being tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General consented to your being tried without a jury?
      `the court that is to try me` IS A `s 2 named court` @desc Which court is to try you? Choose it from the list.
      `the province or territory where that court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does that court sit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 473(1), may I be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    `Under section 473(1), the answer for my trial` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` `I consent to be tried without a jury` `the Attorney General consents to my being tried without a jury` `the court that is to try me` `the province or territory where that court sits`

@ref s 473(1.1)
@export Under section 473(1.1), may the judge order that another offence be tried by that judge together with the offence listed in section 469?
GIVEN `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 235)? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact to it, with attempting to commit it, with conspiring to commit it, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence high treason, treason or murder?
      `I consent to be tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to be tried without a jury?
      `the Attorney General consents to my being tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General consented to your being tried without a jury?
      `the court that is to try me` IS A `s 2 named court` @desc Which court is to try you? Choose it from the list.
      `the province or territory where that court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does that court sit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 473(1.1), may the judge order that another offence be tried by that judge together with the offence listed in section 469` MEANS
    `s 473(1.1) the judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469`
        (`Under section 473(1), the answer for my trial` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` `I consent to be tried without a jury` `the Attorney General consents to my being tried without a jury` `the court that is to try me` `the province or territory where that court sits`)

@ref s 473(2)
@export Under section 473(2), is the withdrawal of my consent to be tried without a jury barred?
GIVEN `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged (for example 235)? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact to it, with attempting to commit it, with conspiring to commit it, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence high treason, treason or murder?
      `I consent to be tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consent to be tried without a jury?
      `the Attorney General consents to my being tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Attorney General consent to your being tried without a jury?
      `the court that is to try me` IS A `s 2 named court` @desc Which court is to try you? Choose it from the list.
      `the province or territory where that court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does that court sit?
      `both the Attorney General and I agree to the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do both you and the Attorney General agree to the withdrawal of the consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 473(2), is the withdrawal of my consent to be tried without a jury barred` MEANS
    `s 473(2) the withdrawal of the consent is barred`
        (`Under section 473(1), the answer for my trial` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` `I consent to be tried without a jury` `the Attorney General consents to my being tried without a jury` `the court that is to try me` `the province or territory where that court sits`)
        `both the Attorney General and I agree to the withdrawal`

§§ `Adjournment when no jury is summoned (s 474)`

-- Situation: the court that is to try me has no jury panel summoned for its term or sittings. The form can ask "Has this happened?" first.
@ref s 474(1)
@export Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day, on the opening day of a term or sittings for which no jury panel is to be summoned, if no judge is present to preside?
GIVEN `the person who would adjourn` IS A `s 2 clerk of the court kind` @desc Who would adjourn the court: a clerk of the court, a person who performs a clerk's duties whatever their title, or someone who is neither?
      `no jury panel is to be summoned for the term or sittings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the competent authority decided that no panel of jurors is to be summoned for the term or sittings of the court for the trial of criminal cases in the territorial division?
      `it is the opening day of the term or sittings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the day of the opening of the term or sittings?
      `a judge is present to preside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a judge present to preside over the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 474(1), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day, on the opening day of a term or sittings for which no jury panel is to be summoned, if no judge is present to preside` MEANS
    `s 474(1) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` (`s 2 clerk of the court` `the person who would adjourn`) `no jury panel is to be summoned for the term or sittings` `it is the opening day of the term or sittings` `a judge is present to preside`

@ref s 474(2)
@export Under section 474(2), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day on a judge's instructions?
GIVEN `the person who would adjourn` IS A `s 2 clerk of the court kind` @desc Who would adjourn the court: a clerk of the court, a person who performs a clerk's duties whatever their title, or someone who is neither?
      `the clerk acts on the instructions of the presiding judge or another judge of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the clerk acting on the instructions of the presiding judge or another judge of the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 474(2), may the clerk of the court adjourn the court and its business to a later day on a judge's instructions` MEANS
    `s 474(2) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day on the instructions of a judge` (`s 2 clerk of the court` `the person who would adjourn`) `the clerk acts on the instructions of the presiding judge or another judge of the court`

§§ `If I abscond during my trial (s 475)`

-- Situation: the accused absconds during the course of the trial. The form can ask "Did you abscond during your trial?" first.
@ref s 475(1)(a)
@export Under section 475(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived my right to be present at my trial if I abscond?
GIVEN `I abscond during the course of my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abscond (go missing without leave, and not come back) during the course of your trial? It makes no difference whether you are charged jointly with another.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived my right to be present at my trial if I abscond` MEANS
    `s 475(1)(a) the accused is deemed to have waived the right to be present at the trial` `I abscond during the course of my trial`

@ref s 475(1)(b)(i)
@export Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court continue my trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict in my absence?
GIVEN `I abscond during the course of my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abscond (go missing without leave, and not come back) during the course of your trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court continue my trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict in my absence` MEANS
    `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court may continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` `I abscond during the course of my trial`

@ref s 475(1)(b)(i)
@export Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court sentence me in my absence if it finds me guilty?
GIVEN `I abscond during the course of my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abscond (go missing without leave, and not come back) during the course of your trial?
      `the court finds me guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court find you guilty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(1)(b)(i), may the court sentence me in my absence if it finds me guilty` MEANS
    `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court may impose a sentence on the accused in the accused's absence` `I abscond during the course of my trial` `the court finds me guilty`

@ref s 475(1)(b)(ii)
@export Under section 475(1)(b)(ii), may the court adjourn my trial to await my appearance?
GIVEN `I abscond during the course of my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abscond (go missing without leave, and not come back) during the course of your trial?
      `a warrant in Form 7 is issued for my arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a warrant in Form 7 been issued for your arrest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(1)(b)(ii), may the court adjourn my trial to await my appearance` MEANS
    `s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court may adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` `I abscond during the course of my trial` `a warrant in Form 7 is issued for my arrest`

@ref s 475(1), the proviso
@export Under section 475(1), may the court continue my trial at any time after adjourning it to await my appearance?
GIVEN `my trial is adjourned to await my appearance because a warrant in Form 7 was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your trial been adjourned to await your appearance after you absconded and a warrant in Form 7 was issued for your arrest?
      `the court is satisfied that it is no longer in the interests of justice to await my appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is no longer in the interests of justice to await your appearance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(1), may the court continue my trial at any time after adjourning it to await my appearance` MEANS
    `s 475(1) the court may, at any time, continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` `my trial is adjourned to await my appearance because a warrant in Form 7 was issued` `the court is satisfied that it is no longer in the interests of justice to await my appearance`

@ref s 475(2)
@export Under section 475(2), may the court draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded?
GIVEN `the court continues my trial in my absence under section 475(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court continued your trial in your absence under section 475(1) after you absconded?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(2), may the court draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded` MEANS
    `s 475(2) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that the accused has absconded` `the court continues my trial in my absence under section 475(1)`

@ref s 475(3)
@export Under section 475(3), am I barred from having the part of my trial conducted in my absence re-opened?
GIVEN `I have reappeared at my trial, which is continuing under section 475(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reappeared at your trial, which is continuing under section 475(1) after you absconded?
      `the court is satisfied that exceptional circumstances make it in the interests of justice to re-open the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that, because of exceptional circumstances, it is in the interests of justice to re-open the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(3), am I barred from having the part of my trial conducted in my absence re-opened` MEANS
    `s 475(3) the accused is not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in the accused's absence re-opened` `I have reappeared at my trial, which is continuing under section 475(1)` `the court is satisfied that exceptional circumstances make it in the interests of justice to re-open the proceedings`

@ref s 475(4)
@export Under section 475(4), does the section preserve my counsel's authority to continue to act for me when I abscond and my trial continues?
GIVEN `I absconded during the course of my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abscond (go missing without leave, and not come back) during the course of your trial?
      `the court continues my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court continued your trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 475(4), does the section preserve my counsel's authority to continue to act for me when I abscond and my trial continues` MEANS
    `s 475(4) the subsection preserves any authority counsel for the accused has to continue to act for the accused in the proceedings` `I absconded during the course of my trial` `the court continues my trial`

§ `Part XIV -- Special jurisdiction`

§§ `Where my offence is treated as committed (s 476)`

-- Situation: the offence happened on water, on a boundary, in a vehicle, vessel or aircraft, or in the mail. The accused picks the circumstance that fits and how the
-- territorial division in question is connected to it; the other paragraphs are given fixed placeholders (not that circumstance), so only the paragraph chosen can answer.
DECLARE `s 476 seat where my offence was committed` IS ONE OF
    `s 476 seat on water or on a bridge between two or more territorial divisions`
    `s 476 seat on or near the boundary of two or more territorial divisions`
    `s 476 seat commenced in one territorial division and completed in another`
    `s 476 seat in or on a vehicle on a journey, or on a vessel on a navigable river, canal or inland water`
    `s 476 seat in an aircraft in the course of a flight`
    `s 476 seat in respect of the mail in the course of its door-to-door delivery`
    `s 476 seat somewhere else`

DECLARE `s 476 seat how the territorial division is connected to my offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 476 seat the water or bridge lies between it and another territorial division`
    `s 476 seat the boundary on or near which the offence was committed is a boundary of it`
    `s 476 seat the offence was commenced in it, or completed in it`
    `s 476 seat the vehicle or vessel passed through it on the journey or voyage`
    `s 476 seat the road or water the vehicle or vessel passed along is a boundary of it`
    `s 476 seat the flight commenced in it`
    `s 476 seat the aircraft passed over it`
    `s 476 seat the flight ended in it`
    `s 476 seat the mail was carried through it on that delivery`
    `s 476 seat it is connected to my offence in none of these ways`

@ref s 476
@export Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division?
GIVEN `where my offence was committed` IS A `s 476 seat where my offence was committed` @desc Where was the offence committed: on water or a bridge between territorial divisions, on or near a boundary between territorial divisions, begun in one division and finished in another, in or on a vehicle on a journey or a vessel on a navigable river, canal or inland water, in an aircraft in flight, in respect of the mail in door-to-door delivery, or somewhere else?
      `metres from the boundary` IS A NUMBER @desc If it was on or near a boundary between territorial divisions: how many metres from the boundary (0 if exactly on it)? Give 0 if the question does not apply.
      `the road or water on which the vehicle or vessel passed is a boundary of two or more territorial divisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was in or on a vehicle or vessel: is the center or another part of the road, river, canal or inland water on which it passed the boundary of two or more territorial divisions?
      `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` IS A `s 476 seat how the territorial division is connected to my offence` @desc How is the territorial division in question connected to the offence (for example: the vehicle passed through it, the flight commenced in it, the offence was completed in it)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 476, is my offence treated as having been committed in this territorial division` MEANS
    `s 476 the offence is deemed to have been committed in the territorial division` `my circumstances` `my connection`
    WHERE
        `my circumstances` MEANS
            `s 476 circumstances of the offence` OF
                `where my offence was committed` EQUALS `s 476 seat on water or on a bridge between two or more territorial divisions`,
                IF `where my offence was committed` EQUALS `s 476 seat on or near the boundary of two or more territorial divisions` THEN JUST `metres from the boundary` ELSE NOTHING,
                `where my offence was committed` EQUALS `s 476 seat commenced in one territorial division and completed in another`,
                `where my offence was committed` EQUALS `s 476 seat in or on a vehicle on a journey, or on a vessel on a navigable river, canal or inland water`,
                `where my offence was committed` EQUALS `s 476 seat in or on a vehicle on a journey, or on a vessel on a navigable river, canal or inland water` AND `the road or water on which the vehicle or vessel passed is a boundary of two or more territorial divisions`,
                `where my offence was committed` EQUALS `s 476 seat in an aircraft in the course of a flight`,
                `where my offence was committed` EQUALS `s 476 seat in respect of the mail in the course of its door-to-door delivery`
        `my connection` MEANS
            `s 476 how the territorial division is connected to the offence` OF
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the water or bridge lies between it and another territorial division`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the boundary on or near which the offence was committed is a boundary of it`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the offence was commenced in it, or completed in it`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the vehicle or vessel passed through it on the journey or voyage`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the road or water the vehicle or vessel passed along is a boundary of it`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the flight commenced in it`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the aircraft passed over it`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the flight ended in it`,
                `how this territorial division is connected to my offence` EQUALS `s 476 seat the mail was carried through it on that delivery`

§§ `Offences at sea and outside Canada (ss 477 to 477.4)`

-- Situation: the offence is alleged to have happened at sea or outside Canada. The form can ask "Is your offence alleged to have happened at sea or outside Canada?" first.
@ref s 477(1)
@export Under section 477(1), is the vessel a "ship" for sections 477.1 to 477.4?
GIVEN `it is a vessel, boat or craft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a vessel, boat or craft?
      `it is designed, used or capable of being used solely or partly for marine navigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it designed, used or capable of being used, solely or partly, for marine navigation (whether or not it has any propulsion)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477(1), is the vessel a ship for sections 477.1 to 477.4` MEANS
    `s 477(1) ship` (`Provision of the Code` OF 477.1, "") `it is a vessel, boat or craft` `it is designed, used or capable of being used solely or partly for marine navigation`   -- the question concerns sections 477.1 to 477.4, so the provision is fixed at 477.1: a placeholder

@ref s 477(2)
@export Under section 477(2), do sections 477.1 to 477.4 limit the operation of another Act of Parliament or a court's jurisdiction apart from them?
GIVEN `what I ask whether they limit` IS A `s 477(2) what is said to be limited` @desc What do you ask whether sections 477.1 to 477.4 limit: the operation of another Act of Parliament, the jurisdiction a court may exercise apart from those sections, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477(2), do sections 477.1 to 477.4 limit the operation of another Act of Parliament or a court's jurisdiction apart from them` MEANS
    `s 477(2) the section limits the operation of any other Act of Parliament or the jurisdiction that a court may exercise apart from sections 477.1 to 477.4` (`Provision of the Code` OF 477.1, "") `what I ask whether they limit`   -- the question concerns sections 477.1 to 477.4, so the provision is fixed at 477.1: a placeholder

@ref s 477.1
@export Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada?
GIVEN `the act or omission would be an offence under a federal law if it occurred in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it had happened in Canada, would the act or omission be an offence under a federal law (within the meaning of section 2 of the Oceans Act)?
      `it is in the exclusive economic zone of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in the exclusive economic zone of Canada?
      `I was in the zone in connection with exploring, exploiting, conserving or managing its natural resources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in the exclusive economic zone of Canada in connection with exploring or exploiting, conserving or managing its natural resources, living or non-living?
      `it was committed by or in relation to a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it committed by or in relation to a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident (within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act)?
      `it is in or above the continental shelf of Canada and is an offence there by virtue of section 20 of the Oceans Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it happen in a place in or above the continental shelf of Canada, where it is an offence by virtue of section 20 of the Oceans Act?
      `it was committed outside Canada on board or by means of a ship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it committed outside Canada on board or by means of a ship?
      `the ship is registered, licensed or numbered under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ship registered or licensed, or has it been issued an identification number, under an Act of Parliament?
      `it is a vessel, boat or craft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a vessel, boat or craft?
      `it is designed, used or capable of being used solely or partly for marine navigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it designed, used or capable of being used, solely or partly, for marine navigation?
      `it was committed outside Canada in the course of hot pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it committed outside Canada in the course of hot pursuit?
      `it was committed outside the territory of any state by a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it committed outside the territory of any state by a Canadian citizen?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.1, am I deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada` MEANS
    `s 477.1 the person is deemed to have committed the act or omission in Canada`
        (`s 477.1 facts of the act or omission` OF `the act or omission would be an offence under a federal law if it occurred in Canada`, `it is in the exclusive economic zone of Canada`, `I was in the zone in connection with exploring, exploiting, conserving or managing its natural resources`, `it was committed by or in relation to a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident`, `it is in or above the continental shelf of Canada and is an offence there by virtue of section 20 of the Oceans Act`, `it was committed outside Canada on board or by means of a ship`, `the ship is registered, licensed or numbered under an Act of Parliament`, `it was committed outside Canada in the course of hot pursuit`, `it was committed outside the territory of any state by a Canadian citizen`)
        (`s 477(1) ship` (`Provision of the Code` OF 477.1, "") `it is a vessel, boat or craft` `it is designed, used or capable of being used solely or partly for marine navigation`)

@ref s 477.2(1)
@export Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent?
GIVEN `the offence is alleged to have been committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence alleged to have been committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada?
      `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada?
      `the proceedings are by way of` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Are the proceedings by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the date the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the proceedings commenced (ISO 8601, for example 2026-01-15)?
      `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General of Canada consented to the proceedings being continued?
      `the date the consent was obtained` IS A DATE @desc If the Attorney General of Canada has consented: on what date was the consent obtained? (Give any date if there is no consent yet.)
      `the date as at which I ask` IS A DATE @desc As at what date do you ask (for example today's date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.2(1), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent` MEANS
    `s 477.2(1) the proceedings are barred from being continued for want of the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` `the offence is alleged to have been committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada` `I am a Canadian citizen` `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` `the proceedings are by way of` `the date the proceedings were commenced` `the consent date` `the date as at which I ask`
    WHERE
        `the consent date` MEANS IF `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` THEN JUST `the date the consent was obtained` ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 477.2(1)
@export Under section 477.2(1), what is the last day by which the Attorney General of Canada's consent must be obtained for the proceedings to be continued?
GIVEN `the date the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the proceedings commenced (ISO 8601, for example 2026-01-15)?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 477.2(1), what is the last day by which the Attorney General of Canada's consent must be obtained for the proceedings to be continued` MEANS
    `s 477.2 the last day on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada may be obtained` `the date the proceedings were commenced`

@ref s 477.2(2)
@export Under section 477.2(2), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)?
GIVEN `the courts have jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the courts have jurisdiction over the offence only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b) (the exclusive economic zone or the continental shelf)?
      `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada?
      `the date the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the proceedings commenced (ISO 8601, for example 2026-01-15)?
      `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General of Canada consented to the proceedings being continued?
      `the date the consent was obtained` IS A DATE @desc If the Attorney General of Canada has consented: on what date was the consent obtained? (Give any date if there is no consent yet.)
      `the date as at which I ask` IS A DATE @desc As at what date do you ask (for example today's date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.2(2), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` MEANS
    `s 477.2(2) the proceedings are barred from being continued for want of the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` `the courts have jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(a) or (b)` `I am a Canadian citizen` `the offence is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` `the date the proceedings were commenced` `the consent date` `the date as at which I ask`
    WHERE
        `the consent date` MEANS IF `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` THEN JUST `the date the consent was obtained` ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 477.2(3)
@export Under section 477.2(3), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)?
GIVEN `the courts have jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the courts have jurisdiction over the offence only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e) (hot pursuit, or an offence outside the territory of any state by a Canadian citizen)?
      `the date the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the proceedings commenced (ISO 8601, for example 2026-01-15)?
      `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General of Canada consented to the proceedings being continued?
      `the date the consent was obtained` IS A DATE @desc If the Attorney General of Canada has consented: on what date was the consent obtained? (Give any date if there is no consent yet.)
      `the date as at which I ask` IS A DATE @desc As at what date do you ask (for example today's date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.2(3), are the proceedings barred from being continued for want of the Attorney General of Canada's consent, the courts having jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` MEANS
    `s 477.2(3) the proceedings are barred from being continued for want of the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` `the courts have jurisdiction only by virtue of paragraph 477.1(d) or (e)` `the date the proceedings were commenced` `the consent date` `the date as at which I ask`
    WHERE
        `the consent date` MEANS IF `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` THEN JUST `the date the consent was obtained` ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 477.2(4)
@export Under section 477.2(4), has the Attorney General's consent been filed with the clerk of the court as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `a consent of the Attorney General is required by subsection (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a consent of the Attorney General of Canada required in your case by subsection 477.2(1), (2) or (3)?
      `the consent has been filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings were instituted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the consent been filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings have been instituted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.2(4), has the Attorney General's consent been filed with the clerk of the court as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `s 477.2(4) the consent has been filed as the subsection requires` `a consent of the Attorney General is required by subsection (1), (2) or (3)` `the consent has been filed with the clerk of the court in which the proceedings were instituted`

-- The seat takes the answer of section 477.1 for the act or omission as a plain fact ("does section 477.1 apply to what I did?"), so as not to ask its eleven facts again; the question
-- `Under section 477.1, ...` gives the accused that answer.
@ref s 477.3(1)
@export Under section 477.3(1), may a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure be exercised at this place?
GIVEN `the power is a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure or other power that could be exercised in Canada for the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure, or other power that could be exercised in Canada in respect of the act or omission?
      `section 477.1 applies to the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or omission one to which section 477.1 applies (deemed committed in Canada)?
      `hot pursuit has been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has hot pursuit been commenced?
      `the place where the power would be exercised` IS A `s 477.3(1) the place where the power is to be exercised` @desc Where would the power be exercised: the place where the act or omission occurred, on board the ship or marine installation or structure where it occurred, a place on the seas that is not part of the territorial sea of another state, a place on the seas that is part of the territorial sea of another state, or another place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.3(1), may a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure be exercised at this place` MEANS
    `s 477.3(1) the power may be exercised at the place` `the power is a power of arrest, entry, search or seizure or other power that could be exercised in Canada for the act or omission` (JUST `section 477.1 applies to the act or omission`) `hot pursuit has been commenced` `the place where the power would be exercised`

@ref s 477.3(2)
@export Under section 477.3(2), does a justice or judge in any territorial division in Canada have jurisdiction to authorize an arrest, entry, search or seizure, or an investigation or other ancillary matter, related to my offence?
GIVEN `the matter is an arrest, entry, search or seizure or an investigation or other ancillary matter related to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an arrest, entry, search or seizure, or an investigation or other ancillary matter, related to the offence?
      `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or the internal waters of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or an area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada?
      `section 477.1 applies to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one to which section 477.1 applies (deemed committed in Canada)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.3(2), does a justice or judge in any territorial division in Canada have jurisdiction to authorize an arrest, entry, search or seizure, or an investigation or other ancillary matter, related to my offence` MEANS
    `s 477.3(2) a justice or judge in any territorial division in Canada has jurisdiction to authorize the matter` (JUST TRUE) `the matter is an arrest, entry, search or seizure or an investigation or other ancillary matter related to the offence` `the offence is committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or the internal waters of Canada` (JUST `section 477.1 applies to the offence`)   -- the question names "a justice or judge", so that premise is fixed: a placeholder

@ref s 477.3(3)
@export Under section 477.3(3), are the powers barred from being exercised outside Canada without the Attorney General of Canada's consent?
GIVEN `the offence is an offence by virtue only of section 477.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or omission an offence only by virtue of section 477.1?
      `it is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada?
      `the powers would be exercised outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the powers be exercised outside Canada?
      `the Attorney General of Canada has consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General of Canada consented?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.3(3), are the powers barred from being exercised outside Canada without the Attorney General of Canada's consent` MEANS
    `s 477.3(3) the powers are barred from being exercised outside Canada without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` `the offence is an offence by virtue only of section 477.1` `it is alleged to have been committed on board a ship registered outside Canada` `the powers would be exercised outside Canada` `the Attorney General of Canada has consented`

-- Certificates (s 477.4). The three questions below share the same facts of the certificate.
@ref s 477.4(3)
@export Under section 477.4(3), is the certificate conclusive proof of the truth of its statement, without proof of the signature or official character of the person who appears to have issued it?
GIVEN `the kind of certificate` IS A `s 477.4(3) the kind of certificate` @desc What kind of certificate is it: one referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act, one issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs, or another kind?
      `it states that a location was in an area of a fishing zone of Canada not within the internal waters or the territorial sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs: does it state that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, in an area of a fishing zone of Canada that is not within the internal waters of Canada or the territorial sea of Canada?
      `it states that a location was outside the territory of any state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs: does it state that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, outside the territory of any state?
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.4(3), is the certificate conclusive proof of the truth of its statement, without proof of the signature or official character of the person who appears to have issued it` MEANS
    `s 477.4(3) the certificate is conclusive proof of the truth of the statement without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have issued it` (`s 477.4(3) the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3)` (`s 477.4(3) facts of the certificate` OF `the kind of certificate`, `it states that a location was in an area of a fishing zone of Canada not within the internal waters or the territorial sea`, `it states that a location was outside the territory of any state`)) `the proceedings are in respect of an offence`

@ref s 477.4(4)
@export Under section 477.4(4), is the certificate admissible in evidence in my proceedings?
GIVEN `the kind of certificate` IS A `s 477.4(3) the kind of certificate` @desc What kind of certificate is it: one referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act, one issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs, or another kind?
      `it states that a location was in an area of a fishing zone of Canada not within the internal waters or the territorial sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs: does it state that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, in an area of a fishing zone of Canada that is not within the internal waters of Canada or the territorial sea of Canada?
      `it states that a location was outside the territory of any state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs: does it state that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, outside the territory of any state?
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.4(4), is the certificate admissible in evidence in my proceedings` MEANS
    `s 477.4(4) the certificate is admissible in evidence in the proceedings` (`s 477.4(3) the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3)` (`s 477.4(3) facts of the certificate` OF `the kind of certificate`, `it states that a location was in an area of a fishing zone of Canada not within the internal waters or the territorial sea`, `it states that a location was outside the territory of any state`)) `the proceedings are in respect of an offence`

@ref s 477.4(4)
@export Under section 477.4(4), is it the case that the production of the certificate cannot be compelled?
GIVEN `the kind of certificate` IS A `s 477.4(3) the kind of certificate` @desc What kind of certificate is it: one referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Oceans Act, one issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs, or another kind?
      `it states that a location was in an area of a fishing zone of Canada not within the internal waters or the territorial sea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs: does it state that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, in an area of a fishing zone of Canada that is not within the internal waters of Canada or the territorial sea of Canada?
      `it states that a location was outside the territory of any state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was issued by or under the authority of the Minister of Foreign Affairs: does it state that a geographical location specified in it was, at a time material to the proceedings, outside the territory of any state?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 477.4(4), is it the case that the production of the certificate cannot be compelled` MEANS
    `s 477.4(4) the production of the certificate cannot be compelled` (`s 477.4(3) the certificate is one referred to in subsection (3)` (`s 477.4(3) facts of the certificate` OF `the kind of certificate`, `it states that a location was in an area of a fishing zone of Canada not within the internal waters or the territorial sea`, `it states that a location was outside the territory of any state`))

§ `Part XIV -- Where I may be tried and how I plead`

§§ `In which province I may be tried (ss 478 to 481.3)`

@ref s 478(1)
@export Under section 478(1), is a court in a province barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province?
GIVEN `the province or territory where the court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does the court sit?
      `my offence was committed entirely in one province or territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed entirely in one province or territory (and not partly in another)?
      `the province or territory where it was committed` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory was it committed? (Give any if it was not committed entirely in one.)
      `another provision of the Criminal Code displaces the bar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another provision of the Criminal Code (for example section 478(2), 478(3), 479, 480, 481, 481.1 or 481.2) allow the court to try the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(1), is a court in a province barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` MEANS
    `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` `the province or territory where the court sits` `where it was committed entirely` (JUST `another provision of the Criminal Code displaces the bar`)
    WHERE
        `where it was committed entirely` MEANS IF `my offence was committed entirely in one province or territory` THEN JUST `the province or territory where it was committed` ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 478(2)
@export Under section 478(2), am I dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where I reside or in which the newspaper is printed?
GIVEN `I am a proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper, or with conspiracy to publish a defamatory libel in a newspaper?
      `the publication is a newspaper as section 297 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the publication a newspaper, as section 297 defines the word?
      `the province where I reside` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province do you reside?
      `the province where the newspaper is printed` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province is the newspaper printed?
      `the province where I am dealt with` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province are you being dealt with, indicted, tried and punished?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(2), am I dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where I reside or in which the newspaper is printed` MEANS
    `s 478(2) the person is dealt with, indicted, tried and punished in the province where the person resides or in which the newspaper is printed` `I am a proprietor, publisher, editor or other person charged with the publication of a defamatory libel in a newspaper` (`s 478(5) newspaper` (`Provision of the Code` OF 478, "(2)") (JUST `the publication is a newspaper as section 297 defines it`)) `the province where I reside` `the province where the newspaper is printed` `the province where I am dealt with`

-- Situation: the accused is charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in Canada but outside the province where they are, and wants to plead guilty there.
-- The form can ask "Are you charged with an offence alleged to have been committed outside the province where you are?" first.
@ref s 478(3)
@export Under section 478(3), may I appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where I am, when I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside that province?
GIVEN `I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province where I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province in which you are?
      `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact, with attempting, with conspiring, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence high treason, treason or murder?
      `the proceedings were instituted by the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and are they conducted by or on behalf of that Government?
      `the Attorney General of Canada consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General of Canada consent?
      `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(3), may I appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where I am, when I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside that province` MEANS
    `s 478(3) the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is` `I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province where I am` (`Under section 469, the answer for my charge` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder`) `the proceedings were instituted by the Government of Canada` `the Attorney General of Canada consents` `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents`

@ref s 478(3)
@export Under section 478(3), shall the court or judge determine me to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law?
GIVEN `I have appeared as subsection 478(3) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you appeared before a court or judge as subsection 478(3) allows?
      `I consent to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to plead guilty?
      `I plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you plead guilty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(3), shall the court or judge determine me to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` MEANS
    `s 478(3) the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` (JUST `I have appeared as subsection 478(3) allows`) `I consent to plead guilty` `I plead guilty`

@ref s 478(3)
@export Under section 478(3), shall I be returned to custody?
GIVEN `I have appeared as subsection 478(3) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you appeared before a court or judge as subsection 478(3) allows?
      `I consent to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to plead guilty?
      `I plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you plead guilty?
      `I was in custody prior to my appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in custody before you appeared?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(3), shall I be returned to custody` MEANS
    `s 478(3) the accused shall be returned to custody` (JUST `I have appeared as subsection 478(3) allows`) `I consent to plead guilty` `I plead guilty` `I was in custody prior to my appearance`

@ref s 478(3)
@export Under section 478(3), shall I be dealt with according to law?
GIVEN `I have appeared as subsection 478(3) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you appeared before a court or judge as subsection 478(3) allows?
      `I consent to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to plead guilty?
      `I plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you plead guilty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(3), shall I be dealt with according to law` MEANS
    `s 478(3) the accused shall be dealt with according to law` (JUST `I have appeared as subsection 478(3) allows`) `I consent to plead guilty` `I plead guilty`

@ref s 478(4)
@export Under section 478(4), am I deemed simply to stand charged of the offence, without a preliminary inquiry or an indictment?
GIVEN `I am an accused described in subsection 478(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an accused described in subsection 478(3) (charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province where you are)? It makes no difference whether you have been ordered to stand trial or an indictment has been preferred.
      `I desire to plead guilty to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you desire to plead guilty to the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(4), am I deemed simply to stand charged of the offence, without a preliminary inquiry or an indictment` MEANS
    `s 478(4) the accused is deemed simply to stand charged of the offence without a preliminary inquiry having been conducted or an indictment having been preferred` `I am an accused described in subsection 478(3)` `I desire to plead guilty to the offence`

@ref s 478(5)
@export Under section 478(5), is the publication a newspaper, as section 297 defines the word, for the purposes of section 478?
GIVEN `the publication is a newspaper as section 297 defines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the publication a newspaper, as section 297 defines the word?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 478(5), is the publication a newspaper, as section 297 defines the word, for the purposes of section 478` MEANS
    `s 478(5) newspaper` (`Provision of the Code` OF 478, "") (JUST `the publication is a newspaper as section 297 defines it`)   -- the question is about the word as used in section 478: the provision is fixed at 478, a placeholder for the subsection

-- Situation: the accused is charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in the province where they are, and wants to plead guilty there.
@ref s 479
@export Under section 479, may I appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where I am, when I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in the province where I am?
GIVEN `I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in the province where I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in the province in which you are?
      `the section of the Code under which I am charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code are you charged? If you are charged with attempting, conspiring to commit, or being an accessory after the fact to an offence, give the section of that offence.
      `the form of the charge` IS A `s 469 form of the charge` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, with being an accessory after the fact, with attempting, with conspiring, or in another form (for example counselling)?
      `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence under any of sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `I am the holder of a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a judicial office?
      `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with being an accessory after the fact: is the offence high treason, treason or murder?
      `the proceedings were instituted by the Government of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and are they conducted by or on behalf of that Government?
      `the Attorney General of Canada consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General of Canada consent?
      `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 479, may I appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where I am, when I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in the province where I am` MEANS
    `s 479 the accused may appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try the offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is` `I am charged with an offence alleged to have been committed in the province where I am` (`Under section 469, the answer for my charge` `the section of the Code under which I am charged` `the form of the charge` `the offence is under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `I am the holder of a judicial office` `the offence I am an accessory after the fact to is high treason, treason or murder`) `the proceedings were instituted by the Government of Canada` `the Attorney General of Canada consents` `the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents`

@ref s 479
@export Under section 479, shall the court or judge determine me to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law?
GIVEN `I have appeared as section 479 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you appeared before a court or judge as section 479 allows?
      `I consent to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to plead guilty?
      `I plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you plead guilty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 479, shall the court or judge determine me to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` MEANS
    `s 479 the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law` (JUST `I have appeared as section 479 allows`) `I consent to plead guilty` `I plead guilty`

@ref s 479
@export Under section 479, shall I be returned to custody?
GIVEN `I have appeared as section 479 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you appeared before a court or judge as section 479 allows?
      `I consent to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to plead guilty?
      `I plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you plead guilty?
      `I was in custody prior to my appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in custody before you appeared?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 479, shall I be returned to custody` MEANS
    `s 479 the accused shall be returned to custody` (JUST `I have appeared as section 479 allows`) `I consent to plead guilty` `I plead guilty` `I was in custody prior to my appearance`

@ref s 479
@export Under section 479, shall I be dealt with according to law?
GIVEN `I have appeared as section 479 allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you appeared before a court or judge as section 479 allows?
      `I consent to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to plead guilty?
      `I plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you plead guilty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 479, shall I be dealt with according to law` MEANS
    `s 479 the accused shall be dealt with according to law` (JUST `I have appeared as section 479 allows`) `I consent to plead guilty` `I plead guilty`

@ref s 480(1)
@export Under section 480(1), may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division or provisional judicial district for an offence in an unorganized tract?
GIVEN `my offence was committed in an unorganized tract of country, or on a lake, river or other water in it, not in a territorial division or provisional judicial district` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed in an unorganized tract of country in a province, or on a lake, river or other water in it, not included in a territorial division or a provisional judicial district?
      `the province or territory of the tract` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province is the unorganized tract?
      `the province or territory of the territorial division or provisional judicial district` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province is the territorial division or provisional judicial district where the proceedings would be?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 480(1), may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division or provisional judicial district for an offence in an unorganized tract` MEANS
    `s 480(1) proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division or provisional judicial district` `my offence was committed in an unorganized tract of country, or on a lake, river or other water in it, not in a territorial division or provisional judicial district` `the province or territory of the tract` `the province or territory of the territorial division or provisional judicial district`

@ref s 480(2)
@export Under section 480(2), does the jurisdiction conferred by section 480(1) continue after a new district or division is constituted in the tract?
GIVEN `a provisional judicial district or new territorial division is constituted in the tract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a provisional judicial district or a new territorial division been constituted in the unorganized tract?
      `appropriate provision has been made by law for the administration of criminal justice there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has appropriate provision been made by law for the administration of criminal justice within that provisional judicial district or new territorial division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 480(2), does the jurisdiction conferred by section 480(1) continue after a new district or division is constituted in the tract` MEANS
    `s 480(2) subsection (2) continues the jurisdiction conferred by subsection (1)` `a provisional judicial district or new territorial division is constituted in the tract` `appropriate provision has been made by law for the administration of criminal justice there`

@ref s 481
@export Under section 481, may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division for an offence in a part of Canada not in a province?
GIVEN `my offence was committed in a part of Canada not in a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed in a part of Canada that is not in a province?
      `the territorial division is in a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the territorial division where the proceedings would be in a province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 481, may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division for an offence in a part of Canada not in a province` MEANS
    `s 481 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` `my offence was committed in a part of Canada not in a province` `the territorial division is in a province`

@ref s 481.1
@export Under section 481.1, may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division for an offence in Canadian waters?
GIVEN `my offence was committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or the internal waters of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or an area of the sea that forms part of the internal waters of Canada? (It makes no difference whether you are in Canada.)
      `the territorial division is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the territorial division where the proceedings would be in Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 481.1, may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division for an offence in Canadian waters` MEANS
    `s 481.1 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` `my offence was committed in or on the territorial sea of Canada or the internal waters of Canada` `the territorial division is in Canada`

@ref s 481.2
@export Under section 481.2, may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division for an act or omission committed outside Canada?
GIVEN `the act or omission was committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act or omission committed outside Canada?
      `it is an offence when committed outside Canada under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offence, when committed outside Canada, under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament? (It makes no difference whether you are in Canada.)
      `another provision of an Act of Parliament limits the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another provision of this or any other Act of Parliament limit this section in your case?
      `the territorial division is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the territorial division where the proceedings would be in Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 481.2, may proceedings be commenced and may I be charged, tried and punished within this territorial division for an act or omission committed outside Canada` MEANS
    `s 481.2 proceedings may be commenced and the accused may be charged, tried and punished within the territorial division` `the act or omission was committed outside Canada` `it is an offence when committed outside Canada under an Act of Parliament` (JUST `another provision of an Act of Parliament limits the section`) `the territorial division is in Canada`

@ref s 481.3
@export Under section 481.3, do the provisions of the Criminal Code on my appearance at proceedings apply to proceedings commenced under section 481, 481.1 or 481.2?
GIVEN `the section under which the proceedings were commenced` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section were the proceedings commenced in this territorial division (481, 481.1 or 481.2)?
      `the matter` IS A `s 481.3 the matter the provisions relate to` @desc What do the provisions concern: the requirement of the appearance of an accused at proceedings, the exceptions to that requirement, or another matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 481.3, do the provisions of the Criminal Code on my appearance at proceedings apply to proceedings commenced under section 481, 481.1 or 481.2` MEANS
    `s 481.3 the provisions of this Act relating to the matter apply to the proceedings` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section under which the proceedings were commenced`, "") `the matter`

§ `Part XIV -- Rules of court and case management`

§§ `The rules of court that apply to my case (s 482)`

-- The rule-making powers themselves (ss 482(1) to (3), 482(5), 482.1(1)) address courts and the Governor in Council and have no seat: the questions below ask what they mean to the accused.
@ref s 482(1)
@export Under section 482(1), do the rules of court made by the court that is to hear my case apply to my prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal?
GIVEN `the court that makes the rules` IS A `s 2 named court` @desc Which court made the rules? Choose it from the list (a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a court of appeal).
      `the province or territory where that court sits` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory does that court sit?
      `the rules are not inconsistent with an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rules not inconsistent with the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament?
      `my case is within the jurisdiction of that court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal within the jurisdiction of that court?
      `my case is in relation to a matter of a criminal nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it instituted in relation to a matter of a criminal nature, or does it arise from or is it incidental to such a prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482(1), do the rules of court made by the court that is to hear my case apply to my prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` MEANS
    `s 482(1) the rules so made apply to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (`s 482(1) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this or any other Act of Parliament` (`s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` `the court that makes the rules` `the province or territory where that court sits`) (`s 2 court of appeal` (`the court that makes the rules` EQUALS `the Court of Appeal`)) `the rules are not inconsistent with an Act of Parliament`) `my case is within the jurisdiction of that court` `my case is in relation to a matter of a criminal nature`

@ref s 482(2)
@export Under section 482(2), are the rules of court made by the court that is to hear my case applicable to my prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal?
GIVEN `the court that makes the rules` IS A `s 482(2) the court` @desc Which court made the rules? Choose it from the list of courts in section 482(2).
      `it is a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province?
      `it is an appeal court within the meaning of section 812` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an appeal court within the meaning of section 812?
      `it is a court referred to in subsection 482(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a court of appeal (a court referred to in subsection 482(1))?
      `the rules are not inconsistent with an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rules not inconsistent with the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament?
      `my case is within the jurisdiction of that court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal within the jurisdiction of that court?
      `my case is in relation to a matter of a criminal nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it instituted in relation to a matter of a criminal nature, or does it arise from or is it incidental to such a prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482(2), are the rules of court made by the court that is to hear my case applicable to my prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` MEANS
    `s 482(2) the rules so made are applicable to the prosecution, proceeding, action or appeal` (`s 482(2) the court may make rules of court not inconsistent with this Act or any other Act of Parliament` `the court that makes the rules` (JUST `it is a court of criminal jurisdiction for a province`) (JUST `it is an appeal court within the meaning of section 812`) (JUST `it is a court referred to in subsection 482(1)`) `the rules are not inconsistent with an Act of Parliament`) `my case is within the jurisdiction of that court` `my case is in relation to a matter of a criminal nature`

@ref s 482(4)
@export Under section 482(4), have the rules of court been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the rules of court are made under section 482` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rules of court ones made under section 482?
      `the rules have been published or made available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the rules been published or otherwise made available to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482(4), have the rules of court been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `s 482(4) the rules of court have been published or otherwise made available to the public as the subsection requires` `the rules of court are made under section 482` `the rules have been published or made available to the public`

@ref s 482(5)
@export Under section 482(5), do the uniform rules made by the Governor in Council prevail and have effect as if enacted by the Criminal Code?
GIVEN `the rules are uniform rules made under the authority of subsection 482(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rules uniform rules made by the Governor in Council under the authority of subsection 482(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482(5), do the uniform rules made by the Governor in Council prevail and have effect as if enacted by the Criminal Code` MEANS
    `s 482(5) the uniform rules prevail and have effect as if enacted by this Act` `the rules are uniform rules made under the authority of subsection 482(5)`

§§ `Case management (s 482.1)`

-- Situation: the court has made rules for case management and given a direction under them. The form can ask "Has a case management rule been made in your court?" first.
@ref s 482.1(2)
@export Under section 482.1(2), have I complied with the case management direction as the subsection requires?
GIVEN `the direction was made in accordance with a rule made under subsection 482.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the direction made in accordance with a rule of court for case management?
      `I have complied with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with the direction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482.1(2), have I complied with the case management direction as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `s 482.1(2) the party has complied with the direction as the subsection requires` `the direction was made in accordance with a rule made under subsection 482.1(1)` `I have complied with the direction`

@ref s 482.1(3)
@export Under section 482.1(3), may a court, justice or judge issue a summons or warrant to compel my presence at case management proceedings?
GIVEN `rules are made under subsection 482.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have rules for case management been made under subsection 482.1(1)?
      `the person issuing it is a court, justice or judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person issuing the summons or warrant a court, a justice or a judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482.1(3), may a court, justice or judge issue a summons or warrant to compel my presence at case management proceedings` MEANS
    `s 482.1(3) a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings` `rules are made under subsection 482.1(1)` `the person issuing it is a court, justice or judge`

@ref s 482.1(4)
@export Under section 482.1(4), do sections 512 and 512.3 apply to the issuing of a summons or warrant to compel my presence at case management proceedings?
GIVEN `the summons or warrant is issued under subsection 482.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the summons or warrant issued under subsection 482.1(3), to compel your presence at case management proceedings?
      `the section in question` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code do you ask about (512 or 512.3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482.1(4), do sections 512 and 512.3 apply to the issuing of a summons or warrant to compel my presence at case management proceedings` MEANS
    `s 482.1(4) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the issuance of the summons or warrant` `the summons or warrant is issued under subsection 482.1(3)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section in question`, "")

@ref s 482.1(5)
@export Under section 482.1(5), do subsections 482(4) and (5) apply to the rules of court for case management?
GIVEN `the rules are made under subsection 482.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rules ones made under subsection 482.1(1), for case management?
      `the subsection in question` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of section 482 do you ask about: (4) or (5)? (Write it with its brackets, for example (4).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 482.1(5), do subsections 482(4) and (5) apply to the rules of court for case management` MEANS
    `s 482.1(5) the provision applies, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to the rules` `the rules are made under subsection 482.1(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 482, `the subsection in question`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc16 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc16-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER for ccc16 (sections 483 to 487.04 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46).
-- Part agent ccc16. One thin layer over the layer-1 modules imported above; it calls their rules and restates none.
-- Source of the layer-1 rules: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence, what its gravity and penalty are,
-- what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a conviction.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
-- This range holds the opening of Part XV: the court's powers in a proceeding against the accused (ss 483 to 485.2), the protections for witnesses and what they mean for the accused (ss 486 to 486.7),
-- the police's search and production powers and the person's protections against them (ss 487 to 487.02), and the DNA definitions (s 487.04).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates, or a phrase picked from a list named in the @desc -- one for each fact the person can state. The layer-1 records are built inside each question.
-- Provisions that address only an official (the judge, the justice, the prosecutor, the peace officer) are asked for what they mean to the accused: what may be done to them, what they must be given, by when.
-- Where a question is a bar ("is ... barred", "is ... prohibited"), JUST TRUE means the bar applies; where it is a grant ("may ...") JUST TRUE means it is granted; where it is a duty ("must ...") JUST TRUE means the duty arises.
-- NOTHING is "not covered" and is never FALSE: the section is silent or its own limit is not met.
-- Terms of section 2 the layer-1 rules take as MAYBE BOOLEAN ("victim", "intimate partner", "offence-related property", "justice system participant" ...) are asked here as plain yes/no questions: the seat cannot ask "not covered".
-- Fixed figures: none is replaced by a minister's order in this range.


§ `The seat's helpers: plain answers turned into the layer-1 choices`

-- Each helper turns a plain answer (a phrase the person picks) into the module's own choice. An answer that is none of the listed phrases becomes the "another ..." choice, which the layer-1 rule answers NOTHING.
GIVEN x IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 486 who applies for the order`
`s 486 seat: who applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x EQUALS "the prosecutor" THEN `s 486 the prosecutor`
        IF x EQUALS "a witness" THEN `s 486 a witness`
        IF x EQUALS "the judge or justice on their own motion" THEN `s 486 the judge or justice on their own motion`
        IF x EQUALS "the accused" THEN `s 486 the accused`
        OTHERWISE `s 486 another person`

GIVEN x IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 486(1) the order sought`
`s 486(1) seat: the order sought` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x EQUALS "exclusion of the public" THEN `s 486(1) the exclusion of all or any members of the public from the court room for all or part of the proceedings`
        IF x EQUALS "a screen" THEN `s 486(1) that the witness testify behind a screen or other device that would allow the witness not to be seen by members of the public`
        OTHERWISE `s 486(1) an order of another kind`

GIVEN x IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 486.4 who applies`
`s 486.4 seat: who applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x EQUALS "the prosecutor" THEN `s 486.4 the prosecutor`
        IF x EQUALS "the victim" THEN `s 486.4 the victim`
        IF x EQUALS "a witness under 18" THEN `s 486.4 a witness under the age of 18 years`
        IF x EQUALS "a witness 18 or older" THEN `s 486.4 a witness of the age of 18 years or more`
        IF x EQUALS "a justice system participant" THEN `s 486.4 a justice system participant`
        IF x EQUALS "the accused" THEN `s 486.4 the accused`
        OTHERWISE `s 486.4 another person`

GIVEN x IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 486.5(9) what would be published`
`s 486.5(9) seat: what would be published` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x EQUALS "the contents of an application" THEN `s 486.5(9) the contents of an application`
        IF x EQUALS "evidence or submissions at a hearing" THEN `s 486.5(9) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection (6)`
        IF x EQUALS "other identifying information" THEN `s 486.5(9) any other information that could identify the person to whom the application relates as a victim, witness or justice system participant in the proceedings`
        OTHERWISE `s 486.5(9) something else`

GIVEN x IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 485.2(8) how the summons was served`
`s 485.2(8) seat: how served` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x EQUALS "delivered to me personally" THEN `s 485.2(8) delivered personally to the person to whom it is directed`
        IF x EQUALS "left at my usual residence with a person found there" THEN `s 485.2(8) left at the person's latest or usual place of residence with a person found there`
        OTHERWISE `s 485.2(8) served in another way`

GIVEN x IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 487(2.2) what the person in possession or control must permit`
`s 487(2.2) seat: what I must permit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF x EQUALS "to use a computer system to search data" THEN `s 487(2.2)(a) to use or cause to be used any computer system at the building or place in order to search any data contained in or available to the computer system for data that the person is authorized by this section to search for`
        IF x EQUALS "to obtain a hard copy of the data and seize it" THEN `s 487(2.2)(b) to obtain a hard copy of the data and to seize it`
        IF x EQUALS "to use copying equipment" THEN `s 487(2.2)(c) to use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data`
        OTHERWISE `s 487(2.2) something else`

GIVEN x IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 487.012(4) the kind of offence the demand concerns`
`s 487.012(4) seat: the kind of offence` MEANS
    IF x EQUALS "an offence under a law of a foreign state"
    THEN `s 487.012(4)(b) an offence committed under a law of a foreign state`
    ELSE `s 487.012(4)(a) an offence that has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament`

-- The most fine and the longest term the sections state, read from the layer-1 punishments.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 487.0197 the most fine in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 487.0197 the punishment the section states`'s `maximum fine`
    WHEN `a fine of` dollars THEN JUST dollars
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine

GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 487.0198 the most fine in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 487.0198 the punishment the section states`'s `maximum fine`
    WHEN `a fine of` dollars THEN JUST dollars
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine

GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 487.0198 the longest term of imprisonment, in words` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 487.0198 the punishment the section states`'s `maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` t THEN JUST (CONCAT (TOSTRING (t's years)), " years", (IF t's `less a day` THEN " less a day" ELSE ""))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no term of imprisonment

-- s 487.04: the person's plain answers become the offence's facts record.
GIVEN `the section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING
      `where the offence provision is found` IS A STRING
      `how I am charged` IS A STRING
      `the purpose` IS A STRING
      `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence carries imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longest term of imprisonment, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the term is less a day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent of an assault with intent was to commit one of the listed sexual offences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 487.04 facts of the offence`
`s 487.04 seat: facts` MEANS `s 487.04 facts of the offence` WITH
    `the provision that creates the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`
    `where that provision is found` IS `where`
    `how the person is charged` IS `how`
    `the purpose` IS `purpose`
    `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment` IS `the offence may be prosecuted by indictment`
    `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS `the offence is prosecuted by indictment`
    `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS `imprisonment`
    `the intent of an assault under subsection 246(1) is to commit an offence referred to in subparagraphs (b)(i) to (vi)` IS `the intent of an assault with intent was to commit one of the listed sexual offences`
    WHERE
        `where` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "this Act as it reads now" THEN `s 487.04 this Act as it reads now`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "this Act before the paragraph came into force" THEN `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which the paragraph that names it comes into force`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "this Act before July 1, 1990" THEN `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before July 1, 1990`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "this Act before the conveyances amendment" THEN `s 487.04 this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which section 14 of the Act to amend the Criminal Code (offences relating to conveyances) comes into force`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "the 1970 Code before January 4, 1983" THEN `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "the 1970 Code before January 1, 1988" THEN `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "the 1970 Code as enacted by chapter 125" THEN `s 487.04 the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act" THEN `s 487.04 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "the Cannabis Act" THEN `s 487.04 the Cannabis Act`
                IF `where the offence provision is found` EQUALS "the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act" THEN `s 487.04 the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
                OTHERWISE `s 487.04 another instrument`
        `how` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `how I am charged` EQUALS "with an attempt" THEN `s 487.04 with an attempt to commit the listed offence`
                IF `how I am charged` EQUALS "with a conspiracy" THEN `s 487.04 with a conspiracy to commit the listed offence`
                OTHERWISE `s 487.04 with the listed offence itself`
        `purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the purpose` EQUALS "a warrant under subsection 487.05(1)" THEN `s 487.04 the purposes of subsection 487.05(1)`
                IF `the purpose` EQUALS "an order under section 487.051" THEN `s 487.04 the purposes of section 487.051`
                OTHERWISE `s 487.04 another purpose`
        `imprisonment` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the offence carries imprisonment for life` THEN `imprisonment for life`
                IF `the longest term of imprisonment, in years` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF `the longest term of imprisonment, in years`, 0, 0, `the term is less a day`)
                OTHERWISE `no imprisonment is stated`

§ `Procedural irregularities and the summons for the Identification of Criminals Act (ss 483 to 485.2)`

-- Situation: a court or justice did not act in time, you did not appear in person, or you were summoned to be identified. Ask 'Has this happened to you?' before showing the group.

-- Under section 483, may a judge or provincial court judge alone do what two or more justices are authorized to do.
@ref s 483
@export Under section 483, may a judge or provincial court judge alone do what the Code authorizes two or more justices to do?
GIVEN `the person is a judge or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting a judge or a provincial court judge?
      `the law of the province authorizes that judge to do what two or more justices are required to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law of the province in which they are appointed authorize them to do anything that is required to be done by two or more justices?
      `the thing is one that the Code authorizes two or more justices to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it something that the Criminal Code or another Act of Parliament authorizes two or more justices to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 483, may a judge or provincial court judge alone do what two or more justices are authorized to do` MEANS
    `s 483 the judge or provincial court judge may do alone what two or more justices are authorized to do` `the person is a judge or provincial court judge` `the law of the province authorizes that judge to do what two or more justices are required to do` `the thing is one that the Code authorizes two or more justices to do`

-- Under section 485(1), is jurisdiction over the offence lost because a court failed to act at a particular time or an adjournment or remand rule was not followed.
@ref s 485(1)
@export Under section 485(1), is jurisdiction over the offence lost because a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice failed to act at a particular time, or an adjournment or remand rule was not followed?
GIVEN `a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice failed to act at a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice fail to act in the exercise of its jurisdiction at a particular time?
      `a rule of the Code on adjournments or remands was not followed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a provision of the Criminal Code about adjournments or remands not complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485(1), is jurisdiction over the offence lost because a court failed to act at a particular time or an adjournment or remand rule was not followed` MEANS
    `s 485(1) jurisdiction over the offence is lost by reason of the failure` `a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice failed to act at a particular time` `a rule of the Code on adjournments or remands was not followed`

-- Under section 485(1.1), is jurisdiction over me lost because I did not appear personally or in person.
@ref s 485(1.1)
@export Under section 485(1.1), is jurisdiction over me lost because I did not appear personally or in person?
GIVEN `I did not appear personally or in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to appear personally or in person?
      `a provision of the Code or a rule of court allows me not to appear personally or in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Criminal Code, or a rule made under section 482 or 482.1, permit you not to appear personally or in person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485(1.1), is jurisdiction over me lost because I did not appear personally or in person` MEANS
    `s 485(1.1) jurisdiction over the accused is lost by reason of the failure to appear personally or in person` `I did not appear personally or in person` `a provision of the Code or a rule of court allows me not to appear personally or in person`

-- Under section 485(2), may a summons be issued against me on the day proposed.
@ref s 485(2)
@export Under section 485(2), may a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice issue a summons against me on the day proposed?
GIVEN `jurisdiction over me is lost and has not been regained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has jurisdiction over you been lost and not regained?
      `the day jurisdiction over me was lost` IS A DATE @desc On what date was jurisdiction over you lost?
      `the day the summons is issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the summons issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485(2), may a summons be issued against me on the day proposed` MEANS
    `s 485(2) the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may issue a summons` `jurisdiction over me is lost and has not been regained` `the day jurisdiction over me was lost` `the day the summons is issued`

-- Under section 485(2), may a warrant for my arrest be issued on the day proposed.
@ref s 485(2)
@export Under section 485(2), may a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice issue a warrant for my arrest on the day proposed, if it or they consider it necessary in the public interest?
GIVEN `jurisdiction over me is lost and has not been regained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has jurisdiction over you been lost and not regained?
      `the day jurisdiction over me was lost` IS A DATE @desc On what date was jurisdiction over you lost?
      `the day the warrant is issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the warrant issued?
      `the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice considers the warrant necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice consider the warrant necessary in the public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485(2), may a warrant for my arrest be issued on the day proposed` MEANS
    `s 485(2) the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may issue a warrant for the arrest` `jurisdiction over me is lost and has not been regained` `the day jurisdiction over me was lost` `the day the warrant is issued` `the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice considers the warrant necessary in the public interest`

-- Under section 485(3), are the proceedings against me deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution.
@ref s 485(3)
@export Under section 485(3), are the proceedings against me deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution on the day I am asking?
GIVEN `the day jurisdiction over me was lost` IS A DATE @desc On what date was jurisdiction over you lost?
      `a summons or warrant was issued under subsection 485(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a summons or a warrant for your arrest issued after jurisdiction over you was lost?
      `the day it was issued` IS A DATE @desc If one was issued, on what date? (Give any date if none was issued.)
      `the day I am asking` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485(3), are the proceedings against me deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution` MEANS
    `s 485(3) the proceedings are deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution` `the day jurisdiction over me was lost` (IF `a summons or warrant was issued under subsection 485(2)` THEN JUST `the day it was issued` ELSE NOTHING) `the day I am asking`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no such day exists, so none is passed on

-- Under section 485.1, is a new information or a new indictment in respect of the same transaction barred.
@ref s 485.1
@export Under section 485.1, is a new information or a new indictment in respect of the same transaction barred, without the Attorney General's consent or a judge's order?
GIVEN `the indictment was dismissed, or deemed dismissed, for want of prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an indictment about this transaction dismissed, or deemed dismissed, for want of prosecution?
      `the Attorney General conducts or intervenes in the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General conduct the prosecution, or intervene in it?
      `the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General has consented personally in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General or the Deputy Attorney General given personal consent in writing to a new information or indictment?
      `a judge has made a written order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judge of that court made a written order allowing it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485.1, is a new information or a new indictment in respect of the same transaction barred` MEANS
    `s 485.1 a new information or a new indictment in respect of the same transaction is barred` `the indictment was dismissed, or deemed dismissed, for want of prosecution` `the Attorney General conducts or intervenes in the prosecution` `the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General has consented personally in writing` `a judge has made a written order`

-- Under section 485.2(1), may a justice or judge summon me to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act.
@ref s 485.2(1)
@export Under section 485.2(1), may a justice or judge summon me to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act?
GIVEN `the application is in writing and on oath in Form 6.1 or made by telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application made in writing and on oath in Form 6.1, or by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing?
      `I am charged with, or found guilty of, an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with, or have you been found guilty of, an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act?
      `I was previously required to appear for those purposes and the measurements, processes or operations were not completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you previously required to appear for the purposes of that Act, and were the measurements, processes or operations not completed?
      `the justice or judge is satisfied that the reasons they were not completed were exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice or judge satisfied that the reasons for the measurements, processes or operations not having been completed were exceptional?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485.2(1), may a justice or judge summon me to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` MEANS
    `s 485.2(1) a justice or judge may issue a summons requiring the accused or offender to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` `the application is in writing and on oath in Form 6.1 or made by telecommunication` `I am charged with, or found guilty of, an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act` `I was previously required to appear for those purposes and the measurements, processes or operations were not completed` `the justice or judge is satisfied that the reasons they were not completed were exceptional`

-- Under section 485.2(7), does the summons I was given have the contents the section requires.
@ref s 485.2(7)
@export Under section 485.2(7), does the summons I was given have the contents the section requires?
GIVEN `the summons is directed to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the summons directed to you?
      `the summons sets out briefly the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the summons set out briefly the offence you are charged with, or were found guilty of?
      `the summons sets out a summary of the listed provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the summons set out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485.2(7), does the summons I was given have the contents the section requires` MEANS
    `s 485.2(7) the summons has the contents required` `the summons is directed to me` `the summons sets out briefly the offence` `the summons sets out a summary of the listed provisions`

-- Under section 485.2(8), was the summons served on me as the section requires.
@ref s 485.2(8)
@export Under section 485.2(8), was the summons served on me as the section requires: by a peace officer, delivered to me personally or left at my usual residence with a person who appears to be at least 16?
GIVEN `a peace officer served it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the summons served by a peace officer?
      `how it was served` IS A STRING @desc How was it served? One of: "delivered to me personally", "left at my usual residence with a person found there", "another way".
      `I could not conveniently be found` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you not conveniently be found?
      `the apparent age of the person it was left with` IS A NUMBER @desc If it was left with someone at your residence, how old did they appear to be, in years? (0 if it was not left with anyone.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 485.2(8), was the summons served on me as the section requires` MEANS
    `s 485.2(8) the summons was served as required` `a peace officer served it` (`s 485.2(8) seat: how served` `how it was served`) `I could not conveniently be found` `the apparent age of the person it was left with`

§ `Open court, support persons, testimony and cross-examination (ss 486 to 486.3)`

-- Situation: your trial is under way or about to begin and a witness or the prosecutor asks for protections for a witness. Ask 'Is a witness protection being sought in your case?' before showing the group.

-- Under section 486(1), must the proceedings against me be held in open court.
@ref s 486(1)
@export Under section 486(1), must the proceedings against me be held in open court?
GIVEN `an order has been made excluding the public or requiring a witness to testify behind a screen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order been made under section 486(1) excluding the public, or that a witness testify behind a screen?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486(1), must the proceedings against me be held in open court` MEANS
    `s 486(1) the proceedings against the accused are held in open court` `an order has been made excluding the public or requiring a witness to testify behind a screen`

-- Under section 486(1), may the judge or justice exclude the public from my trial or order a witness to testify behind a screen.
@ref s 486(1)
@export Under section 486(1), may the presiding judge or justice exclude the public from my trial, or order a witness to testify behind a screen?
GIVEN `who asks for the order` IS A STRING @desc Who asks for the order? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the order asked for` IS A STRING @desc What is asked for? One of: "exclusion of the public", "a screen", "something else".
      `public morals, order or the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order is in the interest of public morals, the maintenance of order or the proper administration of justice?
      `international relations, national defence or national security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order is necessary to prevent injury to international relations or national defence or national security?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486(1), may the judge or justice exclude the public from my trial or order a witness to testify behind a screen` MEANS
    `s 486(1) the presiding judge or justice may order the exclusion of the public or that the witness testify behind a screen` (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who asks for the order`) (`s 486(1) seat: the order sought` `the order asked for`) `public morals, order or the proper administration of justice` `international relations, national defence or national security`

-- Under section 486(3), must the judge or justice state the reason for not making an exclusion order on the application made.
@ref s 486(3)
@export Under section 486(3), when I am charged with one of the listed sexual offences, must the judge or justice state the reason for not making an exclusion order on the application made?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with? (for example 271, or 163.1)
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of that section, written as in the Code, for example "(2)"? (Leave empty if none.)
      `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies for the order? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the accused", "another person".
      `no order is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no order made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486(3), must the judge or justice state the reason for not making an exclusion order on the application made` MEANS
    `s 486(3) the judge or justice must state the reason for not making an order` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`) (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `no order is made`

-- Under section 486(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that an order is, or is not, made.
@ref s 486(4)
@export Under section 486(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that an exclusion order is, or is not, made?
GIVEN `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inference drawn from the fact that an order was, or was not, made under section 486?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that an order is, or is not, made` MEANS
    `s 486(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made`

-- Under section 486.1(1), must the court allow a support person or support animal for a witness against me who is under 18 or has a disability.
@ref s 486.1(1)
@export Under section 486.1(1), must the court allow a support person or a support animal for a witness against me who is under 18 or has a mental or physical disability?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the age of the witness` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the witness, in years?
      `the witness has a mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the witness have a mental or physical disability?
      `the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.1(1), must the court allow a support person or support animal for a witness against me who is under 18 or has a disability` MEANS
    `s 486.1(1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted` (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the age of the witness` `the witness has a mental or physical disability` `the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.1(1.1), must the court allow a support person or support animal for a witness who is the victim of a listed offence.
@ref s 486.1(1.1)
@export Under section 486.1(1.1), must the court allow a support person or a support animal for a witness who is the victim, where I am charged with a sexual offence, criminal harassment, trafficking in persons or an offence against my intimate partner?
GIVEN `the offence is of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose?
      `the offence relates to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons?
      `the victim is my intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence committed against your intimate partner?
      `the witness is a victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the witness a victim of the offence?
      `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.1(1.1), must the court allow a support person or support animal for a witness who is the victim of a listed offence` MEANS
    `s 486.1(1.1) the judge or justice must order that a support person or a support animal be permitted for a victim` (`s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` `the offence is of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose` `the offence relates to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons` (JUST `the victim is my intimate partner`)) (JUST `the witness is a victim`) (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.1(4), is the judge or justice barred from permitting a witness to be a support person.
@ref s 486.1(4)
@export Under section 486.1(4), is the judge or justice barred from permitting a witness to be a support person?
GIVEN `the proposed support person is a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposed support person a witness?
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that permitting the witness to be a support person is necessary for the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.1(4), is the judge or justice barred from permitting a witness to be a support person` MEANS
    `s 486.1(4) the judge or justice is barred from permitting a witness to be a support person` `the proposed support person is a witness` `the judge or justice is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.1(6), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a support person or animal order is, or is not, made.
@ref s 486.1(6)
@export Under section 486.1(6), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a support person or support animal order is, or is not, made?
GIVEN `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inference drawn from the fact that an order was, or was not, made under section 486.1?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.1(6), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a support person or animal order is, or is not, made` MEANS
    `s 486.1(6) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made`

-- Under section 486.2(1), must the court order that a witness against me testify outside the court room or behind a screen so that the witness does not see me.
@ref s 486.2(1)
@export Under section 486.2(1), must the court order that a witness against me who is under 18, or who may have difficulty communicating evidence because of a disability, testify outside the court room or behind a screen?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the age of the witness` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the witness, in years?
      `the witness may have difficulty communicating evidence because of a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the witness able to communicate evidence but likely to have difficulty doing so because of a mental or physical disability?
      `the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.2(1), must the court order that a witness against me testify outside the court room or behind a screen so that the witness does not see me` MEANS
    `s 486.2(1) the judge or justice must order that the witness testify outside the court room or behind a screen, at the option of the witness` (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the age of the witness` `the witness may have difficulty communicating evidence because of a disability` `the order would interfere with the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.2(5), is a witness barred from testifying outside the court room unless I can watch by closed-circuit television or videoconference and can communicate with my counsel.
@ref s 486.2(5)
@export Under section 486.2(5), is a witness barred from testifying outside the court room unless I can watch the testimony by closed-circuit television or videoconference and can communicate with my counsel while watching?
GIVEN `the witness would testify outside the court room under an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the witness testify outside the court room in accordance with an order under section 486.2(1), (1.1) or (2)?
      `arrangements are made for me, the judge or justice and the jury to watch the testimony` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are arrangements made for you, the judge or justice and the jury to watch the testimony by closed-circuit television or videoconference?
      `I am permitted to communicate with my counsel while watching` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you permitted to communicate with your counsel while watching the testimony?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.2(5), is a witness barred from testifying outside the court room unless I can watch by closed-circuit television or videoconference and can communicate with my counsel` MEANS
    `s 486.2(5) the witness is barred from testifying outside the court room in accordance with the order` `the witness would testify outside the court room under an order` `arrangements are made for me, the judge or justice and the jury to watch the testimony` `I am permitted to communicate with my counsel while watching`

-- Under section 486.2(6), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a testimony order is, or is not, made.
@ref s 486.2(6)
@export Under section 486.2(6), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that an order about how a witness testifies is, or is not, made?
GIVEN `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inference drawn from the fact that an order was, or was not, made under section 486.2?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.2(6), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a testimony order is, or is not, made` MEANS
    `s 486.2(6) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made`

-- Under section 486.3(1), must the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is under 18.
@ref s 486.3(1)
@export Under section 486.3(1), must the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is under 18, and appoint counsel to do it?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the age of the witness` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the witness, in years?
      `the proper administration of justice requires me to cross-examine personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the proper administration of justice requires you to conduct the cross-examination personally?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.3(1), must the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is under 18` MEANS
    `s 486.3(1) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the witness under 18` (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the age of the witness` `the proper administration of justice requires me to cross-examine personally`

-- Under section 486.3(2), must the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is the victim of a listed offence.
@ref s 486.3(2)
@export Under section 486.3(2), must the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is the victim, where I am charged with a sexual offence, criminal harassment, trafficking in persons or an offence against my intimate partner?
GIVEN `the offence is of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose?
      `the offence relates to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons?
      `the victim is my intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence committed against your intimate partner?
      `the witness is a victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the witness a victim of the offence?
      `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the proper administration of justice requires me to cross-examine personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the proper administration of justice requires you to conduct the cross-examination personally?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.3(2), must the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is the victim of a listed offence` MEANS
    `s 486.3(2) the judge or justice must order that the accused not personally cross-examine the victim` (`s 486.1(1.1) the proceedings are in respect of one of the offences the subsection names` `the offence is of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose` `the offence relates to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons` (JUST `the victim is my intimate partner`)) (JUST `the witness is a victim`) (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the proper administration of justice requires me to cross-examine personally`

-- Under section 486.3(3), may the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is not entitled to apply under subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 486.3(3)
@export Under section 486.3(3), may the court order that I not personally cross-examine another witness, one who is not entitled to apply under subsection (1) or (2)?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the witness is not entitled to apply under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the witness not entitled to make an application under subsection 486.3(1) or (2)?
      `the order would allow a full and candid account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order would allow the witness to give a full and candid account of the acts complained of?
      `the order would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.3(3), may the court order that I not personally cross-examine a witness who is not entitled to apply under subsection (1) or (2)` MEANS
    `s 486.3(3) the judge or justice may order that the accused not personally cross-examine another witness` (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the witness is not entitled to apply under subsection (1) or (2)` `the order would allow a full and candid account` `the order would otherwise be in the interest of the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.3(5), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed.
@ref s 486.3(5)
@export Under section 486.3(5), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed to cross-examine a witness?
GIVEN `an inference is drawn from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inference drawn from the fact that counsel was, or was not, appointed under section 486.3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.3(5), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed` MEANS
    `s 486.3(5) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed under this section` `an inference is drawn from the fact that counsel is, or is not, appointed`

-- Under section 486.31(1), may the judge or justice order that information that could identify a witness not be disclosed in my proceedings.
@ref s 486.31(1)
@export Under section 486.31(1), may the judge or justice order that information that could identify a witness not be disclosed in the course of my proceedings?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.31(1), may the judge or justice order that information that could identify a witness not be disclosed in my proceedings` MEANS
    `s 486.31(1) the judge or justice may order that information that could identify the witness not be disclosed in the course of the proceedings` (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.31(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a non-disclosure order is, or is not, made.
@ref s 486.31(4)
@export Under section 486.31(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that an order about a witness's identity is, or is not, made?
GIVEN `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inference drawn from the fact that an order was, or was not, made under section 486.31?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.31(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a non-disclosure order is, or is not, made` MEANS
    `s 486.31(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made`

-- Under section 486.7(1), may the presiding judge or justice make an order to protect the security of a witness in my case.
@ref s 486.7(1)
@export Under section 486.7(1), may the presiding judge or justice make an order, other than one under sections 486 to 486.5, to protect the security of a witness in my case?
GIVEN `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who asks for the order? One of: "the prosecutor", "a witness", "the judge or justice on their own motion", "the accused", "another person".
      `the order is one that may be made under sections 486 to 486.5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an order that may be made under any of sections 486 to 486.5?
      `the order is necessary to protect the security of the witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order is necessary to protect the security of the witness?
      `the order is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.7(1), may the presiding judge or justice make an order to protect the security of a witness in my case` MEANS
    `s 486.7(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order to protect the security of a witness` (`s 486 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the order is one that may be made under sections 486 to 486.5` `the order is necessary to protect the security of the witness` `the order is otherwise in the interest of the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.7(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a witness security order is, or is not, made.
@ref s 486.7(4)
@export Under section 486.7(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that an order protecting a witness's security is, or is not, made?
GIVEN `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the inference drawn from the fact that an order was, or was not, made under section 486.7?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.7(4), may an adverse inference be drawn against me from the fact that a witness security order is, or is not, made` MEANS
    `s 486.7(4) an adverse inference may be drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made under this section` `an inference is drawn from the fact that an order is, or is not, made`

-- Under section 486.71, is the judge or justice prohibited from making more than one order regarding the same witness.
@ref s 486.71
@export Under section 486.71, is the judge or justice prohibited from making more than one order regarding the same witness under sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7?
GIVEN `the orders are made under those sections regarding the same witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the orders made under sections 486 to 486.5 or 486.7 and about the same witness?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.71, is the judge or justice prohibited from making more than one order regarding the same witness` MEANS
    `s 486.71 the judge or justice is prohibited from making more than one order regarding the same witness` `the orders are made under those sections regarding the same witness`

§ `Orders restricting publication of the identity of a victim or witness (ss 486.4 to 486.6)`

-- Situation: a ban on publishing who the victim or a witness is has been sought or made. Ask 'Has a publication ban been sought or made in your case?' before showing the group.

-- Under section 486.4(1), may the court ban publication of information that could identify the victim or a witness in my case.
@ref s 486.4(1)
@export Under section 486.4(1), may the court order that information that could identify the victim or a witness in my case not be published?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you are charged with? (for example 271)
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of that section, as written in the Code, for example "(2)"? (Leave empty if none.)
      `the offence is an earlier version of the Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offence under the Criminal Code as it read before the day section 486.4(1)(a)(ii) came into force?
      `the conduct alleged would now be a listed offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the conduct alleged be an offence listed in section 486.4(1)(a)(i) if it occurred today?
      `the other offence in my proceeding` IS A NUMBER @desc If another offence is dealt with in the same proceeding, what is its section number? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.4(1), may the court ban publication of information that could identify the victim or a witness in my case` MEANS
    `s 486.4(1) the presiding judge or justice may make an order directing that information that could identify the victim or a witness not be published` (`s 486.4(1)(b) two or more offences are dealt with in the same proceeding, at least one of which is an offence referred to in paragraph (a)` `the offences in my proceeding` OR `s 486.4(1)(a) the offence is one referred to in paragraph (a)` (`s 486.4(1) offence charged` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`), `the offence is an earlier version of the Code`, `the conduct alleged would now be a listed offence`))
    WHERE
        `the offences in my proceeding` MEANS
            IF `the other offence in my proceeding` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN LIST (`s 486.4(1) offence charged` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`), `the offence is an earlier version of the Code`, `the conduct alleged would now be a listed offence`), (`s 486.4(1) offence charged` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the other offence in my proceeding`, ""), FALSE, FALSE)
            ELSE LIST (`s 486.4(1) offence charged` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`), `the offence is an earlier version of the Code`, `the conduct alleged would now be a listed offence`)

-- Under section 486.4(2), must the presiding judge or justice make a publication ban order on the application made.
@ref s 486.4(2)
@export Under section 486.4(2), in my case for one of the listed offences, must the presiding judge or justice make the publication ban order on the application made?
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of one of the listed offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an offence referred to in paragraph 486.4(1)(a) or (b)?
      `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "the victim", "a witness under 18", "a witness 18 or older", "a justice system participant", "the accused", "another person".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.4(2), must the presiding judge or justice make a publication ban order on the application made` MEANS
    `s 486.4(2)(b) the presiding judge or justice must make the order` `the proceedings are in respect of one of the listed offences` (`s 486.4 seat: who applies` `who applies`)

-- Under section 486.4(4), does a publication ban order made under section 486.4 apply to the disclosure I make.
@ref s 486.4(4)
@export Under section 486.4(4), does a publication ban order made under section 486.4 apply to the disclosure I make?
GIVEN `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made in the course of the administration of justice?
      `the purpose is not to make the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the disclosure not one of making the information known in the community?
      `I am the subject of the order and I disclose only about myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the subject of the order, and is the disclosure about you and your particulars?
      `I did not reveal another protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of, or particulars likely to identify, any other person whose identity is protected by a publication ban?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.4(4), does a publication ban order made under section 486.4 apply to the disclosure I make` MEANS
    `s 486.4(4) the order applies to the disclosure of information` `the disclosure is made in the course of the administration of justice` `the purpose is not to make the information known in the community` `I am the subject of the order and I disclose only about myself` `I did not reveal another protected person`

-- Under section 486.5(1), may a judge or justice make a publication ban order for a victim or witness in my case.
@ref s 486.5(1)
@export Under section 486.5(1), may a judge or justice order that information that could identify a victim or witness in my case not be published, where no order was made under section 486.4?
GIVEN `an order was made under section 486.4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under section 486.4?
      `who applies` IS A STRING @desc Who applies? One of: "the prosecutor", "the victim", "a witness under 18", "a witness 18 or older", "a justice system participant", "the accused", "another person".
      `the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or justice of the opinion that the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.5(1), may a judge or justice make a publication ban order for a victim or witness in my case` MEANS
    `s 486.5(1) the judge or justice may make an order directing that information that could identify the victim or witness not be published` `an order was made under section 486.4` (`s 486.4 seat: who applies` `who applies`) `the order is in the interest of the proper administration of justice`

-- Under section 486.5(4)(b), did the applicant provide notice of the application for a publication ban to the prosecutor, to me and to any other person affected.
@ref s 486.5(4)(b)
@export Under section 486.5(4)(b), did the applicant provide notice of the application for a publication ban to the prosecutor, to me and to any other person affected that the judge or justice specified?
GIVEN `notice was given to the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the application given to the prosecutor?
      `notice was given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the application given to you?
      `notice was given to any other person the judge or justice specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to every other person affected by the order whom the judge or justice specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.5(4)(b), did the applicant provide notice of the application for a publication ban to the prosecutor, to me and to any other person affected` MEANS
    `s 486.5(4)(b) the applicant has provided notice of the application` `notice was given to the prosecutor` `notice was given to me` `notice was given to any other person the judge or justice specified`

-- Under section 486.5(9), am I prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what the section covers.
@ref s 486.5(9)
@export Under section 486.5(9), am I prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the contents of an application for a publication ban, the evidence at a hearing on it, or other information that could identify the person it protects?
GIVEN `the judge or justice refused to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the judge or justice refuse to make an order?
      `what I would publish` IS A STRING @desc What would you publish? One of: "the contents of an application", "evidence or submissions at a hearing", "other identifying information", "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.5(9), am I prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what the section covers` MEANS
    `s 486.5(9) the person is prohibited from publishing, broadcasting or transmitting what would be published` `the judge or justice refused to make an order` (`s 486.5(9) seat: what would be published` `what I would publish`)

-- Under section 486.51(5), is the applicant required to give me notice of an application to vary or revoke a publication ban.
@ref s 486.51(5)
@export Under section 486.51(5), is the applicant required to give me notice of an application to vary or revoke a publication ban order?
GIVEN `it is an application to vary or revoke an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to vary or revoke an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.51(5), is the applicant required to give me notice of an application to vary or revoke a publication ban` MEANS
    `s 486.51(5) the applicant is required to provide notice of the application to vary or revoke the order to the accused` `it is an application to vary or revoke an order made under section 486.4 or 486.5`

-- Under section 486.51(6), am I permitted to make submissions on an application to vary or revoke a publication ban.
@ref s 486.51(6)
@export Under section 486.51(6), am I permitted to make submissions in relation to an application to vary or revoke a publication ban order?
GIVEN `the submissions are about the application to vary or revoke the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the submissions be in relation to the application to vary or revoke the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.51(6), am I permitted to make submissions on an application to vary or revoke a publication ban` MEANS
    `s 486.51(6) the accused is permitted to make submissions in relation to the application` `the submissions are about the application to vary or revoke the order`

-- Under section 486.51(7), is the prosecutor now required to notify me of a change to a publication ban order.
@ref s 486.51(7)
@export Under section 486.51(7), is the prosecutor now required to notify me of a change to a publication ban order?
GIVEN `the order is varied or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the order been varied or revoked?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.51(7), is the prosecutor now required to notify me of a change to a publication ban order` MEANS
    `s 486.51(7) the prosecutor must notify the accused` `the order is varied or revoked`

-- Under section 486.6(1), am I guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction if I fail to comply with a publication ban order.
@ref s 486.6(1)
@export Under section 486.6(1), am I guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction if I fail to comply with a publication ban order made under section 486.4 or 486.5?
GIVEN `the section of the order` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section was the order made? (486.4 or 486.5, for example)
      `the subsection of the order` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection, written as in the Code, for example "(1)"?
      `I fail to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.6(1), am I guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction if I fail to comply with a publication ban order` MEANS
    `s 486.6(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` (`s 486.6(1) the order is one made under any of subsections 486.4(1) to (3) or subsection 486.5(1) or (2)` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the order`, `the subsection of the order`)) `I fail to comply with the order`

-- Under section 486.6(1.1), is the prosecutor barred from prosecuting me for failing to comply with an order that protects me.
@ref s 486.6(1.1)
@export Under section 486.6(1.1), is the prosecutor barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against me for failing to comply with a publication ban order of which I am the subject?
GIVEN `I am the subject of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the subject of the publication ban order?
      `the prosecutor thinks I knowingly failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prosecutor of the opinion that you knowingly failed to comply with the order?
      `the prosecutor thinks the privacy interests of another protected person were compromised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prosecutor of the opinion that the privacy interests of another person protected by a publication ban have been compromised?
      `the prosecutor thinks a warning is not appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prosecutor of the opinion that a warning to you is not appropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 486.6(1.1), is the prosecutor barred from prosecuting me for failing to comply with an order that protects me` MEANS
    `s 486.6(1.1) the prosecutor is barred from commencing or continuing a prosecution against the person who is the subject of the order` `I am the subject of the order` `the prosecutor thinks I knowingly failed to comply` `the prosecutor thinks the privacy interests of another protected person were compromised` `the prosecutor thinks a warning is not appropriate`

§ `Search warrants and general warrants (ss 487 and 487.01)`

-- Situation: the police have a warrant, or want one, to search a place or use an investigative technique. Ask 'Are the police seeking or executing a warrant in your case?' before showing the group.

-- Under section 487(1), may a justice issue a warrant to search the building, receptacle or place.
@ref s 487(1)
@export Under section 487(1), may a justice issue a warrant to search my building, receptacle or place for a thing connected with an offence?
GIVEN `the justice is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice satisfied by information on oath in Form 1 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that one of the things below is in the place?
      `grounds (a): a thing on or in respect of which an offence has been or is suspected to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a thing: anything on or in respect of which any offence has been or is suspected to have been committed?
      `grounds (b): a thing that will afford evidence or reveal the whereabouts of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a thing: anything that will afford evidence of an offence or reveal the whereabouts of a person believed to have committed one?
      `grounds (c): a thing intended to be used to commit an offence against the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a thing: anything intended to be used to commit an offence against the person for which a person may be arrested without warrant?
      `grounds (c.1): offence-related property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there any offence-related property in the place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487(1), may a justice issue a warrant to search the building, receptacle or place` MEANS
    `s 487(1) the justice may issue a warrant to search the building, receptacle or place` `the justice is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1` `grounds (a): a thing on or in respect of which an offence has been or is suspected to have been committed` `grounds (b): a thing that will afford evidence or reveal the whereabouts of a person` `grounds (c): a thing intended to be used to commit an offence against the person` (JUST `grounds (c.1): offence-related property`)

-- Under section 487(2.2), must I permit the person carrying out the search to use a computer system, obtain a hard copy of the data and copy it.
@ref s 487(2.2)
@export Under section 487(2.2), when a search is carried out at a building or place I possess or control, must I, on presentation of the warrant, permit the person carrying out the search to use a computer system there, to obtain a hard copy of the data and seize it, and to use copying equipment?
GIVEN `I am in possession or control of the building or place searched` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in possession or control of the building or place being searched under section 487?
      `the warrant has been presented to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the warrant been presented to you?
      `what I am asked to permit` IS A STRING @desc What are you asked to permit? One of: "to use a computer system to search data", "to obtain a hard copy of the data and seize it", "to use copying equipment", "something else".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487(2.2), must I permit the person carrying out the search to use a computer system, obtain a hard copy of the data and copy it` MEANS
    `s 487(2.2) the person in possession or control must permit the person carrying out the search to do the act` `I am in possession or control of the building or place searched` `the warrant has been presented to me` (`s 487(2.2) seat: what I must permit` `what I am asked to permit`)

-- Under section 487.01(1), may a judge issue a general warrant authorizing a peace officer to use a technique that would otherwise be an unreasonable search or seizure.
@ref s 487.01(1)
@export Under section 487.01(1), may a provincial court judge, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 issue a general warrant authorizing a peace officer to use a technique that would otherwise be an unreasonable search or seizure of me or my property?
GIVEN `the judge is a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge a provincial court judge?
      `the judge is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction?
      `the judge is a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge a judge as defined in section 552?
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe an offence has been or will be committed and information will be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied, by information on oath in writing, that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed and that information about it will be obtained through the technique?
      `the judge is satisfied that issuing it is in the best interests of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant?
      `no other provision provides for a warrant, authorization or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no other provision in the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament that would provide for a warrant, authorization or order permitting the technique to be used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.01(1), may a judge issue a general warrant authorizing a peace officer to use a technique that would otherwise be an unreasonable search or seizure` MEANS
    `s 487.01(1) the judge may issue a warrant in writing authorizing a peace officer to use the device, technique or procedure or do the thing` `the judge is a provincial court judge` `the judge is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (JUST `the judge is a judge as defined in section 552`) `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe an offence has been or will be committed and information will be obtained` `the judge is satisfied that issuing it is in the best interests of the administration of justice` `no other provision provides for a warrant, authorization or order`

-- Under section 487.01(2), does the general warrant provision permit interference with my bodily integrity.
@ref s 487.01(2)
@export Under section 487.01(2), does the general warrant provision permit interference with my bodily integrity?
GIVEN `the act is an interference with my bodily integrity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the act be an interference with the bodily integrity of a person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.01(2), does the general warrant provision permit interference with my bodily integrity` MEANS
    `s 487.01(2) subsection (1) permits the act` `the act is an interference with my bodily integrity`

-- Under section 487.01(5.1), does the general warrant I was given for a covert entry require notice of the entry and search within the time the judge considers reasonable.
@ref s 487.01(5.1)
@export Under section 487.01(5.1), does the general warrant I was given, which authorizes a covert entry and search, require notice of the entry and search to be given within the time after execution that the judge considers reasonable?
GIVEN `the warrant authorizes a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the warrant authorize a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly?
      `the warrant requires notice within the time the judge considers reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the warrant require that notice of the entry and search be given within the time after the execution that the judge considers reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.01(5.1), does the general warrant I was given for a covert entry require notice of the entry and search within the time the judge considers reasonable` MEANS
    `s 487.01(5.1) the warrant requires notice of the covert entry and search as required` `the warrant authorizes a peace officer to enter and search a place covertly` `the warrant requires notice within the time the judge considers reasonable`

§ `Preservation demands and orders, production orders, and what follows (ss 487.011 to 487.02)`

-- Situation: you, or a business you control, have been asked or ordered to keep or hand over data or documents. Ask 'Have you received a demand or an order to preserve or produce data?' before showing the group.

-- Under section 487.012(2), may a peace officer or public officer make a preservation demand to me.
@ref s 487.012(2)
@export Under section 487.012(2), may a peace officer or public officer make a preservation demand to me, only if they have reasonable grounds to suspect an offence and that the computer data is in my possession or control and will assist?
GIVEN `the officer has grounds to suspect a domestic offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament?
      `the officer has grounds to suspect an offence under a foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state?
      `a foreign authority is investigating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an investigation being conducted by a person or authority responsible in that foreign state for investigating such offences?
      `the officer has grounds to suspect the data is in my possession or control and will assist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the officer have reasonable grounds to suspect that the computer data is in your possession or control and will assist in the investigation of the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.012(2), may a peace officer or public officer make a preservation demand to me` MEANS
    `s 487.012(2) the peace officer or public officer may make the demand` `the officer has grounds to suspect a domestic offence` `the officer has grounds to suspect an offence under a foreign law` `a foreign authority is investigating` `the officer has grounds to suspect the data is in my possession or control and will assist`

-- Under section 487.012(3), is a preservation demand barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence.
@ref s 487.012(3)
@export Under section 487.012(3), is a preservation demand barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence?
GIVEN `I am under investigation for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under investigation for the offence the demand is about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.012(3), is a preservation demand barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    `s 487.012(3) the demand is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` `I am under investigation for the offence`

-- Under section 487.012(4), is the preservation demand made to me still in effect on a given day.
@ref s 487.012(4)
@export Under section 487.012(4), is the preservation demand made to me still in effect on a given day, given that it expires 21 days after it is made (90 days for an offence under a foreign law) unless revoked earlier?
GIVEN `the day the demand was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the demand made?
      `the kind of offence` IS A STRING @desc What kind of offence is it about? One of: "an offence under this or any other Act of Parliament", "an offence under a law of a foreign state".
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which date do you want to know?
      `the demand was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand revoked by notice before that date?
      `the day it was revoked` IS A DATE @desc If it was revoked, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.012(4), is the preservation demand made to me still in effect on a given day` MEANS
    `s 487.012(4) the demand is in effect on the day` `the day the demand was made` (`s 487.012(4) seat: the kind of offence` `the kind of offence`) `the day in question` (IF `the demand was revoked` THEN JUST `the day it was revoked` ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no such day exists, so none is passed on

-- Under section 487.012(6), is another demand to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation barred.
@ref s 487.012(6)
@export Under section 487.012(6), is another preservation demand to me for the same computer data, in connection with the same investigation, barred?
GIVEN `a demand has already been made to me to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a demand already been made to you to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.012(6), is another demand to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation barred` MEANS
    `s 487.012(6) another demand to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation is barred` `a demand has already been made to me to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation`

-- Under section 487.013(5), is a preservation order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence.
@ref s 487.013(5)
@export Under section 487.013(5), is a preservation order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence?
GIVEN `I am under investigation for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under investigation for the offence the order is about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.013(5), is a preservation order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    `s 487.013(5) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` `I am under investigation for the offence`

-- Under section 487.0131(1), must I keep the account open or active that the order names.
@ref s 487.0131(1)
@export Under section 487.0131(1), must I keep open or active the account that a keep-account-open order names, unless the account holder asks me to close or deactivate it?
GIVEN `an order was made to keep the account open or active` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under section 487.0131 requiring you to keep the account open or active?
      `the holder of the account has asked me to close or deactivate it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the holder of the account requested that you close or deactivate it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.0131(1), must I keep the account open or active that the order names` MEANS
    `s 487.0131(1) the person must keep the account open or active` `an order was made to keep the account open or active` `the holder of the account has asked me to close or deactivate it`

-- Under section 487.0131(5), is a keep-account-open order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence.
@ref s 487.0131(5)
@export Under section 487.0131(5), is a keep-account-open order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence?
GIVEN `I am under investigation for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection 487.0131(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.0131(5), is a keep-account-open order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    `s 487.0131(5) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` `I am under investigation for the offence`

-- Under section 487.014(1), may a justice or judge order me to produce a document or to prepare and produce a document.
@ref s 487.014(1)
@export Under section 487.014(1), may a justice or judge order me to produce a copy of a document, or to prepare and produce a document containing data, that is in my possession or control?
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer?
      `the document or data is in my possession or control when I receive the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document or data in your possession or control when you receive the order?
      `it is an order for which sections 487.015 to 487.018 provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an order of a kind that section 487.015, 487.016, 487.017 or 487.018 provides for (tracing a communication, transmission data, tracking data, financial data)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.014(1), may a justice or judge order me to produce a document or to prepare and produce a document` MEANS
    `s 487.014(1) the justice or judge may order the person to produce a document or to prepare and produce a document` `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` `the document or data is in my possession or control when I receive the order` `it is an order for which sections 487.015 to 487.018 provide`

-- Under section 487.014(4), is a general production order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence.
@ref s 487.014(4)
@export Under section 487.014(4), is a general production order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence?
GIVEN `I am under investigation for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection 487.014(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 487.014(4), is a general production order barred against me because I am under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    `s 487.014(4) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` `I am under investigation for the offence`

-- Under section 487.0141(6)(a), may I be required to produce documents again less than 72 hours after the last time.
