    `s 537(1)(j) the justice may allow the accused to appear by counsel for a part of the inquiry` `the justice is acting under Part XVIII` `the prosecutor and I consent` `the part of the inquiry is one in which the evidence of a witness is taken`

-- section 537(1)(j.1)
@export Under section 537(1)(j.1), may the justice permit me to be out of court during the whole or any part of the inquiry?
GIVEN `the justice is acting under Part XVIII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice acting at your preliminary inquiry?
      `I have requested to be out of court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you requested to be out of court during the whole or part of the inquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 537(1)(j.1), may the justice permit me to be out of court during the whole or any part of the inquiry` IS
    `s 537(1)(j.1) the justice may permit the accused to be out of court during the whole or any part of the inquiry` `the justice is acting under Part XVIII` `I have requested to be out of court`

-- section 537(1.02)
@export Under section 537(1.02), must the Court inform me that the evidence taken during my absence could still be admissible under section 715 or 715.01?
GIVEN `the justice grants my request to be out of court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the justice granted your request to be out of court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 537(1.02), must the Court inform me that the evidence taken during my absence could still be admissible under section 715 or 715.01` IS
    `s 537(1.02) the Court must inform the accused that the evidence taken during their absence could still be admissible under section 715 or 715.01` `the justice grants my request to be out of court`

-- section 539(1)(b)
@export Under section 539(1)(b), must the justice make an order restricting publication of the evidence taken at my preliminary inquiry if I apply for it?
GIVEN `the application is made by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for an order restricting publication made by you (or any of the accused)?
      `the application is made before the taking of evidence at the preliminary inquiry begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made before the taking of evidence at the preliminary inquiry begins?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 539(1)(b), must the justice make an order restricting publication of the evidence taken at my preliminary inquiry if I apply for it` IS
    `s 539(1)(b) the justice shall make an order restricting publication of the evidence` `the application is made by me` `the application is made before the taking of evidence at the preliminary inquiry begins`

-- section 539(2)
@export Under section 539(2), must the justice inform me of my right to apply for an order restricting publication?
GIVEN `I am represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry?
      `the taking of evidence at the inquiry has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the taking of evidence at the inquiry commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 539(2), must the justice inform me of my right to apply for an order restricting publication` IS
    `s 539(2) the justice shall inform the accused of the right to apply for an order restricting publication` `I am represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` `the taking of evidence at the inquiry has commenced`

-- section 540(1)(a)
@export Under section 540(1)(a), must the justice take the evidence of the prosecution witnesses under oath and allow me or my counsel to cross-examine them?
GIVEN `I am before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you before a justice who is holding a preliminary inquiry into the charge?
      `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the justice limited the witnesses to be heard (under subsection 537(1.01))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 540(1)(a), must the justice take the evidence of the prosecution witnesses under oath and allow me or my counsel to cross-examine them` IS
    `s 540(1)(a) the justice shall take the evidence of the prosecution witnesses under oath and allow the accused or counsel to cross-examine them` `I am before a justice holding a preliminary inquiry` `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard`

-- section 541(1)
@export Under section 541(1), must the justice hear the witnesses I call?
GIVEN `the evidence of the prosecution witnesses has been taken down and, if required, read` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the evidence of the prosecution witnesses been taken down and, if the Part requires it, read?
      `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the justice limited the witnesses to be heard (under subsection 537(1.01))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 541(1), must the justice hear the witnesses I call` IS
    `s 541(1) the justice shall hear the witnesses called by the accused` `the evidence of the prosecution witnesses has been taken down and, if required, read` `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard`

-- section 541(2)
@export Under section 541(2), must the justice address me in the words of subsection (2) when I am not represented by counsel?
GIVEN `I am represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry?
      `the justice has begun to hear a witness called by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the justice begun to hear a witness called by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 541(2), must the justice address me in the words of subsection (2) when I am not represented by counsel` IS
    `s 541(2) the justice shall address the accused in the words of subsection (2)` `I am represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` `the justice has begun to hear a witness called by me`

-- section 541(4)
@export Under section 541(4), must the justice ask me whether I wish to call any witnesses when I am not represented by counsel?
GIVEN `I am represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry?
      `subsections 541(2) and (3) have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the justice already addressed you under subsection 541(2) and taken down your answer under subsection 541(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 541(4), must the justice ask me whether I wish to call any witnesses when I am not represented by counsel` IS
    `s 541(4) the justice shall ask the accused if the accused wishes to call any witnesses` `I am represented by counsel at the preliminary inquiry` `subsections 541(2) and (3) have been complied with`


-- Situation: Section 544 applies only if you abscond during a preliminary inquiry.


§§ `Sections 544 to 549 -- If you abscond, and how the inquiry ends`

-- section 544(1)(a)
@export Under section 544(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived the right to be present at the inquiry because I absconded?
GIVEN `I abscond during the course of a preliminary inquiry into an offence with which I am charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abscond during the course of a preliminary inquiry into an offence with which you are charged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 544(1)(a), am I deemed to have waived the right to be present at the inquiry because I absconded` IS
    `s 544(1)(a) the accused is deemed to have waived the right to be present at the inquiry` `I abscond during the course of a preliminary inquiry into an offence with which I am charged`

-- section 544(2)
@export Under section 544(2), may the justice draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded?
GIVEN `the justice continues the preliminary inquiry under subsection 544(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the justice continued the preliminary inquiry in your absence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 544(2), may the justice draw an inference adverse to me from the fact that I absconded` IS
    `s 544(2) the justice may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that the accused has absconded` `the justice continues the preliminary inquiry under subsection 544(1)`

-- section 544(3)
@export Under section 544(3), am I not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in my absence re-opened when I reappear at a preliminary inquiry that is continuing?
GIVEN `I reappear at a preliminary inquiry that is continuing under subsection 544(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reappeared at a preliminary inquiry that the justice is continuing because you absconded?
      `the justice is satisfied that because of exceptional circumstances it is in the interests of justice to re-open the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice satisfied that, because of exceptional circumstances, it is in the interests of justice to re-open the inquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 544(3), am I not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in my absence re-opened when I reappear at a preliminary inquiry that is continuing` IS
    `s 544(3) the accused is not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in the absence of the accused re-opened` `I reappear at a preliminary inquiry that is continuing under subsection 544(1)` `the justice is satisfied that because of exceptional circumstances it is in the interests of justice to re-open the inquiry`

-- section 544(5)
@export Under section 544(5), must my counsel be given an opportunity to call witnesses on my behalf although I am absent?
GIVEN `the preliminary inquiry has been continued and the evidence of the prosecution has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the preliminary inquiry been continued in your absence and the evidence for the prosecution concluded?
      `I am absent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent?
      `my counsel is present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your counsel present?
      `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the justice limited the witnesses to be heard (under subsection 537(1.01))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 544(5), must my counsel be given an opportunity to call witnesses on my behalf although I am absent` IS
    `s 544(5) counsel for the accused shall be given an opportunity to call witnesses on behalf of the accused` `the preliminary inquiry has been continued and the evidence of the prosecution has concluded` `I am absent` `my counsel is present` `the justice has limited the witnesses to be heard`

-- section 548
@export Under section 548, what decision does the justice make at my preliminary inquiry?
GIVEN `all the evidence has been taken by the justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has all the evidence been taken by the justice?
      `in the opinion of the justice there is sufficient evidence to put me on trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the opinion of the justice, is there sufficient evidence to put you on trial for the offence charged or any other indictable offence in respect of the same transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Decision on the charge`
DECIDE `Under section 548, what decision does the justice make at my preliminary inquiry` IS
    `s 548 the decision the justice made at the preliminary inquiry` `all the evidence has been taken by the justice` `in the opinion of the justice there is sufficient evidence to put me on trial`

-- section 548(1)(a)
@export Under section 548(1)(a), must the justice order me to stand trial?
GIVEN `all the evidence has been taken by the justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has all the evidence been taken by the justice?
      `in the opinion of the justice there is sufficient evidence to put me on trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the opinion of the justice, is there sufficient evidence to put you on trial for the offence charged or any other indictable offence in respect of the same transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 548(1)(a), must the justice order me to stand trial` IS
    `s 548(1)(a) the justice shall order the accused to stand trial` (`s 548 the decision the justice made at the preliminary inquiry` `all the evidence has been taken by the justice` `in the opinion of the justice there is sufficient evidence to put me on trial`)

-- section 548(1)(b)
@export Under section 548(1)(b), must the justice discharge me?
GIVEN `all the evidence has been taken by the justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has all the evidence been taken by the justice?
      `in the opinion of the justice there is sufficient evidence to put me on trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the opinion of the justice, is there sufficient evidence to put you on trial for the offence charged or any other indictable offence in respect of the same transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 548(1)(b), must the justice discharge me` IS
    `s 548(1)(b) the justice shall discharge the accused` (`s 548 the decision the justice made at the preliminary inquiry` `all the evidence has been taken by the justice` `in the opinion of the justice there is sufficient evidence to put me on trial`)

-- section 549(1)
@export Under section 549(1), may the justice order me to stand trial without taking or recording any evidence or further evidence?
GIVEN `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to being ordered to stand trial without evidence being taken?
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 549(1), may the justice order me to stand trial without taking or recording any evidence or further evidence` IS
    `s 549(1) the justice may order the accused to stand trial without taking or recording any evidence or further evidence` `I consent` `the prosecutor consents`


-- Situation: Applies only if a case management judge may be appointed for your trial.


§ `PART XVIII.1 -- Case management judge (sections 551.1 to 551.7)`

-- section 551.1(1)
@export Under section 551.1(1), may the Chief Justice or Chief Judge appoint a judge as the case management judge for my trial?
GIVEN `a trial is to be or is being held before the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your trial to be, or being, held before the court?
      `the Chief Justice or Chief Judge is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Chief Justice or the Chief Judge (or the judge designated) of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice to appoint a case management judge?
      `the mode of my trial` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc What is the mode of your trial?
      `jury selection has begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has jury selection begun?
      `the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented been reached?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 551.1(1), may the Chief Justice or Chief Judge appoint a judge as the case management judge for my trial` IS
    `s 551.1(1) the Chief Justice or Chief Judge may appoint a judge as the case management judge for the trial` `a trial is to be or is being held before the court` `the Chief Justice or Chief Judge is of the opinion that it is necessary for the proper administration of justice` `the mode of my trial` `jury selection has begun` `the stage at which the evidence on the merits is presented has been reached`

-- section 551.5
@export Under section 551.5, must my trial proceed continuously?
GIVEN `the court has adjourned my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court adjourned your trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 551.5, must my trial proceed continuously` IS
    `s 551.5 the trial of the accused shall proceed continuously` `the court has adjourned my trial`


§ `PART XIX -- Indictable offences -- trial without jury (sections 552 to 572)`


-- Situation: Applies where you are charged with an indictable offence in an information.


§§ `Sections 553 to 555.1 -- Which judge may try you`

-- section 553
@export Under section 553, is the offence I am charged with within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge?
GIVEN `I am charged in an information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged in an information?
      `the section of the Code that creates the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code creates the offence you are charged with? (Give the section number, with any decimal part.)
      `the subsection of that section` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of that section creates it? (For example (1); leave empty if none.)
      `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` IS A `s 553(a) the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` @desc Is the offence one that paragraph 553(a) names (theft, obtaining by false pretences, possessing the proceeds of an indictable offence, defrauding, or mischief under subsection 430(4)), and if so which?
      `the theft is theft of cattle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with theft, is it theft of cattle?
      `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subject-matter of the offence a testamentary instrument?
      `the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars?
      `how I am charged` IS A `s 553(b) how the accused is charged` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, or with counselling it, conspiring or attempting to commit it, or being an accessory after the fact to it?
      `the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 553, is the offence I am charged with within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` IS
    `s 553 the offence is within the absolute jurisdiction of a provincial court judge` `my section 553 facts`
    WHERE
        `my section 553 facts` MEANS `s 553 the charge as the accused states it` `I am charged in an information` `the section of the Code that creates the offence` `the subsection of that section` `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` `the theft is theft of cattle` `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` `the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence in dollars` `how I am charged` `the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`

-- section 554(1)
@export Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me?
GIVEN `the class of the offence I am charged with` IS A `Class of offence` @desc Is the offence you are charged with an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or one that the section makes both?
      `how the prosecutor is proceeding` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the prosecutor proceeding by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the most that the offence you are charged with allows on indictment imprisonment for life?
      `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` IS A NUMBER @desc If the most is not life, what is the most the offence allows on indictment, in whole years? (Give 0 if the section states no imprisonment.)
      `I am charged in an information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged in an information?
      `the section of the Code that creates the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code creates the offence you are charged with? (Give the section number, with any decimal part.)
      `the subsection of that section` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of that section creates it? (For example (1); leave empty if none.)
      `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` IS A `s 553(a) the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` @desc Is the offence one that paragraph 553(a) names (theft, obtaining by false pretences, possessing the proceeds of an indictable offence, defrauding, or mischief under subsection 430(4)), and if so which?
      `the theft is theft of cattle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with theft, is it theft of cattle?
      `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subject-matter of the offence a testamentary instrument?
      `the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars?
      `how I am charged` IS A `s 553(b) how the accused is charged` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, or with counselling it, conspiring or attempting to commit it, or being an accessory after the fact to it?
      `the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act?
      `the offence I am charged with is one listed in section 469` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence you are charged with one listed in section 469 of the Criminal Code?
      `I elected a mode of trial when put to my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When you were put to your election, did you elect a mode of trial? (No, if you did not elect.)
      `the mode of trial I elected` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial did you elect: a provincial court judge, a judge without a jury, or a court composed of a judge and jury?
      `the criminal proceedings against me are in Nunavut` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the criminal proceedings against you in Nunavut?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 554(1), may a provincial court judge try me` IS
    `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `my charge` `the answer about section 469` `my answer when put to the election` `the criminal proceedings against me are in Nunavut`
    WHERE
        `my section 553 facts` MEANS `s 553 the charge as the accused states it` `I am charged in an information` `the section of the Code that creates the offence` `the subsection of that section` `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` `the theft is theft of cattle` `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` `the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence in dollars` `how I am charged` `the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
        `my charge` MEANS `s 535 the charge as the accused states it` `the class of the offence I am charged with` `how the prosecutor is proceeding` `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` `my section 553 facts`
        `the answer about section 469` MEANS JUST `the offence I am charged with is one listed in section 469`
        `my answer when put to the election` MEANS `s 536(2) the answer the accused gave, as the accused states it` `I elected a mode of trial when put to my election` `the mode of trial I elected`

-- section 554(2)
