@export Under section 555.1(2), must the judge put me to my election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)?
GIVEN `I am before a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice in proceedings under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you before a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice in proceedings under Part XIX?
      `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` IS A `s 553(a) the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` @desc Is the offence one that paragraph 553(a) names (theft, obtaining by false pretences, possessing the proceeds of an indictable offence, defrauding, or mischief under subsection 430(4)), and if so which?
      `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence prosecuted by indictment?
      `the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice has made an adjudication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice made an adjudication?
      `the evidence establishes that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds 5,000 dollars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the evidence establish that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds 5,000 dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 555.1(2), must the judge put me to my election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` IS
    `s 555.1(2) the judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` `I am before a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice in proceedings under Part XIX` `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` `the offence is prosecuted by indictment` `the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice has made an adjudication` `the evidence establishes that the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or that its value exceeds 5,000 dollars`


-- Situation: Applies where you are tried by a provincial court judge or a judge without a jury.


§§ `Sections 557 to 560 -- Trial by a judge without a jury`

-- section 557
@export Under section 557, must the evidence of witnesses be taken in accordance with a provision of Part XVIII?
GIVEN `I am tried by a provincial court judge or a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice in accordance with Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you tried by a provincial court judge or a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice in accordance with Part XIX?
      `the section of the Code the provision is in` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code is the provision you ask about in? (Give the section number, with any decimal part.)
      `the subsection of that section` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of that section? (For example (1); leave empty if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 557, must the evidence of witnesses be taken in accordance with a provision of Part XVIII` IS
    `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` `I am tried by a provincial court judge or a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice in accordance with Part XIX` `the provision I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the provision I ask about` MEANS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS `the section of the Code the provision is in`, `subsection` IS `the subsection of that section`

-- section 558
@export Under section 558, must I be tried by a judge without a jury?
GIVEN `the class of the offence I am charged with` IS A `Class of offence` @desc Is the offence you are charged with an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or one that the section makes both?
      `how the prosecutor is proceeding` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the prosecutor proceeding by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the most that the offence you are charged with allows on indictment imprisonment for life?
      `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` IS A NUMBER @desc If the most is not life, what is the most the offence allows on indictment, in whole years? (Give 0 if the section states no imprisonment.)
      `the offence I am charged with is one listed in section 469` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence you are charged with one listed in section 469 of the Criminal Code?
      `I elected or re-elected under section 536, 536.1, 561 or 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you elect or re-elect to be tried by a judge without a jury?
      `another provision of Part XIX displaces my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another provision of Part XIX displace your election (for example, the Attorney General requires a jury, or a court declines to record the election)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 558, must I be tried by a judge without a jury` IS
    `s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` `my charge` `the answer about section 469` `I elected or re-elected under section 536, 536.1, 561 or 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` `another provision of Part XIX displaces my election`
    WHERE
        `my charge` MEANS `s 535 the charge as the accused states it` `the class of the offence I am charged with` `how the prosecutor is proceeding` `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` `s 553 facts left blank because the rule called does not read them`
        `the answer about section 469` MEANS JUST `the offence I am charged with is one listed in section 469`

-- section 560(4)
@export Under section 560(4), is the duty of ascertaining from the clerk of the court the time and place fixed for my trial on me?
GIVEN `I am in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in custody?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 560(4), is the duty of ascertaining from the clerk of the court the time and place fixed for my trial on me` IS
    `s 560(4) the duty of ascertaining from the clerk of the court the time and place fixed for the trial is on the accused` `I am in custody`

-- section 560(4)
@export Under section 560(4), must I attend for my trial at the time and place fixed?
GIVEN `I am in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in custody?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 560(4), must I attend for my trial at the time and place fixed` IS
    `s 560(4) the accused shall attend for their trial at the time and place fixed` `I am in custody`


-- Situation: Applies only where you have elected, or are deemed to have elected, a mode of trial and wish to change it.


§§ `Sections 561 to 565 -- Changing your election`

-- section 561(1)
@export Under section 561(1), on what footing may I re-elect a mode of trial after electing, or being deemed to have elected, a mode other than trial by a provincial court judge?
GIVEN `the mode of trial I elected or am deemed to have elected` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial did you elect, or are you deemed to have elected?
      `the mode of trial I wish to re-elect` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial do you wish to re-elect?
      `I am entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence for which you are entitled to request a preliminary inquiry?
      `a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a preliminary inquiry been requested for your charge?
      `the preliminary inquiry has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the preliminary inquiry been completed?
      `the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the preliminary inquiry completed? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the date of my re-election` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you re-elect (or wish to re-elect)?
      `the day first appointed for my trial` IS A DATE @desc What is the day first appointed for your trial?
      `the prosecutor has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecutor consented in writing to the re-election?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 561 the basis on which the accused may re-elect`
DECIDE `Under section 561(1), on what footing may I re-elect a mode of trial after electing, or being deemed to have elected, a mode other than trial by a provincial court judge` IS
    `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` `my re-election facts`
    WHERE
        `my re-election facts` MEANS `s 561 the re-election facts as the accused states them` `the mode of trial I elected or am deemed to have elected` `the mode of trial I wish to re-elect` `I am entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` `a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` `the preliminary inquiry has been completed` `the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` `the date of my re-election` `the day first appointed for my trial` `the prosecutor has consented in writing`

-- section 561(2)
@export Under section 561(2), on what footing may I re-elect another mode of trial after electing to be tried by a provincial court judge?
GIVEN `the mode of trial I elected or am deemed to have elected` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial did you elect, or are you deemed to have elected?
      `the mode of trial I wish to re-elect` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial do you wish to re-elect?
      `I am entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence for which you are entitled to request a preliminary inquiry?
      `a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a preliminary inquiry been requested for your charge?
      `the preliminary inquiry has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the preliminary inquiry been completed?
      `the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the preliminary inquiry completed? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the date of my re-election` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you re-elect (or wish to re-elect)?
      `the day first appointed for my trial` IS A DATE @desc What is the day first appointed for your trial?
      `the prosecutor has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecutor consented in writing to the re-election?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 561 the basis on which the accused may re-elect`
DECIDE `Under section 561(2), on what footing may I re-elect another mode of trial after electing to be tried by a provincial court judge` IS
    `s 561(2) the basis on which the accused who elected a provincial court judge may re-elect` `my re-election facts`
    WHERE
        `my re-election facts` MEANS `s 561 the re-election facts as the accused states them` `the mode of trial I elected or am deemed to have elected` `the mode of trial I wish to re-elect` `I am entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` `a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` `the preliminary inquiry has been completed` `the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` `the date of my re-election` `the day first appointed for my trial` `the prosecutor has consented in writing`

-- section 561.1
@export Under section 561.1, on what footing may I re-elect a mode of trial?
GIVEN `the mode of trial I elected or am deemed to have elected` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial did you elect, or are you deemed to have elected?
      `the mode of trial I wish to re-elect` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial do you wish to re-elect?
      `I am entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with an offence for which you are entitled to request a preliminary inquiry?
      `a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a preliminary inquiry been requested for your charge?
      `the preliminary inquiry has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the preliminary inquiry been completed?
      `the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the preliminary inquiry completed? (Any date if it has not been.)
      `the date of my re-election` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you re-elect (or wish to re-elect)?
      `the day first appointed for my trial` IS A DATE @desc What is the day first appointed for your trial?
      `the prosecutor has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecutor consented in writing to the re-election?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 561 the basis on which the accused may re-elect`
DECIDE `Under section 561.1, on what footing may I re-elect a mode of trial` IS
    `s 561.1 the basis on which the accused may re-elect` `my re-election facts`
    WHERE
        `my re-election facts` MEANS `s 561 the re-election facts as the accused states them` `the mode of trial I elected or am deemed to have elected` `the mode of trial I wish to re-elect` `I am entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` `a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` `the preliminary inquiry has been completed` `the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` `the date of my re-election` `the day first appointed for my trial` `the prosecutor has consented in writing`

-- section 561(3)
@export Under section 561(3), must I give notice in writing of my intention to re-elect to the justice presiding at the preliminary inquiry?
GIVEN `I intend to re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(a) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to re-elect, before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, in a case where a preliminary inquiry has been requested?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561(3), must I give notice in writing of my intention to re-elect to the justice presiding at the preliminary inquiry` IS
    `s 561(3) the accused shall give notice in writing of their intention to re-elect to the justice presiding at the preliminary inquiry` `I intend to re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(a) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry`

-- section 561(4)
@export Under section 561(4), must I give notice in writing to the provincial court judge before whom I appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the court?
GIVEN `I intend to re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(b) or subsection 561(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to re-elect in a case where no preliminary inquiry was requested (or you are not entitled to one), or after electing trial by a provincial court judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561(4), must I give notice in writing to the provincial court judge before whom I appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the court` IS
    `s 561(4) the accused shall give notice in writing to the provincial court judge before whom the accused appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the court` `I intend to re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(b) or subsection 561(2)`

-- section 561(5)
@export Under section 561(5), must I give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court of my original election?
GIVEN `I intend to re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to re-elect, after the completion of the preliminary inquiry, with the prosecutor's consent where it is required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561(5), must I give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court of my original election` IS
    `s 561(5) the accused shall give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court of the accused's original election` `I intend to re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry`

-- section 561(7)
@export Under section 561(7), must I attend at the time and place appointed for my re-election?
GIVEN `a time and place has been appointed under subsection 561(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a provincial court judge or judge appointed a time and place for you to re-elect, under subsection 561(6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561(7), must I attend at the time and place appointed for my re-election` IS
    `s 561(7) the accused shall attend at the time and place appointed` `a time and place has been appointed under subsection 561(6)`

-- section 561.1(4)
@export Under section 561.1(4), must I give notice in writing of my wish to re-elect to the justice of the peace or judge presiding at the preliminary inquiry?
GIVEN `I wish to re-elect under subsection 561.1(1) or (3), before the completion of the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Nunavut, do you wish to re-elect before the completion of the preliminary inquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561.1(4), must I give notice in writing of my wish to re-elect to the justice of the peace or judge presiding at the preliminary inquiry` IS
    `s 561.1(4) the accused shall give notice in writing of the wish to re-elect to the justice of the peace or judge presiding at the preliminary inquiry` `I wish to re-elect under subsection 561.1(1) or (3), before the completion of the preliminary inquiry`

-- section 561.1(6)
@export Under section 561.1(6), must I give notice in writing of my intention to re-elect to the judge before whom I appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the Nunavut Court of Justice?
GIVEN `I have not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), have had one or was not entitled to make such a request, and I intend to re-elect under section 561.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In Nunavut, do you intend to re-elect where you have not requested a preliminary inquiry, have had one or were not entitled to request one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561.1(6), must I give notice in writing of my intention to re-elect to the judge before whom I appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the Nunavut Court of Justice` IS
    `s 561.1(6) the accused shall give notice in writing of the intention to re-elect to the judge before whom the accused appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the Nunavut Court of Justice` `I have not requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3), have had one or was not entitled to make such a request, and I intend to re-elect under section 561.1`

-- section 561.1(9)
@export Under section 561.1(9), must I attend at the time and place appointed for my re-election?
GIVEN `a time and place has been appointed under subsection 561.1(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judge appointed a time and place for you to re-elect, under subsection 561.1(8)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 561.1(9), must I attend at the time and place appointed for my re-election` IS
    `s 561.1(9) the accused shall attend at the time and place appointed` `a time and place has been appointed under subsection 561.1(8)`

-- section 562(1)
@export Under section 562(1), must the provincial court judge or judge proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial after my re-election?
GIVEN `I re-elect under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(i) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect, before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, with the prosecutor's consent, to be tried by a provincial court judge?
      `I re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect after the completion of the preliminary inquiry?
      `I re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect in a case where you did not request a preliminary inquiry or are not entitled to one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 562(1), must the provincial court judge or judge proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial after my re-election` IS
    `s 562(1) the provincial court judge or judge shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial` `I re-elect under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(i) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry` `I re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(a) after the completion of the preliminary inquiry` `I re-elect under paragraph 561(1)(b)`

-- section 562(2)
@export Under section 562(2), must the justice proceed with the preliminary inquiry after my re-election?
GIVEN `I re-elect under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(ii) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or under subsection 561(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect, as of right, before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or after electing trial by a provincial court judge?
      `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you request a preliminary inquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 562(2), must the justice proceed with the preliminary inquiry after my re-election` IS
    `s 562(2) the justice shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry` `I re-elect under subparagraph 561(1)(a)(ii) before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, or under subsection 561(2)` `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536(4)`

-- section 562.1(1)
@export Under section 562.1(1), must the judge proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial after my re-election?
GIVEN `I re-elect under subsection 561.1(1) to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect, under subsection 561.1(1), to be tried by a judge without a jury?
      `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)?
      `I re-elect any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2)?
      `I am able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 562.1(1), must the judge proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial after my re-election` IS
    `s 562.1(1) the judge shall proceed with the trial or appoint a time and place for the trial` `I re-elect under subsection 561.1(1) to be tried by a judge without a jury` `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` `I re-elect any other mode of trial under subsection 561.1(2)` `I am able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)`

-- section 562.1(2)
@export Under section 562.1(2), must the justice of the peace or judge proceed with the preliminary inquiry after my re-election?
GIVEN `I re-elect under section 561.1 before the completion of the preliminary inquiry to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect under section 561.1, before the completion of the preliminary inquiry, to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury?
      `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 562.1(2), must the justice of the peace or judge proceed with the preliminary inquiry after my re-election` IS
    `s 562.1(2) the justice of the peace or judge shall proceed with the preliminary inquiry` `I re-elect under section 561.1 before the completion of the preliminary inquiry to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury` `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)`

-- section 563(a)
@export Under section 563(a), must I be tried on the information that was before the justice at the preliminary inquiry?
GIVEN `I re-elect under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge?
      `a preliminary inquiry was held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a preliminary inquiry held?
      `the provincial court judge by whom I am tried has allowed an amendment to the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the provincial court judge by whom you are tried allowed an amendment to the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 563(a), must I be tried on the information that was before the justice at the preliminary inquiry` IS
    `s 563(a) the accused shall be tried on the information that was before the justice at the preliminary inquiry` `I re-elect under section 561 to be tried by a provincial court judge` `a preliminary inquiry was held` `the provincial court judge by whom I am tried has allowed an amendment to the information`

-- section 563.1(1)(a)
@export Under section 563.1(1)(a), must I be tried on the information that was before the justice of the peace or judge at the preliminary inquiry?
GIVEN `I re-elect under section 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you re-elect under section 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury?
      `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)?
      `I am able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)?
      `a preliminary inquiry was held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a preliminary inquiry held?
      `the judge by whom I am tried has allowed an amendment to the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge by whom you are tried allowed an amendment to the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 563.1(1)(a), must I be tried on the information that was before the justice of the peace or judge at the preliminary inquiry` IS
    `s 563.1(1)(a) the accused shall be tried on the information that was before the justice of the peace or judge at the preliminary inquiry` `I re-elect under section 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` `I request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` `I am able to make a request for a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` `a preliminary inquiry was held` `the judge by whom I am tried has allowed an amendment to the information`

-- section 565(1)
@export Under section 565(1), am I deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury?
GIVEN `I am ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under Part XIX, may be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under Part XIX, may be tried by a judge without a jury?
      `the justice, provincial court judge or judge declined to record my election or re-election under section 567 or subsection 567.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the justice, provincial court judge or judge decline to record your election or re-election because of a joint charge (section 567 or 567.1)?
      `I was put to an election under section 536 or 536.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you put to an election under section 536 or 536.1?
      `I elected a mode of trial when put to my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When you were put to your election, did you elect a mode of trial? (No, if you did not elect.)
      `the mode of trial I elected` IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial` @desc Which mode of trial did you elect: a provincial court judge, a judge without a jury, or a court composed of a judge and jury?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 565(1), am I deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS
    `s 565(1) the accused is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `I am ordered to stand trial for an offence that, under Part XIX, may be tried by a judge without a jury` `the justice, provincial court judge or judge declined to record my election or re-election under section 567 or subsection 567.1(1)` `I was put to an election under section 536 or 536.1` `my answer when put to the election`
    WHERE
        `my answer when put to the election` MEANS `s 536(2) the answer the accused gave, as the accused states it` `I elected a mode of trial when put to my election` `the mode of trial I elected`

-- section 565(2)
@export Under section 565(2), am I deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury because an indictment was preferred against me under section 577?
GIVEN `an indictment has been preferred against me on the basis of a consent or order given under section 577` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an indictment been preferred against you on the basis of a consent or order given under section 577?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 565(2), am I deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury because an indictment was preferred against me under section 577` IS
    `s 565(2) the accused is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `the answer about section 577`
    WHERE
        `the answer about section 577` MEANS JUST `an indictment has been preferred against me on the basis of a consent or order given under section 577`

-- section 565(2)
@export Under section 565(2), may I re-elect to be tried by a judge without a jury without a preliminary inquiry after an indictment was preferred against me under section 577?
GIVEN `an indictment has been preferred against me on the basis of a consent or order given under section 577` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an indictment been preferred against you on the basis of a consent or order given under section 577?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 565(2), may I re-elect to be tried by a judge without a jury without a preliminary inquiry after an indictment was preferred against me under section 577` IS
    `s 565(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a judge without a jury without a preliminary inquiry` `the answer about section 577`
    WHERE
        `the answer about section 577` MEANS JUST `an indictment has been preferred against me on the basis of a consent or order given under section 577`

-- section 565(3)
@export Under section 565(3), must I give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court where the indictment has been filed or preferred?
GIVEN `I intend to re-elect under subsection 565(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to re-elect after an indictment was preferred against you under section 577?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 565(3), must I give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court where the indictment has been filed or preferred` IS
    `s 565(3) the accused shall give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court where the indictment has been filed or preferred` `I intend to re-elect under subsection 565(2)`


-- Situation: Applies where you are tried on an indictment, are jointly charged, or the Attorney General may require a jury.


§§ `Sections 566 to 569 -- The indictment, joint charges and the Attorney General`

-- section 566(1)
@export Under section 566(1), must my trial be on an indictment in writing setting forth the offence with which I am charged?
GIVEN `the class of the offence I am charged with` IS A `Class of offence` @desc Is the offence you are charged with an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or one that the section makes both?
      `how the prosecutor is proceeding` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the prosecutor proceeding by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the most that the offence you are charged with allows on indictment imprisonment for life?
      `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` IS A NUMBER @desc If the most is not life, what is the most the offence allows on indictment, in whole years? (Give 0 if the section states no imprisonment.)
      `my trial is before a provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your trial before a provincial court judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 566(1), must my trial be on an indictment in writing setting forth the offence with which I am charged` IS
    `s 566(1) the trial shall be on an indictment in writing setting forth the offence with which the accused is charged` `my charge` `my trial is before a provincial court judge`
    WHERE
        `my charge` MEANS `s 535 the charge as the accused states it` `the class of the offence I am charged with` `how the prosecutor is proceeding` `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` `s 553 facts left blank because the rule called does not read them`

-- section 566(2)
@export Under section 566(2), may an indictment in Form 4 be preferred against me?
GIVEN `I elect under section 536 or re-elect under section 561 to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect, or re-elect, to be tried by a judge without a jury?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 566(2), may an indictment in Form 4 be preferred against me` IS
    `s 566(2) an indictment in Form 4 may be preferred` `I elect under section 536 or re-elect under section 561 to be tried by a judge without a jury`

-- section 566.1(1)
@export Under section 566.1(1), must my trial be on an indictment in writing setting out the offence with which I am charged?
GIVEN `the class of the offence I am charged with` IS A `Class of offence` @desc Is the offence you are charged with an indictable offence, an offence punishable on summary conviction, or one that the section makes both?
      `how the prosecutor is proceeding` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the prosecutor proceeding by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the most that the offence you are charged with allows on indictment imprisonment for life?
      `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` IS A NUMBER @desc If the most is not life, what is the most the offence allows on indictment, in whole years? (Give 0 if the section states no imprisonment.)
      `I am charged in an information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged in an information?
      `the section of the Code that creates the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code creates the offence you are charged with? (Give the section number, with any decimal part.)
      `the subsection of that section` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of that section creates it? (For example (1); leave empty if none.)
      `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` IS A `s 553(a) the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` @desc Is the offence one that paragraph 553(a) names (theft, obtaining by false pretences, possessing the proceeds of an indictable offence, defrauding, or mischief under subsection 430(4)), and if so which?
      `the theft is theft of cattle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are charged with theft, is it theft of cattle?
      `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subject-matter of the offence a testamentary instrument?
      `the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars?
      `how I am charged` IS A `s 553(b) how the accused is charged` @desc Are you charged with the offence itself, or with counselling it, conspiring or attempting to commit it, or being an accessory after the fact to it?
      `the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act?
      `I have elected or re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you elected or re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury?
      `no party has requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no party has requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)?
      `I was not entitled to make such a request under that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not entitled to make such a request under subsection 536.1(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 566.1(1), must my trial be on an indictment in writing setting out the offence with which I am charged` IS
    `s 566.1(1) the trial must be on an indictment in writing setting out the offence with which the accused is charged` `my charge` `I have elected or re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury` `no party has requested a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` `I was not entitled to make such a request under that subsection`
    WHERE
        `my section 553 facts` MEANS `s 553 the charge as the accused states it` `I am charged in an information` `the section of the Code that creates the offence` `the subsection of that section` `the offence as paragraph 553(a) names it` `the theft is theft of cattle` `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` `the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence in dollars` `how I am charged` `the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`
        `my charge` MEANS `s 535 the charge as the accused states it` `the class of the offence I am charged with` `how the prosecutor is proceeding` `the most the offence allows on indictment is imprisonment for life` `the most years of imprisonment the offence allows on indictment` `my section 553 facts`

-- section 566.1(2)
@export Under section 566.1(2), may an indictment in Form 4 be preferred against me?
GIVEN `I elect under section 536.1 or re-elect under section 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect under section 536.1, or re-elect under section 561.1, to be tried by a judge without a jury?
      `one of the parties requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the parties request a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 566.1(2), may an indictment in Form 4 be preferred against me` IS
    `s 566.1(2) an indictment in Form 4 may be preferred` `I elect under section 536.1 or re-elect under section 561.1 to be tried by a judge without a jury` `one of the parties requests a preliminary inquiry under subsection 536.1(3)`

-- section 567
@export Under section 567, may the justice, provincial court judge or judge decline to record my election, re-election or deemed election?
GIVEN `two or more persons are jointly charged with me in an information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are two or more persons jointly charged in an information with you?
      `all of us elect or re-elect or are deemed to have elected the same mode of trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all of you who are jointly charged elect, re-elect or are deemed to have elected the same mode of trial?
      `the election, re-election or deemed election is for trial by a provincial court judge or a judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the election, re-election or deemed election one for trial by a provincial court judge or a judge without a jury?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 567, may the justice, provincial court judge or judge decline to record my election, re-election or deemed election` IS
    `s 567 the justice, provincial court judge or judge may decline to record the election, re-election or deemed election` `two or more persons are jointly charged with me in an information` `all of us elect or re-elect or are deemed to have elected the same mode of trial` `the election, re-election or deemed election is for trial by a provincial court judge or a judge without a jury`

