-- Situation: Section 570 applies only once you are tried under this Part and found guilty or not guilty.


§§ `Sections 570 to 572 -- Your conviction or acquittal, adjournments and other Parts`

-- section 570(1)
@export Under section 570(1), must the judge or provincial court judge sentence me or otherwise deal with me in the manner authorized by law once I am determined to be guilty?
GIVEN `I am tried under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you tried under Part XIX?
      `the judge or provincial court judge determines me to be guilty of an offence on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge or provincial court judge determine you to be guilty of an offence, on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 570(1), must the judge or provincial court judge sentence me or otherwise deal with me in the manner authorized by law once I am determined to be guilty` IS
    `s 570(1) the judge or provincial court judge shall sentence the accused or otherwise deal with the accused in the manner authorized by law` `I am tried under Part XIX` `the judge or provincial court judge determines me to be guilty of an offence on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt`

-- section 570(1)
@export Under section 570(1), must a conviction in Form 35 and a certified copy of it, or an order in Form 36 and a certified copy of it, be drawn up on request?
GIVEN `I am tried under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you tried under Part XIX?
      `the judge or provincial court judge determines me to be guilty of an offence on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judge or provincial court judge determine you to be guilty of an offence, on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt?
      `a request has been made by me, the prosecutor, a peace officer or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request been made, by you, the prosecutor, a peace officer or any other person, for a conviction or order and a certified copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 570(1), must a conviction in Form 35 and a certified copy of it, or an order in Form 36 and a certified copy of it, be drawn up on request` IS
    `s 570(1) a conviction in Form 35 and a certified copy of it, or an order in Form 36 and a certified copy of it, shall be drawn up` `I am tried under Part XIX` `the judge or provincial court judge determines me to be guilty of an offence on acceptance of a plea of guilty or on a finding of guilt` `a request has been made by me, the prosecutor, a peace officer or any other person`

-- section 570(2)
@export Under section 570(2), must the judge or provincial court judge immediately acquit me when I am found not guilty?
GIVEN `I am tried under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you tried under Part XIX?
      `I am found not guilty of an offence with which I am charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you found not guilty of an offence with which you are charged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 570(2), must the judge or provincial court judge immediately acquit me when I am found not guilty` IS
    `s 570(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall immediately acquit the accused in respect of that offence` `I am tried under Part XIX` `I am found not guilty of an offence with which I am charged`

-- section 570(2)
@export Under section 570(2), must a certified copy of the order of acquittal be drawn up and delivered to me on request?
GIVEN `I am tried under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you tried under Part XIX?
      `I am found not guilty of an offence with which I am charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you found not guilty of an offence with which you are charged?
      `a request has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request for a certified copy of the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 570(2), must a certified copy of the order of acquittal be drawn up and delivered to me on request` IS
    `s 570(2) a certified copy of the order shall be drawn up and delivered to the accused` `I am tried under Part XIX` `I am found not guilty of an offence with which I am charged` `a request has been made`

-- section 570(4)
@export Under section 570(4), is a copy of a conviction or order sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal?
GIVEN `the copy is a copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37?
      `the copy is certified by the judge, the clerk or other proper officer of the court or the provincial court judge, or is proved to be a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy certified by the judge, by the clerk or other proper officer of the court, or by the provincial court judge, or proved to be a true copy?
      `the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 570(4), is a copy of a conviction or order sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` IS
    `s 570(4) the copy is sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` `the copy is a copy of a conviction in Form 35 or of an order in Form 36 or 37` `the copy is certified by the judge, the clerk or other proper officer of the court or the provincial court judge, or is proved to be a true copy` `the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates is proved`

-- section 570(5)
@export Under section 570(5), must the judge or provincial court judge issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 when I am convicted?
GIVEN `the accused is an organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused an organization (not an individual)?
      `the accused is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused convicted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 570(5), must the judge or provincial court judge issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 when I am convicted` IS
    `s 570(5) the judge or provincial court judge shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21` (JUST `the accused is an organization`) `the accused is convicted`

-- section 571(1)
@export Under section 571(1), may a judge or provincial court judge acting under Part XIX adjourn my trial from time to time?
GIVEN `the judge or provincial court judge is acting under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or provincial court judge acting under Part XIX in your case?
      `the trial is finally terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trial finally terminated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 571(1), may a judge or provincial court judge acting under Part XIX adjourn my trial from time to time` IS
    `s 571(1) a judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part may adjourn a trial from time to time` `the judge or provincial court judge is acting under Part XIX` `the trial is finally terminated`

-- section 571(2)
@export Under section 571(2), must the judge or provincial court judge consider the interests of justice in deciding whether to adjourn my trial?
GIVEN `the judge or provincial court judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge or provincial court judge deciding whether to adjourn the trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 571(2), must the judge or provincial court judge consider the interests of justice in deciding whether to adjourn my trial` IS
    `s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of justice` `the judge or provincial court judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial`

-- section 572
@export Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, a provision of Part XVIII about the transmission of the record by a provincial court judge who holds a preliminary inquiry, or a provision of Part XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me?
GIVEN `the section of the Code the provision is in` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Criminal Code is the provision you ask about in? (Give the section number, with any decimal part.)
      `the subsection of that section` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection of that section? (For example (1); leave empty if none.)
      `the proceedings are proceedings under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings against you proceedings under Part XIX?
      `the provision is inconsistent with Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision inconsistent with Part XIX?
      `the provision of Part XVIII relates to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where the judge holds a preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the provision is in Part XVIII, does it relate to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where the judge holds a preliminary inquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 572, does a provision of Part XVI, a provision of Part XVIII about the transmission of the record by a provincial court judge who holds a preliminary inquiry, or a provision of Part XX or XXIII apply to the proceedings against me` IS
    `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` `the provision I ask about` `the proceedings are proceedings under Part XIX` `the provision is inconsistent with Part XIX` `the provision of Part XVIII relates to transmission of the record by a provincial court judge where the judge holds a preliminary inquiry`
    WHERE
        `the provision I ask about` MEANS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS `the section of the Code the provision is in`, `subsection` IS `the subsection of that section`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc22 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc22-seat.l4 -- the seat layer for sections 573 to 672 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XIX.1, the Nunavut Court of Justice; Part XX, procedure in jury trials and general provisions). Part agent ccc22. Layer 2.
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking about the procedure of their own trial.
-- Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model (the maintainer, 2026-11-09, per the brief); this is a plain seat layer with no charge-generator contract.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs, one for each fact the accused can state: yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from the list of the layer-1 module that owns the rule. Each @desc is worded as the accused would be asked.
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes the answer of another rule as a MAYBE value (sections 579(1) and 579(2), 657.3(3)(c)), the question asks the plain facts and builds the value inside its own body, then calls the SAME layer-1 rule; no rule is restated here.
-- The questions that a judge, the Attorney General or the clerk would ask are not here; a provision that addresses only an official is encoded in layer 1 for what it decides (NOTES.md, Coverage).
--
-- HOW A RESULT READS. JUST TRUE: the text's own words give the answer the question asks (the grant, the bar, the duty or the rule applies). JUST FALSE: the text says no to those facts in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not decide these facts; a caller must never read NOTHING as no.
-- Where the question is titled as the bar ("does the section bar ...") JUST TRUE means the bar applies; where it is titled as the permission ("may ...") JUST TRUE means it is permitted. The direction of every title is the direction of its body.
--
-- The accused's questions are grouped under § headings in the text's order. A group that only arises in a situation the person may not be in says so in its heading comment, so a form can ask "Has this happened to you?" before it shows the group.

§ `Criminal Code (Canada) -- the accused's questions about the trial (sections 573 to 672)`

§§ `Part XIX.1 -- the Nunavut Court of Justice (ss 573 to 573.2)`
-- Only if the case is before the Nunavut Court of Justice or a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut: ask "Is your case in Nunavut?" before showing this group.

@export Under section 573.1(2), does the section bar review of the decision or order?
GIVEN `the decision or order is of a kind that could only be made in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision or order one that, in a province or a territory other than Nunavut, only a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 could make?
      `another statutory right of review is available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another statutory right of review available to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 573.1(2), does the section bar review of the decision or order` MEANS
    `s 573.1(2) the section bars review of the decision or order` `the decision or order is of a kind that could only be made in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` `another statutory right of review is available`

@export Under section 573.2(1), may habeas corpus proceedings be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut?
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings about an order made or a warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice?
      `the order or warrant is of a kind that could only be made or issued in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order or warrant one that, in a province or a territory other than Nunavut, only a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552 could make or issue?
      `another statutory right of review or appeal is available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another statutory right of review or appeal available to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 573.2(1), may habeas corpus proceedings be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` MEANS
    `s 573.2(1) habeas corpus proceedings may be brought before a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut` `the proceedings are in respect of an order made or warrant issued by a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` `the order or warrant is of a kind that could only be made or issued in a province or a territory other than Nunavut by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge as defined in section 552` `another statutory right of review or appeal is available`


§§ `Indictments, process and stays (ss 574 to 580)`

@export Under section 574(3), does the section bar preferring the indictment without the written order of a judge?
GIVEN `the prosecution is conducted by a prosecutor other than the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prosecution conducted by a prosecutor other than the Attorney General?
      `the Attorney General intervenes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General intervene in the prosecution?
      `a judge of that court has given a written order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judge of that court given a written order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 574(3), does the section bar preferring the indictment without the written order of a judge` MEANS
    `s 574(3) the section bars preferring the indictment without the written order of a judge` `the prosecution is conducted by a prosecutor other than the Attorney General` `the Attorney General intervenes` `a judge of that court has given a written order`

@export Under section 576(3), does the section bar trying a person on a coroner’s inquisition?
GIVEN `the person is to be tried on a coroner’s inquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to be tried on a coroner’s inquisition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 576(3), does the section bar trying a person on a coroner’s inquisition` MEANS
    `s 576(3) the section bars trying a person on a coroner’s inquisition` `the person is to be tried on a coroner’s inquisition`

@export Under section 577, has a direct indictment been preferred?
GIVEN `an indictment has been preferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an indictment been preferred against you?
      `situation` IS A `s 577 where the accused is in the preliminary-inquiry process` @desc Where are you in the preliminary inquiry process: you have not been given the opportunity to request a preliminary inquiry; a preliminary inquiry has been commenced but not concluded; a preliminary inquiry has been held and you have been discharged; or none of those?
      `the prosecution is conducted by the Attorney General or is one in which the Attorney General intervenes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prosecution conducted by the Attorney General, or one in which the Attorney General intervenes?
      `the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General is filed in court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General been filed in court?
      `a judge of the court so orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a judge of the court ordered the indictment to be preferred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 577, has a direct indictment been preferred` MEANS
    `s 577 a direct indictment has been preferred` `an indictment has been preferred` situation `the prosecution is conducted by the Attorney General or is one in which the Attorney General intervenes` `the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General is filed in court` `a judge of the court so orders`

@export Under section 578(1), may the court issue a summons or a warrant for my arrest?
GIVEN `notice of the recommencement of proceedings has been given under subsection 579(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of the recommencement of proceedings been given under subsection 579(2)?
      `an indictment has been filed with the court before which the proceedings are to commence or recommence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an indictment been filed with the court before which the proceedings are to commence or recommence?
      `the court considers it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider it necessary?
      `process` IS A `Process document` @desc Which document is it: an information, an indictment, a count, a summons, a warrant for arrest, an appearance notice, an undertaking, a release order, a recognizance, a subpoena or a search warrant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 578(1), may the court issue a summons or a warrant for my arrest` MEANS
    `s 578(1) the court may issue a summons or a warrant for the arrest of the accused` `notice of the recommencement of proceedings has been given under subsection 579(2)` `an indictment has been filed with the court before which the proceedings are to commence or recommence` `the court considers it necessary` process

@export Under section 579(1), are the proceedings against me stayed and any undertaking or release order relating to them vacated?
GIVEN `the person directing is the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who directed the stay the Attorney General, or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose?
      `proceedings in relation to an accused or a defendant have been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the proceedings against you been commenced?
      `judgment has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has judgment been given?
      `the entry has been made on the record that the proceedings are stayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entry been made on the record that the proceedings are stayed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 579(1), are the proceedings against me stayed and any undertaking or release order relating to them vacated` MEANS
    `s 579(1) the proceedings are stayed and any undertaking or release order relating to them is vacated` (`s 579(1) the Attorney General may direct the clerk to enter a stay` `the person directing is the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for that purpose` `proceedings in relation to an accused or a defendant have been commenced` `judgment has been given`) `the entry has been made on the record that the proceedings are stayed`

@export Under section 579(2), are the proceedings against me deemed never to have been commenced?
GIVEN `the day the stay was entered` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the stay entered?
      `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expire?
      `notice of the recommencement was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the recommencement given to the clerk of the court?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (any date if none was given)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc As at what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 579(2), are the proceedings against me deemed never to have been commenced` MEANS
    `s 579(2) the proceedings are deemed never to have been commenced` `the day the stay was entered` `the day the time within which the proceedings could have been commenced expires` (IF `notice of the recommencement was given` THEN JUST `the day the notice was given` ELSE NOTHING) `the day asked about`

@export Under section 580, is the indictment sufficient?
GIVEN `the indictment is on paper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the indictment on paper?
      `the indictment is in Form 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the indictment in Form 4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 580, is the indictment sufficient` MEANS
    `s 580 the indictment is sufficient` `the indictment is on paper` `the indictment is in Form 4`


§§ `Counts, particulars and details (ss 581 to 588)`

@export Under section 581(3), does the count contain sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence?
GIVEN `the detail gives the accused reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the detail give you reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against you?
      `the detail identifies the transaction referred to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the detail identify the transaction referred to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 581(3), does the count contain sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` MEANS
    `s 581(3) the count contains sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` `the detail gives the accused reasonable information with respect to the act or omission to be proved against them` `the detail identifies the transaction referred to`

@export Under section 581(3), does the absence or insufficiency of details vitiate the count?
GIVEN `the count gives the accused reasonable information and identifies the transaction referred to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the count give you reasonable information and identify the transaction referred to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 581(3), does the absence or insufficiency of details vitiate the count` MEANS
    `s 581(3) the absence or insufficiency of details vitiates the count` `the count gives the accused reasonable information and identifies the transaction referred to`

@export Under section 582, does the section bar a conviction for high treason or first degree murder?
GIVEN `the offence is high treason or first degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence high treason or first degree murder?
      `in the indictment charging the offence the person is specifically charged with that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the indictment charging the offence, are you specifically charged with that offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 582, does the section bar a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` MEANS
    `s 582 the section bars a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` `the offence is high treason or first degree murder` `in the indictment charging the offence the person is specifically charged with that offence`

@export Under section 587(1), may the court order the prosecutor to furnish particulars?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that particulars are necessary for a fair trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 587(1), may the court order the prosecutor to furnish particulars` MEANS
    `s 587(1) the court may order the prosecutor to furnish particulars` `the court is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial`


§§ `Joinder of counts and separate trials (ss 589 to 596)`

@export Under section 589, does the section bar joining the count to a count that charges murder?
GIVEN `the count charges an indictable offence other than murder and is to be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the count charge an indictable offence other than murder, and is it to be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder?
      `the count that charges the offence other than murder arises out of the same transaction as a count that charges murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the count that charges the offence other than murder arise out of the same transaction as a count that charges murder?
      `the accused signifies consent to the joinder of the counts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to the joinder of the counts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 589, does the section bar joining the count to a count that charges murder` MEANS
    `s 589 the section bars joining the count to a count that charges murder` `the count charges an indictable offence other than murder and is to be joined in an indictment to a count that charges murder` `the count that charges the offence other than murder arises out of the same transaction as a count that charges murder` `the accused signifies consent to the joinder of the counts`

@export Under section 590(2), may I apply to the court to amend or to divide the count?
GIVEN `the application is made at a stage of the accused’s trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made at a stage of your trial?
      `the count charges in the alternative different matters, acts or omissions stated in the alternative in the enactment, or is double or multifarious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the count charge in the alternative different matters, acts or omissions stated in the alternative in the enactment, or is it double or multifarious?
      `the ground is that, as framed, the count embarrasses the accused in their defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your ground that, as framed, the count embarrasses you in your defence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 590(2), may I apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` MEANS
    `s 590(2) the accused may apply to the court to amend or to divide the count` `the application is made at a stage of the accused’s trial` `the count charges in the alternative different matters, acts or omissions stated in the alternative in the enactment, or is double or multifarious` `the ground is that, as framed, the count embarrasses the accused in their defence`

@export Under section 591(3), may the court order that the accused or counts be tried separately?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the interests of justice so require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the interests of justice so require?
      `there is more than one accused or defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one accused or defendant?
      `the order sought` IS A `s 591(3) the order sought` @desc What order is sought: that you be tried separately on one or more of the counts, or that one or more of several accused be tried separately on one or more of the counts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 591(3), may the court order that the accused or counts be tried separately` MEANS
    `s 591(3) the court may order that the accused or counts be tried separately` `the court is satisfied that the interests of justice so require` `there is more than one accused or defendant` `the order sought`


§§ `Accused at large; trial in another place (ss 597 to 600)`

@export Under section 597(1), may the court issue a warrant in Form 7 for my arrest?
GIVEN `an indictment has been preferred against a person who is at large` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an indictment been preferred against you, and are you at large?
      `the person does not appear or remain in attendance for their trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to appear or to remain in attendance for your trial?
      `the court is the court before which the accused should have appeared or remained in attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court the court before which you should have appeared or remained in attendance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 597(1), may the court issue a warrant in Form 7 for my arrest` MEANS
    `s 597(1) the court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the accused` `an indictment has been preferred against a person who is at large` `the person does not appear or remain in attendance for their trial` `the court is the court before which the accused should have appeared or remained in attendance`

@export Under section 598(1), does the subsection bar trial by a court composed of a judge and jury?
GIVEN `subsection 597(1) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 597(1) apply to you?
      `the person has elected or is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you elected, or are you deemed to have elected, to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury?
      `at the time the person failed to appear or to remain in attendance for the trial they had re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When you failed to appear or to remain in attendance for the trial, had you re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge without a jury?
      `the person establishes to the satisfaction of a judge of the court in which they are indicted that there was a legitimate excuse for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established to the satisfaction of a judge of the court in which you are indicted that there was a legitimate excuse for the failure?
      `the Attorney General requires pursuant to section 568 or 569 that the accused be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General require, under section 568 or 569, that you be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 598(1), does the subsection bar trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` MEANS
    `s 598(1) the subsection bars trial by a court composed of a judge and jury` `subsection 597(1) applies to the person` `the person has elected or is deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `at the time the person failed to appear or to remain in attendance for the trial they had re-elected to be tried by a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge without a jury` `the person establishes to the satisfaction of a judge of the court in which they are indicted that there was a legitimate excuse for the failure` `the Attorney General requires pursuant to section 568 or 569 that the accused be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury`

@export Under section 599(1), may the court or judge order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province?
GIVEN `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the prosecutor or by you?
      `the other territorial division is in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other territorial division in the same province?
      `it appears expedient to the ends of justice, including to promote a fair and efficient trial, or to ensure the safety and security of a victim or witness or to protect their interests and those of society` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear expedient to the ends of justice, including to promote a fair and efficient trial, or to ensure the safety and security of a victim or witness or to protect their interests and those of society?
      `a competent authority has directed that a jury is not to be summoned at the time appointed in the territorial division where the trial would otherwise by law be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a competent authority directed that a jury is not to be summoned at the time appointed in the territorial division where the trial would otherwise by law be held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 599(1), may the court or judge order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` MEANS
    `s 599(1) the court or judge may order the trial to be held in another territorial division in the same province` `the application is made by the prosecutor or the accused` `the other territorial division is in the same province` `it appears expedient to the ends of justice, including to promote a fair and efficient trial, or to ensure the safety and security of a victim or witness or to protect their interests and those of society` `a competent authority has directed that a jury is not to be summoned at the time appointed in the territorial division where the trial would otherwise by law be held`


§§ `Objections, amendments and copies (ss 601 to 605)`

@export Under section 601(1), may the objection be taken?
GIVEN `the objection is to an indictment preferred under this Part or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the objection to an indictment preferred under this Part, or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face?
      `the objection is taken by motion to quash the indictment or count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the objection taken by motion to quash the indictment or count?
      `the accused has entered a plea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you entered a plea?
      `the court before which the proceedings take place has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court before which the proceedings take place given leave?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 601(1), may the objection be taken` MEANS
    `s 601(1) the objection may be taken` `the objection is to an indictment preferred under this Part or to a count in an indictment, for a defect apparent on its face` `the objection is taken by motion to quash the indictment or count` `the accused has entered a plea` `the court before which the proceedings take place has given leave`

@export Under section 601(2), may the court amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence?
GIVEN `the trial is a trial of an indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trial a trial of an indictment?
      `there is a variance between the evidence and a count in the indictment as preferred, as amended, or as it would have been if amended in conformity with a particular furnished under section 587` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a variance between the evidence and a count in the indictment as preferred, as amended, or as it would have been if amended in conformity with a particular furnished under section 587?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 601(2), may the court amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` MEANS
    `s 601(2) the court may amend the indictment, count or particular to make it conform to the evidence` `the trial is a trial of an indictment` `there is a variance between the evidence and a count in the indictment as preferred, as amended, or as it would have been if amended in conformity with a particular furnished under section 587`

@export Under section 603(a), am I entitled to inspect without charge?
GIVEN `the accused has been ordered to stand trial or is at their trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been ordered to stand trial, or are you at your trial?
      `thing` IS A `s 603(a) what the accused inspects` @desc What do you want to inspect: the indictment, your own statement, the evidence, the exhibits, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 603(a), am I entitled to inspect without charge` MEANS
    `s 603(a) the accused is entitled to inspect without charge` `the accused has been ordered to stand trial or is at their trial` thing

@export Under section 603(b), am I entitled to receive a copy?
GIVEN `the accused has been ordered to stand trial or is at their trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been ordered to stand trial, or are you at your trial?
      `the accused pays a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you pay a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the province?
      `thing` IS A `s 603(b) what the accused receives a copy of` @desc A copy of what do you want: the evidence, your own statement, if any, the indictment, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 603(b), am I entitled to receive a copy` MEANS
    `s 603(b) the accused is entitled to receive a copy` `the accused has been ordered to stand trial or is at their trial` `the accused pays a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the province` thing

@export Under section 603, does the section bar postponing the trial to enable me to secure copies?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the failure of the accused to secure the copies before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence on the part of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that your failure to secure the copies before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence on your part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 603, does the section bar postponing the trial to enable me to secure copies` MEANS
    `s 603 the section bars postponing the trial to enable the accused to secure copies` `the court is satisfied that the failure of the accused to secure the copies before the trial is not attributable to lack of diligence on the part of the accused`


§§ `Pleas and special pleas (ss 606 to 619)`

@export Under section 606(1), may I enter the plea?
GIVEN `the accused is called on to plead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you called on to plead?
      `plea` IS A `s 606(1) the plea` @desc Which plea: guilty, not guilty, autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon, an expungement order, justification of a defamatory libel, or some other plea?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 606(1), may I enter the plea` MEANS
    `s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` `the accused is called on to plead` plea

@export Under section 606(1.1), may the court accept a plea of guilty?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the accused is making the plea voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that you are making the plea voluntarily?
      `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the plea is an admission of the essential elements of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that you understand that the plea is an admission of the essential elements of the offence?
      `the court is satisfied that the accused understands the nature and consequences of the plea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that you understand the nature and consequences of the plea?
      `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the court is not bound by any agreement made between the accused and the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that you understand that the court is not bound by any agreement made between you and the prosecutor?
      `the court is satisfied that the facts support the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the facts support the charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 606(1.1), may the court accept a plea of guilty` MEANS
    `s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` `the court is satisfied that the accused is making the plea voluntarily` `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the plea is an admission of the essential elements of the offence` `the court is satisfied that the accused understands the nature and consequences of the plea` `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the court is not bound by any agreement made between the accused and the prosecutor` `the court is satisfied that the facts support the charge`

