@export Under section 667(3), may I require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination?
GIVEN `a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) is produced against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) produced against you?
      `the court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given leave?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 667(3), may I require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` MEANS
    `s 667(3) the accused may require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` `a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) is produced against the accused` `the court has given leave`

@export Under section 667(4), does the subsection bar receiving the certificate in evidence?
GIVEN `the certificate is a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate one issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c)?
      `the party intending to produce it has given the accused reasonable notice of the party’s intention together with a copy of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the party intending to produce it given you reasonable notice of the party’s intention together with a copy of the certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 667(4), does the subsection bar receiving the certificate in evidence` MEANS
    `s 667(4) the subsection bars receiving the certificate in evidence` `the certificate is a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c)` `the party intending to produce it has given the accused reasonable notice of the party’s intention together with a copy of the certificate`

@export Under section 669.2(1), may the proceedings be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person?
GIVEN `tribunal` IS A `s 669.2(1) the tribunal` @desc By whom are you being tried: a judge or provincial court judge; a justice or other person who is, or is a member of, a summary conviction court; a court composed of a judge and jury; or some other tribunal?
      `the accused or defendant is being tried by the tribunal and the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person dies or is for any reason unable to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person who is trying you dead or for any reason unable to continue?
      `the other judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person have jurisdiction to try you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 669.2(1), may the proceedings be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` MEANS
    `s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` tribunal `the accused or defendant is being tried by the tribunal and the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person dies or is for any reason unable to continue` `the other judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant`

@export Under section 669.3, does the judge or provincial court judge continue to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial?
GIVEN `a court composed of a judge and a jury, a judge or a provincial court judge is conducting a trial and the judge or provincial court judge is appointed to another court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a court composed of a judge and a jury, a judge or a provincial court judge conducting your trial, and is the judge or provincial court judge appointed to another court?
      `the trial has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trial been completed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 669.3, does the judge or provincial court judge continue to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` MEANS
    `s 669.3 the judge or provincial court judge continues to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` `a court composed of a judge and a jury, a judge or a provincial court judge is conducting a trial and the judge or provincial court judge is appointed to another court` `the trial has been completed`


§§ `Formal defects in jury process; saving of the powers of the court (ss 670 to 672)`

@export Under section 670, does the section bar staying or reversing the judgment on the ground?
GIVEN `a verdict has been returned on an indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict been returned on an indictment?
      `ground` IS A `s 670 the ground` @desc What is the ground: an irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury; that a person who served on the jury was not returned as a juror by a sheriff or other officer; or some other ground?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 670, does the section bar staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` MEANS
    `s 670 the section bars staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` `a verdict has been returned on an indictment` ground

@export Under section 671, does the section bar treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict?
GIVEN `there is an omission to observe directions contained in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission to observe directions contained in an Act?
      `directions` IS A `s 671 the directions` @desc The directions are about what: the qualification, selection, balloting or distribution of jurors, the preparation of the jurors’ book, the selecting of jury lists, the drafting of panels from the jury lists, or something else?
      `the verdict was rendered in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the verdict rendered in criminal proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 671, does the section bar treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` MEANS
    `s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` `there is an omission to observe directions contained in an Act` directions `the verdict was rendered in criminal proceedings`

@export Under section 672, does the Act leave the power, authority, practice or form unaltered?
GIVEN `the power or authority is one that a court or judge had, or the practice or form is one that existed, immediately before April 1, 1955` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a power or authority that a court or judge had, or a practice or form that existed, immediately before April 1, 1955?
      `it is with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors?
      `the power or authority, practice or form is expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it expressly altered by, or inconsistent with, this Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 672, does the Act leave the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` MEANS
    `s 672 the Act leaves the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` `the power or authority is one that a court or judge had, or the practice or form is one that existed, immediately before April 1, 1955` `it is with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors` `the power or authority, practice or form is expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc23 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc23-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER for Part XX.1 (Mental Disorder, ss 672.1 to 672.95) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused) and whose mental condition is, or may be, in issue.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
-- It asks what the accused would ask about an assessment of mental condition, fitness to stand trial, the verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder,
-- the hearing and the disposition that follows, review and appeal, transfer between provinces and enforcement. Nothing here is new law: every question calls a layer-1 rule and restates none.
-- Provisions that address only an official (the Review Board's constitution, quorum and rules, the registrar's taxation, the clerk's duties, regulations) have no question;
-- they are in layer 1 for what they decide, and the accused meets them only through the questions below.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, number and date inputs, one for each fact the accused can state, each with an @desc worded as the accused is asked.
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes an answer another rule of this part computes (for example whether an extension is within the maximum, or whether a statement is a protected statement),
-- the question asks the producer's plain facts and calls the producer in its WHERE, so a `NOTHING` is carried through and never turned into `FALSE`.
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes a date the court may or may not have set (an extension, a later day), the question asks "is there one" and then the day.
-- The one section 2 answer asked as a fact is `peace officer` (a list of capacities, asked as "is the person a peace officer"); "unfit to stand trial" is computed by `ccc-definitions` from its five plain inputs.
-- Answers are three-valued where the layer-1 rule is: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING (the text does not say). Read a bar's answer as the bar: JUST TRUE = the bar applies.

§ `Assessment orders (ss 672.11 to 672.21)`

@export Under section 672.11, may the court order an assessment of my mental condition?
GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction over the accused in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have jurisdiction over you in respect of an offence?
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether you are unfit to stand trial?
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused was, at the time of the alleged offence, suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether you were, at the time of the alleged offence, suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)?
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of the alleged offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the balance of your mind was disturbed at the time of the alleged offence?
      `the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of your newly-born child?
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine the appropriate disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine the appropriate disposition?
      `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, or of unfit to stand trial, been rendered in respect of you?
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused should be revoked under subsection 672.84(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether a finding that you are a high-risk accused should be revoked under subsection 672.84(3)?
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether an order should be made under section 672.851 for a stay of proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether an order should be made under section 672.851 for a stay of proceedings?
      `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict of unfit to stand trial been rendered against you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.11, may the court order an assessment of my mental condition` IS
    `s 672.11 the court may order an assessment of the mental condition of the accused` `the court has jurisdiction over the accused in respect of an offence` `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused was, at the time of the alleged offence, suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of the alleged offence` `the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine the appropriate disposition` `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused` `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused should be revoked under subsection 672.84(3)` `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether an order should be made under section 672.851 for a stay of proceedings` `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered against the accused`

@export Under section 672.14, what is the longest period, in days, that the assessment order may be in force?
GIVEN `compelling circumstances that warrant it exist, and the court or Review Board is satisfied of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do compelling circumstances that warrant a longer period exist, and is the court or Review Board satisfied of it?
      `the order is to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order to determine whether you are unfit to stand trial?
      `the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you and the prosecutor agree to a longer period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 672.14, what is the longest period, in days, that the assessment order may be in force` IS
    `s 672.14 the longest period the assessment order may be in force, in days` `compelling circumstances that warrant it exist, and the court or Review Board is satisfied of it` `the order is to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` `the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period`

@export Under section 672.15(1), may the court or Review Board extend the assessment order?
GIVEN `the court or Review Board acts of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court or Review Board act of its own motion?
      `the accused or the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you or the prosecutor applied for the order?
      `the application is made during or at the end of the period during which the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made during or at the end of the period during which the order is in force?
      `the further period is required, in its opinion, to complete the assessment of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the further period required, in its opinion, to complete the assessment of you?
      `the days of the extension` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days is the assessment order to be extended?
      `the days of the initial order together with all extensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the assessment order in force in all, counting the initial order together with all extensions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.15(1), may the court or Review Board extend the assessment order` IS
    `s 672.15(1) the court or Review Board may extend the assessment order` `the court or Review Board acts of its own motion` `the accused or the prosecutor applies` `the application is made during or at the end of the period during which the order is in force` `the further period is required, in its opinion, to complete the assessment of the accused` `the extension is within the maximum, by s 672.15(2)`
    WHERE
        `the extension is within the maximum, by s 672.15(2)` MEANS `s 672.15(2) the extension is within the maximum` `the days of the extension` `the days of the initial order together with all extensions`

@export Under section 672.16(1), is the court barred from detaining me in custody under the assessment order?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied on the evidence that custody is necessary to assess the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied on the evidence that custody is necessary to assess you?
      `on the evidence of a medical practitioner custody is desirable to assess the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the evidence of a medical practitioner, is custody of you desirable to assess you?
      `the accused consents to custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to custody?
      `custody of the accused is required in respect of any other matter or by virtue of any other provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is custody of you required in respect of any other matter or by virtue of any other provision of this Act?
      `the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows that detention is justified on either of the grounds set out in subsection 515(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shown that your detention is justified on either of the grounds set out in subsection 515(10)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.16(1), is the court barred from detaining me in custody under the assessment order` IS
    `s 672.16(1) the court is barred from detaining the accused in custody under the assessment order` `the court is satisfied on the evidence that custody is necessary to assess the accused` `on the evidence of a medical practitioner custody is desirable to assess the accused` `the accused consents to custody` `custody of the accused is required in respect of any other matter or by virtue of any other provision of this Act` `the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows that detention is justified on either of the grounds set out in subsection 515(10)`

@export Under section 672.19, does the section bar an assessment order from directing treatment?
GIVEN `the term directs that psychiatric or any other treatment of the accused be carried out, or directs the accused to submit to such treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term direct that psychiatric or any other treatment of you be carried out, or direct you to submit to such treatment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.19, does the section bar an assessment order from directing treatment` IS
    `s 672.19 the section bars an assessment order from directing treatment` `the term directs that psychiatric or any other treatment of the accused be carried out, or directs the accused to submit to such treatment`

@export Under section 672.191, have I appeared as the section requires?
GIVEN `the day the assessment order begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the assessment order begin? (a date)
      `the number of days the order is to be in force` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days is the order to be in force?
      `the day the accused appears before the court or Review Board that made the order` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you appear before the court or Review Board that made the order? (a date)
      `the accused appeared as soon as practicable after the assessment was completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appear before the court or Review Board that made the order as soon as practicable after the assessment was completed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.191, have I appeared as the section requires` IS
    `s 672.191 the accused has appeared as the section requires` `the day the assessment order begins` `the number of days the order is to be in force` `the day the accused appears before the court or Review Board that made the order` `the accused appeared as soon as practicable after the assessment was completed`

@export Under section 672.2(4), must the report be provided to me and my counsel without delay?
GIVEN `a report has been filed with a court or Review Board under subsection 672.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a report been filed with a court or Review Board under subsection 672.2(2)?
      `subsection 672.51(3) requires the court or Review Board to withhold the information from the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 672.51(3) require the court or Review Board to withhold the information from you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.2(4), must the report be provided to me and my counsel without delay` IS
    `s 672.2(4) the report must be provided to the accused and counsel without delay` `a report has been filed with a court or Review Board under subsection 672.2(2)` `subsection 672.51(3) requires the court or Review Board to withhold the information from the accused`

@export Under section 672.21(2), does the section bar the protected statement from being admitted in evidence?
GIVEN `it is a statement made by the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a statement that you made?
      `it is made during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition?
      `it is made to the person specified in the assessment order or the disposition, or to anyone acting under that person’s direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made to the person specified in the assessment order or the disposition, or to anyone acting under that person’s direction?
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent?
      `the proceeding is before a court, tribunal, body or person with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding before a court, tribunal, body or person with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence?
      `the purpose is determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose determining whether you are unfit to stand trial?
      `the purpose is making a disposition or placement decision respecting the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose making a disposition or placement decision respecting you?
      `the purpose is determining, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused or whether to revoke such a finding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to determine, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that you are a high-risk accused, or whether to revoke such a finding?
      `the purpose is determining whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to determine whether the balance of your mind was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and are you a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of your newly-born child?
      `the purpose is determining whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose determining whether you were, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)?
      `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you put your mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or does the prosecutor raise the issue after verdict?
      `the purpose is challenging the credibility of an accused in a proceeding where the testimony of the accused is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that the accused made previously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to challenge your credibility in a proceeding where your testimony is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that you made previously?
      `the purpose is establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to establish your perjury, where you are charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.21(2), does the section bar the protected statement from being admitted in evidence` IS
    `s 672.21(2) the section bars the protected statement from being admitted in evidence` `it is a protected statement, or a reference to a protected statement, made by an accused, by s 672.21(1)` `the accused consents` `the proceeding is before a court, tribunal, body or person with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence` `the evidence is admissible for the purpose, by s 672.21(3)`
    WHERE
        `it is a protected statement, or a reference to a protected statement, made by an accused, by s 672.21(1)` MEANS `s 672.21(1) protected statement` `it is a statement made by the accused` `it is made during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition` `it is made to the person specified in the assessment order or the disposition, or to anyone acting under that person’s direction`
        `the evidence is admissible for the purpose, by s 672.21(3)` MEANS `s 672.21(3) evidence of a protected statement is admissible for the purpose` `the purpose is determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` `the purpose is making a disposition or placement decision respecting the accused` `the purpose is determining, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused or whether to revoke such a finding` `the purpose is determining whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` `the purpose is determining whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict` `the purpose is challenging the credibility of an accused in a proceeding where the testimony of the accused is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that the accused made previously` `the purpose is establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding`

@export Under section 672.21(3), is evidence of a protected statement admissible for the purpose?
GIVEN `the purpose is determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose determining whether you are unfit to stand trial?
      `the purpose is making a disposition or placement decision respecting the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose making a disposition or placement decision respecting you?
      `the purpose is determining, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused or whether to revoke such a finding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to determine, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that you are a high-risk accused, or whether to revoke such a finding?
      `the purpose is determining whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to determine whether the balance of your mind was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and are you a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of your newly-born child?
      `the purpose is determining whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose determining whether you were, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)?
      `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you put your mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or does the prosecutor raise the issue after verdict?
      `the purpose is challenging the credibility of an accused in a proceeding where the testimony of the accused is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that the accused made previously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to challenge your credibility in a proceeding where your testimony is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that you made previously?
      `the purpose is establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to establish your perjury, where you are charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.21(3), is evidence of a protected statement admissible for the purpose` IS
    `s 672.21(3) evidence of a protected statement is admissible for the purpose` `the purpose is determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` `the purpose is making a disposition or placement decision respecting the accused` `the purpose is determining, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused or whether to revoke such a finding` `the purpose is determining whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` `the purpose is determining whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict` `the purpose is challenging the credibility of an accused in a proceeding where the testimony of the accused is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that the accused made previously` `the purpose is establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding`

§ `Fitness to stand trial (ss 672.22 to 672.33)`

@export Under section 672.22, am I presumed fit to stand trial?
GIVEN `unable on account of mental disorder to conduct a defence at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable on account of mental disorder to conduct a defence at any stage of the proceedings before a verdict is rendered?
      `unable on account of mental disorder to instruct counsel to conduct a defence at any such stage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable on account of mental disorder to instruct counsel to conduct a defence at any such stage?
      `unable on account of mental disorder to understand the nature or object of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable on account of mental disorder to understand the nature or object of the proceedings?
      `unable on account of mental disorder to understand the possible consequences of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable on account of mental disorder to understand the possible consequences of the proceedings?
      `unable on account of mental disorder to communicate with counsel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable on account of mental disorder to communicate with counsel?
      `the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied on the balance of probabilities that you are unfit to stand trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.22, am I presumed fit to stand trial` IS
    `s 672.22 the accused is presumed fit to stand trial` `the accused is unfit to stand trial, by s 2 unfit to stand trial` `the court is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the accused is unfit to stand trial`
    WHERE
