    `s 672.52(3) the court or Review Board must state its reasons and provide every party with a copy of the disposition and the reasons` `the court or Review Board makes a disposition`

@export Under section 672.53, does the procedural irregularity affect the validity of the hearing?
GIVEN `there is a procedural irregularity in relation to a disposition hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a procedural irregularity in relation to a disposition hearing?
      `it causes the accused substantial prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it cause you substantial prejudice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.53, does the procedural irregularity affect the validity of the hearing` IS
    `s 672.53 the procedural irregularity affects the validity of the hearing` `there is a procedural irregularity in relation to a disposition hearing` `it causes the accused substantial prejudice`

§ `Dispositions (ss 672.54 to 672.63)`

@export Under section 672.54(a), may the court or Review Board direct that I be discharged absolutely?
GIVEN `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder been rendered in respect of you?
      `it is a risk of serious physical or psychological harm to members of the public, including any victim of or witness to the offence, or any person under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a risk of serious physical or psychological harm to members of the public, including any victim of or witness to the offence, or any person under the age of 18 years?
      `the harm results from conduct that is criminal in nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the harm result from conduct that is criminal in nature?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.54(a), may the court or Review Board direct that I be discharged absolutely` IS
    `s 672.54(a) the court or Review Board may direct that the accused be discharged absolutely` `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered in respect of the accused` `the accused is a significant threat to the safety of the public, in the opinion of the court or Review Board, by s 672.5401`
    WHERE
        `the accused is a significant threat to the safety of the public, in the opinion of the court or Review Board, by s 672.5401` MEANS `s 672.5401 significant threat to the safety of the public` `it is a risk of serious physical or psychological harm to members of the public, including any victim of or witness to the offence, or any person under the age of 18 years` `the harm results from conduct that is criminal in nature`

@export Under section 672.54(b), may the court or Review Board direct that I be discharged subject to conditions?
GIVEN `the court or Review Board is making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court or Review Board making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.54(b), may the court or Review Board direct that I be discharged subject to conditions` IS
    `s 672.54(b) the court or Review Board may direct that the accused be discharged subject to conditions` `the court or Review Board is making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84`

@export Under section 672.54(c), may the court or Review Board direct that I be detained in custody in a hospital?
GIVEN `the court or Review Board is making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court or Review Board making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.54(c), may the court or Review Board direct that I be detained in custody in a hospital` IS
    `s 672.54(c) the court or Review Board may direct that the accused be detained in custody in a hospital` `the court or Review Board is making a disposition under subsection 672.45(2), section 672.47, subsection 672.64(3) or section 672.83 or 672.84`

@export Under section 672.55(1), does the section bar the disposition from directing treatment?
GIVEN `the disposition directs that any psychiatric or other treatment of the accused be carried out or that the accused submit to such treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the disposition direct that any psychiatric or other treatment of you be carried out or that you submit to such treatment?
      `the accused has consented to the condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to the condition?
      `the court or Review Board considers the condition to be reasonable and necessary in the interests of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court or Review Board consider the condition to be reasonable and necessary in your interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.55(1), does the section bar the disposition from directing treatment` IS
    `s 672.55(1) the section bars the disposition from directing treatment` `the disposition directs that any psychiatric or other treatment of the accused be carried out or that the accused submit to such treatment` `the accused has consented to the condition` `the court or Review Board considers the condition to be reasonable and necessary in the interests of the accused`

@export Under section 672.57, must the court or Review Board issue a warrant of committal of me?
GIVEN `the court or Review Board makes a disposition under paragraph 672.54(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court or Review Board make a disposition under paragraph 672.54(c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.57, must the court or Review Board issue a warrant of committal of me` IS
    `s 672.57 the court or Review Board must issue a warrant of committal of the accused` `the court or Review Board makes a disposition under paragraph 672.54(c)`

@export Under section 672.58, may the court direct that my treatment be carried out?
GIVEN `a verdict of unfit to stand trial is rendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a verdict of unfit to stand trial rendered?
      `the court has not made a disposition under section 672.54 in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made no disposition under section 672.54 in respect of you?
      `the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor apply?
      `the days of the specified period` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days does the order specify that the treatment is to be carried out?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.58, may the court direct that my treatment be carried out` IS
    `s 672.58 the court may direct that treatment of the accused be carried out` `a verdict of unfit to stand trial is rendered` `the court has not made a disposition under section 672.54 in respect of the accused` `the prosecutor applies` `the days of the specified period`

@export Under section 672.61(1), does the section bar psychosurgery, electro-convulsive therapy or another prescribed prohibited treatment?
GIVEN `it is a procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue, or inserts indwelling electrodes for pulsed electrical stimulation for the purpose of altering behaviour or treating psychiatric illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue, or inserts indwelling electrodes for pulsed electrical stimulation for the purpose of altering behaviour or treating psychiatric illness?
      `it is a neurological procedure used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy, where any of those conditions is clearly demonstrable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a neurological procedure used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy, where any of those conditions is clearly demonstrable?
      `it is a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders?
      `it induces, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it induce, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions?
      `the regulations made by the Governor in Council under section 672.95 prescribe it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations made by the Governor in Council under section 672.95 prescribe it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.61(1), does the section bar psychosurgery, electro-convulsive therapy or another prescribed prohibited treatment` IS
    `s 672.61(1) the section bars psychosurgery, electro-convulsive therapy or another prescribed prohibited treatment` `it is psychosurgery, by s 672.61(2)` `it is electro-convulsive therapy, by s 672.61(2)` `it is another prohibited treatment that is prescribed, by s 672.1(1) prescribed`
    WHERE
        `it is psychosurgery, by s 672.61(2)` MEANS `s 672.61(2) psychosurgery` `it is a procedure that by direct or indirect access to the brain removes, destroys or interrupts the continuity of histologically normal brain tissue, or inserts indwelling electrodes for pulsed electrical stimulation for the purpose of altering behaviour or treating psychiatric illness` `it is a neurological procedure used to diagnose or treat intractable physical pain, organic brain conditions, or epilepsy, where any of those conditions is clearly demonstrable`
        `it is electro-convulsive therapy, by s 672.61(2)` MEANS `s 672.61(2) electro-convulsive therapy` `it is a procedure for the treatment of certain mental disorders` `it induces, by electrical stimulation of the brain, a series of generalized convulsions`
        `it is another prohibited treatment that is prescribed, by s 672.1(1) prescribed` MEANS `s 672.1(1) prescribed` `the regulations made by the Governor in Council under section 672.95 prescribe it`

@export Under section 672.62(2), may the court direct that treatment be carried out without my consent?
GIVEN `it is a disposition made under section 672.58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disposition made under section 672.58?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.62(2), may the court direct that treatment be carried out without my consent` IS
    `s 672.62(2) the court may direct that treatment be carried out without the consent of the accused` `it is a disposition made under section 672.58`

@export Under section 672.63, is the disposition in force on the day?
GIVEN `the day the disposition is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the disposition made? (a date)
      `there is a day: the later day that the court or Review Board specifies in the disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court or Review Board specified a later day in the disposition? (answer yes if it has, and give the day in the next question)
      `the later day that the court or Review Board specifies in the disposition` IS A DATE @desc What later day does the disposition specify? (a date; any date if none is specified)
      `there is a day: the day the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Review Board held a hearing to review the disposition and made another disposition? (answer yes if it has, and give the day in the next question)
      `the day the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Review Board hold that hearing and make another disposition? (a date; any date if there was none)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc For what day do you want to know whether the disposition is in force? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.63, is the disposition in force on the day` IS
    `s 672.63 the disposition is in force on the day` `the day the disposition is made` (IF `there is a day: the later day that the court or Review Board specifies in the disposition` THEN JUST `the later day that the court or Review Board specifies in the disposition` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `there is a day: the day the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition` THEN JUST `the day the Review Board holds a hearing to review the disposition and makes another disposition` ELSE NOTHING) `the day asked about`

§ `High-risk accused and dual status offenders (ss 672.64 to 672.71)`

@export Under section 672.64(1), may the court find me to be a high-risk accused?
GIVEN `the prosecutor makes an application before any disposition to discharge the accused absolutely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor make an application before any disposition to discharge you absolutely?
      `I have been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder?
      `the section of the Code under which the offence was charged` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code was the offence charged? (the section number, for example 271)
      `it is an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an indictable offence?
      `it is an attempt to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an attempt to commit the offence?
      `it involves, in respect of another person, the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence involve, in respect of another person, the use or attempted use of violence against the other person?
      `it involves, in respect of another person, conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of, or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on, the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence involve, in respect of another person, conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of, or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on, the other person?
      `the accused was 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence?
      `the court is satisfied that there is a substantial likelihood that the accused will use violence that could endanger the life or safety of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that there is a substantial likelihood that you will use violence that could endanger the life or safety of another person?
      `the court is of the opinion that the acts that constitute the offence were of such a brutal nature as to indicate a risk of grave physical or psychological harm to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of the opinion that the acts that constitute the offence were of such a brutal nature as to indicate a risk of grave physical or psychological harm to another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.64(1), may the court find me to be a high-risk accused` IS
    `s 672.64(1) the court may find the accused to be a high-risk accused` `the prosecutor makes an application before any disposition to discharge the accused absolutely` `the accused has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a serious personal injury offence, by s 672.81(1.3)` `the accused was 18 years of age or more at the time of the commission of the offence` `the court is satisfied that there is a substantial likelihood that the accused will use violence that could endanger the life or safety of another person` `the court is of the opinion that the acts that constitute the offence were of such a brutal nature as to indicate a risk of grave physical or psychological harm to another person`
    WHERE
        `the accused has been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a serious personal injury offence, by s 672.81(1.3)` MEANS IF `I have been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` THEN `s 672.81(1.3) serious personal injury offence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the Code under which the offence was charged`, "") `it is an indictable offence` `it is an attempt to commit the offence` `it involves, in respect of another person, the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` `it involves, in respect of another person, conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of, or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on, the other person` ELSE JUST FALSE

@export Under section 672.64(3), does the section bar a condition that would permit me, as a high-risk accused, to be absent from the hospital?
GIVEN `the accused is a high-risk accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a high-risk accused?
      `it is appropriate, in the opinion of the person in charge of the hospital, for the accused to be absent from the hospital for medical reasons or for any purpose that is necessary for the accused’s treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it appropriate, in the opinion of the person in charge of the hospital, for you to be absent from the hospital for medical reasons or for any purpose that is necessary for your treatment?
      `the accused is escorted by a person who is authorized by the person in charge of the hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you escorted by a person who is authorized by the person in charge of the hospital?
      `a structured plan has been prepared to address any risk related to the accused’s absence and, as a result, that absence will not present an undue risk to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a structured plan been prepared to address any risk related to your absence, and will that absence, as a result, not present an undue risk to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.64(3), does the section bar a condition that would permit me, as a high-risk accused, to be absent from the hospital` IS
    `s 672.64(3) the section bars a condition that would permit the high-risk accused to be absent from the hospital` `the accused is a high-risk accused` `it is appropriate, in the opinion of the person in charge of the hospital, for the accused to be absent from the hospital for medical reasons or for any purpose that is necessary for the accused’s treatment` `the accused is escorted by a person who is authorized by the person in charge of the hospital` `a structured plan has been prepared to address any risk related to the accused’s absence and, as a result, that absence will not present an undue risk to the public`

@export Under section 672.68(2), must the Review Board decide whether to place me, as the offender, in custody in a hospital or in a prison?
GIVEN `the Minister applies, or the Review Board acts of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister apply, or does the Review Board act of its own motion?
      `the person is an offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an offender, that is, a person that a court has determined to be guilty of an offence?
      `the person is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence?
      `the person is subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence?
      `the Review Board is of the opinion that the place of custody is inappropriate to meet the mental health needs of the offender or to safeguard the well-being of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Review Board of the opinion that the place of custody is inappropriate to meet the mental health needs of the offender or to safeguard the well-being of other persons?
      `the Review Board has given the offender and the Minister reasonable notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Review Board given the offender and the Minister reasonable notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.68(2), must the Review Board decide whether to place me, as the offender, in custody in a hospital or in a prison` IS
    `s 672.68(2) the Review Board must decide whether to place the offender in custody in a hospital or in a prison` `the Minister applies, or the Review Board acts of its own motion` `the person is a dual status offender, by s 672.1(1) dual status offender` `the Review Board is of the opinion that the place of custody is inappropriate to meet the mental health needs of the offender or to safeguard the well-being of other persons` `the Review Board has given the offender and the Minister reasonable notice`
    WHERE
        `the person is a dual status offender, by s 672.1(1) dual status offender` MEANS `s 672.1(1) dual status offender` `the person is an offender` `the person is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence` `the person is subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence`

@export Under section 672.68(4), is the placement decision made in time?
GIVEN `the day the Review Board receives an application from, or gives notice to, the Minister under subsection 672.68(2)` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Review Board receive an application from, or give notice to, the Minister under subsection 672.68(2)? (a date)
      `the day the Review Board makes its placement decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Review Board make its placement decision? (a date)
      `the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period?
      `the longer period agreed, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the longer period that the Review Board and the Minister have agreed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.68(4), is the placement decision made in time` IS
    `s 672.68(4) the placement decision is made in time` `the day the Review Board receives an application from, or gives notice to, the Minister under subsection 672.68(2)` `the day the Review Board makes its placement decision` `the Review Board and the Minister agree to a longer period` `the longer period agreed, in days`

@export Under section 672.71(1), is each day of detention a day of service of the term of imprisonment and am I deemed to be lawfully confined in a prison?
GIVEN `the person is an offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an offender, that is, a person that a court has determined to be guilty of an offence?
      `the person is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence?
      `the person is subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence?
      `the person is detained pursuant to a placement decision or a custodial disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained under a placement decision or a custodial disposition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.71(1), is each day of detention a day of service of the term of imprisonment and am I deemed to be lawfully confined in a prison` IS
    `s 672.71(1) each day of detention is a day of service of the term of imprisonment and the accused is deemed to be lawfully confined in a prison` `the person is a dual status offender, by s 672.1(1) dual status offender` `the person is detained pursuant to a placement decision or a custodial disposition`
    WHERE
        `the person is a dual status offender, by s 672.1(1) dual status offender` MEANS `s 672.1(1) dual status offender` `the person is an offender` `the person is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence` `the person is subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence`

§ `Appeals (ss 672.72 to 672.78)`

@export Under section 672.72(1), may I, as a party, appeal against the disposition or placement decision?
GIVEN `the person is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the hearing?
      `it is a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board?
      `the appeal is to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made?
      `the ground raises a question of law or fact alone or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the ground raise a question of law or fact alone or of mixed law and fact?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.72(1), may I, as a party, appeal against the disposition or placement decision` IS
    `s 672.72(1) the party may appeal against the disposition or placement decision` `the person is a party` `it is a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board` `the appeal is to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made` `the ground raises a question of law or fact alone or of mixed law and fact`

@export Under section 672.72(2), is notice of appeal given in time?
GIVEN `the day the appellant receives a copy of the disposition or placement decision and the reasons for it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the appellant receive a copy of the disposition or placement decision and the reasons for it? (a date)
      `the day the appellant gives notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the appellant give notice of appeal? (a date)
      `there is a day: the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, has directed a further time, to the end of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, directed a further time for giving notice of appeal? (answer yes if it has, and give the last day of it in the next question)
      `the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, has directed a further time, to the end of` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the further time that the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, has directed? (a date; any date if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.72(2), is notice of appeal given in time` IS
    `s 672.72(2) notice of appeal is given in time` `the day the appellant receives a copy of the disposition or placement decision and the reasons for it` `the day the appellant gives notice of appeal` (IF `there is a day: the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, has directed a further time, to the end of` THEN JUST `the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, has directed a further time, to the end of` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 672.75, is the application of the disposition suspended pending the determination of the appeal?
GIVEN `a notice of appeal has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice of appeal been filed?
      `the appeal is against a disposition made under section 672.58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal against a disposition made under section 672.58?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.75, is the application of the disposition suspended pending the determination of the appeal` IS
    `s 672.75 the application of the disposition is suspended pending the determination of the appeal` `a notice of appeal has been filed` `the appeal is against a disposition made under section 672.58`

@export Under section 672.78(1), may the court of appeal allow the appeal and set aside the order?
GIVEN `the court of appeal is of the opinion that the disposition or placement decision is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of appeal of the opinion that the disposition or placement decision is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence?
      `the court of appeal is of the opinion that it is based on a wrong decision on a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of appeal of the opinion that it is based on a wrong decision on a question of law?
      `the court of appeal is of the opinion that there was a miscarriage of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of appeal of the opinion that there was a miscarriage of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.78(1), may the court of appeal allow the appeal and set aside the order` IS
    `s 672.78(1) the court of appeal may allow the appeal and set aside the order` `the court of appeal is of the opinion that the disposition or placement decision is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence` `the court of appeal is of the opinion that it is based on a wrong decision on a question of law` `the court of appeal is of the opinion that there was a miscarriage of justice`

§ `Review of dispositions and stay of proceedings (ss 672.81 to 672.852)`

@export Under section 672.81(1), has the Review Board held the hearing in time?
GIVEN `the Review Board is reviewing a disposition other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Review Board reviewing a disposition other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a)?
      `the day the disposition was made or last reviewed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the disposition made or last reviewed? (a date)
      `the day the Review Board holds the hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Review Board hold the hearing? (a date)
      `the months allowed, by s 672.81 the longest time before the next hearing, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months does your disposition allow before the Review Board must hold the next hearing? (12 months, or the longer period of an extension under subsection 672.81(1.1), (1.2), (1.31) or (1.32))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.81(1), has the Review Board held the hearing in time` IS
    `s 672.81(1) the Review Board has held the hearing in time` `the Review Board is reviewing a disposition other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a)` `the day the disposition was made or last reviewed` `the day the Review Board holds the hearing` `the months allowed, by s 672.81 the longest time before the next hearing, in months`

@export Under section 672.81(1.1), may the Review Board extend the time for holding the hearing to a maximum of twenty-four months?
GIVEN `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you represented by counsel?
      `the accused consents to the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to the extension?
      `the Attorney General consents to the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General consent to the extension?
      `the months after the making or reviewing of the disposition to which the time is extended` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many months after the disposition was made or last reviewed is the time for the next hearing to be extended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.81(1.1), may the Review Board extend the time for holding the hearing to a maximum of twenty-four months` IS
    `s 672.81(1.1) the Review Board may extend the time for holding the hearing to a maximum of twenty-four months` `the accused is represented by counsel` `the accused consents to the extension` `the Attorney General consents to the extension` `the months after the making or reviewing of the disposition to which the time is extended`

@export Under section 672.81(1.31), may the Review Board extend the time for holding a hearing in respect of a high-risk accused to a maximum of 36 months?
GIVEN `the accused is a high-risk accused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a high-risk accused?
      `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you represented by counsel?
      `the accused consents to the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to the extension?
      `the Attorney General consents to the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Attorney General consent to the extension?
      `the months after making or reviewing the disposition to which the time is extended` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many months after the disposition was made or last reviewed is the time for the next hearing to be extended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 672.81(1.31), may the Review Board extend the time for holding a hearing in respect of a high-risk accused to a maximum of 36 months` IS
    `s 672.81(1.31) the Review Board may extend the time for holding a hearing in respect of a high-risk accused to a maximum of 36 months` `the accused is a high-risk accused` `the accused is represented by counsel` `the accused consents to the extension` `the Attorney General consents to the extension` `the months after making or reviewing the disposition to which the time is extended`

