    `s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` `a peace officer arrests the accused under section 672.91` `the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or an assessment order` `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that it is necessary in the public interest that the accused be detained in custody having regard to all the circumstances` `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that the accused is subject to a disposition or an assessment order of a court, or Review Board, of another province` `the peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, that, if the accused is released from custody, the accused will fail to attend, as required, before a justice`

