-- answers: s 676(4) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal against the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole, being less than 25
@export Under section 676(4), may the Attorney General appeal against the number of years I must serve before parole, being less than 25?
GIVEN `the appeal is brought by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal brought by the Attorney General, or by counsel the Attorney General instructed for the purpose?
      `the kind of homicide offence I was convicted of` IS A `Kind of homicide offence` @desc Which kind of homicide offence were you convicted of?
      `my manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were convicted of manslaughter, was it in the circumstances set out in paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)?
      `the number of years without eligibility for parole that I was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years without eligibility for parole were you given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
