    `s 676(4) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal against the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole, being less than 25` `the appeal is brought by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for the purpose` `the kind of homicide offence I was convicted of` `my manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` `the number of years without eligibility for parole that I was given`

-- answers: s 676(5) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal against the decision of the court not to make an order under section 743.6
@export Under section 676(5), may the Attorney General appeal against the court's decision not to delay my eligibility for parole?
