    `s 676(6) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal against the decision of the court not to make an order under subsection 745.51(1)` `the appeal is brought by the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for the purpose` `the court decided not to make an order against me under subsection 745.51(1)`

-- answers: s 676.1 the party ordered to pay costs may appeal the order or the amount of costs ordered
@export Under section 676.1, may I appeal an order that I pay costs, or the amount of costs ordered?
GIVEN `I am ordered to pay costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been ordered to pay costs?
      `the court of appeal or a judge of it has granted me leave to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court of appeal, or a judge of a court of appeal, granted you leave to appeal the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 676.1, may I appeal an order that I pay costs, or the amount of costs ordered` IS
    `s 676.1 the party ordered to pay costs may appeal the order or the amount of costs ordered` `I am ordered to pay costs` `the court of appeal or a judge of it has granted me leave to appeal`

§§ `Notice of appeal, release pending appeal, and the court of appeal (sections 678 to 690)`
-- Arises once you have appealed or are about to; ask "Have you appealed, or do you want to appeal?" before showing the group.

-- answers: s 678(1) the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal was given in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court
@export Under section 678(1), did I give my notice of appeal in the manner and within the period that the rules of court direct?
GIVEN `my notice was given in the manner the rules of court direct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your notice given in the manner the rules of court direct?
      `the number of days after which I gave my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the decision did you give your notice?
      `the number of days that the rules of court allow for the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days do the rules of court allow for giving the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 678(1), did I give my notice of appeal in the manner and within the period that the rules of court direct` IS
    `s 678(1) the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal was given in the manner and within the period directed by rules of court` `my notice was given in the manner the rules of court direct` `the number of days after which I gave my notice` `the number of days that the rules of court allow for the notice`

-- answers: s 678(2) the court of appeal or a judge may extend the time for giving notice of appeal or of an application for leave to appeal
@export Under section 678(2), may the court of appeal extend the time for giving my notice of appeal?
GIVEN `my notice is a notice of appeal or of an application for leave to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a notice of appeal, or a notice of an application for leave to appeal, under Part XXI?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 678(2), may the court of appeal extend the time for giving my notice of appeal` IS
    `s 678(2) the court of appeal or a judge may extend the time for giving notice of appeal or of an application for leave to appeal` `my notice is a notice of appeal or of an application for leave to appeal`

-- answers: s 678.1 service of the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal may be effected substitutionally
@export Under section 678.1, may notice of my appeal be served on the respondent in another way, because the respondent cannot be found?
GIVEN `the respondent cannot be found after reasonable efforts have been made to serve the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent been impossible to find, after reasonable efforts to serve the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 678.1, may notice of my appeal be served on the respondent in another way, because the respondent cannot be found` IS
    `s 678.1 service of the notice of appeal or of the application for leave to appeal may be effected substitutionally` `the respondent cannot be found after reasonable efforts have been made to serve the notice`

-- answers: s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal
@export Under section 679(1), may a judge of the court of appeal release me from custody until my appeal is decided?
GIVEN `the kind of appeal I have taken` IS A `s 679(1) kind of appeal` @desc What kind of appeal have you taken: against conviction to the court of appeal, against sentence only to the court of appeal, to the Supreme Court of Canada, or another?
      `I have given notice of appeal (or of my application for leave to appeal) under section 678` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice of appeal, or, where leave is required, notice of your application for leave to appeal, under section 678?
      `I have been granted leave to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been granted leave to appeal?
      `I have filed and served my notice of appeal (or my application for leave to appeal)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada: have you filed and served your notice of appeal, or your application for leave to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 679(1), may a judge of the court of appeal release me from custody until my appeal is decided` IS
    `s 679(1) a judge of the court of appeal may release an appellant from custody pending the determination of the appeal` `the kind of appeal I have taken` `I have given notice of appeal (or of my application for leave to appeal) under section 678` `I have been granted leave to appeal` `I have filed and served my notice of appeal (or my application for leave to appeal)`

-- answers: s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada
-- RETITLED 2026-11-12 (second audit pass): was "Under section 679(3), may a judge order that I be released while my appeal against conviction is decided?"; scope: the body answers an appeal against conviction and an appeal or application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, the title named only the first
@export Under section 679(3), may a judge order that I be released while my appeal against conviction, or my appeal or application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, is decided?
GIVEN `the kind of appeal I have taken` IS A `s 679(1) kind of appeal` @desc What kind of appeal have you taken: against conviction to the court of appeal, against sentence only to the court of appeal, to the Supreme Court of Canada, or another?
      `I establish that my appeal or application for leave to appeal is not frivolous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that your appeal, or your application for leave to appeal, is not frivolous?
      `I establish that I will surrender myself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that you will surrender yourself into custody as the order requires?
      `I establish that my detention is not necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that your detention is not necessary in the public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 679(3), may a judge order that I be released while my appeal against conviction, or my appeal or application for leave to appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, is decided` IS
    `s 679(3) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against conviction or to the Supreme Court of Canada` `the kind of appeal I have taken` `I establish that my appeal or application for leave to appeal is not frivolous` `I establish that I will surrender myself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order` `I establish that my detention is not necessary in the public interest`

-- answers: s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only
@export Under section 679(4), may a judge order that I be released while my appeal against sentence only is decided?
GIVEN `the kind of appeal I have taken` IS A `s 679(1) kind of appeal` @desc What kind of appeal have you taken: against conviction to the court of appeal, against sentence only to the court of appeal, to the Supreme Court of Canada, or another?
      `I establish that my appeal has sufficient merit that it would cause unnecessary hardship if I were detained in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that your appeal has sufficient merit that, in the circumstances, it would cause unnecessary hardship if you were detained in custody?
      `I establish that I will surrender myself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that you will surrender yourself into custody as the order requires?
      `I establish that my detention is not necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that your detention is not necessary in the public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 679(4), may a judge order that I be released while my appeal against sentence only is decided` IS
    `s 679(4) a judge of the court of appeal may order that the appellant be released pending the determination of the appeal against sentence only` `the kind of appeal I have taken` `I establish that my appeal has sufficient merit that it would cause unnecessary hardship if I were detained in custody` `I establish that I will surrender myself into custody in accordance with the terms of the order` `I establish that my detention is not necessary in the public interest`

-- answers: s 679(5) the judge must make a release order referred to in section 515 that includes a condition that the accused surrender themselves into custody
@export Under section 679(5), if the judge does not refuse my application, must the release order include a condition that I surrender myself into custody?
GIVEN `the judge of the court of appeal does not refuse my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge of the court of appeal not refused your application for release?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 679(5), if the judge does not refuse my application, must the release order include a condition that I surrender myself into custody` IS
    `s 679(5) the judge must make a release order referred to in section 515 that includes a condition that the accused surrender themselves into custody` `the judge of the court of appeal does not refuse my application`

-- answers: s 679(5.1) the person having custody of the appellant must immediately release the appellant
@export Under section 679(5.1), must the person who has custody of me release me immediately if I comply with the release order?
GIVEN `I comply with the release order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you comply with the release order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 679(5.1), must the person who has custody of me release me immediately if I comply with the release order` IS
    `s 679(5.1) the person having custody of the appellant must immediately release the appellant` `I comply with the release order`

-- answers: s 679(7) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person pending the hearing and determination of the reference as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)
@export Under section 679(7), do the release rules of section 679 govern my release or detention while the Minister's reference is heard?
GIVEN `the Minister of Justice has directed or referred my case under section 696.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister of Justice given a direction or made a reference in your case under section 696.3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
