    `s 688(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present applies` `I am in custody and represented by counsel` `the proceeding is of this kind` `the rules of court provide that I am entitled to be present` `the court of appeal or a judge of it has given me leave to be present`

-- answers: s 688(2.1) the court may order that, instead of the appellant appearing in person, the appellant appear by audioconference, videoconference or closed-circuit television
