§§ `Appealing to the Supreme Court of Canada (Part XXI, sections 691 to 696)`
-- Arises once the court of appeal has decided; ask "Has the court of appeal decided your appeal, or the Crown's appeal?" before showing the group.

-- answers: s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction
@export Under section 691(1), may I appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against my conviction that the court of appeal affirmed?
GIVEN `I was convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of an indictable offence?
      `the court of appeal affirmed my conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court of appeal affirm your conviction?
      `my appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissented?
      `my appeal is on a question of law and the Supreme Court of Canada has granted me leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal on a question of law, and has the Supreme Court of Canada granted you leave to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 691(1), may I appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against my conviction that the court of appeal affirmed` IS
    `s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction` `I was convicted of an indictable offence` `the court of appeal affirmed my conviction` `my appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` `my appeal is on a question of law and the Supreme Court of Canada has granted me leave`

-- answers: s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal
@export Under section 691(2), may I appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the court of appeal setting aside my acquittal?
GIVEN `I was acquitted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you acquitted of an indictable offence?
      `my acquittal was by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your acquittal by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder?
      `the court of appeal set aside my acquittal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court of appeal set aside your acquittal?
      `my appeal is on a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal on a question of law?
      `a judge of the court of appeal dissents on the question of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a judge of the court of appeal dissent on the question of law?
      `the Court of Appeal entered a verdict of guilty against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court of Appeal enter a verdict of guilty against you?
      `the Supreme Court of Canada has granted me leave to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Supreme Court of Canada granted you leave to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 691(2), may I appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the court of appeal setting aside my acquittal` IS
    `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` `I was acquitted of an indictable offence` `my acquittal was by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` `the court of appeal set aside my acquittal` `my appeal is on a question of law` `a judge of the court of appeal dissents on the question of law` `the Court of Appeal entered a verdict of guilty against me` `the Supreme Court of Canada has granted me leave to appeal`

-- answers: s 692(1) the person found not criminally responsible may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada
-- RETITLED 2026-11-12 (second audit pass): was "Under section 692(1), may I appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against a verdict that I am not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder?"; route: the body answers two routes (the verdict affirmed on that ground, or a verdict of guilty entered by the court of appeal), the title named the first only and described it as an appeal against the verdict
@export Under section 692(1), having been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, may I appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada because the court of appeal affirmed that verdict or entered a verdict of guilty against me?
GIVEN `I have been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder?
      `the court of appeal affirmed that verdict` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court of appeal affirm that verdict?
      `the court of appeal entered a verdict of guilty against me under subparagraph 686(4)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court of appeal enter a verdict of guilty against you under subparagraph 686(4)(b)(ii)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 692(1), having been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, may I appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada because the court of appeal affirmed that verdict or entered a verdict of guilty against me` IS
    `s 692(1) the person found not criminally responsible may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `I have been found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` `the court of appeal affirmed that verdict` `the court of appeal entered a verdict of guilty against me under subparagraph 686(4)(b)(ii)`

-- answers: s 692(2) the person found unfit to stand trial may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada
