    `s 693(1) the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` `the court of appeal set aside my conviction, or dismissed an appeal the Crown took, under section 675 or paragraph 676(1)(a), (b) or (c) or subsection 676(3)` `the appellant is the Attorney General` `the appeal is on a question of law on which a judge of the court of appeal dissents` `the appeal is on a question of law and leave has been granted`

-- answers: s 694 notice of appeal in writing has been served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act
-- RETITLED 2026-11-12 (second audit pass): was "Under section 694, has notice of appeal in writing been served on the respondent, so that an appeal lies to the Supreme Court of Canada?"; consequence: the section says no appeal lies unless notice is served (a necessary condition), the title read it as service being enough for an appeal to lie
