      `in the opinion of the Court or judge it is desirable in the interests of justice that I have legal assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the opinion of the Court or judge, is it desirable in the interests of justice that you have legal assistance?
      `it appears that I have not sufficient means to obtain legal assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear that you do not have sufficient means to obtain legal assistance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 694.1(1), may the Supreme Court of Canada assign a lawyer to act for me on my appeal to it` IS
    `s 694.1(1) the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge may assign counsel to act on behalf of an accused who is a party to an appeal to the Court` `I am a party to an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada, or to proceedings preliminary or incidental to one` `in the opinion of the Court or judge it is desirable in the interests of justice that I have legal assistance` `it appears that I have not sufficient means to obtain legal assistance`

