§§ `Asking the Minister of Justice to review a conviction (Part XXI.1, sections 696.1 to 696.6) and the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission (Part XXI.2)`
-- Arises only if you think you were wrongly convicted and your appeals are over; ask "Have your appeals ended and do you think you were wrongly convicted?" before showing the group.

-- answers: s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice
-- RETITLED 2026-11-12 (second audit pass): was "Under section 696.1(1), may I apply to the Minister of Justice for a review of my conviction on the grounds of miscarriage of justice?"; scope: the body answers a conviction or a finding as a dangerous offender or long-term offender, the title named only a conviction
