    `s 696.3(4) the decision of the Minister of Justice is final and is not subject to appeal` `the decision was made by the Minister of Justice under subsection 696.3(3)`

-- answers: s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account
@export Under section 696.4, must the Minister of Justice take this matter into account in deciding my application?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 696.4 matter` @desc Which matter: whether the application rests on new matters of significance, the relevance and reliability of the information presented, that an application is not a further appeal and gives an extraordinary remedy, or another?
      `the decision is a decision under subsection 696.3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one the Minister makes under subsection 696.3(3) on your application?
      `the Minister considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister consider the matter relevant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 696.4, must the Minister of Justice take this matter into account in deciding my application` IS
    `s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` `the matter` `the decision is a decision under subsection 696.3(3)` `the Minister considers the matter relevant`

-- answers: s 696.72(a) the Commission's mandate is to review the application
@export Under section 696.72(a), is it the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission's mandate to review my application?
GIVEN `my application was made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice?
      `section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard's Law) has come into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard's Law) come into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 696.72(a), is it the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission's mandate to review my application` IS
    `s 696.72(a) the Commission's mandate is to review the application` `my application was made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice` `section 3 of the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission Act (David and Joyce Milgaard's Law) has come into force`

-- answers: s 696.8 the Commission has ensured that the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada
@export Under section 696.8, has the Commission ensured that I am able to communicate readily with it from where I am in Canada?
GIVEN `I am an applicant or a potential applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant, or someone who may apply?
      `I am able to communicate readily with the Commission from where I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able to communicate readily with the Commission from where you are in Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 696.8, has the Commission ensured that I am able to communicate readily with it from where I am in Canada` IS
    `s 696.8 the Commission has ensured that the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada` `I am an applicant or a potential applicant` `I am able to communicate readily with the Commission from where I am`

-- answers: s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need
@export Under section 696.84(2), is this a support that the Commission provides to applicants in need?
GIVEN `the support` IS A `s 696.84(2) support` @desc Which support: directing you to services in your community, translation and interpretation, help with necessities such as food and housing, help obtaining legal assistance for your application, or another?
      `I am an applicant in need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant in need?
      `I am without means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you without means?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 696.84(2), is this a support that the Commission provides to applicants in need` IS
    `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `the support` `I am an applicant in need` `I am without means`

§ `Criminal Code -- being summoned or arrested to give evidence, and evidence taken outside the courtroom (sections 697 to 715.27)`

§§ `Being required to attend as a witness: subpoena and warrant (Part XXII, sections 697 to 703.2)`
-- Arises if you may be a witness in someone else's case; ask "Has anyone told you that you may have to give evidence?" before showing the group.

-- answers: s 698(1) a subpoena may be issued in accordance with Part XXII requiring the person to attend to give evidence
@export Under section 698(1), may a subpoena be issued requiring me to attend to give evidence?
GIVEN `I am likely to give material evidence in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you likely to give material evidence in a proceeding under the Criminal Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 698(1), may a subpoena be issued requiring me to attend to give evidence` IS
    `s 698(1) a subpoena may be issued in accordance with Part XXII requiring the person to attend to give evidence` `I am likely to give material evidence in a proceeding`

-- answers: s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence
@export Under section 698(2), may a warrant in Form 17 be issued to have me arrested and brought to give evidence?
GIVEN `I am likely to give material evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you likely to give material evidence?
      `it is made to appear that I will not attend in response to a subpoena if one is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been made to appear that you will not attend if a subpoena is issued?
      `it is made to appear that I am evading service of a subpoena` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been made to appear that you are evading service of a subpoena?
      `the court, justice or provincial court judge has power to issue a subpoena requiring my attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court, justice or provincial court judge asked to issue the warrant have power to issue a subpoena requiring your attendance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 698(2), may a warrant in Form 17 be issued to have me arrested and brought to give evidence` IS
    `s 698(2) a court, justice or provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 17 to cause the person to be arrested and to be brought to give evidence` `I am likely to give material evidence` `it is made to appear that I will not attend in response to a subpoena if one is issued` `it is made to appear that I am evading service of a subpoena` `the court, justice or provincial court judge has power to issue a subpoena requiring my attendance`

-- answers: s 698(3) the bar on issuing a warrant in Form 17 applies
@export Under section 698(3), is a warrant in Form 17 barred against me because no subpoena was first issued to me?
GIVEN `a warrant in Form 17 is to be issued for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a warrant in Form 17 about to be issued for you?
      `it is made to appear that I will not attend in response to a subpoena (paragraph 698(2)(a))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been made to appear that you will not attend in response to a subpoena if one is issued?
      `a subpoena has first been issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a subpoena issued to you first?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 698(3), is a warrant in Form 17 barred against me because no subpoena was first issued to me` IS
    `s 698(3) the bar on issuing a warrant in Form 17 applies` `it is made to appear that I will not attend in response to a subpoena (paragraph 698(2)(a))` `a subpoena has first been issued to me` `a warrant in Form 17 is to be issued for me`

-- answers: s 700(2) the person must attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings
@export Under section 700(2), must I attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings after I am served with a subpoena?
GIVEN `I am served with a subpoena issued under Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been served with a subpoena issued under Part XXII?
      `I am excused by the presiding judge, justice or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been excused by the presiding judge, justice or provincial court judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 700(2), must I attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings after I am served with a subpoena` IS
    `s 700(2) the person must attend and remain in attendance throughout the proceedings` `I am served with a subpoena issued under Part XXII` `I am excused by the presiding judge, justice or provincial court judge`

-- answers: s 701(2) the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed
-- RETITLED 2026-11-12 (second audit pass): was "Under section 701(2), must a subpoena issued to me from a superior court for an out-of-province witness be served on me personally?"; modal: the body tests whether the subpoena has been served personally (JUST TRUE when it has, NOTHING otherwise), the title asked whether it must be
@export Under section 701(2), has the subpoena issued to me under paragraph 699(2)(b) been served on me personally?
GIVEN `the subpoena was issued under paragraph 699(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the subpoena issued under paragraph 699(2)(b) (to a person outside the province where the proceedings began)?
      `the subpoena has been served personally on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the subpoena been served on you personally?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 701(2), has the subpoena issued to me under paragraph 699(2)(b) been served on me personally` IS
    `s 701(2) the subpoena has been served personally on the person to whom it is directed` `the subpoena was issued under paragraph 699(2)(b)` `the subpoena has been served personally on me`

-- answers: s 702(1) the subpoena has effect anywhere in Canada according to its terms
-- RETITLED 2026-11-12 (second audit pass): was "Under section 702(1), does a subpoena issued to me by a provincial court judge or a superior court have effect anywhere in Canada?"; scope: the body answers four kinds of issuing court as well as a provincial court judge, the title named a provincial court judge and a superior court only
@export Under section 702(1), does a subpoena issued to me by a provincial court judge, or out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction, have effect anywhere in Canada?
GIVEN `the subpoena was issued by a provincial court judge or out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the subpoena issued by a provincial court judge, or out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 702(1), does a subpoena issued to me by a provincial court judge, or out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction, have effect anywhere in Canada` IS
    `s 702(1) the subpoena has effect anywhere in Canada according to its terms` `the subpoena was issued by a provincial court judge or out of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, a court of appeal, an appeal court or a court of criminal jurisdiction`

§§ `Being arrested or held as a witness (Part XXII, sections 704 to 708.1)`
-- Arises only if you have been served with a subpoena, bound by a recognizance, or arrested as a witness; ask "Have you been served, bound or arrested to give evidence?" before showing the group.

-- answers: s 704(3) the person is entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued
@export Under section 704(3), am I entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for my arrest was issued?
GIVEN `I was arrested under section 704` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you arrested under section 704 (a witness warrant for a person bound by recognizance who is about to abscond or has absconded)?
      `I have requested a copy of the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked for a copy of the information on which the warrant for your arrest was issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 704(3), am I entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for my arrest was issued` IS
    `s 704(3) the person is entitled to receive a copy of the information on which the warrant for the arrest was issued` `I was arrested under section 704` `I have requested a copy of the information`

-- answers: s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person
@export Under section 705(1), may a warrant in Form 17 be issued for my arrest because I did not attend or remain in attendance after being served?
GIVEN `I was served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding?
      `I did not attend or remain in attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not attend, or not remain in attendance?
      `it is established that the subpoena was served on me in accordance with Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it established that the subpoena was served on you in accordance with Part XXII?
      `it is established that I am likely to give material evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it established that you are likely to give material evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 705(1), may a warrant in Form 17 be issued for my arrest because I did not attend or remain in attendance after being served` IS
    `s 705(1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was required to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` `I was served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding` `I did not attend or remain in attendance` `it is established that the subpoena was served on me in accordance with Part XXII` `it is established that I am likely to give material evidence`

-- answers: s 705(2) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was bound to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person
@export Under section 705(2), may a warrant in Form 17 be issued for my arrest because I did not attend, though bound by a recognizance?
GIVEN `I was bound by a recognizance to attend to give evidence in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you bound by a recognizance to attend to give evidence in a proceeding?
      `I did not attend or did not remain in attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not attend, or not remain in attendance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 705(2), may a warrant in Form 17 be issued for my arrest because I did not attend, though bound by a recognizance` IS
    `s 705(2) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge before whom the person was bound to attend may issue a warrant in Form 17 for the arrest of the person` `I was bound by a recognizance to attend to give evidence in a proceeding` `I did not attend or did not remain in attendance`

-- answers: s 705(4) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may, by an endorsement on the warrant in Form 29.1, authorize the release of the person on an undertaking with conditions
@export Under section 705(4), may the court that issued the warrant endorse it to authorize my release on an undertaking?
GIVEN `the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge issues a warrant for me under section 705` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge issued a warrant for you under section 705?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 705(4), may the court that issued the warrant endorse it to authorize my release on an undertaking` IS
    `s 705(4) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may, by an endorsement on the warrant in Form 29.1, authorize the release of the person on an undertaking with conditions` `the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge issues a warrant for me under section 705`

-- answers: s 705(6) the person may apply to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge to vary the undertaking
@export Under section 705(6), may I apply to vary the undertaking on which I was released?
GIVEN `I am the person the warrant under subsection 705(1) or (2) was issued for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the warrant under subsection 705(1) or (2) the one issued for you?
      `I have been released on an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released on an undertaking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 705(6), may I apply to vary the undertaking on which I was released` IS
    `s 705(6) the person may apply to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge to vary the undertaking` `I am the person the warrant under subsection 705(1) or (2) was issued for` `I have been released on an undertaking`

-- answers: s 705.1(1) a peace officer may release the person
@export Under section 705.1(1), may a peace officer release me if I give an undertaking in Form 10.1?
GIVEN `I was arrested by a peace officer under a warrant issued under subsection 705(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you arrested by a peace officer under a warrant issued under subsection 705(1) or (2)?
      `the warrant has been endorsed under subsection 705(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the warrant been endorsed under subsection 705(4)?
      `I give an undertaking in Form 10.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you give an undertaking in Form 10.1?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 705.1(1), may a peace officer release me if I give an undertaking in Form 10.1` IS
    `s 705.1(1) a peace officer may release the person` `I was arrested by a peace officer under a warrant issued under subsection 705(1) or (2)` `the warrant has been endorsed under subsection 705(4)` `I give an undertaking in Form 10.1`

-- answers: s 705.1(6) the lack of the person's signature invalidates the undertaking
@export Under section 705.1(6), does my failure or refusal to sign my undertaking invalidate it?
GIVEN `I fail or refuse to sign the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail or refuse to sign the undertaking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 705.1(6), does my failure or refusal to sign my undertaking invalidate it` IS
    `s 705.1(6) the lack of the person's signature invalidates the undertaking` `I fail or refuse to sign the undertaking`

-- answers: s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect
@export Under section 705.1(7), do the conditions of my undertaking remain in effect?
GIVEN `I gave an undertaking under section 705.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give an undertaking under section 705.1?
      `the conditions have been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the conditions been cancelled?
      `the conditions have been changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the conditions been changed?
      `I have appeared and remained in attendance at the proceeding as the mandatory condition requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you appeared and remained in attendance at the proceeding as the mandatory condition requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 705.1(7), do the conditions of my undertaking remain in effect` IS
    `s 705.1(7) the conditions with respect to the undertaking remain in effect` `I gave an undertaking under section 705.1` `the conditions have been cancelled` `the conditions have been changed` `I have appeared and remained in attendance at the proceeding as the mandatory condition requires`

-- answers: s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order
@export Under section 706, may the court order that I be detained in custody or released on recognizance so that I will appear and give evidence?
GIVEN `the order` IS A `s 706 order` @desc Which order: that you be detained in custody, released on recognizance with sureties, released on recognizance without sureties, or another?
      `I was brought before the court under a warrant issued under subsection 698(2) or section 704 or 705` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you brought before the court under a warrant issued under subsection 698(2) or section 704 or 705?
      `the order is made so that I will appear and give evidence when required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made so that you will appear and give evidence when required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 706, may the court order that I be detained in custody or released on recognizance so that I will appear and give evidence` IS
    `s 706 the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may make the order` `the order` `I was brought before the court under a warrant issued under subsection 698(2) or section 704 or 705` `the order is made so that I will appear and give evidence when required`

-- answers: s 707(1) the bar on detaining a witness for more than thirty days applies
@export Under section 707(1), does the bar on holding me as a witness for more than thirty days apply to my detention?
GIVEN `I am detained in custody for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence as a witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in custody only so that you will appear and give evidence as a witness?
      `the number of days I have been detained` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days have you been detained?
      `I was brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the province where I am detained, before the thirty days expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you brought, before the thirty days expired, before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the province where you are detained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 707(1), does the bar on holding me as a witness for more than thirty days apply to my detention` IS
    `s 707(1) the bar on detaining a witness for more than thirty days applies` `I am detained in custody for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence as a witness` `the number of days I have been detained` `I was brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction in the province where I am detained, before the thirty days expired`

-- answers: s 707(2) the judge must fix a time before the expiration of the thirty days for the hearing of the application and cause notice of it to be given, and the person having custody of the witness must cause the witness to be brought before a judge
@export Under section 707(2), if I apply to be brought before a judge, must the judge fix a hearing time and must the person holding me bring me?
GIVEN `I am detained in custody as a witness as described in subsection 707(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained in custody for the purpose only of appearing and giving evidence as a witness?
      `I applied to be brought before a judge before the thirty days expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply, before the thirty days expired, to be brought before a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 707(2), if I apply to be brought before a judge, must the judge fix a hearing time and must the person holding me bring me` IS
    `s 707(2) the judge must fix a time before the expiration of the thirty days for the hearing of the application and cause notice of it to be given, and the person having custody of the witness must cause the witness to be brought before a judge` `I am detained in custody as a witness as described in subsection 707(1)` `I applied to be brought before a judge before the thirty days expired`

-- answers: s 707(3) the judge must order the witness to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties
@export Under section 707(3), must the judge discharge me or release me on recognizance if the judge is not satisfied that my continued detention is justified?
GIVEN `I am brought before a judge under section 707` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been brought before a judge under section 707?
      `the judge is not satisfied that my continued detention is justified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge not satisfied that your continued detention is justified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 707(3), must the judge discharge me or release me on recognizance if the judge is not satisfied that my continued detention is justified` IS
    `s 707(3) the judge must order the witness to be discharged or to be released on recognizance, with or without sureties` `I am brought before a judge under section 707` `the judge is not satisfied that my continued detention is justified`

-- answers: s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness
@export Under section 707(3), may the judge order my continued detention as a witness?
GIVEN `I am brought before a judge under section 707` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been brought before a judge under section 707?
      `the judge is satisfied that my continued detention is justified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge satisfied that your continued detention is justified?
      `the total number of days I would have been detained, from the time I was first detained, if the detention is continued` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting from the day you were first detained, how many days in total would you have been detained if the detention is continued?
      `I have done what is required of me under section 550, or the trial has ended, or I have appeared and given evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you done what section 550 requires of you, has the trial ended, or have you appeared and given your evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 707(3), may the judge order my continued detention as a witness` IS
    `s 707(3) the judge may order the continued detention of the witness` `I am brought before a judge under section 707` `the judge is satisfied that my continued detention is justified` `the total number of days I would have been detained, from the time I was first detained, if the detention is continued` `I have done what is required of me under section 550, or the trial has ended, or I have appeared and given evidence`

-- answers: s 708(1) the person is guilty of contempt of court
@export Under section 708(1), am I guilty of contempt of court for failing to attend or remain in attendance to give evidence?
GIVEN `I am required by law to attend or remain in attendance to give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required by law to attend, or remain in attendance, for the purpose of giving evidence?
      `I failed to attend or remain in attendance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to attend, or fail to remain in attendance?
      `I have a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 708(1), am I guilty of contempt of court for failing to attend or remain in attendance to give evidence` IS
    `s 708(1) the person is guilty of contempt of court` `I am required by law to attend or remain in attendance to give evidence` `I failed to attend or remain in attendance` `I have a lawful excuse`

-- answers: s 708(2) a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may deal summarily with the person
@export Under section 708(2), may the court deal with me summarily for contempt of court?
GIVEN `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found guilty of contempt of court under section 708?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 708(2), may the court deal with me summarily for contempt of court` IS
    `s 708(2) a court, judge, justice or provincial court judge may deal summarily with the person` `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708`

-- answers: s 708(2) the greatest fine the person is liable to
@export Under section 708(2), what is the greatest fine I am liable to for contempt of court?
GIVEN `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found guilty of contempt of court under section 708?
GIVETH A MAYBE Fine
DECIDE `Under section 708(2), what is the greatest fine I am liable to for contempt of court` IS
    `s 708(2) the greatest fine the person is liable to` `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708`

-- answers: s 708(2) the longest imprisonment the person is liable to
@export Under section 708(2), what is the longest imprisonment I am liable to for contempt of court?
GIVEN `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found guilty of contempt of court under section 708?
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
DECIDE `Under section 708(2), what is the longest imprisonment I am liable to for contempt of court` IS
    `s 708(2) the longest imprisonment the person is liable to` `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708`

-- answers: s 708(2) the person may be ordered to pay the costs that are incident to the service of any process under Part XXII and to the person's detention, if any
@export Under section 708(2), may I be ordered to pay the costs of serving process and of my detention?
GIVEN `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found guilty of contempt of court under section 708?
      `the costs are incident to the service of process under Part XXII or to my detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs incident to the service of any process under Part XXII, or to your detention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 708(2), may I be ordered to pay the costs of serving process and of my detention` IS
    `s 708(2) the person may be ordered to pay the costs that are incident to the service of any process under Part XXII and to the person's detention, if any` `I am guilty of contempt of court under section 708` `the costs are incident to the service of process under Part XXII or to my detention`

-- answers: s 708.1 the copy has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of the Criminal Code
@export Under section 708.1, does a faxed or otherwise telecommunicated copy of my summons, warrant or subpoena have the same probative force as the original?
GIVEN `the copy is a copy of a summons, warrant or subpoena` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a copy of a summons, a warrant or a subpoena?
      `the copy was transmitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the copy transmitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing (for example, a fax)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 708.1, does a faxed or otherwise telecommunicated copy of my summons, warrant or subpoena have the same probative force as the original` IS
    `s 708.1 the copy has the same probative force as the original for the purposes of the Criminal Code` `the copy is a copy of a summons, warrant or subpoena` `the copy was transmitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`

§ `Evidence taken away from the trial: commission, video link, earlier evidence and video recordings (Part XXII, sections 709 to 715.2)`

§§ `Evidence on commission (sections 709 to 714)`
-- Arises when a witness cannot attend the trial or is outside Canada.

-- answers: s 709(1) the party may apply for an order appointing a commissioner to take the evidence of the witness
@export Under section 709(1), may I apply for an order appointing a commissioner to take the evidence of a witness who cannot attend my trial?
GIVEN `I am a party to the proceedings by way of indictment or summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the proceedings (by indictment or on summary conviction)?
      `the witness is not likely to be able to attend at the time of the trial, by reason of illness or any other good and sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the witness unlikely to be able to attend at the time of the trial, by reason of physical disability from illness or any other good and sufficient cause?
      `the witness is out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the witness out of Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 709(1), may I apply for an order appointing a commissioner to take the evidence of a witness who cannot attend my trial` IS
    `s 709(1) the party may apply for an order appointing a commissioner to take the evidence of the witness` `I am a party to the proceedings by way of indictment or summary conviction` `the witness is not likely to be able to attend at the time of the trial, by reason of illness or any other good and sufficient cause` `the witness is out of Canada`

-- answers: s 711 the evidence may be admitted in evidence in the proceedings
-- RETITLED 2026-11-12 (second audit pass): was "Under section 711, may a witness's evidence taken by a commissioner be admitted in evidence at my trial?"; route: the body answers only the witness mentioned in paragraph 709(1)(a) whose evidence a commissioner took under section 710, and answers JUST FALSE for any other route (a witness out of Canada is paragraph 709(1)(b), which this function does not answer); the title asked about any witness's commission evidence
@export Under section 711, may the evidence of a witness who cannot attend my trial through illness or other good and sufficient cause, taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710, be admitted in evidence?
GIVEN `the evidence of a witness unable to attend was taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the evidence of the witness taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710?
      `it is proved by oral evidence or affidavit that the witness is unable to attend by reason of death, illness or other good and sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved, by oral evidence or by affidavit, that the witness is unable to attend by reason of death, illness or some other good and sufficient cause?
      `the transcript of the evidence is signed by the commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transcript signed by the commissioner by or before whom it was taken?
      `it is proved to the court that reasonable notice was given and that the accused or the prosecutor had or might have had full opportunity to cross-examine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved to the court that reasonable notice of the time for taking the evidence was given to the other party, and that you or your counsel, or the prosecutor or counsel, had or might have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 711, may the evidence of a witness who cannot attend my trial through illness or other good and sufficient cause, taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710, be admitted in evidence` IS
    `s 711 the evidence may be admitted in evidence in the proceedings` `the evidence of a witness unable to attend was taken by a commissioner appointed under section 710` `it is proved by oral evidence or affidavit that the witness is unable to attend by reason of death, illness or other good and sufficient cause` `the transcript of the evidence is signed by the commissioner` `it is proved to the court that reasonable notice was given and that the accused or the prosecutor had or might have had full opportunity to cross-examine`

-- answers: s 713(1) the failure of the accused to be present or represented prevents the admission of the evidence in the proceedings
@export Under section 713(1), does my failure to be present or represented when the commission evidence was taken prevent its admission?
GIVEN `I failed to be present or to be represented by counsel as the order provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to be present, or to be represented by counsel, as the order provided?
      `the evidence was otherwise taken in accordance with the order and with Part XXII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the evidence otherwise taken in accordance with the order and with Part XXII?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 713(1), does my failure to be present or represented when the commission evidence was taken prevent its admission` IS
    `s 713(1) the failure of the accused to be present or represented prevents the admission of the evidence in the proceedings` `I failed to be present or to be represented by counsel as the order provided` `the evidence was otherwise taken in accordance with the order and with Part XXII`

-- answers: s 714.1 the court may order that the witness give evidence by audioconference or videoconference
@export Under section 714.1, may the court order that a witness in Canada give evidence by audioconference or videoconference?
GIVEN `the witness is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the witness in Canada?
      `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of the opinion that it would be appropriate, having regard to all the circumstances (the witness's location, the cost, the nature of the evidence, the suitability of the place, the accused's right to a fair and public hearing, the seriousness of the offence, and any prejudice to the parties)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 714.1, may the court order that a witness in Canada give evidence by audioconference or videoconference` IS
    `s 714.1 the court may order that the witness give evidence by audioconference or videoconference` `the witness is in Canada` `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances`

-- answers: s 714.2(1) the court shall receive the evidence given by the witness by videoconference
@export Under section 714.2(1), must the court receive the evidence of a witness outside Canada by videoconference?
GIVEN `the witness is outside Canada and gives evidence by videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the witness give evidence by videoconference from outside Canada?
      `a party satisfies the court that reception would be contrary to the principles of fundamental justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a party satisfied the court that receiving the testimony would be contrary to the principles of fundamental justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 714.2(1), must the court receive the evidence of a witness outside Canada by videoconference` IS
    `s 714.2(1) the court shall receive the evidence given by the witness by videoconference` `the witness is outside Canada and gives evidence by videoconference` `a party satisfies the court that reception would be contrary to the principles of fundamental justice`

-- answers: s 714.2(2) the party gave the notice in time
@export Under section 714.2(2), did the party who wants to call a witness outside Canada by videoconference give notice in time?
GIVEN `the party wishes to call a witness to give evidence by videoconference from outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a party wish to call a witness to give evidence by videoconference from outside Canada?
      `the party has given notice to the court and the other parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the party given notice to the court and the other parties of that intention?
      `the number of days before the witness is scheduled to testify at which the notice was or would be given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before the witness is scheduled to testify was the notice given (or would it be given)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 714.2(2), did the party who wants to call a witness outside Canada by videoconference give notice in time` IS
    `s 714.2(2) the party gave the notice in time` `the party wishes to call a witness to give evidence by videoconference from outside Canada` `the party has given notice to the court and the other parties` `the number of days before the witness is scheduled to testify at which the notice was or would be given`

-- answers: s 714.6 the evidence is deemed to be given in Canada, and given under oath or affirmation in accordance with Canadian law, for the purposes of the laws relating to evidence, procedure, perjury and contempt of court
