§§ `Evidence previously taken and video-recorded evidence (sections 715 to 715.2)`
-- Arises when earlier testimony or a video statement may be used at your trial.

-- answers: s 715(1) the evidence may be admitted as evidence in the proceedings without further proof
@export Under section 715(1), may evidence given at an earlier trial or at the preliminary inquiry be admitted at my trial without further proof?
GIVEN `at my trial, a person gave evidence at a previous trial on the same charge or evidence was taken at the investigation or preliminary inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At your trial, did a person give evidence at a previous trial on the same charge, or was that person's evidence taken in the investigation of the charge or at the preliminary inquiry?
      `the person refuses to be sworn or to give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person refuse to be sworn or to give evidence?
      `facts are proved on oath that the person is dead, insane, too ill to travel or testify, or absent from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are facts proved on oath from which it can reasonably be inferred that the person is dead, has become insane, is so ill that the person cannot travel or testify, or is absent from Canada?
      `it is proved that the evidence was taken in my presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the evidence was taken in your presence?
      `I prove that I did not have full opportunity to cross-examine the witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you did not have full opportunity to cross-examine the witness?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715(1), may evidence given at an earlier trial or at the preliminary inquiry be admitted at my trial without further proof` IS
    `s 715(1) the evidence may be admitted as evidence in the proceedings without further proof` `at my trial, a person gave evidence at a previous trial on the same charge or evidence was taken at the investigation or preliminary inquiry` `the person refuses to be sworn or to give evidence` `facts are proved on oath that the person is dead, insane, too ill to travel or testify, or absent from Canada` `it is proved that the evidence was taken in my presence` `I prove that I did not have full opportunity to cross-examine the witness`

-- answers: s 715(3) the accused is deemed to have been present during the taking of the evidence and to have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness
@export Under section 715(3), am I deemed to have been present and to have had full opportunity to cross-examine, because I absconded?
GIVEN `evidence was taken at a previous trial or other proceeding in my absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was evidence taken at a previous trial or preliminary hearing or other proceeding against you in your absence?
      `I was absent by reason of having absconded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you absent because you had absconded?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715(3), am I deemed to have been present and to have had full opportunity to cross-examine, because I absconded` IS
    `s 715(3) the accused is deemed to have been present during the taking of the evidence and to have had full opportunity to cross-examine the witness` `evidence was taken at a previous trial or other proceeding in my absence` `I was absent by reason of having absconded`

-- answers: s 715(4) subsections 715(1) to (3) apply to the evidence
@export Under section 715(4), do subsections 715(1) to (3) apply to evidence received under subsection 540(7)?
GIVEN `the evidence was received under subsection 540(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the evidence received under subsection 540(7) (a preliminary inquiry, by a justice, of a witness's credible and trustworthy evidence)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715(4), do subsections 715(1) to (3) apply to evidence received under subsection 540(7)` IS
    `s 715(4) subsections 715(1) to (3) apply to the evidence` `the evidence was received under subsection 540(7)`

-- answers: s 715.01(1) the transcript of testimony given by a police officer in the presence of the accused during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry may be received in evidence at the trial
@export Under section 715.01(1), may a transcript of a police officer's testimony from a voir dire or preliminary inquiry be received at my trial?
GIVEN `the testimony was given by a police officer, as section 183 defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the testimony given by a police officer as defined in section 183?
      `the testimony was given in my presence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given in your presence?
      `the testimony was given during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry held in relation to my trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry held in relation to your trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.01(1), may a transcript of a police officer's testimony from a voir dire or preliminary inquiry be received at my trial` IS
    `s 715.01(1) the transcript of testimony given by a police officer in the presence of the accused during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry may be received in evidence at the trial` `the testimony was given by a police officer, as section 183 defines the term` `the testimony was given in my presence` `the testimony was given during a voir dire or preliminary inquiry held in relation to my trial`

-- answers: s 715.01(2) the bar on receiving the transcript in evidence applies
@export Under section 715.01(2), is the transcript barred from being received because no notice and copy were given to me?
GIVEN `the transcript is one referred to in subsection 715.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transcript one of a police officer's testimony under subsection 715.01(1)?
      `the party producing the transcript gave me reasonable notice and a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the party who wants to produce the transcript give you reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the transcript?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.01(2), is the transcript barred from being received because no notice and copy were given to me` IS
    `s 715.01(2) the bar on receiving the transcript in evidence applies` `the transcript is one referred to in subsection 715.01(1)` `the party producing the transcript gave me reasonable notice and a copy`

-- answers: s 715.01(6) section 715.01 applies to the evidence
@export Under section 715.01(6), does section 715.01 apply to evidence received under subsection 540(7)?
GIVEN `the evidence was received under subsection 540(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the evidence received under subsection 540(7)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.01(6), does section 715.01 apply to evidence received under subsection 540(7)` IS
    `s 715.01(6) section 715.01 applies to the evidence` `the evidence was received under subsection 540(7)`

-- answers: s 715.1(1) the video recording is admissible in evidence
@export Under section 715.1(1), is a video recording of a victim or witness under 18 admissible in evidence at my trial?
GIVEN `the proceeding is against me and a victim or other witness was under 18 when the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding against you, and was a victim or other witness under 18 when the offence is alleged to have been committed?
      `the recording was made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence and the victim or witness describes the acts in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a video recording made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence, in which the victim or witness describes the acts complained of?
      `the victim or witness adopts the contents of the recording while testifying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the victim or witness, while testifying, adopt the contents of the recording?
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that admitting it would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the presiding judge or justice of the opinion that admitting the recording would interfere with the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.1(1), is a video recording of a victim or witness under 18 admissible in evidence at my trial` IS
    `s 715.1(1) the video recording is admissible in evidence` `the proceeding is against me and a victim or other witness was under 18 when the offence is alleged to have been committed` `the recording was made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence and the victim or witness describes the acts in it` `the victim or witness adopts the contents of the recording while testifying` `the judge or justice is of the opinion that admitting it would interfere with the proper administration of justice`

-- answers: s 715.2(1) the video recording is admissible in evidence
@export Under section 715.2(1), is a video recording of a victim or witness with a disability admissible in evidence at my trial?
GIVEN `the proceeding is against me and a victim or other witness can communicate evidence but may have difficulty by reason of a mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding against you, and can a victim or other witness communicate evidence but may have difficulty doing so by reason of a mental or physical disability?
      `the recording was made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence and the victim or witness describes the acts in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a video recording made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence, in which the victim or witness describes the acts complained of?
      `the victim or witness adopts the contents of the recording while testifying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the victim or witness, while testifying, adopt the contents of the recording?
      `the judge or justice is of the opinion that admitting it would interfere with the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the presiding judge or justice of the opinion that admitting the recording would interfere with the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.2(1), is a video recording of a victim or witness with a disability admissible in evidence at my trial` IS
    `s 715.2(1) the video recording is admissible in evidence` `the proceeding is against me and a victim or other witness can communicate evidence but may have difficulty by reason of a mental or physical disability` `the recording was made within a reasonable time after the alleged offence and the victim or witness describes the acts in it` `the victim or witness adopts the contents of the recording while testifying` `the judge or justice is of the opinion that admitting it would interfere with the proper administration of justice`

