GIVEN `I appear by audioconference or videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appear by audioconference or videoconference?
      `I am represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you represented by counsel?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.243, must I be given the opportunity to communicate privately with my counsel while I appear remotely` IS
    `s 715.243 the accused or offender must be given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel` `I appear by audioconference or videoconference` `I am represented by counsel`

-- answers: s 715.27(2) the court may allow or require prospective jurors to participate in the jury selection process by videoconference
@export Under section 715.27(2), may the court allow or require prospective jurors to take part in jury selection by videoconference in my trial?
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor consent?
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent?
      `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of the opinion that it would be appropriate, having regard to all the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.27(2), may the court allow or require prospective jurors to take part in jury selection by videoconference in my trial` IS
    `s 715.27(2) the court may allow or require prospective jurors to participate in the jury selection process by videoconference` `the prosecutor consents` `I consent` `the court is of the opinion that it would be appropriate having regard to all the circumstances`

-- answers: s 715.27(3) the limitation on requiring prospective jurors to participate by videoconference is met
@export Under section 715.27(3), is the limit on requiring prospective jurors to take part by videoconference met in my trial?
GIVEN `the court has approved a location that will be provided for their participation, where the technology for videoconferencing is available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court approved a location that will be provided for their participation where the technology for videoconferencing is available?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.27(3), is the limit on requiring prospective jurors to take part by videoconference met in my trial` IS
    `s 715.27(3) the limitation on requiring prospective jurors to participate by videoconference is met` `the court has approved a location that will be provided for their participation, where the technology for videoconferencing is available`

-- answers: s 715.27(4) the court shall give prospective jurors the option to participate in person
@export Under section 715.27(4), must the court give prospective jurors the option to participate in person in my trial?
GIVEN `the court allows prospective jurors to participate by videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court allow prospective jurors to participate by videoconference?
      `no location approved by the court is provided for their participation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no location approved by the court provided for their participation by those means?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.27(4), must the court give prospective jurors the option to participate in person in my trial` IS
    `s 715.27(4) the court shall give prospective jurors the option to participate in person` `the court allows prospective jurors to participate by videoconference` `no location approved by the court is provided for their participation`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc25 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc25-seat.l4 -- the seat layer over Part XXII.1 (Remediation Agreements) and Part XXII.2 (Alternative Measures and Restorative Justice Processes) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: sections 715.3 to 715.6.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code. For Part XXII.1 the person is an organization that is accused of an offence listed in the schedule to that Part,
-- because remediation agreements are made only with organizations; for Part XXII.2 the person is any person alleged to have committed an offence.
-- This layer puts the questions that person would ask over the rules already encoded in the three layer-1 modules imported above. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds
-- the inputs its layer-1 function wants from plain answers and calls the function.
--
-- HOW AN ANSWER READS. JUST TRUE: yes, on these facts. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words on these facts. NOTHING: the text does not answer on these facts (not "no").
-- A question that asks "must", "may" or "is barred" answers the direction of its own title: JUST TRUE for "yes, must" or "yes, barred".
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Facts the Code leaves to a person other than the one asking (what the prosecutor is of the opinion, whether the court is satisfied, whether the Attorney General consented) are asked as plain yes-or-no facts.
-- The answers of other sections are taken as plain facts too: whether the offence is listed in the schedule to Part XXII.1, whether a person is a victim as section 2 defines it, whether a person is one of those section 2.2 names.
-- A "yes" or "no" the person gives is passed on as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE. For the question "is the third party one of the persons section 2.2 names", a "no" is passed on as NOTHING, never as JUST FALSE,
-- because section 2.2 itself answers NOTHING outside the persons it names.
-- Section 715.55(1) uses the core's Party list to say who the person is; "police officer" in sections 715.47 and 715.57 is read as a peace officer (fork F6). No seat for an official: sections that bind only a court or a prosecutor appear here
-- only for what they mean to the accused (must the prosecutor notify us, is the proceeding stayed, may the charge be dismissed).

§ `Part XXII.1 Remediation Agreements -- the questions an organization accused of an offence would ask`

-- s 715.3(1).
@export Under section 715.3(1), is my body an organization for the purposes of Part XXII.1 (remediation agreements)?
GIVEN `the kind of body my organization is` IS A `s 2 organization: the kind of body` @desc What kind of body is the organization that is charged? (choose the closest)
      `it was created for a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your organization created for a common purpose?
      `it has an operational structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your organization have an operational structure?
      `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your organization hold itself out to the public as an association of persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.3(1), is my body an organization for the purposes of Part XXII.1 (remediation agreements)` IS
    `s 715.3(1) organization` (`s 2 organization` `the kind of body my organization is` `it was created for a common purpose` `it has an operational structure` `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a public body`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a trade union`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a municipality`)

-- s 715.3(1).
@export Under section 715.3(1), is this agreement a remediation agreement?
GIVEN `it is an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an agreement?
      `the kind of body my organization is` IS A `s 2 organization: the kind of body` @desc What kind of body is the organization that is charged? (choose the closest)
      `it was created for a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your organization created for a common purpose?
      `it has an operational structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your organization have an operational structure?
      `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your organization hold itself out to the public as an association of persons?
      `my organization is accused of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your organization accused of having committed the offence?
      `the offence is listed in the schedule to Part XXII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence listed in the schedule to Part XXII.1?
      `the other party is a prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other party to the agreement a prosecutor?
      `the agreement is to stay any proceedings related to that offence if my organization complies with its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement to stay any proceedings related to the offence if your organization complies with its terms?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.3(1), is this agreement a remediation agreement` IS
    `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` `it is an agreement` (`s 715.3(1) organization` (`s 2 organization` `the kind of body my organization is` `it was created for a common purpose` `it has an operational structure` `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a public body`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a trade union`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a municipality`)) `my organization is accused of having committed the offence` (JUST `the offence is listed in the schedule to Part XXII.1`) `the other party is a prosecutor` `the agreement is to stay any proceedings related to that offence if my organization complies with its terms`

-- s 715.3(1).
@export Under section 715.3(1), is this person a victim for the purposes of Part XXII.1?
GIVEN `the person is a victim within section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a victim as section 2 defines it?
      `the offence is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act?
      `the person is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person outside Canada?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.3(1), is this person a victim for the purposes of Part XXII.1` IS
    `s 715.3(1) victim` (JUST `the person is a victim within section 2`) `the offence is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` `the person is outside Canada`

-- s 715.3(2).
@export Under section 715.3(2), may a third party who is not one of the persons named in section 2.2 act on the victim’s behalf?
GIVEN `the third party is one of the persons named in section 2.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third party one of the persons section 2.2 names (for example a relative of a victim who has died)?
      `the court has authorized the third party to act on the victim’s behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court authorized the third party to act on the victim’s behalf?
      `the victim requests that the third party act on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the victim asked that the third party act on their behalf?
      `the prosecutor deems it appropriate that the third party act on the victim’s behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor consider it appropriate that the third party act on the victim’s behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.3(2), may a third party who is not one of the persons named in section 2.2 act on the victim’s behalf` IS
    `s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` (IF `the third party is one of the persons named in section 2.2` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) `the court has authorized the third party to act on the victim’s behalf` `the victim requests that the third party act on their behalf` `the prosecutor deems it appropriate that the third party act on the victim’s behalf`

-- s 715.32(1).
@export Under section 715.32(1), may the prosecutor enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement with my organization?
GIVEN `the kind of body my organization is` IS A `s 2 organization: the kind of body` @desc What kind of body is the organization that is charged? (choose the closest)
      `it was created for a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your organization created for a common purpose?
      `it has an operational structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your organization have an operational structure?
      `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your organization hold itself out to the public as an association of persons?
      `my organization is alleged to have committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your organization alleged to have committed the offence?
      `the offence is listed in the schedule to Part XXII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence listed in the schedule to Part XXII.1?
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that there is a reasonable prospect of conviction with respect to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor hold the opinion that there is a reasonable prospect of conviction with respect to the offence?
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission did not cause and was not likely to have caused serious bodily harm or death, or injury to national defence or national security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor hold the opinion that the act or omission did not cause, and was not likely to have caused, serious bodily harm or death, or injury to national defence or national security?
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission was not committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization or terrorist group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor hold the opinion that the act or omission was not committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization or terrorist group?
      `the prosecutor is of the opinion that negotiating the agreement is in the public interest and appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor hold the opinion that negotiating the agreement is in the public interest and appropriate in the circumstances?
      `the Attorney General has consented to the negotiation of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General consented to the negotiation of the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.32(1), may the prosecutor enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement with my organization` IS
    `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (`s 715.3(1) organization` (`s 2 organization` `the kind of body my organization is` `it was created for a common purpose` `it has an operational structure` `it holds itself out to the public as an association of persons`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a public body`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a trade union`) (`the kind of body my organization is` EQUALS `a municipality`)) `my organization is alleged to have committed the offence` (JUST `the offence is listed in the schedule to Part XXII.1`) `the prosecutor is of the opinion that there is a reasonable prospect of conviction with respect to the offence` `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission did not cause and was not likely to have caused serious bodily harm or death, or injury to national defence or national security` `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the act or omission was not committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization or terrorist group` `the prosecutor is of the opinion that negotiating the agreement is in the public interest and appropriate in the circumstances` `the Attorney General has consented to the negotiation of the agreement`

-- s 715.32(3).
@export Under section 715.32(3), does this subsection bar the prosecutor from considering this matter?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 715.32(3) the matter` @desc Which matter? (choose one)
      `my organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your organization alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.32(3), does this subsection bar the prosecutor from considering this matter` IS
    `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor must not consider the matter` `the matter` `my organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`

-- s 715.33(1).
@export Under section 715.33(1), must the prosecutor give my organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations?
GIVEN `the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor wish to negotiate a remediation agreement with your organization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.33(1), must the prosecutor give my organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations` IS
    `s 715.33(1) the prosecutor must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations` `the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement`

-- s 715.33(1).
@export Under section 715.33(1), does the notice I received meet the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)?
GIVEN `the notice is written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations given to my organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations, given to your organization?
      `it includes a summary description of the offence to which the agreement would apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include a summary description of the offence to which the agreement would apply?
      `it includes an indication of the voluntary nature of the negotiation process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate the voluntary nature of the negotiation process?
      `it includes an indication of the legal effects of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate the legal effects of the agreement?
      `it includes an indication that, by agreeing to the terms of the notice, my organization explicitly waives the inclusion of the negotiation period and the period during which the agreement is in force in any assessment of the reasonableness of the delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate that, by agreeing to its terms, your organization explicitly waives the inclusion of the negotiation period and the period during which the agreement is in force in any assessment of the reasonableness of the delay between the day the charge is laid and the end of trial?
      `it includes an indication that negotiations must be carried out in good faith and that my organization must provide all information requested by the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate that negotiations must be carried out in good faith and that your organization must provide all information requested by the prosecutor that it is aware of or can obtain through reasonable efforts?
      `it includes an indication of how the information my organization discloses during the negotiations may be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate how the information your organization discloses during the negotiations may be used?
      `it includes a warning that knowingly making false or misleading statements may lead to recommencement of proceedings or prosecution for obstruction of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it warn that knowingly making false or misleading statements or giving false or misleading information during the negotiations may lead to recommencement of proceedings or prosecution for obstruction of justice?
      `it includes an indication that either party may withdraw from the negotiations by providing written notice to the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate that either party may withdraw from the negotiations by providing written notice to the other party?
      `it includes an indication that reasonable efforts must be made by both parties to identify any victim as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate that both parties must make reasonable efforts to identify any victim as soon as practicable?
      `it includes a deadline to accept the offer to negotiate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give a deadline to accept the offer to negotiate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.33(1), does the notice I received meet the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` IS
    `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` `the notice I received`
    WHERE
        `the notice I received` MEANS `s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF `the notice is written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations given to my organization`, `it includes a summary description of the offence to which the agreement would apply`, `it includes an indication of the voluntary nature of the negotiation process`, `it includes an indication of the legal effects of the agreement`, `it includes an indication that, by agreeing to the terms of the notice, my organization explicitly waives the inclusion of the negotiation period and the period during which the agreement is in force in any assessment of the reasonableness of the delay`, `it includes an indication that negotiations must be carried out in good faith and that my organization must provide all information requested by the prosecutor`, `it includes an indication of how the information my organization discloses during the negotiations may be used`, `it includes a warning that knowingly making false or misleading statements may lead to recommencement of proceedings or prosecution for obstruction of justice`, `it includes an indication that either party may withdraw from the negotiations by providing written notice to the other party`, `it includes an indication that reasonable efforts must be made by both parties to identify any victim as soon as practicable`, `it includes a deadline to accept the offer to negotiate`

-- s 715.33(2).
@export Under section 715.33(2), is this admission or statement accepting responsibility, made by my organization during the negotiations, inadmissible in evidence against it?
GIVEN `it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission?
      `it was made by my organization during the negotiations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your organization make it during the negotiations?
      `it is offered in evidence against my organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it offered in evidence against your organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission?
      `it is contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility that the agreement includes under paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b)?
      `the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the parties reach an agreement, and has the court approved it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.33(2), is this admission or statement accepting responsibility, made by my organization during the negotiations, inadmissible in evidence against it` IS
    `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` `it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` `it was made by my organization during the negotiations` `it is offered in evidence against my organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission` `it is contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b)` `the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court`

-- s 715.34(1).
@export Under section 715.34(1), does the remediation agreement include everything that it must include?
GIVEN `the agreement has (a) a statement of facts and an undertaking not to contradict them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement include a statement of facts related to the offence, and an undertaking by your organization not to make or condone any public statement that contradicts those facts?
      `the agreement has (b) the organization’s admission of responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include your organization’s admission of responsibility for the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence?
      `the agreement has (c) the obligation to provide further identifying information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the obligation to provide any other information that will assist in identifying any person involved in the act or omission, or any related wrongdoing, that your organization becomes aware of, or can obtain through reasonable efforts, after the agreement was entered into?
      `the agreement has (d) the obligation to cooperate in any investigation, prosecution or other proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the obligation to cooperate in any investigation, prosecution or other proceeding in Canada, or elsewhere if the prosecutor considers it appropriate, resulting from the act or omission, including by providing information or testimony?
      `the agreement has (e) the agreement identifies any property, benefit or advantage obtained or derived directly or indirectly from the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement identify any property, benefit or advantage obtained or derived directly or indirectly from the act or omission?
      `the agreement has (e)(i) an obligation to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it include an obligation to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of Canada, to be disposed of in accordance with paragraph 4(1)(b.2) of the Seized Property Management Act?
      `the agreement has (e)(ii) an obligation to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or an obligation to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of a province, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs?
      `the agreement has (e)(iii) an obligation to otherwise deal with it as the prosecutor directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or an obligation to otherwise deal with it, as the prosecutor directs?
      `the agreement has (f) the obligation to pay a penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the obligation to pay a penalty to the Receiver General or to the treasurer of a province, for each offence to which the agreement applies, the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment?
      `the agreement has (g) an indication of any reparations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate any reparations, including restitution consistent with paragraph 738(1)(a) or (b), that your organization is required to make to a victim?
      `the agreement has (g) a statement by the prosecutor of the reasons why reparations are not appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there are none, does it include a statement by the prosecutor of the reasons why reparations to a victim are not appropriate in the circumstances?
      `the agreement has (g) an indication of any measure required in lieu of reparations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc And an indication of any measure required in lieu of reparations to a victim?
      `the agreement has (h) the obligation to pay a victim surcharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the obligation to pay a victim surcharge for each offence to which the agreement applies (other than an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act), the amount to be paid and any other terms respecting payment?
      `the agreement has (h) every offence to which the agreement applies is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every offence to which the agreement applies an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act?
      `the agreement has (i) the obligation to report on the implementation of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the obligation to report to the prosecutor on the implementation of the agreement?
      `the agreement has (i) the manner in which the report is to be made and other terms respecting reporting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate the manner in which the report is to be made and any other terms respecting reporting?
      `the agreement has (j) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate the legal effects of the agreement?
      `the agreement has (k) an acknowledgement that the agreement has been made in good faith and the information provided is accurate and complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include your organization’s acknowledgement that the agreement has been made in good faith and that the information it has provided during the negotiation is accurate and complete?
      `the agreement has (k) a commitment to continue to provide accurate and complete information while the agreement is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include a commitment that your organization will continue to provide accurate and complete information while the agreement is in force?
      `the agreement has (l) an indication of the use that can be made of information obtained as a result of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate the use that can be made of information obtained as a result of the agreement?
      `the agreement has (m) a warning that a breach may lead to termination and recommencement of proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it warn that the breach of any term of the agreement may lead to an application by the prosecutor for termination of the agreement and a recommencement of proceedings?
      `the agreement has (n) the obligation not to deduct the costs for income tax purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the obligation not to deduct, for income tax purposes, the costs of any reparations or other measures referred to in paragraph (g) or any other costs incurred to fulfil the terms of the agreement?
      `the agreement has (o) a notice of the prosecutor’s right to vary or terminate the agreement with the approval of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give notice of the prosecutor’s right to vary or terminate the agreement with the approval of the court?
      `the agreement has (p) the deadline by which the organization must meet the terms of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate the deadline by which your organization must meet the terms of the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.34(1), does the remediation agreement include everything that it must include` IS
    `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` `the agreement I was given`
    WHERE
        `the agreement I was given` MEANS `s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF `the agreement has (a) a statement of facts and an undertaking not to contradict them`, `the agreement has (b) the organization’s admission of responsibility`, `the agreement has (c) the obligation to provide further identifying information`, `the agreement has (d) the obligation to cooperate in any investigation, prosecution or other proceeding`, `the agreement has (e) the agreement identifies any property, benefit or advantage obtained or derived directly or indirectly from the act or omission`, `the agreement has (e)(i) an obligation to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of Canada`, `the agreement has (e)(ii) an obligation to forfeit it to Her Majesty in right of a province`, `the agreement has (e)(iii) an obligation to otherwise deal with it as the prosecutor directs`, `the agreement has (f) the obligation to pay a penalty`, `the agreement has (g) an indication of any reparations`, `the agreement has (g) a statement by the prosecutor of the reasons why reparations are not appropriate`, `the agreement has (g) an indication of any measure required in lieu of reparations`, `the agreement has (h) the obligation to pay a victim surcharge`, `the agreement has (h) every offence to which the agreement applies is an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`, `the agreement has (i) the obligation to report on the implementation of the agreement`, `the agreement has (i) the manner in which the report is to be made and other terms respecting reporting`, `the agreement has (j) an indication of the legal effects of the agreement`, `the agreement has (k) an acknowledgement that the agreement has been made in good faith and the information provided is accurate and complete`, `the agreement has (k) a commitment to continue to provide accurate and complete information while the agreement is in force`, `the agreement has (l) an indication of the use that can be made of information obtained as a result of the agreement`, `the agreement has (m) a warning that a breach may lead to termination and recommencement of proceedings`, `the agreement has (n) the obligation not to deduct the costs for income tax purposes`, `the agreement has (o) a notice of the prosecutor’s right to vary or terminate the agreement with the approval of the court`, `the agreement has (p) the deadline by which the organization must meet the terms of the agreement`

-- s 715.34(2).
@export Under section 715.34(2), is this admission or statement accepting responsibility, made by my organization as a result of the agreement, inadmissible in evidence against it?
GIVEN `it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission?
      `it was made by my organization as a result of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your organization make it as a result of the agreement?
      `it is offered in evidence against my organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it offered in evidence against your organization in civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission?
