GIVEN `a charge is laid against me in respect of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a charge been laid against you in respect of that offence?
      `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that I have partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied on a balance of probabilities that you have partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures?
      `in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the court’s opinion that the prosecution of the charge would be unfair, having regard to the circumstances and your compliance with the alternative measures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.52(1)(b), may the court dismiss the charge against me` IS
    `s 715.52(1)(b) the court may dismiss the charge` `a charge is laid against me in respect of that offence` `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that I have partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures` `in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair`

-- s 715.52(2).
@export Under section 715.52(2), is Part XXII.2 to be construed as preventing this act?
GIVEN `the act` IS A `s 715.52(2) the act` @desc Which act? (choose one)
      `the act is done in accordance with the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act done in accordance with the law?
      `subsection (1)(a) requires the court to dismiss the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 715.52(1)(a) require the court to dismiss the charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.52(2), is Part XXII.2 to be construed as preventing this act` IS
    `s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` `the act` `the act is done in accordance with the law` `subsection (1)(a) requires the court to dismiss the charge`

-- s 715.53(b).
@export Under section 715.53(b), may I freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time?
GIVEN `I am a participant in the restorative justice process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a participant in the restorative justice process?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.53(b), may I freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time` IS
    `s 715.53(b) the participant may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time` `I am a participant in the restorative justice process`

-- s 715.54(1).
@export Under section 715.54(1), may a restorative justice process be used at this stage?
GIVEN `it is a stage of a criminal justice process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a stage of a criminal justice process?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.54(1), may a restorative justice process be used at this stage` IS
    `s 715.54(1) a restorative justice process may be used at the stage` `it is a stage of a criminal justice process`

-- s 715.54(3).
@export Under section 715.54(3), do sections 715.49 to 715.52 apply to the restorative justice process (name the section you mean)?
GIVEN `the section of the Code, as a decimal` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Code? (give it as a decimal, for example 715.5 for section 715.5)
      `the subsection of the Code, as the Code writes it` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection, as the Code writes it (for example "(6)")? Leave it empty if you mean the whole section.
      `the restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under Part XXII.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the restorative justice process used as an alternative measure under Part XXII.2?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.54(3), do sections 715.49 to 715.52 apply to the restorative justice process (name the section you mean)` IS
    `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` `the provision` `the restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under Part XXII.2`
    WHERE
        `the provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the Code, as a decimal`, `the subsection of the Code, as the Code writes it`

-- s 715.55(1).
@export Under section 715.55(1), does this person participate in the conference?
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the person? (choose one)
      `the person could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the person assist with the objectives of the conference (to facilitate alternative measures or restorative justice processes, and to make recommendations)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.55(1), does this person participate in the conference` IS
    `s 715.55(1) the person participates in the conference` `the person` `the person could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2)`

-- s 715.55(4).
@export Under section 715.55(4), must the conference be convened and conducted in accordance with the rules and practices of the province or territory?
GIVEN `rules and practices are established under subsection (3) in the province or territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General or a designated minister of the province or territory established rules and practices for conferences?
      `those rules and practices apply to the conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do those rules and practices apply to this conference?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.55(4), must the conference be convened and conducted in accordance with the rules and practices of the province or territory` IS
    `s 715.55(4) the conference must be convened and conducted in accordance with the rules and practices` `rules and practices are established under subsection (3) in the province or territory` `those rules and practices apply to the conference`

-- s 715.56.
@export Under section 715.56, do sections 715.57 to 715.6 apply in respect of me (name the section you mean)?
GIVEN `the section of the Code, as a decimal` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Code? (give it as a decimal, for example 715.5 for section 715.5)
      `the subsection of the Code, as the Code writes it` IS A STRING @desc Which subsection, as the Code writes it (for example "(6)")? Leave it empty if you mean the whole section.
      `I have been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.56, do sections 715.57 to 715.6 apply in respect of me (name the section you mean)` IS
    `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` `the provision` `I have been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48`
    WHERE
        `the provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section of the Code, as a decimal`, `the subsection of the Code, as the Code writes it`

-- s 715.57.
@export Under section 715.57, is the police officer to keep a record of the warning issued or referral made?
GIVEN `the person is the police officer who issues a warning or makes a referral under section 715.47` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the police officer who issued the warning or made the referral to you under section 715.47?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.57, is the police officer to keep a record of the warning issued or referral made` IS
    `s 715.57 the police officer is to keep a record of the warning issued or referral made, including the identity of the person warned or referred` `the person is the police officer who issues a warning or makes a referral under section 715.47`

-- s 715.58(2).
@export Under section 715.58(2), may a peace officer disclose this information to any person?
GIVEN `the information is in a record kept under section 715.58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information in a record kept under section 715.58?
      `it is necessary to disclose the information in the conduct of the investigation of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary to disclose the information in the conduct of the investigation of an offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.58(2), may a peace officer disclose this information to any person` IS
    `s 715.58(2) a peace officer may disclose the information to any person` `the information is in a record kept under section 715.58` `it is necessary to disclose the information in the conduct of the investigation of an offence`

-- s 715.6(1).
@export Under section 715.6(1), may the information in the record be made available to this recipient?
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `s 715.6(1) the recipient` @desc Who is the recipient? (choose one)
      `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59?
      `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the recipient is a person a judge has deemed to have a valid interest: is the judge satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes?
      `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Or is the judge satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.6(1), may the information in the record be made available to this recipient` IS
    `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `the recipient` `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes` `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice`

-- s 715.6(3).
@export Under section 715.6(3), is the person barred from disclosing the information in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify me?
GIVEN `the record is made available for inspection to the person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the record made available for inspection to the person under subparagraph 715.6(1)(d)(i) (research or statistical purposes)?
      `the information is disclosed in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the form in which the information is disclosed reasonably be expected to identify you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.6(3), is the person barred from disclosing the information in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify me` IS
    `s 715.6(3) the person may not disclose the information in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` `the record is made available for inspection to the person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i)` `the information is disclosed in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify me`

-- s 715.6(5).
@export Under section 715.6(5), is this evidence inadmissible?
GIVEN `the evidence` IS A `s 715.6(5) the evidence` @desc What is the evidence? (choose one)
      `it is offered for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it offered for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour?
      `it is offered in proceedings before a court in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it offered in proceedings before a court in respect of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.6(5), is this evidence inadmissible` IS
    `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `the evidence` `it is offered for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour` `it is offered in proceedings before a court in respect of me`

-- s 715.6(6).
@export Under section 715.6(6), does this subsection bar the introduction of the record into evidence?
GIVEN `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59?
      `the introduction into evidence is for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record introduced for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c)?
      `the day on which the record is introduced into evidence` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the record introduced into evidence?
      `the day on which the period during which the alternative measure was applied ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period during which the alternative measure was applied end?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 715.6(6), does this subsection bar the introduction of the record into evidence` IS
    `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` `the introduction into evidence is for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c)` `the day on which the record is introduced into evidence` `the day on which the period during which the alternative measure was applied ended`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc26 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc26-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER of part ccc26 (sections 716 to 736 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the first half of Part XXIII, Sentencing).
--
-- SEAT: the person accused of an offence, who may be found guilty and sentenced: what the sentencing sections say will happen, and what they leave open.
-- Every question begins "Under section N," with the Act's own numbering, takes plain inputs (yes or no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices) with an @desc
-- worded as the person would be asked, and calls the layer-1 rule of the same name in the modules imported below; nothing here restates a rule. A MAYBE answer is
-- JUST TRUE (yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) or NOTHING (the text does not say: never read as no). A question is named for what the rule answers,
-- in the rule's own direction: a rule that bars is asked as a bar, a rule that permits as a permission, a rule that requires as a requirement.
-- Provisions whose subject is a victim's, a community representative's or a government's own conduct (a victim's way of presenting a statement, the court's inquiries of the
-- prosecutor about victims, the Attorney General's consent, a government's direction of the proceeds of a fine) are in layer 1 only; what an official must or may do to,
-- for or about the accused (copies given to the offender, endorsements, adjournments, the court's powers) is asked here. The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation, not the official text.
-- A length of time is asked in years, months and days, and whether it is "less a day" (two years less a day is 2 years, 0 months, 0 days, less a day: yes).


§ `Purpose and principles of sentencing (ss 718 to 718.21)`

@export Under section 718.01, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence?
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence involved the abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.01, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    `s 718.01 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` `the offence involved the abuse of a person under the age of eighteen years`

@export Under section 718.02, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence?
GIVEN `the offence charged: the section number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the provision named in: the offence charged?
      `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of that provision, as printed? (blank if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.02, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    `s 718.02 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence charged: the section number`, `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)`)

@export Under section 718.03, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence?
GIVEN `the offence charged: the section number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the provision named in: the offence charged?
      `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of that provision, as printed? (blank if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.03, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    `s 718.03 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence charged: the section number`, `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)`)

@export Under section 718.04, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence?
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances, including because the person is Aboriginal and female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence involved the abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances, including because the person is Aboriginal and female?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.04, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    `s 718.04 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` `the offence involved the abuse of a person who is vulnerable because of personal circumstances, including because the person is Aboriginal and female`

@export Under section 718.05, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence?
GIVEN `the offence charged: the section number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the provision named in: the offence charged?
      `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of that provision, as printed? (blank if none)
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.05, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    `s 718.05 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence charged: the section number`, `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)`) `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision`

@export Under section 718.06, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence?
GIVEN `the offence charged: the section number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the provision named in: the offence charged?
      `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)` IS A STRING @desc What is the subsection of that provision, as printed? (blank if none)
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.06, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    `s 718.06 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the offence charged: the section number`, `the offence charged: the subsection (blank if none)`) `the offence is a second or subsequent offence under that provision`

@export Under section 718.07, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence?
GIVEN `the offence was committed for the benefit of a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence was committed for the benefit of a criminal organization?
      `the offence was committed at the direction of a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence was committed at the direction of a criminal organization?
      `the offence was committed in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence was committed in association with a criminal organization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.07, does the section require primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` MEANS
    `s 718.07 requires primary consideration to denunciation and deterrence` `the offence was committed for the benefit of a criminal organization` `the offence was committed at the direction of a criminal organization` `the offence was committed in association with a criminal organization`

@export Under section 718.1, is the sentence proportionate?
GIVEN `the sentence is proportionate to the gravity of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sentence is proportionate to the gravity of the offence?
      `the sentence is proportionate to the degree of responsibility of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sentence is proportionate to the degree of responsibility of the offender?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.1, is the sentence proportionate` MEANS
    `s 718.1 the sentence is proportionate` `the sentence is proportionate to the gravity of the offence` `the sentence is proportionate to the degree of responsibility of the offender`

@export Under section 718.2, does the section require the court to take the principles into consideration?
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court imposes a sentence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2, does the section require the court to take the principles into consideration` MEANS
    `s 718.2 requires the court to take the principles into consideration` `the court imposes a sentence`

@export Under section 718.2(a), is the circumstance deemed aggravating?
GIVEN `circumstance` IS A `s 718.2(a) circumstance` @desc Which circumstance is it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(a), is the circumstance deemed aggravating` MEANS
    `s 718.2(a) the circumstance is deemed aggravating` circumstance

@export Under section 718.2(a), should the sentence be increased?
GIVEN `there is a relevant aggravating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a relevant aggravating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(a), should the sentence be increased` MEANS
    `s 718.2(a) the sentence should be increased` `there is a relevant aggravating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender`

@export Under section 718.2(a), should the sentence be reduced?
GIVEN `there is a relevant mitigating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a relevant mitigating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(a), should the sentence be reduced` MEANS
    `s 718.2(a) the sentence should be reduced` `there is a relevant mitigating circumstance relating to the offence or the offender`

@export Under section 718.2(b), does the sentence meet the principle of parity?
GIVEN `the sentence is similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sentence is similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(b), does the sentence meet the principle of parity` MEANS
    `s 718.2(b) the sentence meets the principle of parity` `the sentence is similar to sentences imposed on similar offenders for similar offences committed in similar circumstances`

@export Under section 718.2(c), is the combined sentence barred as unduly long or harsh?
GIVEN `consecutive sentences are imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that consecutive sentences are imposed?
      `the combined sentence is unduly long or harsh` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the combined sentence is unduly long or harsh?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(c), is the combined sentence barred as unduly long or harsh` MEANS
    `s 718.2(c) the combined sentence is barred as unduly long or harsh` `consecutive sentences are imposed` `the combined sentence is unduly long or harsh`

@export Under section 718.2(d), is deprivation of liberty barred?
GIVEN `less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(d), is deprivation of liberty barred` MEANS
    `s 718.2(d) deprivation of liberty is barred` `less restrictive sanctions may be appropriate in the circumstances`

@export Under section 718.2(e), should the sanction be considered?
GIVEN `the sanction is available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sanction is available?
      `the sanction is imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sanction is imprisonment?
      `the sanction is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sanction is reasonable in the circumstances?
      `the sanction is consistent with the harm done to victims or to the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sanction is consistent with the harm done to victims or to the community?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(e), should the sanction be considered` MEANS
    `s 718.2(e) the sanction should be considered` `the sanction is available` `the sanction is imprisonment` `the sanction is reasonable in the circumstances` `the sanction is consistent with the harm done to victims or to the community`

@export Under section 718.2(e), is particular attention due to the circumstances of the offender?
GIVEN `the offender is Aboriginal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are Aboriginal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.2(e), is particular attention due to the circumstances of the offender` MEANS
    `s 718.2(e) particular attention is due to the circumstances of the offender` `the offender is Aboriginal`

@export Under section 718.201, does the section require the court to consider the increased vulnerability of female victims?
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.201, does the section require the court to consider the increased vulnerability of female victims` MEANS
    `s 718.201 requires the court to consider the increased vulnerability of female victims` `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner`

@export Under section 718.201, is particular attention due to the circumstances of the victim?
GIVEN `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner?
      `the victim is Aboriginal and female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the victim is Aboriginal and female?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.201, is particular attention due to the circumstances of the victim` MEANS
    `s 718.201 particular attention is due to the circumstances of the victim` `the offence involved the abuse of an intimate partner` `the victim is Aboriginal and female`

@export Under section 718.21, does the section require the court to take the factor into consideration?
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence on an organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court imposes a sentence on an organization?
      `factor` IS A `s 718.21 factor` @desc Which of the factors that the section lists is it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.21, does the section require the court to take the factor into consideration` MEANS
    `s 718.21 requires the court to take the factor into consideration` `the court imposes a sentence on an organization` factor

@export Under section 718.3(1), is the punishment in the discretion of the court?
GIVEN `the enactment prescribes different degrees or kinds of punishment in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the enactment prescribes different degrees or kinds of punishment in respect of the offence?
      `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.3(1), is the punishment in the discretion of the court` MEANS
    `s 718.3(1) the punishment is in the discretion of the court` `the enactment prescribes different degrees or kinds of punishment in respect of the offence` `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment`

@export Under section 718.3(2), is the punishment in the discretion of the court?
GIVEN `the enactment prescribes a punishment in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the enactment prescribes a punishment in respect of the offence?
      `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.3(2), is the punishment in the discretion of the court` MEANS
    `s 718.3(2) the punishment is in the discretion of the court` `the enactment prescribes a punishment in respect of the offence` `the punishment is within the limitations prescribed in the enactment`

@export Under section 718.3(2), is the punishment a minimum punishment?
GIVEN `the enactment declares the punishment to be a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the enactment declares the punishment to be a minimum punishment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.3(2), is the punishment a minimum punishment` MEANS
    `s 718.3(2) the punishment is a minimum punishment` `the enactment declares the punishment to be a minimum punishment`

@export Under section 718.3(4)(a), must the court consider directing that the term be served consecutively to the sentence the accused is already subject to?
GIVEN `the accused is subject at the time of sentencing to a sentence of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are subject at the time of sentencing to a sentence of imprisonment?
      `the court imposes a term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court imposes a term of imprisonment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 718.3(4)(a), must the court consider directing that the term be served consecutively to the sentence the accused is already subject to` MEANS
    `s 718.3(4)(a) the court must consider directing that the term be served consecutively to the sentence the accused is already subject to` `the accused is subject at the time of sentencing to a sentence of imprisonment` `the court imposes a term of imprisonment`

@export Under section 718.3(4)(b), must the court consider directing that the terms be served consecutively?
GIVEN `terms of imprisonment are imposed at the same time for more than one offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that terms of imprisonment are imposed at the same time for more than one offence?
