§ `Fines (ss 734 to 736)`

@export Under section 734(1), may the court fine the offender by making an order under section 734.1?
GIVEN `the court convicts a person of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court convicts a person of an offence?
      `the person is an organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an organization?
      `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the punishment for the offence includes a minimum term of imprisonment?
      `the fine would be imposed in lieu of any other sanction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fine would be imposed in lieu of any other sanction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 734(1), may the court fine the offender by making an order under section 734.1` MEANS
    `s 734(1) the court may fine the offender by making an order under section 734.1` `the court convicts a person of an offence` `the person is an organization` `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum term of imprisonment` `the fine would be imposed in lieu of any other sanction`

@export Under section 734(2), does the ability-to-pay condition bar the fine?
GIVEN `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum fine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the punishment for the offence includes a minimum fine?
      `the fine is imposed in lieu of a forfeiture order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fine is imposed in lieu of a forfeiture order?
      `the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court is satisfied that you are able to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 734(2), does the ability-to-pay condition bar the fine` MEANS
    `s 734(2) the ability-to-pay condition bars the fine` `the punishment for the offence includes a minimum fine` `the fine is imposed in lieu of a forfeiture order` `the court is satisfied that the offender is able to pay the fine or discharge it under section 736`

@export Under section 734(3), is the person in default of payment of the fine?
GIVEN `the fine has been paid in full by the time set out in the order made under section 734.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fine has been paid in full by the time set out in the order made under section 734.1?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 734(3), is the person in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    `s 734(3) the person is in default of payment of the fine` `the fine has been paid in full by the time set out in the order made under section 734.1`

@export Under section 734(4), is a term of imprisonment deemed to be imposed in default of payment of the fine?
GIVEN `the offender is fined under section 734` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are fined under section 734?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 734(4), is a term of imprisonment deemed to be imposed in default of payment of the fine` MEANS
    `s 734(4) a term of imprisonment is deemed to be imposed in default of payment of the fine` `the offender is fined under section 734`

@export Under section 734(5), what is the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine, in days?
GIVEN `the unpaid amount of the fine` IS A NUMBER @desc State the unpaid amount of the fine.
      `the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection 734(7)` IS A NUMBER @desc State the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection 734(7).
      `the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed` IS A NUMBER @desc State the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed.
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction: imprisonment is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a term of imprisonment imposed or stated for: the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction?
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction: the imprisonment is for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that imprisonment for life?
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (years)` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is a term, how many years does it last? (0 if it is for life or there is none)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (months)` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is a term, how many months does it last? (0 if it is for life or there is none)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (days)` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is a term, how many days does it last? (0 if it is for life or there is none)
      `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (less a day)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a term, is it "less a day" (for example, two years less a day)? (No if it is for life or there is none)
      `the offence is proceeded with by` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Is the offence proceeded with by indictment or on summary conviction?
      `the date of default` IS A DATE @desc State the date of default.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 734(5), what is the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine, in days` MEANS
    `s 734(5) the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the fine, in days` `the unpaid amount of the fine` `the costs and charges of committing and conveying the defaulter to prison, calculated in accordance with regulations made under subsection 734(7)` `the provincial minimum hourly wage, at the time of default, in the province in which the fine was imposed` (IF NOT `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction: imprisonment is imposed` THEN `no imprisonment is stated` ELSE (IF `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction: the imprisonment is for life` THEN `imprisonment for life` ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (years)`, `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (months)`, `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (days)`, `the maximum term of imprisonment that the court could itself impose on conviction (less a day)`))) `the offence is proceeded with by` `the date of default`

@export Under section 734(6), may all or any part of the fine be taken out of the moneys found?
GIVEN `the fine was imposed under section 734` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fine was imposed under section 734?
      `the moneys were found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the moneys were found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender?
      `the court is satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court is satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender?
      `the court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court so directs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 734(6), may all or any part of the fine be taken out of the moneys found` MEANS
    `s 734(6) all or any part of the fine may be taken out of the moneys found` `the fine was imposed under section 734` `the moneys were found in the possession of the offender at the time of the arrest of the offender` `the court is satisfied that ownership of or right to possession of those moneys is not disputed by claimants other than the offender` `the court so directs`

