-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc27 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc27-seat.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 737 to 751.1 -- THE SEAT LAYER (ccc27).
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code, and who asks what follows from a conviction in these sections:
-- the victim surcharge, restitution, a conditional sentence, where a sentence is served, delay of parole eligibility, the life sentences and their review,
-- time in custody, pardons, the disabilities that follow a conviction, and costs in a libel prosecution. (Assumed, not ruled: the seat is the accused, as the brief says.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the ten layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated:
-- each question builds the module's own records from plain answers and calls the module's own function. Every question is named "Under section N, ..."
-- with the Act's own numbering and asks in the direction its body answers (a bar is titled as a bar, a grant as a grant, a duty as a duty).
-- A question answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text says so in its own words, and NOTHING where the text does not say (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
-- Provisions addressed only to an official (for example the keeper of a prison in section 744, and the Chief Justice's duties in sections 745.61 and 745.64) are
-- encoded in layer 1 and are not questions here, because they mean nothing to the accused beyond the questions below.
-- The "s 2 ..." inputs are the section 2 terms the part's rules turn on, taken as inputs per PLAN.md; they are left blank when section 2 does not decide them.

§ `Section 737 -- the victim surcharge`

@export Under section 737(1), must I pay a victim surcharge?
GIVEN `I was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of the offence?
      `I was discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you discharged under section 730 of the offence?
      `the Act of the offence` IS A `s 737(1) Act of the offence` @desc Under which Act is the offence: this Act (the Criminal Code), the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, the Cannabis Act, or some other Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 737(1), must I pay a victim surcharge` IS
    `s 737(1) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge` `I was convicted` `I was discharged under section 730` `the Act of the offence`

-- A hybrid offence is taken in the mode of the conviction (fork F-1 in NOTES.md).
@export Under section 737(2), how much is the victim surcharge, in dollars?
GIVEN `a fine was imposed on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a fine imposed on you?
      `the amount of my fine, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the fine, in dollars? (0 if no fine was imposed)
      `I was convicted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of an offence prosecuted by indictment? (No, if on summary conviction.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 737(2), how much is the victim surcharge, in dollars` IS
    `s 737(2) the amount of the victim surcharge` `my fine` `my mode of conviction`
    WHERE
        `my fine` MEANS
            IF `a fine was imposed on me`
            THEN `a fine of` `the amount of my fine, in dollars`
            ELSE `no fine is stated`
        `my mode of conviction` MEANS
            IF `I was convicted by indictment`
            THEN `by indictment`
            ELSE `on summary conviction`

@export Under section 737(2.1), may the court order me to pay no victim surcharge, or a reduced amount?
GIVEN `my offence was committed after the day on which subsections (2.1) to (2.4) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed after the day on which subsections 737(2.1) to (2.4) came into force?
      `I am unable to pay a victim surcharge on account of my precarious financial circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to pay a victim surcharge on account of your precarious financial circumstances?
      `the only circumstance I rely on is my imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your imprisonment the only circumstance you rely on?
      `the court is satisfied that the surcharge would be disproportionate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that a victim surcharge would be disproportionate to the gravity of the offence or to your degree of responsibility?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 737(2.1), may the court order me to pay no victim surcharge, or a reduced amount` IS
    `s 737(2.1) the court may order the offender to pay no victim surcharge, or a reduced amount` `my offence was committed after the day on which subsections (2.1) to (2.4) came into force` (`s 737(2.2) undue hardship` `I am unable to pay a victim surcharge on account of my precarious financial circumstances` `the only circumstance I rely on is my imprisonment`) `the court is satisfied that the surcharge would be disproportionate`

@export Under section 737(3), may the court order a victim surcharge above the amount in subsection (2)?
GIVEN `the court considers it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider it appropriate in the circumstances?
      `the court is satisfied that I am able to pay the higher amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that you are able to pay the higher amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 737(3), may the court order a victim surcharge above the amount in subsection (2)` IS
    `s 737(3) the court may order a victim surcharge exceeding the amount in subsection (2)` `the court considers it appropriate` `the court is satisfied that I am able to pay the higher amount`

@export Under section 737(4), by what day must I pay the victim surcharge?
GIVEN `the day the surcharge was imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the victim surcharge imposed?
      `the days my province allows for payment` IS MAYBE NUMBER @desc How many days has the lieutenant governor in council of your province allowed for payment? (leave blank if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 737(4), by what day must I pay the victim surcharge` IS
    `s 737(4) the last day for payment` `the day the surcharge was imposed` `the days my province allows for payment`

@export Under section 737(6), is my notice the written notice the court must give me?
GIVEN `my notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice you were given in writing?
      `it sets out the amount of the victim surcharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the amount of the victim surcharge?
      `it sets out how the victim surcharge is to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the manner in which the victim surcharge is to be paid?
      `it sets out the time by which the victim surcharge must be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the time by which the victim surcharge must be paid?
      `it sets out the procedure for applying for a change under section 734.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the procedure for applying for a change in the manner or time of payment, under section 734.3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 737(6), is my notice the written notice the court must give me` IS
    `s 737(6) the notice is the written notice the court shall cause to be given` `my notice is in writing` `it sets out the amount of the victim surcharge` `it sets out how the victim surcharge is to be paid` `it sets out the time by which the victim surcharge must be paid` `it sets out the procedure for applying for a change under section 734.3`


§ `Sections 737.1 to 741.2 -- restitution`

@export Under section 737.1(1), must the court consider making a restitution order against me?
GIVEN `I was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of the offence?
      `I was discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you discharged under section 730 of the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 737.1(1), must the court consider making a restitution order against me` IS
    `s 737.1(1) the court shall consider making a restitution order under section 738 or 739` `I was convicted` `I was discharged under section 730`

@export Under section 738(1), may the court order me to make restitution to another person?
GIVEN `I was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of the offence?
      `I was discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you discharged under section 730 of the offence?
      `the Attorney General applied, or the court acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Attorney General apply for restitution, or is the court acting on its own motion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 738(1), may the court order me to make restitution to another person` IS
    `s 738(1) the court may order the offender to make restitution to another person` `I was convicted` `I was discharged under section 730` `the Attorney General applied, or the court acts on its own motion`

@export Under section 738(1)(a), what is the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property?
GIVEN `the damage, loss or destruction resulted from the offence or my arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the damage, loss or destruction result from the commission of the offence or from your arrest or attempted arrest?
      `the replacement value of the property, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the replacement value of the property as of the date the order is imposed, in dollars?
      `the value of any part of the property that was returned, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in dollars, of any part of the property returned to that person, as of the date it was returned? (0 if none)
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount readily ascertainable?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 738(1)(a), what is the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` IS
    `s 738(1)(a) the ceiling on restitution for damage to, or the loss or destruction of, property` `the damage, loss or destruction resulted from the offence or my arrest` `the replacement value of the property, in dollars` `the value of any part of the property that was returned, in dollars` `the amount is readily ascertainable`

@export Under section 738(1)(b), what is the ceiling on restitution for bodily or psychological harm?
GIVEN `the harm is bodily or psychological harm to a person caused by the offence or my arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it bodily or psychological harm to a person as a result of the commission of the offence or your arrest or attempted arrest?
      `the pecuniary damages incurred as a result of the harm, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are all the pecuniary damages incurred as a result of the harm, including loss of income or support, in dollars?
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount readily ascertainable?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 738(1)(b), what is the ceiling on restitution for bodily or psychological harm` IS
    `s 738(1)(b) the ceiling on restitution for bodily or psychological harm` `the harm is bodily or psychological harm to a person caused by the offence or my arrest` `the pecuniary damages incurred as a result of the harm, in dollars` `the amount is readily ascertainable`

@export Under section 738(1)(c), what is the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of my household?
GIVEN `my partner, child or another person was harmed or threatened by the offence or my arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your intimate partner or child, or any other person, harmed or threatened with harm as a result of the offence or your arrest or attempted arrest?
      `that person was a member of my household at the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that person a member of your household at the relevant time?
      `the actual and reasonable moving expenses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the actual and reasonable expenses of moving out of your household, for temporary housing, food, child care and transportation, in dollars?
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount readily ascertainable?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 738(1)(c), what is the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of my household` IS
    `s 738(1)(c) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of moving out of the offender's household` `my partner, child or another person was harmed or threatened by the offence or my arrest` `that person was a member of my household at the relevant time` `the actual and reasonable moving expenses, in dollars` `the amount is readily ascertainable`

@export Under section 738(1)(d), what is the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity?
GIVEN `the section of my offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code is the offence? (for example 402.2)
      `the person incurred expenses to re-establish their identity because of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person incur expenses to re-establish their identity as a result of the offence?
      `the reasonable part of those expenses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the reasonable part of those expenses, in dollars?
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount readily ascertainable?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 738(1)(d), what is the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity` IS
    `s 738(1)(d) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of re-establishing identity` (`Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS `the section of my offence`, `subsection` IS "") `the person incurred expenses to re-establish their identity because of the offence` `the reasonable part of those expenses, in dollars` `the amount is readily ascertainable`

@export Under section 738(1)(e), what is the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of removing an intimate image?
GIVEN `the section of my offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code is the offence? (for example 162.1)
      `the subsection of my offence` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection? (for example "(1)"; leave empty if none)
      `the person incurred expenses to remove the intimate image because of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person incur expenses to remove the intimate image from the Internet or other digital network as a result of the offence?
      `the reasonable part of those expenses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the reasonable part of those expenses, in dollars?
      `the amount is readily ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount readily ascertainable?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 738(1)(e), what is the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of removing an intimate image` IS
    `s 738(1)(e) the ceiling on restitution for the expenses of removing the intimate image` (`Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS `the section of my offence`, `subsection` IS `the subsection of my offence`) `the person incurred expenses to remove the intimate image because of the offence` `the reasonable part of those expenses, in dollars` `the amount is readily ascertainable`

@export Under section 739, may the court order me to pay restitution to a person who bought, or lent against, property I obtained by the offence?
GIVEN `I was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of the offence?
      `I was discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you discharged under section 730 of the offence?
      `the kind of person` IS A `s 739 head` @desc Is the person (a) someone to whom the property was conveyed or transferred for valuable consideration, in good faith and without notice, or (b) someone from whom you borrowed money on the security of that property, in good faith and without notice?
      `the property has been returned to the owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the property been returned to the lawful owner or the person who had lawful possession when the offence was committed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 739, may the court order me to pay restitution to a person who bought, or lent against, property I obtained by the offence` IS
    `s 739 the court may order the offender to pay restitution to the person` `I was convicted` `I was discharged under section 730` `the kind of person` `the property has been returned to the owner`

@export Under section 739.1, do my financial means or my ability to pay prevent the court from making a restitution order?
GIVEN `the ground relied on is my financial means or ability to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground relied on your financial means or your ability to pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 739.1, do my financial means or my ability to pay prevent the court from making a restitution order` IS
    `s 739.1 the offender's financial means or ability to pay prevents the court from making an order under section 738 or 739` `the ground relied on is my financial means or ability to pay`

@export Under section 740, must the court make the restitution order first?
GIVEN `the court finds a restitution order applicable and appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court find it applicable and appropriate to make an order of restitution under section 738 or 739?
      `a forfeiture order may be made in respect of the same property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May an order of forfeiture be made in respect of property that is the same as property in respect of which the restitution order may be made?
      `a fine is being considered and I could not comply with both orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court considering a fine, and does it appear that you would not have the means or ability to comply with both orders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 740, must the court make the restitution order first` IS
    `s 740 the court shall first make the order of restitution` `the court finds a restitution order applicable and appropriate` `a forfeiture order may be made in respect of the same property` `a fine is being considered and I could not comply with both orders`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (second seat audit): was "Under section 741(1), am I in default of the restitution order"; the body answers for an order made under section 732.1, 738, 739 or 742.3, so the title now names all four.
@export Under section 741(1), am I in default of an order to pay an amount made under section 732.1, 738, 739 or 742.3?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `s 741(1) order` @desc Under which section was the order made: 732.1, 738, 739, 742.3, or another?
      `I failed to pay all of the amount by the day in the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to pay all of the amount ordered by the day specified in the order?
      `I failed to make a periodic payment required by the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to make a periodic payment required under the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 741(1), am I in default of an order to pay an amount made under section 732.1, 738, 739 or 742.3` IS
    `s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` `the kind of order` `I failed to pay all of the amount by the day in the order` `I failed to make a periodic payment required by the order`

@export Under section 741(1), may the person to whom the amount was to be paid enter the unpaid amount as a judgment in a civil court against me?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `s 741(1) order` @desc Under which section was the order made: 732.1, 738, 739, 742.3, or another?
      `I failed to pay all of the amount by the day in the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to pay all of the amount ordered by the day specified in the order?
      `I failed to make a periodic payment required by the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to make a periodic payment required under the order?
      `the order is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the order been filed?
      `the civil court has jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court a civil court in Canada with jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 741(1), may the person to whom the amount was to be paid enter the unpaid amount as a judgment in a civil court against me` IS
    `s 741(1) the person to whom the amount was to be made may enter any amount that remains unpaid as a judgment in a civil court` (`s 741(1) the offender is in default of the order` `the kind of order` `I failed to pay all of the amount by the day in the order` `I failed to make a periodic payment required by the order`) `the order is filed` `the civil court has jurisdiction`

@export Under section 741.2, does a restitution order affect a civil remedy against me?
GIVEN `the only reason relied on is the restitution order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason relied on that an order of restitution under section 738 or 739 has been made for the act or omission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 741.2, does a restitution order affect a civil remedy against me` IS
    `s 741.2 a civil remedy for an act or omission is affected by the restitution order` `the only reason relied on is the restitution order`


§ `Sections 742 to 742.31 -- a conditional sentence of imprisonment`

-- The record's minimum imprisonment is only tested for "none stated", so "a minimum exists" is written as life, a placeholder the rule does not read beyond that test.
@export Under section 742.1, may the court order that I serve my sentence in the community?
GIVEN `I am convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you convicted of an offence?
      `the years of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years is the term of imprisonment? (the whole years)
      `the months of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months more? (0 if none)
      `the days of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days more? (0 if none)
      `my sentence is described as less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence described as "less a day" (for example "two years less a day")?
      `service in the community would not endanger the safety of the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community?
      `service in the community is consistent with sections 718 to 718.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would be consistent with the fundamental purpose and principles of sentencing in sections 718 to 718.2?
      `my offence carries a minimum term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offence one punishable by a minimum term of imprisonment?
      `the maximum term for my offence is life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence, as prosecuted, life?
      `the maximum term for my offence, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum term of imprisonment for the offence as prosecuted, in years? (0 if none is stated)
      `the section of my offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code is the offence? (for example 334)
      `the subsection of my offence` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection? (for example "(1)"; leave empty if none)
      `my sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b) (attempt to commit murder)?
      `I am prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence prosecuted by way of indictment? (No, if on summary conviction.)
      `my offence is of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence of a sexual nature, or committed for a sexual purpose?
      `the victim was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offence involve a victim under 18 years of age?
      `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one` IS MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a terrorism offence, as section 2 defines it? (leave blank if not decided)
      `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one` IS MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a criminal organization offence, as section 2 defines it? (leave blank if not decided)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.1, may the court order that I serve my sentence in the community` IS
    `s 742.1 the court may order that the offender serve the sentence in the community` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my sentence` MEANS
            `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` WITH
                years IS `the years of my sentence of imprisonment`
                months IS `the months of my sentence of imprisonment`
                days IS `the days of my sentence of imprisonment`
                `less a day` IS `my sentence is described as less a day`)
        `my maximum` MEANS
            IF `the maximum term for my offence is life`
            THEN `imprisonment for life`
            ELSE (IF `the maximum term for my offence, in years` GREATER THAN 0
                  THEN `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` WITH years IS `the maximum term for my offence, in years`, months IS 0, days IS 0, `less a day` IS FALSE)
                  ELSE `no imprisonment is stated`)
        `my facts` MEANS
            `s 742.1 facts of the sentence` WITH
                `the person is convicted of an offence` IS `I am convicted of an offence`
                `the sentence of imprisonment the court imposes` IS `my sentence`
                `the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community` IS `service in the community would not endanger the safety of the community`
                `the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would be consistent with the fundamental purpose and principles of sentencing set out in sections 718 to 718.2` IS `service in the community is consistent with sections 718 to 718.2`
                `the punishment for the offence as prosecuted` IS Punishment WITH
                    `mode` IS `my mode of prosecution`
                    `maximum imprisonment` IS `my maximum`
                    `minimum imprisonment` IS (IF `my offence carries a minimum term of imprisonment` THEN `imprisonment for life` ELSE `no imprisonment is stated`)
                    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
                    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
                `the offence` IS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS `the section of my offence`, `subsection` IS `the subsection of my offence`
                `the sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b)` IS `my sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b)`
                `the mode in which the offence is prosecuted` IS `my mode of prosecution`
                `the offence is of a sexual nature or was committed for a sexual purpose` IS `my offence is of a sexual nature or for a sexual purpose`
                `the offence involves a victim under 18 years of age` IS `the victim was under 18`
                `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one` IS `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one`
                `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one` IS `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one`
        `my mode of prosecution` MEANS
            IF `I am prosecuted by indictment` THEN `by indictment` ELSE `on summary conviction`

@export Under section 742.3(1)(c)(i), did I report to a supervisor in time?
GIVEN `the working days that passed before I reported` IS A NUMBER @desc How many working days after the conditional sentence order was made did you report to a supervisor?
      `the longer period the court directed, in working days` IS MAYBE NUMBER @desc Did the court direct a longer period than two working days? If so, how many working days? (leave blank if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.3(1)(c)(i), did I report to a supervisor in time` IS
    `s 742.3(1)(c)(i) the offender reported to a supervisor in time` `the working days that passed before I reported` `the longer period the court directed, in working days`

@export Under section 742.3(1)(d), have I complied with the condition to remain within the jurisdiction of the court?
GIVEN `I am outside the jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you outside the jurisdiction of the court?
      `I have written permission from the court or the supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain written permission from the court or the supervisor to go outside that jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.3(1)(d), have I complied with the condition to remain within the jurisdiction of the court` IS
    `s 742.3(1)(d) the offender has complied with the condition to remain within the jurisdiction of the court` `I am outside the jurisdiction of the court` `I have written permission from the court or the supervisor`

@export Under section 742.3(2)(d), may the court prescribe this much community service?
GIVEN `the hours of community service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of community service?
      `the months over which it is to be performed` IS A NUMBER @desc Over how many months is it to be performed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.3(2)(d), may the court prescribe this much community service` IS
    `s 742.3(2)(d) the court may prescribe the community service` `the hours of community service` `the months over which it is to be performed`

@export Under section 742.3(3), has the court met its obligations on making my order?
GIVEN `I was given a copy of the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given a copy of the order?
      `the victim asked for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the victim ask for a copy?
      `the victim was given a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim given a copy?
      `the substance of subsection (1) and sections 742.4 and 742.6 was explained to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the substance of subsection 742.3(1) and sections 742.4 and 742.6 explained to you?
      `I was given the explanation of how to apply for a change to the optional conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given an explanation of the procedure for applying under section 742.4 for a change to the optional conditions?
      `reasonable measures were taken to ensure I understand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court take reasonable measures to ensure that you understand the order and the explanations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.3(3), has the court met its obligations on making my order` IS
    `s 742.3(3) the court has met its obligations on making the order` `I was given a copy of the order` `the victim asked for a copy` `the victim was given a copy` `the substance of subsection (1) and sections 742.4 and 742.6 was explained to me` `I was given the explanation of how to apply for a change to the optional conditions` `reasonable measures were taken to ensure I understand`

@export Under section 742.31(1), is the use of a bodily substance I provided under my conditional sentence order barred?
GIVEN `the use is to determine whether I comply with a condition to abstain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use for the purpose of determining whether you are complying with a condition of the order to abstain from drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.31(1), is the use of a bodily substance I provided under my conditional sentence order barred` IS
    `s 742.31(1) the use of a bodily substance provided under a conditional sentence order is barred` `the use is to determine whether I comply with a condition to abstain`

@export Under section 742.31(2), is the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance I provided barred?
GIVEN `the use or disclosure` IS A `s 742.31(2) use or disclosure` @desc Is the use or disclosure (1) a disclosure to you, (2) in proceedings under section 742.6, (3) anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes, or (4) any other use or disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.31(2), is the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance I provided barred` IS
    `s 742.31(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance is barred` `the use or disclosure`

@export Under section 742.31(4), am I guilty of an offence if I contravene subsection (1) or (2)?
GIVEN `I contravene subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use, disclose or allow the disclosure of a bodily substance or of the results of its analysis contrary to section 742.31(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.31(4), am I guilty of an offence if I contravene subsection (1) or (2)` IS
    `s 742.31(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` `I contravene subsection (1) or (2)`


§ `Sections 742.4 to 742.7 -- changing the conditions, transfer, breach`

@export Under section 742.4(2)(a), may I request the court to hold a hearing to consider the proposed change?
GIVEN `the days after I received the notification` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after you received the supervisor's notification of the proposed change is it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.4(2)(a), may I request the court to hold a hearing to consider the proposed change` IS
    `s 742.4(2)(a) the requester may request the court to hold a hearing to consider the proposed change` `s 742.4(2)(a) the offender` `the days after I received the notification`

@export Under section 742.4(4), on what day does the proposed change take effect if no hearing is requested or ordered?
GIVEN `the day the court received the notification` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the court receive the supervisor's notification?
      `a hearing was requested or ordered within the seven days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a hearing requested or ordered within seven days after the notification was received?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 742.4(4), on what day does the proposed change take effect if no hearing is requested or ordered` IS
    `s 742.4(4) the day the proposed change takes effect` `the day the court received the notification` `a hearing was requested or ordered within the seven days`

@export Under section 742.5(1), may the court that made my order transfer it to a court in the territorial division where I now live?
GIVEN `I am bound by a conditional sentence order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you bound by a conditional sentence order?
      `s 2 territorial division: the offender becomes a resident of a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made` IS MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Have you become a resident of a territorial division other than the one where the order was made? (leave blank if not decided)
      `a supervisor has applied for the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a supervisor applied for the transfer?
      `the other court would have had jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court in the other territorial division, having regard to the mode of trial, have had jurisdiction to make the order if you had been tried and convicted there?
      `the two territorial divisions are in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the two territorial divisions in the same province?
      `the Attorney General of the province consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Attorney General of the province in which the order was made consent?
      `the proceedings were instituted by the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the proceedings that led to the order instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada?
      `the Attorney General of Canada consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Attorney General of Canada consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.5(1), may the court that made my order transfer it to a court in the territorial division where I now live` IS
    `s 742.5(1) the court that made the order may transfer the order to a court in that other territorial division` `I am bound by a conditional sentence order` `s 2 territorial division: the offender becomes a resident of a territorial division other than the territorial division where the order was made` `a supervisor has applied for the transfer` `the other court would have had jurisdiction` `the two territorial divisions are in the same province` `the Attorney General of the province consented` `the proceedings were instituted by the Attorney General of Canada` `the Attorney General of Canada consented`

@export Under section 742.6(3.2), are proceedings against me for the alleged breach barred for want of consent?
GIVEN `I was found, arrested or in custody outside the province of the alleged breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found, arrested or in custody in a place outside the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed?
      `the Attorney General of the province of the breach consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Attorney General of the province in which the breach is alleged to have been committed consent?
      `the proceedings were instituted by the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the proceedings that led to the order instituted by or on behalf of the Attorney General of Canada?
      `the Attorney General of Canada consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Attorney General of Canada consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.6(3.2), are proceedings against me for the alleged breach barred for want of consent` IS
    `s 742.6(3.2) proceedings in that place are barred for want of consent` `I was found, arrested or in custody outside the province of the alleged breach` `the Attorney General of the province of the breach consented` `the proceedings were instituted by the Attorney General of Canada` `the Attorney General of Canada consented`

@export Under section 742.6(8), may I require the attendance of the supervisor or a witness for cross-examination?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 742.6(8) person` @desc Is the person (1) the supervisor, (2) a witness whose signed statement is included in the report, or (3) someone else?
      `the court gave me leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given you leave?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.6(8), may I require the attendance of the supervisor or a witness for cross-examination` IS
    `s 742.6(8) the offender may require the attendance of the person for cross-examination` `the person` `the court gave me leave`

@export Under section 742.6(9), may the court take this action on a breach of a condition?
GIVEN `the action` IS A `s 742.6(9) action` @desc Is the action (a) take no action, (b) change the optional conditions, (c) suspend the order and direct that you serve part of the unexpired sentence in custody, (d) terminate the order and commit you to custody until the sentence expires, or (e) another action?
      `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that I breached a condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that you breached a condition of the order?
      `I proved a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you proved a reasonable excuse for the breach?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.6(9), may the court take this action on a breach of a condition` IS
    `s 742.6(9) the court may take the action` `the action` `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that I breached a condition` `I proved a reasonable excuse`

-- Subsection (10) only; the running of the order starts again on a detention order under subsection 515(6) (subsection (12)), which this question does not apply.
@export Under section 742.6(10), is the running of my conditional sentence order suspended on this day, under subsection (10)?
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `the day a warrant was issued for my arrest for the alleged breach` IS MAYBE DATE @desc On what day was a warrant issued for your arrest for the alleged breach? (leave blank if none)
      `the day I was arrested without warrant for the alleged breach` IS MAYBE DATE @desc On what day were you arrested without warrant for the alleged breach? (leave blank if none)
      `the day my appearance was compelled` IS MAYBE DATE @desc On what day was your appearance compelled, when you were already detained or before a court? (leave blank if none)
      `the day it was determined whether a breach occurred` IS MAYBE DATE @desc On what day was it determined whether a breach of condition had occurred? (leave blank if not yet)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.6(10), is the running of my conditional sentence order suspended on this day, under subsection (10)` IS
    `s 742.6(10) the running of the conditional sentence order is suspended on the day` `the day in question` (`s 742.6(10) the day the suspension of the running of the conditional sentence order begins` `the day a warrant was issued for my arrest for the alleged breach` `the day I was arrested without warrant for the alleged breach` `the day my appearance was compelled`) `the day it was determined whether a breach occurred`

@export Under section 742.6(15), how many days are deemed to be time served under my conditional sentence order?
GIVEN `the allegation was withdrawn or dismissed or I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the allegation of breach withdrawn or dismissed, or were you found to have had a reasonable excuse?
      `the days the running of my order was suspended` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days was the running of the order suspended?
      `I was detained under an order referred to in subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you detained under an order made under subsection 515(6), so that subsection 742.6(12) applies?
      `the days my order ran while I was so detained` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days did the order run while you were so detained? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 742.6(15), how many days are deemed to be time served under my conditional sentence order` IS
    `s 742.6(15) the days deemed to be time served under the conditional sentence order` `the allegation was withdrawn or dismissed or I had a reasonable excuse` `the days the running of my order was suspended` `I was detained under an order referred to in subsection (12)` `the days my order ran while I was so detained`

@export Under section 742.7(1), is the running of my conditional sentence order suspended on this day because I am imprisoned for another offence?
GIVEN `I am subject to a conditional sentence order and imprisoned for another offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to a conditional sentence order and imprisoned as a result of a sentence imposed for another offence, whenever committed?
      `the day is within the period of imprisonment for the other offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day within the period of imprisonment for that other offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.7(1), is the running of my conditional sentence order suspended on this day because I am imprisoned for another offence` IS
    `s 742.7(1) the running of the conditional sentence order is suspended on the day` `I am subject to a conditional sentence order and imprisoned for another offence` `the day is within the period of imprisonment for the other offence`

@export Under section 742.7(2), must the custodial period ordered be served consecutively to my other imprisonment?
GIVEN `an order was made under paragraph 742.6(9)(c) or (d) to commit me to custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order made under paragraph 742.6(9)(c) or (d) to commit you to custody?
      `the court considers consecutive service not in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider that serving the period consecutively would not be in the interests of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 742.7(2), must the custodial period ordered be served consecutively to my other imprisonment` IS
    `s 742.7(2) the custodial period ordered shall be served consecutively to any other period of imprisonment that the offender is serving` `an order was made under paragraph 742.6(9)(c) or (d) to commit me to custody` `the court considers consecutive service not in the interests of justice`


§ `Sections 743 to 744 -- imprisonment, and delay of parole eligibility`

-- The aggregate of consecutive terms is read only when the answer to the aggregate question is yes; for a single term answer no and leave the aggregate figures at 0.
@export Under section 743.1(1), must I be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary?
GIVEN `another provision otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another provision otherwise provide for where your sentence is to be served?
      `my sentence is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence imprisonment for life?
      `the years of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years is the term of imprisonment? (the whole years)
      `the months of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months more? (0 if none)
      `the days of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days more? (0 if none)
      `my sentence is described as less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence described as "less a day" (for example "two years less a day")?
      `I am sentenced to two or more terms of less than two years each, to be served one after the other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you sentenced to two or more terms of less than two years each, to be served one after the other?
      `the years of the aggregate of those terms` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole years do those terms amount to in the aggregate? (0 if not applicable)
      `the months of the aggregate of those terms` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months more? (0 if none)
      `the days of the aggregate of those terms` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days more? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743.1(1), must I be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary` IS
    `s 743.1(1) the person shall be sentenced to imprisonment in a penitentiary` `my other provision` `my sentence of imprisonment` `my aggregate`
    WHERE
        `my other provision` MEANS
            `another provision otherwise provides`
        `my sentence of imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `my sentence is imprisonment for life`
            THEN `imprisonment for life`
            ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` WITH
                years IS `the years of my sentence of imprisonment`
                months IS `the months of my sentence of imprisonment`
                days IS `the days of my sentence of imprisonment`
                `less a day` IS `my sentence is described as less a day`)
        `my aggregate` MEANS
            IF `I am sentenced to two or more terms of less than two years each, to be served one after the other`
            THEN JUST (`Length of time` WITH
                years IS `the years of the aggregate of those terms`
                months IS `the months of the aggregate of those terms`
                days IS `the days of the aggregate of those terms`
                `less a day` IS FALSE)
            ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 743.6(1), may the court order that I serve one half of my sentence, or ten years, whichever is less, before full parole?
GIVEN `the day I was sentenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you sentenced?
      `my sentence is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence imprisonment for life?
      `the years of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years is the term of imprisonment? (the whole years)
      `the months of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months more? (0 if none)
      `the days of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days more? (0 if none)
      `my sentence is described as less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence described as "less a day" (for example "two years less a day")?
      `my life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a life sentence imposed as a minimum punishment? (No, if the sentence is a term of years.)
      `my offence is set out in Schedule I or II to the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence set out in Schedule I or II to the Corrections and Conditional Release Act?
      `I was prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence prosecuted by way of indictment? (No, if on summary conviction.)
      `the court is satisfied that denunciation or deterrence requires it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied, having regard to the circumstances of the offence and your character and circumstances, that the expression of society's denunciation of the offence or the objective of specific or general deterrence so requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743.6(1), may the court order that I serve one half of my sentence, or ten years, whichever is less, before full parole` IS
    `s 743.6(1) the court may order that the portion of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole is one half of the sentence or ten years, whichever is less` `the day I was sentenced` `my sentence of imprisonment` `my life sentence was imposed as a minimum punishment` `my offence is set out in Schedule I or II to the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` `my mode of prosecution` `the court is satisfied that denunciation or deterrence requires it`
    WHERE
        `my sentence of imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `my sentence is imprisonment for life`
            THEN `imprisonment for life`
            ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` WITH
                years IS `the years of my sentence of imprisonment`
                months IS `the months of my sentence of imprisonment`
                days IS `the days of my sentence of imprisonment`
                `less a day` IS `my sentence is described as less a day`)
        `my mode of prosecution` MEANS
            IF `I was prosecuted by indictment` THEN `by indictment` ELSE `on summary conviction`

@export Under section 743.6, how many months of my sentence must I serve before full parole if the court makes such an order?
GIVEN `my sentence is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence imprisonment for life?
      `the years of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years is the term of imprisonment? (the whole years)
      `the months of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months more? (0 if none)
      `the days of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days more? (0 if none)
      `my sentence is described as less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence described as "less a day" (for example "two years less a day")?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 743.6, how many months of my sentence must I serve before full parole if the court makes such an order` IS
    `s 743.6 the months of the sentence that must be served before the offender may be released on full parole under the order` `my sentence of imprisonment`
    WHERE
        `my sentence of imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `my sentence is imprisonment for life`
            THEN `imprisonment for life`
            ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` WITH
                years IS `the years of my sentence of imprisonment`
                months IS `the months of my sentence of imprisonment`
                days IS `the days of my sentence of imprisonment`
                `less a day` IS `my sentence is described as less a day`)

@export Under section 743.21(1), am I barred from communicating with this person while in custody?
GIVEN `an order was issued under subsection 743.21(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sentencing judge issued an order prohibiting you from communicating with a victim, witness or other person identified in the order?
      `the person is one the order identifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person a victim, a witness or another person identified in the order?
      `I am in the custodial period of my sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it during the custodial period of your sentence?
      `the communication is in accordance with the conditions in the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication in accordance with the conditions specified in the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743.21(1), am I barred from communicating with this person while in custody` IS
    `s 743.21(1) the offender is barred from communicating with the person` `an order was issued under subsection 743.21(1)` `the person is one the order identifies` `I am in the custodial period of my sentence` `the communication is in accordance with the conditions in the order`

@export Under section 743.21(2), am I guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the order?
GIVEN `I fail to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the order?
      `I have a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 743.21(2), am I guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the order` IS
    `s 743.21(2) the person is guilty of an offence` `I fail to comply with the order` `I have a lawful excuse`


§ `Sections 745 to 745.52 -- imprisonment for life`

@export Under section 745, what sentence must be pronounced against me if I am to be sentenced to imprisonment for life?
GIVEN `I am to be sentenced to imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you to be sentenced to imprisonment for life?
      `I was convicted of high treason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of high treason?
      `my offence is neither high treason nor a kind of homicide offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence neither high treason nor any kind of homicide offence?
      `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` IS MAYBE `Kind of homicide offence` @desc Which kind of homicide offence is it: first degree murder, second degree murder, manslaughter or infanticide? (leave blank if not decided)
      `I was previously convicted of murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you previously convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in the Code?
      `I was previously convicted of an intentional killing under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you previously convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing?
      `my manslaughter was in the circumstances of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)?
      `I was under 18 at the time of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under the age of 18 at the time of the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 745 sentence`
DECIDE `Under section 745, what sentence must be pronounced against me if I am to be sentenced to imprisonment for life` IS
    `s 745 the sentence to be pronounced` `I am to be sentenced to imprisonment for life` `I was convicted of high treason` `my offence is neither high treason nor a kind of homicide offence` `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` `I was previously convicted of murder` `I was previously convicted of an intentional killing under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `my manslaughter was in the circumstances of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` `I was under 18 at the time of the offence`

@export Under section 745, how many years must I serve before I am eligible for parole?
GIVEN `the sentence pronounced` IS A `s 745 sentence` @desc Which sentence was pronounced: (a), (b), (b.1), (c), (c.1) or (d) of section 745, or the sentence fixed by section 745.1?
      `the years the judge substituted under section 745.4` IS MAYBE NUMBER @desc How many years did the judge substitute for ten under section 745.4? (leave blank if none)
      `the years the judge substituted under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)` IS MAYBE NUMBER @desc How many years did the judge substitute for 10 under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)? (leave blank if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 745, how many years must I serve before I am eligible for parole` IS
    `s 745 the years of the sentence the person must serve before eligibility for parole` `the sentence pronounced` `the years the judge substituted under section 745.4` `the years the judge substituted under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)`

@export Under section 745.1, if I was under 18 at the time of the offence, how many years must I serve before I am eligible for parole?
GIVEN `my age at the time of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you at the time of the offence?
      `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` IS MAYBE `Kind of homicide offence` @desc Which kind of homicide offence is it: first degree murder, second degree murder, manslaughter or infanticide? (leave blank if not decided)
      `my manslaughter was in the circumstances of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)?
      `the years the judge specified` IS MAYBE NUMBER @desc Did the judge specify a period between five and seven years? If so, how many? (leave blank if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 745.1, if I was under 18 at the time of the offence, how many years must I serve before I am eligible for parole` IS
    `s 745.1 the years without eligibility for parole` `my age at the time of the offence` `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` `my manslaughter was in the circumstances of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` `the years the judge specified`

@export Under section 745.4, may the judge substitute for ten years a greater number of years without eligibility for parole?
GIVEN `this is the sentencing of an offender convicted of second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the time of the sentencing under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of second degree murder?
      `section 745.5 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 745.5 apply (an offender under sixteen at the time of the offence)?
      `the judge` IS A `s 745.4 judge` @desc Is the judge (1) the judge who presided at the trial, (2) another judge of the same court, or (3) a judge of another court?
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge who presided at the trial unable to do so?
      `the number of years proposed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years without eligibility for parole are proposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.4, may the judge substitute for ten years a greater number of years without eligibility for parole` IS
    `s 745.4 the judge may, by order, substitute for ten years a number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole` `this is the sentencing of an offender convicted of second degree murder` `section 745.5 applies` `the judge` `the presiding judge is unable to do so` `the number of years proposed`

@export Under section 745.51(1), may the judge order that the periods without eligibility for parole for each murder be served consecutively?
GIVEN `this is the sentencing of an offender convicted of murder who was already convicted of other murders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the time of sentencing under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of murder and who has already been convicted of one or more other murders?
      `the murders were committed after the day section 745.51 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the murders committed on a day after the day on which section 745.51 came into force, and are you sentenced under the Criminal Code, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act?
      `the judge` IS A `s 745.4 judge` @desc Is the judge (1) the judge who presided at the trial, (2) another judge of the same court, or (3) a judge of another court?
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge who presided at the trial unable to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.51(1), may the judge order that the periods without eligibility for parole for each murder be served consecutively` IS
    `s 745.51(1) the judge may, by order, decide that the periods without eligibility for parole for each murder conviction are to be served consecutively` `this is the sentencing of an offender convicted of murder who was already convicted of other murders` `the murders were committed after the day section 745.51 came into force` `the judge` `the presiding judge is unable to do so`

@export Under section 745.52(1), may the judge decide the number of years without eligibility for parole for my manslaughter?
GIVEN `the sentencing` IS A `s 745.52(1) sentencing` @desc Is this a sentencing under paragraph 745(c.1), a sentencing under paragraph 745.1(a), or another sentencing?
      `I was convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)?
      `the judge` IS A `s 745.4 judge` @desc Is the judge (1) the judge who presided at the trial, (2) another judge of the same court, or (3) a judge of another court?
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judge who presided at the trial unable to do so?
      `the number of years proposed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years without eligibility for parole are proposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.52(1), may the judge decide the number of years without eligibility for parole for my manslaughter` IS
    `s 745.52(1) the judge may, by order, decide the number of years without eligibility for parole` `the sentencing` `I was convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` `the judge` `the presiding judge is unable to do so` `the number of years proposed`


§ `Sections 745.6 to 745.64 -- review of the years without eligibility for parole`

@export Under section 745.6(1), may I apply for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole?
GIVEN `I was convicted of murder or high treason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of murder or high treason?
      `I committed it before the day paragraph 745.6(1)(a.1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit the murder or high treason before the day on which paragraph 745.6(1)(a.1) came into force?
      `the years without eligibility for parole I was sentenced to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole were you sentenced to?
      `the years of my sentence I have served` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of your sentence have you served?
      `I was convicted of more than one murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of more than one murder?
      `my application is in writing to the appropriate Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application in writing to the appropriate Chief Justice in the province in which your conviction took place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.6(1), may I apply for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole` IS
    `s 745.6(1) the person may apply for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole` `I was convicted of murder or high treason` `I committed it before the day paragraph 745.6(1)(a.1) came into force` `the years without eligibility for parole I was sentenced to` `the years of my sentence I have served` `I was convicted of more than one murder` `my application is in writing to the appropriate Chief Justice`

@export Under section 745.6(2.1), may I make an application under subsection (1) on this day, having served less than 15 years when subsection (2.1) came into force?
GIVEN `I was convicted of murder or high treason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of murder or high treason?
      `I had served less than 15 years on the day subsection (2.1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you served less than 15 years of your sentence on the day on which subsection 745.6(2.1) came into force?
      `the day I served 15 years of my sentence` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you serve 15 years of your sentence?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.6(2.1), may I make an application under subsection (1) on this day, having served less than 15 years when subsection (2.1) came into force` IS
    `s 745.6(2.1) the person may make an application under subsection (1) on the day` `I was convicted of murder or high treason` `I had served less than 15 years on the day subsection (2.1) came into force` `the day I served 15 years of my sentence` `the day in question`

@export Under section 745.6(2.2), may I make an application under subsection (1) on this day, having served at least 15 years when subsection (2.2) came into force?
GIVEN `I was convicted of murder or high treason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of murder or high treason?
      `I had served at least 15 years on the day subsection (2.2) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you served at least 15 years of your sentence on the day on which subsection 745.6(2.2) came into force?
      `the day of my determination` IS MAYBE DATE @desc On what day were you the subject of a determination under subsection 745.61(4), or of a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) applies? (leave blank if none)
      `the day subsection (2.2) came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did subsection 745.6(2.2) come into force?
      `I have not made an application under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not yet made an application under subsection (1)?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.6(2.2), may I make an application under subsection (1) on this day, having served at least 15 years when subsection (2.2) came into force` IS
    `s 745.6(2.2) the person may make an application under subsection (1) on the day` `I was convicted of murder or high treason` `I had served at least 15 years on the day subsection (2.2) came into force` `the day of my determination` `the day subsection (2.2) came into force` `I have not made an application under subsection (1)` `the day in question`

@export Under section 745.6(2.4), may I make an application under subsection (1) on this day, having made no application in time?
GIVEN `I made an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an application in accordance with subsection 745.6(2.1), (2.2) or (2.3)?
      `the last day of my 90-day period` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of the 90-day period referred to in that subsection?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.6(2.4), may I make an application under subsection (1) on this day, having made no application in time` IS
    `s 745.6(2.4) the person may make an application under subsection (1) on the day` `I made an application in accordance with subsection (2.1), (2.2) or (2.3)` `the last day of my 90-day period` `the day in question`

@export Under section 745.6(3), who is the appropriate Chief Justice for my conviction?
GIVEN `the province or territory where I was convicted` IS A `Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory did your conviction take place?
GIVETH A `s 745.6(3) Chief Justice`
DECIDE `Under section 745.6(3), who is the appropriate Chief Justice for my conviction` IS
    `s 745.6(3) the appropriate Chief Justice` `the province or territory where I was convicted`

@export Under section 745.61(4), may I make another application on this day after a determination that I had not shown a substantial likelihood of success?
GIVEN `the Chief Justice or judge determined that I had not shown a substantial likelihood of success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Chief Justice or judge determine that you had not shown that there is a substantial likelihood that the application will succeed?
      `a time was set or a decision made that I may not apply again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Chief Justice or judge set a time for another application, or decide that another application may not be made?
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the determination made?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.61(4), may I make another application on this day after a determination that I had not shown a substantial likelihood of success` IS
    `s 745.61(4) the applicant may make another application on the day` `the Chief Justice or judge determined that I had not shown a substantial likelihood of success` `a time was set or a decision made that I may not apply again` `the date of the determination` `the day in question`

@export Under section 745.62(1), may I appeal to the Court of Appeal from a determination or decision under section 745.61?
GIVEN `the appeal is from a determination or decision under section 745.61` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal from a determination or a decision made under section 745.61?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.62(1), may I appeal to the Court of Appeal from a determination or decision under section 745.61` IS
    `s 745.62(1) the appellant may appeal to the Court of Appeal on any question of law or fact or mixed law and fact` `s 745.62(1) the applicant` `the appeal is from a determination or decision under section 745.61`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (second seat audit): was "Under section 745.63(8), may I make another application on this day after the jury did not reduce my years"; the body does not compute that the years were not reduced, it takes the date of the determination or conclusion under subsection (4), so the title now says that and no more.
@export Under section 745.63(8), may I make another application on this day, after the jury's determination or conclusion under subsection (4)?
GIVEN `the jury set a date or decided that I may not apply again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the jury set a date on or after which another application may be made, or decide that such an application may not be made?
      `the date of the determination or conclusion` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the jury's determination or conclusion under subsection 745.63(4)?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 745.63(8), may I make another application on this day, after the jury's determination or conclusion under subsection (4)` IS
    `s 745.63(8) the applicant may make another application on the day` `the jury set a date or decided that I may not apply again` `the date of the determination or conclusion` `the day in question`


§ `Sections 746 to 746.1 -- time in custody and the bar on parole`

@export Under section 746, how many days in custody are included in calculating my period of imprisonment served?
GIVEN `the day I was arrested and taken into custody` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence?
      `the day the sentence was imposed or commuted` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the sentence imposed (or, for a sentence of death, commuted to imprisonment for life)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 746, how many days in custody are included in calculating my period of imprisonment served` IS
    `s 746 the days spent in custody that are included` `the day I was arrested and taken into custody` `the day the sentence was imposed or commuted`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (second seat audit): was "Under section 746.1(1), am I barred from being considered for parole until the years without eligibility have expired"; the body decides being considered for parole and being released pursuant to a grant of parole together, so the title now names both.
@export Under section 746.1(1), am I barred from being considered for parole, or from being released pursuant to a grant of parole, until the years without eligibility have expired?
GIVEN `I was sentenced to life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to the Criminal Code?
      `Parliament has otherwise provided by an enactment referring expressly to section 746.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Parliament otherwise provided, by an enactment making express reference to section 746.1?
      `the specified years have expired or been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the specified number of years of imprisonment expired or been terminated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 746.1(1), am I barred from being considered for parole, or from being released pursuant to a grant of parole, until the years without eligibility have expired` IS
    `s 746.1(1) the person is barred from being considered for parole or released pursuant to a grant of parole` `I was sentenced to life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years` `Parliament has otherwise provided by an enactment referring expressly to section 746.1` `the specified years have expired or been terminated`

@export Under section 746.1(2), am I barred from this kind of release until all but three years of the years without eligibility have been served?
GIVEN `I was sentenced to life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to the Criminal Code?
      `I was under 18 and convicted of murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder and under the age of eighteen at the time of the offence?
      `the specified years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years without eligibility for parole were specified?
      `the years I have served` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of imprisonment have you served?
      `the kind of release` IS A `s 746.1 kind of release` @desc Is the release (1) day parole, (2) an absence without escort, (3) an absence with escort other than for medical reasons or to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner's inquest, (4) an absence with escort for those reasons, or (5) another release?
      `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Parole Board of Canada approved the absence with escort?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 746.1(2), am I barred from this kind of release until all but three years of the years without eligibility have been served` IS
    `s 746.1(2) the kind of release is barred until the expiration of all but three years` `I was sentenced to life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years` `I was under 18 and convicted of murder` `the specified years` `the years I have served` `the kind of release` `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort`

@export Under section 746.1(3), am I barred from this kind of release until all but one fifth of the years without eligibility have been served?
GIVEN `I was convicted of first degree or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder?
      `I was under 18 at the time of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you under the age of eighteen at the time of the offence?
      `I was sentenced to life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to the Criminal Code?
      `the years I am to serve without eligibility` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years are you to serve without eligibility for parole?
      `the years I have served` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of imprisonment have you served?
      `the kind of release` IS A `s 746.1 kind of release` @desc Is the release (1) day parole, (2) an absence without escort, (3) an absence with escort other than for medical reasons or to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner's inquest, (4) an absence with escort for those reasons, or (5) another release?
      `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Parole Board of Canada approved the absence with escort?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 746.1(3), am I barred from this kind of release until all but one fifth of the years without eligibility have been served` IS
    `s 746.1(3) the kind of release is barred until the expiration of all but one fifth of the period` `I was convicted of first degree or second degree murder` `I was under 18 at the time of the offence` `I was sentenced to life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years` `the years I am to serve without eligibility` `the years I have served` `the kind of release` `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort`


§ `Sections 748 to 751.1 -- pardons, disabilities and costs`

@export Under section 748(2), may the Governor in Council grant me a free pardon or a conditional pardon?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offence?
      `the kind of pardon` IS A `s 748(2) kind of pardon` @desc Is the pardon a free pardon, a conditional pardon, or another kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 748(2), may the Governor in Council grant me a free pardon or a conditional pardon` IS
    `s 748(2) the Governor in Council may grant the pardon` `I have been convicted of an offence` `the kind of pardon`

@export Under section 748(3), am I deemed never to have committed the offence after a free pardon?
GIVEN `the Governor in Council granted me a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Governor in Council grant you a free pardon?
      `the offence is the one the pardon was granted for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the offence in respect of which the pardon was granted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 748(3), am I deemed never to have committed the offence after a free pardon` IS
    `s 748(3) the person is deemed thereafter never to have committed the offence` `the Governor in Council granted me a free pardon` `the offence is the one the pardon was granted for`

@export Under section 748(4), does a pardon prevent or mitigate my punishment on a later conviction for a different offence?
GIVEN `the pardon is a free pardon or a conditional pardon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the pardon a free pardon or a conditional pardon?
      `the later conviction is for a different offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsequent conviction for an offence other than the one for which the pardon was granted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 748(4), does a pardon prevent or mitigate my punishment on a later conviction for a different offence` IS
    `s 748(4) the pardon prevents or mitigates the punishment to which the person might otherwise be lawfully sentenced on the subsequent conviction` `the pardon is a free pardon or a conditional pardon` `the later conviction is for a different offence`

@export Under section 750(1), does my public office or employment become vacant on my conviction?
GIVEN `I am convicted of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you convicted of an indictable offence?
      `my sentence is imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence imprisonment for life?
      `the years of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years is the term of imprisonment? (the whole years)
      `the months of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months more? (0 if none)
      `the days of my sentence of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days more? (0 if none)
      `my sentence is described as less a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence described as "less a day" (for example "two years less a day")?
      `I hold an office under the Crown or other public employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, at the time you are convicted, an office under the Crown or other public employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 750(1), does my public office or employment become vacant on my conviction` IS
    `s 750(1) the office or employment becomes vacant` `I am convicted of an indictable offence` `my sentence of imprisonment` `I hold an office under the Crown or other public employment`
    WHERE
        `my sentence of imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `my sentence is imprisonment for life`
            THEN `imprisonment for life`
            ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` WITH
                years IS `the years of my sentence of imprisonment`
                months IS `the months of my sentence of imprisonment`
                days IS `the days of my sentence of imprisonment`
                `less a day` IS `my sentence is described as less a day`)

@export Under section 750(2), am I incapable of the capacity named, while the disability in subsection (2) lasts?
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies to me` IS MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 750(1) apply to you? (leave blank if not decided)
      `the capacity` IS A `s 750(2) capacity` @desc Is it (1) holding an office under the Crown or other public employment, (2) being elected as a member of Parliament or of a legislature, (3) sitting or voting as a member, (4) exercising a right of suffrage, or (5) another capacity?
      `I have undergone the punishment imposed or substituted for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you undergone the punishment imposed on you, or the punishment substituted for it by competent authority?
      `I have received a free pardon from Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received a free pardon from Her Majesty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 750(2), am I incapable of the capacity named, while the disability in subsection (2) lasts` IS
    `s 750(2) the person is incapable of the capacity` `subsection (1) applies to me` `the capacity` `I have undergone the punishment imposed or substituted for it` `I have received a free pardon from Her Majesty`

-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (second seat audit): was "Under section 750(3), do I have capacity to contract with Her Majesty after my conviction"; the body decides three capacities together (to contract, to receive a benefit under a contract, to hold office), so the title now names all three.
@export Under section 750(3), do I have, after my conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty?
GIVEN `I am convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you convicted of the offence?
      `the section of my offence` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Code is the offence? (for example 121, 124, 418 or 380)
      `the offence under section 380 was committed against Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an offence under section 380, was it committed against Her Majesty?
      `my offence is one under the Financial Administration Act named in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offence under paragraph 80(1)(d), subsection 80(2) or section 154.01 of the Financial Administration Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 750(3), do I have, after my conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` IS
    `s 750(3) the person has, after the conviction, capacity to contract with Her Majesty, to receive any benefit under a contract between Her Majesty and any other person, or to hold office under Her Majesty` `I am convicted of the offence` (`Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS `the section of my offence`, `subsection` IS "") `the offence under section 380 was committed against Her Majesty` `my offence is one under the Financial Administration Act named in subsection (3)`

@export Under section 750(4), may I apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of the capacities I lost?
GIVEN `subsection (3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 750(3) apply to you?
      `a record suspension I applied for was ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a record suspension for which you applied been ordered under the Criminal Records Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 750(4), may I apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of the capacities I lost` IS
    `s 750(4) the person may apply to the Governor in Council for the restoration of one or more of the capacities lost` `subsection (3) applies to me` `a record suspension I applied for was ordered`

@export Under section 751.1, may the party who won enter judgment against me for the costs fixed under section 751?
GIVEN `the costs were fixed under section 751` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the costs fixed under section 751?
      `the costs were not paid forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the costs not paid forthwith?
      `the order is filed in a civil court with jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the order been filed in a civil court of the province in which the trial was held that has jurisdiction to enter a judgment for that amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 751.1, may the party who won enter judgment against me for the costs fixed under section 751` IS
    `s 751.1 the party in whose favour judgment is given may enter judgment for the amount of the costs` `the costs were fixed under section 751` `the costs were not paid forthwith` `the order is filed in a civil court with jurisdiction`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc28 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc28-seat.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Parts XXIV to XXVI (sections 752 to 784) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code, asking on facts they can state what the Code says about a person who faces
-- an application to be found a dangerous offender or a long-term offender (Part XXIV), about the effect and enforcement of the undertaking, release order
-- or recognizance they or their sureties are bound by (Part XXV), and about the extraordinary remedies of certiorari, habeas corpus, mandamus,
-- procedendo and prohibition (Part XXVI). Nothing here is new law: each question calls the rule of the layer-1 modules imported above.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), one per fact the person can state, each with an @desc
-- worded as that person would be asked. The records the modules expect (an offence, a punishment limb, a previous conviction, a length of time) are built
-- inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called. A record field the rule never reads is given a fixed
-- placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER. Each question returns a MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE is yes on the facts given; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; NOTHING is
-- 'not covered' (the text is silent, or its grant or prohibition is limited by its own wording and the facts fall outside the limit). A question that asks
-- whether a provision BARS something is titled as the bar: JUST TRUE means the bar applies, and JUST FALSE or NOTHING is not a grant.
--
-- LIMITS. (1) The offence is stated by the Code, section, subsection or paragraph and the way the person was convicted; a coarser statement than the list names
-- (the section alone where the list names a paragraph) is not matched. (2) Previous convictions are asked up to two and are taken as offences under the Code
-- as it now reads. (3) The court's own judgments (satisfied, of the opinion, reasonable grounds, considers proper) are asked as facts, never guessed.
-- (4) The Schedule to Part XXV and sections 734.4 and 2 are other parts' ranges: their answers are inputs where a rule needs them. (5) The text states no
-- period for most of the court's orders in these Parts, so no time limit is asked for them.



§ `Helpers (not law): building the module records from plain inputs`

-- helper: the offence record of section 752, built from the plain inputs.
GIVEN source IS A `s 752 source of the offence`
      section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A STRING
      implication IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated`
      committed IS A DATE
      intent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 752 offence`
`s 752 seat build the offence` MEANS
    `s 752 offence` OF source, (`Provision of the Code` OF section, subsection), implication, committed, intent

-- helper: the imprisonment a penalty limb allows, from "does it allow life" and "how many years at most (0 if none stated)".
GIVEN life IS A BOOLEAN
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Imprisonment
`s 752 seat the imprisonment the section allows` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF life THEN `imprisonment for life`
        IF years GREATER THAN 0 THEN `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF years, 0, 0, FALSE)
        OTHERWISE `no imprisonment is stated`

-- helper: a previous conviction record of section 752.01, built from the plain inputs (the offence is under this Act as it now reads, the conviction itself).
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A STRING
      years IS A NUMBER
      family IS A BOOLEAN
      spio IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 752.01 previous conviction`
`s 752.01 seat build the previous conviction` MEANS
    `s 752.01 previous conviction` OF
        (`s 752 offence` OF `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`, (`Provision of the Code` OF section, subsection), `s 752 convicted of the offence itself`, (Date 1 1 2020), FALSE),   -- placeholder: the date and the intent are not read for an offence under this Act as it now reads
        (`Length of time` OF years, 0, 0, FALSE),
        family,
        JUST spio

§ `Part XXIV: dangerous offenders and long-term offenders`
-- These questions arise only for a person who has been, or may be, convicted of a serious offence and faces an application to be found a dangerous offender or a long-term offender. The form can ask 'Have you been convicted of a serious offence and does the prosecutor intend to apply under Part XXIV?' before showing them.

-- Section 752, paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition of 'serious personal injury offence'. The offence is stated as the Code, the section, the subsection or paragraph, and how the person was convicted; the penalty limb of that section and the conduct are asked as facts. 'No' is the definition's own closed list (it 'means'); 'not covered' is a limb that states no imprisonment.
@export Under section 752, is the offence I was convicted of a serious personal injury offence?
GIVEN `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence first degree murder or second degree murder?
      `the way I was prosecuted for the offence` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Were you prosecuted by indictment or on summary conviction for the offence?
      `the section allows imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the section you were convicted under allow imprisonment for life?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the section allows, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in years, that the section allows, other than life? (0 if the section states none.)
      `my conduct was in respect of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your conduct in the offence in respect of another person?
      `my conduct was the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve the use or attempted use of violence against the other person?
      `my conduct endangered or was likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person?
      `my conduct inflicted or was likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 752, is the offence I was convicted of a serious personal injury offence` IS
    `s 752 the offence is a serious personal injury offence` `my offence` `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` `the limb of the penalty provision` `my conduct`
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE   -- placeholder: this rule does not read the date or the intent
        `the limb of the penalty provision` MEANS Punishment OF `the way I was prosecuted for the offence`, (`s 752 seat the imprisonment the section allows` `the section allows imprisonment for life` `the longest term of imprisonment the section allows, in years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- the limb's minimum and fines are not read by the rule
        `my conduct` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF `my conduct was in respect of another person`, `my conduct was the use or attempted use of violence against the other person`, `my conduct endangered or was likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person`, `my conduct inflicted or was likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person`

-- Section 752, the definition of 'designated offence' (a primary designated offence, or one of the listed provisions of this Act or of the former Code, or an attempt or conspiracy to commit one). 'No' is the definition's own closed list.
@export Under section 752, is the offence I was convicted of a designated offence?
GIVEN `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `the date I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you commit the offence? (Only the former Code turns on the date.)
      `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offence is former subsection 246(1): was your intent to commit one of the offences in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b) of the definition of primary designated offence? (No if the question does not arise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 752, is the offence I was convicted of a designated offence` IS
    `s 752 the offence is a designated offence` `my offence`
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` `the date I committed the offence` `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)`

-- Section 752, the definition of 'primary designated offence'. 'No' is the definition's own closed list.
@export Under section 752, is the offence I was convicted of a primary designated offence?
GIVEN `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `the date I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you commit the offence? (Only the former Code turns on the date.)
      `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offence is former subsection 246(1): was your intent to commit one of the offences in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b) of the definition of primary designated offence? (No if the question does not arise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 752, is the offence I was convicted of a primary designated offence` IS
    `s 752 the offence is a primary designated offence` `my offence`
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` `the date I committed the offence` `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)`

-- Section 752.01: the prosecutor's duty to advise the court whether they intend to apply under subsection 752.1(1). The seat asks two previous convictions (the section's counts are 'at least two'); a previous conviction is taken as an offence under the Code as it now reads, so the former Code is not asked of previous convictions (limit, NOTES.md). An unknown or absent previous conviction is entered with section 0.
@export Under section 752.01, must the prosecutor advise the court whether they intend to apply for me to be assessed?
GIVEN `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the offence is a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prosecutor of the opinion that the offence you were found guilty of is a serious personal injury offence?
      `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `the date I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you commit the offence? (Only the former Code turns on the date.)
      `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offence is former subsection 246(1): was your intent to commit one of the offences in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b) of the definition of primary designated offence? (No if the question does not arise.)
      `the offence was committed against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed against your intimate partner, or a member of your family or of your intimate partner's family?
      `the section number of my first previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence of your first previous conviction? (0 if you have no such conviction.)
      `the subsection or paragraph of my first previous conviction` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph, as the Code writes it? (Empty if only the section is known.)
      `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my first previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years were you sentenced to imprisonment for that conviction? (0 if none.)
      `my first previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence committed against your intimate partner, or a member of your family or of your intimate partner's family?
      `my first previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence a serious personal injury offence?
      `the section number of my second previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence of your second previous conviction? (0 if you have no such conviction.)
      `the subsection or paragraph of my second previous conviction` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph, as the Code writes it? (Empty if only the section is known.)
      `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my second previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years were you sentenced to imprisonment for that conviction? (0 if none.)
      `my second previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence committed against your intimate partner, or a member of your family or of your intimate partner's family?
      `my second previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence a serious personal injury offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 752.01, must the prosecutor advise the court whether they intend to apply for me to be assessed` IS
    `s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the offence is a serious personal injury offence` `my offence` `the offence was committed against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` `my previous convictions`
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` `the date I committed the offence` `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)`
        `my first previous conviction` MEANS `s 752.01 seat build the previous conviction` `the section number of my first previous conviction` `the subsection or paragraph of my first previous conviction` `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my first previous conviction` `my first previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` `my first previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence`
        `my second previous conviction` MEANS `s 752.01 seat build the previous conviction` `the section number of my second previous conviction` `the subsection or paragraph of my second previous conviction` `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my second previous conviction` `my second previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` `my second previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence`
        `my previous convictions` MEANS LIST `my first previous conviction`, `my second previous conviction`

-- Section 752.1(1): on the prosecutor's application, if the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the offender might be found a dangerous offender or a long-term offender, the court shall remand the offender for assessment. The offence is stated so that the rules of section 752 and of section 753.1(2)(a) decide whether it is one the subsection names.
@export Under section 752.1(1), shall the court remand me for an assessment?
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied for me to be remanded for an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecutor applied for you to be remanded for an assessment?
      `the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that I might be found a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that you might be found a dangerous offender or a long-term offender?
      `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence first degree murder or second degree murder?
      `the way I was prosecuted for the offence` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Were you prosecuted by indictment or on summary conviction for the offence?
      `the section allows imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the section you were convicted under allow imprisonment for life?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the section allows, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in years, that the section allows, other than life? (0 if the section states none.)
      `my conduct was in respect of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your conduct in the offence in respect of another person?
      `my conduct was the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve the use or attempted use of violence against the other person?
      `my conduct endangered or was likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person?
      `my conduct inflicted or was likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 752.1(1), shall the court remand me for an assessment` IS
    `s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` `the prosecutor has applied for me to be remanded for an assessment` `the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that I might be found a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` (`s 752 the offence is a serious personal injury offence` `my offence` `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` `the limb of the penalty provision` `my conduct`) (`s 753.1(2)(a) the offence is one the paragraph names` `my offence`)
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE   -- placeholder: this rule does not read the date or the intent
        `the limb of the penalty provision` MEANS Punishment OF `the way I was prosecuted for the offence`, (`s 752 seat the imprisonment the section allows` `the section allows imprisonment for life` `the longest term of imprisonment the section allows, in years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- the limb's minimum and fines are not read by the rule
        `my conduct` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF `my conduct was in respect of another person`, `my conduct was the use or attempted use of violence against the other person`, `my conduct endangered or was likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person`, `my conduct inflicted or was likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person`

-- Section 753(1): after an assessment report is filed, the court shall find the offender a dangerous offender if satisfied of the matters in paragraph (a) or (b). Whether the court is satisfied is stated as the facts the court is satisfied of.
@export Under section 753(1), shall the court find me to be a dangerous offender?
GIVEN `an application was made under Part XXIV after an assessment report was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an application made under Part XXIV after an assessment report was filed?
      `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence first degree murder or second degree murder?
      `the way I was prosecuted for the offence` IS A `Mode of proceeding` @desc Were you prosecuted by indictment or on summary conviction for the offence?
      `the section allows imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the section you were convicted under allow imprisonment for life?
      `the longest term of imprisonment the section allows, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in years, that the section allows, other than life? (0 if the section states none.)
      `my conduct was in respect of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your conduct in the offence in respect of another person?
      `my conduct was the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve the use or attempted use of violence against the other person?
      `my conduct endangered or was likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person?
      `my conduct inflicted or was likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offence involve conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person?
      `the court is satisfied that I constitute a threat to the life, safety or physical or mental well-being of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that you constitute a threat to the life, safety or physical or mental well-being of other persons?
      `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of repetitive behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of repetitive behaviour showing a likelihood of death, injury or severe psychological damage to other persons (paragraph (a)(i))?
      `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of persistent aggressive behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of persistent aggressive behaviour showing a substantial degree of indifference to the consequences (paragraph (a)(ii))?
      `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes behaviour of such a brutal nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the evidence establishes behaviour of such a brutal nature that normal standards of behavioural restraint are unlikely to restrain it (paragraph (a)(iii))?
      `the court is satisfied that I have shown a failure to control my sexual impulses and a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that, by your conduct in a sexual matter, you have shown a failure to control your sexual impulses and a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons (paragraph (b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753(1), shall the court find me to be a dangerous offender` IS
    `s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` `an application was made under Part XXIV after an assessment report was filed` `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (a)` `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (b)` `the court is satisfied that I constitute a threat to the life, safety or physical or mental well-being of other persons` `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of repetitive behaviour` `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of persistent aggressive behaviour` `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes behaviour of such a brutal nature` `the court is satisfied that I have shown a failure to control my sexual impulses and a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil`
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE   -- placeholder: this rule does not read the date or the intent
        `the limb of the penalty provision` MEANS Punishment OF `the way I was prosecuted for the offence`, (`s 752 seat the imprisonment the section allows` `the section allows imprisonment for life` `the longest term of imprisonment the section allows, in years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- the limb's minimum and fines are not read by the rule
        `my conduct` MEANS `s 752 conduct in the offence` OF `my conduct was in respect of another person`, `my conduct was the use or attempted use of violence against the other person`, `my conduct endangered or was likely to endanger the life or safety of the other person`, `my conduct inflicted or was likely to inflict severe psychological damage on the other person`
        `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (a)` MEANS `s 752 serious personal injury offence (a)` `my offence` `the offence is first degree murder or second degree murder` `the limb of the penalty provision` `my conduct`
        `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (b)` MEANS `s 752 serious personal injury offence (b)` `my offence`

-- Section 753(1.1): the presumption for a repeat primary designated offender, rebuttable on a balance of probabilities. 'Each of those convictions' is read as at least two previous convictions each of a primary designated offence with two years of imprisonment or more (fork, NOTES.md). The seat asks two previous convictions; one with section 0 counts for nothing.
@export Under section 753(1.1), are the conditions for a dangerous offender finding presumed to have been met?
GIVEN `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `the date I committed the offence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you commit the offence? (Only the former Code turns on the date.)
      `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offence is former subsection 246(1): was your intent to commit one of the offences in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b) of the definition of primary designated offence? (No if the question does not arise.)
      `the court is satisfied that a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more would be appropriate for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more for the offence?
      `the section number of my first previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence of your first previous conviction? (0 if you have no such conviction.)
      `the subsection or paragraph of my first previous conviction` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph, as the Code writes it? (Empty if only the section is known.)
      `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my first previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years were you sentenced to imprisonment for that conviction? (0 if none.)
      `my first previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence committed against your intimate partner, or a member of your family or of your intimate partner's family?
      `my first previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence a serious personal injury offence?
      `the section number of my second previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence of your second previous conviction? (0 if you have no such conviction.)
      `the subsection or paragraph of my second previous conviction` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph, as the Code writes it? (Empty if only the section is known.)
      `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my second previous conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years were you sentenced to imprisonment for that conviction? (0 if none.)
      `my second previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence committed against your intimate partner, or a member of your family or of your intimate partner's family?
      `my second previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that offence a serious personal injury offence?
      `the contrary is proved on a balance of probabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved on a balance of probabilities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753(1.1), are the conditions for a dangerous offender finding presumed to have been met` IS
    `s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` `my offence` `the court is satisfied that a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more would be appropriate for the offence` `my previous convictions` `the contrary is proved on a balance of probabilities`
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` `the date I committed the offence` `my intent was to commit an offence in subparagraphs (i) to (v) of paragraph (b)`
        `my first previous conviction` MEANS `s 752.01 seat build the previous conviction` `the section number of my first previous conviction` `the subsection or paragraph of my first previous conviction` `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my first previous conviction` `my first previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` `my first previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence`
        `my second previous conviction` MEANS `s 752.01 seat build the previous conviction` `the section number of my second previous conviction` `the subsection or paragraph of my second previous conviction` `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to for my second previous conviction` `my second previous conviction was against my intimate partner or a member of their or my family` `my second previous conviction was a serious personal injury offence`
        `my previous convictions` MEANS LIST `my first previous conviction`, `my second previous conviction`

-- Section 753(2): the application must be made before sentence is imposed, unless the notice and evidence conditions of paragraphs (a) and (b) are met and it is made not later than six months after sentence. Six months is counted by date (the day clamped to the end of a shorter month).
@export Under section 753(2), is the application for a dangerous offender finding made in time?
GIVEN `the application is made before sentence is imposed on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made before sentence is imposed on you?
      `before sentence the prosecutor gave me notice of a possible intention to apply under section 752.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before sentence was imposed, did the prosecutor give you notice of a possible intention to make an application under section 752.1?
      `relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of sentence became available in the interim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it shown that relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of sentence became available in the interim?
      `the date sentence was imposed on me` IS A DATE @desc On what date was sentence imposed on you?
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the application made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753(2), is the application for a dangerous offender finding made in time` IS
    `s 753(2) the application under subsection (1) is made in time` `the application is made before sentence is imposed on me` (`s 753(2)(a) and (b) apply` `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS `s 753(2)(a) the notice was given and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` `before sentence the prosecutor gave me notice of a possible intention to apply under section 752.1` `the date sentence was imposed on me` `the date of the application`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS `s 753(2)(b) relevant evidence became available in the interim and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` `relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of sentence became available in the interim` `the date sentence was imposed on me` `the date of the application`

-- Section 753(4.1): the court shall impose an indeterminate sentence unless satisfied that a lesser measure will adequately protect the public.
@export Under section 753(4.1), shall the court impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period?
GIVEN `the court has found me to be a dangerous offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court found you to be a dangerous offender?
      `the court is satisfied by the evidence that there is a reasonable expectation that a lesser measure will adequately protect the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that a lesser measure under paragraph 753(4)(b) or (c) will adequately protect the public against the commission by you of murder or a serious personal injury offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753(4.1), shall the court impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` IS
    `s 753(4.1) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` `the court has found me to be a dangerous offender` `the court is satisfied by the evidence that there is a reasonable expectation that a lesser measure will adequately protect the public`

-- Section 753(5): if the court does not find the offender a dangerous offender it may treat the application as one to find a long-term offender, find that, hold another hearing, or impose sentence. A power under an 'if' gate: when the court did find a dangerous offender the answer is 'not covered', not 'no'.
@export Under section 753(5), may the court take this course?
GIVEN `the court does not find me to be a dangerous offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court decline to find you to be a dangerous offender?
      `the course the court takes` IS A `s 753(5) course` @desc Which course does the court take: treating the application as one to find a long-term offender, finding that you are a long-term offender, holding another hearing for that purpose, or imposing sentence for the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753(5), may the court take this course` IS
    `s 753(5) the court may take this course` `the court does not find me to be a dangerous offender` `the course the court takes`

-- Section 753.01(5): on an application by the prosecutor, after a dangerous offender's later conviction, the court shall impose an indeterminate sentence unless satisfied that a sentence for the offence will adequately protect the public.
@export Under section 753.01(5), shall the court impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period?
GIVEN `the application is for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period?
      `the court is satisfied by the evidence that a sentence for the offence, with or without a new period of long-term supervision, will adequately protect the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that a sentence for the offence, with or without a new period of long-term supervision, will adequately protect the public against the commission by you of murder or a serious personal injury offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.01(5), shall the court impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` IS
    `s 753.01(5) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` `the application is for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` `the court is satisfied by the evidence that a sentence for the offence, with or without a new period of long-term supervision, will adequately protect the public`

-- Section 753.01(6): on an application for a new period of long-term supervision the court shall so order unless satisfied that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public.
@export Under section 753.01(6), shall the court order that I be subject to a new period of long-term supervision?
GIVEN `the application is for a new period of long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for a new period of long-term supervision?
      `the court is satisfied by the evidence that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public against the commission by you of murder or a serious personal injury offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.01(6), shall the court order that I be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` IS
    `s 753.01(6) the court shall order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` `the application is for a new period of long-term supervision` `the court is satisfied by the evidence that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public`

-- Section 753.1(1): on application following the filing of an assessment report the court may find an offender a long-term offender if satisfied of paragraphs (a) to (c). A power: no application is 'no'; an 'if' gate that is not met is 'not covered'.
@export Under section 753.1(1), may the court find me to be a long-term offender?
GIVEN `an application was made following the filing of an assessment report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an application made under Part XXIV following the filing of an assessment report?
      `the court is satisfied that a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more would be appropriate for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more for the offence?
      `the court is satisfied that there is a substantial risk that I will reoffend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that there is a substantial risk that you will reoffend?
      `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable possibility of eventual control of the risk in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that there is a reasonable possibility of eventual control of the risk in the community?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.1(1), may the court find me to be a long-term offender` IS
    `s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` `an application was made following the filing of an assessment report` `the court is satisfied that a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more would be appropriate for the offence` `the court is satisfied that there is a substantial risk that I will reoffend` `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable possibility of eventual control of the risk in the community`

-- Section 753.1(2): the court shall be satisfied that there is a substantial risk of reoffending if (a) the offender was convicted of one of the listed offences, or engaged in serious conduct of a sexual nature in another offence, and (b) shows one of two patterns. 'No' is the subsection's own 'if'.
@export Under section 753.1(2), shall the court be satisfied that there is a substantial risk that I will reoffend?
GIVEN `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` IS A `s 752 source of the offence` @desc Which Code is the offence you were convicted of under? Choose: this Act as it now reads; the former Criminal Code (chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970); the former Code as enacted by section 19 of chapter 125 of the Statutes of Canada, 1980-81-82-83; or this Act as it read before paragraph (c.1) of the definition of designated offence came into force.
      `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence you were convicted of, as a number (for example 271, or 153.1)?
      `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` IS A STRING @desc What subsection or paragraph of that section, as the Code writes it (for example (1)(a))? Leave it empty if you only know the section.
      `how I was convicted of the offence` IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated` @desc Were you convicted of the offence itself, of an attempt to commit it, or of a conspiracy to commit it?
      `I engaged in serious conduct of a sexual nature in the commission of another offence of which I have been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you engage in serious conduct of a sexual nature in the commission of another offence of which you have been convicted?
      `I have shown a pattern of repetitive behaviour that shows a likelihood of causing death or injury or inflicting severe psychological damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you shown a pattern of repetitive behaviour, of which the offence forms a part, that shows a likelihood of your causing death or injury to other persons or inflicting severe psychological damage on other persons (paragraph (b)(i))?
      `by my conduct in a sexual matter I have shown a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons through similar offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By your conduct in any sexual matter, including that involved in the offence, have you shown a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons in the future through similar offences (paragraph (b)(ii))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.1(2), shall the court be satisfied that there is a substantial risk that I will reoffend` IS
    `s 753.1(2) the court shall be satisfied that there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend` `my offence` `I engaged in serious conduct of a sexual nature in the commission of another offence of which I have been convicted` `I have shown a pattern of repetitive behaviour that shows a likelihood of causing death or injury or inflicting severe psychological damage` `by my conduct in a sexual matter I have shown a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons through similar offences`
    WHERE
        `my offence` MEANS `s 752 seat build the offence` `the Code the offence I was convicted of is under` `the section number of the offence I was convicted of` `the subsection or paragraph of the offence I was convicted of` `how I was convicted of the offence` (Date 1 1 2020) FALSE   -- placeholder: this rule does not read the date or the intent

-- Section 753.1(3): a minimum sentence of two years of imprisonment, and long-term supervision not exceeding ten years.
@export Under section 753.1(3), are the sentence and the order I received within the limits in paragraphs (a) and (b)?
GIVEN `the court has found me to be a long-term offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court found you to be a long-term offender?
      `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole years of imprisonment were you sentenced to?
      `the extra months of imprisonment I was sentenced to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many extra months of imprisonment (beyond the whole years)?
      `the years of long-term supervision ordered` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many whole years were you ordered to be subject to long-term supervision?
      `the extra months of long-term supervision ordered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many extra months of long-term supervision (beyond the whole years)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.1(3), are the sentence and the order I received within the limits in paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS
    `s 753.1(3) the sentence and order are within paragraphs (a) and (b)` `the court has found me to be a long-term offender` `my term of imprisonment` `my period of long-term supervision`
    WHERE
        `my term of imprisonment` MEANS `Length of time` OF `the years of imprisonment I was sentenced to`, `the extra months of imprisonment I was sentenced to`, 0, FALSE
        `my period of long-term supervision` MEANS `Length of time` OF `the years of long-term supervision ordered`, `the extra months of long-term supervision ordered`, 0, FALSE

-- Section 753.2(1): an offender subject to long-term supervision shall be supervised in the community once they have finished serving the sentence and all other sentences of imprisonment. A person not subject to long-term supervision is outside the subsection.
@export Under section 753.2(1), shall I be supervised in the community?
GIVEN `I am subject to long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to long-term supervision?
      `I have finished serving the sentence for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you finished serving the sentence for the offence?
      `I have finished serving all other sentences of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you finished serving all other sentences of imprisonment, imposed before or after the conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.2(1), shall I be supervised in the community` IS
    `s 753.2(1) the offender shall be supervised in the community` `I am subject to long-term supervision` `I have finished serving the sentence for the offence` `I have finished serving all other sentences of imprisonment`

-- Section 753.2(3): the offender, a member of the Parole Board of Canada, or (on the Board's approval) the offender's parole supervisor may apply to a superior court of criminal jurisdiction on the ground that the offender no longer presents a substantial risk. The applicant is chosen from the list, and the answer is given for that applicant.
@export Under section 753.2(3), may this applicant apply for an order reducing or terminating the period of long-term supervision?
GIVEN `who is applying` IS A `s 753.2(3) applicant` @desc Who is applying: you (the offender), a member of the Parole Board of Canada, your parole supervisor with the Board's approval, your parole supervisor without it, or someone else?
      `the court applied to is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made to a superior court of criminal jurisdiction?
      `the ground is that I no longer present a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground that you no longer present a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.2(3), may this applicant apply for an order reducing or terminating the period of long-term supervision` IS
    `s 753.2(3) the applicant may apply for an order reducing or terminating the period of long-term supervision` `who is applying` (JUST `the court applied to is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`) `the ground is that I no longer present a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community`

-- Section 753.3(1): an offender who, without reasonable excuse, fails or refuses to comply with long-term supervision is guilty of an indictable offence (not more than 10 years) or an offence punishable on summary conviction. 'Without reasonable excuse' limits the offence: an offender with a reasonable excuse is 'not covered', not 'no'.
@export Under section 753.3(1), am I guilty of an offence for failing to comply with long-term supervision?
GIVEN `I am subject to long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to long-term supervision?
      `I failed or refused to comply with long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail or refuse to comply with your long-term supervision?
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.3(1), am I guilty of an offence for failing to comply with long-term supervision` IS
    `s 753.3(1) the offender is guilty of an offence` `I am subject to long-term supervision` `I failed or refused to comply with long-term supervision` `I had a reasonable excuse`

-- Section 753.4(1): where an offender subject to long-term supervision commits an offence and a court imposes imprisonment, the supervision is interrupted until all sentences are served, unless the court orders its termination.
@export Under section 753.4(1), is my long-term supervision interrupted?
GIVEN `I am subject to long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to long-term supervision?
      `I committed one or more offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit one or more offences under this or any other Act?
      `a court imposed a sentence of imprisonment for the offence or offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a court impose a sentence of imprisonment for the offence or offences?
      `I have finished serving all the sentences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you finished serving all the sentences?
      `the court ordered the termination of the long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court order the termination of the long-term supervision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 753.4(1), is my long-term supervision interrupted` IS
    `s 753.4(1) the long-term supervision is interrupted` `I am subject to long-term supervision` `I committed one or more offences` `a court imposed a sentence of imprisonment for the offence or offences` `I have finished serving all the sentences` `the court ordered the termination of the long-term supervision`

-- Section 754(1): except for an application for remand for assessment, the court may not hear an application under Part XXIV unless the Attorney General consented, at least seven days' notice was given following the application, and a copy was filed. JUST TRUE means the court may not hear it; JUST FALSE means this subsection does not bar it.
@export Under section 754(1), does the section bar the court from hearing the application?
GIVEN `the application is an application for remand for assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application an application for remand for assessment?
      `the Attorney General of the province in which I was tried has consented to the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General of the province in which you were tried consented to the application, before or after it was made?
      `the number of days of notice the prosecutor gave me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of notice did the prosecutor give you, outlining the basis of the application?
      `the notice was given following the making of the application and outlined its basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given following the making of the application, outlining the basis on which it is intended to found the application?
      `a copy of the notice has been filed with the clerk of the court or the provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the notice been filed with the clerk of the court or the provincial court judge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 754(1), does the section bar the court from hearing the application` IS
    `s 754(1) the court may not hear the application` `the application is an application for remand for assessment` `the Attorney General of the province in which I was tried has consented to the application` `the number of days of notice the prosecutor gave me` `the notice was given following the making of the application and outlined its basis` `a copy of the notice has been filed with the clerk of the court or the provincial court judge`

-- Section 755(1): the court shall not order long-term supervision for an offender sentenced to life imprisonment. JUST TRUE means the court shall not; JUST FALSE means this subsection does not bar it.
@export Under section 755(1), does the section bar the court from ordering that I be subject to long-term supervision?
GIVEN `I have been sentenced to life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been sentenced to life imprisonment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 755(1), does the section bar the court from ordering that I be subject to long-term supervision` IS
    `s 755(1) the court shall not order that the offender be subject to long-term supervision` `I have been sentenced to life imprisonment`

-- Section 755(2): the periods of long-term supervision to which an offender is subject at any time must not total more than 10 years. The seat asks up to three periods (whole years and extra months); enter 0 for a period you do not have. A month is read as 28 to 31 days only where days are given; here only whole years and months are asked, so the answer is exact.
@export Under section 755(2), do my periods of long-term supervision total no more than 10 years?
GIVEN `the years of my first period of long-term supervision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole years is your first period of long-term supervision?
      `the extra months of my first period of long-term supervision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many extra months in that period?
      `the years of my second period of long-term supervision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole years is your second period (0 if none)?
      `the extra months of my second period of long-term supervision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many extra months in that period?
      `the years of my third period of long-term supervision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole years is your third period (0 if none)?
      `the extra months of my third period of long-term supervision` IS A NUMBER @desc How many extra months in that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 755(2), do my periods of long-term supervision total no more than 10 years` IS
    `s 755(2) the periods of long-term supervision do not total more than 10 years` `my periods`
    WHERE
        `my periods` MEANS LIST (`Length of time` OF `the years of my first period of long-term supervision`, `the extra months of my first period of long-term supervision`, 0, FALSE), (`Length of time` OF `the years of my second period of long-term supervision`, `the extra months of my second period of long-term supervision`, 0, FALSE), (`Length of time` OF `the years of my third period of long-term supervision`, `the extra months of my third period of long-term supervision`, 0, FALSE)

-- Section 758(1): the offender shall be present at the hearing of the application. Subsection (2) lets the court have the offender removed or permit them to be out of court.
@export Under section 758(1), must I be present at the hearing of the application?
GIVEN `the application is to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an application under Part XXIV to be heard?
      `the court has removed me or permitted me to be out of court under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court had you removed from court for misconduct, or permitted you to be out of court, under subsection (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 758(1), must I be present at the hearing of the application` IS
    `s 758(1) the offender shall be present at the hearing of the application` `the application is to be heard` `the court has removed me or permitted me to be out of court under subsection (2)`

-- Section 759(1): an offender found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender may appeal from a decision made under Part XXIV on any ground of law or fact or mixed law and fact.
@export Under section 759(1), may I appeal to the court of appeal?
GIVEN `I was found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender?
      `the appeal is from a decision made under Part XXIV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal from a decision made under Part XXIV?
      `the ground of my appeal` IS A `s 759 ground of appeal` @desc Is the ground a ground of law, a ground of fact, a ground of mixed law and fact, or another ground?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 759(1), may I appeal to the court of appeal` IS
    `s 759(1) the offender may appeal to the court of appeal` `I was found to be a dangerous offender or a long-term offender` `the appeal is from a decision made under Part XXIV` `the ground of my appeal`

-- Section 761(1): where a person is in custody under an indeterminate sentence, the Parole Board shall review as soon as possible after seven years from custody and every two years after, subject to subsection (2) for sentences imposed before 15 October 1977.
@export Under section 761(1), shall the Parole Board of Canada review my condition, history and circumstances?
GIVEN `I am in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period?
      `my sentence was imposed before October 15, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your sentence imposed before October 15, 1977?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 761(1), shall the Parole Board of Canada review my condition, history and circumstances` IS
    `s 761(1) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person` `I am in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` `my sentence was imposed before October 15, 1977`

-- Section 761(2): where a person is in custody under an indeterminate sentence imposed before 15 October 1977, the Parole Board shall review at least once in every year.
@export Under section 761(2), shall the Parole Board of Canada review my condition, history and circumstances at least once in every year?
GIVEN `I am in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period?
      `the day my sentence was imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your sentence imposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 761(2), shall the Parole Board of Canada review my condition, history and circumstances at least once in every year` IS
    `s 761(2) the Parole Board of Canada shall review the condition, history and circumstances of the person at least once in every year` `I am in custody under a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` `the day my sentence was imposed`

§ `Part XXV: effect and enforcement of undertakings, release orders and recognizances`
-- These questions arise only for a person bound by an undertaking, release order or recognizance, or whose surety is. The form can ask 'Are you, or is someone for you, bound by one of these?' before showing them.

-- Section 764(1): an accused bound by an undertaking or release order to appear for trial stays bound, with their sureties, despite arraignment or conviction, until discharged or sentenced.
@export Under section 764(1), does my undertaking or release order continue to bind me and my sureties after my arraignment or conviction?
GIVEN `the document I am bound by` IS A `Process document` @desc Which document are you bound by: an undertaking, a release order, a recognizance, or something else?
      `I am bound by the document to appear for trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you bound by it to appear for trial?
      `I have been discharged or sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been discharged or sentenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 764(1), does my undertaking or release order continue to bind me and my sureties after my arraignment or conviction` IS
    `s 764(1) the undertaking or release order continues to bind the accused and their sureties for their appearance` `the document I am bound by` `I am bound by the document to appear for trial` `I have been discharged or sentenced`

-- Section 765: arrest on another charge does not cancel the undertaking or release order, which continues to bind until the accused is discharged or sentenced in respect of the offence it relates to.
@export Under section 765, does my undertaking or release order continue to bind me and my sureties despite my arrest on another charge?
GIVEN `the document I am bound by` IS A `Process document` @desc Which document are you bound by: an undertaking, a release order, a recognizance, or something else?
      `I am bound by the document to appear for trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you bound by it to appear for trial?
      `I have been discharged or sentenced in respect of the offence the document relates to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been discharged or sentenced in respect of the offence the document relates to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 765, does my undertaking or release order continue to bind me and my sureties despite my arrest on another charge` IS
    `s 765 the undertaking or release order continues to bind the accused and their sureties despite the arrest on another charge` `the document I am bound by` `I am bound by the document to appear for trial` `I have been discharged or sentenced in respect of the offence the document relates to`

-- Section 766(1): a surety for a person subject to a release order or recognizance may apply in writing to be relieved. An undertaking has no surety and is not named.
@export Under section 766(1), may my surety apply to be relieved of their obligation?
GIVEN `the document I am bound by` IS A `Process document` @desc Which document are you bound by: an undertaking, a release order, a recognizance, or something else?
      `my surety applies in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your surety apply in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 766(1), may my surety apply to be relieved of their obligation` IS
    `s 766(1) the surety may apply to be relieved of their obligation` `the document I am bound by` `my surety applies in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice`

-- Section 770(1): where a person subject to an undertaking, release order or recognizance does not comply with a condition, a court, provincial court judge or justice having knowledge of the facts shall endorse a certificate in Form 33.
@export Under section 770(1), shall a court endorse a certificate of default on my undertaking, release order or recognizance?
GIVEN `the document I am bound by` IS A `Process document` @desc Which document are you bound by: an undertaking, a release order, a recognizance, or something else?
      `the proceedings are proceedings to which the Criminal Code applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings proceedings to which the Criminal Code applies?
      `I did not comply with a condition of the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not comply with any of its conditions?
      `a court, provincial court judge or justice has knowledge of the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a court, provincial court judge or justice have knowledge of the facts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 770(1), shall a court endorse a certificate of default on my undertaking, release order or recognizance` IS
    `s 770(1) the court, provincial court judge or justice shall endorse or cause to be endorsed a certificate` `the document I am bound by` `the proceedings are proceedings to which the Criminal Code applies` `I did not comply with a condition of the document` `a court, provincial court judge or justice has knowledge of the facts`

-- Section 771(2): if subsection (1) has been complied with, the judge may, after giving the parties an opportunity to be heard, grant or refuse the application and make any order about the forfeiture that the judge considers proper. Before the hearing the answer is 'no'; if subsection (1) was not complied with it is 'not covered'.
@export Under section 771(2), may the judge take this course on an application to forfeit the amount set out in my document?
GIVEN `subsection 771(1) has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has subsection 771(1) been complied with (a hearing time and place fixed, and notice sent to each principal and surety)?
      `the judge has given the parties an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judge given the parties an opportunity to be heard?
      `the course the judge takes` IS A `s 771(2) course` @desc Does the judge grant the application, refuse it, or make another order about forfeiture that the judge considers proper?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 771(2), may the judge take this course on an application to forfeit the amount set out in my document` IS
    `s 771(2) the judge may take this course` `subsection 771(1) has been complied with` `the judge has given the parties an opportunity to be heard` `the course the judge takes`

-- Section 771(3): if a judge orders forfeiture of the amount, the principal and their sureties become judgment debtors of the Crown, each in the amount the judge orders them to pay.
@export Under section 771(3), do I and my sureties become judgment debtors of the Crown?
GIVEN `a judge orders forfeiture of the amount set out in the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a judge order forfeiture of the amount set out in the undertaking, release order or recognizance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 771(3), do I and my sureties become judgment debtors of the Crown` IS
    `s 771(3) the principal and their sureties become judgment debtors of the Crown` `a judge orders forfeiture of the amount set out in the document`

-- Section 773(1): where a writ of fieri facias has issued and the sheriff's return shows goods cannot be found or the proceeds are insufficient, a judge may, on the application of the Attorney General or counsel acting for them, fix a time and place for the sureties to show cause.
@export Under section 773(1), may a judge fix a time and place for my sureties to show cause why a warrant of committal should not be issued?
GIVEN `a writ of fieri facias has been issued under Part XXV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a writ of fieri facias been issued under Part XXV?
      `the sheriff's return shows that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a certificate in the sheriff's return show that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found to satisfy the writ?
      `the sheriff's return shows that the proceeds of the execution are not sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it show that the proceeds of the execution of the writ are not sufficient to satisfy it?
      `the application is made by the Attorney General or counsel acting on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the Attorney General or counsel acting on their behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 773(1), may a judge fix a time and place for my sureties to show cause why a warrant of committal should not be issued` IS
    `s 773(1) a judge of the court may fix a time and place for the sureties to show cause` `a writ of fieri facias has been issued under Part XXV` `the sheriff's return shows that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found` `the sheriff's return shows that the proceeds of the execution are not sufficient` `the application is made by the Attorney General or counsel acting on their behalf`

§ `Part XXVI: extraordinary remedies`
-- These questions arise only where certiorari, habeas corpus, mandamus, procedendo or prohibition is in play for the person. The form can ask 'Is a writ of habeas corpus, certiorari, mandamus, procedendo or prohibition being sought for you or against you?' before showing them.

-- Section 774.1: despite any other provision, the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus must appear in court in person. The function answers whether the person does appear as the section requires (JUST FALSE: the subject does not appear in person); it does not answer whether the duty applies to someone who is not the subject (NOTHING).
@export Under section 774.1, does the subject of a writ of habeas corpus appear in court in person as the section requires?
GIVEN `I am the subject of a writ of habeas corpus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the subject of a writ of habeas corpus?
      `I appear in court in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appear in court in person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 774.1, does the subject of a writ of habeas corpus appear in court in person as the section requires` IS
    `s 774.1 the person who is the subject of a writ of habeas corpus appears in court in person as they must` `I am the subject of a writ of habeas corpus` `I appear in court in person`

-- Section 776: no conviction or order shall be removed by certiorari where an appeal was taken, or where the defendant appeared and pleaded, the merits were tried, an appeal might have been taken and the defendant did not appeal. JUST TRUE means it may not be removed by certiorari; JUST FALSE means this section does not bar it.
@export Under section 776, does the section bar the removal of my conviction or order by certiorari?
GIVEN `an appeal was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an appeal taken, whether or not carried to a conclusion?
      `I appeared and pleaded and the merits were tried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appear and plead, and were the merits tried?
      `an appeal might have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Might an appeal have been taken?
      `I did not appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 776, does the section bar the removal of my conviction or order by certiorari` IS
    `s 776 the conviction or order shall not be removed by certiorari` `an appeal was taken` `I appeared and pleaded and the merits were tried` `an appeal might have been taken` `I did not appeal`

-- Section 777(1): on removal by certiorari, no conviction, order or warrant is held invalid by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency where the court is satisfied of the offence, the jurisdiction, and (if any punishment was imposed) that it was not in excess.
@export Under section 777(1), shall my conviction, order or warrant not be held to be invalid by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency?
GIVEN `my conviction, order or warrant has been removed by certiorari` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the conviction, order or warrant been removed by certiorari?
      `the invalidity alleged is by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the invalidity alleged by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency in it?
      `the court is satisfied that an offence of the nature described was committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court, on perusal of the evidence, satisfied that an offence of the nature described in the conviction, order or warrant was committed?
      `the court is satisfied that there was jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that there was jurisdiction to make the conviction or order or issue the warrant?
      `a punishment was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a punishment imposed?
      `the court is satisfied that the punishment was not in excess of the lawful punishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the punishment imposed was not in excess of the punishment that might lawfully have been imposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 777(1), shall my conviction, order or warrant not be held to be invalid by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency` IS
    `s 777(1) the conviction, order or warrant shall not be held to be invalid by reason of the irregularity, informality or insufficiency` `my conviction, order or warrant has been removed by certiorari` `the invalidity alleged is by reason of an irregularity, informality or insufficiency in it` `the court is satisfied that an offence of the nature described was committed` `the court is satisfied that there was jurisdiction` `a punishment was imposed` `the court is satisfied that the punishment was not in excess of the lawful punishment`

-- Section 784(3): where an application for habeas corpus ad subjiciendum is refused by a judge, no application may again be made on the same grounds unless fresh evidence is adduced. JUST TRUE means no further application on those grounds; JUST FALSE means this subsection does not bar it.
@export Under section 784(3), does the section bar a further application for habeas corpus on the same grounds?
GIVEN `my application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum was refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction?
      `the new application is on the same grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new application on the same grounds?
      `fresh evidence is adduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is fresh evidence adduced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 784(3), does the section bar a further application for habeas corpus on the same grounds` IS
    `s 784(3) no application may again be made on the same grounds` `my application for a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum was refused by a judge of a court having jurisdiction` `the new application is on the same grounds` `fresh evidence is adduced`

-- Section 784(5): an appeal lies to the court of appeal, and with leave to the Supreme Court of Canada, at the instance of the applicant, the Attorney General of the province concerned or the Attorney General of Canada, but not at the instance of any other party.
@export Under section 784(5), does an appeal lie at the instance of this appellant from the judgment on the return of a writ of habeas corpus?
GIVEN `a judgment is issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a judgment issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum?
      `the appeal` IS A `s 784(5) appeal` @desc Is the appeal to the court of appeal, or from a judgment of the court of appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada?
      `who is appealing` IS A `s 784(5) appellant` @desc Who is appealing: the applicant, the Attorney General of the province concerned, the Attorney General of Canada, or another party?
      `the Supreme Court of Canada gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Supreme Court of Canada given leave?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 784(5), does an appeal lie at the instance of this appellant from the judgment on the return of a writ of habeas corpus` IS
    `s 784(5) the appeal lies at the instance of this appellant` `a judgment is issued on the return of a writ of habeas corpus ad subjiciendum` `the appeal` `who is appealing` `the Supreme Court of Canada gives leave`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc29 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc29-seat.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), the seat layer over lines 16684-17450 (Parts XXVII and XXVIII, and the schedules in them).
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state what the law of summary conviction
-- proceedings, peace bonds, appeals and miscellaneous provisions does to them. There is never a seat for an official: a duty or power of a court, a justice or a clerk
-- appears here only as what it means to the person (what may be done to them, what they must be given, what they may do).
-- Nothing here is new law: every question is one call of a layer-1 rule, and a question that has no layer-1 rule is not asked here.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each input is a fact the person can state (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a short list), with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- A seam of layer 1 that is itself an answer of another section (a MAYBE BOOLEAN) is asked here as a yes-or-no fact and passed in as JUST of that answer; "not covered" cannot be stated as a fact.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is a yes the text gives; JUST FALSE is a no the text gives in its own words; NOTHING means the text does not answer on these facts. A caller never reads NOTHING as no.

§ `Summary conviction proceedings: the time limit and the general penalty (sections 786 and 787)`

-- The person is, or may be, the defendant in proceedings for an offence punishable on summary conviction.

-- s 786(2) the proceedings are barred because they were instituted more than 12 months after the subject matter arose
@export Under section 786(2), are the proceedings barred because they were instituted more than 12 months after the subject matter arose?
GIVEN `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the subject matter of the proceedings arise?
      `the date the proceedings were instituted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the proceedings instituted (the information laid)?
      `the prosecutor and the defendant so agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the prosecutor and the defendant agree that the proceedings may be instituted later?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 786(2), are the proceedings barred because they were instituted more than 12 months after the subject matter arose` MEANS
    `s 786(2) the proceedings are barred because they were instituted more than 12 months after the subject matter arose` `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose` `the date the proceedings were instituted` `the prosecutor and the defendant so agree`

-- s 786(2) the day on which the 12 months end
@export Under section 786(2), on what day do the 12 months end?
GIVEN `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the subject matter of the proceedings arise?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 786(2), on what day do the 12 months end` MEANS
    `s 786(2) the day on which the 12 months end` `the date the subject matter of the proceedings arose`

-- s 787(1) the general penalty applies to the offence
@export Under section 787(1), does the general penalty apply to the offence?
GIVEN `the offence is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one punishable on summary conviction?
      `the law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a law otherwise provide (so that the general rule does not apply)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 787(1), does the general penalty apply to the offence` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty applies to the offence` `the offence is punishable on summary conviction` `the law otherwise provides`

-- s 787(1) the fine is not more than $5,000
@export Under section 787(1), is the fine not more than $5,000?
GIVEN `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the fine, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 787(1), is the fine not more than $5,000` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the fine is not more than $5,000` `the fine in dollars`

-- s 787(1) the term of imprisonment is not more than two years less a day
@export Under section 787(1), is the term of imprisonment not more than two years less a day?
GIVEN `the term of imprisonment in whole months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months is the term of imprisonment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 787(1), is the term of imprisonment not more than two years less a day` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the term of imprisonment is not more than two years less a day` `the term of imprisonment in whole months`

-- s 787(2) the court may order imprisonment in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order
@export Under section 787(2), may the court order imprisonment in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order?
GIVEN `the imposition of a fine or the making of an order for the payment of money is authorized by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a law authorize the imposition of a fine, or an order for the payment of money?
      `the law provides that imprisonment may be imposed in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law already provide that imprisonment may be imposed in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 787(2), may the court order imprisonment in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order` MEANS
    `s 787(2) the court may order imprisonment in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order` `the imposition of a fine or the making of an order for the payment of money is authorized by law` `the law provides that imprisonment may be imposed in default of payment of the fine or compliance with the order`

§ `The information and the trial (sections 788 to 809)`

-- The person has been charged by an information, or may be, in proceedings for an offence punishable on summary conviction.

-- s 788(1) the proceedings are required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2
@export Under section 788(1), are the proceedings required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings summary conviction proceedings under Part XXVII?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 788(1), are the proceedings required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2` MEANS
    `s 788(1) the proceedings are required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2` (JUST `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part`)

-- s 789(2) the information is barred from containing any reference to previous convictions
@export Under section 789(2), is the information barred from containing any reference to previous convictions?
GIVEN `a greater punishment may be imposed for the offence by reason of previous convictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a greater punishment be imposed for this offence because of previous convictions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 789(2), is the information barred from containing any reference to previous convictions` MEANS
    `s 789(2) the information is barred from containing any reference to previous convictions` `a greater punishment may be imposed for the offence by reason of previous convictions`

-- s 794(1) the information need not set out or negative the exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification
@export Under section 794(1), need the information not set out or negative the exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification?
GIVEN `it is an exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification prescribed by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter an exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification that the law prescribes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 794(1), need the information not set out or negative the exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification` MEANS
    `s 794(1) the information need not set out or negative the exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification` `it is an exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification prescribed by law`

-- s 800(2) a defendant may appear in the way
@export Under section 800(2), may I appear in the way I propose?
GIVEN way IS A `s 800(2) way of appearing` @desc In which way do you propose to appear (personally, by counsel, by agent, or another way)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 800(2), may I appear in the way I propose` MEANS
    `s 800(2) a defendant may appear in the way` way

-- s 800(2) the summary conviction court may require the defendant to appear personally
@export Under section 800(2), may the summary conviction court require me to appear personally?
GIVEN `the defendant is a defendant in proceedings to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a defendant in summary conviction proceedings under Part XXVII?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 800(2), may the summary conviction court require me to appear personally` MEANS
    `s 800(2) the summary conviction court may require the defendant to appear personally` `the defendant is a defendant in proceedings to which this Part applies`

-- s 801(1)(a) the defendant is required to be asked whether they plead guilty or not guilty to the information
@export Under section 801(1)(a), am I required to be asked whether I plead guilty or not guilty to the information?
GIVEN `the defendant appears for the trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appear for the trial?
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence that is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in respect of an offence that is punishable on summary conviction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 801(1)(a), am I required to be asked whether I plead guilty or not guilty to the information` MEANS
    `s 801(1)(a) the defendant is required to be asked whether they plead guilty or not guilty to the information` `the defendant appears for the trial` `the proceedings are in respect of an offence that is punishable on summary conviction`

-- s 802(1) the defendant is entitled to make full answer and defence
@export Under section 802(1), am I entitled to make full answer and defence?
GIVEN `the person is the defendant in proceedings to which this Part applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the defendant in summary conviction proceedings under Part XXVII?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 802(1), am I entitled to make full answer and defence` MEANS
    `s 802(1) the defendant is entitled to make full answer and defence` `the person is the defendant in proceedings to which this Part applies`

-- s 802(2) the prosecutor or defendant may examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way
@export Under section 802(2), may I examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way I propose?
GIVEN way IS A `s 802(2) way of examining` @desc In which way do you propose to examine and cross-examine witnesses (personally, by counsel, by agent, or another way)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 802(2), may I examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way I propose` MEANS
    `s 802(2) the prosecutor or defendant may examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way` way

-- s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent
@export Under section 802.1, am I barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent?
GIVEN `the longest term of imprisonment, in months, to which the defendant is liable on summary conviction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, to which you are liable on summary conviction for the offence?
      `the defendant is an organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant an organization (and not an individual)?
      `the defendant is appearing to request an adjournment of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defendant appearing only to request an adjournment of the proceedings?
      `the agent is authorized under a program approved or criteria established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agent authorized under a program approved, or criteria established, by the lieutenant governor in council of the province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 802.1, am I barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` MEANS
    `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` `the longest term of imprisonment, in months, to which the defendant is liable on summary conviction` (JUST `the defendant is an organization`) `the defendant is appearing to request an adjournment of the proceedings` `the agent is authorized under a program approved or criteria established by the lieutenant governor in council of the province`

-- s 803(2)(a) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in the absence of the defendant
@export Under section 803(2)(a), may the summary conviction court proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in my absence?
GIVEN `the defendant does not appear at the time and place appointed for the trial after having been notified of that time and place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to appear at the time and place appointed for the trial, after being notified of that time and place?
      `the defendant does not appear for the resumption of a trial adjourned in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to appear for the resumption of a trial adjourned under section 803(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 803(2)(a), may the summary conviction court proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in my absence` MEANS
    `s 803(2)(a) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in the absence of the defendant` `the defendant does not appear at the time and place appointed for the trial after having been notified of that time and place` `the defendant does not appear for the resumption of a trial adjourned in accordance with subsection (1)`

-- s 803(4) the summary conviction court may dismiss the information with or without costs
@export Under section 803(4), may the summary conviction court dismiss the information with or without costs?
GIVEN `the prosecutor does not appear at the time and place appointed for the resumption of an adjourned trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the prosecutor fail to appear at the time and place appointed for the resumption of an adjourned trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 803(4), may the summary conviction court dismiss the information with or without costs` MEANS
    `s 803(4) the summary conviction court may dismiss the information with or without costs` `the prosecutor does not appear at the time and place appointed for the resumption of an adjourned trial`

-- s 808(2) the certified copy of the order of dismissal is a bar to the subsequent proceedings
@export Under section 808(2), is the certified copy of the order of dismissal a bar to the subsequent proceedings?
GIVEN `the copy of the order of dismissal is certified in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the copy of the order of dismissal certified in accordance with section 808(1)?
      `the subsequent proceedings are against the defendant in respect of the same cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the later proceedings against you in respect of the same cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 808(2), is the certified copy of the order of dismissal a bar to the subsequent proceedings` MEANS
    `s 808(2) the certified copy of the order of dismissal is a bar to the subsequent proceedings` `the copy of the order of dismissal is certified in accordance with subsection (1)` `the subsequent proceedings are against the defendant in respect of the same cause`

-- s 809(1)(a) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the informant by the defendant
@export Under section 809(1)(a), may the summary conviction court award costs to be paid by me to the informant?
GIVEN `the summary conviction court convicts or makes an order against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the summary conviction court convict you or make an order against you?
      `it considers the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with the fees that section 840 allows?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 809(1)(a), may the summary conviction court award costs to be paid by me to the informant` MEANS
    `s 809(1)(a) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the informant by the defendant` `the summary conviction court convicts or makes an order against the defendant` `it considers the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with such of the fees established by section 840 as may be taken or allowed`

-- s 809(3) the amount for which the defendant is liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment
@export Under section 809(3), what is the amount for which I am liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment?
GIVEN `a fine or sum of money or both are adjudged to be paid by the defendant and a term of imprisonment in default of payment is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered you to pay a fine or a sum of money, or both, with a term of imprisonment if you do not pay?
      `the fine or sum of money adjudged to be paid, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, is the fine or sum of money you are adjudged to pay?
      `the costs awarded against the defendant, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, are the costs awarded against you?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 809(3), what is the amount for which I am liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment` MEANS
    `s 809(3) the amount for which the defendant is liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment` `a fine or sum of money or both are adjudged to be paid by the defendant and a term of imprisonment in default of payment is imposed` `the fine or sum of money adjudged to be paid, in dollars` `the costs awarded against the defendant, in dollars`

-- s 809(4) the person who is liable to pay the costs is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month
@export Under section 809(4), is the person who is liable to pay the costs, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month?
GIVEN `no fine or sum of money is adjudged to be paid by a defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court adjudged that no fine or sum of money is to be paid by the defendant?
      `costs are awarded against the defendant or the informant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have costs been awarded against the defendant or the informant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 809(4), is the person who is liable to pay the costs, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month` MEANS
    `s 809(4) the person who is liable to pay the costs is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month` `no fine or sum of money is adjudged to be paid by a defendant` `costs are awarded against the defendant or the informant`

§ `Peace bonds and recognizances (sections 810 to 811.1)`

-- Only arises where someone has laid an information that they fear the person will cause personal injury, harm a child, commit a criminal organization, terrorism, sexual or intimate partner offence, or similar: ask "Has someone laid an information against you for a peace bond?" before showing the group.

-- s 810(3) the justice or court may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties
@export Under section 810(3), may the justice or court order that I enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties?
GIVEN `the justice or court is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the person on whose behalf the information was laid has reasonable grounds for the fear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the justice or court satisfied by the evidence that the person on whose behalf the information was laid has reasonable grounds for the fear?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 810(3), may the justice or court order that I enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties` MEANS
    `s 810(3) the justice or court may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties` `the justice or court is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the person on whose behalf the information was laid has reasonable grounds for the fear`

-- s 810(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months
@export Under section 810(3), is the period of the recognizance not more than 12 months?
GIVEN `the period of the recognizance in months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months is the recognizance to last?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 810(3), is the period of the recognizance not more than 12 months` MEANS
    `s 810(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` `the period of the recognizance in months`

-- s 810(3.01) the justice or court may commit the defendant to prison
