GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 810.01(3), is the period of the recognizance not more than 12 months` MEANS
    `s 810.01(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` `the period of the recognizance in months`

-- s 810.01(4) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison
@export Under section 810.01(4), may the provincial court judge commit me to prison?
GIVEN `the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail or refuse to enter into the recognizance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 810.01(4), may the provincial court judge commit me to prison` MEANS
    `s 810.01(4) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison` `the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance`

-- s 810.01(3.1) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a longer period
