§ `Appeals in summary conviction matters (sections 812 to 840)`

-- Only arises where the person has been convicted, or the proceedings against them have ended in an order or an acquittal: ask "Have you been convicted, or has an order been made against you?" before showing the group.

-- s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court
@export Under section 813, may the appellant (the defendant, the informant or the Attorney General) appeal to the appeal court against the decision?
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 813 appellant` @desc Who is the appellant (the defendant, the informant, the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent, or the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of Canada's agent, or another person)?
      decision IS A `s 813 decision appealed` @desc What is the decision appealed against (a conviction or order made against the defendant, a sentence, a verdict of unfit to stand trial, a verdict of not criminally responsible, an order dismissing an information, an order staying proceedings, or another decision)?
      `the law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a law otherwise provide (so that the general rule does not apply)?
      `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 813, may the appellant (the defendant, the informant or the Attorney General) appeal to the appeal court against the decision` MEANS
    `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` appellant decision `the law otherwise provides` `the proceedings were instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government`

-- s 815(1) the appellant is required to give notice of appeal
@export Under section 815(1), am I, as an appellant, required to give notice of appeal?
GIVEN `the person is an appellant who proposes to appeal to the appeal court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an appellant who proposes to appeal to the appeal court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 815(1), am I, as an appellant, required to give notice of appeal` MEANS
    `s 815(1) the appellant is required to give notice of appeal` `the person is an appellant who proposes to appeal to the appeal court`

-- s 815(1) the notice of appeal is given within the period directed by the rules of court
@export Under section 815(1), is the notice of appeal given within the period directed by the rules of court?
GIVEN `the days between the decision and the giving of notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days passed between the decision and the giving of notice of appeal?
      `the period directed by the rules of court, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What period do the rules of court direct for giving notice of appeal, in days?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 815(1), is the notice of appeal given within the period directed by the rules of court` MEANS
    `s 815(1) the notice of appeal is given within the period directed by the rules of court` `the days between the decision and the giving of notice` `the period directed by the rules of court, in days`

-- s 815(2) the appeal court or a judge thereof may extend the time within which notice of appeal may be given
@export Under section 815(2), may the appeal court or a judge thereof extend the time within which notice of appeal may be given?
GIVEN `it is the appeal court or a judge of the appeal court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the appeal court, or a judge of the appeal court, that acts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 815(2), may the appeal court or a judge thereof extend the time within which notice of appeal may be given` MEANS
    `s 815(2) the appeal court or a judge thereof may extend the time within which notice of appeal may be given` `it is the appeal court or a judge of the appeal court`

-- s 816(1) the appellant is required to remain in custody
@export Under section 816(1), am I, as an appellant, required to remain in custody?
GIVEN `the person was the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court and is an appellant under section 813` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court, and are you an appellant under section 813?
      `the person is in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in custody?
      `the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard makes a release order referred to in section 515` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard made a release order referred to in section 515?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 816(1), am I, as an appellant, required to remain in custody` MEANS
    `s 816(1) the appellant is required to remain in custody` `the person was the defendant in proceedings before a summary conviction court and is an appellant under section 813` `the person is in custody` `the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard makes a release order referred to in section 515`

-- s 819(1) the day on which the thirty days expire
@export Under section 819(1), on what day do the thirty days expire?
GIVEN `the day on which notice of the appeal was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was notice of the appeal given?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 819(1), on what day do the thirty days expire` MEANS
    `s 819(1) the day on which the thirty days expire` `the day on which notice of the appeal was given`

-- s 820(1) the person waives the right of appeal under section 813 by paying the fine
@export Under section 820(1), do I waive my right of appeal under section 813 by paying the fine?
GIVEN `the only act relied on as a waiver is that the person paid the fine imposed on conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only act relied on as a waiver that you paid the fine imposed on conviction?
      `the person paid without in any way indicating an intention to appeal or reserving the right to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay without in any way indicating an intention to appeal or reserving the right to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 820(1), do I waive my right of appeal under section 813 by paying the fine` MEANS
    `s 820(1) the person waives the right of appeal under section 813 by paying the fine` `the only act relied on as a waiver is that the person paid the fine imposed on conviction` `the person paid without in any way indicating an intention to appeal or reserving the right to appeal`

-- s 822(4) the appeal court may order that the appeal be heard by way of trial de novo
@export Under section 822(4), may the appeal court order that the appeal be heard by way of trial de novo?
GIVEN `an appeal is taken under section 813` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal one taken under section 813 (an appeal to the appeal court from the summary conviction court)?
      `the defendant, the informant, the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by the defendant, the informant, the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent?
      `the appeal court is of the opinion that the interests of justice would be better served by hearing and determining the appeal by holding a trial de novo` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal court of the opinion that the interests of justice would be better served by hearing the appeal by way of a new trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 822(4), may the appeal court order that the appeal be heard by way of trial de novo` MEANS
    `s 822(4) the appeal court may order that the appeal be heard by way of trial de novo` `an appeal is taken under section 813` `the defendant, the informant, the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent applies` `the appeal court is of the opinion that the interests of justice would be better served by hearing and determining the appeal by holding a trial de novo`

-- s 827(3) the term of imprisonment does not exceed one month
@export Under section 827(3), does the term of imprisonment not exceed one month?
GIVEN `the term of imprisonment in whole months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months is the term of imprisonment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 827(3), does the term of imprisonment not exceed one month` MEANS
    `s 827(3) the term of imprisonment does not exceed one month` `the term of imprisonment in whole months`

-- s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground
@export Under section 830(1), may I appeal against the decision on the ground?
GIVEN `the person is a party to proceedings to which this Part applies or the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to summary conviction proceedings under Part XXVII (or the Attorney General)?
      `the decision is a conviction, judgment, verdict of acquittal, verdict of not criminally responsible or of unfit to stand trial, or other final order or determination of a summary conviction court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a conviction, judgment, verdict of acquittal, verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or of unfit to stand trial, or other final order or determination of a summary conviction court?
      ground IS A `s 830(1) ground` @desc On which ground do you appeal (erroneous in point of law, in excess of jurisdiction, a refusal or failure to exercise jurisdiction, or another ground)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 830(1), may I appeal against the decision on the ground` MEANS
    `s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground` `the person is a party to proceedings to which this Part applies or the Attorney General` `the decision is a conviction, judgment, verdict of acquittal, verdict of not criminally responsible or of unfit to stand trial, or other final order or determination of a summary conviction court` ground

-- s 830(2) the appeal is required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from
@export Under section 830(2), is the appeal required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from?
GIVEN `the appellant files with the appeal court a statement of facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the appellant file a statement of facts with the appeal court?
      `the days between the filing of the notice of appeal and the filing of the statement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days passed between filing the notice of appeal and filing the statement of facts?
      `the statement of facts is agreed to in writing by the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement of facts agreed to in writing by the respondent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 830(2), is the appeal required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from` MEANS
    `s 830(2) the appeal is required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from` `the appellant files with the appeal court a statement of facts` `the days between the filing of the notice of appeal and the filing of the statement` `the statement of facts is agreed to in writing by the respondent`

-- s 830(3) the notice of appeal is served and filed within thirty days after the date of the decision
@export Under section 830(3), is the notice of appeal served and filed within thirty days after the date of the decision?
GIVEN `there are applicable rules of court otherwise providing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there applicable rules of court that otherwise provide for the time and manner of appeal?
      `the days after the date of the decision on which the notice of appeal is served and filed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the date of the decision was the notice of appeal served and filed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 830(3), is the notice of appeal served and filed within thirty days after the date of the decision` MEANS
    `s 830(3) the notice of appeal is served and filed within thirty days after the date of the decision` `there are applicable rules of court otherwise providing` `the days after the date of the decision on which the notice of appeal is served and filed`

-- s 830(3) the last day for serving and filing the notice of appeal
@export Under section 830(3), what is the last day for serving and filing the notice of appeal?
GIVEN `the date of the decision that is the subject of the appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the decision that you are appealing made?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 830(3), what is the last day for serving and filing the notice of appeal` MEANS
    `s 830(3) the last day for serving and filing the notice of appeal` `the date of the decision that is the subject of the appeal`

-- s 836 the person is taken to have abandoned all rights of appeal under section 813
@export Under section 836, am I taken to have abandoned all my rights of appeal under section 813?
GIVEN `the person appeals under section 830` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you appeal under section 830 (the summary appeal on a transcript or an agreed statement of facts)?
      `the person is entitled to an appeal under section 813 in respect of the same decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an appeal under section 813 in respect of the same decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 836, am I taken to have abandoned all my rights of appeal under section 813` MEANS
    `s 836 the person is taken to have abandoned all rights of appeal under section 813` `the person appeals under section 830` `the person is entitled to an appeal under section 813 in respect of the same decision`

-- s 837 no appeal under section 830 lies from the conviction or order
@export Under section 837, does no appeal under section 830 lie from the conviction or order?
GIVEN `it is provided by law that no appeal lies from the conviction or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a law provide that no appeal lies from the conviction or order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 837, does no appeal under section 830 lie from the conviction or order` MEANS
    `s 837 no appeal under section 830 lies from the conviction or order` `it is provided by law that no appeal lies from the conviction or order`

-- s 839(1) an appeal to the court of appeal may be taken against the decision
@export Under section 839(1), may an appeal to the court of appeal be taken against the decision?
GIVEN decision IS A `s 839(1) decision` @desc What is the decision (a decision of a court on an appeal under section 822, a decision of an appeal court under section 834, or another decision)?
      `the ground involves a question of law alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the ground of appeal involve a question of law alone?
      `leave is given by the court of appeal or a judge of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court of appeal, or a judge of it, given leave to appeal?
      `the appeal court is the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal court the court of appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 839(1), may an appeal to the court of appeal be taken against the decision` MEANS
    `s 839(1) an appeal to the court of appeal may be taken against the decision` decision `the ground involves a question of law alone` `leave is given by the court of appeal or a judge of it` `the appeal court is the court of appeal`

§ `Electronic documents and forms (sections 841 to 849)`

-- Arises where a court deals with a document in electronic form.

-- s 843(2) the filing is complete
@export Under section 843(2), is the filing complete?
GIVEN `a document is required to be filed in a court and the filing is done by transfer of data by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a document required to be filed in a court, and is the filing being done by sending the data electronically?
      `the transfer is accepted by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court accepted the transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 843(2), is the filing complete` MEANS
    `s 843(2) the filing is complete` `a document is required to be filed in a court and the filing is done by transfer of data by electronic means` `the transfer is accepted by the court`

-- s 847 the person is entitled to obtain a printed copy of the electronic document from the court
@export Under section 847, am I entitled to obtain a printed copy of the electronic document from the court?
GIVEN `the person is entitled to obtain a copy of a document from a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to obtain a copy of the document from the court?
      `the document is in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document in electronic form?
      `the person pays a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the relevant province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you pay a reasonable fee set by the tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the province?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 847, am I entitled to obtain a printed copy of the electronic document from the court` MEANS
    `s 847 the person is entitled to obtain a printed copy of the electronic document from the court` `the person is entitled to obtain a copy of a document from a court` `the document is in electronic form` `the person pays a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the relevant province`

-- s 849(1) the form is deemed to be good, valid and sufficient
@export Under section 849(1), is the form deemed to be good, valid and sufficient?
GIVEN `it is a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or a form to the like effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a form set out in Part XXVII, varied to suit the case, or a form to the like effect?
      `it is used in the circumstances for which it is provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form used in the circumstances for which it is provided?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 849(1), is the form deemed to be good, valid and sufficient` MEANS
    `s 849(1) the form is deemed to be good, valid and sufficient` `it is a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or a form to the like effect` `it is used in the circumstances for which it is provided`

§ `Schedules (schedule XXII.1 and schedule XXVII)`

-- Arises where the offence is one that may lead to a remediation agreement, or where a fee is charged in summary proceedings.

-- sch XXII.1 the offence is listed
@export Under schedule XXII.1, is the offence listed?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence, as printed in the Code (for example 380 or 462.31)? If you are charged with a conspiracy, an attempt, being an accessory after the fact or a counselling, give the section number of the offence it relates to.
      `the subsection of the offence` IS A STRING @desc What subsection is that offence under, as the Code writes it (for example "(3)")? Leave it empty if the offence is under the section itself.
      `the offence is under section 3 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one under section 3 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act (bribing a foreign public official)?
      `the offence is under section 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one under section 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act (maintenance or destruction of books and records to facilitate or hide the bribing of a foreign public official)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under schedule XXII.1, is the offence listed` MEANS
    `sch XXII.1 the offence is listed` (`sch XXII.1 offence` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence`, `the subsection of the offence`), `the offence is under section 3 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`, `the offence is under section 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`)

-- sch XXVII the amount in dollars stated in the row of the item
@export Under schedule XXVII, what is the amount in dollars stated in the row of the item?
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER @desc Which item of the schedule is it (1 to 29)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under schedule XXVII, what is the amount in dollars stated in the row of the item` MEANS
    `sch XXVII the amount in dollars stated in the row of the item` item

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc30 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, FORM 1 to FORM 23 (raw text lines 17451-18463) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state what the Forms they are
-- handed or served say: what they must do, what follows if they do not, what may be put on them, how long it lasts, and how to get out of it.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
--
-- This layer phrases the rules encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each
-- question builds nothing of its own and calls the layer-1 rule with the answers given.
-- SCOPE OF EVERY ANSWER. A Form is the prescribed wording of a document; what a question here answers is what the FORM says. Where the Form points at a section
-- ("an offence under subsection 145(3)", "a warrant for your arrest (section 512)") the section itself is another part's, and its own answer is that part's.
-- NAMES. Every question begins "Under form N," with the Form's own number (the extension of the "Under section N," rule to a Form: assumed, not ruled), so that no two
-- parts' questions can share a name and each says the scope its answer claims.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. JUST TRUE: the Form says so on those facts. JUST FALSE: the Form itself says no (an "if" that is unmet, "unless", "only", a flat negative).
-- NOTHING: the Form does not cover those facts (it is silent, lists without closing the list, or limits its own grant): never read it as "no".
-- Provisions that address only an official (an officer's command in a warrant, a keeper's precept) are not questions here: there is never a seat for an official.
-- Forms that are only prescribed wording (Forms 1, 2 and 4 bodies, 5, the informations, the reports, the applications, 6.1, 6.4, 7 identification, 15, 17, 18) have no question.
-- The seat layer's own case file is ccc30-cases-seat.l4.

§ `Criminal Code (Canada), Forms 1 to 23 -- the accused's questions`

§§ `Search warrants and the information (Forms 2, 4 and 5.1)`
-- Applies when a search has been made of your premises, or when you are charged by an information or an indictment.

-- Form 2 and Form 4, the Note. The date of birth of the accused "may be mentioned on the information or indictment".
@export Under form 2, may the date of birth of the accused be mentioned on this document?
GIVEN document IS A `Process document` @desc What kind of document is it? One of: an information, an indictment, a count, a summons, a warrant for arrest, an appearance notice, an undertaking, a release order, a recognizance, a subpoena, a search warrant
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 2, may the date of birth of the accused be mentioned on this document` IS
    `form 2 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` document

-- Form 5.1, the notice that tells you a warrant was executed.
@export Under form 5.1, may the things seized in the search of my premises be brought before the court?
GIVEN `anything was seized during the execution of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was anything seized during the search of your premises?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.1, may the things seized in the search of my premises be brought before the court` IS
    `form 5.1 the things that were seized may be brought before the court` `anything was seized during the execution of the warrant`

@export Under form 5.1, may I obtain a copy of the report on the things that were seized from the clerk of the court?
GIVEN `a report on the things seized was filed with the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the peace officer, public officer or other person who executed the warrant file with the court a report on the things that were seized?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.1, may I obtain a copy of the report on the things that were seized from the clerk of the court` IS
    `form 5.1 the person may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court` `a report on the things seized was filed with the court`

§§ `A demand or order served on you for computer data, an account or documents (Forms 5.001 to 5.0091)`
-- Applies only if you have been served with a preservation demand, a preservation order, a keep-account-open order, a production order or a non-disclosure order.

-- Form 5.001, the duty to preserve until the date inserted, unless the demand is revoked or a document is obtained.
@export Under form 5.001, am I still required to preserve the computer data?
GIVEN `the data was in my possession or control when I received the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the computer data in your possession or control when you received the preservation demand?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what day are you asking? (day, month, year)
      `the date inserted in the demand` IS A DATE @desc What date is written in the demand as the date until which you must preserve the data?
      `the demand was revoked before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the demand revoked before that date?
      `a document with the data was obtained before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a document that contains the data obtained under a warrant or an order before that date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.001, am I still required to preserve the computer data` IS
    `form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data`
        `the data was in my possession or control when I received the demand`
        `the day I am asking about`
        `the date inserted in the demand`
        `the demand was revoked before that date`
        `a document with the data was obtained before that date`

@export Under form 5.001, may I be subject to a fine or to imprisonment for contravening the preservation demand?
GIVEN `I contravened the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene the preservation demand?
      `I have a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a lawful excuse for contravening it?
      consequence IS A `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 consequence` @desc Which consequence are you asking about? One of: forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine, forms 5.001 to 5.0091 imprisonment, forms 5.001 to 5.0091 both a fine and imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.001, may I be subject to a fine or to imprisonment for contravening the preservation demand` IS
    `form 5.001 contravening the demand without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` `I contravened the demand` `I have a lawful excuse` consequence

-- Form 5.002, the information asks that the order last "90 days after the day on which the order is made".
@export Under form 5.002, what is the last day of the 90 days for which the information asks me to preserve the data?
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the preservation order made? (day, month, year)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under form 5.002, what is the last day of the 90 days for which the information asks me to preserve the data` IS
    `form 5.002 the last day of the period requested` `the day on which the order is made`

-- Form 5.003, the preservation order.
@export Under form 5.003, am I still required to preserve the specified computer data?
GIVEN `the data was in my possession or control when I received the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the computer data in your possession or control when you received the preservation order?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what day are you asking? (day, month, year)
      `the date inserted in the order` IS A DATE @desc What date is written in the order as the date until which you must preserve the data?
      `the order was revoked before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order revoked before that date?
      `a document with the data was obtained before that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a document that contains the data obtained under a warrant or an order before that date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.003, am I still required to preserve the specified computer data` IS
    `form 5.003 the person is required to preserve the specified computer data`
        `the data was in my possession or control when I received the order`
        `the day I am asking about`
        `the date inserted in the order`
        `the order was revoked before that date`
        `a document with the data was obtained before that date`

@export Under form 5.003, may I be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both for contravening the preservation order?
GIVEN `I contravened the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene the preservation order?
      `I have a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a lawful excuse for contravening it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.003, may I be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both for contravening the preservation order` IS
    `form 5.003 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` `I contravened the order` `I have a lawful excuse`

-- Form 5.0032, the keep-account-open order.
@export Under form 5.0032, am I still required to keep the specified account open or active?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what day are you asking? (day, month, year)
      `the date inserted in the order` IS A DATE @desc What date is written in the order as the date until which you must keep the account open or active?
      `the holder asked me to close or deactivate the account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the holder of the account asked you to close or deactivate it?
      `the order was revoked or varied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the order been revoked or varied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.0032, am I still required to keep the specified account open or active` IS
    `form 5.0032 para (a) the person is required to keep the specified account open or active`
        `the day I am asking about` `the date inserted in the order` `the holder asked me to close or deactivate the account` `the order was revoked or varied`

-- Form 5.005, the production order for documents.
@export Under form 5.005, did I produce the document as the production order requires?
GIVEN `the days the order allows` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the order give you to produce the document?
      `the days I took` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did you take to produce the document?
      `I produced it at the place stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you produce it at the place stated in the order?
      `I produced it in the form stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you produce it in the form stated in the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.005, did I produce the document as the production order requires` IS
    `form 5.005 the document was produced as the order requires` `the days the order allows` `the days I took` `I produced it at the place stated` `I produced it in the form stated`

@export Under form 5.005, do I have the right to apply to revoke or vary the order?
GIVEN `the order is addressed to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order addressed to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.005, do I have the right to apply to revoke or vary the order` IS
    `forms 5.0032 to 5.0091 the person has the right to apply to revoke or vary the order` `the order is addressed to me`

-- Form 5.006, the order to trace a communication binds only on service.
@export Under form 5.006, am I ordered to prepare and produce the document?
GIVEN `I have been served in accordance with subsection 487.015(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been served with the order in accordance with subsection 487.015(4)?
      `the data was in my possession or control when I was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the transmission data in your possession or control when you were served?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.006, am I ordered to prepare and produce the document` IS
    `form 5.006 the person is ordered to prepare and produce the document` `I have been served in accordance with subsection 487.015(4)` `the data was in my possession or control when I was served`

-- Form 5.0091, the non-disclosure order.
@export Under form 5.0091, am I prohibited from disclosing the existence of the demand or order on this day?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what day are you asking? (day, month, year)
      `the day on which the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the non-disclosure order made? (day, month, year)
      `the number of days in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the day on which the order was made does the order prohibit disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.0091, am I prohibited from disclosing the existence of the demand or order on this day` IS
    `form 5.0091 the person is prohibited from disclosing on the day` `the day I am asking about` `the day on which the order was made` `the number of days in the period`

§§ `Taking of bodily substances for DNA analysis (Forms 5.03, 5.041 and 5.061)`
-- Applies only if an order, authorization or summons to take bodily substances from you for forensic DNA analysis has been made or served.

@export Under form 5.03, does the order authorize this person to take the samples of bodily substances from me?
GIVEN `the person is able by training or experience to take them by the procedures in subsection 487.06(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person taking the samples able, by training or experience, to take them by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1)?
      `the person is a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person taking the samples a peace officer?
      `the person takes them under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is not a peace officer, are they taking the samples under the direction of a peace officer?
      `no more samples are taken than are reasonably required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number of samples taken no more than the number reasonably required for forensic DNA analysis?
      `the terms and conditions in the order are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any terms and conditions stated in the order complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.03, does the order authorize this person to take the samples of bodily substances from me` IS
    `form 5.03 the order authorizes the person to take the samples`
        `the person is able by training or experience to take them by the procedures in subsection 487.06(1)`
        `the person is a peace officer`
        `the person takes them under the direction of a peace officer`
        `no more samples are taken than are reasonably required`
        `the terms and conditions in the order are complied with`

@export Under form 5.041, if I fail to appear as ordered, may a justice of the peace issue a warrant for my arrest?
GIVEN `I failed to appear at the place, day and time set out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to appear at the place, day and time set out in the order or summons?
      instrument IS A `forms 5.041 and 5.061 instrument` @desc What are you required to appear under? One of: forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4), forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11), forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4), forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3), forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.041, if I fail to appear as ordered, may a justice of the peace issue a warrant for my arrest` IS
    `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest in Form 5.062` `I failed to appear at the place, day and time set out` instrument

@export Under form 5.041, am I guilty of an offence if I fail to comply without reasonable excuse?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with the order or summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the order or summons?
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a reasonable excuse for failing to comply?
      instrument IS A `forms 5.041 and 5.061 instrument` @desc What did you fail to comply with? One of: forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.051(4), forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11), forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4), forms 5.041 and 5.061 a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3), forms 5.041 and 5.061 an order made under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, forms 5.041 and 5.061 another instrument
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.041, am I guilty of an offence if I fail to comply without reasonable excuse` IS
    `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `I failed to comply with the order or summons` `I have a reasonable excuse` instrument

-- The punishment the Form quotes: an indictable limb of "imprisonment for a term of not more than two years" (no minimum, no fine stated).
@export Under form 5.041, what is the most imprisonment I can face on indictment for failing to comply without reasonable excuse?
GIVETH A Imprisonment
DECIDE `Under form 5.041, what is the most imprisonment I can face on indictment for failing to comply without reasonable excuse` IS
    `form 5.041 as quoted from section 487.0552(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment`

@export Under form 5.061, may the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, use the force they used to take the samples from me?
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer or is acting under a peace officer's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who took the samples a peace officer, or acting under a peace officer's direction?
      `the person is taking the samples of bodily substances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they taking the samples of bodily substances?
      `the force used is no more than is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the force used no more than was necessary to take the samples?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 5.061, may the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, use the force they used to take the samples from me` IS
    `form 5.061 the person may use the force used` `the person is a peace officer or is acting under a peace officer's direction` `the person is taking the samples of bodily substances` `the force used is no more than is necessary`

§§ `A summons, an appearance notice, an undertaking or a release order (Forms 6, 9, 10, 11, 11.1 and 12)`
-- Applies if you have been summoned, handed an appearance notice, asked to sign an undertaking, or released on a release order.

-- Form 6, the summons.
@export Under form 6, am I warned that failing to appear or to attend court, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under subsection 145(3)?
GIVEN `I failed to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act or to attend court as the summons requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, or to attend court, as the summons requires?
      `I have a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 6, am I warned that failing to appear or to attend court, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under subsection 145(3)` IS
    `form 6 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act or to attend court, as required in the summons is an offence under subsection 145(3)`
        `I failed to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act or to attend court as the summons requires` `I have a lawful excuse`

@export Under form 6, may my summons be cancelled?
GIVEN `I did not comply with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the summons?
      `I am charged with an offence committed after the summons was issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with committing an offence after the summons was issued to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 6, may my summons be cancelled` IS
    `form 6 the summons may be cancelled` `I did not comply with the summons` `I am charged with an offence committed after the summons was issued to me`

@export Under form 6, may I be detained in custody as a result of my summons being cancelled?
GIVEN `the summons has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your summons been cancelled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 6, may I be detained in custody as a result of my summons being cancelled` IS
    `form 6 the person may be detained in custody as a result of the cancellation` `the summons has been cancelled`

-- Form 9, the appearance notice.
@export Under form 9, is it a lawful excuse that the appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence I am alleged to have committed?
GIVEN `my excuse is that the notice does not accurately describe the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the excuse you offer that the appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence you are alleged to have committed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 9, is it a lawful excuse that the appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence I am alleged to have committed` IS
    `form 9 the inaccuracy of the description is a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(3)` `my excuse is that the notice does not accurately describe the offence`

@export Under form 9, if no charges have been laid and I fail to appear at a judicial referral hearing, may charges be laid against me for the alleged offence?
GIVEN `no charges have been laid against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have no charges been laid against you?
      `I fail to appear at the judicial referral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to appear at a judicial referral hearing under section 523.1, as the appearance notice requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 9, if no charges have been laid and I fail to appear at a judicial referral hearing, may charges be laid against me for the alleged offence` IS
    `form 9 item 6(b) warning: charges may be laid against the person for the alleged offence` `no charges have been laid against me` `I fail to appear at the judicial referral hearing`

@export Under form 9, may my appearance notice be cancelled?
GIVEN `I did not comply with the appearance notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the appearance notice?
      `I am charged with an offence committed after I was released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you charged with committing an offence after you were released?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 9, may my appearance notice be cancelled` IS
    `form 9 the appearance notice may be cancelled` `I did not comply with the appearance notice` `I am charged with an offence committed after I was released`

-- Form 10, the undertaking: what may be checked on it, the limits, how it is varied, how long it lasts, and whether you have to accept it.
@export Under form 10, may the peace officer check this condition on my undertaking?
GIVEN `the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition reasonable in the circumstances of the offence?
      purpose IS A `form 10 purpose of a condition` @desc What is the condition necessary for? One of: form 10 to ensure the accused's attendance in court, form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a victim of the offence, form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a witness to the offence, form 10 to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence, form 10 to prevent the commission of another offence, form 10 none of those purposes
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, may the peace officer check this condition on my undertaking` IS
    `form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` `the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence` purpose

@export Under form 10, is the amount I am asked to promise to pay within the limit?
GIVEN `the amount I am asked to promise to pay, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, are you asked to promise to pay if you fail to comply with a condition of the undertaking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, is the amount I am asked to promise to pay within the limit` IS
    `form 10 item 5 paragraph (j) the amount the person may be required to promise to pay is within the limit` `the amount I am asked to promise to pay, in dollars`

@export Under form 10, may I be required to deposit money or other valuable security?
GIVEN `the amount to be deposited, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, are you asked to deposit in money or other valuable security?
      `I am ordinarily resident in the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in the province?
      `the distance in kilometres from where I am in custody to where I reside` IS A NUMBER @desc How many kilometres is it from the place in which you are in custody to the place where you reside?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, may I be required to deposit money or other valuable security` IS
    `form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit`
        `the amount to be deposited, in dollars` `I am ordinarily resident in the province` `the distance in kilometres from where I am in custody to where I reside`

@export Under form 10, may the conditions of my undertaking be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and myself?
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor consent in writing to the variation?
      `I consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent in writing to the variation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, may the conditions of my undertaking be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and myself` IS
    `form 10 item 7 the conditions may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and the person` `the prosecutor consents in writing` `I consent in writing`

@export Under form 10, do the conditions of my undertaking remain in effect?
GIVEN `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the conditions of the undertaking been cancelled or changed?
      `I have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, do the conditions of my undertaking remain in effect` IS
    `form 10 the conditions remain in effect` `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` `I have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court`

@export Under form 10, does the Form warn that failing to follow a condition of my undertaking, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under section 145?
GIVEN `I failed to follow a condition of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to follow any of the conditions set out in the undertaking?
      `I have a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a lawful excuse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, does the Form warn that failing to follow a condition of my undertaking, without a lawful excuse, is an offence under section 145` IS
    `form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to follow any of the conditions is an offence under section 145` `I failed to follow a condition of the undertaking` `I have a lawful excuse`

@export Under form 10, could the funds or valuable security promised or deposited be forfeited?
GIVEN `I do not comply with the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with the undertaking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, could the funds or valuable security promised or deposited be forfeited` IS
    `form 10 the funds or valuable security promised or deposited could be forfeited` `I do not comply with the undertaking`

@export Under form 10, does the Form say that I do not have to accept the conditions of the undertaking?
GIVEN `I am asked to accept the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you being asked to accept the conditions of the undertaking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, does the Form say that I do not have to accept the conditions of the undertaking` IS
    `form 10 the person does not have to accept the conditions` `I am asked to accept the conditions`

@export Under form 10, if I do not accept the conditions, will I be brought to a justice for a bail hearing?
GIVEN `I accept the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you accept the conditions of the undertaking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 10, if I do not accept the conditions, will I be brought to a justice for a bail hearing` IS
    `form 10 if the person does not accept the conditions, the person will be brought to a justice for a bail hearing` `I accept the conditions`

-- Form 11, the release order.
@export Under form 11, am I released, given whether I have complied with the obligations marked on the release order?
GIVEN `I have complied with every obligation marked on the release order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with every financial obligation that is indicated by a check mark on the release order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 11, am I released, given whether I have complied with the obligations marked on the release order` IS
    `form 11 item 4 the person is released` `I have complied with every obligation marked on the release order`

@export Under form 11, may the conditions of my release order be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, myself and my sureties?
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prosecutor consent in writing to the variation?
      `I consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent in writing to the variation?
      `I have sureties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have any sureties?
      `my sureties consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your sureties consent in writing to the variation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 11, may the conditions of my release order be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, myself and my sureties` IS
    `form 11 item 6 the conditions may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, the person and the sureties, if any` `the prosecutor consents in writing` `I consent in writing` `I have sureties` `my sureties consent in writing`

@export Under form 11, do the conditions of my release order remain in effect?
GIVEN `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the conditions of the release order been cancelled or changed?
      `I have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 11, do the conditions of my release order remain in effect` IS
    `form 11 the conditions remain in effect` `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` `I have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court`

@export Under form 11, if I do not accept the conditions, will I be detained?
GIVEN `I accept the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you accept the conditions of the release order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 11, if I do not accept the conditions, will I be detained` IS
    `form 11 if the person does not accept the conditions, the person will be detained` `I accept the conditions`

-- Form 11.1, the order to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act.
@export Under form 11.1, if I do not comply with the order to appear, does the Form state that the consequence I name may follow?
GIVEN `I do not comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with the order to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act?
      consequence IS A `form 11.1 consequence of not complying` @desc Which consequence do you want to know whether the Form states? One of: form 11.1 the person may be arrested, form 11.1 the release order may be cancelled, form 11.1 the person may be detained in custody as a result, form 11.1 another consequence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 11.1, if I do not comply with the order to appear, does the Form state that the consequence I name may follow` IS
    `form 11.1 if the person does not comply with the order, the Form states that` `I do not comply with the order` consequence

-- Form 12, the surety declaration: for the surety on your release, and so for you.
@export Under form 12, may my surety ask to no longer be a surety?
GIVEN way IS A `form 12 way of ceasing to be a surety` @desc How does the surety want to stop being a surety? One of: form 12 by making an application, form 12 by bringing the accused to the court in order to be discharged from the surety's obligation (section 767), form 12 by taking and giving the accused into custody (section 768), form 12 in another way
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 12, may my surety ask to no longer be a surety` IS
    `form 12 item 8 the surety may, at any time, ask to no longer be a surety` way

§§ `A warrant for your arrest or for your committal (Forms 7, 8, 21 and 23)`
-- Applies if a warrant has been issued for your arrest or for your committal to prison.

@export Under form 7, may the peace officers enter my dwelling-house to arrest me?
GIVEN `the warrant has the dwelling-house box checked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the box on the warrant that also authorizes entry into a dwelling-house checked?
      `the officers had reasonable grounds immediately before entering to believe I was present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officers have, immediately before entering the dwelling-house, reasonable grounds to believe that the person to be arrested was present in it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 7, may the peace officers enter my dwelling-house to arrest me` IS
    `form 7 the officer may enter the dwelling-house to arrest the accused` `the warrant has the dwelling-house box checked` `the officers had reasonable grounds immediately before entering to believe I was present`

@export Under form 7, which sections does the warrant for my arrest cite for the ground it states?
GIVEN ground IS A `form 7 ground` @desc Which ground does the warrant check? One of: form 7 ground (a), form 7 ground (b), form 7 ground (c), form 7 ground (d), form 7 ground (e), form 7 ground (f), form 7 ground (g), form 7 ground (h), form 7 ground (i), form 7 ground (j)
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Provision of the Code`)
DECIDE `Under form 7, which sections does the warrant for my arrest cite for the ground it states` IS
    `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` ground

@export Under form 8, which sections does the warrant for my committal cite for the ground it states?
GIVEN ground IS A `form 8 ground` @desc Which ground does the warrant check? One of: form 8 ground (a), form 8 ground (b), form 8 ground (c), form 8 ground (d), form 8 ground (e), form 8 ground (f)
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Provision of the Code`)
DECIDE `Under form 8, which sections does the warrant for my committal cite for the ground it states` IS
    `form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` ground

@export Under form 21, does the warrant still direct the keeper to imprison me for the term of my imprisonment?
GIVEN `my term was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your term of imprisonment imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs?
      `I have paid those amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying me to the prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the fine or costs, and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying you to the prison, been paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 21, does the warrant still direct the keeper to imprison me for the term of my imprisonment` IS
    `form 21 the keeper is to imprison the offender for the term of imprisonment` `my term was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs` `I have paid those amounts and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying me to the prison`

@export Under form 23, does the warrant still direct the keeper to imprison me for failing to enter into a recognizance to keep the peace?
GIVEN `I have entered into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since entered into the recognizance?
      `I have been discharged in due course of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been discharged in due course of law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under form 23, does the warrant still direct the keeper to imprison me for failing to enter into a recognizance to keep the peace` IS
    `form 23 the keeper is to imprison the accused` `I have entered into the recognizance` `I have been discharged in due course of law`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc31 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc31-seat.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER over ccc31 (Forms 24 to 54 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46).
-- Written by work/gen-seat.py from a list of questions; every question calls a layer-1 rule and restates none.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking, on facts they can state, whether what
-- they did is an offence, what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply from arrest through trial, sentence and
-- appeal, and what follows from a conviction. (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this
-- is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.) This range holds the prescribed Forms 24 to 54, so what it answers for that person is what a
-- warrant, an order, a recognizance, a notice or a statement made in the Form says about them: whether they may be held, for how long, what they
-- must do and by when, what rights the Form gives them, and what may follow if they do not comply.
-- The questions are named "Under Form N," or "Under Form N paragraph M," (an extension of the rule "Under section N," / "Under schedule N paragraph M,"
-- to a Form: NOTES.md records the departure), so that no two parts' questions can share a name and each says the scope its answer claims.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. Every question answers true, false or null:
--   true  = the Form's words reach the case on the facts given;
--   false = the Form says no in its own words ("until", "unless", "if", "while", a period that has run);
--   null  = not covered: the Form is silent, or limits itself in its own wording, or a premise it recites is not made out, or the answer of another
--           section or Act (an input here) is not given. NEVER read null as false.
-- Several questions ask "Has this happened to you?" first: the group heading's comment says which situation (being held, endorsed, on probation).
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Each is a fact the person can state (yes or no, a number, a date, a short choice written in the @desc). A period in a Form (a term of
-- imprisonment, a probation order) is asked as years, months and days. Where the Form lets the court choose among alternatives (a, b, c ...), the
-- person says which alternative their document ticks. The answers of other sections (s 2, s 522, s 638(1), ss 490.013, 490.022, 490.02904) are taken as
-- plain facts; where a fact is not known, answer false and read the result with care (NOTES.md "Seams").
§ `Being held in custody, and being released (Forms 24, 25, 26, 27, 30, 35, 39, 49, 50)`

-- Asked only by a person who has been committed to custody, or whose witness has been, under a warrant or order of one of these Forms.
-- The date asked about is the day on which the question is put; a term begins on the day the person was received into custody (fork F16 of NOTES.md).
@export Under Form 24 (section 550): is the keeper directed to keep a witness who failed or refused to enter into a recognizance in custody until the accused's trial? true = the keeper is directed to keep the witness; false = the witness has entered into the recognizance before the trial, or the trial has taken place; null = the witness has not been delivered to the keeper
GIVEN `the witness has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the witness been delivered to the keeper of the prison with the warrant of committal?
      `my trial has taken place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trial of the accused on the charge taken place?
      `before the trial the witness entered into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the witness enter into the recognizance before the trial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 24, is the keeper directed to keep the witness who would not enter into the recognizance in custody until my trial` IS
    `form 24 the keeper is directed to keep the witness in custody` `the witness has been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` `my trial has taken place` `before the trial the witness entered into the recognizance`

@export Under Form 25 (section 708): is the keeper still ordered to keep me, as a witness convicted of contempt for not attending, in custody on the date asked about? true = still ordered; false = the term has run or the sums and costs have been sooner paid; null = the Form does not say (alternative "c", paid while the first term is still running)
GIVEN `the order I am held under` IS A STRING @desc Which alternative does the keeper's order in your warrant tick: "a" (for the term of ___), "b" (for the term, unless the sums and costs are sooner paid) or "c" (two terms, unless the sums and costs are sooner paid)?
      `the day I was received into custody` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you received into custody under the warrant (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-01-01)?
      `the first term, years` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of the first term in the warrant (0 if none).
      `the first term, months` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of the first term (0 if none).
      `the first term, days` IS A NUMBER @desc The days of the first term (0 if none).
      `the second term, years` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of the second term in alternative "c" (0 if none).
      `the second term, months` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of the second term (0 if none).
      `the second term, days` IS A NUMBER @desc The days of the second term (0 if none).
      `the second term is consecutive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does alternative "c" state that the second term is consecutive to the first?
      `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying you to the prison been paid before the date asked about?
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you ask (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-01-15)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 25, am I still to be kept in custody under the warrant of committal for contempt` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order I am held under` EQUALS "a" THEN `held under` `form 25 (a) for the term of`
        IF `the order I am held under` EQUALS "b" THEN `held under` `form 25 (b) for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid`
        IF `the order I am held under` EQUALS "c" THEN `held under` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `held under` order MEANS
            `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` order `the day I was received into custody` (`Length of time` OF `the first term, years`, `the first term, months`, `the first term, days`, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF `the second term, years`, `the second term, months`, `the second term, days`, FALSE) `the second term is consecutive` `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid` `the date asked about`

@export Under Form 25 (section 708): "for so doing this is a sufficient warrant". true = the warrant is sufficient for the keeper who keeps the defaulter as the order directs; null = not covered
GIVEN `the keeper keeps me in custody as the order directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the keeper keep you in custody as the order in the warrant directs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 25, does the warrant protect the keeper who keeps me in custody as the order directs` IS
    `form 25 this is a sufficient warrant for the keeper` `the keeper keeps me in custody as the order directs`

@export Under Form 26 (section 827): is the keeper still commanded to keep me in custody for the term for not paying the costs of an appeal? true = still commanded; false = the term has run, or the sum and the costs and charges have all been sooner paid; null = I have not been delivered to the keeper
GIVEN `I have been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been delivered to the keeper of the prison with the warrant?
      `the day I was received into custody` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you received into custody (ISO 8601)?
      `the term, years` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of the term in the warrant (0 if none).
      `the term, months` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of the term (0 if none).
      `the term, days` IS A NUMBER @desc The days of the term (0 if none).
      `the sum has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum adjudged as costs been paid before the date asked about?
      `the costs and charges have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying you to the prison been paid before the date asked about?
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you ask (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 26, am I still to be kept in custody for not paying the costs of an appeal` IS
    `form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` `I have been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` `the day I was received into custody` (`Length of time` OF `the term, years`, `the term, months`, `the term, days`, FALSE) `the sum has been paid` `the costs and charges have been paid` `the date asked about`

@export Under Form 27 (section 773): is the keeper still ordered to keep me in custody for the period, or until the judgment debt for the forfeiture is satisfied? true = still ordered; false = the period has run or the debt has been satisfied; null = I have not been delivered to the keeper, or the debt is not shown to be due to Her Majesty for a forfeiture
GIVEN `I have been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been delivered to the keeper of the prison with the warrant of committal?
      `the debt is due to Her Majesty for a forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment debt due to Her Majesty in respect of the forfeiture of an amount set out in an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance?
      `the day I was received into custody` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you received into custody (ISO 8601)?
      `the period, years` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of the period in the warrant (0 if none).
      `the period, months` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of the period (0 if none).
      `the period, days` IS A NUMBER @desc The days of the period (0 if none).
      `the debt has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has satisfaction been made of the judgment debt before the date asked about?
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you ask (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 27, am I still to be kept in custody for the forfeiture of an amount` IS
    `form 27 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `I have been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` `the debt is due to Her Majesty for a forfeiture` `the day I was received into custody` (`Length of time` OF `the period, years`, `the period, months`, `the period, days`, FALSE) `the debt has been satisfied` `the date asked about`

@export Under Form 30 (section 537): is the keeper directed to have the accused before a justice, to answer to the charge, before the period of remand expires? true = the keeper is directed; null = the accused was not committed by a warrant for a remand, or the order was not made before the remand expires
GIVEN `I was committed to the keeper by a warrant for a remand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you committed to the keeper's custody by a warrant for a period of remand?
      `the order was made before my remand expires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made before the period of remand expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 30, is the keeper to have me before the justice at the time and place stated` IS
    `form 30 the keeper is directed to have the accused before the justice` `I was committed to the keeper by a warrant for a remand` `the order was made before my remand expires`

@export Under Form 35 (sections 570 and 806): does the imprisonment in default of payment of the sums and costs in the record of my conviction still apply? true = still applies; false = I am not in default, or the sums and costs have been sooner paid, or the term has run; null = the punishment recorded is imprisonment for a term only ("a"), which has no default term
GIVEN `the punishment my conviction records` IS A STRING @desc Which punishment does the record of your conviction state: "a" (imprisonment for a term), "b" (a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default) or "c" (imprisonment and, in addition, a sum and costs, with imprisonment in default)?
      `I did not pay the sums forthwith or within the time fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to pay the sums forthwith, or within the time fixed if the record fixes one?
      `the day I was received into custody in default` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you received into custody in default of payment (ISO 8601)?
      `the default term, years` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of the default term (0 if none).
      `the default term, months` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of the default term (0 if none).
      `the default term, days` IS A NUMBER @desc The days of the default term (0 if none).
      `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the sums and the costs and charges of the committal and of conveying you to the prison been paid before the date asked about?
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you ask (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 35, am I still to be imprisoned in default of paying the sums in my conviction` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the punishment my conviction records` EQUALS "a" THEN `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (a) imprisonment for the term of` `I did not pay the sums forthwith or within the time fixed` `the day I was received into custody in default` (`Length of time` OF `the default term, years`, `the default term, months`, `the default term, days`, FALSE) `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid` `the date asked about`
        IF `the punishment my conviction records` EQUALS "b" THEN `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (b) a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` `I did not pay the sums forthwith or within the time fixed` `the day I was received into custody in default` (`Length of time` OF `the default term, years`, `the default term, months`, `the default term, days`, FALSE) `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid` `the date asked about`
        IF `the punishment my conviction records` EQUALS "c" THEN `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (c) imprisonment and, in addition, a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` `I did not pay the sums forthwith or within the time fixed` `the day I was received into custody in default` (`Length of time` OF `the default term, years`, `the default term, months`, `the default term, days`, FALSE) `the sums and the costs and charges have been paid` `the date asked about`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export Under Form 39 (sections 519 and 550): is the keeper directed to release the person detained under a warrant of committal or order? true = directed to release; false = the person is detained for another cause; null = the person is not detained under the warrant or order the discharge names
GIVEN `I am detained by the keeper under the warrant or order the discharge names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you detained by the keeper under the warrant of committal or order named in the order for your discharge?
      `I am detained by the keeper for another cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also detained by the keeper for any other cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 39, must the keeper release me` IS
    `form 39 the keeper is directed to release the person` `I am detained by the keeper under the warrant or order the discharge names` `I am detained by the keeper for another cause`

@export Under Form 49 (section 672.57): is the keeper directed to keep an accused found unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible in custody until delivered by due course of law? true = directed to keep; false = the accused has been delivered by due course of law; null = the accused has not been delivered to the keeper with the warrant
GIVEN `I have been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been delivered to the keeper (administrator, warden) of the prison, hospital or other place with the warrant?
      `I have been delivered by due course of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been delivered by due course of law (released or moved by an order made as the law provides)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 49, am I to be kept in custody until I am delivered by due course of law` IS
    `form 49 the keeper is directed to keep the accused in custody` `I have been delivered to the keeper with the warrant` `I have been delivered by due course of law`

@export Under Form 49 (section 672.57): is the accused subject to a condition the warrant lists while in the keeper's prison, hospital or other place? true = subject to it; false = the accused is not in that place; null = the condition is not one the warrant lists
GIVEN `the condition is one the warrant lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition one of those the warrant sets out?
      `I am in the keeper's prison, hospital or other place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the keeper's prison, hospital or other place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 49, must I comply with a condition of the warrant while I am in the hospital or other place` IS
    `form 49 the accused is subject to the condition` `the condition is one the warrant lists` `I am in the keeper's prison, hospital or other place`

@export Under Form 50 (subsection 672.7(2)): is the keeper commanded to execute the warrant of committal the question names, after the Review Board decided that the accused be detained in custody? true = commanded to execute that warrant (the box ticked); null = a recital is not made out, or the other box is ticked
GIVEN `I have been charged with the offence the warrant sets out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been charged with the offence the warrant sets out?
      `I was found unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder?
      `the Review Board decided that I be detained in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Review Board hold a hearing and decide that you shall be detained in custody?
      `I am required to be detained under a court's warrant of committal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to be detained in custody under a warrant of committal issued by a court?
      `the box ticked` IS A STRING @desc Which box does the warrant tick: "court" (execute the warrant of committal issued by the court) or "board" (execute the warrant issued by the Review Board)?
      `the warrant asked about` IS A STRING @desc Which warrant do you ask about: "court" or "board"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 50, is the keeper commanded to execute the warrant of committal as the Review Board has decided` IS
    IF NOT ((`the box ticked` EQUALS "court" OR `the box ticked` EQUALS "board") AND (`the warrant asked about` EQUALS "court" OR `the warrant asked about` EQUALS "board"))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` `I have been charged with the offence the warrant sets out` `I was found unfit to stand trial or not criminally responsible` `the Review Board decided that I be detained in custody` `I am required to be detained under a court's warrant of committal` (`which warrant` `the box ticked`) (`which warrant` `the warrant asked about`)
    WHERE
        `which warrant` word MEANS
            IF word EQUALS "court"
            THEN `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms`
            ELSE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued herewith by the Review Board`

§ `Endorsed warrants, release, and the recognizance (Forms 28, 29, 29.1, 32)`

-- Asked by a person who is the subject of an endorsed warrant, who is to be released on one, or who has given or stands surety for a recognizance.
@export Under Form 28 (section 528): does a justice's endorsement authorize the arrest of the accused within the territorial division it names? true = authorized; null = not made on an application, not signed by a justice, or the arrest is outside the territorial division the endorsement names
GIVEN `the endorsement is made in accordance with an application made to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the endorsement made in accordance with an application made to the justice?
      `the person who signed it is a justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who signed the endorsement a justice (s 2)?
      `the arrest is within the territorial division the endorsement names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the arrest within the territorial division the endorsement names?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 28, may I be arrested in the territorial division the endorsement names` IS
    `form 28 the endorsement authorizes the arrest of the accused` `the endorsement is made in accordance with an application made to the justice` (JUST `the person who signed it is a justice`) `the arrest is within the territorial division the endorsement names`

@export Under Form 29 (section 507): does the endorsement authorize the release of the accused under section 499, where the warrant is issued under section 507, 508 or 512 for an offence other than one mentioned in section 522? true = release authorized; null = issued under another section, or the offence is one mentioned in section 522
GIVEN `the section the warrant is issued under` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code was the warrant issued (for example 507, 508 or 512)?
      `the offence is mentioned in section 522` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence one mentioned in section 522 (an offence only a judge may release on)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 29, does the endorsement authorize my release under section 499 on this endorsed warrant` IS
    `form 29 the endorsement authorizes the release of the accused under section 499` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section the warrant is issued under`, "") (JUST `the offence is mentioned in section 522`)

@export Under Form 29.1 (subsection 705(4)): does the endorsement authorize the release of a witness arrested on a warrant under subsection 705(1) or (2)? true = release authorized and the conditions complied with; false = the conditions the endorsement specifies are not complied with; null = the warrant is not under 705(1) or (2), or the person is not a served or bound witness
GIVEN `the subsection the warrant is issued under` IS A STRING @desc Under which subsection of section 705 was the warrant issued: "(1)", "(2)" or another?
      `I was served with a subpoena` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding?
      `I was bound by a recognizance to attend and give evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you bound by a recognizance to attend and give evidence in a proceeding?
      `I comply with the conditions the endorsement specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you comply with the conditions the endorsement specifies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 29.1, may I, a witness arrested on a warrant, be released on the endorsement` IS
    `form 29.1 the endorsement authorizes the release of the witness` (`Provision of the Code` OF 705, `the subsection the warrant is issued under`) `I was served with a subpoena` `I was bound by a recognizance to attend and give evidence` `I comply with the conditions the endorsement specifies`

@export Under Form 32 part 2 (recognizance): may the amount or security be forfeited if the person fails to comply with a condition listed? true = may be forfeited; null = the person has not failed to comply ("if I fail to comply": the Form says nothing of the case where there is no failure)
GIVEN `I have failed to comply with a condition listed in my recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed to comply with a condition listed in your recognizance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 32 part 2, may the amount or security I promised or deposited be forfeited` IS
    `form 32 part 2 the amount or security may be forfeited` `I have failed to comply with a condition listed in my recognizance`

@export Under Form 32 part 3 (recognizance): does the recognizance list the conditions the court ordered and the duration each remains in effect? true = it does; false = it omits the condition or its duration; null = the court ordered no condition
GIVEN `the court ordered a condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court order a condition?
      `my recognizance lists the condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your recognizance list the condition?
      `my recognizance says how long it remains in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your recognizance say for how long the condition remains in effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 32 part 3, does my recognizance list the conditions ordered and how long each lasts` IS
    `form 32 part 3 the recognizance lists the conditions ordered and the duration of each` `the court ordered a condition` `my recognizance lists the condition` `my recognizance says how long it remains in effect`

@export Under Form 32 part 4 (recognizance): may the person apply to a judge or a justice of the peace to have any condition in the Form cancelled or varied? true = may apply; null = the condition is not in the Form, or the application is not to a judge or a justice of the peace
GIVEN `the condition is in my recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition in your recognizance?
      `I would apply to a judge or a justice of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you apply to a judge or a justice of the peace?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 32 part 4, may I apply to a judge or justice to cancel or vary a condition of my recognizance` IS
    `form 32 part 4 the person may apply to cancel or vary a condition` `the condition is in my recognizance` `I would apply to a judge or a justice of the peace`

@export Under Form 32 part 5 (recognizance; sections 763 and 764): do the conditions remain in effect until cancelled or changed, or until the person is discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court? true = still in effect; false = one of those has happened
GIVEN `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the conditions been cancelled or changed?
      `I have been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been discharged?
      `I have been sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been sentenced?
      `I have been otherwise detained by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been otherwise detained by the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 32 part 5, are the conditions of my recognizance still in effect` IS
    `form 32 part 5 the conditions remain in effect` `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` `I have been discharged` `I have been sentenced` `I have been otherwise detained by the court`

@export Under Form 32 part 6 (recognizance): must the person who signed the recognizance comply with the conditions listed? true = must comply; null = the person has not signed, or the condition is not listed
GIVEN `I have signed the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed the recognizance?
      `the condition is listed in my recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition listed in your recognizance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 32 part 6, must I comply with a condition listed in my recognizance` IS
    `form 32 part 6 the person must comply with the condition` `I have signed the recognizance` `the condition is listed in my recognizance`

@export Under Form 32 part 6 (recognizance): may the money the surety promised or deposited be forfeited if the person giving the recognizance fails to comply with a condition? true = may be forfeited; null = the person has not failed to comply ("if I fail to comply": the Form says nothing of the case where there is no failure)
GIVEN `I have failed to comply with a condition in my recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you (the person giving the recognizance) failed to comply with a condition in it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 32 part 6, may the money my surety promised or deposited be forfeited` IS
    `form 32 part 6 the money the surety has promised or deposited may be forfeited` `I have failed to comply with a condition in my recognizance`

@export Under Form 32 (recognizance): is a condition of the List of Conditions one the Form lists for a section? true = the Form lists it for that section; null = the Form does not list it for that section (the Form's parentheses give the sections without "only"), or the paragraph is not one of the List
GIVEN `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` IS A STRING @desc Which paragraph of the List of Conditions in your recognizance: "a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "e.1", "e.2", "f", "f.1", "g", "h", "i", "j", "k", "l", "m", "n", "o", "p" or "q"?
      `the section` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which section of the Criminal Code is the condition ordered (for example 810.1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 32, is a condition in the List of Conditions one the Form lists for this section` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "a" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (a) has a surety` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "b" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (b) agrees to keep the peace and be of good behaviour` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "c" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (c) abstains from possessing a firearm and the other things listed, and surrenders them and the documents` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "d" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (d) participates in a treatment program` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "e" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (e) wears an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "e.1" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (e.1) wears an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General has consented to this condition` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "e.2" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (e.2) abstains from communicating with the intimate partner and others, except as the justice considers necessary` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "f" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (f) remains within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave is obtained` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "f.1" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (f.1) refrains from going to any specified place, except as the justice considers necessary` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "g" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (g) returns to and remains at their place of residence at specified times` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "h" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (h) abstains from the consumption of drugs, except in accordance with a medical prescription` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "i" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (i) abstains from the consumption of alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, except in accordance with a medical prescription` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "j" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (j) abstains from any contact with a person under the age of 18 years` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "k" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (k) abstains from using the Internet or other digital network` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "l" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (l) abstains from attending a public park or public swimming area, daycare centre, schoolground or playground` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "m" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (m) appears personally or by counsel at the sittings of the appeal court` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "n" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (n) appears in court as required` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "o" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (o) refrains from affecting property under a warrant or restraint order` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "p" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (p) agrees to prosecute the writ of certiorari at their own expense` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        IF `the paragraph of the List of Conditions` EQUALS "q" THEN `form 32 the condition is listed for the section` `form 32 condition (q) any other reasonable conditions` (`Provision of the Code` OF `the section`, "")
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Writs and jury challenges (Forms 34, 40, 41)`

-- Form 34 is asked by a person named in a writ of fieri facias (for example after a forfeiture). Forms 40 and 41 are asked by an accused about to be tried by a jury.
@export Under Form 34 (section 771): how much of the amount set opposite a person's name in the writ of fieri facias is the sheriff still commanded to levy from that person's goods, chattels, lands and tenements? answers an amount in dollars (0 once the amount is levied); null = the person is not named in the writ
GIVEN `I am named in the writ` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you named in the writ?
      `the amount set opposite my name` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in dollars set opposite your name in the writ.
      `the amount already levied from me` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in dollars the sheriff has already levied from you.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Form 34, how much is the sheriff still commanded to levy from my goods and lands` IS
    `form 34 the amount the sheriff is commanded to levy from the person` `I am named in the writ` `the amount set opposite my name` `the amount already levied from me`

@export Under Form 40 (section 629): is the accused's challenge to the array of the panel, on the ground that the sheriff or deputy sheriff who returned it was guilty of partiality, fraud or wilful misconduct, in the Form's terms? true = the challenge is in the Form's terms; null = the panel was not returned by a sheriff or deputy sheriff, or the ground is not one the Form names
GIVEN `the panel was returned by a sheriff or deputy sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the panel returned by a sheriff or a deputy sheriff?
      `the ground` IS A STRING @desc The ground: "partiality", "fraud", "wilful misconduct" or another ground (write "other")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 40, is my challenge to the array of the panel of jurors on this ground in the Form's terms` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the ground` EQUALS "partiality" THEN `form 40 the challenge to the array is in the Form's terms` `form 40 the accused` `the panel was returned by a sheriff or deputy sheriff` `form 40 partiality`
        IF `the ground` EQUALS "fraud" THEN `form 40 the challenge to the array is in the Form's terms` `form 40 the accused` `the panel was returned by a sheriff or deputy sheriff` `form 40 fraud`
        IF `the ground` EQUALS "wilful misconduct" THEN `form 40 the challenge to the array is in the Form's terms` `form 40 the accused` `the panel was returned by a sheriff or deputy sheriff` `form 40 wilful misconduct`
        OTHERWISE `form 40 the challenge to the array is in the Form's terms` `form 40 the accused` `the panel was returned by a sheriff or deputy sheriff` `form 40 another ground`

@export Under Form 41 (section 639): is the accused's challenge to a juror for cause, on a ground set out in accordance with subsection 638(1), in the Form's terms? true = in the Form's terms; null = the ground is not shown to be a ground of subsection 638(1)
GIVEN `the ground is one subsection 638(1) allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground one that subsection 638(1) allows for a challenge for cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 41, is my challenge to a juror for cause on this ground in the Form's terms` IS
    `form 41 the challenge for cause is in the Form's terms` `form 41 the accused` (JUST `the ground is one subsection 638(1) allows`)

§ `Statements about the harm done, and restitution (Forms 34.1, 34.2, 34.3, 48.2)`

-- Asked by a person being sentenced (Forms 34.1, 34.2, 34.3) or found not criminally responsible (Form 48.2), about what a victim's or a community's statement may contain.
@export Under Form 34.1 (subsection 737.1(4)): may a loss or damage be claimed as restitution? true = its amount is readily ascertainable by the court; false = it is not ("must be readily ascertainable by the court")
GIVEN `the amount of the loss or damage is readily ascertainable by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the court readily ascertain the amount of the loss or damage (bills, receipts, estimates)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 34.1, may a victim claim this loss from me as restitution` IS
    `form 34.1 the loss may be claimed as restitution` `the amount of the loss or damage is readily ascertainable by the court`

@export Under Form 34.2 (subsection 722(4)): may a victim impact statement include the content? true = the Form says it may (an example the Form gives); false = the Form says it must not include it; null = not covered (the Form's examples are not a closed list; or, once the approval for an opinion or recommendation is given, the Form is silent)
GIVEN `the kind of content` IS A STRING @desc What kind of content: "emotional impact", "physical impact", "economic impact", "fears for security", "drawing", "irrelevant", "allegation", "comment", "complaint", "opinion"? (write "other" for anything else)
      `the approval was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court approved an opinion or recommendation about the sentence (answer false if not asked)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 34.2, may a victim impact statement include this content` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "emotional impact" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 emotional impact` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "physical impact" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 physical impact` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "economic impact" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 economic impact` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "fears for security" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 fears for security` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "drawing" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 a drawing, poem or letter` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "irrelevant" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 a statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "allegation" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 an unproven allegation` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "comment" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 a comment about an offence for which the offender was not convicted` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "complaint" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 a complaint about an individual, other than the offender, involved in the investigation or prosecution` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "opinion" THEN `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 an opinion or recommendation about the sentence` `the approval was given`
        OTHERWISE `form 34.2 the statement may include the item` `form 34.2 any other content` `the approval was given`

@export Under Form 34.2 (subsection 722(4)): is a victim impact statement an application for compensation or restitution? false = the Form says it is not
GIVEN `I ask the question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Answer true to ask whether the statement is an application for compensation or restitution.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 34.2, is a victim impact statement an application for compensation or restitution` IS
    IF `I ask the question`
    THEN `form 34.2 this is an application for compensation or restitution`
    ELSE NOTHING

@export Under Form 34.3 (subsection 722.2(2)): may a community impact statement include the content? true = the Form says it may (an example the Form gives); false = the Form says it must not include it; null = not covered (the Form's examples are not a closed list; or, once the approval for an opinion or recommendation is given, the Form is silent)
GIVEN `the kind of content` IS A STRING @desc What kind of content: "emotional", "physical", "economic", "fears", "drawing", "irrelevant", "allegation", "comment", "complaint", "opinion"? (write "other" for anything else)
      `the approval was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court approved an opinion or recommendation about the sentence (answer false if not asked)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 34.3, may a community impact statement include this content` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "emotional" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 emotional impact on community members` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "physical" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 physical impact on community members` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "economic" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 economic impact on the community` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "fears" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 fears of community members for their security` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "drawing" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 a drawing, poem or letter` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "irrelevant" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 a statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss suffered by the community` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "allegation" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 an unproven allegation` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "comment" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 a comment about an offence for which the offender was not convicted` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "complaint" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 a complaint about an individual, other than the offender, involved in the investigation or prosecution` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "opinion" THEN `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 an opinion or recommendation about the sentence` `the approval was given`
        OTHERWISE `form 34.3 the statement may include the item` `form 34.3 any other content` `the approval was given`

@export Under Form 34.3 (subsection 722.2(2)): is a community impact statement an application for compensation or restitution? false = the Form says it is not
GIVEN `I ask the question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Answer true to ask whether the statement is an application for compensation or restitution.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 34.3, is a community impact statement an application for compensation or restitution` IS
    IF `I ask the question`
    THEN `form 34.3 this is an application for compensation or restitution`
    ELSE NOTHING

@export Under Form 48.2 (subsection 672.5(14)): may a victim impact statement for a person found not criminally responsible include the content? true = the Form says it may (an example the Form gives); false = the Form says it must not include it; null = not covered (the Form's examples are not a closed list; or, once the approval for an opinion or recommendation is given, the Form is silent)
GIVEN `the kind of content` IS A STRING @desc What kind of content: "emotional impact", "physical impact", "economic impact", "fears for security", "drawing", "irrelevant", "allegation", "comment", "complaint", "opinion"? (write "other" for anything else)
      `the approval was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court or the Review Board approved an opinion or recommendation about the disposition (answer false if not asked)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 48.2, may a victim impact statement for a person found not criminally responsible include this content` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "emotional impact" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 emotional impact` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "physical impact" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 physical impact` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "economic impact" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 economic impact` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "fears for security" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 fears for security` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "drawing" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 a drawing, poem or letter` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "irrelevant" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 a statement about the conduct of the accused that is not relevant to the harm or loss` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "allegation" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 an unproven allegation` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "comment" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 a comment about conduct for which the accused was not found not criminally responsible` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "complaint" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 a complaint about an individual, other than the accused, involved in the investigation or prosecution` `the approval was given`
        IF `the kind of content` EQUALS "opinion" THEN `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 an opinion or recommendation about the disposition` `the approval was given`
        OTHERWISE `form 48.2 the statement may include the item` `form 48.2 any other content` `the approval was given`

@export Under Form 48.2 (subsection 672.5(14)): is a victim impact statement for a person found not criminally responsible an application for compensation or restitution? false = the Form says it is not
GIVEN `I ask the question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Answer true to ask whether the statement is an application for compensation or restitution.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 48.2, is a victim impact statement for a person found not criminally responsible an application for compensation or restitution` IS
    IF `I ask the question`
    THEN `form 48.2 this is an application for compensation or restitution`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `After conviction: probation, tax information, samples (Forms 46, 47, 51)`

-- Asked by an offender under a probation order (Form 46), by a person whose tax information is sought for an investigation (Form 47), or by a person served with a notice to provide samples (Form 51).
@export Under Form 46 (section 732.1): on what date do the conditions of the probation order begin? answers a date: the date of the order, or, for paragraphs (d), (e) and (f), the date of expiration of the sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order; null = the paragraph is not one of (a) to (g)
GIVEN `the paragraph my order ticks` IS A STRING @desc Which paragraph of the probation order does the court tick: "a" (discharge on conditions), "b" (sentence suspended), "c" (fine, with imprisonment in default), "d" (imprisonment), "e" (after a conditional sentence order), "f" (after a sentence for another offence) or "g" (intermittent sentence)?
      `the date of my order` IS A DATE @desc The date of the probation order (ISO 8601).
      `the date my sentence or conditional sentence order expires` IS A DATE @desc The date your sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order expires (ISO 8601; the order date if none).
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Form 46, on what date do the conditions of my probation order begin` IS
    IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "a" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "b" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "c" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "d" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "e" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "f" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "g"
    THEN JUST (`form 46 the conditions begin on` `my adjudication` `the date of my order` `the date my sentence or conditional sentence order expires`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `my adjudication` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "a" THEN `form 46 (a) discharged on conditions`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "b" THEN `form 46 (b) passing of sentence suspended and released on conditions`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "c" THEN `form 46 (c) fine, imprisonment in default of payment, and conditions in addition`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "d" THEN `form 46 (d) imprisoned and, in addition, conditions`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "e" THEN `form 46 (e) conditions following the expiration of a conditional sentence order`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "f" THEN `form 46 (f) conditions following the expiration of a sentence of imprisonment related to another offence`
                OTHERWISE `form 46 (g) intermittent sentence, conditions when not in confinement`

@export Under Form 46 (section 732.1): must the offender comply with the conditions of the probation order on a day? true = within the period of the order (and, for paragraph (g), not in confinement); false = before the period begins, after it ends, or (g) in confinement; null = the paragraph is not one of (a) to (g)
GIVEN `the paragraph my order ticks` IS A STRING @desc Which paragraph of the probation order does the court tick: "a" (discharge on conditions), "b" (sentence suspended), "c" (fine, with imprisonment in default), "d" (imprisonment), "e" (after a conditional sentence order), "f" (after a sentence for another offence) or "g" (intermittent sentence)?
      `the date of my order` IS A DATE @desc The date of the probation order (ISO 8601).
      `the date my sentence or conditional sentence order expires` IS A DATE @desc The date your sentence of imprisonment or conditional sentence order expires (ISO 8601; the order date if none).
      `the years of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of the period of the order (0 if none).
      `the months of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of the period (0 if none).
      `the days of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The days of the period (0 if none).
      `I am in confinement on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in confinement on the day you ask about?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 46, do the conditions of my probation order bind me on this day` IS
    IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "a" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "b" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "c" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "d" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "e" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "f" OR `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "g"
    THEN `form 46 the offender must comply with the conditions on the day` `my adjudication` `the date of my order` `the date my sentence or conditional sentence order expires` (`Length of time` OF `the years of the period`, `the months of the period`, `the days of the period`, FALSE) `I am in confinement on that day` `the day I ask about`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `my adjudication` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "a" THEN `form 46 (a) discharged on conditions`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "b" THEN `form 46 (b) passing of sentence suspended and released on conditions`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "c" THEN `form 46 (c) fine, imprisonment in default of payment, and conditions in addition`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "d" THEN `form 46 (d) imprisoned and, in addition, conditions`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "e" THEN `form 46 (e) conditions following the expiration of a conditional sentence order`
                IF `the paragraph my order ticks` EQUALS "f" THEN `form 46 (f) conditions following the expiration of a sentence of imprisonment related to another offence`
                OTHERWISE `form 46 (g) intermittent sentence, conditions when not in confinement`

@export Under Form 46 (section 732.1): is the offender in compliance with the standing conditions (keep the peace and be of good behaviour, appear before the court when required, notify of a change of name or address in advance, promptly notify of a change of employment or occupation)? true = in compliance; false = a duty is not met
GIVEN `I have kept the peace and been of good behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you kept the peace and been of good behaviour?
      `the court has required me to appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court required you to appear?
      `I appeared when required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appear before the court when required?
      `my name or address has changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your name or address changed?
      `I notified in advance of the change of name or address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the court or your probation officer in advance of the change of name or address?
      `my employment or occupation has changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employment or occupation changed?
      `I notified promptly of the change of employment or occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you promptly notify the court or your probation officer of the change of employment or occupation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 46, am I in compliance with the standing conditions of my probation order` IS
    `form 46 the offender is in compliance with the standard conditions` `I have kept the peace and been of good behaviour` `the court has required me to appear` `I appeared when required` `my name or address has changed` `I notified in advance of the change of name or address` `my employment or occupation has changed` `I notified promptly of the change of employment or occupation`

@export Under Form 47 (section 462.48): does an order made on the recitals authorize and require the addressee to produce the income tax information? true = it appears on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe the person named committed or benefited from the offence, the information is likely to be of substantial value to the investigation, and disclosure is in the public interest; null = a recital is not made out
GIVEN `it appears on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe I committed or benefited from the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that you committed or benefited from the commission of the offence?
      `the information is likely to be of substantial value to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the information or documents likely to be of substantial value to an investigation of the offence or a related matter?
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that access is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 47, does an order made on these grounds authorize and require the disclosure of my income tax information` IS
    `form 47 the order authorizes and requires the addressee to produce the information` `it appears on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe I committed or benefited from the offence` `the information is likely to be of substantial value to the investigation` `there are reasonable grounds to believe that access is in the public interest`

@export Under Form 51 (the notice to provide samples), paragraph 1: is the first reporting day permitted, "not earlier than 24 hours after the day on which the notice is served"? true = at least one day after the day of service; false = earlier
GIVEN `the day the notice was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the notice was served on you (ISO 8601).
      `the first day I am told to report` IS A DATE @desc The first day the notice tells you to report (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 51 paragraph 1, is the first day I am told to report to give a sample a permitted day` IS
    `form 51 para 1 the first report is on a permitted day` `the day the notice was served on me` `the first day I am told to report`

@export Under Form 51 (the notice to provide samples), paragraph 2: must the person report on a day, every stated number of days (not less than seven) after the first report? true = on the schedule; false = not on the schedule, or not after the first report; null = the notice states fewer than seven days
GIVEN `the first day I reported` IS A DATE @desc The date of your first report (ISO 8601).
      `the number of days the notice states` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the notice states between reports.
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 51 paragraph 2, must I report to give a sample on this day` IS
    `form 51 para 2 the person must report on the day` `the first day I reported` `the number of days the notice states` `the day I ask about`

@export Under Form 51 (the notice to provide samples), paragraph 3: has the person the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation? true = the person served with the notice has the right; null = not covered
GIVEN `I have been served with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been served with the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 51 paragraph 3, may I apply to a court to end the obligation to provide samples` IS
    `form 51 para 3 the person may apply to terminate the obligation` `I have been served with the notice`

@export Under Form 51 (the notice to provide samples), paragraph 4: what may follow if the person is found not to have complied? answers "a fine or imprisonment, or both" or "proceedings under section 742.6" (conditional sentence), or the notice states no consequence if the person is not found to have failed to comply
GIVEN `I am found to have not complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you found to have not complied with the obligation to provide samples?
      `my obligation is part of a conditional sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the obligation part of a conditional sentence?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Form 51 paragraph 4, what may follow if I do not comply with the obligation to provide samples` IS
    CONSIDER `form 51 para 4 the consequence of not complying` `I am found to have not complied` `my obligation is part of a conditional sentence`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST consequence THEN
        CONSIDER consequence
        WHEN `form 51 a fine or imprisonment, or both` THEN JUST "a fine or imprisonment, or both"
        WHEN `form 51 proceedings under section 742.6, the consequences of which may include imprisonment` THEN JUST "proceedings under section 742.6, the consequences of which may include imprisonment"
        WHEN `form 51 the notice states no consequence, the person not having been found to have failed to comply` THEN JUST "the notice states no consequence, the person not having been found to have failed to comply"

§ `My mental condition: assessment orders (Forms 48, 48.1)`

-- Asked by an accused whose mental condition is to be assessed on an order of the court (Form 48) or of the Review Board (Form 48.1).
@export Under Form 48 (section 672.13): does the court have grounds to order an assessment of the accused's mental condition for a purpose? true = it has the grounds and the purpose's own condition (if any) is met; false = the purpose's "if" is not met (purpose 3: the accused is not a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child; purposes 4 and 5: the verdict has not been rendered); null = the court lacks the grounds the Form recites
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A NUMBER @desc Which purpose: 1 (whether the accused is unfit to stand trial), 2 (whether the accused was exempt from criminal responsibility by s 16(1)), 3 (whether the balance of the mind was disturbed), 4 (the appropriate disposition) or 5 (whether to order a stay of proceedings)?
      `the court has reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of your mental condition may be necessary to determine the purpose?
      `I am a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of my newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of your newly-born child?
      `the child is a newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child a newly-born child (a person under the age of one year, s 2)?
      `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict of unfit to stand trial been rendered in respect of you?
      `a verdict of not criminally responsible has been rendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder been rendered in respect of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 48, does the court have grounds to order an assessment of my mental condition for this purpose` IS
    IF NOT (`the purpose` AT LEAST 1 AND `the purpose` AT MOST 5)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `form 48 the court has grounds to order an assessment for the purpose` (`which purpose`) `the court has reasonable grounds` `I am a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of my newly-born child` (JUST `the child is a newly-born child`) `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered` `a verdict of not criminally responsible has been rendered`
    WHERE
        `which purpose` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the purpose` EQUALS 1 THEN `form 48 purpose 1 whether the accused is unfit to stand trial`
                IF `the purpose` EQUALS 2 THEN `form 48 purpose 2 whether the accused suffered from a mental disorder so as to exempt the accused from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)`
                IF `the purpose` EQUALS 3 THEN `form 48 purpose 3 whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence`
                IF `the purpose` EQUALS 4 THEN `form 48 purpose 4 the appropriate disposition under section 672.54, 672.58 or 672.64, or whether to revoke a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused`
                OTHERWISE `form 48 purpose 5 whether the court should order a stay of proceedings under section 672.851`

@export Under Form 48 (section 672.13): is the order in force for a total of the stated number of days, including travelling time, counted from the day of the order? true = within those days; false = before or after
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE @desc The date of the assessment order (ISO 8601).
      `the total number of days the order is in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The total number of days the order is in force, including travelling time.
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 48, is the assessment order of the court still in force on this day` IS
    `form 48 the order is in force` `the date of the order` `the total number of days the order is in force` `the day I ask about`

@export Under Form 48 (section 672.13): is the accused to comply with a condition the order sets out? true = the accused is to remain out of custody on the conditions and the condition is one the order sets out; null = the accused is to remain in custody, or the condition is not one the order sets out
GIVEN `the box ticked` IS A STRING @desc Which box does the order tick: "custody" (in custody at the place named) or "out" (out of custody, on conditions)?
      `the condition is one the order sets out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition one the order sets out?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 48, must I comply with a condition of the assessment order of the court` IS
    IF `the box ticked` EQUALS "out"
    THEN `form 48 the accused must comply with the condition` `form 48 out of custody, on the conditions set out` `the condition is one the order sets out`
    ELSE `form 48 the accused must comply with the condition` `form 48 in custody at the place named` `the condition is one the order sets out`

@export Under Form 48.1 (section 672.13): does the Review Board have grounds to order an assessment for a purpose? true = it has the grounds and the verdict condition is met; false = the verdict has not been rendered ("if a verdict ... has been rendered"); null = the Board lacks the grounds the Form recites
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A NUMBER @desc Which purpose: 1 (to make a disposition or decide whether to refer a high-risk finding for review) or 2 (to decide whether to recommend an inquiry into a stay of proceedings)?
      `the Review Board has reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Review Board have reasonable grounds to believe that evidence of your mental condition may be necessary for the purpose?
      `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict of unfit to stand trial been rendered in respect of you?
      `a verdict of not criminally responsible has been rendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder been rendered in respect of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 48.1, does the Review Board have grounds to order an assessment of my mental condition for this purpose` IS
    IF NOT (`the purpose` EQUALS 1 OR `the purpose` EQUALS 2)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `form 48.1 the Review Board has grounds to order an assessment for the purpose` (`which purpose`) `the Review Board has reasonable grounds` `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered` `a verdict of not criminally responsible has been rendered`
    WHERE
        `which purpose` MEANS
            IF `the purpose` EQUALS 1
            THEN `form 48.1 purpose 1 to make a disposition under section 672.54 or determine whether to refer a high-risk finding for review under subsection 672.84(1)`
            ELSE `form 48.1 purpose 2 to determine whether to recommend an inquiry into a stay of proceedings under section 672.851`

@export Under Form 48.1 (section 672.13): is the order in force for a total of the stated number of days, including travelling time, counted from the day of the order? true = within those days; false = before or after
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE @desc The date of the assessment order (ISO 8601).
      `the total number of days the order is in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The total number of days the order is in force, including travelling time.
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 48.1, is the assessment order of the Review Board still in force on this day` IS
    `form 48.1 the order is in force` `the date of the order` `the total number of days the order is in force` `the day I ask about`

§ `The sex offender registration notices (Forms 52, 53, 54)`

-- Asked only by a person who has been given an order (Form 52) or a notice (Forms 53, 54) to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act. Whether the order is for life is the answer of sections 490.013, 490.022 and 490.02904, which the person states from their own order.
@export Under Form 52 (the order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act), paragraph 2: for what period must the person report after the day of sentence or the order? answers the number of years, or "life"; null = not covered
GIVEN `the years my order states` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years your order says you must report after you were sentenced or the order was made (0 if it says for life).
      `my order is for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your order say you must report for life?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Form 52 paragraph 2, for how many years must I report to the registration centre` IS
    CONSIDER `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` `the years my order states` (IF `my order is for life` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        CONSIDER period
        WHEN `form 52 for a period of years` numberOfYears THEN JUST (CONCAT "for ", TOSTRING numberOfYears, " years")
        WHEN `form 52 for life` THEN JUST "for life"

@export Under Form 52 (the order to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act), paragraph 2: must the person report on a day, when required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act and within the period? true = required and within the period (or for life); false = not required that day, or outside the period
GIVEN `the years my order states` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years your order says you must report (0 if it says for life).
      `my order is for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your order say you must report for life?
      `the day my period starts` IS A DATE @desc The date the order was made (ISO 8601).
      `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to report on the day you ask about, under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 52 paragraph 2, must I report to the registration centre on this day` IS
    IF `my order is for life`
    THEN `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 52 for life` `the day my period starts` `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` `the day I ask about`
    ELSE `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 52 for a period of years` OF `the years my order states`) `the day my period starts` `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` `the day I ask about`

@export Under Form 52 paragraph 6: has the person the right to apply to a court to terminate the order? true = the person the order is given to has the right; null = not covered
GIVEN `I am subject to the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person the order is given to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 52 paragraph 6, may I apply to a court to end my duty to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS
    `form 52 para 6 the person may apply to terminate the order` `I am subject to the order`

@export Under Form 52 paragraph 7: may the person be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or both, if found not to have complied? true = may be; false = the person is not found to have contravened
GIVEN `I am found to have not complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you found to have contravened or not complied with the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 52 paragraph 7, may I be fined or imprisoned if I do not comply` IS
    `form 52 para 7 the consequence of contravening the order` `I am found to have not complied`

@export Under Form 53 (the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act), paragraph 2: for what period must the person report after the day of sentence or the order? answers the number of years, or "life"; null = not covered
GIVEN `the years my obligation states` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years your obligation says you must report after you were sentenced or the order was made (0 if it says for life).
      `my obligation is for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your obligation say you must report for life?
      `a shorter period applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 490.022(2) set a shorter period for you?
      `the shorter period in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The shorter period in years (0 if none).
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Form 53 paragraph 2, for how many years must I report to the registration centre` IS
    CONSIDER `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` `the years my obligation states` (IF `my obligation is for life` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) `a shorter period applies` `the shorter period in years`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        CONSIDER period
        WHEN `form 53 for a period of years` numberOfYears THEN JUST (CONCAT "for ", TOSTRING numberOfYears, " years")
        WHEN `form 53 for life` THEN JUST "for life"

@export Under Form 53 (the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act), paragraph 2: must the person report on a day, when required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act and within the period? true = required and within the period (or for life); false = not required that day, or outside the period
GIVEN `the years my obligation states` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years your obligation says you must report (0 if it says for life).
      `my obligation is for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your obligation say you must report for life?
      `the day my period starts` IS A DATE @desc The date you were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder (ISO 8601).
      `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to report on the day you ask about, under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 53 paragraph 2, must I report to the registration centre on this day` IS
    IF `my obligation is for life`
    THEN `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 53 for life` `the day my period starts` `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` `the day I ask about`
    ELSE `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 53 for a period of years` OF `the years my obligation states`) `the day my period starts` `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` `the day I ask about`

@export Under Form 53 paragraph 7: has the person the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation? true = the person the notice is given to has the right; null = not covered
GIVEN `I am subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person the notice is given to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 53 paragraph 7, may I apply to a court to end my duty to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS
    `form 53 para 7 the person may apply to terminate the obligation` `I am subject to the obligation`

@export Under Form 53 paragraph 8: may the person be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or both, if found not to have complied? true = may be; false = the person is not found to have contravened
GIVEN `I am found to have not complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you found to have contravened or not complied with the obligation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 53 paragraph 8, may I be fined or imprisoned if I do not comply` IS
    `form 53 para 8 the consequence of contravening the obligation` `I am found to have not complied`

@export Under Form 54 (the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act), paragraph 2: for what period must the person report after the day of sentence or the order? answers the number of years, or "life"; null = not covered
GIVEN `the years my obligation states` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years your obligation says you must report after you were sentenced or the order was made (0 if it says for life).
      `my obligation is for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your obligation say you must report for life?
      `a shorter period applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 490.02904(2) set a shorter period for you?
      `the shorter period in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The shorter period in years (0 if none).
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Form 54 paragraph 2, for how many years must I report to the registration centre` IS
    CONSIDER `form 54 para 2 the period for which the person must report` `the years my obligation states` (IF `my obligation is for life` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) `a shorter period applies` `the shorter period in years`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        CONSIDER period
        WHEN `form 54 for a period of years` numberOfYears THEN JUST (CONCAT "for ", TOSTRING numberOfYears, " years")
        WHEN `form 54 for life` THEN JUST "for life"

@export Under Form 54 (the obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act), paragraph 2: must the person report on a day, when required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of that Act and within the period? true = required and within the period (or for life); false = not required that day, or outside the period
GIVEN `the years my obligation states` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years your obligation says you must report (0 if it says for life).
      `my obligation is for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your obligation say you must report for life?
      `the day my period starts` IS A DATE @desc The date you were sentenced, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder (ISO 8601).
      `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to report on the day you ask about, under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask about (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 54 paragraph 2, must I report to the registration centre on this day` IS
    IF `my obligation is for life`
    THEN `form 54 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 54 for life` `the day my period starts` `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` `the day I ask about`
    ELSE `form 54 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 54 for a period of years` OF `the years my obligation states`) `the day my period starts` `I am required to report that day under section 4.1 or 4.3` `the day I ask about`

@export Under Form 54 paragraph 7: has the person the right to apply to a court to terminate the obligation? true = the person the notice is given to has the right; null = not covered
GIVEN `I am subject to the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person the notice is given to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 54 paragraph 7, may I apply to a court to end my duty to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS
    `form 54 para 7 the person may apply to terminate the obligation` `I am subject to the obligation`

@export Under Form 54 paragraph 8: may the person be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or both, if found not to have complied? true = may be; false = the person is not found to have contravened
GIVEN `I am found to have not complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you found to have contravened or not complied with the obligation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Form 54 paragraph 8, may I be fined or imprisoned if I do not comply` IS
    `form 54 para 8 the consequence of not complying` `I am found to have not complied`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ccc32 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-12; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- ccc32-seat.l4 -- the SEAT LAYER over the part-ccc32 modules: the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, lines 19056-19797 of the text
-- (the related and transitional provisions of amending Acts, and the AMENDMENTS NOT IN FORCE).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or may be, accused of an offence under the Criminal Code (the accused), asking on facts they can state whether what they did is an offence,
-- what its gravity and penalty are, what defences, rights and procedures apply at each stage from arrest through trial, sentence and appeal, and what follows from a conviction.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: Singapore's Penal Code is the model, as the maintainer instructed on 2026-11-09, but this is a plain seat layer; no charge-generator contract.)
-- This range holds the TRANSITIONAL rules (which text governs a person charged, bailed, tried or sentenced around a change of the law) and the amendments NOT YET IN FORCE
-- (a new offence, a new review body for convictions, a new victim surcharge). The questions below say so in their headings.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, a choice from a list), one for each fact the accused can state, each with an @desc worded as the accused would be asked.
-- The modules' own records are built inside each question; the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here. A day that the text leaves to commencement
-- ("the day on which section 12 of that Act comes into force") is asked as a date: it is a fixed fact about the amending Act, not about the accused, and none of those days is in the sources.
-- A yes or no the accused gives for a borrowed term (for example whether someone is an "intimate partner" within section 2) is passed on as a firm yes or no: this layer cannot say "not covered" on the accused's behalf.
--
-- HOW AN ANSWER READS. Nearly every question answers a yes-or-no-or-not-covered value (a MAYBE BOOLEAN).
-- Five ask for a value instead: the commencement day of 2026, c. 19 (a DATE), how a reference to child pornography is read after 2024, c. 23 (a MAYBE STRING),
-- the class of offence and the most years of imprisonment on indictment under the future section 264.01(4) (a `Class of offence` and a NUMBER), and the form of the new proceeding under the future paragraph 696.6(2)(a).
--   JUST TRUE    yes: the facts bring the case within the provision, on its own words;
--   JUST FALSE   no: the text says no in its own words (an "only", a flat negative, an "until", a period fixed in the text, or a failed "if" within the provision, which is a marginal reading for a lawyer);
--   NOTHING      not covered: the provision does not reach the case, the text is silent, or it points outside the Act. Never read NOTHING as no.
-- No answer here says whether you will be convicted, acquitted or sentenced: each says what the one provision decides.
--
-- THE AMENDMENTS NOT IN FORCE. A question whose heading says "not in force" asks about the FUTURE text of a provision. Show those questions only to a person who asks about the future text.
--
-- Where the existing encoding departs from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18 (recorded, not fixed, in this pass):
--   * Judgments the text leaves to someone else are taken as plain facts (whether the Commission "considers" a factor relevant, whether a matter is a "new matter of significance").
--   * Provisions that address only an official (the Review Board, the Commission, the Minister) are asked for what they mean to the accused: what is continued, deemed, limited, owed to them.
--   * Committee reviews and reports to Parliament (about 20 provisions) are machinery and have no question.


§ `Transitional provisions of amending Acts, 1991 to 2015 -- what governs if you were detained, charged, sentenced or heard around a change of the law`

-- layer 1: `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force`
@export Does the order for detention I am held under (an order under section 614, 615 or 617 of the Criminal Code or section 200 or 201 of the National Defence Act, as those sections read before 1991, c. 43 changed them) stay in force, under section 10(1) of 1991, c. 43?
GIVEN `the kind I choose` IS A `1991 c 43 s 10(1) kind of order for detention` @desc Which kind of order for detention is it? Choose the section it was made under.
      `the order was made under that section as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 3 or 18 of 1991, c. 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made under that section as it read immediately before sections 3 and 18 of 1991, c. 43 came into force?
      `an order has been made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court or Review Board already made an order about me under section 672.54?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(1) of 1991 c 43, does my detention order made by a lieutenant governor's warrant stay in force` IS
    `1991 c 43 s 10(1) the order for detention continues in force` `the kind I choose` `the order was made under that section as it read immediately before the coming into force of section 3 or 18 of 1991, c. 43` `an order has been made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54`

-- layer 1: `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force`
@export Was the Review Board's review of my case held within twelve months after section 10 of 1991, c. 43 came into force (section 10(2))?
GIVEN `the day on which section 10 of 1991, c. 43 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 10 of 1991, c. 43 come into force?
      `the day the Review Board reviewed the case` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Review Board review my case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(2) of 1991 c 43, was the Review Board's review of my case within twelve months` IS
    `1991 c 43 s 10(2) the review was within twelve months after the coming into force` `the day on which section 10 of 1991, c. 43 came into force` `the day the Review Board reviewed the case`

-- layer 1: `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review`
@export Does a particular section of the Criminal Code (sections 672.5 to 672.85, with the changes the circumstances require) apply to the Review Board's review of my detention under section 10(2) of 1991, c. 43?
GIVEN `the section number of the section of the Code` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the provision you are asking about? (For example 672.54.)
      `the subsection of the section of the Code` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection, if any? (Leave empty if none; for example "(1)".)
      `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding the review of my case under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(3) of 1991 c 43, does a given section of the Criminal Code apply to the Review Board's review of my case` IS
    `1991 c 43 s 10(3) the section applies, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to the review` `the section of the Code as a provision of the Code` `the proceeding is a review under subsection 10(2) of 1991, c. 43`
    WHERE
        `the section of the Code as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the section of the Code`, `the subsection of the section of the Code`

-- layer 1: `2009 c 29 s 5 the person is within the limit on subsections 719(3) to (3.4)`
@export Am I within the limit that section 5 of 2009, c. 29 sets on subsections 719(3) to (3.4) of the Criminal Code (the limit on credit for time held before sentence), which apply only to persons charged after the day they came into force, given the day I was charged?
GIVEN `the day on which subsections 719(3) to (3.4) of the Act come into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did subsections 719(3) to (3.4) come into force?
      `the day the person was charged` IS A DATE @desc On what day was I charged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 5 of 2009 c 29, am I within the limit on subsections 719(3) to (3.4) because of when I was charged` IS
    `2009 c 29 s 5 the person is within the limit on subsections 719(3) to (3.4)` `the day on which subsections 719(3) to (3.4) of the Act come into force` `the day the person was charged`

-- layer 1: `2011 c 2 s 7(1) the application is dealt with and disposed of under the Code as it read immediately before that day`
@export Is my application for a reduction of the time before I can apply for parole (an application under section 745.6) dealt with under the Criminal Code as it read immediately before the change (2011, c. 2, s. 7(1))?
GIVEN `the application was made under section 745.6 as that section read immediately before the day on which section 3 of 2011, c. 2 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I make the application under section 745.6 as it read immediately before the day on which section 3 of 2011, c. 2 came into force?
      `the application is still not finally disposed of on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was my application still not finally disposed of on that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(1) of 2011 c 2, is my application under section 745.6 dealt with under the old law` IS
    `2011 c 2 s 7(1) the application is dealt with and disposed of under the Code as it read immediately before that day` `the application was made under section 745.6 as that section read immediately before the day on which section 3 of 2011, c. 2 comes into force` `the application is still not finally disposed of on that day`

-- layer 1: `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended`
@export May I make a new application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended, within 180 days after the end of two years after I became the subject of a determination (2011, c. 2, s. 7(2))?
GIVEN `the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I make an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2?
      `the person is the subject of a determination under subsection 745.61(4) as it read before the day on which subsection 7(2) comes into force, or of a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) as it read before that day applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I the subject of a determination under 745.61(4) as it read before the change, or of a determination or conclusion under 745.63(8) as it read before the change?
      `the day on which the person is the subject of the determination or conclusion` IS A DATE @desc On what day did I become the subject of that determination or conclusion?
      `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` IS A DATE @desc On what day do I make (or want to make) the new application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(2) of 2011 c 2, may I make a new application under section 745.6(1) now` IS
    `2011 c 2 s 7(2) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` `the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` `the person is the subject of a determination under subsection 745.61(4) as it read before the day on which subsection 7(2) comes into force, or of a determination or conclusion to which subsection 745.63(8) as it read before that day applies` `the day on which the person is the subject of the determination or conclusion` `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)`

-- layer 1: `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended`
@export May I make a new application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended, within 180 days after the end of the time that was set for me (2011, c. 2, s. 7(3))?
GIVEN `the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I make an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2?
      `a time is set in respect of the person under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as enacted by subsections 4(3) and 5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a time set for me under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a)?
      `the day on which that time ends` IS A DATE @desc On what day does (or did) that time end?
      `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)` IS A DATE @desc On what day do I make (or want to make) the new application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 7(3) of 2011 c 2, may I make a new application under section 745.6(1) after a time set for me has ended` IS
    `2011 c 2 s 7(3) the person may make an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended` `the person made an application referred to in subsection 7(1) of 2011, c. 2` `a time is set in respect of the person under paragraph 745.61(3)(a) or 745.63(6)(a) as enacted by subsections 4(3) and 5(1)` `the day on which that time ends` `the day on which the person makes an application under subsection 745.6(1) as amended by subsection 3(1)`

-- layer 1: `2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon`
@export Is a reference to an application for a record suspension in paragraph 672.35(c) or subsection 750(4) also a reference to my application for a pardon (2012, c. 1, s. 163(a))?
GIVEN `the section number of the provision the reference is in` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the provision the reference is in? (672.35 or 750.)
      `the subsection of the provision the reference is in` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection or paragraph? (For example "(c)" or "(4)".)
      `the application is an application for a pardon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my application an application for a pardon?
      `the application is not finally disposed of on the day on which section 163 of 2012, c. 1 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it still not finally disposed of on the day section 163 of 2012, c. 1 came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 163(a) of 2012 c 1, is a reference to an application for a record suspension also a reference to my pardon application` IS
    `2012 c 1 s 163(a) the reference to an application for a record suspension is also a reference to an application for a pardon` `the provision the reference is in as a provision of the Code` `the application is an application for a pardon` `the application is not finally disposed of on the day on which section 163 of 2012, c. 1 comes into force`
    WHERE
        `the provision the reference is in as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the provision the reference is in`, `the subsection of the provision the reference is in`

-- layer 1: `2012 c 1 s 165(b) the reference to a record suspension is also a reference to a pardon`
@export Is a reference to a record suspension in the definition record suspension in subsection 490.011(1) also a reference to my pardon (2012, c. 1, s. 165(b))?
GIVEN `the section number of the provision the reference is in` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the provision the reference is in? (490.011.)
      `the subsection of the provision the reference is in` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection? (For example "(1)".)
      `the reference is in the definition record suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference in the definition record suspension?
      `the pardon is a pardon that is granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my pardon one that was granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 165(b) of 2012 c 1, is a reference to a record suspension in the Code also a reference to my pardon` IS
    `2012 c 1 s 165(b) the reference to a record suspension is also a reference to a pardon` `the provision the reference is in as a provision of the Code` `the reference is in the definition record suspension` `the pardon is a pardon that is granted or issued under the Criminal Records Act`
    WHERE
        `the provision the reference is in as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the provision the reference is in`, `the subsection of the provision the reference is in`

-- layer 1: `2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing`
@export Does subsection 278.3(5) as it read before the change continue to apply to my hearing, because it takes place on the day section 6 of 2015, c. 13 came into force or within 14 days after (2015, c. 13, s. 37)?
GIVEN `the day on which section 6 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 6 of 2015, c. 13 come into force?
      `the day the hearing takes place` IS A DATE @desc On what day does my hearing take place?
      `the hearing is a hearing referred to in subsection 278.3(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a hearing referred to in subsection 278.3(5) (a hearing on production of records in the accused's possession)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37 of 2015 c 13, does the old subsection 278.3(5) still apply to my hearing` IS
    `2015 c 13 s 37 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` `the day on which section 6 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` `the day the hearing takes place` `the hearing is a hearing referred to in subsection 278.3(5)`

-- layer 1: `2015 c 13 s 38 section 380.3 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the request for restitution`
@export Does section 380.3 as it read before the change continue to apply to a request for restitution made to the court before section 11 of 2015, c. 13 came into force (2015, c. 13, s. 38)?
GIVEN `the day on which section 11 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 11 of 2015, c. 13 come into force?
      `the day the request for restitution was made to the court under section 380.3` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the request for restitution made to the court under section 380.3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 38 of 2015 c 13, does the old section 380.3 still apply to a request for restitution made against me` IS
    `2015 c 13 s 38 section 380.3 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the request for restitution` `the day on which section 11 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` `the day the request for restitution was made to the court under section 380.3`

-- layer 1: `2015 c 13 s 39 section 380.4 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the statement`
@export Does section 380.4 as it read before the change continue to apply to a statement filed with the court before section 11 of 2015, c. 13 came into force (2015, c. 13, s. 39)?
GIVEN `the day on which section 11 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 11 of 2015, c. 13 come into force?
      `the day the statement was filed with the court under section 380.4` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the statement filed with the court under section 380.4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39 of 2015 c 13, does the old section 380.4 still apply to a community impact statement filed in my case` IS
    `2015 c 13 s 39 section 380.4 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the statement` `the day on which section 11 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` `the day the statement was filed with the court under section 380.4`

-- layer 1: `2015 c 13 s 40 the conduct is within the limit on section 423.1`
@export Is the conduct I engaged in within the limit that section 40 of 2015, c. 13 sets on section 423.1 (intimidation of a justice system participant or a journalist), as amended, which applies only to conduct on or after the day section 12 came into force?
GIVEN `the day on which section 12 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 12 of 2015, c. 13 come into force?
      `the day the conduct was engaged in` IS A DATE @desc On what day did I engage in the conduct I am charged with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40 of 2015 c 13, is what I did within the limit on section 423.1 as amended` IS
    `2015 c 13 s 40 the conduct is within the limit on section 423.1` `the day on which section 12 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` `the day the conduct was engaged in`

-- layer 1: `2015 c 13 s 41 section 672.5 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the statement`
@export Does section 672.5 as it read before the change continue to apply to a statement filed with the court or Review Board before section 22 of 2015, c. 13 came into force (2015, c. 13, s. 41)?
GIVEN `the day on which section 22 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 22 of 2015, c. 13 come into force?
      `the day the statement was filed with the court or Review Board under section 672.5` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the statement filed with the court or Review Board under section 672.5?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41 of 2015 c 13, does the old section 672.5 still apply to a victim impact statement filed before the change` IS
    `2015 c 13 s 41 section 672.5 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the statement` `the day on which section 22 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` `the day the statement was filed with the court or Review Board under section 672.5`

-- layer 1: `2015 c 13 s 42 the conduct is within the limit on the amendments to section 718`
@export Is the conduct I engaged in within the limit that section 42 of 2015, c. 13 sets on the amendments to section 718 (the purposes and principles of sentencing), which apply only to sentences for conduct on or after the day section 23 came into force?
GIVEN `the day on which section 23 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did section 23 of 2015, c. 13 come into force?
      `the day the conduct was engaged in` IS A DATE @desc On what day did I engage in the conduct I am to be sentenced for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 42 of 2015 c 13, is the conduct I may be sentenced for within the limit on the amendments to section 718` IS
    `2015 c 13 s 42 the conduct is within the limit on the amendments to section 718` `the day on which section 23 of 2015, c. 13 comes into force` `the day the conduct was engaged in`

-- layer 1: `2015 c 13 s 42.1 the conduct is within the limit on the amendment to paragraph 718.2(e)`
@export Is the conduct I engaged in within the limit that section 42.1 of 2015, c. 13 sets on the amendment to paragraph 718.2(e) (the sentencing principle for Indigenous offenders), which applies only to sentences for conduct on or after the day section 24 came into force?
