§ `NOT IN FORCE -- the victim surcharge (section 737(1) as it would be replaced by 2018 c 16)`
-- This group asks about the FUTURE text of section 737(1) (2018, c. 16, s. 190, not in force, and conditional on another Bill), and nothing else.

-- layer 1: `s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence`
@export Under the future subsection 737(1) (2018, c. 16, s. 190, not in force), must I pay a victim surcharge for each offence, if I am convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence under the Criminal Code, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act, subject to subsection (1.1)?
GIVEN `the offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I convicted, or discharged under section 730, of the offence?
      `the offence is an offence under the Criminal Code, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence an offence under the Criminal Code, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act?
      `s 737(1.1) subsection 737(1.1) relieves the offender of the surcharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 737(1.1) relieve me of the surcharge? (Answer yes or no.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 737(1) (not in force), must I pay a victim surcharge` IS
    `s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence` `the offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730, of the offence` `the offence is an offence under the Criminal Code, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act` (JUST `s 737(1.1) subsection 737(1.1) relieves the offender of the surcharge`)

§ `NOT IN FORCE -- the new review of convictions by the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission (Part XXI.1, as replaced by 2024 c 33) and release pending the review`
-- Every question in this group asks about the FUTURE text of Part XXI.1 and of section 679(7) (2024, c. 33, ss. 2, 3, 5 and 6), which is not in force. The applicant of this Part is the person who was found guilty (or found a dangerous or long-term offender, or not criminally responsible).

-- layer 1: `s 696.2(1) (not in force) an application for a review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Commission by or on behalf of the person`
