§ `NOT IN FORCE -- exemption from, and termination of, the duty to comply with a sex offender registration order (sections 490.04 to 490.06, as amended by 2026 c 16)`
-- Every question in this group asks about the FUTURE text of sections 490.04, 490.05 and 490.06 (2026, c. 16, ss. 50 to 52, not in force). The lead-ins of those sections are in-force text of another part: an item outside the replaced paragraphs is answered as not covered.

-- layer 1: `s 490.04(1) (not in force) the order or obligation is one listed in paragraph (a), (a.1) or (b)`
@export Under the future paragraphs 490.04(1)(a), (a.1) and (b) (not in force), is the order or obligation I am subject to one of the orders and obligations listed there, about which a person may apply for an exemption order?
GIVEN `the kind I choose` IS A `s 490.04(1) (not in force) the order or obligation` @desc Which is it: an order under section 490.012; an order under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act; an obligation under section 490.02901; an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act; or something else?
      `the day the order was made or the obligation began` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order made, or the obligation begun?
      `the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(a.1) comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did paragraph 490.04(1)(a.1) come into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.04(1) (not in force), is my order or obligation one listed in paragraphs (a), (a.1) and (b)` IS
    `s 490.04(1) (not in force) the order or obligation is one listed in paragraph (a), (a.1) or (b)` `the kind I choose` `the day the order was made or the obligation began` `the day on which paragraph 490.04(1)(a.1) comes into force`

-- layer 1: `s 490.04(2) (not in force) the person is permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b)`
@export Under the future subsection 490.04(2) (not in force), am I permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b) if, on or after October 26, 2023, I made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 about the same obligation?
GIVEN `the person has made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 in respect of the same obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have I made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 about the same obligation?
      `the day the person made that application` IS A DATE @desc On what day did I make that application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.04(2) (not in force), am I permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b) after an earlier application` IS
    `s 490.04(2) (not in force) the person is permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b)` `the person has made an application for an exemption order under section 490.02905 or 490.029111 in respect of the same obligation` `the day the person made that application`

-- layer 1: `s 490.04(3)(a) (not in force) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction is a court that may receive the application`
@export Under the future paragraph 490.04(3)(a) (not in force), is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction a court that may receive my application for an exemption order?
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my application made under paragraph (1)(a) about an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction?
      `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my application made under paragraph (1)(a.1)?
      `the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.22(2) of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Chief Military Judge not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.22(2) of the National Defence Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.04(3)(a) (not in force), is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction a court that may receive my application` IS
    `s 490.04(3)(a) (not in force) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction is a court that may receive the application` `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a.1)` `the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.22(2) of the National Defence Act`

-- layer 1: `s 490.04(4) (not in force) the court may make an exemption order`
@export Under the future subsection 490.04(4) (not in force), may the court make an exemption order on my application, or does one of the bars apply (an indictable offence with a sentence of two years or more and a victim under 18, or the matters in paragraph (b))?
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my application made under paragraph (1)(a)?
      `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my application made under paragraph (1)(a.1)?
      `the designated offence that is the basis of the order was prosecuted by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the designated offence that is the basis of the order prosecuted by indictment?
      `the sentence for that offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sentence for that offence a term of imprisonment of two years or more?
      `the victim of that offence was under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim of that offence under the age of 18 years?
      `s 490.04(4)(b) before or after the order was made, the person did what subparagraphs (b)(i) and following describe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before or after the order was made, did I do what subparagraph (b)(i) and the following paragraphs of that subsection describe? (Answer yes or no.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.04(4) (not in force), may the court make an exemption order for me` IS
    `s 490.04(4) (not in force) the court may make an exemption order` `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a.1)` `the designated offence that is the basis of the order was prosecuted by indictment` `the sentence for that offence is a term of imprisonment of two years or more` `the victim of that offence was under the age of 18 years` (JUST `s 490.04(4)(b) before or after the order was made, the person did what subparagraphs (b)(i) and following describe`)

-- layer 1: `s 490.04(8) (not in force) the court shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove the information from the database`
@export Under the future subsection 490.04(8) (not in force), if the court makes an exemption order, must it also order the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove the information about me from the database?
GIVEN `the court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court make an exemption order?
      `the source I choose` IS A `s 490.04(8) (not in force) what the information was registered on receipt of` @desc What was the information registered on receipt of: a copy of the order under section 490.012; a copy of the order under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act; the notice under section 490.02901; the Form 1 under subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act; or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.04(8) (not in force), if the court makes an exemption order, must it also order my information removed from the database` IS
    `s 490.04(8) (not in force) the court shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove the information from the database` `the court makes an exemption order` `the source I choose`

-- layer 1: `s 490.05(1) (not in force) the order or obligation is one listed in the replaced paragraphs`
@export Under the future paragraphs 490.05(1)(a), (a.1), (b.1), (c) and (d) (not in force), is my order or obligation, which applies for life, one of those listed?
GIVEN `the kind I choose` IS A `s 490.05(1) (not in force) the order or obligation` @desc Which is it: an order under section 490.012; an order under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act; an obligation under section 227.06 of the National Defence Act; an obligation under section 490.02901; an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act; or something else?
      `the order or obligation applies for life under the provision the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it apply for life under the provision the paragraph names?
      `none of the offences listed in the prescribed form served on the person under the National Defence Act in respect of the obligation has a maximum term of imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does none of the offences listed in the prescribed form served on me under the National Defence Act about the obligation have a maximum term of imprisonment for life?
      `the day the obligation began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the obligation begin?
      `the condition set out in the paragraph the item names is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition set out in the paragraph the item names met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.05(1) (not in force), is my order or obligation one listed in the replaced paragraphs` IS
    `s 490.05(1) (not in force) the order or obligation is one listed in the replaced paragraphs` `the kind I choose` `the order or obligation applies for life under the provision the paragraph names` `none of the offences listed in the prescribed form served on the person under the National Defence Act in respect of the obligation has a maximum term of imprisonment for life` `the day the obligation began` `the condition set out in the paragraph the item names is met`

-- layer 1: `s 490.05(3)(a) (not in force) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction is a court that may receive the application`
@export Under the future paragraph 490.05(3)(a) (not in force), is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction a court that may receive my application for an order terminating the obligation?
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my application made under paragraph (1)(a) about an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction?
      `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a.1) or (b.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is my application made under paragraph (1)(a.1) or (b.1)?
      `the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.23(2) of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Chief Military Judge not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.23(2) of the National Defence Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.05(3)(a) (not in force), is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction a court that may receive my application` IS
    `s 490.05(3)(a) (not in force) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction is a court that may receive the application` `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of an order made by a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a.1) or (b.1)` `the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 227.23(2) of the National Defence Act`

-- layer 1: `s 490.06(2) (not in force) the appeal court shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove the information from the database`
@export Under the future subsection 490.06(2) (not in force), if an appeal court makes an exemption order, must it also order the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove the information about me from the database?
GIVEN `the appeal court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the appeal court make an exemption order?
      `the source I choose` IS A `s 490.06(2) (not in force) what the information was registered on receipt of` @desc What was the information registered on receipt of: a copy of the order under section 490.012; a copy of the order under section 227.01 of the National Defence Act; the notice under section 490.02901; the Form 1 under subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act; or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.06(2) (not in force), if an appeal court makes an exemption order, must it also order my information removed from the database` IS
    `s 490.06(2) (not in force) the appeal court shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove the information from the database` `the appeal court makes an exemption order` `the source I choose`

§ `NOT IN FORCE -- the new offence of coercion or control of an intimate partner (section 264.01, 2026 c 19) and what it changes elsewhere`
-- Every question in this group asks about the FUTURE text of the Criminal Code (2026, c. 19, ss. 2(2), 4, 24(5), 28, 42, 45(2)), which is not in force. Show it only to a person who asks about the future text.

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(2) (not in force) the acts make up a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct` (and the functions this question's raw text names)
@export Under the future section 264.01(2) (2026, c. 19, s. 28, not in force), do my acts make up a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct: any combination, or repeated instances, of violence (paragraph (a)), coercion to sexual activity (paragraph (b)) and other conduct that could reasonably be expected to make my intimate partner believe their safety is threatened (paragraph (c))?
GIVEN `the number of acts of using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against my intimate partner, a child under 18 in their care or charge, another person known to them or an animal known to them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such acts were there? (Paragraph (a) of the future section 264.01(2).)
      `the number of acts of coercing or attempting to coerce my intimate partner to engage in sexual activity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such acts were there? (Paragraph (b).)
      `the number of other acts that could reasonably be expected, in all the circumstances, to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such other acts were there? (Paragraph (c): for example controlling their movements, money, work, appearance or beliefs, threatening self-harm, or damaging property.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(2) (not in force), do my acts make up a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct` IS
    `s 264.01(2) (not in force) the acts make up a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct`
        (`s 264.01(2) (not in force) acts` OF `the number of acts of using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against my intimate partner, a child under 18 in their care or charge, another person known to them or an animal known to them`, `the number of acts of coercing or attempting to coerce my intimate partner to engage in sexual activity`, `the number of other acts that could reasonably be expected, in all the circumstances, to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened`)

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(1) (not in force) the accused commits an offence` (and the functions this question's raw text names)
@export Under the future section 264.01(1) (2026, c. 19, s. 28, not in force), would I commit the offence of coercion or control of an intimate partner: a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct, with intent, knowledge or recklessness that it would make my intimate partner believe their safety is threatened?
GIVEN `the number of acts of using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence` IS A NUMBER @desc How many acts of using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against my intimate partner, a child under 18 in their care or charge, another person known to them or an animal known to them were there? (Paragraph (a).)
      `the number of acts of coercing sexual activity` IS A NUMBER @desc How many acts of coercing or attempting to coerce my intimate partner to engage in sexual activity were there? (Paragraph (b).)
      `the number of other acts that threaten safety` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other acts were there that could reasonably be expected to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened? (Paragraph (c).)
      `I acted with intent to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act with the intent to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened?
      `I acted knowing that the pattern would cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act knowing that the pattern would cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened?
      `I acted being reckless as to whether the pattern would cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act being reckless as to whether the pattern would cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened?
      `the person is my intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person my intimate partner, as the Criminal Code defines intimate partner in section 2? (Answer yes or no.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(1) (not in force), would my conduct be the offence of coercion or control of an intimate partner` IS
    `s 264.01(1) (not in force) the accused commits an offence`
        (`s 264.01(2) (not in force) the acts make up a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct` (`s 264.01(2) (not in force) acts` OF `the number of acts of using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence`, `the number of acts of coercing sexual activity`, `the number of other acts that threaten safety`))
        `I acted with intent to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened`
        `I acted knowing that the pattern would cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened`
        `I acted being reckless as to whether the pattern would cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety is threatened`
        (JUST `the person is my intimate partner`)

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct is within paragraph (c)`
@export Under the future section 264.01(2)(c) (not in force), is other conduct of mine within paragraph (c), if in all the circumstances it could reasonably be expected to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened?
GIVEN `in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In all the circumstances, could the conduct reasonably be expected to cause my intimate partner to believe that their safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(2)(c) (not in force), is my other conduct within paragraph (c)` IS
    `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct is within paragraph (c)` `in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened`

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(3) (not in force) the circumstances referred to in paragraph (2)(c) include the circumstance`
@export Under the future section 264.01(3) (not in force), is the circumstance I name one of the circumstances referred to in paragraph (2)(c)?
GIVEN `the circumstance I choose` IS A `s 264.01(3) (not in force) the circumstance` @desc Which circumstance: the nature of the relationship, whether the intimate partner is in a position of vulnerability, whether the accused manipulated them by targeting their vulnerabilities, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(3) (not in force), is a given circumstance one that paragraph (2)(c) includes` IS
    `s 264.01(3) (not in force) the circumstances referred to in paragraph (2)(c) include the circumstance` `the circumstance I choose`

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(5) (not in force) a person’s safety includes the kind of safety`
@export Under the future section 264.01(5) (not in force), does a person's safety include the kind of safety I name (psychological safety)?
GIVEN `the kind I choose` IS A `s 264.01(5) (not in force) the kind of safety` @desc Which kind of safety: psychological safety, or another kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(5) (not in force), does a person's safety include a given kind of safety` IS
    `s 264.01(5) (not in force) a person’s safety includes the kind of safety` `the kind I choose`

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(4) (not in force) the class of the offence` (and the functions this question's raw text names)
@export Under the future section 264.01(4) (not in force), is the offence indictable, punishable on summary conviction, or both?
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(4) (not in force), is the offence indictable, summary or both` IS
    `s 264.01(4) (not in force) the class of the offence`

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(4) (not in force) the punishment for the offence` (and the functions this question's raw text names)
@export Under the future section 264.01(4)(a) (not in force), what is the longest term of imprisonment, in years, that I can be sentenced to if convicted on indictment?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(4) (not in force), what is the most I can be imprisoned for, in years, if convicted on indictment` IS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment on indictment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` length THEN length's years
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN 0
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN 0
    WHERE
        `the maximum imprisonment on indictment` MEANS (`s 264.01(4) (not in force) the punishment for the offence` `by indictment` `a placeholder for the summary limb, which the indictable limb does not read`)'s `maximum imprisonment`
        `a placeholder for the summary limb, which the indictable limb does not read` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- layer 1: `s 109(1)(b) (not in force) the offence is one listed in paragraph (b)`
@export Under the future paragraph 109(1)(b) (2026, c. 19, s. 4, not in force), is the offence I am convicted of one of the offences the paragraph lists (including criminal harassment and the new coercion or control of an intimate partner)?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence charged` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (For example 264 or 264.01.)
      `the subsection of the offence charged` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection, if any? (For example "(1)"; leave empty if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1)(b) (not in force), is my offence one listed in the future paragraph` IS
    `s 109(1)(b) (not in force) the offence is one listed in paragraph (b)` `the offence charged as a provision of the Code`
    WHERE
        `the offence charged as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence charged`, `the subsection of the offence charged`

-- layer 1: `s 3.01(1)(b.1) (not in force) the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted`
@export Under the future paragraph 3.01(1)(b.1) (2026, c. 19, s. 2(2), not in force), does the offence of coercion or control of an intimate partner count as an offence in which violence is used, threatened or attempted?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence charged` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (For example 264.01.)
      `the subsection of the offence charged` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection, if any? (Leave empty if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 3.01(1)(b.1) (not in force), does my offence count as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted` IS
    `s 3.01(1)(b.1) (not in force) the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted` `the offence charged as a provision of the Code`
    WHERE
        `the offence charged as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence charged`, `the subsection of the offence charged`

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) the act is within paragraph (a)`
@export Under the future paragraph 264.01(2)(a) (not in force), is my act of using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence within paragraph (a), given who or what it was against?
GIVEN `the act is using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence?
      `the target I choose` IS A `s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) the target of the act` @desc Against whom or what: the intimate partner; a person under 18 who is the intimate partner's child or in their lawful care or charge; any other person known to the intimate partner; any animal known to the intimate partner; or another target?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(2)(a) (not in force), is an act of violence of mine within paragraph (a)` IS
    `s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) the act is within paragraph (a)` `the act is using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence` `the target I choose`

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(2)(b) (not in force) the act is within paragraph (b)`
@export Under the future paragraph 264.01(2)(b) (not in force), is my conduct within paragraph (b): coercing or attempting to coerce my intimate partner to engage in sexual activity?
GIVEN `the accused coerced or attempted to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I coerce or attempt to coerce my intimate partner to engage in sexual activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(2)(b) (not in force), is my conduct within paragraph (b), coercing sexual activity` IS
    `s 264.01(2)(b) (not in force) the act is within paragraph (b)` `the accused coerced or attempted to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity`

-- layer 1: `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct is listed in one of the subparagraphs`
@export Under the future paragraph 264.01(2)(c) (not in force), is my conduct one of the kinds listed in subparagraphs (i) to (viii) (the list is not closed)?
GIVEN `the conduct I choose` IS A `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct` @desc Which kind of conduct: controlling or monitoring location, movements, actions or social interactions; controlling care of a child or animal; controlling employment or education; controlling finances or property; controlling gender expression, appearance, dress, diet or medication or health services; controlling expression of thoughts, opinions, beliefs or culture; threatening suicide or self-harm; damaging or threatening property; or other conduct?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 264.01(2)(c) (not in force), is my conduct one of the kinds listed in subparagraphs (i) to (viii)` IS
    `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct is listed in one of the subparagraphs` `the conduct I choose`

-- layer 1: `s 183 "offence" (a)(xxxix.4) (not in force) the offence is within paragraph (a) of the definition`
@export Under the future subparagraph (xxxix.4) of paragraph (a) of the definition offence in section 183 (2026, c. 19, s. 24(5), not in force), is my offence within paragraph (a) of that definition (the offences for which a judge may authorize the interception of private communications)?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence charged` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (For example 264.01.)
      `the subsection of the offence charged` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection, if any? (Leave empty if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 183 (not in force), is the offence of coercion or control of an intimate partner within paragraph (a) of the definition offence in Part VI` IS
    `s 183 "offence" (a)(xxxix.4) (not in force) the offence is within paragraph (a) of the definition` `the offence charged as a provision of the Code`
    WHERE
        `the offence charged as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence charged`, `the subsection of the offence charged`

-- layer 1: `s 487.04 "secondary designated offence" (c)(v.1) (not in force) the offence is within paragraph (c) of the definition`
@export Under the future subparagraph (v.1) of paragraph (c) of the definition secondary designated offence in section 487.04 (2026, c. 19, s. 42, not in force), is my offence within paragraph (c) of that definition (a secondary designated offence is an offence, other than a primary designated offence, that is within one of the paragraphs of the definition; a DNA order may be made for it)?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence charged` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (For example 264.01.)
      `the subsection of the offence charged` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection, if any? (Leave empty if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 487.04 (not in force), is the offence of coercion or control of an intimate partner within paragraph (c) of the definition secondary designated offence` IS
    `s 487.04 "secondary designated offence" (c)(v.1) (not in force) the offence is within paragraph (c) of the definition` `the offence charged as a provision of the Code`
    WHERE
        `the offence charged as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence charged`, `the subsection of the offence charged`

-- layer 1: `s 490.011(1) "secondary offence" (a)(ix.1) (not in force) the offence is within paragraph (a) of the definition`
@export Under the future subparagraph (ix.1) of paragraph (a) of the definition secondary offence in subsection 490.011(1) (2026, c. 19, s. 45(2), not in force), is my offence within paragraph (a) of that definition (a secondary offence for the sex offender registry)?
GIVEN `the section number of the offence charged` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the section number of the offence? (For example 264.01.)
      `the subsection of the offence charged` IS A STRING @desc What is its subsection, if any? (Leave empty if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 490.011(1) (not in force), is the offence of coercion or control of an intimate partner within paragraph (a) of the definition secondary offence` IS
    `s 490.011(1) "secondary offence" (a)(ix.1) (not in force) the offence is within paragraph (a) of the definition` `the offence charged as a provision of the Code`
    WHERE
        `the offence charged as a provision of the Code` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF `the section number of the offence charged`, `the subsection of the offence charged`
